# Zolai-English lexicon: general vocabulary and Bible names, sorted by keyword.
# A row with q is not yet confirmed by a speaker of the language; a row without q is confirmed.
a = (t:part) (w:the/a/an) (d:prefix placed before a verb, number or describing word to make a noun phrase, as in a masa, the first, a nihna, the second, and a thatpa, the one who kills) (e:~ kipat cil/~ khiatna/~ nihna Abijah ahi uh hi | the second was Abijah/Mi ~ thatpa kithat ding hi | the one who kills a person shall be put to death/~ sia lamsang peuhmah pelh un | avoid every kind of evil/kim khatte in ~ masa ding uh hi | some will be the first) (r:1.1.1/13.6.28/3.24.17/52.5.22/42.13.30) particle prefixed to form nouns
a = (t:part) (d:particle prefixed to form verb past tense) (e:~ piangsak hi/Mi khempeuh in ~ ne uh a | all the people ate/Zeisu Oliv Mual ah ~ pai hi | Jesus went to the Mount of Olives/thuhilh thei tanu li ~ nei hi | he had four daughters who could prophesy/Moses in Topa’ mai-ah amau’ thu ~ gen hi | Moses spoke of their case before the Lord) (r:1.1.1/43.11.35/41.6.42/43.8.1/44.21.9/4.27.5)
A = (t:pron) (w:his/her/its/their) (d:the third person marker a written with a capital at the start of a sentence or quoted line; before a noun it shows the possessor, his, her, its or their, and before a verb it marks the subject) (e:~ tapa Hammuel, a tapa Zakkur/~ tapa Isaak a suah ciangin | when his son Isaac was born/~ tate in amah it uh a | her children love her/~ kumpipa uh leh a uliante | their king and his officials/~ taitehte leh a kuangte | its wick trimmers and its trays) (s:ama) (b:a) (r:13.4.26/1.21.5/20.31.28/30.1.15/2.25.38) (q:draft)
A = (t:part) (d:the prefix a written with a capital at the start of a sentence, before a describing word or a noun made from a verb, as in A nung ciangin, afterwards, A mawkna-in, in vain, and A beina, the end) (e:~ nung ciangin innkiu suang a piang hi/~ nung ciangin numei zong a si hi | afterwards the woman also died/~ mawkna-in kei hong bia uh hi | they worship me in vain/~ beina hong tung ta hi | the end has come) (b:a) (r:41.12.10/40.15.9/42.20.32/26.7.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
aa = (t:part) (w:belonging to/of) (d:placed after a possessor to mean what belongs to it; keima aa is mine, nomau aa is yours, ko aa is ours and Topa aa is the Lord's) (e:kham khempeuh in keima ~ ahi hi/Ka ngaihno’ ~ ka hi a | I belong to my beloved/Tui, ko ~ hi | the water is ours/ukna in Topa ~ hi a | dominion belongs to the Lord/na peuhmah nomau ~ hi ding hi | everything will be yours) (r:37.2.8/22.7.10/1.26.20/19.22.28/4.18.14) (q:draft)
aai = (t:n) (w:lot) (d:ai written with a long vowel, a lot cast to decide something; aai saan is to cast lots) (e:note adingin ~ ka saan ding hi/Topa mai Shiloh-ah ~ saan sak hi | he had lots cast at Shiloh before the Lord) (b:ai) (r:6.18.6/6.18.10) (q:draft)
aak = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:rooster/cock) (d:the male domestic fowl; aak a khuang means the rooster crows) (e:thakhatin ~ a khuang hi/tuni-in ~ a khuang kei ding hi | the rooster will not crow today/tuzan ~ nihvei a khuan’ ma-in | tonight, before the rooster crows twice/thakhat mahin ~ a khuang pah hi | at that very moment the rooster crowed) (s:ak/aklui) (r:43.18.27/41.14.30/42.22.34/42.22.60) (q:draft)
aam = (t:v) (w:be jealous/jealous) (d:be jealous, unwilling to share with a rival what is one's own; in the verses said of God toward his people, as in a aam Pasian, a jealous God) (e:a ~ Pasian ka hi a/zong kong ~ nawn kei ding hi | and I will no longer be jealous over you/Kha Siangtho in eite hong ~ mahmah hi | the Holy Spirit is very jealous for us/note ka hong ~ mahmah hi | I am very jealous for you) (s:haza) (r:2.20.5/26.16.42/59.4.5/47.11.2) (q:draft)
Aam = (t:adj) (w:Jealous) (d:aam, jealous, written with a capital as a name of God; ama min Aam is whose name is Jealous) (e:ama min ~ a hi pa/Topa ama' min ~ a hipa in | the Lord, whose name is Jealous) (b:aam) (r:2.34.14) (q:draft)
aana = (t:n) (w:authority/power) (d:the right and power to rule or command; ukna aana is ruling authority, aana nei is to have authority and aana zang is to exercise it) (e:mipawlte tungah ukna ~ ka pia ding/vangliatna leh ~ sahang kiangah a pia uh hi | they give power and authority to the beast/a topa’ ta hai tungah ~ nei-in | having authority over his master's foolish son/gam bup tungah ~ zang uh a | they exercised authority over the whole region) (s:thuneihna) (r:66.2.26/66.17.13/20.17.2/15.4.20) (q:draft)
aana = (t:n) (w:force/compulsion) (d:used in aana tawh, by force or under orders; aana tawh na a sem mite are forced laborers) (e:~ tawh na a sem mite la hi/~ tawh na a semte a uk ahi hi | he was in charge of the forced laborers/sila bangin ~ tawh an kigawi sak a | made to grind grain by force like slaves) (s:zawhthawhna/zawhthawh) (r:11.5.13/11.4.6/25.5.13) (q:draft)
Aaron = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aaron) (d:brother of Moses, of the tribe of Levi, and the first high priest of Israel) (r:2.4.14)
Aaronte = (t:name) (w:Aaron) (d:Aaron with the plural te, Aaron and the one named with him; Moses leh Aaronte is Moses and Aaron together) (b:Aaron) (r:19.99.6)
aat = (t:v) (w:reap/harvest) (d:at written with a long vowel; cut a standing crop, reap, the opposite of tuh, sow) (e:mangbuh a tuh uh-a ling ~ uh hi) (s:anla) (a:tuh) (b:at) (r:24.12.13) (q:draft)
aat = (t:v) (w:cut) (d:at written with a long vowel; cut with a blade; aat khia is to cut off) (e:temta neu khat tawh ~ khia-a) (b:at) (r:24.36.23) (q:draft)
aate = (t:n) (w:inheritance/property/possessions) (d:aa, what belongs to someone, with the plural te; in Numbers 36.4 the land that a family inherits) (e:amau’ ~ pen a manawh minamte’) (s:neihsate/luahna) (b:aa) (r:4.36.4) (q:draft)
Abaddon = (t:name) (w:Abaddon) (d:Hebrew name, meaning destruction, of the angel of the Abyss, who is called Apollyon in Greek) (r:66.9.11)
Abagtha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abagtha) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes) (r:17.1.10)
aban = (t:adv) (w:one after another/in turn) (d:used in aban banin, adding one thing to another, step by step) (e:~ banin thu ka phawk khia hi) (s:banbanin) (r:21.7.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
Abana = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Abana) (d:river of Damascus, named by Naaman together with the Pharpar) (r:12.5.12)
Abarim = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Abarim) (d:mountain range in Moab, east of the Jordan, which includes Mount Nebo) (e:Hih ~ mual tungah paito in la) (r:4.27.12/4.33.47) (q:draft)
abat = (t:v) (w:become like/be like) (d:bat, be like, with the prefix a written joined; ciangkhut khat abat is to become as one stick) (e:ciangkhut khat ~ theih nadingin) (b:bat) (r:26.37.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
Abba = (t:n) (w:Abba/Father) (d:Aramaic word for father, used in prayer to God and followed by its translation Pa, Father) (e:~, Pa aw, na khempeuh na bawl) (s:Pa) (r:41.14.36/45.8.15) (q:draft)
Abda = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abda) (d:name of two men: the father of Adoniram, the officer of Solomon over forced labor, and a Levite, the son of Shammua) (r:11.4.6)
Abde = (t:see) <Abde-el>
Abde-el = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdeel) (d:father of Shelemiah, an officer of King Jehoiakim) (r:24.36.26) (q:draft)
Abdeel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdeel) (d:father of Shelemiah, an officer of King Jehoiakim) (r:24.36.26)
Abdi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdi) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite of the clan of Merari and a descendant of Elam in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.26/13.6.44) (q:draft)
Abdiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdiel) (d:son of Guni and father of Ahi, of the tribe of Gad) (r:13.5.15)
Abdon = (t:name) (c:male/city) (w:Abdon) (d:name of several men, among them a judge of Israel, the son of Hillel from Pirathon, and of a town of the Levites in Asher) (r:13.8.30/6.21.30)
Abednego = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abednego) (d:Babylonian name given to Azariah, one of the three friends of Daniel who were thrown into the blazing furnace) (r:27.3.30/27.3.16)
abei = (t:adj) (w:last/final) (d:bei, come to an end, with the prefix a written joined; abei ni is the last day, the opposite of akipat ni, the first day) (e:akipat ni-a kipan ~ ni dong) (s:tawp/nunung/khakbel) (a:akipat/masapen) (b:bei) (r:16.8.18) (q:draft)
Abel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abel) (d:second son of Adam and Eve, a shepherd killed by his brother Cain; in 2 Samuel 20.18 the town Abel Beth Maakah) (r:1.4.2/1.4.4)
Abelbeth = (t:see) <Abelbeth-ma>
Abelbeth-ma = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Beth Maakah) (d:town in the far north of Israel; the first part of the name, which is written Abelbeth-ma-akah in the text) (r:11.15.20) (q:draft)
Abelbethma = (t:see) <Abelbethma-akah>
Abelbethma-akah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Beth Maakah) (d:town in the far north of Israel, near Dan) (r:12.15.29) (q:draft)
Abelbethmaakah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Beth Maakah) (d:town in the far north of Israel, near Dan) (r:10.20.14/11.15.20)
Abelkeramim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abel Keramim) (d:place in the land of the Ammonites, east of the Jordan) (r:7.11.33)
Abelmaim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Maim) (d:town in the north of Israel taken by Ben-Hadad, the same as Abel Beth Maakah) (r:14.16.4)
Abelmeholah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abel Meholah) (d:town in the Jordan valley, the home of the prophet Elisha) (r:7.7.22/11.19.16)
Abelmizraim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Abel-mizraim/Abel Mizraim) (d:place near the Jordan where the Egyptians mourned for Jacob, at the threshing floor of Atad) (r:1.50.11)
Abelshittim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abel Shittim) (d:place in the plains of Moab by the Jordan, where Israel camped before entering Canaan) (r:4.33.49)
Abi = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abijah/Abi) (d:mother of King Hezekiah and daughter of Zechariah; Abi in the Tedim text and Abijah in the NIV) (e:Ama nu’ min ~ hi a) (r:12.18.2) (q:draft)
Abi-albon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abi-Albon) (d:the Arbathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.31) (q:draft)
Abiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abijah) (d:one of those who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah; Abijah in the NIV) (e:Meshullam, ~, Mijamin) (r:16.10.7) (q:draft)
Abialbon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abi-Albon) (d:the Arbathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.31)
Abiasaf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiasaph) (d:son of Korah, of the tribe of Levi) (r:2.6.24)
Abiathar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiathar) (d:priest, son of Ahimelek, who served David together with Zadok) (r:10.20.25/11.4.4)
Abib = (t:name) (w:Abib/Aviv) (d:first month of the Hebrew year, the month of the Passover and of the departure from Egypt) (r:2.13.4)
Abida = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abida) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah) (r:1.25.4)
Abidan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abidan) (d:son of Gideoni, leader of the tribe of Benjamin in the wilderness) (r:4.1.11/4.10.24)
Abiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiel) (d:name of two men: the grandfather of King Saul, and the Arbathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:9.14.51/9.9.1)
Abiezer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiezer) (d:name of two men: a descendant of Manasseh, and a warrior of David from Anathoth) (r:10.23.27/13.11.28)
Abigail = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abigail) (d:name of two women: the wife of Nabal of Carmel who became a wife of David, and a sister of David, the mother of Amasa) (r:10.3.3/9.25.23)
Abigailte = (t:name) (w:Abigail) (d:Abigail with the plural te, Abigail and the one named with her; Ahinoam leh Abigailte is Ahinoam and Abigail together) (b:Abigail) (r:9.30.5/10.2.2)
Abihail = (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Abihail) (d:name of several men and women, among them the father of Queen Esther and the wife of Abishur) (r:13.2.29/4.3.35)
Abihu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abihu) (d:second son of Aaron, a priest who died with his brother Nadab for offering unauthorized fire) (r:4.3.2)
Abihud = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abihud) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin) (r:13.8.3)
Abijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abijah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Samuel, a son of King Jeroboam, and the son of Rehoboam who was king of Judah) (r:9.8.2)
Abijam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abijah) (d:king of Judah, son of Rehoboam and father of Asa; Abijam in the Tedim text of 1 Kings and Abijah in the NIV) (r:11.14.31/11.15.1)
Abilene = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Abilene) (d:region northwest of Damascus, ruled by the tetrarch Lysanias) (r:42.3.1)
Abimael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abimael) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.28)
Abimelek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abimelech/Abimelek) (d:name of two rulers: the king of Gerar in the time of Abraham and Isaac, and the son of Gideon who ruled at Shechem) (r:1.20.2/7.9.22)
Abinadab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abinadab) (d:name of several men, among them the second son of Jesse and a son of King Saul) (r:13.2.13/13.8.33)
Abinoam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abinoam) (d:father of Barak) (r:7.4.12/7.5.1)
Abiram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiram) (d:son of Eliab of the tribe of Reuben, who rebelled against Moses with Korah and Dathan) (r:4.16.1/19.106.17)
Abiramte = (t:name) (w:Abiram) (d:Abiram with the plural te, Abiram and the one named with him; Dathan leh Abiramte is Dathan and Abiram together) (b:Abiram) (r:4.16.12/4.16.24)
Abishag = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abishag) (d:young woman from Shunem who attended King David in his old age) (r:11.2.21/11.1.15)
Abishai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abishai) (d:son of Zeruiah, brother of Joab, and a commander in the army of David) (r:13.18.12/13.19.11)
Abishua = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abishua) (d:name of two men: the son of Phinehas in the line of the high priests, and a son of Bela of Benjamin) (r:13.6.4/13.8.4)
Abishur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abishur) (d:son of Shammai, of the tribe of Judah, and husband of Abihail) (r:13.2.29/13.2.28)
Abital = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abital) (d:wife of David and mother of Shephatiah) (r:13.3.3/10.3.4)
Abithar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiathar) (d:spelling of Abiathar in 1 Samuel 30.7, the priest, son of Ahimelek, who served David) (r:9.30.7)
Abiud = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abihud) (d:son of Zerubbabel in the genealogy of Jesus in Matthew) (r:40.1.13)
Abner = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abner) (d:son of Ner and commander of the army of King Saul) (r:10.2.12/9.14.51)
Abrabia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Arabia) (d:spelling of Arabia in 2 Chronicles 9.14, the land whose kings brought gold and silver to Solomon) (r:14.9.14)
Abraham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abraham) (d:ancestor of the people of Israel, husband of Sarah and father of Isaac, first named Abram) (r:1.21.3)
Abram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abram) (d:the earlier name of Abraham, before God renamed him) (r:1.13.2)
Abronah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abronah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, before Ezion Geber) (r:4.33.34/4.33.35)
Absalom = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Absalom) (d:third son of David, who rebelled against his father and was killed by Joab) (r:10.3.3/10.17.26)
Achzib = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Achzib/Akzib) (d:name of two towns, one in the lowland of Judah and one on the coast of Asher; written Akzib in the text)
Acil = (t:n) (w:beginning) (d:a cil, the beginning, written as one word at the start of a sentence; Acil panin is from the beginning) (e:~ panin hih thute note kiangah) (s:kipatna/kipatcil/kipattung) (a:tawpna/beina) (r:43.16.4) (q:draft)
ada = (t:see) <i-ada>
Ada = (t:see) <Ada-iah>
Ada-iah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adaiah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Jedidah, the mother of King Josiah) (e:Bozkath khuami ~’ tanu ahi hi) (r:12.22.1/16.11.5) (q:draft)
Adadah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Adadah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.22)
adah = (t:see) <La-adah>
Adah = (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Adah) (d:name of two women: a wife of Lamech, and a wife of Esau, the mother of Eliphaz) (r:1.4.19/1.36.10)
adai = (t:see) <Ma-adai>
Adaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adaiah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Jedidah, the mother of King Josiah, and a Levite ancestor of Asaph) (r:13.6.41/12.22.1)
Adalia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adalia) (d:one of the ten sons of Haman) (r:17.9.7)
Adam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adam) (d:the first man, husband of Eve and father of Cain, Abel and Seth) (r:13.1.1/46.15.22)
Adamah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adamah) (d:fortified town of Naphtali; in Joshua 3.16 the town near Zarethan that the NIV calls Adam) (r:6.19.36)
Adaminekeb = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Adami Nekeb) (d:place on the border of the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.33)
adang = (t:prep) (w:for) (e:kanu ~, kapa ~)
adangdangte = (t:pron) (w:others/the like) (d:dang, other, repeated, with the prefix a and the plural te; the other things of the same kind, and the like) (e:zukhamna a kipan ~ ahi hi) (s:adangte) (b:dangdangte) (r:48.5.21) (q:draft)
adangte = (t:pron) (w:others/the others/the rest) (d:dangte, the others, with the prefix a written joined; the remaining people or things of a group) (e:~ tawh kisim khawm lo hi/~ ading bang hang lunghimawh na hi uh hiam | why do you worry about the rest/~ in gimna thuak uh hi | the others suffer hardship/leh ~ tungah ka gen nai kei hi | and I had not yet told the others) (s:adangteng/midangte) (b:dangte) (r:4.1.47/20.28.12/42.12.26/16.2.16) (q:draft)
adangteng = (t:pron) (w:the rest/all the others) (d:dang, other, with the prefix a and teng, all of; all the rest, all who remain) (e:~ salin kiman ding hi/~ khempeuh sangin a hoihzawk tuanlam uh a mu hi | he found them better than all the others) (s:adangte) (b:dangteng) (r:26.30.17/27.1.19) (q:draft)
Adar = (t:name) (w:Adar) (d:the twelfth month of the Hebrew calendar, in which the feast of Purim is kept) (e:~ kha a ni sawm-le-thum ni) (r:17.9.17/17.3.13) (q:draft)
Adbe = (t:see) <Adbe-el>
Adbe-el = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adbeel) (d:third son of Ishmael) (e:tua ciangin Kedar, ~, Mibsam) (r:1.25.13/13.1.29) (q:draft)
Adbeel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adbeel) (d:third son of Ishmael) (r:1.25.13)
Addan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Addon/Addan) (d:town in Babylonia from which exiles returned with Zerubbabel, Addon in the NIV) (e:Kherub, ~, leh Immer khuate panin) (r:15.2.59/16.7.61) (q:draft)
addar = (t:see) <Ataroth-addar>
Addar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Addar) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin) (e:Bela’ tapate in: ~, Gera, Abihud) (r:13.8.3) (q:draft)
Addar = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Addar) (d:town on the southern border of Judah) (e:Hezron dung tawnin ~ ciang dong paito-in) (r:6.15.3) (q:draft)
Addi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Addi) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke, father of Melki) (e:Melkhi in ~’ ta hi) (r:42.3.28) (q:draft)
Addon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Addon) (d:town in Babylonia from which exiles returned with Zerubbabel) (r:16.7.61) (q:draft)
adei = (t:n) (w:room/chamber) (d:dei, room, with the prefix a written joined; adei tungnung is apparently the upper court of the temple, where the room of Gemariah was) (e:~ tungnunga Shafan’ tapa thuvan pipa Gemariah’ inndei sungah | in the room of Gemariah son of Shaphan the secretary, in the upper court) (s:inndei) (b:dei) (r:24.36.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
adiah = (t:see) <Ma-adiah>
adiak = (t:adv) (w:especially/particularly) (d:diak, especially, with the prefix a written joined; used in adiak diakin, most especially, above all) (e:~ diakin thu-um innkuanpihte tungah/~ diakin thu-um innkuanpihte tungah nakpi-in bawl ni | let us do so most of all to the family of believers) (s:phadiak) (b:diak) (r:48.6.10) (q:draft)
Adiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adiel) (d:name of several men, among them a leader of Simeon, a priest, and the father of Azmaveth, the treasurer of David) (r:13.9.12/13.4.36)
adik = (t:adj) (w:right/just) (d:dik, right, with the prefix a written joined: that which is right; adik nate are things that are right) (e:zahtakhuai nate, ~ nate, a siangtho nate/~ nate, a siangtho nate, deihhuai nate | things that are right, pure and lovely) (s:thutang/aman) (a:akhial) (b:dik) (r:50.4.8) (q:draft)
Adin = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adin) (d:head of a family that returned from exile, and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.16/15.8.6) (q:draft)
Adina = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adina) (d:son of Shiza, a chief of the Reubenites and one of the mighty men of David) (r:13.11.42)
ading = (t:prep) (w:for) (d:placed after a noun or pronoun: for the benefit or use of, on behalf of) (e:Pasian ~ inn a lam hi/kote ~ thu hong ngetsak un | pray for us/amau ~ ciat la uh hi | each took for himself/Nipi ni mite ~ a piang hi | the Sabbath was made for people) (s:nading/dinga) (b:ding) (r:44.7.47/52.5.25/4.31.53/41.2.27) (q:draft)
Ading = (t:prep) (w:to/for) (d:ading, for, written with a capital in the quoted altar inscription, to an unknown god) (e:Kithei-lo Pasian ~ | to an unknown god) (b:ading) (r:44.17.23) (q:draft)
adinga = (t:prep) (w:for/for the sake of) (d:ading with the linking ending a, for or for the sake of, used before a following verb or noun phrase) (e:note’ ~ hong pai ahi hi/kei’ ~ ama bawlsate kong gen ding hi | I will tell what he has done for me/nangma ~ na hatsak mi’ tapa | the son of man you have made strong for yourself/amau ~ na sehnasa munah | at the place you assigned for them) (b:ading) (r:43.12.30/19.104.8/19.66.16/19.80.17) (q:draft)
adingin = (t:prep) (w:for) (d:ading, for, with the ending in: for the benefit or sake of the one named before it) (e:Mi gilote’ ~ nopsakna om lo hi/Topa in eite’ ~ na lianpite bawl khin ta | the Lord has done great things for us/Mittawte’ ~ mit ka hi a | I was eyes to the blind/keimah ~ pawi na bawl ding uh hi | you shall hold a festival for me) (b:ading) (r:23.57.21/25.3.25/19.126.3/18.29.15/2.23.14) (q:draft)
adingun = (t:prep) (w:for) (d:ading, for, with the plural ending un, used when a group is addressed) (e:na tapate’ ~ na la kei ding uh hi/a tanute uh na tapate’ ~ | their daughters for your sons) (b:ading) (r:5.7.3) (q:draft)
Adithaim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Adithaim) (d:town in the lowland of Judah) (r:6.15.36)
