Ahasu-eras = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Xerxes/Ahasuerus) (d:king of Persia in the book of Esther, and the father of Darius the Mede in Daniel; the NIV writes Xerxes, older English Bibles Ahasuerus) (e:Kumpipa ~ in a ukna gam) (r:17.10.1/27.9.1) (q:draft)
Ahasueras = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Xerxes/Ahasuerus) (d:king of Persia in the book of Esther, and the father of Darius the Mede in Daniel) (r:27.9.1/15.4.6)
ahau = (t:adj) (w:rich) (d:hau, rich, with the prefix a written joined: the rich; ahau azawng is rich and poor alike) (e:leibate, ~ azawng, a thuakna uh/~ azawng, a thuakna uh kibang ding hi | rich and poor, their lot will be the same) (s:sumhau/hausa) (a:azawng) (b:hau) (r:23.24.2) (q:draft)
Ahava = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ahava) (d:place in Babylonia and the canal named after it, where Ezra gathered the exiles before the journey to Jerusalem) (e:~ lui panin ka dingkhia uh hi) (r:15.8.31/15.8.15) (q:draft)
Ahaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahaz) (d:king of Judah, son of Jotham and father of Hezekiah) (e:Topa in ~ kiangah thu genkik a) (r:23.7.10/23.14.28) (q:draft)
Ahaziah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahaziah) (d:name of two kings, the son of Ahab who ruled Israel and the son of Jehoram who ruled Judah) (r:11.22.40/13.3.11)
Ahaziahte = (t:name) (w:Ahaziahte/Ahaziah) (d:Ahaziah with the plural ending te, Ahaziah and the kings named with him) (b:Ahaziah) (r:12.12.18)
Ahban = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahban) (d:son of Abishur and Abihail, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.29)
ahem = (t:adj) (w:maimed/deformed) (d:hem, deformed, with the prefix a written joined: one that is maimed; said of an animal unfit for offering) (e:a gamtang theilo, ~, meima nai a nei/Ganhing a mittaw, a gamtang theilo, ~ | an animal that is blind, injured or maimed) (s:bui) (b:hem) (r:3.22.22) (q:draft)
ahhong = (t:see) <teembaw-ahhong>
ahi = (t:ppm) (d:word indicating nominative case) (e:Pasian thu ~ hi/Sihna’ gu in mawhna ~ hi | the sting of death is sin/Dan’ tapa in Hushim ~ hi | the son of Dan is Hushim/Mihing Tapa in Nipi ni ukpa ~ hi | the Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath) (r:46.15.56/1.46.23/42.6.5)
Ahi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahi) (d:son of Abdiel, head of a family of the tribe of Gad) (e:Guni’ tapa Abdiel’ tapa ~ pen) (r:13.5.15) (q:draft)
AHI = (t:v) (w:is/be) (d:ahi, is, written in capital letters in an inscription or a name that is set in capitals) (e:NAZARETH KHUAMI ZEISU ~ HI/Topa IN EITE’ DIKTATNA ~ HI | the Lord is our righteousness) (r:43.19.19/24.23.6) (q:draft)
ahia = (t:part) (d:sentence final denoting interrogation or exclamation) (e:hih bang ~?)
Ahiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiah) (d:one of the leaders who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (e:~, Hanan, Anan) (r:16.10.26) (q:draft)
ahiam = (t:part) (d:sentence final denoting interrogation or exclamation) (e:hih kua ~?)
Ahiam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiam) (d:son of Sharar the Hararite, one of the mighty men of David) (r:10.23.33/13.11.35)
Ahian = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahian) (d:son of Shemida, of the tribe of Manasseh) (r:13.7.19)
Ahiezer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiezer) (d:son of Ammishaddai, leader of the tribe of Dan in the wilderness) (r:4.1.12/4.7.66)
ahih = (t:v) (w:happen/occur) (d:a with hih, the form of hi, be, used before ciangin, leh, manin and hangin: it being so, this having happened) (e:Tua bang ~ ciangin tua tuikulh-a cina dangte/Tua bang ~ leh, gupna kua in ngah zo ding | if that is so, who can be saved/numei tawh paktatna tamlua ~ manin | since there is so much sexual immorality/Tua ~ ciangin Gerar-ah Isaak teng hi | that being so, Isaac stayed in Gerar) (r:44.28.9/42.18.26/46.7.2/1.26.6)
ahih = (t:n) (w:task)
ahih hangin = (t:conj) (w:but) (d:ahih, being so, with hangin, although: although that is so; joins two statements that contrast) (e:~ Josef khiat mah bangin/~ Rachel mel hoih-in deihhuai hi | but Rachel was beautiful and lovely/~ nangma thu ka deih hi | but I love your law/~ i Pasian’ thu kho tawntung ding hi | but the word of our God will stand forever) (r:1.6.8/1.40.22/1.29.17/19.119.163/23.40.8)
ahih hangin = (t:conj) (w:even so/however/still) (e:~ mipa’ adinga a kilawm/~ a gil uh kiallai veve hi | but they are still hungry/~ a pua lam panin kimu thei lo hi | still they could not be seen from outside/~ a sisate a lawng peuhmah nin ding hi | however, whoever touches their carcasses will be unclean) (s:ahita) (r:1.2.20/23.9.20/14.5.9/3.11.36)
ahih hangin = (t:conj) (w:yet) (e:~ amau teci pan’na a kituak kei hi/~ a gualzo tawntung kei ding hi | yet he will not remain victorious/~ kuamah in ciam ngam vet lo uh hi | yet no one dared to taste it/~ keima deihna bang hi kei hen | yet not as I will) (s:hitaseleh) (r:41.14.59/27.11.12/9.14.26/41.14.36)
ahih hangin = (t:conj) (w:nevertheless/nonetheless) (e:~ Topa in kei hong huh hi/~ a tak takin, ka nun’tak lai teng | nevertheless, as surely as I live/~ kei hong sisak lo hi | nevertheless he has not let me die) (s:ahita) (r:19.118.13/4.14.21/19.118.18)
ahihciangin = (t:conj) (w:therefore/so) (d:ahih ciangin written as one word; tua ahihciangin is that being so, therefore) (e:tua ~ amaute ama' lamah kihei a/~ amaute ama' lamah kihei a, ama' innah lut | so they turned aside to him and entered his house) (r:1.19.3) (q:draft)
ahihkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to be/be the case) (d:a with hih, the form of hi, be, used before a suffix, and khak, happen to; ahihkhak leh is if it should be so) (e:Pasian thu um lo ~ leh/nangma ngaihsutna bang ~ leh | if it is your will) (s:hikha) (r:60.3.1/42.22.42) (q:draft)
ahihlam = (t:phrase) (w:that it is/that it was) (d:a hih lam written as one word, the fact of being so, mostly before thei, phawk or mu: know, realize or see that it is) (e:Jesuh ~ thei lo uh hi/mite in Jesuh ~ a theipah uh hi | the people recognized at once that it was Jesus/siampi lianpen pa ~ ka thei kei hi | I did not know that he was the high priest/pilna pen haina zawhna ~ ka mu hi | I saw that wisdom is better than folly) (r:42.24.16/41.6.54/44.23.5/21.2.13) (q:draft)
ahihleh = (t:conj) (w:if) (d:ahih, being so, with leh, if: if it is, if he is, after a noun or a clause) (e:Amah mizawng ~ ama hong khap puan/Ama biakna keel ~ | if his offering is a goat/Numei ~ shekel sawmthum hi ding hi | if a female, it shall be thirty shekels/a siang ~, tua nu suakta-in | if she is clean, the woman goes free) (s:hileh) (r:5.24.12/3.3.12/3.27.4/4.5.28)
ahihleh = (t:part) (d:particle comparison between verbs to delineate their relationship) (e:pai ~ lunggulh kei ing/Tikhikas ~ Efesa khua-ah ka paisak khin hi | as for Tychicus, I have sent him to Ephesus/Mary in ~ a lungsimah hih thute ciamtehin | but Mary kept these things in her heart/mipilte ~ a manin gamta uh hi | but the wise walk rightly/mihing ~ phatna tawh kize-et hi | but a person is tested by praise) (r:55.4.12/42.2.19/20.15.21/20.27.21)
ahihloh = (t:v) (w:not be) (d:hihloh, not being, with the prefix a written as one word; ahihleh ahihloh is whether it is so or not, and ahihloh hangin is although it is not) (e:ngeina ~ hangin kumpipa kiangah/ahihleh ~ bangmah ka thei kei hi | whether it is so or not, I do not know) (b:hihloh) (r:17.4.16/43.9.25) (q:draft)
ahihlohna = (t:n) (w:not being) (d:ahihloh, not being, with the noun suffix na: the fact that something is not so, used where English says that it is not) (e:ei’ pawl taktak ~ uh hong kilang hi/A mawk thuak ~ thei-in | knowing that he did not suffer in vain/sawltak ~ uh na muhkhiatnate uh | your finding out that they are not apostles/nang adingin bangmah ~ tuni-in na kitelsak hi | today you have made clear that they are nothing to you) (s:hihlohna) (b:ahihloh) (r:62.2.19/48.1.11/23.53.11/66.2.2/10.19.6) (q:draft)
ahihna = (t:n) (d:the fact that something is so; placed after a clause that is the object of a verb of knowing, seeing or showing, where English says that) (e:Saul hong pai taktak ~ thei hi/Nuihna in haina ~ | that laughter is madness/nangma khut in a sep ~ amaute thei sak in | let them know that your hand has done it/hih thute hong piang ding ~ phawk un | know that these things will happen) (b:ahih) (r:9.26.4/21.2.2/19.109.27/42.21.32) (q:draft)
ahihte = (t:n) (w:those who do/doers) (d:The verb hih, do, with the prefix a and the plural te: the people who do the thing named before it, as in mawhna ahihte, those who sin.) (e:gitlohna ~ khempeuh a kha tung/Tua bang ~ tungah Pasian’ thukhenna | God's judgment on those who do such things/mawhna ~ in Thukham bangin thukhenna a thuak ding | those who sin will be judged according to the law) (s:bawlte) (b:ahih) (r:45.2.9/45.2.2/45.2.12) (q:draft)
Ahihub = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahihud) (d:spelling of Ahihud in 1 Chronicles 8.7, a man of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.7)
Ahihud = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahihud) (d:name of two men: a leader of the tribe of Asher, son of Shelomi, who helped divide the land, and a man of Benjamin) (r:4.34.27/13.8.7)
Ahijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahijah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest in the time of Saul, the prophet of Shiloh, and one of David's warriors) (r:9.14.3/13.11.36)
Ahikam = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ahikam) (d:son of Shaphan, an official of King Josiah who protected Jeremiah, and father of Gedaliah) (r:24.26.24/24.40.6)
ahilh = (t:v) (w:teach/taught) (d:The verb hilh, teach, written together with the preceding a, the third person marker; it is usually written a hilh.) (e:thunget nading ~ mah bangin/amaute in a kiptakin ~ uh | they teach with confidence/~ tuak lo thu hilhin | teaching things that ought not to be taught) (s:thuhilh/sinsak) (b:hilh) (r:42.11.1/56.1.11/54.1.7) (q:draft)
Ahilud = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahilud) (d:father of Jehoshaphat, the recorder of David and Solomon) (r:10.8.16)
Ahima = (t:see) <Ahima-az>
Ahima-az = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimaaz) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zadok the priest, and a son-in-law of Solomon who was governor in Naphtali) (r:9.14.50/13.6.8) (q:draft)
Ahima-za = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimaaz) (d:spelling of Ahimaaz in 2 Samuel 18.22, the son of Zadok the priest who ran with news to David) (e:Zadok’ tapa ~ in Joab kiangah) (r:10.18.22) (q:draft)
Ahimaaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimaaz) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zadok the priest, and a son-in-law of Solomon who was governor in Naphtali) (r:13.6.8)
Ahiman = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiman) (d:name of two men: one of the three sons of Anak driven out of Hebron by Caleb, and a Levite gatekeeper) (r:6.15.14)
Ahimelek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimelek) (d:name of two priests: the priest at Nob who helped David and was killed by Saul, and a son of Abiathar) (r:10.8.17)
Ahimoth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimoth) (d:Levite of the line of Kohath, a son of Elkanah) (r:13.6.25)
Ahinadab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahinadab) (d:son of Iddo, one of Solomon's twelve district governors, at Mahanaim) (r:11.4.14)
ahing = (t:adj) (w:alive/living) (d:The word hing, alive, with the prefix a written as one word: who is alive, that lives; ahing tawntung is living or lasting for ever.) (e:tu ni-a ~ eite khempeuh tawh/~ tawntung nuntak tawntungna an | food that endures to eternal life) (s:anungta/nungta/hinglai) (a:sisa) (b:hing) (r:5.5.3/43.6.27) (q:draft)
Ahinoam = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Ahinoam) (d:name of two women: a wife of David from Jezreel, the mother of Amnon, and the wife of Saul) (r:9.25.43/10.3.2)
Ahio = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahio) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Abinadab who walked in front of the cart carrying the ark) (r:10.6.3)
ahipa = (t:n) (w:the one who is/he who is) (d:The verb ahi, is, with pa, the male one: it closes a describing phrase and is said of God, as in Pasian ahipa, the one who is God.) (e:amah bek Pasian ~ tungah/ama min Siangtho ~ in hih bangin ci | he whose name is holy says this/zahtak ding ~’ tungah | to the One who is to be feared) (s:hipa) (b:ahi) (r:19.136.4/23.57.15/19.76.11) (q:draft)
Ahira = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahira) (d:son of Enan, leader of the tribe of Naphtali in the wilderness) (r:4.1.15/4.10.27)
Ahiram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiram) (d:son of Benjamin, ancestor of the Ahiramite clan) (r:4.26.38)
Ahisamak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahisamach/Ahisamak) (d:man of the tribe of Dan, father of the craftsman Oholiab) (r:2.31.6)
Ahishar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahishar) (d:official in charge of Solomon's palace; in 1 Chronicles 7.10 the name stands for Ahishahar, a man of Benjamin) (r:11.4.6)
ahita = (t:conj) (w:nevertheless/even so) (d:The verb ahi, be, with ta; it is used in ahita zongin, which means even so or nevertheless.) (e:~ zongin gamdang numeite in amah) (s:ahih hangin) (b:ahi) (r:16.13.26) (q:draft)
ahite = (t:n) (w:those who are/the ones that are) (d:The verb ahi, be, with the plural te, turning the words before it into a noun: innkuan lutang ahite is those who are heads of families, kham ahite is the things that are of gold.) (e:Pasian’ ta ~ peuhmah in leitung nate/a beh sungah lutang ~ | those who were heads in their clan/kham ~ kham mahin la-in | he took what was of gold as gold/a sunglamah Jew mi ~ ahi hi | are those who are Jews inwardly) (s:hite) (b:ahi) (r:62.5.4/6.22.14/13.26.32/12.25.15/45.2.29) (q:draft)
Ahithofel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahithophel) (d:man of Giloh, David's counselor, who joined Absalom's revolt) (r:10.15.12/10.23.34)
Ahitub = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahitub) (d:name of several priests, among them the grandson of Eli who was the father of Ahimelek, and the father of Zadok) (r:9.14.3/13.6.7)
ahizo = (t:v) (w:be able to be/be possible) (d:The verb ahi, be, with zo, be able: ahizo nawn lo is no longer able to be, and ahizo zahzahin is as far as is possible.) (e:minam ~ nawn lo zah dongin/i Jew mipihte ~ zahzahin i tanhkik hi | we bought back our fellow Jews as far as possible) (s:hithei) (b:ahi) (r:23.7.8/16.5.8) (q:draft)
Ahlab = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ahlab) (d:town in the territory of Asher whose people were not driven out) (r:7.1.31)
Ahlai = (t:name) (w:Ahlai) (d:name of two people: a child of Sheshan in the line of Judah, and the parent of Zabad, one of David's warriors) (r:13.2.31/13.11.41)
Ahoah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahoah) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin, ancestor of the Ahohite clan) (r:13.8.4)
Ahoh = (t:name) (w:Ahoh/Ahohite) (d:ancestor named in Ahoh-te beh, the Ahohite clan of Benjamin, to which several of David's warriors belonged) (r:13.11.29/13.27.4)
ahoih = (t:adj) (w:good/what is good) (d:The word hoih, good, with the prefix a: that which is good, the good one; ahoih nate is good things, and ahoih ahoih lo is whether good or bad.) (e:~ nate na len tawntung un/thakiam loin ~ nate na gamta un | do what is good without growing tired/thuman leh thutang, ~ leh a kilawm | what is right and just, good and fitting/i gamtatna ~ ~ lo bangin | according to what we have done, good or bad) (s:apha/pha) (a:asia/hoihlo/gilo) (b:hoih) (r:52.5.21/47.5.10/53.3.13/20.2.9) (q:draft)
ahoihin = (t:adv) (w:well/rightly) (d:The word ahoih, what is good, with the suffix in: in a good way; ahoihin gamta is do what is right.) (e:~ gamta in) (s:phatakin) (a:sialamin) (b:ahoih) (r:45.13.3) (q:draft)
ahoihte = (t:n) (w:good ones/good things) (d:The word ahoih, that which is good, with the plural suffix te: the good ones; gamtatna ahoihte is good deeds.) (e:gamtatna ~ ah lungsim utna nei-in/gamtatna ~ ahih tawntung nading | so that they keep on doing good deeds/~ ahoih lo tawh ahi zongin | whether good ones for a bad one) (s:phate/hoihnate) (a:siatnate) (b:ahoih) (r:56.2.14/3.27.10/56.3.8) (q:draft)
ahoihzaw = (t:see) <ahoihzaw-in>
ahoihzaw-in = (t:adv) (w:better/even better/even more) (d:The word hoih, good, with the prefix a, zaw, more, and the suffix in: in a better way, even better than what is named before sangin.) (e:sangin zong ~ na hih ding) (r:57.1.21) (q:draft)
Ahserah = (t:name) (w:Asherah) (d:spelling of Asherah in 2 Kings 13.6, a Canaanite goddess and the wooden pole set up for her worship) (r:12.13.6)
ahsiampi = (t:see) <mai-ahsiampi>
Ahumai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahumai) (d:son of Jahath, of the Zorathite clans of Judah) (r:13.4.2)
ahun = (t:n) (w:the time/the hour/opportunity) (d:The word hun, time, with the prefix a: its time, the right time; ahun hong tung ding is the time will come, and ahun hunin is from time to time.) (e:Pa aw, ~ a tung zo hi/kong gen nading ~ hong tung ding hi | the time will come when I will tell you/~ na teel un | make good use of the time/~ dang-ate mah bangin | as at the other times) (b:hun) (r:43.17.1/43.16.25/49.5.16/7.20.30) (q:draft)
Ahuzzam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahuzzam) (d:son of Ashhur and Naarah, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.6)
Ahuzzath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahuzzath) (d:adviser of Abimelek king of Gerar, who came with him to Isaac) (r:1.26.26)
Ahzai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahzai) (d:priest, son of Meshillemoth and ancestor of Amashsai) (r:16.11.13)
ai = (t:n) (w:lot) (d:A lot cast to decide something; ai saan is to cast lots, and ai a pha is the one on which the lot falls.) (e:adingin ~ a pha keel paipihin/amau’ kongpi ding ~ saan uh hi | they cast lots for their gate) (s:aii/aai/aisaan) (r:3.16.9/19.22.18/13.26.13) (q:draft)
ai = (t:n) (w:divination/witchcraft) (d:Divination or witchcraft; ai saan is to practise divination, and ai saan thei is one who divines or casts spells.) (e:~ saan thei kong omsak nawn kei ding/~ a saan, khong a khai | who practises divination or sorcery/ahih kei leh ~ saanna na sem kei ding | nor shall you practise divination) (s:aisan) (r:33.5.12/5.18.10/3.19.26) (q:draft)
Ai = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ai) (d:Canaanite city east of Bethel, taken and burned by Joshua) (e:Beth-el leh ~ kikalah a buksim dingin) (r:6.8.12/6.8.23) (q:draft)
Ai-ath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aiath) (d:place in Benjamin on the route of the Assyrian army toward Jerusalem, probably the same as Ai) (e:~ khua hong tung uh a) (r:23.10.28) (q:draft)
Aiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aiah) (d:name of two men: a son of Zibeon the Horite, and the father of Rizpah, Saul's concubine) (r:13.1.40/10.21.11)
Aiath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aiath) (d:place in Benjamin on the route of the Assyrian army toward Jerusalem, probably the same as Ai) (r:23.10.28)
aii = (t:n) (w:lot) (d:A lot drawn or cast to decide a share, the same word as ai; aii sawk is to draw lots, and aii kia is the lot falls.) (e:leitang hawmna-ah ~ sawk thei ding uh/amaute tungah a ~ kia masa | the first lot fell to them) (s:ai/aai/aisaan) (r:26.47.22/6.21.10) (q:draft)
Aiialon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Aijalon) (d:spelling of Aijalon in Joshua 19.42, a town in the territory of Dan) (r:6.19.42)
Aija = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aija) (d:town of Benjamin near Bethel where people lived after the exile, probably the same as Ai) (e:Geba, Mikmash, ~, Bethel le a khuaneute) (r:16.11.31) (q:draft)
Aijalon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aijalon) (d:name of two places: a Levite town in the territory of Dan with a valley of the same name, and a town in Zebulun where Elon was buried) (r:7.12.12/13.6.69)
aikam = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (e:aktui ngen leh, ~ a pia ding) (s:momai/mom-ai) (r:42.11.12) (q:draft)
aikamte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpions) (e:gul gilote leh ~ na sikgawp nading uh) (s:momaite) (b:aikam) (r:42.10.19) (q:draft)
aikungte = (t:see) <zawl-aikungte>
Ain = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ain) (d:town in the south of Judah, given to Simeon; also a place on the eastern border of Canaan) (r:6.19.7/13.4.32)
Aineas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aeneas) (d:paralysed man at Lydda who was healed by Peter) (r:44.9.33/44.9.34)
Ainon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Aenon) (d:place near Salim with much water, where John baptized) (r:43.3.23)
aisaan = (t:n) (w:lot/allotment) (d:The lot that is cast to decide something, and the share that falls to someone by it; aisaan sagihna is the seventh lot.) (e:Dan minam adingin ~ sagihna hong tung hi/Asher minam’ adingin ~ ngana hong tung | the fifth lot came out for the tribe of Asher/Kohath behte adingin ~ hong tung hi | the lot came out for the Kohathite clans) (s:ai/aii/aai) (r:6.19.40/6.19.24/6.21.4) (q:draft)
aisaan = (t:v) (w:cast lots/divine) (d:To decide or find out something by casting lots; lai aisaan-in is by casting lots, and aisaan man is the fee for divination.) (e:nasep ding uh ~ uh hi/lai ~-in a puante a hawm uh hi | they divided his clothes by casting lots/Midian upate ~ man ding tawh kuan khia | the elders of Midian left with the fee for divination) (r:13.25.8/4.22.7/41.15.24) (q:draft)
aisaana = (t:n) (w:casting of lots/lot) (d:A spelling of aisaanna, the casting of lots, built on aisaan; aisaana tawh is by lot.) (e:~ tawh na luah ding uh leitang/~ tawh Manasseh minam a langte’ gam sung panin | by lot from the land of the half-tribe of Manasseh) (s:aisaanna) (b:aisaan) (r:4.34.13/13.6.61) (q:draft)
aisaanin = (t:v) (w:casting lots/by casting lots) (d:The verb aisaan, cast lots, with the suffix in: by casting lots; lai aisaanin has the same meaning.) (e:lai ~ a puante a hawm uh a) (b:aisaan) (r:40.27.35) (q:draft)
aisaanna = (t:n) (w:casting of lots/lot) (d:The verb aisaan, cast lots, with the noun suffix na: deciding or sharing out something by lot; aisaanna tawh is by lot.) (e:leitang pen ~ tawh kihawm ding hi/tua khua a sim dingin ~ tawh i pai ding | we will go by lot to attack that town/a kibangin ~ tawh amaute koih uh hi | they assigned them alike by lot/~ tawh khuapi sawm-le-thum ngah uh hi | they received thirteen towns by lot) (s:aisaana) (b:aisaan) (r:4.26.55/13.24.7/7.20.9/13.24.5/6.21.4) (q:draft)
Aisaante = (t:name) (w:Aisaante) (d:the diviners, written with a capital in Aisaante’ Tawsaw, the diviners' tree near Shechem) (r:7.9.37)
aisan = (t:n) (w:divination/sorcery/secret arts) (d:Seeking hidden knowledge by lots, omens or magic; aisan siam, aisan thei and aisan mi are a diviner or sorcerer.) (e:mi pilte leh ~ siamte sam hi/lehdona in ~ mawhna bangmah hi | rebellion is like the sin of divination/~ theite in zong amau laibute hong paipih | those who practised sorcery also brought their books/na kamsangte uh leh na ~ theite uh | your prophets and your diviners) (s:ai/mitphial/khongkhai) (b:ai) (r:2.7.11/27.2.27/9.15.23/44.19.19/24.29.8) (q:draft)
aisanin = (t:adv) (w:by divination/by fortune-telling) (d:The word aisan, divination, with the suffix in: by means of divination or fortune-telling.) (e:~ ama tote ading summeet ngah thei/Ka mite in ~ sing them peuh thu dotin | my people consult a piece of wood by divination) (b:aisan) (r:44.16.16/28.4.12) (q:draft)
aisanna = (t:n) (w:necromancer/divination/casting of lots) (d:aisan with the noun suffix na: the practice of divination; aisanna tawh is by lot) (e:vankahna leh ~ zang uh a | they practised spiritism and divination/~ tawh Benjamin minam kila hi | the tribe of Benjamin was taken by lot/amau’ gamhte ~ tawh kipia hi | their inheritances were given by lot) (b:aisan) (r:12.17.17/9.10.20/6.14.2)
aisannate = (t:n) (w:sorceries/witchcraft) (d:Acts of sorcery or divination, aisanna with the plural te.) (e:na mibumna leh na ~ ah/Jezebel’ paktatnate leh ~ tua zahin a tam | the idolatries and witchcraft of Jezebel are so many) (s:bumnate) (b:aisanna) (r:23.47.12/12.9.22) (q:draft)
aisannu = (t:n) (w:sorceress/witch) (d:The word aisan, divination or sorcery, with nu marking a woman: a woman who practises sorcery.) (e:Numei ~ na hing khawi kei ding uh hi) (b:aisan) (r:2.22.18) (q:draft)
aisanpa = (t:n) (w:diviner/soothsayer) (d:The word aisan, divination, with pa marking a man: a man who practises divination.) (e:Beor’ tapa, ~ Balaam zong/kamsangpa, ~ leh upa-pa | the prophet, the diviner and the elder) (b:aisan) (r:6.13.22/23.3.2) (q:draft)
aisante = (t:n) (w:diviners/spiritists/sorcerers) (d:The word aisan, divination, with the plural te: those who practise divination or magic, often named together with vankahte, mediums.) (e:vankahte leh ~ a gamsung panin beisak hi/siampite leh ~ sam uh a | they called the priests and the diviners/~ pen mihai a suaksakpa | who makes fools of diviners/vankahtheite leh ~ tawh nasem hi | he consulted mediums and spiritists) (s:saante/khongkhaite) (b:aisan) (r:9.28.3/23.44.25/9.6.2/12.21.6) (q:draft)
Aisante = (t:n) (w:diviners) (d:The word aisante, diviners, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a place name, as in the diviners' tree.) (e:~’ Tawsaw lam panin pawlkhat hong pai | a company is coming from the direction of the diviners' tree/~’ thu ngai kei un | do not listen to the diviners) (b:aisante) (r:7.9.37/23.8.20) (q:draft)
aitawi = (t:n) (w:exorcist/sorcerer) (d:The word ai, divination or charm, with tawi, hold: one who practises spirit arts; in Acts 19.13 it is said of Jews who went about driving out evil spirits.) (e:Jew mi ~ pawlkhat in zong) (r:44.19.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
aite = (t:n) (w:charms/amulets/magic charms) (d:Plural of ai: objects worn or tied on for magic or divination.) (e:paknamtui bungte leh a kivom ~/na zat uh na ~ uh ka deih kei hi | I am against the charms that you use/a khip ding uh ~ na bawl uh a | you make charms for them to tie on) (b:ai) (r:23.3.20/26.13.20/26.13.18) (q:draft)
aituam = (t:adj) (w:own/personal/private) (d:It follows a possessor and stresses that the thing belongs to that person alone: ama aituam is his own, and ama aituam dingin is for himself.) (e:ama ~ dingin sakolte tampi/keima ~ leenggui lo khat ka nei hi | I have a vineyard of my own/amau’ ~ vai bek lunghimawh uh hi | they care only about their own affairs/ama ~ innah teeng hi | he lived in his own house) (r:5.17.16/22.8.12/50.2.21/7.8.29) (q:draft)
ak = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:rooster/chicken/fowl) (d:The domestic fowl; in the verses it is the rooster that crows, as in ak a khuang, the rooster crows.) (e:khit phetin ~ a khuang pah hi/tuzan ~ a khuan ma-in | tonight before the rooster crows/~ khuan’ laitak ahi zongin | or when the rooster crows) (s:aak/aklui) (r:40.26.74/40.26.34/41.13.35) (q:draft)
ak = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:raven/crow) (d:The second part of va-ak, raven or crow.) (e:va-~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.15/19.147.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
akah = (t:see) <Ma-akah>
akahte = (t:see) <Ma-akahte>
akan = (t:see) <Ja-akan>
Akan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Akan) (d:son of Ezer, a Horite of the land of Seir) (r:1.36.27)
akath = (t:see) <Ma-akath>
Akbor = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Achbor/Akbor) (d:name of two men: the father of Baal-Hanan king of Edom, and an official of Judah, the father of Elnathan) (r:1.36.38/13.1.49)
Akeldama = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Akeldama) (d:field near Jerusalem bought with the money of Judas; the name means Field of Blood) (r:44.1.19)
aketh = (t:see) <Ma-aketh>
Akhaia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Achaia) (d:Roman province in the south of Greece, with Corinth as its chief city) (r:44.18.12/52.1.7)
Akhaikas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Achaicus) (d:Christian from Corinth who visited Paul together with Stephanas and Fortunatus) (r:46.16.17)
Akhan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Achan) (d:man of the tribe of Judah, son of Karmi, who took devoted things from Jericho and was stoned) (r:6.7.20/6.7.24)
akhang = (t:n) (w:increase/profit) (d:The word khang, increase, with the prefix a written joined; ameet akhang is interest and profit taken on a loan.) (e:ama tung panin ameet ~ la kei un la) (s:meet/met) (a:supna) (b:khang) (r:3.25.36) (q:draft)
Akhar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Achar) (d:name given to Achan in 1 Chronicles 2.7, the man who brought trouble on Israel) (e:Israel a nawngkaisak ~ ahi hi) (r:13.2.7) (q:draft)
akhial = (t:adj) (w:wrong/in the wrong) (d:The word khial, wrong, with the prefix a written joined: that which is wrong; akhial min pua is apparently to accept being called wrong, to take a rebuke.) (e:~ min pua nuam lo hi) (a:adik/amaan) (b:khial) (r:20.13.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhiatna = (t:n) (w:meaning/explanation) (d:The word khiatna, meaning, with the prefix a, its, written as one word: the meaning or explanation of it.) (e:~ a thei kei ding uh hi/na ~ taktak theithei uh hi | they know the true meaning of things) (s:cihnopna/hilhtelna/gentelna) (b:khiatna) (r:40.13.13/21.8.1) (q:draft)
Akhim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Akim) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Matthew, son of Zadok and father of Elihud) (r:40.1.14)
Akhish = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Achish) (d:Philistine king of Gath with whom David took refuge from Saul) (e:Gath kumpipa ~ kiangah pai hi) (r:9.21.10/9.27.6) (q:draft)
Akhor = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Achor) (d:valley near Jericho where Achan was stoned; the name means trouble) (r:6.7.24/23.65.10)
akhuapi = (t:n) (w:city) (d:The word khuapi, city, with the prefix a written joined: the city.) (e:amaute in ~ bawl uh tawp uh hi) (b:khuapi) (r:1.11.8) (q:draft)
akibawl = (t:v) (w:be made) (d:The verb kibawl, be made, with the prefix a written joined: that which is made; sumngo tawh akibawl is made of bronze.) (e:a ngakna sumngo tawh ~ khat zong bawl in) (b:kibawl) (r:2.30.18) (q:draft)
akici = (t:v) (w:be called/so-called) (d:The verb kici, be called, with the prefix a written joined: that is called, so-called; pasian akici are those that are called gods.) (e:leitungah pasian ~ a tampi a om uh hangin) (b:kici) (r:46.8.5) (q:draft)
akihisak = (t:adj) (w:proud/arrogant/haughty) (d:Proud or arrogant, from kihisak, be proud, with the prefix a written joined; akihisak mite are the proud.) (e:Topa in ~ mite mudah a) (a:lungsimniam) (b:kihisak) (r:20.16.5) (q:draft)
akilawm = (t:adj) (w:fitting/proper/deserving/reasonable) (d:Fitting, proper or deserved, from kilawm with the prefix a written as one word; sihna thuak ding akilawm is deserving of death, and akilawm kei hi is it is not reasonable.) (e:Na khempeuh ~ akituakin na hih un/sihna thuak ding ~ mawhna | an offence deserving death/paisak leng ~ kei hi | it is not reasonable to send him/a om mite mai-ah ~ gamta-in | behaving properly before outsiders) (b:kilawm) (r:46.14.40/44.25.25/44.25.27/52.4.11) (q:draft)
akiman = (t:see) <akiman'na>
akiman'na = (t:n) (w:use/worth/benefit) (d:kiman, be of use, with the prefix a and the noun suffix na; bangmah akiman’na om lo is there is nothing of worth in it) (e:kei adingin bangmah ~ om lo hi) (s:kimanna/phattuamna) (r:21.2.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
akipan = (t:prep) (w:from/since/beginning with) (d:marks the starting point in time, place or a list, often after pan; amah akipan a innkuanpihte means him and all his household) (e:ka neu lai ~ ka tang zo/a cil pan ~ kei tawh omkhawm | being with me from the beginning/ka zak uh ni pan ~ | since the day we heard/Samuel pan ~ Pasian’ kamsangte khempeuh | all the prophets of God beginning with Samuel/inn kong lut khit phet ~ | from the moment I entered the house) (s:panin/pan) (a:dong/dongin) (b:kipan) (r:41.10.20/43.15.27/51.1.9/44.3.24/42.7.45) (q:draft)
akipanin = (t:prep) (w:from/since/beginning with) (d:a kipanin written as one word; follows the time or thing that is the starting point) (e:tua hun ~ naupang a dam hi/Tua ~ tua nungzuipa in | from that time on that disciple/Lei piancil ~ kuamah in | since the world began no one/A naupa leh a thumna ~ | beginning with the second and the third) (s:panin/pan) (a:dong/dongin) (b:akipan) (r:40.17.18/43.9.32/43.19.27/42.20.30) (q:draft)
akipat = (t:adj) (w:first/beginning) (d:kipat, begin, with the prefix a written joined; akipat ni is the first day) (e:~ ni-a kipan abei ni dong) (s:masapen) (a:abei) (b:kipat) (r:16.8.18) (q:draft)
akipawl = (t:v) (w:be joined with/be associated with/go with) (d:kipawl, associate, with the prefix a written as one word, placed after tawh and before a noun: that is joined with, that goes with) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh ~ lungdamna tawh/mawhna tawh ~ i lungsim | our mind that goes with sin) (b:kipawl) (r:52.1.6/45.7.5) (q:draft)
akisa = (t:v) (w:be about to/be ready) (d:Be about to do something, from kisa, get ready, with the prefix a written joined; thu dong dinga akisa mite are those who were about to question him.) (e:thu dong dinga ~ mite in Paul) (r:44.22.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisak = (t:v) (w:prepare/get ready/be about to) (d:the prefix a written together with kisak, a form of kisa get ready; pai dinga akisak lai takin, just as he was getting ready to go) (e:pai dinga ~ lai takin) (b:kisak) (r:44.20.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisim = (t:v) (w:be counted/be numbered) (d:Be counted, from kisim with the prefix a written as one word; misimna-a akisim are those who are counted in the census.) (e:Misimna-a ~, kum sawmnih panin | those counted in the census, from twenty years old) (b:kisim) (r:2.30.14) (q:draft)
akituakin = (t:adv) (w:fittingly/properly/in an orderly way) (d:kituakin, fittingly, with the prefix a written as one word; paired with akilawm as akilawm akituakin, in a fitting and proper way) (e:Na khempeuh akilawm ~ na hih un/Lungdamna Thu tawh akilawm ~ gamtat ding | to behave in a way worthy of the gospel) (s:kilawmin) (b:kituakin) (r:46.14.40/50.1.27) (q:draft)
