anlumte = (t:n) (w:loaves/bread) (d:anlum, loaf of bread, with the plural suffix te) (e:hih ~ pen siampite bek in/A ~ balnen a | he broke the loaves/Pasian biakna-a a kipia ~ a ne uh hi | they ate the bread offered to God) (s:mohte/khomunte) (b:anlum) (r:41.2.26/41.6.41) (q:draft)
Anna = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Anna) (d:prophetess, daughter of Penuel, of the tribe of Asher, who saw the child Jesus in the temple) (e:Fanuel’ tanu ~ minnei kamsang numei khat) (r:42.2.36) (q:draft)
Annas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Annas) (d:high priest, father-in-law of Caiaphas, to whom Jesus was taken first after his arrest) (r:43.18.24/42.3.2) (q:draft)
anne = (t:v) (w:eat/have a meal) (d:an, food, with ne, eat: eat a meal; anne tuidawn is eat and drink) (e:tua nu in ~ dingin amah sam hi/~-in tuidawn in | eat and drink/~ tuidawn, nuamsa-in om in | eat, drink and be merry/amaute in ~ tuidawnin lungdam uh hi | they ate and drank and were happy) (s:ne) (r:12.4.8/42.12.19/11.18.41/11.4.20) (q:draft)
anneek = (t:n) (w:eating/meal) (d:an, food, with neek, a form of ne, eat: the eating of food; anneek tuidawn, eating and drinking, and anneek sabuai, a table for meals) (e:note in ~ tuidawn akipan na khempeuh) (s:annekna/nekna) (r:46.10.31/44.6.2) (q:draft)
annek = (t:v) (w:eat) (d:an, food, with nek, the form of ne, eat, used before other words: the eating of food, and so what is eaten; annek ding is food to eat and annek tuidawn is food and drink) (e:~ sim, lim diak hi/~ ding tampi hong pia hi | he gives food to eat in plenty/khuisatna in ka ~ suak a | sighing has become my food/~ tuidawn kitasam lo ding uh hi | they will not lack food and drink) (r:20.9.17/18.36.31/18.3.24/23.51.14) of food, edible
annekna = (t:n) (w:eating/meal/feast) (d:annek, eat food, with the noun suffix na: the eating of a meal; annekna sabuai is the table for a meal and annekna mun a banquet hall) (e:ka ~, ka tuidawnna in ka u/khut sil loin ~ in mi ninsak lo hi | eating with unwashed hands does not defile a person/a ~ sabuai panin Jesuh dingkhia-in | Jesus got up from the meal table/~ ding sabuai a bawl hi | she has set her table for the meal) (s:nekna/anneek) (b:annek) (r:46.8.13/17.7.8/40.15.20/43.13.4/20.9.2) (q:draft)
annektawm = (t:n) (w:food/provisions) (d:what is eaten at a meal, from annek eating of food; the part tawm is not clear) (e:innsung ~ dinga kibawl bawngtal khat) (s:nektawm) (r:16.5.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
annekte = (t:n) (w:food/meals) (d:annek, eating of food, with the plural te: things that are eaten, food) (e:a dahte’ ~ pawl zong na ne kei/~ un zong a ne teng hong ninsak ding hi | your food will make all who eat it unclean) (s:nekte) (b:annek) (r:26.24.17/28.9.4) (q:draft)
annel = (t:n) (w:flour/fine flour) (d:an, grain, with nel, fine: finely ground grain, the flour used for bread and for grain offerings) (e:sathau tawh a kibawl ~ hi ding hi/beel sunga ~ bei lo a | the flour in the jar was not used up/~ lawh sawmthum | thirty measures of fine flour/Nangmah in ~ la in la | take fine flour) (s:nel/buhnel/buhneel) (r:3.2.7/11.4.22/11.17.16/3.24.5)
annelte = (t:n) (w:flour/fine flour) (d:annel, flour, with the plural te, in a list of goods) (e:a ~ le mangbuhte, a bawngte/~, leenggahzute, sathaute | the flour, the wine and the oil) (b:annel) (r:66.18.13/13.9.29) (q:draft)
anneng = (t:n) (w:crumbs/scraps) (d:an, food, with neng, small bits; bits of food that fall from the table) (e:uite in tate ~ kiate sabuai nuai-ah/a topa sabuai panin ~ kiate a ne uh hi | they eat the crumbs that fall from their master’s table/ka sabuai nuai-ah ~ kia tawm ngei uh hi | they used to pick up scraps under my table) (s:nengkia) (r:41.7.28/40.15.27/7.1.7) (q:draft)
annengte = (t:n) (w:crumbs) (d:anneng, a crumb of food, with the plural te) (e:sabuai tung panin a kia ~/a kia ~ nenuamin a ngak hi | he waited, longing to eat the crumbs that fell) (b:anneng) (r:40.15.27/42.16.21) (q:draft)
anngawlin = (t:v) (w:starve/go without food) (d:an, food, with ngawl, be without, and the linking suffix in: going without food; anngawlin puk si is starve to death) (e:~ a puk si ding hi) (r:24.38.9) (q:draft)
anngen = (t:v) (w:beg for food/ask for bread) (d:an, food, with ngen, ask: ask or beg for food) (e:naupang note ~ dingin vaksak uh a) (r:25.4.4) (q:draft)
anote = (t:n) (w:its young/its cubs) (d:the prefix a written together with no young and the plural te; Vompi leh anote, the Bear with its cubs, a constellation) (e:Vompi leh ~) (b:note) (r:18.38.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
anoth = (t:see) <Beth-anoth>
anpal = (t:n) (w:firstfruits/first grain) (d:an, grain, with pal, first to ripen: the first of the grain harvest, given as an offering; anpal ni is the day of firstfruits) (e:~ tawh na biakna dingin/Na ~, na leenggahzu leh na sathau | the firstfruits of your grain, your wine and your oil/~ ni-in a siangtho kikhopna khat | a sacred assembly on the day of firstfruits/~ tawh biak nading ka vaihawmsak hi | I made provision for the offering of firstfruits) (r:3.2.14/5.18.4/4.28.26/16.13.31) (q:draft)
anpalin = (t:n) (w:firstfruits) (d:anpal, firstfruits, with the suffix in: as firstfruits) (e:Topa’ tungah ~ a kipia hi ding hi) (b:anpal) (r:3.23.17) (q:draft)
anpalte = (t:n) (w:firstfruits) (d:anpal, firstfruits, with the plural te: the first of the crops, brought to the Lord) (e:na ~ tawh Topa zahtak in/I leitang panin a piang ~ | the firstfruits that our land produces/na ~ uh lakah a tung masa pen | the very first of your firstfruits) (s:palte) (b:anpal) (r:20.3.9/2.23.19/16.10.35) (q:draft)
anphalte = (t:n) (w:sheaves) (d:bundles of cut grain brought to the threshing floor; plural with te) (e:ancilna phualah ~ kaihkhop bangin) (s:anlomte/buhlomte) (r:33.4.12) (q:draft)
anphual = (t:n) (w:grain pile/heap of grain) (d:an, grain, with phual, place: the heap of grain at the threshing floor) (e:~ nawl-ah lum dingin pai hi) (r:8.3.7) (q:draft)
anphualte = (t:n) (w:shocks/stacks of grain/grain piles) (d:anphual, a pile of grain, with the plural te: stacked sheaves of cut grain in the field) (e:~ leh ankung ding laite) (b:anphual) (r:7.15.5) (q:draft)
anpia = (t:see) <anpia-in>
anpia-in = (t:v) (w:serve food/wait at table) (d:an, food, with pia, give, and the linking suffix in: giving out food, waiting at table) (e:Martha pen ~ a manlah hi/note lakah ~ na a sempa bangin | among you like one who works serving food) (r:43.12.2/42.22.27) (q:draft)
anpiak = (t:n) (w:serving of food) (d:an, food, with piak, the form of pia, give, used before other words: the serving of food; anpiak nasep is the office of the one who serves the king his food and drink) (e:~ nasep-ah koih kik a) (r:1.40.21) (q:draft)
anpiakna = (t:n) (w:provision of food/food supply) (d:anpiak, giving of food, with the noun suffix na: the food that is supplied) (e:ka mite a’ ding ~ tawh) (b:anpiak) (r:11.5.9) (q:draft)
anpiang = (t:n) (w:produce/crop/harvest) (d:an, grain, with piang, come forth: what the fields yield) (e:~ sawm-ah-khat khempeuh) (r:5.14.28) (q:draft)
anpiangte = (t:n) (w:crops/produce/grain) (d:anpiang, produce, with the plural te: the crops that the fields yield) (e:Lo a na ~ hong kaihkhop sakin) (s:piangte) (b:anpiang) (r:18.39.12) (q:draft)
anpiapa = (t:n) (w:cupbearer/butler) (d:the man who serves food and drink to the king: an, food, and pia, give, with pa marking a man) (e:Kei pen kumpipa’ ~ ka hi hi) (r:16.2.1) (q:draft)
anpiate = (t:n) (w:cupbearers/servers) (d:those who serve food and drink at table: an, food, and pia, give, with the plural te; the NIV has cupbearers) (e:a ~ leh a puansilhte) (r:14.9.4) (q:draft)
ansaalte = (t:n) (w:barns/granaries) (d:ansaal, also written ansal, barn, with the plural te) (e:na ~ an tawh kidim ding a) (s:ansalte/saalte) (r:20.3.10) (q:draft)
Ansai = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ansai/Three Taverns) (d:first part of the place name Ansai Thumna, the Three Taverns, a stopping place on the road to Rome where believers came to meet Paul) (r:44.28.15)
ansal = (t:n) (w:barn/granary/storehouse) (d:building where threshed grain is stored) (e:~ khempeuh kisia khin ta hi/a takteng ~ sungah koihin | putting the good grain into the barn/a ~ uh honsak un | break open their granaries) (s:saal) (r:29.1.17/5.28.8/42.3.17/24.50.26) (q:draft)
ansalte = (t:n) (w:barns/granaries/storehouses) (d:buildings where grain is stored, ansal with the plural te) (e:na ~ an tawh kidim ding a/a lianzaw ~ ka lam ding a | I will build bigger barns/~ khempeuh a vekin kisia khinta hi | all the barns are completely ruined) (s:ansaalte/saalte) (b:ansal) (r:20.3.10/42.12.18/29.1.17) (q:draft)
ansang = (t:n) (w:gleanings/leftover grain) (d:ears of grain left in the field after the reapers; ansang tawm means to glean) (e:~ tawm dingin pai kei in/nitak dong lo sungah ~ tawm hi | she gleaned in the field until evening/Refaim Kuam sunga ~ a kaihkhop khit ciangin | after one has gathered the gleanings in the Valley of Rephaim) (s:sangh) (r:8.2.8/23.17.5/8.2.17) (q:draft)
ansangh = (t:n) (w:gleanings/leftover grain) (d:spelling of ansang with a final h: ears of grain left behind the reapers; ansangh tawm, glean) (e:mangbuhham lak khit dong ~ tawm hi/~ hong tawm sakin an late nungah | let me glean behind the harvesters) (s:sangh) (b:ansang) (r:8.2.23/8.2.7) (q:draft)
ansanghte = (t:n) (w:gleanings/leftover grain) (d:ears of grain left in the field after the reapers, with the plural te; ansanghte tawm, glean) (e:nung lo sungah ~ tawm hi) (s:sanghte) (b:ansangh) (r:8.2.3) (q:draft)
ansangte = (t:n) (w:gleanings/leftover grain) (d:ansang, ears of grain left in the field after the reapers, with the plural te; ansangte tawm, glean) (e:nung lo sungah ~ a tawm hi) (s:sanghte) (b:ansang) (r:8.2.3) (q:draft)
ansi = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:the light husks of grain that the wind blows away) (e:huih letkhiat ~ tawh kibang uh hi/huih mai-a ~ leng bangsak in | make them like chaff flying before the wind/mual neute pen ~ bangin | the hills like chaff) (s:anvai/buhsi/buhvai) (r:19.1.4/23.29.5/19.83.13/23.41.15) (q:draft)
ansing = (t:n) (w:fuel/firewood) (d:wood for cooking food, fuel: an, food, and sing, wood) (e:galhiamte ~ dingin khawm ding uh hi) (r:26.39.9) (q:draft)
ansite = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:ansi, chaff, the empty husks of grain, with the plural suffix te) (e:huih letkhiat ~ tawh kibangsak in/a ~ ahihleh a mit ngei lo mei sungah | but the chaff into unquenchable fire) (s:anvaite) (b:ansi) (r:19.35.5/40.3.12) (q:draft)
ansukna = (t:n) (w:grinding/pounding of grain) (d:an, grain, with suk, pound or crush, and na: the grinding of grain; ansukna ging, the sound of grinding) (e:~ gingte na zak theih phat nawn loh hun) (r:21.12.4) (q:draft)
antah = (t:n) (w:bait) (d:food set in a trap to draw an animal; thang antah is the bait of a snare) (e:Thang ~ om lopi-in/note a dingin thang ~ hi ding hi | will be a snare to you) (r:30.3.5/20.7.23/7.2.3) (q:draft)
antak = (t:n) (w:solid food) (d:food that must be chewed, an with tak, real or solid; set against nawi, milk, as the food of the mature) (e:Note in ~ nezo nai lo/Ahi zongin ~ i cih pen | but what is called solid food) (b:an) (r:46.3.2/58.5.12/58.5.14) (q:draft)
antan = (t:v) (w:fast) (d:go without food as a religious act; written with an apostrophe before ding and nading, and with na it forms the noun for fasting or a fast) (e:gam khempeuh ah ~’ ding thu zasak hi/~’ nading thu pia un la | give the order for a fast/Ahava lui-ah ~’ nading thu ka taangko hi | at the Ahava river I proclaimed a fast/a ~’ thaman uh a ngah khinta | they have received their reward for fasting) (r:14.20.3/41.9.29/29.2.15/15.8.21/40.6.16) (q:draft)
antang = (t:n) (w:grain/corn) (d:threshed grain kept as food; in everyday speech husked rice) (e:~ lei dingin Josef' kiangah/tuipi sehnel zahin ~ tampi khol hi | he stored up much grain, like the sand of the sea/a late uh ~ suan-in paikhia uh hi | they loaded their donkeys with grain and left/Izipt gam panin a puak uh ~ | the grain they had brought from Egypt) (s:buhtang/buh) (r:1.41.57/1.41.49/1.42.26/1.43.2) (q:draft)
antangin = (t:v) (w:fast) (d:an tang, abstain from food, written as one word with the linking ending in: fasting) (e:hih bang lel-a ~ na thungetna uh) (r:23.58.4) (q:draft)
antangte = (t:n) (w:grain) (d:antang, grain, with the plural te: stores of grain) (e:Faro’ ukna nuai-ah ~ kholin) (b:antang) (r:1.41.35) (q:draft)
antanna = (t:n) (w:fasting/fast) (d:going without food as a religious act) (e:Kei’ deih ~ hih bang pawl ahi hi/Thungetna le ~ tawh lobuang | except by prayer and fasting/Hih bang lelin ~ tawh na thungetna uh | your prayer with fasting like this/~ ding le thumna bawlna ding ngeinate | the customs of fasting and lamentation) (b:antan) (r:23.58.6/40.17.21/23.58.4/17.9.31) (q:draft)
antannate = (t:n) (w:fasts) (d:antanna fasting, a fast, with the plural te) (e:kha sawmna sunga ~ pen) (b:antanna) (r:38.8.19) (q:draft)
ante = (t:n) (w:crops/foods/produce) (d:an, food or grain, with the plural te: the crops of the fields, or kinds of food) (e:tua gama piang ~ na nek uh/amau’ lo ~ tangngol pia a | he gave the crops of their fields to the grasshopper/Ka khawhsa ~ midangte’ nek suak hen | may others eat the crops I have grown/lo-a ~ a susia gawp guahzu | a rain that destroys the crops in the field) (s:anpiangte) (b:an) (r:4.15.19/19.78.46/18.31.8/20.28.3) (q:draft)
anteh = (t:n) (w:vegetables/greens/herbs) (d:leafy plants eaten as food; anteh huan is a vegetable garden) (e:~ bek hong nesak in la/amaute ~ an a pia hi | he gave them vegetables as food/upna neute in ~ bek ne ngam uh hi | those weak in faith dare eat only vegetables/~ huan dingin ka neih theih nadingin | so that I may have it for a vegetable garden) (s:mehteh) (r:27.1.12/20.15.17/27.1.16/45.14.2/11.21.2) (q:draft)
antehna = (t:n) (w:grain measure/measure) (d:an, grain, and teh, measure, with the noun suffix na; antehna seu is the basket used to measure grain) (e:I ~ seu neuseekin sum tampi) (b:anteh) (r:30.8.5) (q:draft)
anthak = (t:n) (w:new crop/new grain) (d:the grain of the new harvest: an, grain, and thak, new; the opposite of anlui, old grain) (e:~ hong tun’ a kum kua mateng) (a:anlui) (r:3.25.22) (q:draft)
Anthak = (t:name) (w:Anthak/new crop) (d:anthak, the new crop, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (r:3.25.22)
