anthul = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:flax) (d:the plant whose fibres are made into linen; anthul kung is a flax stalk and anthul khau a flax cord) (e:a koihsa ~ kungte lakah amaute seel/~ kungte a pak laitak ahi hi | the flax was in bloom/mei in a kat ~ khau tawh kibang a | like a flax cord burned by fire) (r:2.9.31/6.2.6/7.15.14)
Anti = (t:part) (w:anti) (d:borrowed from English and used only before Khazih: Anti Khazih, the antichrist, one who opposes Christ) (e:tu-in ~ Khazih tampi a om uh hi/mi kheem mi leh ~ Khazih ahi hi | is the deceiver and the antichrist/Khazih’ gal ahi ~ Khazih hong piang ding | the antichrist, the enemy of Christ, will come/na zaksa uh ~ Khazih’ kha ahi hi | is the spirit of the antichrist that you have heard of) (r:62.2.18/62.2.22/63.1.7/62.4.3) (q:draft)
Antiok = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Antioch) (d:name of two cities: Antioch in Syria, where the disciples were first called Christians, and Antioch in Pisidia) (r:44.11.27/44.6.5)
Antipas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Antipas) (d:faithful witness of Christ who was put to death in Pergamum) (r:66.2.13)
Antipatris = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Antipatris) (d:city on the road from Jerusalem to Caesarea, where the soldiers brought Paul by night) (r:44.23.31)
anu = (t:n) (w:female) (d:nu, female, with the prefix a written as one word, said of an animal: a female one, the opposite of apa, a male one; tuuno anu, a ewe lamb) (e:kum khat a pha tuuno ~ khat/keelhonte sung panin ~ hita leh apa hita leh | from the flock, whether female or male) (a:apa) (b:nu) (r:3.14.10/3.3.6) (q:draft)
anuai = (t:see) <anuai-a>
anuai-a = (t:adj) (w:following/below) (d:literally that which is below: points to what comes next in the text; anuai-a bangin means as follows) (e:thu ~ bangin gelh uh hi/amaute in ~ min kigen khuapite pia uh a | they gave the following towns mentioned by name/A lai sung thu hih ~ bang ahi hi | the content of the letter is as follows/~ khuapite leh lonona gamte pia uh hi | they gave the following towns and pasturelands) (r:15.4.8/6.21.9/15.4.11/6.21.3) (q:draft)
anuai-ah = (t:adv) (w:under it/beneath it) (d:a nuai, its underside, with the place marker ah: under it) (e:Gamsate in ~ tawlnga uh a) (r:27.4.21) (q:draft)
