Anub = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Anub) (d:a son of Koz in the genealogy of Judah) (r:13.4.8)
anung = (t:adv) (w:afterwards/later) (d:the prefix a written together with nung, after; anung ciangin is afterwards, later on) (e:~ ciangin innkiu suang a piang hi) (s:nungciangin) (a:amasa) (b:nung) (r:42.20.17) (q:draft)
Anung = (t:adv) (w:afterward/later) (d:a nung, after it, written as one word with a capital at the start of a sentence or line; Anung ciangin is afterward, later on) (e:~ ciangin inn kiu suang a piang hi/~ ciangin hong piang ding thu khempeuh | all the things that will happen later) (s:nungciangin) (a:amasa) (b:anung) (r:60.2.7/43.16.13) (q:draft)
anungta = (t:adj) (w:living) (d:nungta, live, with the prefix a: that is alive, living) (e:~ lametna thu a om nading) (s:ahing) (b:nungta) (r:60.1.3)
anungta = (t:adj) (w:alive) (s:ahing/hing) (b:nungta)
Anungta = (t:adj) (w:living) (d:anungta written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ lametna thu a om nading) (b:anungta) (r:60.1.3) (q:draft)
anvaakna = (t:n) (w:upbringing/nurture) (d:anvaak, also written anvak, feed and rear, with the noun suffix na; anvaakna ngah, be brought up) (e:Gamaliel’ khe kiangah ~ ngahin) (r:44.22.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
anvai = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:the light husks of grain that the wind blows away) (e:huih in a letkhiat ~ tawh kibang/a tunga ~ them tu bang lel hi) (s:ansi/buhsi/buhvai) (r:19.1.4/18.41.28)
