asang = (t:adj) (w:high) (d:the prefix a written together with sang, high; asang belte, the highest ones, means the rulers) (e:~ belte tawh ahi zongin) (a:niam) (b:sang) (r:49.6.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
asangna = (t:see) <asangna-ah>
asangna-ah = (t:adv) (w:on high) (d:a sangna, the height or high place, with the place marker ah: on high, said of the Lord who is exalted for ever) (e:nang pen ~ a om tawntung) (s:sangah) (r:19.92.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
Asaph = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asaph) (d:Levite musician of the time of David; the Bible text spells the name Asaf)
Asarel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asarel) (d:son of Jehallelel, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.16)
asau = (t:n) (w:length) (d:the prefix a written together with sau, long; asau tehna is the measuring of length) (e:~ tehna, agik tehna) (s:dung/dunglam/saulam) (b:sau) (r:3.19.35) (q:draft)
asauna = (t:n) (w:size/length) (d:the prefix a written together with sauna, length: how long or tall a thing is, its size) (e:kherubte gel ~ leh a pian’ lim) (s:golna/dung) (b:sauna) (r:11.6.25) (q:draft)
aseiah = (t:see) <Ma-aseiah>
asem = (t:v) (w:serve/work) (d:the prefix a written together with sem, work; ama na asem means those who do his work, who serve him) (e:kumpipa in ama na ~ a innsung mang) (s:nasem) (b:sem) (r:17.1.10) (q:draft)
Asenath = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Asenath) (d:daughter of Potiphera priest of On, wife of Joseph and mother of Manasseh and Ephraim) (r:1.41.50/1.46.20)
ash = (t:see) <Ga-ash>
Ashahel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asahel) (d:brother of Joab, commander of the fourth monthly division of the army of David; a spelling of Asahel) (r:13.27.7)
Ashan = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Ashan) (d:town in the lowland of Judah, allotted to Simeon and given to the priests) (r:6.15.42/6.19.7)
Asharelah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asarelah) (d:son of Asaph, one of the temple musicians) (r:13.25.2)
Asharoth = (t:name) (w:Ashtoreths) (d:the Ashtoreths, images of the goddess Ashtoreth, worshipped together with the Baals) (r:7.2.13)
ashbea = (t:see) <Beth-ashbea>
Ashbel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashbel) (d:second son of Benjamin, ancestor of the Ashbelite clan) (r:1.46.21/13.8.1)
Ashdod = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Ashdod) (d:one of the five cities of the Philistines, near the coast, where the captured ark of God was taken) (r:38.9.6/6.15.46)
Ashel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asahel) (d:Levite sent by Jehoshaphat to teach in the towns of Judah; a spelling of Asahel) (r:14.17.8)
Asher = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asher) (d:son of Jacob and Zilpah, ancestor of the tribe of Asher; also the tribe and its territory) (r:1.30.13/4.26.46)
Ashera = (t:name) (w:Asherah) (d:Canaanite goddess; Ashera milimte are the Asherah poles, her wooden images) (e:~ milimte leh milim dangte satvui a) (r:14.34.7) (q:draft)
Asherah = (t:name) (w:Asherah) (d:Canaanite goddess; Asherah milimte are the Asherah poles, her wooden images) (r:2.34.13/33.5.14)
Asherahte = (t:name) (w:Asherah poles) (d:the name Asherah with the plural te: the Asherah poles, wooden images of the goddess) (b:Asherah) (r:14.24.18/14.33.19)
Asheroth = (t:name) (w:Asherahs) (d:the Asherahs, images of the goddess Asherah, a Hebrew plural; written Asheroth-te) (r:7.3.7)
Asherte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Asher/Asherites) (d:the people of the tribe of Asher) (b:Asher) (r:13.6.74)
ashgaz = (t:see) <Sha-ashgaz>
Ashhur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashhur) (d:man of the tribe of Judah, founder of Tekoa, who had two wives, Helah and Naarah) (r:13.4.5/13.2.24)
Ashima = (t:name) (w:Ashima) (d:god made and worshipped by the people of Hamath who were settled in Samaria) (r:12.17.30)
Ashimah = (t:name) (w:Ashimah) (d:false god of Samaria by which people swore; the NIV has the sin of Samaria) (r:30.8.14)
Ashkelon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashkelon) (d:Philistine city on the Mediterranean coast) (r:24.47.5/24.47.7)
Ashkenaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashkenaz) (d:son of Gomer and grandson of Japheth; also a kingdom called to fight against Babylon) (r:1.10.3)
Ashnah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ashnah) (d:name of two towns in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.33/6.15.43)
Ashod = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashdod) (d:Philistine city, Ashdod, whose people opposed the rebuilding of the walls of Jerusalem) (r:16.4.7)
Ashpenaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashpenaz) (d:chief of the court officials of King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon) (r:27.1.3/27.1.11)
Ashtaroth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashtaroth) (d:city in Bashan where King Og reigned, later given to the half-tribe of Manasseh) (r:6.13.12/6.13.31)
Ashtarothah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ashtaroth) (d:Ashtaroth with the place marker ah: in Ashtaroth, the city of King Og of Bashan) (b:Ashtaroth) (r:6.9.10)
Ashterath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashterath) (d:home town of Uzzia, one of David's mighty warriors, called the Ashterathite in the NIV) (r:13.11.44)
Ashteroth = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ashteroth-karnaim/Ashteroth Karnaim) (d:first part of Ashteroth-Karnaim, a place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Rephaites) (r:1.14.5)
Ashtoreth = (t:name) (w:Ashtoreth) (d:goddess of the Sidonians, whom Solomon worshipped and for whom he built a high place) (r:11.11.5/12.23.13)
Ashur = (t:name) (w:Ashur) (d:Assyria, the power named in the oracles of Balaam; also the Ashurites over whom Ish-Bosheth was made king) (r:4.24.22)
Ashurbanipal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashurbanipal) (d:king of Assyria who deported peoples and settled them in Samaria) (r:15.4.10)
Ashvath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashvath) (d:son of Japhlet, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.33)
asia = (t:adj) (w:evil/bad/wrong) (d:sia, bad, with the prefix a written as one word: that which is bad or evil, often paired with apha, good; asia-a gamta is to act wickedly) (e:~ gamtatna in khialhna lianpi ahi hi/~ leh apha a khen thei nai lo | not yet able to tell bad from good/~-a gamta teiteite si ding hi | those who keep doing evil will die/apha leh ~ thei hi | he knows good and evil) (s:gilo/hoihlo) (a:apha/ahoih) (b:sia) (r:20.14.22/20.11.19/5.1.39/1.3.22) (q:draft)
Asia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Asia) (d:the Roman province of Asia in the west of Asia Minor, usually written Asia gam) (e:~ gamah tawlkhat khawl lai hi) (r:44.19.22/44.2.9) (q:draft)
asiel = (t:see) <Ja-asiel>
Asiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asiel) (d:ancestor of Jehu, a clan leader of the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.35)
Asinkritas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asyncritus) (d:Christian in Rome greeted by Paul) (r:45.16.14)
Asiria = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Assyria) (d:the Assyrian empire, whose king threatened Jerusalem in the days of Hezekiah; also spelled <Assiria>) (r:12.18.30)
Askhelon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashkelon) (d:Philistine city taken by the tribe of Judah; also spelled <Ashkelon>) (r:7.1.18)
Asnah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asnah) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.50)
Aspatha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aspatha) (d:one of the ten sons of Haman killed by the Jews) (r:17.9.7)
Asriel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asriel) (d:descendant of Manasseh and ancestor of the Asrielite clan) (r:13.7.14/4.26.31)
asseiah = (t:see) <Ma-asseiah>
Asshur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashur) (d:son of Shem and ancestor of the Assyrians; also the land of Assyria as a trading partner of Tyre) (r:1.10.22)
Asshurim = (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Ashurites) (d:people descended from Dedan, a grandson of Abraham and Keturah) (r:1.25.3)
Assir = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Assir) (d:name of two Levites of the line of Kohath, a son of Korah and a son of Ebiasaph) (r:2.6.24/13.6.22) (q:draft)
Assiri = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ashur/Assyria) (d:Assyria, named as the direction in which the land of the descendants of Ishmael lay) (r:1.25.18) (q:draft)
Assiria = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Assyria) (d:empire on the upper Tigris with its capital at Nineveh, which conquered the northern kingdom of Israel) (e:~ gam) (r:1.10.11/1.2.14)
Assiriate = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Assyrians) (d:the people of Assyria) (b:Assiria) (r:24.2.36/23.14.25)
Assos = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Assos) (d:seaport in the Roman province of Asia where Paul rejoined his companions) (r:44.20.14/44.20.13)
Astaroth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashtaroth) (d:city in Bashan given to the Gershonite Levites; also spelled <Ashtaroth>) (r:13.6.71)
asu = (t:see) <Ja-asu>
asungkuate = (t:n) (w:internal organs/entrails/inner parts) (d:sungkuate, the inner organs of an animal, with the prefix a written together: its internal organs, named in the laws of offerings) (e:~ tunga a om a thau khempeuh) (b:sungkuate) (r:3.3.3) (q:draft)
asusia = (t:v) (w:destroy) (d:susia, destroy, with the prefix a written together; leitung asusia dingin is in order to destroy the earth) (e:leitung ~ dingin tuiciin a om) (s:siasak/siatsak) (b:susia) (r:1.9.11) (q:draft)
at = (t:v) (w:reap/harvest) (d:cut grain at harvest; buh at is to reap the grain, and at is set against vawh, sow) (e:Buh ~ ding tampi a om hi/khaici tuh lo, a ~ kei uh hi | they do not sow seed or reap/midang in a ~ hi | another reaps/a gah a ~ kik ding hi | he will reap its fruit in return/tawmkha a vawhte in tawmkha a ~ ding hi | those who sow little will reap little) (s:anla) (a:vawh/tuh) (r:40.9.37/42.12.24/43.4.37/48.6.7/47.9.6) (q:draft)
at = (t:v) (w:cut/circumcise) (d:cut with a blade; vun at, cut the skin, is the expression for circumcise, and at khia is cut off) (e:leh vun ~ lote a dik a sa/a tapa Isaak a vun ~ hi | he circumcised his son Isaac/Israel mite a nihveina vun ~ kik in | circumcise the Israelites a second time/Saul’ puanmong ~ khia ahih manin | because he had cut off the corner of the robe of Saul) (r:45.3.30/9.24.5/1.21.4/6.5.2) (q:draft)
at = (t:v) (w:write/write down/inscribe) (d:put something in writing, used beside gelh; with lai, writing, it forms lai-at, secretary) (e:laizial khat sungah ~ in/sawmgiat na ~ ding hi | you shall write eighty/tu-in sawmnga ~ meegmeeng in | now quickly write fifty) (s:gelh/laigelh) (r:23.30.8/42.16.7/42.16.6) (q:draft)
Atad = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Atad) (d:name attached to a threshing floor near the Jordan where Joseph mourned seven days for Jacob) (r:1.50.10)
atak = (t:adv) (w:truly/especially) (d:tak, true, with the prefix a written together; atak takin ci leeng, to speak truly, introduces a point that is especially true) (e:~ takin ci leeng) (s:taktakin) (b:tak) (r:61.2.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
atam = (t:n) (w:quantity/amount) (d:tam, many, with the prefix a written together: how much there is, quantity; atam tehna is the measuring of quantity) (e:agik tehna, ~ tehnate ah) (s:omzah) (b:tam) (r:3.19.35) (q:draft)
Atarah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Atarah) (d:second wife of Jerahmeel and mother of Onam) (r:13.2.26)
Ataroth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ataroth) (d:name of several towns, among them one built up by the Gadites east of the Jordan and one on the border of Ephraim) (r:4.32.34/4.32.3)
Ataroth-addar = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ataroth Addar) (d:town on the border between Ephraim and Benjamin, on the hill south of Lower Beth Horon) (e:mualtunga ~ khua-ah paisuk hi) (r:6.18.13/6.16.5) (q:draft)
Atarothaddar = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ataroth Addar) (d:town on the border between Ephraim and Benjamin; also written <Ataroth-addar>) (r:6.18.13/6.16.5)
atawntungin = (t:adv) (w:forever/for ever) (d:tawntungin, continually, with the prefix a written as one word: for all time, forever) (e:zanni, tuni, ~ kikheel loin a om hi/~ a uk ding hi | he will rule forever) (s:paisuak/ngitnget) (a:tawlkhat) (b:tawntungin) (r:58.13.8/27.6.26) (q:draft)
ate = (t:part) (d:the linking a with plural te after a word of place or time, those of or the ones at, as nuai-ate those below and nidang-ate those of former days) (e:ahun dang-~ mah bangin Gibeah lang khatah/a nuai-~ sangin neuzaw hi | are smaller than those below/nidang-~ mah bangin | as in former days/ama mai-~ lak hita leh | or among those before him) (r:7.20.30/39.3.4/26.42.5/12.18.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ater = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ater) (d:name of two men, the ancestor of a family that returned from the exile and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:15.2.16/16.10.17)
ath = (t:see) <Mefa-ath>
Athaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Athaiah) (d:son of Uzziah, a descendant of Judah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.11.4)
athaim = (t:see) <Kushan-rish-athaim>
athak = (t:adj) (w:new) (d:thak, new, with the prefix a, that which is new, the new one; paired with alui, the old) (e:kikheel a, ~ a piang zo hi/a gah alui leh ~ | fruits old and new/anvui ~ a van sungah hong pua hi | he brought new grain in his sack) (a:alui) (b:thak) (r:47.5.17/22.7.13/12.4.42) (q:draft)
Athak = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Athak) (d:a town in Judah to which David sent a share of the plunder) (e:Hormah, Borashan, ~) (r:9.30.30) (q:draft)
Athaliah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Athaliah) (d:queen of Judah, mother of King Ahaziah, who seized the throne; also the name of two men) (r:12.11.1)
Atharim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Atharim) (d:place in the Negev on the road by which Israel approached Canaan) (r:4.21.1)
athau = (t:n) (w:fat/its fat) (d:thau, fat, written together with a, its: the fat of an animal brought as an offering) (e:thunuam-a biakna sisan leh ~ a piapa in/amah in ~ a iik tawh paipih ding hi | he shall bring the fat with the breast) (s:sathau) (b:thau) (r:3.7.33/3.7.30) (q:draft)
Athen = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Athens) (d:chief city of Greece, where Paul spoke at the Areopagus) (r:44.18.1/44.17.22)
Athlai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Athlai) (d:descendant of Bebai who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.28)
atin = (t:v) (w:reaping/cutting) (d:at, reap or cut, with the linking ending in, used before a following verb; ki-atin is being cut or circumcised) (e:kum thumna ciangin khai tuhin ~/khaici tuhin, vawhin, buh ~ | sowing seed, planting, reaping grain/po lopa hing khempeuh ki-~ inn-ah kipua | all the green grass is cut and carried home/vun dawn a ki-~ Abraham kum sawmkua-le-kua pha hi | Abraham was ninety-nine when his foreskin was cut) (a:tuhin/vawhin) (b:at) (r:12.19.29/40.6.26/20.27.25/1.17.24) (q:draft)
atkeh = (t:see) <ki-atkeh>
atkhia = (t:v) (w:cut off/cut away) (d:at, cut, with khia, out or off: cut a part off or away) (e:a selte ~ ding a/temta neu khat tawh ~ a | he cut it off with a small knife/siambu panin kei hong ~ hi | he has cut me off from the loom/Topa in ~ ta hen | may the Lord cut them off) (s:attan/satkhia/tan) (b:at) (r:23.18.5/19.12.3/24.36.23/23.38.12) (q:draft)
atkhiat = (t:v) (w:cut off) (d:at, cut, with khiat, off or away; the form of atkhia used before sak, manin and similar words) (e:Saul’ puanmong a ~ manin/a tapa’ vun dawn ~ sakin | cutting off the foreskin of her son/a kawng ciangah ~ sakin amaute a sawlkhia hi | he cut them off at the hips and sent them away) (b:atkhia) (r:9.24.5/2.4.25/10.10.4) (q:draft)
atkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:cut off) (d:at, cut, and khiat, off, with sak: cut a part off something that belongs to another, as the corner of a robe) (e:puantualpi mong ~ sim hi) (b:atkhiat) (r:9.24.4) (q:draft)
atkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:cutting off/cut off) (d:at, cut, with khiat, off, sak, do to someone, and the suffix in: cutting a part off a person) (e:na bilte hong ~ na tate hong thahsak) (b:atkhiatsak) (r:26.23.25) (q:draft)
atkhiatsakna = (t:n) (w:cutting off) (d:atkhiatsak, cut off, with the noun suffix na: the cutting off of a part, here of garments) (e:a puante uh ~ tawh amaute daisakin) (b:atkhiatsak) (r:13.19.4) (q:draft)
atkik = (t:v) (w:write again/rewrite) (d:at, write, with kik, again: write something out a second time) (e:thu omteng khempeuh ~ in) (s:gelhkik) (b:at) (r:24.36.28) (q:draft)
atmang = (t:see) <ki-atmang>
atna = (t:n) (w:circumcision/cutting) (d:noun of at, cut; vun atna, cutting of the skin, is circumcision) (e:vun ~ takpi hi lo hi/vun ~ hangin noptuamna a om hi | circumcision has value/Vun ~ a thuak khit ciangin | after he had received circumcision/ama vun at lohna in vun ~ bangin | his uncircumcision as circumcision) (s:vunatna) (b:at) (r:45.2.28/45.2.25/45.4.10/45.2.26) (q:draft)
atna = (t:n) (w:reaping/harvest) (d:noun of at, reap: the reaping of what someone has sown) (e:a gah a ~ ka thei hi) (s:anlak) (b:at) (r:18.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
atnate = (t:see) <sing-atnate>
atnen = (t:v) (w:cut up/chop finely/slice) (d:at, cut, with nen, fine: cut something up into small pieces) (e:mehbeel sungah ~ hi) (s:semnen) (r:12.4.39) (q:draft)
atnente = (t:see) <ki-atnente>
Atoroth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Atroth) (d:first part of <Atoroth-shofan>, a town built up by the Gadites) (r:4.32.35)
Atoroth-shofan = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Atroth Shophan) (d:town east of the Jordan built up by the Gadites) (r:4.32.35) (q:draft)
atpa = (t:n) (w:scribe/secretary/writer) (d:found in lai-atpa, from lai, writing, and at, write, with pa marking a man: one who writes, a scribe or secretary) (e:Sheva in lai-~ ahi hi/Seraiah in lai-~ ahi hi | Seraiah was secretary/lai-~ Shimshai in Kumpi Artakzaksis tungah | Shimshai the secretary to King Artaxerxes/kumpipa’ lai-~ leh siampi lianpa hong paito-in | the royal secretary and the high priest came up) (s:thuvanpipa) (r:10.20.25/13.24.6/10.8.17/15.4.8/12.12.10) (q:draft)
Atroth = (t:see) <Atroth-bethjoab>
Atroth-bethjoab = (t:name) (w:Atroth Beth Joab) (d:clan or town of Judah listed among the descendants of Salma) (r:13.2.54) (q:draft)
Atrothbethjoab = (t:name) (w:Atroth Beth Joab) (d:clan or town of Judah listed among the descendants of Salma; also written <Atroth-bethjoab>) (r:13.2.54)
Atrothshofan = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Atroth Shophan) (d:town east of the Jordan built up by the Gadites; also written <Atoroth-shofan>) (r:4.32.35)
atsa = (t:adj) (w:reaped/harvested/cut) (d:at, reap or cut, with sa, already done: buhlom atsa, cut sheaves; with vun and the prefix ki, vun ki-atsa, circumcised) (e:buhlom ~ kinusia bangin/leitung in ~ a suak hi | the earth was harvested/Vun ki-~ mi khat Pasian in a sap leh | if God calls a man who is circumcised) (b:at) (r:24.9.22/66.14.16/46.7.18) (q:draft)
atsak = (t:v) (w:circumcise/have cut) (d:at, cut, with sak, cause: have something cut; with vun, skin, it is the expression for circumcise someone) (e:ama vun a ~ hi/amaute’ vun dawn ~ hi | he circumcised them/amaute’ tate vun ~ lo | not circumcising their children/mi pawlkhat in ~ nuam sam uh hi | some wanted to have him circumcised) (s:vunat) (b:at) (r:44.16.3/1.17.23/44.21.21/48.2.4) (q:draft)
atsat = (t:v) (w:cut through/sever/hamstring) (d:at, cut, with sat, strike: cut through; zagui atsat is to cut the leg sinew of a horse, hamstring) (e:leengkai sakol khempeuh a zagui ~ a/sakol galkap khempeuh a zagui ~ sak a | he hamstrung all the chariot horses) (s:sattat) (r:10.8.4/13.18.4) (q:draft)
Attai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Attai) (d:name of several men, among them a grandson of Sheshan of Judah and a Gadite warrior who joined David) (r:13.2.36/13.12.11)
Attalia = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Attalia) (d:seaport in Pamphylia from which Paul and Barnabas sailed back to Antioch) (r:44.14.25)
attan = (t:v) (w:cut off/sever) (d:cut through so that a part comes off, as thumbs, a tail or a tongue; ngawng attan is break or cut the neck) (e:a khepite ~ uh hi/bawngla ngawng ~ ding uh hi | they shall break the neck of the heifer/thuhoih lo a gente’ leei ki-~ ding hi | the tongue of those who speak evil will be cut off/a nungguh ciangah a ki-~ a mei thau buppi | the whole fat tail cut off close to the backbone) (s:sattan/tan/atkhia) (r:7.1.6/5.21.4/20.10.31/3.3.9) (q:draft)
attatsak = (t:v) (w:hamstring/cut through/sever) (d:at, cut, and tat, sever, with sak: cut right through; a zagui attatsak is to cut their leg sinews, hamstring) (e:sakol galkap khempeuh a zagui ~ a) (s:sattat/atsat) (r:13.18.4) (q:draft)
atte = (t:n) (w:the circumcised) (d:at, cut, with the plural suffix te, in vun atte, those whose skin is cut, the circumcised) (e:vun ~ leh vun at lote/hih thupha vun ~ bek a pia hiam | is this blessing given only to the circumcised) (s:vunatte) (b:at) (r:45.3.30/45.4.9) (q:draft)
atte = (t:n) (w:reapers/harvesters) (d:at, reap, with the plural suffix te, those who cut the grain, as in buh atte and an atte) (e:Buh ~ in thaman ngah thei a/a vawhte leh a ~ a lungdam khawm ding | the sowers and the reapers will rejoice together/note’ lo lai-ah an ~ na kheem uh a | you cheated the reapers in your fields) (s:anlate) (b:at) (r:43.4.36/59.5.4) (q:draft)
atte = (t:n) (w:secretaries/scribes/writers) (d:at, write, with the plural suffix te, second part of lai-atte, those who write, the secretaries of a king) (e:Ahijah in lai-~ ahi uh hi/kumpipa’ lai-~ khempeuh kisam a | all the royal secretaries were summoned/Hezekiah’ lai-~ in a tei Solomon’ paunak dangte | more proverbs of Solomon copied by the scribes of Hezekiah) (s:laigelhte) (b:at) (r:11.4.3/20.25.1/17.3.12) (q:draft)
attem = (t:see) <sing-attem>
atual = (t:n) (w:court/courtyard) (d:tual, courtyard, with the prefix a written together; atual sungnung is the inner court of the temple) (e:~ sungnung bawl hi) (b:tual) (r:11.6.36) (q:draft)
atuam = (t:adj) (w:different/various/separate) (d:tuam, separate, with the prefix a; usually doubled as atuam atuam, of different kinds, each its own) (e:Nasepna za ~ ~ a om hangin/A hong piaksa hehpihna ~ ~ a om hangin | though there are different gifts of grace/deihgawhna ~ ~ zui-in | following all kinds of desires) (s:apawlpawl/pawlpawl) (a:kibang/kikim) (b:tuam) (r:46.12.5/46.12.4/55.3.6) (q:draft)
atuamin = (t:adv) (w:separately/apart/in various ways) (d:atuam, separate or different, with the adverb ending in; doubled as atuam atuamin, each separately, in various ways) (e:nungzuite ~ a khen khit ciangin/kiangah atuam ~ thu a piak kikkik | he spoke again and again in various ways/na atuam ~ pumpi sungah a guang kim hi | he has placed the parts in the body each in its own way) (s:tuamtuamin) (a:khawmin) (b:atuam) (r:44.19.9/58.1.1/46.12.18) (q:draft)
atuamte = (t:adj) (w:various/different) (d:atuam, different or separate, with the plural te; the doubled atuam atuamte means of many different kinds) (e:deihgawhna atuam ~ sungah a kia thei) (b:atuam) (r:54.6.9) (q:draft)
atuamtuam = (t:adj) (w:various/different/of different kinds) (d:tuamtuam, different, with the prefix a written together: of different kinds, each one different from the other) (e:~ thupha a ngah ciat uh hi/Pasian’ hehpihna thupha ~ a keem mi phate bangin | like good stewards of the varied grace of God/~ a om ciat uh hi | each is of a different kind) (s:apawlpawl/pawlpawl) (a:kibang) (b:tuamtuam) (r:46.7.7/60.4.10/46.15.39) (q:draft)
atul = (t:see) <atul-amakin>
atul-amakin = (t:adv) (w:in thousands upon thousands/in countless numbers) (d:in numbers too great to count; atul is a tul, a thousand, and the part amak is not clear) (e:~ a ding miaimuai vantung mite’ awging) (r:66.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
atung = (t:n) (w:above/top) (d:tung, top or upper side, with the prefix a written together; atung lam nate are the things above) (e:~ lam nate bek lunggulhin om un) (a:nuailam) (b:tung) (r:51.3.2) (q:draft)
Augustas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Augustus) (d:Caesar Augustus, the Roman emperor who ordered the census at the time of the birth of Jesus) (r:42.2.1)
Augustus = (t:name) (w:Augustus) (d:name of the Roman emperor; Augustus pawl is the Imperial Regiment to which the centurion Julius belonged) (r:44.27.1)
ausan = (t:adj) (w:scarlet/crimson) (d:bright red, of dyed yarn and cloth, named together with dum, blue, and dupsan, purple) (e:a dum, a dupsan, a ~ khaute/a dum, a dupsan, a ~ puante | blue, purple and scarlet cloths/puknah leh a ~ khaute la-in | taking hyssop and scarlet yarn/a dum leh a ~ leh a dupsan puante | blue and crimson and purple cloths) (r:2.35.6/4.19.6/2.25.4/14.3.14) (q:draft)
autok = (t:n) (w:lobe of the liver) (d:the lobe on the liver of a sacrificed animal, the prefix a and utok written as one word) (e:a sin tunga ~ leh a kal nihte) (b:utok) (r:2.29.13) (q:draft)
avan = (t:see) <Za-avan>
aven = (t:see) <Beth-aven>
Aven = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Aven) (d:valley in Syria named beside Damascus, in Aven Kuam, the Valley of Aven) (e:~ Kuama teng mi khempeuh) (r:30.1.5) (q:draft)
Avith = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Avith) (d:city of Hadad son of Bedad, a king of Edom) (r:1.36.35/13.1.46)
Avva = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Avva) (d:place from which the king of Assyria brought settlers to the towns of Samaria) (r:12.17.24)
Avvim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Avvim) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin; also the Avvites, a people who lived in villages as far as Gaza) (r:6.18.23)
aw = (t:part) (w:O) (d:vocative particle placed after the name or title of the one addressed) (e:lungsim a thei Topa ~/Vantungte ~, lungdamin la sa un | O heavens, sing for joy/Pasian ~, mawhnei keimah hong hehpih in | O God, have mercy on me, a sinner/Topa ~, kote kisiat ding nong awi hiam | Lord, are you willing that we perish) (r:44.1.24/1.49.18/23.49.13/42.18.13/41.4.38)
aw = (t:n) (w:voice/sound) (d:the voice of a person or of God, and the sound of an instrument) (e:~ in meikuang taangkhia sak hi/~ in liatna tawh kidim hi | the voice is full of majesty/amau ~ kiza lo hi | their voice is not heard/harp lasakna ~ tawh kituakin lam uh hi | they dance to the sound of harp music) (s:awging/kamging) (r:19.29.7/19.29.4/19.19.3/18.21.12)
aw = (t:intj) (w:yes) (d:answer of agreement to a question or an invitation) (s:awleh)
Aw = (t:intj) (w:O) (d:exclamation of address, here written with a capital and placed before the one addressed) (e:~ ka tapa Absalom/ka topa, ~ kumpipa | my lord, O king/~, ka gam, ka gam | O land, land/~ mual lianpi, Bashan mual | O great mountain, mount Bashan) (s:O) (b:aw) (r:10.19.4/12.6.26/24.22.29/19.68.15) (q:draft)
aw-uun = (t:n) (w:hushed voice/low voice) (d:a low, hushed voice, from aw, voice, with uun; aw-uun duadua is a faint murmuring voice) (e:~ duadua khat ka za a) (s:awneem) (r:18.4.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
awging = (t:n) (w:voice/sound) (d:aw, voice, with ging, sound: the sound of a voice or of anything that is heard) (e:ama ~ hong kiza a/a kuum tung san panin ~ kiza lai hi | a voice was still heard from above the vault/Lau nading ~ a bil-ah za ngitnget ding a | he will keep hearing terrifying sounds in his ears/amah dingin ~ pha tawh | he stood and with a loud voice) (s:aw/ging) (r:18.37.4/26.1.25/18.15.21/11.8.55) (q:draft)
awgingte = (t:n) (w:sounds/voices/noises) (d:awging, sound or voice, with the plural te: the sounds of music, singing, weeping or prayer) (e:tum theih ~ khempeuh zong kiza nawn lo/thuumna ~ mite in khen thei lo uh hi | the people could not distinguish the sounds of wailing/kumpi inn sunga lungdam lasakna ~ | the sounds of joyful singing in the palace/Ka thumna ~ hong ngai in | listen to the sounds of my pleading) (s:awte/gingte) (b:awging) (r:26.26.13/30.8.3/15.3.13/19.130.2) (q:draft)
awh = (t:v) (w:wear around the neck) (d:said of beads or a necklace, khi: khi awh, the necklace that is worn, one jewel of your necklace in the NIV; the meaning of awh alone is not shown by the verse) (e:na khi ~ in ka lungsim hong zo hi) (r:22.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
awhsak = (t:v) (w:put together/join) (d:said of God putting the parts of the body together; the base awh is not certain) (e:Pasian in pumpi ~ a) (r:46.12.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
awhte = (t:n) (w:chains/necklaces) (d:things worn hung around the neck, awh with the plural te; ngawng-awhte, neck chains) (e:ngawng-a ~ bangin khainiangte bawlin/ngawng kimkotah a om ngawng-~ | the chains that were around the necks) (b:awh) (r:14.3.16/7.8.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
awi = (t:v) (w:warm oneself/sit by a fire) (d:with mei, fire: mei awi is warm oneself at a fire) (e:palikte tawh mei a ~ khawm hi/ding-in mei a ~ hi | he stood warming himself at the fire/meikhuk-a mei a ~ hi | he warmed himself at the fire in the firepot/Piter mei ~-a om a muh ciangin | when she saw Peter warming himself at the fire) (r:41.14.54/41.14.67/43.18.18/24.36.22) (q:draft)
awi = (t:v) (w:be willing/approve/want/agree to) (d:be willing that something is done or happens; in questions with hiam, do you want or do you not mind) (e:va bot le-ung nong ~ hiam/kote kisiat ding nong ~ hiam | are you willing that we perish/tua bang ahih mite a ~ uh hi | they approve of those who do such things/tua mite a kat nading na ~ hiam | do you want those people to be destroyed) (s:thukimpih) (r:40.13.28/42.11.47/41.4.38/45.1.32/42.9.54) (q:draft)
awk = (t:n) (w:blackness) (e:tua ni ~ in valhtum hen) (r:18.3.5)
awk = (t:v) (w:seize/catch/be caught) (d:catch or be caught in a trap, net or snare) (e:Thang-ah a khetul-in ~ a/amau khe mah a ~ hi | their own feet are caught/ngasa nam tampi a ~ thei ngeen | a net that can catch many kinds of fish/ngenthang sung mah-ah migilote ~ sak in | let the wicked be caught in their own nets) (s:man) (a:suakta) (r:18.18.9/19.9.15/40.13.47/19.141.10)
awkcip = (t:v) (w:be snared/be caught fast/be trapped) (d:awk, be caught, with cip, tightly: be held fast in a trap or snare) (e:amau’ mawhna sungah ~ a) (s:awkkha) (a:suakta) (b:awk) (r:20.29.6) (q:draft)
awkcipin = (t:v) (w:be trapped/be ensnared) (d:awk be caught in a snare and cip tight, with the linking suffix in: caught fast) (e:a haivai thute-ah ~) (b:awkcip) (r:54.6.9) (q:draft)
awkin = (t:v) (w:be snared/be caught/be trapped) (d:form of awk, be caught in a snare, with the linking suffix in) (e:amaute ~ kiman ding hi/thangah ~, salin hong kipaipih ding hi | snared in a trap, you will be taken captive/thang hong siah a, ~ leilakah ka kipuk hi | he set a trap for me, and caught in it I fell to the ground) (b:awk) (r:23.8.15/23.28.13/25.1.13) (q:draft)
awkkha = (t:v) (w:be trapped/be ensnared) (d:awk, be caught in a snare, with kha, happen to: get caught, as by a promise one has made) (e:na thuciamna hangin na ~ hiam) (s:awkcip/awklawh) (a:suakta) (r:20.6.2) (q:draft)
awklawh = (t:v) (w:be ensnared/get caught) (d:awk, be caught in a snare, with lawh, which shows that this comes on someone as a result of something) (e:note in zong na ~ kha ding uh hi/a pawi bawlnate uh ~ uh hen la | may they be ensnared by their feasts) (s:awkkha) (r:20.22.25/45.11.9) (q:draft)
awklum = (t:v) (w:hang oneself) (d:die by hanging, from awk be caught in a noose) (e:a pai khit ciangin a ~ hi) (r:40.27.5) (q:draft)
awkna = (t:n) (w:entrapment/snare/trap) (d:awk, be caught, with the noun suffix na: the state of being caught, or the catching itself, as in awkna ding thang, a trap to be caught in) (e:tua ~ pan suahtakna a ngah khak/sakhi in a ~ ding thang zuanin | as a deer heads for the trap that will catch it/amau’ ~ ding mah thang siah uh a | they set a trap to catch themselves/ngasa namkim a ~ ngen tawh | with a net that catches every kind of fish) (b:awk) (r:55.2.25/54.6.9/20.7.22/20.1.18/40.13.47) (q:draft)
awkpih = (t:v) (w:be trapped by/be ensnared by) (d:awk, be caught, with pih: be caught by means of something, usually by the words or deeds of oneself) (e:amau kampau mah ~ uh hi/Migilote’ in a zuaugenna uh ~ a | the wicked are trapped by their lies/amau’ huaihamna mah ~ uh hi | they are trapped by their own greed/amau’ gamtat siatna mah ~ uh hi | they are trapped by their own evil deeds) (b:awk) (r:20.18.7/20.12.13/20.11.6/20.21.7) (q:draft)
awksak = (t:v) (w:trap/catch/ensnare) (d:awk, be caught, with the causative sak: cause to be caught in a pit, net or snare) (e:a thang-ah ~ uh hi/gum sungah ~ uh hi | they trapped him in a pit/migilote amau’ gitlohna mahah ~ a | he catches the wicked in their own wickedness/ngenthang ka zak ding a, amah ka ~ ding hi | I will spread a net and I will trap him) (s:man) (a:suaktasak/khah) (b:awk) (r:26.19.8/19.35.8/26.19.4/18.5.13/26.17.20) (q:draft)
awksakna = (t:n) (w:ensnaring/trapping) (d:awksak, ensnare, with the noun suffix na: the act of causing someone to be caught, as the wicked in the work of their own hands) (e:~ tawh amah hong kilang hi) (b:awksak) (r:19.9.16) (q:draft)
awkte = (t:n) (w:those caught/those ensnared) (d:awk, be caught, with the plural te; a awkte, those who are caught in a trap) (e:tua thang ah a ~ tungah) (b:awk) (r:20.22.14) (q:draft)
awl = (t:see) <tang-awl>
awle = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:crocodile/sea monster/Leviathan) (d:large water creature; the verses use it for the monster of the Nile and for Leviathan) (e:Gun sungah a om, ~ lianpi ahi/gun a ninsak, ~ tawh na kibang zaw hi | you are more like a monster that muddies the river/a kikualvial gulpi ahi ~ gim pia ding a | he will punish Leviathan, the coiling serpent) (r:26.29.3/18.3.8/26.32.2/23.27.1) (q:draft)
Awle = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:Leviathan/crocodile) (d:awle, crocodile, written with a capital for the sea monster Leviathan) (e:~ a mu mi peuhmah lau-in/sikkawi tawh ~ man zo ding a | can you catch Leviathan with a hook/gualnop nadinga na bawl ~ pai hi | Leviathan, which you made to play, goes there/~’ lutangte na sukham a | you crushed the heads of Leviathan) (b:awle) (r:18.41.9/19.104.26/18.41.1/19.74.14) (q:draft)
awleh = (t:intj) (w:yes) (s:aw)
awlin = (t:see) <tang-awlin>
awlmawh = (t:v) (w:heed/care about/pay attention to/consider) (d:mostly used with a negative, not minding or not caring) (e:i siampite a ~ nawn kei hi/na sat hangin a ~ tuan kei uh hi | though you struck them they did not care/bang mah a ~ thei tuan kei hi | she did not consider it at all) (s:thudon/don) (r:25.4.16/24.5.3/25.1.9) (q:draft)
awm = (t:n) (w:chest/breast) (d:the front of the upper body; awm beeng is beat the breast in grief) (e:A ~ leh a bante ngun tawh/~ beengin a ciah uh hi | they went away beating their breasts/ka ~ sungah tui suak hi | it has turned to water within my chest/dahin na ~ uh beng un | beat your breasts in grief) (r:27.2.32/42.18.13/42.23.48/19.22.14/23.32.12) (q:draft)
awmah = (t:n) (w:chest/breast) (d:awm chest with the place marker ah: on the chest) (e:a ~ kham kawnggak gakin) (b:awm) (r:66.1.13) (q:draft)
awmdal = (t:n) (w:breastpiece/breastplate) (d:covering worn on the chest, the breastpiece of the high priest or a breastplate of armour) (e:~ mong a kual nihte/a ~ sungah Urim leh Thummim koih hi | he put the Urim and Thummim in the breastpiece/a galdal thep leh a ~ kikal kha hi | it struck between the scale armour and the breastplate/sik ~ tawh kibang hi | is like a breastplate of iron) (s:awmdalna) (r:2.28.24/66.9.9/3.8.8/14.18.33) (q:draft)
awmdalah = (t:n) (w:breastpiece/breastplate) (d:awmdal breastpiece with the place marker ah: on the breastpiece) (e:siampipuan le ~ bulh dingin) (b:awmdal) (r:2.35.9) (q:draft)
awmdalna = (t:n) (w:breastplate) (d:awmdal, chest covering, with the noun suffix na: armour worn over the chest) (e:dikna ~ na bulh un la/A ~ un sik awmdal tawh kibang hi | their breastplates were like breastplates of iron/upna leh itna tawh kipawl ~ | the breastplate of faith and love) (s:awmdal) (b:awmdal) (r:49.6.14/66.9.9/52.5.8) (q:draft)
awmdalnate = (t:n) (w:breastplates) (d:awmdalna breastplate, a covering for the chest, with the plural te) (e:kat banga eng ~ a nei uh hi) (b:awmdalna) (r:66.9.17) (q:draft)
awmgak = (t:n) (w:sash/chest band) (d:awm, chest, with gak, tie: a band tied round the chest) (e:a awm-ah kham ~ gakin/a awm-ah kham kibawl ~ a gak | wearing a sash made of gold around his chest) (r:66.15.6/66.1.13) (q:draft)
awmtal = (t:v) (w:crawl/go on the belly) (d:move along the ground on the belly, as a snake does) (e:a bokvak ganhing bangin hong ~ ding uh a/A ~ peuhmah leh khe li-a a pai peuhmah | whatever goes on its belly and whatever walks on four feet) (s:bokvak) (r:33.7.17/3.11.42) (q:draft)
awn = (t:num) (w:million) (d:the number one million; awn khat is one million) (e:mihing ~ khat leh sang khat/ngun talen ~ khat | one million talents of silver/galkap ~ khat leh leeng galkap zathum tawh | with an army of a million and three hundred chariots) (r:13.21.5/13.22.14/14.14.9) (q:draft)
awn = (t:v) (w:lean/sway/reel/bend) (d:lean, bend or sway to one side, as a hut or a reed in the wind or a drunk person; awn sak is cause to lean) (e:a mut buk bangin ~ ding hi/Huih in a mut ~ diamdiam lopa kungte | reeds swaying in the wind/kham theih zu tawh ~ uh hi | they reel from strong drink/~ sukin an ka pia hi | I bent down and fed them) (s:hoi) (r:23.24.20/19.119.36/42.7.24/23.28.7/28.11.4) (q:draft)
awn = (t:v) (w:give way/give up a place/make room/yield) (d:move aside for someone: give up a seat or a place, or fall back before an enemy) (e:Hih pa ading omna na ~ in/khangnote in tutna hong ~ uh a | the young men gave up their seats to me/Israel mite in Benjamin mite ~ uh hi | the Israelites gave way to the Benjamites) (r:42.14.9/18.29.8/7.20.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
awneem = (t:n) (w:soft voice/gentle whisper) (d:aw, voice, with neem, soft: a soft, gentle voice) (e:~ neu khat om hi) (s:aw-uun) (r:11.19.12) (q:draft)
awng = (t:v) (w:shout/cry out/roar) (d:raise a loud cry, of joy, of battle or of anger) (e:nakpi takin ~ uh a/Israelte khempeuh nakpi takin ~ uh a, lei thawn hi | all Israel shouted loudly and the ground shook/Jakob Pasian’ tungah lungdamin ~ un | shout for joy to the God of Jacob/Amah kiko loin, ~ khia lo a | he will not cry out or shout) (s:kiko/ot) (a:daih) (r:6.6.20/23.42.2/9.4.5/19.81.1) (q:draft)
awng = (t:adj) (w:empty/vacant/unoccupied) (d:empty or free, of a seat or a place with no one in it; mun awng is an open space) (e:ahih hangin David’ mun ~ hi/na tutna ~ ding ahih manin | because your seat will be empty/kote’ giah nading a ~ ding hiam | is there room for us to spend the night/mun ~, tong tulnih bang kihalna om ding hi | there shall be an open space, a distance of about two thousand cubits) (s:hawm) (a:dim) (r:9.20.25/9.20.18/1.24.23/6.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
awngah = (t:adj) (w:open/empty) (d:awng, empty or open, with the place marker ah; mun awngah is in the open place, the public square of a town) (e:khua laizang mun ~ khawmin/nisuahna lam mun-~ amaute khawm a | he gathered them in the square on the east side) (b:awng) (r:5.13.16/14.29.4) (q:draft)
awnggawp = (t:v) (w:shout/clamour/cry out loudly) (d:awng, shout, with gawp, which shows that it is done with force) (e:ci-in a ~ uh hi/pawlkhat in thu khat genin ~ uh a | some were shouting one thing/hinkhawi ding kilawm lo hi, ci-in amaute ~ uh hi | they shouted that he ought not to be kept alive) (s:awngkekgawp) (b:awng) (r:44.17.7/44.19.32/44.25.24) (q:draft)
awnghawh = (t:v) (w:relieve oneself/ease oneself) (d:go aside to empty the bowels, a polite expression) (e:~ nading mun khat na nei ding uh hi/Inn vot sunga inndei-ah ~ hi in teh | he must be relieving himself in the inner room of the cool house) (r:5.23.12/7.3.24) (q:draft)
awngin = (t:v) (w:shouting/with a shout) (d:awng, shout, with the linking ending in: shouting, and then doing something else) (e:Tua ciangin mi khempeuh ~/Israelte leh Judah mite ~ ding uh a | the men of Israel and Judah rose up with a shout/Jew mihonte ~ kiko uh a | the Jewish crowd cried out, shouting/lungdamin ~ amaute in la sakhawm uh hi | shouting for joy they sing together) (s:kikoin) (b:awng) (r:9.10.24/9.17.52/43.19.12/19.65.13) (q:draft)
awngin = (t:adj) (w:empty/unoccupied) (d:awng empty with the linking ending in, being empty) (e:a tun’ ciangin tua inn ~) (b:awng) (r:40.12.44) (q:draft)
awngkeek = (t:v) (w:thunder/roar) (d:shout with a very loud voice; from awng shout) (e:Jerusalem panin hong ~ a) (s:awngkek) (r:29.3.16) (q:draft)
awngkek = (t:v) (w:cry out/roar/shriek) (d:give a loud cry: roar or thunder, said of the Lord, and cry out in fear) (e:Jerusalem khua panin hong ~ hi/Jerusalem panin hong ~ a | he thunders from Jerusalem/ahih manin a ~ gawp uh hi | and so they cried out loudly) (s:awngkeek) (r:30.1.2/41.6.49/29.3.16) (q:draft)
awngkekgawp = (t:v) (w:shout furiously/yell/roar) (d:awngkek, shout aloud, with gawp, which shows that it is done with force; of an angry crowd) (e:Mihonte hehlua-in ~ uh a/ci-in ~ uh hi | they shouted furiously, saying/ama tungah hehin ~ uh ahi hiam | why they were shouting at him in anger) (s:awnggawp) (b:awngkek) (r:44.22.23/44.19.28/44.22.24) (q:draft)
awngkhia = (t:v) (w:shout out/cry aloud/raise a shout) (d:awng, shout, with khia, out) (e:lungdamin ~ unla, phatna la sa un/Amah kiko-in nakpitakin ~ a | he cries out and shouts aloud/Mual liante aw, lungdamin la sa-in ~ un | O great mountains, sing for joy and shout/tua ciangin Jehoshafat ~ hi | then Jehoshaphat cried out) (s:kikokhia) (b:awng) (r:19.98.4/23.42.13/23.49.13/11.22.32) (q:draft)
awngna = (t:see) <mun-awngna>
awngsak = (t:v) (w:make shout/let shout) (d:awng shout, with the causative sak) (e:mual dawn panin amaute ~ un) (b:awng) (r:23.42.11) (q:draft)
awngsuak = (t:v) (w:keep shouting/cry out) (d:awng shout, with suak; said of the prophets of Baal who went on crying out) (e:amaute ~ uh a) (r:11.18.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
awngsuk = (t:v) (w:thunder/shout down) (d:awng, shout, with suk, downward: shout down from above, said of the Lord thundering from heaven) (e:Topa hong ~ a) (s:hawksuk) (b:awng) (r:10.22.14) (q:draft)
awngte = (t:adj) (w:empty/deserted) (d:awng, empty, with the plural te; mun awngte, empty places, is used for ruins) (e:mun ~ leh a kim a pamah) (b:awng) (r:14.34.6) (q:draft)
awngthawl = (t:n) (w:cave/hole/gap/vacuum) (s:awngthawlpi) empty space
awngthawl = (t:adj) (w:invalid/null/nullified/null and void/empty) (d:empty, with nothing in it or with no use; a awngthawl mun is an empty place) (e:a ~ dingin bawl loin | he did not make it to be empty/A ~ mun sungah kei hong zong un | seek me in an empty place/Ten’ nading leh a mun ~ hi ding a | it will be for dwellings and open land) (s:awngthawlpi) (r:23.45.18/23.45.19/26.48.15) empty space
awngthawlpi = (t:adj) (w:without form/void) (e:nei loin a ~ ahi hi) (s:awngthawl/hawmguak) (r:1.1.2) a completely empty space
