awnna = (t:n) (w:open space/square) (d:in khuapi kulhkongpi mun awnna, the open place at the city gate; the base awn is not certain) (e:khuapi kulhkongpi mun ~ ama kiangah) (r:14.32.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
awnsa = (t:adj) (w:bruised/bent) (d:awn lean, bend over, with sa already: already bent; said of a reed) (e:A ~ pumpeeng kuai tan lo a) (s:kisunimsa) (b:awn) (r:40.12.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
awnsak = (t:v) (w:incline/turn/cause to lean) (d:awn, lean, with the causative sak; used of turning the heart toward something) (e:lamah ka lungsim ~ in la/ama lamah i lungsim hong ~ hen | may he turn our hearts toward him) (b:awn) (r:19.119.36/11.8.58) (q:draft)
awnsuk = (t:v) (w:tilt down/lean over) (d:awn, lean or tilt, with suk, downward: of a pot, tilt over toward someone) (e:a leilu lam panin hong ~ hi) (b:awn) (r:24.1.13) (q:draft)
awte = (t:n) (w:voices/sounds) (d:aw, voice, with the plural te: voices, or the sounds of joy, song and prayer) (e:lungdamna leh kipahna ~/zi nei thakte leh mothakte’ ~ kiza kik ding hi | the voices of bridegrooms and brides will be heard again/keima thuumna ~ hong ngai in | listen to the sounds of my pleading/amau kam ~ a gen uh hi | they spoke with their own voices) (s:awgingte) (b:aw) (r:24.25.10/66.10.3/24.33.11/19.140.6) (q:draft)
awtna = (t:n) (w:shouting/uproar) (d:a loud shouting of many people; the same verse also has the spelling otna) (e:Filistia mite in ~ gamlumna a zak) (s:otna) (r:9.4.6) (q:draft)
awzol = (t:v) (w:speak smoothly/speak cordially) (d:aw voice and zol coax: speak in a friendly, winning voice) (e:a ~ uh hangin) (r:24.9.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
