bakte = (t:n) (w:pieces) (d:in the hyphenated word sa-bakte, the pieces of meat of an animal that has been cut up) (e:a sa-~ leh a lu tawh tuate koihin | putting them with its pieces and its head) (r:2.29.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
bakuth = (t:see) <Allon-bakuth>
bal = (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear apart) (d:tear with the hands or teeth; bal khia is tear away, bal nen is break into small pieces, crumble) (e:a samatsa uh a ~ gawpgawp ngia hon/na khut sung panin kumpigam ~ khia-in | tearing the kingdom out of your hands/~ nenin a tungah sathau na sung ding hi | crumble it and pour oil on it/mi khat in keelno khat a ~ gawp bangin | as one tears a young goat apart/a puan uh ~ kek-in | tearing their clothes) (s:balkek/balzan) (a:phop) (r:26.22.27/9.15.28/9.28.17/3.2.6/7.14.6/24.41.5) (q:draft)
