Balaam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Balaam) (d:prophet, son of Beor, whom Balak king of Moab hired to curse Israel) (r:4.22.5/4.24.12)
baladan = (t:see) <Merodak-baladan>
Baladan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Baladan) (d:father of Marduk-Baladan king of Babylon) (r:23.39.1/12.20.12)
Balah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Balah) (d:town in the territory of Simeon, in the south of Judah) (r:6.19.3)
Balak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Balak) (d:king of Moab, son of Zippor, who hired Balaam to curse Israel) (r:4.22.39/4.24.12)
balgawp = (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/rip apart/maul) (d:To tear a person or an animal violently to pieces, as a wild beast does to its prey; built from bal, tear, and gawp, severely.) (e:note kong ~ ding hi/hong kaikhia-in hong ~ ding uh hi | they will drag me off and tear me to pieces/naupang sawmli-le-nih ~ hi | they mauled forty-two boys/amah in eite hong ~ hangin | though he has torn us to pieces/gamsate in a ~ ganhing thaute | the fat of animals torn by wild beasts) (s:petgawp/balzan/balthanggawp) (b:bal) (r:19.50.22/3.7.24/19.7.2/12.2.24/28.6.1) (q:draft)
balgawpin = (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/maul) (d:The verb balgawp, tear apart violently, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb.) (e:amaute ~ ka paisan ding hi/hong ~ hong sugawp hi | he tore me apart and crushed me) (b:balgawp) (r:28.5.14/18.16.12) (q:draft)
balgawpte = (t:n) (w:those torn to pieces/torn animals) (d:Animals that wild beasts have torn; balgawp, tear to pieces, with the plural te.) (e:gamsate in a ~ hita leh) (s:balzante) (b:balgawp) (r:3.22.8) (q:draft)
balkeek = (t:v) (w:tear/rend/rip) (d:To tear cloth or something like it apart; often a puan balkeek, to tear one’s clothes as a sign of grief or horror.) (e:siampi ukpa in a puan ~ a/~ hun om a, phop hun om hi | there is a time to tear and a time to mend/amah in a khate-in ~ ding a | he shall tear it open by its wings/Hih puan ~ kei ni | let us not tear this garment/seh sawm-le-nih suahin ~ hi | he tore it into twelve pieces) (s:balkek/bal) (a:phop/khui) (r:41.14.63/21.3.7/3.1.17/43.19.24/11.11.30) (q:draft)
balkeekin = (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear away) (d:The verb balkeek, tear, with the linking suffix in, which joins it to the next verb; mostly of tearing one’s clothes in grief.) (e:a puante ~ lei lakah lum hi/Na puan uh ~ puanham silh un | tear your clothes and put on sackcloth/nangma tung panin na kumpigam ~ | tearing your kingdom away from you/vantungte ~ hong paisuk | rend the heavens and come down) (s:balkekin) (b:balkeek) (r:10.13.31/1.37.34/10.3.31/11.11.11/23.64.1) (q:draft)
balkek = (t:v) (w:tear/rend) (d:To tear cloth apart; in the verses almost always to tear one’s clothes as a sign of grief.) (e:dahna hangin a puante ~ hi/a puan uh ~ lo uh hi | they did not tear their clothes/Bang hangin na puante ~ na hi hiam | why have you torn your clothes/~ hun om a, phop hun om hi | there is a time to tear and a time to mend/a puan ~ uh a, mihonpi lakah tai-in | they tore their clothes and ran into the crowd) (s:balkeek/bal) (a:phop/khui) (r:12.22.11/18.1.20/24.36.24/12.5.8/21.3.7/44.14.14) (q:draft)
balkekin = (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear away) (d:The verb balkek, tear, with the linking suffix in, tearing and then doing something else; often of tearing one’s clothes in grief.) (e:a puante ~ puanhampi silh a/nangma tung panin na kumpi gam ~ | tearing your kingdom away from you/vantung ~ hong paisuk | rend the heavens and come down/ka puante ~, ka sam leh ka khamul botin | tearing my clothes and pulling out my hair and beard) (s:balkeekin) (b:balkek) (r:12.19.1/11.11.11/23.64.1/15.9.3) (q:draft)
balkekna = (t:n) (w:tearing/rending) (d:The act of tearing one’s clothes, from balkek, tear, with the noun suffix na; a balkekna thu is the news that he had torn them.) (e:a puante a ~ thu) (b:balkek) (r:12.5.8) (q:draft)
balkeksa = (t:adj) (w:torn) (d:Torn, of clothes torn as a sign of grief; balkek, tear, with sa, already done.) (e:a puantungsilh ~ leh a lu tungah/a puan uh ~-in Hezekiah kiangah hong pai uh | they came to Hezekiah with their clothes torn) (s:kikeeksa) (b:balkek) (r:10.15.32/12.18.37) (q:draft)
balkeksak = (t:v) (w:tear off/strip) (d:To tear the clothes off someone; balkek, tear, with the causative sak.) (e:Paul le Silas’ puan ~ uh a) (b:balkek) (r:44.16.22) (q:draft)
balkham = (t:v) (w:tear/tear off) (d:To tear at or tear off a part of the body, said of a lion tearing the arm or head of its prey; bal, tear, with kham.) (e:leh a luzang ~ hi) (r:5.33.20) (q:draft)
balkhia = (t:v) (w:tear out/tear away/rip off) (d:To tear something out or away from where it is; bal, tear, with khia, out.) (e:kumpigam khempeuh ka ~ kei ding hi/na tapa’ khut sung panin ka ~ ding hi | I will tear it out of your son’s hand/natna a ban’na mun ~ ding hi | he shall tear out the place where the mold is/David innkuan panin kumpigam ~-in | tearing the kingdom away from the house of David/Solomon khut panin kumpigam a ~ ding | about to tear the kingdom out of Solomon’s hand) (s:eukhia) (b:bal) (r:11.11.13/3.13.56/11.11.12/11.14.8/11.11.31) (q:draft)
balkhiat = (t:v) (w:tear away/tear out) (d:The form of balkhia, tear away, used before a following word such as khit.) (e:Israel gam a ~ khit ciangin) (b:balkhia) (r:12.17.21) (q:draft)
balneenin = (t:v) (w:break in pieces) (d:The verb balneen, break in pieces, also written balnen, with the ending in linking it to the following verb.) (e:khomun ~ a pia hi) (s:balnenin) (r:42.24.30) (q:draft)
balnen = (t:v) (w:break in pieces/break/maul) (d:To break or tear something into pieces; khomun balnen is to break bread, and of a lion or bear it is to maul its victim.) (e:khomun a ~ lai takin/khomun ~ dingin ka kikhop lai takun | when we met together to break bread/Eite ~ khomun | the bread that we break/thupha a piak khit ciangin ~ a | after giving thanks he broke them/la zong ~ lo hi | nor had it mauled the donkey) (r:42.24.35/44.20.7/46.10.16/42.9.16/11.13.28)
balnenin = (t:v) (w:break in pieces) (d:The verb balnen, break in pieces, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb.) (e:khomun ~ a neek khit uh ciangin/khomun leh ngasa ~ a nungzuite a pia hi | he broke the loaves and the fish and gave them to his disciples/hehpihna a phat khit ciangin khomun ~ | after giving thanks he broke the bread/amau innah anlum ~ | breaking bread in their homes/amah ~ a that humpinelkai | the lion that mauled and killed him) (s:balneenin) (b:balnen) (r:44.20.11/40.15.36/41.14.22/44.2.46/11.13.26)
balnenna = (t:n) (w:breaking) (d:The act of breaking; balnen, break in pieces, with the noun suffix na, as in khomun balnenna, the breaking of bread.) (e:khomun ~ leh thungetna a bawl) (b:balnen) (r:44.2.42) (q:draft)
balnensa = (t:see) <balnensa-in>
balnensa-in = (t:adv) (w:broken in pieces/crumbled) (d:In the state of having been broken into pieces; balnen, break in pieces, with sa, already done, and the ending in.) (e:helsa leh ~ na paipih ding a) (r:3.6.21) (q:draft)
balnensak = (t:v) (w:tear in pieces for) (d:To tear prey in pieces for others, as a lion does for its mate and cubs; balnen, break or tear in pieces, with sak.) (e:a zi leh a tate’ adingin ~ a) (b:balnen) (r:34.2.12) (q:draft)
baltat = (t:v) (w:tear apart/tear in two/sever) (d:To tear a thing right through so that the parts come apart; bal, tear, with tat, be severed.) (e:ahih hangin ~ lo ding hi) (r:3.1.17) (q:draft)
Balteshazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belteshazzar) (d:Babylonian name given to Daniel at the court of Nebuchadnezzar) (r:27.4.9)
balthang = (t:v) (w:tear apart/tear to pieces) (d:To tear apart, said of a wild animal tearing its prey.) (e:gamsate bangin kong ~ gawp ding) (s:balzan/balgawp) (r:28.13.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
balthanggawp = (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/tear apart) (d:To tear completely to pieces; balthang, tear apart, with gawp, severely.) (e:amaute in Paul ~ kha ding hi/gamsate bangin kong ~ ding hi | like a wild beast I will tear you apart) (s:balgawp/balzan) (b:balthang) (r:44.23.10/28.13.8) (q:draft)
balzan = (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/tear apart/tear down) (d:To tear into pieces, as a wild animal does to its prey; of walls and strongholds, to tear down.) (e:Gamsa in a ~ ahih leh/a khut guak tawh humpinelkai ~ hi | he tore the lion apart with his bare hands/a pusuak khia peuhpeuh ~ gawp ding hi | it will tear to pieces anyone who comes out/a galdalna kulhpite khempeuh ~ gawpin | tearing down all her strongholds/gamsate in a ~ sa peuhmah | any meat torn by wild beasts) (s:balgawp/balthanggawp/petgawp) (r:2.22.13/27.6.24/7.14.6/24.5.6/25.2.2/2.22.31) (q:draft)
balzante = (t:n) (w:those torn to pieces/torn animals) (d:Animals torn by wild beasts; balzan, tear to pieces, with the plural te.) (e:Gamlak ganhingte’ ~ nang' kiangah kong puak kei hi) (s:balgawpte) (b:balzan) (r:1.31.39) (q:draft)
Bamoth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bamoth) (d:stopping place of the Israelites in Moab between Nahaliel and the valley below Pisgah) (r:4.21.19/4.21.20)
Bamoth-baal = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bamoth Baal) (d:high place in Moab to which Balak took Balaam to see the Israelite camp) (e:Balaam samin ~ munah paipih to hi) (r:4.22.41) (q:draft)
Bamothbaal = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bamoth Baal) (d:town on the plateau of Moab allotted to the tribe of Reuben, the high place to which Balak took Balaam) (r:6.13.17)
ban = (t:v) (w:reach/extend to/stretch to) (d:To reach up to or extend as far as a point, said of height, of borders and of sound.) (e:na cihtakna in meii ~ hi/kahlei dawn in van ~ hi | the top of the ladder reached heaven/kahna in Eglaim khua ~ a | the wailing reaches as far as Eglaim/nisuahna gam mual tung dong ~ hi | it stretched as far as the eastern hill country/a dawn in vantung a ~ ding tausangpi | a tower whose top will reach the heavens) (s:phak) (r:19.36.5/1.28.12/23.15.8/1.10.30/1.11.4) (q:draft)
ban = (t:n) (w:arm) (d:The arm, also written baan; a figure for strength or power.) (e:siatna bawlte’ ~ kuaitan in la/Topa a ~ tom lo a | the arm of the Lord is not too short/a ~ tungah a om a banbulh | the band that was on his arm) (s:baan) (r:19.10.15/18.4.3/23.59.1/10.1.10) (q:draft)
ban = (t:n) (d:What comes next to or on top of something; with the place marker ah, ban-ah, next to, in addition to.) (e:mi thumte’ ~-ah min ngah hi/Abraham’ hun lai-a kialpi ~-ah | besides the famine of Abraham’s time/ka tanute’ ~-ah zi na lak beh leh | if you take wives besides my daughters/meihal tawh kihal biakna ~-ah na hal ding hi | you shall burn them on top of the burnt offering) (r:10.23.22/1.26.1/1.31.50/2.29.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
banah = (t:prep) (w:in addition to/besides/beside) (d:In addition to or on top of what is named before it; the noun ban, what comes next, with the place marker ah, as in tua banah, besides that.) (e:a kikaikhawmsa mite ~ midangte/zingsanga meihal biakna ~ | in addition to the morning burnt offering/khat ~ khat i ngah sawnsawn hi | we keep receiving one on top of another/tua ~ amaute in lasa numei leh pasal | besides that they had male and female singers/kulhnei khuapite ah a koihte ~ | besides those he stationed in the fortified cities) (b:ban) (r:23.56.8/4.28.23/43.1.16/16.7.67/14.17.19) (q:draft)
Banaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:spelling of Benaiah, here a Levite musician appointed when David brought the ark to Jerusalem) (r:13.15.18/13.16.5)
banbanin = (t:adv) (w:one after another/in succession/in turn) (d:One after another, in a series; usually a banbanin, of things that follow each other in order.) (e:khat khit khat a ~ na tuak/amaute in a ~ | they, one after another/a sepna khempeuh a ~ a cingtakin a gen hi | he reported in full, one thing after another, all that he had done/thupha a ~ hong pia hi | he has given us blessing upon blessing/a ~ thu ka phawkkhia hi | I found things out one after another) (s:aban/khatkhatin) (r:26.7.26/43.1.16/40.26.22/44.21.19/21.7.27) (q:draft)
banbuhte = (t:n) (w:armlets/bracelets) (d:Rings worn on the arm, named in lists of gold ornaments; ban, arm, with buh, ring, and the plural te.) (e:~ leh taute, min gelhna zungbuhte/min gelhna zungbuhte, leh ~ | signet rings and armlets) (s:banbulhte) (r:4.31.50/2.35.22) (q:draft)
banbulh = (t:n) (w:armlet/bracelet/arm band) (d:An ornament or band worn on the arm; from ban, arm, and bulh, put on.) (e:a om a ~ kong la a) (r:10.1.10) (q:draft)
banbulhte = (t:n) (w:armlets/arm bands) (d:Ornaments or bands fastened on the arm, banbulh with the plural te; in Isaiah 3.20 the NIV has anklets, and in Matthew 23.5 they are the phylacteries worn on the arm.) (e:lukhute, ~, kawngtente, paknamtui bungte/a talsuan le a ~ uh a gol pipi-in bawlin | they make their phylacteries large/min gelhna zungbuhte, le ~ | signet rings and armlets) (s:banbuhte) (b:banbulh) (r:23.3.20/40.23.5/2.35.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
bang = (t:det) (w:what) (d:Question word, what; it also begins the phrases bang hangin, why, and bang ci, how.) (e:~ hiam? ~ maw? ~ ci?/a sepna khempeuh thamanin ~ ngah ahi hiam | what does he gain from all his work/Tu lai khang mite ~ tawh ka genteh ding hiam | to what shall I compare this generation/Topa lungdam sakna in ~ ahi hiam | what is it that pleases the Lord) (r:49.5.10/44.21.22/21.3.9/40.11.16)
bang = (t:adj) (w:like) (d:Like, similar to; placed after the thing with which something is compared.) (e:kote mah ~ na suak ding uh hi/Kote mah na ~ ta hi | you have become like us/nguntang na ~ ngei a | you were once like pure silver/a nidanga mah hong ~ hi | it became as it was before) (r:1.34.15/23.14.10/23.1.22/11.13.6)
Bang = (t:det) (w:what) (d:The word bang, what, written with a capital at the start of a clause; Bang hang hiam cih leh, literally if one asks for what reason, means because or for.) (e:~ hang hiam cih leh/~ hih ka hi hiam | what have I done/~ zah a lian laimalte tawh | with what large letters/~ hangin kei hong peel a | why do you hide from me) (b:bang) (r:29.1.19/24.31.22/9.17.29/48.6.11/18.13.24) (q:draft)
banga = (t:adv) (w:like/as/such) (d:Like, in the manner of; bang with the linking ending a before a verb or describing word, often in tua banga and hih banga, in that way, like this.) (e:Tua ~ a paih khit ciangin/namsau ~ a leii uh a tatte | those who sharpen their tongues like swords/Lebanon gam taamtaak sing ~ a sang | tall like a cedar of Lebanon/Hih ~ na gamtat nadingin | for you to act like this/hih ~ geelna tampi nei hi | he has many such plans) (b:bang) (r:42.5.6/1.19.7/19.64.3/19.37.35/1.20.10/18.23.14) (q:draft)
bangah = (t:adv) (w:at about) (d:At about, after a measure of distance; bang, like or about, with the place marker ah.) (e:thal lot khat tan ~ a ta nungngatin/tai zanih ciang ~ tuikhang bangin a luang hi | it flowed like a flood for about two hundred miles) (b:bang) (r:1.21.16/66.14.20) (q:draft)
bangah = (t:adv) (w:in what) (d:In what, in what respect, in a question; bang, what, with the place marker ah.) (e:pawlpi dangte sangin ~ a gina lozaw) (b:bang) (r:47.12.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangbang = (t:pron) (w:whatever) (d:Whatever, anything at all; often bangbang hita leh, whatever it may be.) (e:nang cih ~ hoihsa ing/~ hita leh ama kisap zah | whatever it may be, as much as he needs/~ gimna, ~ natna hita leh | whatever disaster or whatever disease it may be/ama nitna in ~ hita leh | whatever his uncleanness may be/mipa’ cih ~ a min hi pahpah hi | whatever the man called it, that was its name) (s:thuthu) (r:5.15.8/1.2.19/11.8.37/3.22.5)
bangbang = (t:conj) (w:as/like) (d:Just as, exactly in keeping with; placed after a verb or noun, as in a piak zawh bangbang, as much as he is able to give.) (e:Pasian thukham ~ na zui in/a piak zawh ~ pia ding hi | he shall give as much as he is able/hong dawn’ kikna ~ ka hong gen ding hi | I will tell you just as he answers/a piak zawh ~ pia-in | giving as much as he is able) (r:3.14.22/24.42.4/3.14.30)
bangbangin = (t:conj) (w:just as/according to whatever/exactly as) (d:In exactly the way that, in keeping with whatever; placed after a verb or noun.) (e:Ama’ deih ~ na gamta un/thukham laibu sunga a kigelh ~ | just as it is written in the Book of the Law/Jonadab’ hong sawl ~ ka mang uh a | we obeyed just as Jonadab commanded us/Pa’ vaihawmna ~ a gamta ding ka hi hi | I do exactly as the Father has directed/Keima gamtat ~ a gamta ding na hi uh hi | you will do just as I have done) (b:bangbang) (r:24.39.12/24.35.10/6.8.34/43.14.31/26.24.24) (q:draft)
bangbangin = (t:adv) (w:however/in whatever way) (d:However, in whatever way; with a following zongin, no matter how.) (e:Mite in ~ ai a san zongin) (b:bangbang) (r:20.16.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangbangun = (t:conj) (w:just as/whatever) (d:Just as or whatever, said of several people; bangbang with the ending in and the plural u, as in a omzia bangbangun, just as they were, and a ut bangbangun, whatever they please.) (e:a omzia ~ a om paisuak ding/a omzia ~ nungta uh hen | let them live just as they were/na ut ~ gamta un | do whatever you please/A ut ~ suntangpi-in gamtat ding | to do as they please in broad daylight) (b:bangbang) (r:46.7.20/61.2.13/46.7.17/21.11.9) (q:draft)
bangbek = (t:adv) (w:only as/just according to) (d:Exactly as and in no other way; bang, like, with bek, only.) (e:Topa’ deihna ~ hizaw hi) (r:20.16.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangci = (t:adv) (w:how) (d:Question word, how, in what way; also with the ending in, bangci-in.) (e:~ a gamtat ding/gamdang ah ~ sak thei ding i hi hiam | how can we sing in a foreign land/Hih thute ~ piang zo ding ahi hiam | how can these things be/Hih thu in ~ piang ding ahi hiam | how will this be/tua mawhna sungah ~-in i hing lai ding hiam | how can we still live in that sin) (s:koici) (r:19.137.4/43.3.9/42.1.34/45.6.2)
bangci = (t:phrase) (w:how come) (e:~ a kici thei hiam) (r:42.20.41)
bangcia = (t:adv) (w:why) (e:~ hici gamtat na hi hiam) (r:1.3.13) for what reason or purpose
bangcih = (t:adv) (w:what/how) (d:The form of bangci, how, used before ding and thei; bangcih ding asks what is to be done or what one will do.) (e:Hih mite ~ ding ihi hiam/~ ding na hi uh hiam | what will you do/midikte in ~ thei nawn ding hiam | what can the righteous still do/sing kawm lakah ~ ding na hi hiam | what will you do in the thickets/khat mansuah leh ~ ding ahi hiam | if he loses one, what will he do) (b:bangci) (r:44.4.16/28.9.5/19.11.3/24.12.5/42.15.4) (q:draft)
Bangcih = (t:name) (w:Bangcih)
bangcite = (t:pron) (w:who/what kind) (d:What sort of person, which one; bangci, how, with te, as in a bangcite ahi hiam, which asks who it is that fits a description.) (e:nasem i cih a ~ ahi hiam/A pil a citak nasempa i cih a ~ ahi hiam | who then is the wise and faithful servant) (b:bangci) (r:40.24.45/42.12.42) (q:draft)
bangin = (t:adv) (w:accordingly) (d:According to, in keeping with what is named before it; tua mah bangin, in that same way, accordingly.) (e:amau gamtatna ~ thukkik in/Noah in tua mah ~ hih hi | Noah did accordingly/Tua mah ~ piang pah hi | and so it happened/Pasian in Noah a thu piaksa ~ | as God had commanded Noah) (b:bang) (r:25.3.64/1.6.22/1.1.7/1.7.9)
bangin = (t:adv) (w:therefore) (d:In tua mah bangin, so then, therefore, drawing a conclusion from what has been said.) (e:Tua mah ~ a hehpih nopte a hehpih hi | therefore he has mercy on those he wants to have mercy on) (r:45.9.18)
bangin = (t:ppm) (w:like so/like/as) (d:Marker placed after a noun or clause: like, as, in the way of.) (e:singkungno ~ hong sel kik hi/numei nausuak na a sa ~ amaute liinggawp uh hi | they trembled like a woman in labor/Pasian’ lim ~ amah piangsak hi | he created him in the likeness of God/na Pa uh a migi mah ~ | just as your Father is perfect) (b:bang) (r:18.14.9/19.48.6/1.1.27/40.5.48)
banginah = (t:conj) (w:just as/as) (d:Just as; bangin, like, with ah, introducing the first half of a comparison.) (e:mai-ah a ham loh ~) (b:bangin) (r:44.8.32) (q:draft)
bangkeek = (t:conj) (w:as if/just as though) (d:bang, like, with keek; in the same verse also written as two words, bang keekin) (e:molhtumin a zang ding ~) (r:23.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangkhat = (t:pron) (w:something/anything) (d:Something, anything; often followed by peuhpeuh or teitei, something or other.) (e:Amaute’ nek ding ~ peuhpeuh pia un/~ teitei a piak ding kisam hi | he too must have something to offer) (a:bangmah) (r:40.14.16/58.8.3) (q:draft)
bangkik = (t:v) (w:be restored/become as before) (d:To be once more as it was; bang, be like, with kik, again, usually after a ngei or a ngeina, its former state.) (e:damin a ngeina ~ hi/kumpipa’ khut a ngei ~ a | the king’s hand became as it was before/a thahat pen hun laitak a ~ ding hi | he will be again as in his strongest days/a ngei uh ~ ding uh a | they will be as they were before) (b:bang) (r:41.3.5/18.33.25/11.13.6/26.16.55) (q:draft)
bangkikin = (t:v) (w:being restored/becoming as before) (d:The verb bangkik, be as before, with the linking ending in; a ngei bangkikin, becoming again as it was.) (e:a ngei ~ amah a siang hi/nangma cilesa a ngei hong ~ | your flesh will become as it was before) (b:bangkik) (r:12.5.14/12.5.10) (q:draft)
banglai = (t:todo) (q:draft, in a them banglai khempeuh, perhaps every little bit that still remains, one verse only)
banglel = (t:adj) (w:just like/no better than) (d:No more than, just like; bang, like, with lel, merely, placed after a noun and a.) (e:hih uisi a ~ mi khat in/Faro pen tua ~ ahi hi | Pharaoh is just like that) (r:10.16.9/12.18.21) (q:draft)
bangmah = (t:pron) (w:nothing/anything) (d:With a negative verb, nothing or not anything; bang, what, with the emphatic mah.) (e:sung tawntung ~ mu loin/~ ka kisam kei ding hi | I shall lack nothing/naupang in ~ thei lo hi | the boy knew nothing/~ in amaute tuksak zo lo hi | nothing can make them stumble/hih manna sim loh ~ om peuhmah lo hi | there is nothing at all except this manna) (a:bangkhat) (b:bang) (r:44.9.9/20.21.30/19.23.1/9.20.39/19.119.165/4.11.6) (q:draft)
bangmahin = (t:adv) (w:in the same way/just so) (d:In that very way, just as; placed after tua or after the person whose conduct is followed.) (e:Noah zong tua ~ gamta a/Tua ~ siampi liante in | in the same way the chief priests/a pa Asa’ gamtat ~ | just as his father Asa had done/kumpi Jehoiakim ~ Pasian’ hoihsak lohte hong sem hi | he did what God disapproved, just as King Jehoiakim had) (s:kibangmahin) (r:1.6.22/40.27.41/14.20.32/24.52.2) (q:draft)
bangmahin = (t:adv) (w:not at all/as nothing) (d:With a negative verb, in no way, as nothing at all.) (e:~ ngaihsun nawn lo uh hi/ngun ~ kingaihsun lo hi | silver was thought of as nothing/A kat ma-in zong ~ kimang lo | even before it burned it was of no use at all) (b:bangmah) (r:28.8.8/11.10.21/14.9.20/26.15.5) (q:draft)
bangmahpi = (t:pron) (w:nothing at all/anything at all) (d:Nothing at all, with a negative verb; bangmah with the strengthening suffix pi.) (e:kei pen ~ ka hihloh hangin) (b:bangmah) (r:47.12.11) (q:draft)
bangpi = (t:adv) (d:In tua bangpi-in, being like that, that being so; it introduces a question that expects the answer no.) (e:Tua ~-in hih gam luah thei ding/Tua ~-in kote hong kihon ding ahi hiam | that being so, shall we be saved) (b:bang) (r:26.33.26/23.64.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangpi = (t:pron) (w:what) (d:What great thing, what at all; bang, what, with the augmentative pi.) (e:~ hi zenzen ka hi uh hiam) (b:bang) (r:46.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangpian = (t:adv) (w:something like/a kind of) (d:Something like, something that looks like it; placed after a noun.) (e:a kibawl suangphahpek ~ om hi) (r:2.24.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangsak = (t:v) (w:make like/cause to be like) (d:To make like, to cause to be like; bang with the causative sak, and with kik, make as it was before, restore.) (e:a sak suang ka ~ a/huih mai-a ansi leng ~ in | make them like chaff blown before the wind/Milim a bawl mite pen milimte mah ~ in | make those who make idols just like the idols/a nidang hun uh ka ~ kik ding hi | I will make their former days as they were/nopsaknate a ngei hong ~ kik ta in | restore our fortunes as before) (s:kibangsak/batsak) (b:bang) (r:23.50.7/29.3.1/19.83.13/19.135.18/19.126.4) (q:draft)
bangsakin = (t:v) (w:making like/restoring) (d:The verb bangsak, make like, with the linking ending in; a ngei bangsakin, making as it was before.) (e:Ammon mite a ngei ~ ka hausakkik ding hi/Moab gam a ngei ~ ka hausakkik ding hi | I will restore Moab and make it rich again) (b:bangsak) (r:24.49.6/24.48.47) (q:draft)
bangsakkik = (t:v) (w:restore) (d:To make a thing as it was before, to restore it to its former state; usually after a ngei, as before.) (e:nopsaknate a ngei hong ~ ta in/biakinn a ngei a ~ dingin | to restore the temple to what it was/Jakob’ nopsaknate a ngeina na ~ hi | you restored the fortunes of Jacob/a nidang hun lai mah uh ka ~ ding hi | I will restore them to their former days/kote ka ngei uh hong ~ inla | restore us to what we were) (s:batsakkik) (b:bangsak) (r:19.126.4/14.24.12/19.85.1/29.3.1/19.85.4) (q:draft)
bangsakkikin = (t:v) (w:restoring) (d:The verb bangsakkik, make as it was before, with the linking ending in.) (e:note na ngei uh hong ~/A siate a ngei ~ ka dingsakkik ding hi | I will restore its ruins and set it up again) (b:bangsakkik) (r:5.30.3/44.15.16) (q:draft)
bangsakkikte = (t:n) (w:restorers) (d:Those who restore; bangsakkik, restore, with the plural te.) (e:mun siate a ngei a ~) (b:bangsakkik) (r:23.58.12) (q:draft)
bangsakzo = (t:v) (w:make like) (d:To be able to make like; bangsak, make like, with zo, be able or succeed.) (e:beel sunga tuiso ~ a) (b:bangsak) (r:18.41.31) (q:draft)
bangta = (t:v) (w:have become like/be like now) (d:To have become like; bang, be like, with ta, which marks a change that has come about.) (e:Kote mah na ~ hi/tu-in ahihleh tui mawkmawk na ~ hi | but now you have become like mere water) (s:kibangta) (b:bang) (r:23.14.10/23.1.22) (q:draft)
bangtan = (t:adv) (w:how long/how much) (d:Question word of extent, how far or how much; with vei or sawt it asks how long.) (e:~ vei paupau ding na hi hiam/na thupiak ding ~ sawtlai ding ahi hiam | how long will it be before you give the order/Tua bang thu ~ vei gengen ding a | how long will you keep saying such things) (s:bangtanvei) (r:18.8.2/10.2.26) (q:draft)
bangtanvei = (t:adv) (w:how long) (d:Question word, for how long a time; also written bangtan vei.) (e:~ hai omom nuam lai na hi/~ pilna thudon loin om ding | how long will you pay no heed to wisdom/~ thu gengenin, kei hong gimsak ding | how long will you torment me with talk) (s:bangtan) (r:20.1.22/18.19.2) (q:draft)
bangte = (t:pron) (w:such ones/such things) (d:People or things like that; bang with the plural te, used as tua bangte, such ones.) (e:tua ~ tawh khial kha kei un/Vantung Gam in tua ~ gam ahi hi | the kingdom of heaven belongs to such as these/Tua ~ hoih het lo hi | such things are not good at all/tua ~ ka en tawntung hi | I have always looked after such ones) (b:bang) (r:20.7.25/42.18.16/40.19.14/59.4.16/18.31.18) (q:draft)
bangteng = (t:pron) (w:what/what things) (d:What, of all the things concerned; hih bangteng, all this, such things.) (e:~ in Topa lungkimsak ahi hiam/nangma tungah hih ~ hong tungsak hi | has brought all this upon you/hih ~ a thuak ding kisam hi lo ahi hiam | did he not have to suffer all this/hih ~ a thuak ka hi hi | I am suffering all this) (b:bang) (r:49.5.10/26.23.30/42.24.26/55.1.12) (q:draft)
bangtumlo = (t:n) (w:nonsense/folly) (d:aimless or senseless talk, apparently bang, what, tum, aim at, lo, not) (e:~ teng tawh kipan pah) (r:21.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangtung = (t:n) (w:lintel) (d:In bangtung zawl, the beam over a doorway, the lintel; apparently bang, wall, with tung, top.) (e:a ~ zawl leh kongkhak khuamte in/~ zawl-ah tuang ding uh a | they will perch on the lintel) (s:bangtungzawl) (r:11.6.31/36.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangtungzawl = (t:n) (w:lintel/top of the doorframe) (d:The beam across the top of a door, above the two doorposts.) (e:~ leh kongkhak khuam nihte nuh un/inn kongkhak khuam nihte leh ~ nuh ding uh hi | they shall smear the two doorposts and the lintel of the house/~ leh kongkhak khuam nih tunga sisan | the blood on the lintel and the two doorposts) (s:kongtungzawl/bangtung) (r:2.12.22/2.12.7/2.12.23) (q:draft)
bangun = (t:conj) (w:as) (d:As, in the way that; the marker bangin with the plural u, used when the subject is several people.) (e:na gensa ~ Topa va bia un/Note tungah hong kibawl ding na deih ~ | as you want others to do to you/adang mite a ihmut ~ eite ihmu loin | let us not sleep as others sleep/Note in hoih na sakpen ~ ka gamta ding hi | I will do as seems best to you/nong ngetna ~ thu ka ngen ding a | I will pray as you have asked) (b:bang) (r:2.12.31/42.6.31/52.5.6/10.18.4/24.42.4)
bangzah = (t:adv) (w:how much/how many/how) (d:Asks or exclaims about amount or degree, how much or how many; bangzah takin sang is how high.) (e:Meiite ~ takin sang ahi hiam/a kham val seeng ~ na khawm uh hiam | how many baskets of leftovers did you gather/Na nuntak kum ~ pha ta a hi hiam | how many years have you lived/na sepnate ~ takin lian | how great are your works/na teen’na mun ~ takin etlawm ahi hiam | how lovely is your dwelling place) (r:18.35.5/19.84.1/40.16.9/1.47.8/19.92.5) (q:draft)
bangzaha = (t:adv) (w:how/how much) (d:How, how much; bangzah with a, placed before a describing word, as in bangzaha lian, how great.) (e:vangliatna ~ lian ahi zongin) (b:bangzah) (r:49.1.19/49.1.18) (q:draft)
bangzahin = (t:adv) (w:how/how much/however much) (d:How, how much, in exclamations and questions of degree; with hangin, however much.) (e:leitung khempeuhah na min ~ lian/Mihingte in ~ i hahkat hangin | however hard we humans try/~ hoihin nuam ahi hiam | how good and pleasant it is/Hih mun ~ lamdang | how awesome is this place/na puanbukte uh ~ hoih ahi hiam | how beautiful are your tents) (b:bangzah) (r:19.8.9/21.8.17/19.133.1/1.28.17/4.24.5) (q:draft)
bangzahta = (t:adv) (w:how much/how greatly/however much) (d:Emphatic form of bangzah, how much, used in exclamations and questions, and with hangin for however much.) (e:na itna kip ~ in manpha/~-in mi khat a hauh hangin | however rich a person may be/Nangma bawlnate ~-in dipkuathuai | how awesome are your deeds/~-in a sazang khauh ahi hiam | how strong are its muscles) (b:bangzah) (r:19.36.7/42.12.15/19.66.3/18.40.16) (q:draft)
bangzahtakin = (t:adv) (w:how/how much) (d:How, how much, asking about degree; bangzah, how much, with takin.) (e:~ lamdang ahi hiam) (b:bangzah) (r:22.5.9) (q:draft)
bangzahvei = (t:adv) (w:how much more/how many times) (d:How many times, how much more; bangzah, how much, with vei, times.) (e:note in ~ a manpha zaw) (r:42.12.24) (q:draft)
bangzia = (t:see) <bangzia-in>
bangzia-in = (t:adv) (w:in the manner/in the way) (d:bangzia, manner or way, with the ending in; mostly in hih bangzia-in, in this way, like this) (e:hih ~ na om ding uh/tu-a ~ mi khempeuh tungah sihna hong tung hi | in this way death came to all people/hih ~ ciamtehin ka hih ngeina ahi hi | it is my custom to mark them in this way/Hih ~ na gamtatna uh adang tampi | many other things that you do in this way/a manpha mahmah nate hih ~ hong pia a | in this way he has given us very precious things) (s:danin) (r:52.5.18/45.5.12/53.3.17/41.7.13/61.1.4) (q:draft)
Banhadad = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hadad) (d:name of several kings of Aram who ruled in Damascus, among them the one defeated by Ahab at Aphek) (r:11.20.30)
Bani = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bani) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite of the line of Merari and the head of a family that returned from the exile) (e:a pa Amzi, a pa ~, a pa Shemer) (r:13.6.46/15.2.10) (q:draft)
banin = (t:v) (w:reach/border on/touch) (d:ban, reach, with the linking ending in: reaching to, bordering on or touching; van banin is reaching up to the sky) (e:leilu lamah Asher ~ nisuahna lamah Issakhar ban/a khuapite lianin van ~ ki-uum hi | the cities are large and walled up to the sky/khat’ kha in kawm ~ | the wing of one touching the wall/sakol kamkaih ~ a luang hi | it flowed as high as the horses' bridles/a sangna mun panin hong ~ kei hong la a | he reached down from on high and took me) (b:ban) (r:6.17.10/5.1.28/11.6.27/66.14.20/10.22.17) (q:draft)
banin = (t:adv) (w:one after another/in succession/in turn) (d:used in the expression a ban banin: one following the other, in turn, step by step) (e:khat khit khat a ban ~ kithat a/giahphual a ban ~ sat uh a | they camped at one place after another/inn khatah a ban ~ pawi bawlin | holding feasts in one house after another/Mangmuhna a ban ~ pia-in | giving one vision after another/a patna panin a ban ~ gen a | he told it in order from the beginning) (s:banbanin/kizomin) (r:28.7.7/26.7.5/2.17.1/18.1.4/28.12.10/44.11.4) (q:draft)
bankap = (t:v) (w:shoot at) (d:shoot at, said of the archer in a tuahkhak peuh a bankap, who shoots at whoever he meets; the second part is kap, shoot) (e:a tuahkhak peuh a ~ thaltawipa) (r:20.26.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
banna = (t:n) (w:affected part/affected article/place reached) (d:ban, reach, with na: the thing or place that something has got onto; natna a banna is the article or stone affected by the disease or mold) (e:natna a ~ suang lakhia-in/natna a ~ na pen ni sagih sung koihcip | isolate the affected article for seven days/natna a ~ pen mei tawh na hal ding | you must burn whatever has the mold/natna a ~ mun balkhia ding hi | he is to tear out the affected part) (b:ban) (r:3.14.40/3.13.54/3.13.50/3.13.57/3.13.56) (q:draft, low confidence)
bansak = (t:v) (w:cause to reach/let overtake/bring upon) (d:ban, reach, with sak, cause: make something reach or come upon someone) (e:na hehna so amaute ~ in) (b:ban) (r:19.69.24) (q:draft)
bansau = (t:adj) (w:long-sleeved) (d:ban, arm, with sau, long; puantualpi bansau is the long-sleeved robe of Joseph and of Tamar, the ornate robe of the NIV) (e:adingin puantualpi ~ khat bawlsak hi/puantualpi ~ puakin a pa uh’ kiangah paipih uh | they took the long-sleeved robe to their father/ama silh puantualpi ~ balkek hi | she tore the long-sleeved robe she was wearing) (r:1.37.3/10.13.19/1.37.32) (q:draft)
bantan = (t:v) (w:cut off/strike off) (d:of a sword, strike an arm so as to cut it; apparently ban, arm, with tan, cut off) (e:Namsau in a ban ~ hen la) (r:38.11.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
bante = (t:n) (w:arms) (d:ban, arm, with the plural te) (e:A awm leh a ~ ngun tawh kibawl a) (s:baante) (b:ban) (r:27.2.32) (q:draft)
banto = (t:v) (w:reach up to/reach) (d:ban, reach, with to, upward: reach up as far as the sky, the clouds or heaven) (e:na thumanna in meiipi ~ hi/a lutang in meii lak a ~ zongin | though his head reaches the clouds/a siangtho ama teen’na ~ hi | it reached his holy dwelling place/vantung dong na ~ a | you reach up to the sky) (b:ban) (r:19.57.10/18.20.6/14.30.27/27.4.22) (q:draft)
banzo = (t:v) (w:reach/attain/equal/match) (d:ban, reach, with zo, be able: manage to reach, come up to or be equal to; with kei or lo, cannot reach, falls short of) (e:tua vantung nangawn na ~ kei hi/hih paakte ~ nai lo lai hi | was still not equal to these flowers/khangno dangte ~ kei kha zenzen leteh | if you should fall short of the other young men/galkidona in note’ singgah le ante hong ~ hi | war has reached your fruit and crops) (s:batzawh/tunzo) (b:ban) (r:18.11.8/40.6.29/27.1.10/23.16.9) (q:draft)
baptaiz = (t:v) (w:baptize) (d:loanword from English: immerse a person in water as the sign of repentance and faith) (e:Filip in a ~ hi/note lakah kuamah ka ~ kei hi | I baptized none of you/Midangte ka ~ lam ka thei kei hi | I do not know whether I baptized anyone else/Johan hong kilang a, gampa lakah ~ a | John appeared, baptizing in the wilderness/tui sungah ~ dingin kei hong sawlpa | the one who sent me to baptize in water) (s:tuiphum/phum) (r:44.8.38/46.1.16/46.1.14/41.1.4/43.1.33) (q:draft)
Baptaiz = (t:name) (w:Baptist) (d:title of John, who baptized in the Jordan; written Baptaiz-pa Johan, John the Baptist) (r:40.3.1)
baptaizna = (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:the act of baptizing or of being baptized; baptaizna mun is the place of baptizing) (e:~ khat thuak ding ka nei hi/Johan ~ thu in vantung pan hong piang | was the baptism of John from heaven/Johan’ ~ ka ngah uh hi | we received the baptism of John/Paul’ min tawh ~ ka ngah hi | I was baptized in the name of Paul) (s:tuiphumna/kibaptaizna/kituiphumna/bataizna) (b:baptaiz) (r:42.12.50/43.1.28/41.11.30/44.19.3/46.1.15) (q:draft)
baptaiznate = (t:n) (w:baptisms) (d:baptaizna, baptism, with the plural te; baptaiznate thuhilhna is teaching about baptisms) (e:~ thuhilhna, khutngakna, misite’ thawhkikna) (b:baptaizna) (r:58.6.1) (q:draft)
baptaizpa = (t:n) (w:Baptist/baptizer) (d:baptaiz, baptize, with the male ending pa: the man who baptizes; title of John the Baptist, written with a capital) (e:~ Johan a cihna ahih lam/~ Johan in an lum ne lo | John the Baptist came eating no bread/tuapa in Kha Siangtho sungah ~ ahi hi | he is the one who baptizes with the Holy Spirit/~ Johan in nangma kiangah kote hong dongsak hi | John the Baptist sent us to ask you) (s:tuiphumpa/Tuiphumpa) (b:baptaiz) (r:40.17.13/40.14.8/42.7.33/43.1.33/42.7.20) (q:draft)
Baptaizpa = (t:name) (w:Baptist) (d:title of John son of Zechariah, who baptized in the Jordan and prepared the way for Jesus) (b:Baptaiz) (r:40.17.13/40.14.2)
Bar = (t:see) <Bar-Zeisu>
Bar-Zeisu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bar-Jesus) (d:Jewish sorcerer and false prophet at Paphos on Cyprus, also called Elymas) (e:a min ~ kici thuzuau kamsangpa khat) (r:44.13.6) (q:draft)
Barabbas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barabbas) (d:prisoner, a rebel and murderer, whom Pilate released instead of Jesus) (r:42.23.19/40.27.16)
Barak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barak) (d:son of Abinoam from Kedesh in Naphtali, who with Deborah defeated Sisera) (r:7.4.12/7.5.1)
Barakhel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barakel) (d:a Buzite, father of Elihu who spoke to Job) (r:18.32.2)
Barakhiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Berekiah) (d:father of the Zechariah who was murdered between the temple and the altar) (r:40.23.35)
Barekhel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barakel) (d:a Buzite, father of Elihu; another spelling of <Barakhel>) (r:18.32.6)
Bariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bariah) (d:son of Shemaiah, a descendant of David in the line of Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.22)
Barjesuh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bar-Jesus) (d:Jewish sorcerer and false prophet at Paphos; another spelling of <Bar-Zeisu>) (r:44.13.6)
Barkos = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barkos) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.53/16.7.55)
Barnabas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barnabas) (d:Levite from Cyprus, first named Joseph, who was a companion of Paul on his first missionary journey) (r:44.15.37/44.11.25)
Barnbas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barnabas) (d:another spelling of <Barnabas>, the companion of Paul) (r:44.13.43)
barnea = (t:see) <Kadesh-barnea>
Barsabbas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barsabbas) (d:name of two men: Joseph called Barsabbas, put forward with Matthias, and Judas called Barsabbas, sent to Antioch with Silas) (r:44.1.23/44.15.22)
Bartholomai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartholomew) (d:one of the twelve apostles of Jesus) (r:41.3.18/40.10.3)
Bartholomew = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartholomew) (d:one of the twelve apostles of Jesus; another spelling of <Bartholomai>) (r:40.10.3/41.3.18)
Bartimai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartimaeus) (d:blind beggar, son of Timaeus, whom Jesus healed near Jericho) (r:41.10.46)
Bartimias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartimaeus) (d:blind beggar whom Jesus healed near Jericho; another spelling of <Bartimai>) (r:41.10.46)
Baruk = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Baruch) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Neriah, scribe of the prophet Jeremiah) (r:24.32.16/16.10.6)
Barzillai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barzillai) (d:Gileadite from Rogelim who provided for David when he fled from Absalom) (r:10.19.32/10.19.31)
basan = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:lentil) (d:a pulse listed after bepi, beans, among the foods brought to David; apparently the same word as besan) (e:an, ankan, bepi leh ~) (s:besan) (r:10.17.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
Basemath = (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Basemath) (d:name of two women: a daughter of Ishmael who was a wife of Esau, and a daughter of Solomon who married Ahimaaz) (r:1.36.3)
Bashan = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bashan) (d:fertile region east of the Jordan and north of Gilead, the kingdom of Og) (r:13.5.11/19.135.11)
Bashante = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bashan) (d:Bashan with the plural te, in Gilead leh Bashante, the lands of Gilead and Bashan) (b:Bashan) (r:6.17.5)
Bashon = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bashan) (d:another spelling of <Bashan>, the region east of the Jordan) (r:5.3.10)
Bassha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Baasha) (d:son of Ahijah of the tribe of Issachar, king of Israel who reigned in Tirzah) (r:11.15.33)
Basshebeth = (t:see) <Josheb-Basshebeth>
bat = (t:v) (w:reach/extend to) (d:form of ban, reach, used before a following word such as mateng, dongin or loh: reach as far as a place or point) (e:Medeba ciang dong a ~ mateng/a khetphim in lei a ~ dongin | until the tent peg reached the ground/Tua sing in meiipi a ~ dongin khangto a | that tree grew up until it reached the clouds/Pasian’ khuavak in a ~ lohna | where the light of God does not reach) (r:4.21.30/7.4.21/26.31.10/18.25.3) (q:draft)
bat = (t:v) (w:be like/resemble/become like) (d:form of bang, be like, used before a following word such as hangin, nading or kei) (e:gammang tulak a ~ ngei hangin/na mawhnate uh puansan a ~ hangin | though your sins are like scarlet/a cing nei lo tuute a ~ loh nadingin | so that they will not be like sheep without a shepherd/ka khut a ngei a ~ nadingin | so that my hand may be as it was before/naupang na ~ kei uhleh | unless you become like children) (s:suun) (a:kilamdang) (r:26.36.34/23.1.18/4.27.17/11.13.6/40.18.3) (q:draft)
bat = (t:v) (w:owe) (d:form of ba, owe, used before a following word: be in debt; sum bat is money owed) (e:hong sum ~ taang dingin/no-a’ hong ~ peuhmah na maisak ding uh hi | you must cancel whatever he owes you) (r:18.22.6/5.15.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
bataizna = (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:apparently another spelling or a misprint of baptaizna) (e:Khazih sungah ~ a ngah mi) (s:baptaizna/tuiphumna) (r:48.3.27) (q:draft)
bate = (t:n) (w:debtors) (d:ba, owe, with the plural te: those who owe; sum bate, those who owe money) (e:a topa’ sum ~ a vekpi-un sam a/a topa’ sum a ~ khat khatin sam a | he called his master's debtors one by one) (s:leibate) (a:sumneite) (b:ba) (r:42.16.5/35.2.6) (q:draft)
Bathsheba = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Bathsheba) (d:daughter of Eliam and wife of Uriah the Hittite, later wife of David and mother of Solomon) (r:10.11.3/11.1.16)
Bathshua = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Bathshua) (d:Canaanite wife of Judah, mother of Er, Onan and Shelah) (r:13.2.3)
batin = (t:n) (w:as a debt) (d:bat, owe, with in: keima batin seh, charge it to me as my debt) (e:keima ~ na seh in) (b:bat) (r:57.1.18) (q:draft)
batkhak = (t:v) (w:become like) (d:bat, be like, with khak, happen to; na batkhak loh nadingun, so that you do not come to be like them) (e:siate na ~ loh nadingun kidawm un) (r:42.20.46) (q:draft, low confidence)
batkim = (t:v) (w:all be like) (d:bat, be like, with kim, every one: all become like someone) (e:keimah nong ~ nadingun) (r:44.26.29) (q:draft)
batna = (t:n) (w:likeness/resemblance) (d:noun of bang, be like: the fact of being like something, as in zukham a batna, her being like a drunk person) (e:zukham a ~ ka mu hi/tu-in Eden Huan a ~ | its now being like the garden of Eden) (s:kibatna) (b:bat) (r:66.17.6/26.36.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
batna = (t:n) (w:debt) (d:the owing of a debt; a batna pa is the one to whom the debt is owed, the creditor) (e:a ~ pa un a nih tuakun) (s:leibatna/leiba) (b:bat) (r:42.7.42) (q:draft, low confidence)
batnate = (t:n) (w:creditors/debts) (d:batna, debt, with the plural te; ka lei batnate, those to whom I am in debt) (e:ka lei ~ koi pen ahi hiam) (s:leibatnate) (b:batna) (r:23.50.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
batsak = (t:v) (w:make like) (d:cause to be like, bat, be like, with the causative sak; a ngei batsak kik, make as it was before, restore) (e:suangkang satvui a ~ ciangin/biakinn a ngei ~ kik ding ngaihsun hi | he decided to make the temple as it was before) (s:bangsak) (b:bat) (r:23.27.9/14.24.4) (q:draft)
batsak = (t:v) (w:put on/fasten on) (d:put an ornament on someone, in the verse a ring on the nose) (e:a nak tungah nakbah ka ~ a) (s:butsak) (r:1.24.47) (q:draft, low confidence)
batsakkik = (t:v) (w:restore) (d:batsak, make like, with kik, again; a ngei batsakkik is to make a thing as it was before) (e:biakinn a ngei ~ ding ngaihsun hi/a ngei ~ nadingin pia uh hi | they gave it for restoring it as it was before) (s:bangsakkik/bawlkik) (b:batsak) (r:14.24.4/14.34.10) (q:draft)
batsuk = (t:v) (w:reach down to) (d:bat, reach, with suk, downward) (e:tau kimciang a ~ theih nadingin) (b:bat) (r:2.27.5) (q:draft)
battheih = (t:v) (w:be able to be like/can become like) (d:bat, form of bang, be like, with theih, can; a battheih nading, so that one may be like or become like) (e:mittaw a ~ nadingin/Khrih’ sawltak taktak a ~ nadingun | so that they may look like true apostles of Christ) (b:bat) (r:43.9.39/47.11.13) (q:draft)
battheihna = (t:n) (d:battheih, can be like, with the noun suffix na; a battheihna dingin, so that it may become like) (e:ciangkhut khat a ~ dingin) (b:battheih) (r:26.37.17) (q:draft)
batzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to reach/attain) (d:bat, reach, with zawh, manage to; with a negative, be beyond what one can reach) (e:kei’ ~ ding hi lo hi/ama muhna in a ~ lohin sang mahmah a | they are too high for his sight to reach) (s:banzo/tunzo) (r:21.7.23/19.10.5) (q:draft)
Bavvai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bavvai) (d:son of Henadad, ruler of half the district of Keilah, who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.18)
bawh = (t:v) (w:pounce on/swoop on/dart at/rush upon) (d:spring suddenly on prey or at something, of an animal or bird; of fighters, fall suddenly on an enemy or a town) (e:humpinelkai bangin a hong ~ hi/muvanlai sa ~ bangin nawh len’ hi | it flies fast like an eagle swooping on prey/na galte uh delhin a nungdalte ~ un la | pursue your enemies and fall on their rear/manlangin hong pai-in Gibeah khua ~ uh hi | they came quickly and rushed upon Gibeah/Mu ak ~ sanga manlang zawin | swifter than a hawk swooping on a chicken) (s:leenlak) (r:25.3.10/7.20.37/18.9.26/6.10.19/25.4.19) (q:draft)
bawh = (t:v) (w:uproot/pull up) (d:pull a plant up or out of the ground, often with zung, root: zung bawh, pull up by the roots) (e:singkung zung ~ bangin mawhneite kibotkhia ding/mi khatpeuh in a phung pan zung ~ a | someone pulls it up by the root from its place/na ~ uh leh, taang kung tawh na botkhawm kha | if you pull them up you may uproot the wheat too/hehna tawh leenggui kizung ~ a | the vine was uprooted in fury) (s:bot/botkhia/zunglot) (a:suan) (r:20.2.22/18.8.18/40.13.29/26.19.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawhhuan = (t:v) (w:rush at/fall upon) (d:spring on a person all together; contains bawh, pounce on) (e:kiko-in Stefen ~ uh a) (r:44.7.57) (q:draft)
bawhin = (t:v) (w:pounce on/seize/snatch) (d:bawh with the linking suffix in, rushing upon and seizing, followed by another verb) (e:amah in nang hong ~ na buk panin/Bang hang in van kinusiate ~ | why did you pounce on the plunder/khagilo in Saul hong ~ | an evil spirit came forcefully on Saul) (b:bawh) (r:19.52.5/9.15.19/9.18.10) (q:draft)
bawhkhiat = (t:v) (w:uproot/pluck out/tear away) (d:bawh, pull up or off by force, with khiat, out; before sak, tear something away from someone) (e:Suan hun om a, ~ hun om hi/Tua leenggui ~ nadingin | in order to pull up that vine/Asherah nusian milimte hong ~ sakin | uprooting your Asherah images/Note’ khut panin tuate hong ~ sakin | tearing them from your hands) (s:botkhia/zunglot) (a:suan) (b:bawh) (r:21.3.2/33.5.14/26.17.9/26.13.20) (q:draft)
bawhkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:tear away from) (d:bawhkhiat, tear away, with sak, from or for someone, and in linking it to the following verb) (e:khut panin tuate hong ~) (b:bawhkhiat) (r:26.13.20) (q:draft)
bawhsak = (t:v) (w:pull out/pluck out) (d:bawh, pull up or out, with sak: pull out another person's hair) (e:a sam uh ka ~ gawp hi) (b:bawh) (r:16.13.25) (q:draft)
bawhsat = (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:break a cord or rope by pulling; bawhsat hak, hard to break) (e:kiheek khauhual ~ hak hi) (r:21.4.12) (q:draft)
bawhsuk = (t:v) (w:crouch down/bow down) (d:of an animal about to give birth, crouch down to the ground; suk shows downward movement) (e:lei-ah a ~ hun thei na hi hiam) (r:18.39.3) (q:draft)
bawk = (t:v) (w:swell/be swollen) (d:become swollen, said of feet and other parts of the body; of breasts, fill out) (e:na khe uh zong ~ lo hi/a khe uh zong ~ beek lo hi | nor did their feet swell at all/a khut le a khe a ~ mi khat | a man whose hands and feet were swollen/Ama pumpi khempeuh ~ ahi zongin | whether his whole body would swell/Na nawite zong hoih tak mahin hong ~ a | your breasts also filled out well) (s:pawm) (r:5.8.4/16.9.21/42.14.2/44.28.6/26.16.7) (q:draft)
bawk = (t:n) (w:swelling) (d:a raised place on the skin, examined by the priest for skin disease) (e:a ~ hita leh meima hita leh/a vun sungah a ~ kaang omin | there is a white swelling in the skin/tua in meikangma pan-a ~ hi a | it is a swelling from the burn/ama pumpi vun tungah a ~ ahi a | a swelling on the skin of his body) (r:3.14.56/3.13.10/3.13.28/3.13.2) (q:draft)
bawk = (t:n) (w:cluster/bunch/cake) (d:a cluster of fruit, as leenggah bawk, a bunch of grapes; also a pressed cake of dried fruit, as leenggahkeu bawk, a cake of raisins) (e:nisuh gah ~ pha tawh kibang hi/leenggah ~ khat bek a hiang tawh | a single cluster of grapes with its branch/leenggahkeu ~ nih zong pia uh hi | they also gave him two cakes of raisins/leenggah ~ tawh kibang a | like clusters of grapes) (s:bom) (r:22.7.7/4.13.23/9.30.12/22.7.8) (q:draft)
bawkbak = (t:adv) (w:crawling) (d:in bawkbak a paite, those that move crawling on the ground, reptiles) (e:~ a, paite ahi zongin) (r:45.1.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawkgawp = (t:v) (w:swell up) (d:bawk, swell, with gawp, badly) (e:a ci hong ~ ding hi) (b:bawk) (r:44.28.6) (q:draft)
bawkgawpin = (t:v) (w:swell up) (d:bawkgawp, swell badly, with in linking it to the following verb) (e:ka mitkhute ~ khua ka mu) (b:bawkgawp) (r:18.16.16) (q:draft)
bawkin = (t:v) (w:swell) (d:bawk, swell, with in linking it to the following verb) (e:ka mitkhute ~ hong liahcip hi) (b:bawk) (r:18.16.16) (q:draft)
bawksak = (t:v) (w:give/hold) (d:in pawi bawksak, give a feast for someone; possibly a misprint of bawlsak, make for) (e:adingin pawi khat ~ hi) (r:17.1.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawkte = (t:n) (w:clusters/bunches/cakes) (d:bawk, cluster, with the plural te: leenggah bawkte, clusters of grapes; leenggahkeu bawkte, cakes of raisins) (e:amau’ leenggah ~ a kha hi/min zo ahih ciangin a ~ at ding | since they are ripe, cut the clusters/leenggahkeu ~, leh leenggahzu leh sathau | raisin cakes, wine and oil) (s:bomte) (b:bawk) (r:5.32.32/66.14.18/13.12.40) (q:draft)
bawl = (t:v) (w:make/create) (d:make or form something from material, or bring it into being; thuciamna bawl is make a covenant) (e:tuikhukpi zong ka ~ hi/puan dum bek tawh na ~ ding hi | you shall make it entirely of blue cloth/Amah in singkha sing zawlte ~ a | he made poles of acacia wood/mihingte a mawkna dingin ~ na hi hiam | have you created mankind for nothing/nangmah in leitung na ~ thak hi | you make the earth new) (s:piang/Piangsak) (a:susia) (r:21.2.6/2.28.31/2.37.4/19.89.47/19.104.30)
Bawl = (t:v) (w:make/create) (d:bawl, make, written with a capital of God as Maker: eite hong Bawl Topa, the Lord our Maker) (e:eite hong ~ Topa mai-ah khukdin’ ni) (b:bawl) (r:19.95.6) (q:draft)
bawla = (t:v) (w:making/having made/doing) (d:bawl, make or do, with the linking ending a; another verb follows) (e:buan ~ ka mitah a nuh khit ciangin/Leitung ~ a kipsak Topa | the Lord who made the earth and established it/Thuhoih ~ gamta mi | the person who does good/zawhthawh ~ sum sutte | those who take money by force) (b:bawl) (r:43.9.11/24.33.2/49.6.8/46.6.10) (q:draft)
bawlbawl = (t:v) (w:keep doing/go on doing/continue/be preparing) (d:bawl, do or make, said twice: keep on doing, as in mawhna bawlbawl, go on sinning; in some verses be doing or preparing) (e:mawhna ~ ding ihi hiam/Pasian’ tate in mawhna ~ lo uh hi | the children of God do not keep on sinning/nu-le-pa mawhna ~ uh hi | they keep on committing sexual sin/na hankhuk ding uh a ~ ka hi ta hi | I am now preparing your grave/ka luanghawm kivui nadingin a hong ~ ahi hi | she did it to prepare my body for burial) (b:bawl) (r:45.6.1/28.4.18/62.5.18/34.1.14/40.26.12) (q:draft)
bawlgawp = (t:v) (w:treat roughly/do violently) (d:bawl, do, with gawp, badly or without restraint; zahpih bawlgawp, mock outright) (e:Pasian simmawhin zahpih ~ hi) (b:bawl) (r:18.34.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlgawpna = (t:n) (w:rough treatment/harsh treatment) (d:bawlgawp with the noun suffix na) (e:ka hong zawhthawh ~ ding) (b:bawlgawp) (r:18.33.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlin = (t:v) (w:make/making) (d:form of bawl with the linking suffix in, making and then going on to the next action) (e:singkha sing zawl ~ sumngo tawh/Zeisu in buan ~ mit a vaksak ni | the day Jesus made mud and opened the eyes/Nangma adingin kham khainiang ~ | making gold earrings for you/singkha sing zawlte ~ kham tawh na zut ding a | make poles of acacia wood and overlay them with gold) (b:bawl) (r:2.27.6/43.9.14/22.1.11/2.25.28) (q:draft)
bawlkha = (t:v) (w:make/happen to make) (d:bawl, make, with kha, happen to; bawlkha kei in, take care not to make) (e:tawh thuciamna ~ kei in/a teng mite tawh thuciamna ~ kei inla | do not make a treaty with those who live there) (r:2.34.15/2.34.12) (q:draft)
bawlkhak = (t:v) (w:make/happen to make) (d:form of bawlkha, happen to make, used before loh nading: take care not to make) (e:milim na ~ loh nadingun kidawm un) (b:bawlkha) (r:5.4.23) (q:draft)
bawlkhin = (t:v) (w:have made/have done) (d:bawl, make or do, with khin, already and completely) (e:kiciamna ka ~ hi/Ka hong ~ a, ka hong don ding hi | I have made you and I will care for you/kiciamna khat ~ uh hi | they have taken an oath/a ukpa-in kei hong ~ hi | he has made me ruler/Hih bangin keimah hong ~ na hih manin | because you have done this for me) (s:bawlzo) (b:bawl) (r:18.31.1/23.46.4/44.23.21/1.45.8/19.52.9) (q:draft)
bawlkhit = (t:v) (w:finish doing/have done) (d:bawl, do or make, with khit, finished; bawlkhit ciangin, after doing) (e:teekteekin a ~ uh ciangin/kisiansuahna ka ~ hun ciangin | when I had completed the purification) (s:sepkhit) (r:44.13.29/44.24.18) (q:draft)
bawlkhol = (t:v) (w:prepare/make ready) (d:bawl, make, with khol, beforehand: get something ready in advance, as a way, a place or a city) (e:ama lampi ~ ding hi/Note om nading mun ~ dingin ka pai ding hi | I am going to prepare a place for you/keimah ading pumpi khat na ~ zo hi | you have prepared a body for me/ka giah nading omna mun zong na ~ in | prepare also a place for me to stay/amau om nading khuapi a ~ hi | he has prepared a city for them) (r:19.85.13/43.14.2/58.10.5/57.1.22/58.11.16) (q:draft)
bawlkholh = (t:v) (w:prepare/make ready beforehand) (d:form of bawlkhol used before a following word such as khit or sak) (e:mun ka va ~ khit ciangin/amah a it mite a dingin a ~ saksa | what he has prepared for those who love him) (b:bawlkhol) (r:43.14.3/46.2.9) (q:draft)
bawlkholhna = (t:see) <bawlkholhna-in>
bawlkholhna-in = (t:n) (w:preparation) (d:bawlkhol, make ready beforehand, with the noun suffix na and in: as a preparing of something in advance) (e:pai nading lam a ~ a tuite) (r:66.16.12) (q:draft)
bawlkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore/repair/remake) (d:make again or put right what was spoiled, from bawl, make, and kik, again; used of rebuilding a city, restoring a people and undoing a deed) (e:a ngeina bangin Jerusalem ~ uh hi/a cithei-in ka ~ ding hi | I will restore their fortunes/a ~ nawn kei ding hi | he will not build them up again/sem ding siampite ~ hi | he again made priests to serve/a gamtatnasa a ~ theih nading lampi | a way to undo what he had done) (s:lamkik/puah/bawlpha) (a:susia) (b:bawl) (r:16.3.8/19.28.5/26.16.53/11.13.33/58.12.17) (q:draft)
bawlkikin = (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore) (d:bawlkik, rebuild, with the linking ending in: rebuilding, followed by a further action) (e:Topa’ biakinn ~ kipsak uh hi) (b:bawlkik) (r:14.24.13) (q:draft)
bawlkikzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to repair/be able to restore) (d:bawlkik, make again, with zawh, be able; bawlkikzawh nawn loh, beyond repair) (e:~ nawn loh dongin siatna ngah) (r:20.6.15) (q:draft)
bawlkim = (t:v) (w:do for each one/do for all) (d:bawl, do or make, with kim, every one: do the same for each one) (e:tua bangin na ~ ding uh) (r:4.15.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawllai = (t:v) (w:still do/keep doing/go on doing) (d:bawl, do, with lai, still) (e:amaute in khialhna ~ veve uh) (r:23.26.10) (q:draft)
bawlma = (t:v) (w:before making) (d:bawl, make, with ma, before: before he made) (e:nangawn a ~ pekin kei ka om) (r:20.8.26) (q:draft)
bawlna = (t:n) (w:deed/doing/act/action) (d:what someone does or has done, nominal form of bawl; ka bawlna thu, what I am doing) (e:ka ~ thu na thei kei hi/na ~ a lamdangte khempeuh ka gen ding | I will tell of all your wonderful deeds/ama ~ pha hangin a nuam uh | they were glad because of his good deeds/sepna ~ tawh a mantak ki-it ni | let us love truly with actions) (s:hihna/sepna/gamtatna) (b:bawl) (r:43.13.7/4.22.2/19.9.1/42.13.17/62.3.18) (q:draft)
bawlnasa = (t:v) (w:had made/had done) (d:bawl, make or do, with na and sa, already: what someone did before, or, before mun, the place where something was made before) (e:biakna tau khat a ~ munah/Ka mihingte tungah a ~ hangun | because of what they did to my people) (s:hihsa) (b:bawl) (r:1.13.4/29.3.2) (q:draft)
bawlnate = (t:n) (w:deeds/works/doings) (d:plural of bawlna: the things someone has done, often the mighty works of God) (e:a vanglian nangma ~ taangko ding a/mite’ lak-a a ~ ah amah dipkuat-huai | he is awesome in his deeds among people/a vanglian na ~ kigengen ding hi | your mighty acts will be told/a lamdang na ~ ka sut kikkik uh | we tell of your wonderful deeds again and again) (s:gamtatnate/nasepnate/sepnate/hihnate) (b:bawlna) (r:19.145.6/19.66.5/19.145.4/19.75.1) (q:draft)
bawlnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to do/wish to commit/urge to do) (d:bawl, do, with nop, want, and the noun suffix na; mawh bawlnopna, the desire to do wrong) (e:Mawh ~ lungsim hong neisak kei inla/mawhna ~ panin suakta-in | set free from the desire to sin) (s:gamtatnopna/sepnopna) (r:19.141.4/45.6.22) (q:draft)
bawlpa = (t:n) (w:maker/one who makes) (d:the one who makes or made something: bawl, make, with pa marking a man; paknamtui bawlpa is a perfume-maker and savun bawlpa a tanner) (e:I bil a ~ in khua za lo/paknamtui ~ Hananiah in puah hi | Hananiah the perfume-maker repaired it/savun ~ Simon kiangah | with Simon the tanner/ci-in a ~ kiangah a gen ding | will it say to the one who made it) (s:piangsakpa/seekpa) (b:bawl) (r:19.94.9/44.9.43/16.3.8/45.9.20) (q:draft)
Bawlpa = (t:n) (w:Maker/Creator) (d:title of God written with a capital: the one who made people and all things; often amah a Bawlpa, his Maker) (e:Amah a ~’ tungah Israel lungdam hen/Amah a ~’ mai-ah sitbaang loin | pure before his Maker/Amah a ~ tawh a kido mipa | the man who quarrels with his Maker/amaute a ~’ khut sungah | into the hands of their Creator) (s:Piangsakpa) (b:bawlpa) (r:19.149.2/23.17.7/18.4.17/23.45.9/60.4.19) (q:draft)
bawlpah = (t:v) (w:prepare at once/make immediately) (d:bawl, make or prepare, with pah, at once) (e:manlang taka a na ~ a nasempa) (r:1.18.7) (q:draft)
bawlpha = (t:v) (w:repair/restore/rebuild/strengthen/reform) (d:bawl, make, with pha, good: mend or strengthen a wall, a gate or a place, or put conduct right) (e:na nasepnate uh ~ un/tua kongpi ~-in | he rebuilt that gate/Hih mun ~ ding a | will they restore this place/Millo a muanhuai-in ~ hi | he made the Millo strong) (s:puah/bawlkik) (a:susia) (r:24.18.11/16.4.2/16.3.14/14.32.5) (q:draft)
bawlpha = (t:v) (w:work in/be at work in/make effective/make complete) (d:work on a person with good effect, of God, his word or a good quality: bring someone to a good or finished state) (e:kicing takin hong ~ ta hen/a um note sungah a ~ Pasian’ thu | the word of God at work in you who believe/keimah tungah hong ~ a | he worked in me/eite tungah hong ~ a lian mahmah vangliatna | his very great power at work in us) (r:59.1.4/52.2.13/48.2.7/49.1.19) (q:draft)
bawlphat = (t:v) (w:restore/repair/put right) (d:form of bawlpha used before other words and endings; bawlphat thakna is renewal) (e:~ zawh nawn loh dongin kisia ding/Kha Siangtho’ hong ~ thakna tawh | by the renewing of the Holy Spirit) (b:bawlpha) (r:20.29.1/56.3.5) (q:draft)
bawlphatna = (t:n) (w:working/operation/power at work) (d:noun of bawlphat, make good: effective working, said of the power of God at work) (e:~ bangin keimah hong piak/vanglianpi tawh hong ~ bangin semin | labouring according to his mighty working in me/a ~ vangliatna hangin | by the power of his working) (b:bawlphat) (r:49.3.7/51.1.29/50.3.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlphatna = (t:n) (w:renewal) (d:the making new of a person) (e:Tua ~-ah Grik mi a om kei hi) (b:bawlphat) (r:51.3.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlpih = (t:v) (w:do together with/join in making) (d:bawl, do or make, with pih, together with someone: take part with others in what they do) (e:si theh biaknate ke’n ~ loin) (b:bawl) (r:19.16.4) (q:draft)
bawlpihte = (t:n) (d:bawlpih, make together with, with the plural te: those with whom something is made, in the verse those with whom the covenant was made) (e:kiciamna a ~’ suante zong na hi) (b:bawlpih) (r:44.3.25) (q:draft)
bawlsa = (t:n) (w:creation/what is made) (d:what has been made, above all everything that God created: bawl, make, with sa, already done) (e:Pasian ~ nate/Pasian’ ~ khempeuh in Pasian’ tate | all that God created waits for the children of God/Pasian’ ~ khempeuh nupi nausuak ding bangin | all creation, like a woman about to give birth) (s:piansaksa) (b:bawl) (r:45.8.19/18.14.15/45.8.22)
bawlsa = (t:v) (w:prepared/made) (d:already made or prepared: bawl, make, with sa marking a finished act; placed before a noun it tells what someone has made) (e:nau nek ding ~ hi/amau ~ paknamtui tawi-in hanah | taking the spices they had prepared to the tomb/a ~ meh lim leh an | the tasty food and bread she had made/Amah in a ~ tuipite uk a | he rules the seas he made) (b:bawl) (r:2.23.20/42.24.1/1.27.17/19.95.5)
bawlsak = (t:v) (w:make for/do for/have make) (d:bawl, make or do, with sak: make or do something for someone, or have someone make it; kilemna bawlsak is to make atonement for someone) (e:a huh ding ka ~ ding hi/kei adingin biakinn khat amaute ~ in | have them make a sanctuary for me/ama ading kilemna ~ ding a | he will make atonement for him/pheituamte na ~ ding hi | you shall make undergarments for them) (s:piangsak) (b:bawl) (r:1.2.18/2.25.8/3.6.7/2.28.42)
bawlsakna = (t:n) (w:making/preparing) (d:noun of bawlsak: the making or preparing of something for someone; with mun, the place prepared; with ding, in order to make) (e:ama adingin ka ~ munah/Levi mite’ ading kilemna ~ dingin | to make atonement for the Levites) (b:bawlsak) (r:13.15.12/4.8.12) (q:draft)
bawlsaknasa = (t:adj) (w:prepared) (d:bawlsakna, making for someone, with sa, already: that has been prepared for someone or something) (e:ama adingin a ~ munah) (b:bawlsakna) (r:14.1.4) (q:draft)
bawlsakpa = (t:n) (w:doer/maker) (d:bawlsak, do or make for someone, with pa marking a man: he who did something for someone) (e:note adingin hong ~ in) (b:bawlsak) (r:5.10.21) (q:draft)
bawlsaksate = (t:n) (w:things done for) (d:bawlsak, do or make for someone, with sa, already done, and the plural te: the things that have been done for someone) (e:na lian hong ~ ngaihsun un) (r:9.12.24) (q:draft)
bawlsate = (t:v) (w:made/things made/works) (d:bawlsa with the plural te: the things that someone has made or prepared) (e:Pasian ~/Na khut tawh na ~ khempeuh tungah | over all the works of your hands/ama ~ khempeuh tungah ama hehpihna om | his compassion is on all he has made/a khutmete tawh a ~ amaute in bia | they worship what their fingers have made) (b:bawlsa) (r:1.1.31/19.8.6/19.145.9/23.2.8)
bawlsia = (t:v) (w:persecute/mistreat/oppress) (d:treat someone cruelly, persecute, mistreat or oppress: bawl, do, with sia, bad) (e:a sih dongin ka ~ hi/Uliante in thu om lopi-in kei hong ~ uh | rulers persecute me without cause/~-in a that uh hi | they mistreated and killed them/Mizawngte a ~ aana nei mipa | a ruler who oppresses the poor) (s:nengniam/gawt/gimbawl/gawtbawl) (r:44.22.4/40.22.6/19.119.161/20.28.3) (q:draft)
bawlsiapa = (t:n) (w:persecutor/oppressor) (d:the man who mistreats or persecutes, bawlsia with pa marking a man) (e:pawlpi ~ ka hi hi/mi ~’ khut sung pan | from the hand of the oppressor/A lawmte a ~ in | the man who was mistreating his fellow/Pasian’ pawlpite a ~ ka hih ciangin | because I persecuted the churches of God) (s:nengniampa) (a:bawlsiatpa) (b:bawlsia) (r:50.3.6/20.29.13/24.21.12/44.7.27/46.15.9) (q:draft)
bawlsiasak = (t:v) (w:let oppress/allow to mistreat) (d:bawlsia, mistreat, with sak, cause or allow: let someone mistreat another; in the verses with nawn kei, no longer allow it) (e:a dangte ka ~ nawn kei ding hi/mi gilote ka ~ nawn kei ding hi | I will no longer let the wicked oppress) (b:bawlsia) (r:26.34.22/38.9.8) (q:draft)
bawlsiat = (t:v) (w:persecute/mistreat/oppress) (d:form of bawlsia used before nouns and endings; bawlsiat thuakna, the suffering of persecution) (e:Na hong ~ Zeisu ka hi hi/note hong ~ nadingun hong pia ding uh | they will hand you over to be persecuted/Ka tanute na ~ a | if you mistreat my daughters/Israel mi khat a ~ laitak a muh ciangin | when he saw an Israelite being mistreated) (s:gimbawl/gawtbawl) (b:bawlsia) (r:44.26.15/48.4.29/40.24.9/1.31.50/44.7.24) (q:draft)
bawlsiate = (t:n) (w:persecutors/tormentors/oppressors) (d:those who persecute or mistreat, bawlsia with the plural ending -te) (e:No hong ~ thupha na pia un/kei hong ~ tungah phu hong laksak in | avenge me on my persecutors/Kei hong ~ na zahhuaisak inla | put my persecutors to shame/no hong ~’ khut sungah | into the hands of your tormentors) (s:nengniamte) (b:bawlsia) (r:45.12.14/19.119.84/24.15.15/24.17.18/23.51.23) (q:draft)
bawlsiatin = (t:v) (w:mistreated/oppressed) (d:bawlsiat, mistreat, with the ending in; mi’ bawlsiatin, as ones whom others mistreat) (e:sal suakin mi’ ~ amaute omsak in) (b:bawlsiat) (r:16.4.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlsiatna = (t:n) (w:persecution/mistreatment/oppression/abuse) (d:cruel treatment that someone suffers, above all for the sake of faith: noun of bawlsiat, mistreat; bawlsiatna thuak is to suffer persecution) (e:~ a thuak ding uh hi/~ ahi zongin a thuak ciangin | when they suffer persecution/note in ~ khempeuh ahi zongin | in all your persecutions/nasia takin ~ ka thuaknate | the severe persecutions I endured) (s:kibawlsiatna) (r:55.3.12/40.13.21/53.1.4/55.3.11) (q:draft)
Bawlsiatna = (t:n) (w:oppression/persecution/mistreatment) (d:bawlsiatna written with a capital; bawlsiatna a thuak mite are the oppressed) (e:~ a thuak mite khah nading/~ le gimna na thuakna khempeuh uhah | in all the persecutions and trials you endure) (b:bawlsiatna) (r:42.4.18/53.1.4) (q:draft)
bawlsiatnate = (t:n) (w:persecutions/mistreatments/acts of oppression) (d:plural of bawlsiatna: acts of persecution or oppression) (e:leh ~ ka thuak khit uh ciangin/Mi ~ khawlin | stopping the oppression of people) (b:bawlsiatna) (r:52.2.2/23.58.9) (q:draft)
bawlsiatpa = (t:n) (w:victim/oppressed man) (d:bawlsiat, mistreat, with pa, a man; a bawlsiatpa, the man who is being mistreated, while the one who mistreats is bawlsiapa) (e:a ~ honkhia-in Iziptpa a that hi/khut sung pan a ~ hon khia un | rescue the victim from the hand) (a:bawlsiapa) (b:bawlsiat) (r:44.7.24/24.21.12) (q:draft)
bawlsiatte = (t:n) (w:those oppressed/the tormented) (d:bawlsiat, mistreat, with the plural te: those whom someone mistreats or torments) (e:dawimangpa in a ~ khempeuh a damsak hi/cina khempeuh leh dawi ~ hong paipihin | bringing all the sick and those tormented by demons) (b:bawlsiat) (r:44.10.38/44.5.16) (q:draft)
bawlta = (t:v) (w:make/do) (d:bawl, make or do, with ta, which marks what has now come about) (e:hong ciamnuih ~ uh hi/misite’ gamah lupna ~ leng zong | even if I make my bed in the realm of the dead) (b:bawl) (r:18.30.1/19.139.8) (q:draft)
bawltawm = (t:v) (w:make for oneself/invent/make up) (d:bawl, make, with tawm, by oneself: make something of one’s own; before a noun it means made by people themselves, man-made, as in mihingte’ bawltawm thukhamte, rules made by men) (e:amaute’ ~ pasian hangin lungdamin/Mi in ama’ pasian ding ~ thei ahi hiam | can a person make his own gods/Mihingte’ ~ thukhamte | rules made by men/mi a siamte in a ~ sette | devices invented by skilled men) (s:phuahtawm) (r:44.7.41/24.16.20/41.7.7/14.26.15) (q:draft)
bawltawmte = (t:n) (w:man-made things) (d:bawltawm, make for oneself, with the plural te; milim bawltawmte, idols that people made themselves) (e:milim ~ le a gamdang milimte) (b:bawltawm) (r:24.8.19) (q:draft)
bawlte = (t:n) (w:doers/makers) (d:those who do or make, bawl with plural te; siatna bawlte are evildoers, sumbuk bawlte are traders) (e:siatna ~ khempeuh na mudah hi/thusia ~’ vaihawmna | the plots of evildoers/Hia lai-ah siatna ~ cimawh-in kun uh | there the evildoers lie fallen) (b:bawl) (r:19.5.5/26.17.4/19.64.2/19.36.12) (q:draft)
bawlte = (t:n) (w:deeds/things done/works) (d:the things that someone did or made) (e:tungah a ~ khempeuh/Topa in a hoih a ~ khempeuh hangin | because of all the good the Lord had done/a khut tawh a ~ zong mu lo uh | they do not see what his hands have done/siatna na ~ uh khawl un | stop the evil you do) (s:bawlnate/septe/hihnate) (b:bawl) (r:2.18.8/5.3.21/2.18.9/23.5.12/23.1.16) (q:draft)
bawlthak = (t:v) (w:renew/make new) (d:bawl, make, with thak, new) (e:nangmah in leitung na ~ hi) (s:thakbawl/thaksuaksak/thaksuahsak) (r:19.104.30) (q:draft)
bawlthei = (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do/be able to perform) (d:bawl, do or make, with thei, be able) (e:hih bangin nalamdang ~ ding ahi hiam/bang hangin hih bang na lamdangte ~ ahi hiam | how can he do such wonders) (s:hihthei/semthei) (b:bawl) (r:43.9.16/40.13.54) (q:draft)
bawltheih = (t:v) (w:can do/can make/be able to perform) (d:bawl, make or do, with theih, be able, the form used before nading or ding) (e:lim le nalamdang ~ nading vangliatna/note tawh thuciamna hong bangci ~ ding | how can we make a treaty with you/Bangci-in nalamdang hici ~ ahi hiam | how can he do such miracles/nalamdang ~ nading thu ngah ahih manin | because it was given power to do signs) (s:hihtheih) (b:bawl) (r:44.14.3/6.9.7/41.6.2/66.13.14) (q:draft)
bawltheite = (t:n) (w:those able to do) (d:bawlthei, can do, with the plural te; nalamdang bawltheite, those who can work miracles) (e:tua ciangin nalamdang ~) (b:bawlthei) (r:46.12.28) (q:draft)
bawlthuah = (t:v) (w:go on holding/hold for longer/do in addition) (d:bawl, do or hold, with thuah, in addition: go on holding a feast for more days) (e:adang ni sagih sung mah ~ uh hi/tua pawi a ~ lai ding uh | that they would keep the feast still longer) (r:14.30.23) (q:draft)
bawltuak = (t:v) (w:be lawful to do/be right to do) (d:bawl, do, with tuak, be lawful or proper) (e:Nipi ni-in phatna ~ hi) (r:40.12.12) (q:draft)
bawlung = (t:n) (w:ball) (e:~ bangin hong lawn ding hi) (r:23.22.18) (q:draft)
bawlzah = (t:n) (w:amount made/quota) (d:bawl, make, with zah, amount: the number of things made) (e:a leiseek ~ mah uh amaute) (r:2.5.8) (q:draft)
bawlzaw = (t:v) (w:do more/do rather) (d:bawl, do, with zaw, more or rather: do more than others, or do in one way rather than another) (e:sianthona le thutakna tawh ~ ni/om mite khempeuh sangin siatna ~-in | doing more evil than all who lived) (s:hihzaw) (b:bawl) (r:46.5.8/11.14.9) (q:draft)
bawlzo = (t:v) (w:have made/have done) (d:bawl, make or do, with zo marking an act as carried through) (e:Ka teelpa tawh thuciamna ka ~ a/Israel tawh thuciamna khat ka ~ hi | I have made a covenant with Israel/ka mite in mawhna nam nih a ~ uh hi | my people have committed two sins/tangvalte tawh kiciamna khat ka ~ hi | I have made an agreement with the young men) (s:bawlkhin) (b:bawl) (r:19.89.3/9.21.2/2.34.27/24.2.13) (q:draft)
bawlzo = (t:v) (w:be able to do/manage to do) (d:bawl with zo in its sense of be able: a bawlzo nawn lo is no longer able to do) (e:siatna a ~ nawn lo dingin) (b:bawl) (r:19.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawm = (t:n) (w:basket/cage) (d:a container made to hold things, such as a basket of fruit or a cage for birds and animals) (e:~ khat sunga theigahte/nga a hoihte teelin ~ sungah a guang uh | they picked the good fish and put them in baskets/kulh pualamah ~ tawh a khaisuk uh hi | they lowered him outside the wall in a basket/theigah ~ nih dim ka mu hi | I saw two baskets full of figs) (s:seeng) (r:24.24.2/26.19.9/40.13.48/44.9.25/24.24.1) (q:draft)
bawng = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:cow/ox/cattle) (d:cow or ox, the general word for cattle of either sex; bawngpi is the female, bawngtal the male and bawngno the young) (e:pi pen ~ hita leh tuu hita leh/Ke’n ~ kap nga ka nei zo hi | I have got five pairs of oxen/~ tul sawmthum leh tulguk | thirty-six thousand cattle/Mihing’ ek tangin ~’ ek na zang ding | you shall use cow dung instead of human dung) (r:3.22.28/42.14.19/4.31.44/26.4.15)
bawnghon = (t:n) (w:herd/herds/cattle) (d:a herd of cattle: bawng, cow, with hon, herd; often paired with tuuhon, flock of sheep) (e:tuuhon leh ~, innkuan mi tampi nei/na ~ leh na tuuhon panun | from your herds and your flocks/A haupa in tuuhon leh ~ tampi nei hi | the rich man had very many flocks and herds) (r:1.26.14/2.12.38/5.15.19/10.12.2) (q:draft)
bawnghonte = (t:n) (w:herds/herds of cattle) (d:plural of bawnghon, herd of cattle; usually paired with tuuhonte, flocks) (e:na ~ hoih takin kem in/na tuuhonte uh leh na ~ uh la un | take your flocks and your herds/a tuuhonte leh a ~, a late | their flocks and herds and donkeys) (b:bawnghon) (r:20.27.23/2.12.32/1.34.28) (q:draft)
bawngkhumna = (t:n) (w:cowhouse) (d:a shed or enclosure where cattle are kept: bawng, cow, with khumna, place of shutting in) (e:~ panin a kikhah bawngnote bangin) (r:39.4.2)
bawngkhumna = (t:n) (w:barn)
bawngkhumna = (t:n) (w:shed)
Bawngkhumna = (t:n) (w:stall/cowhouse) (d:bawngkhumna written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ panin a kikhah bawngnote bangin) (b:bawngkhumna) (r:39.4.2) (q:draft)
bawngla = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:heifer/young cow) (d:a young female of cattle) (e:~ khat leh keel nih bang bek/Ama muhna ah a ~ kihal ding hi | the heifer is to be burned in his sight/Izipt gam in ~ hoih mahmah tawh kibang hi | Egypt is like a very beautiful heifer/Kum thum a pha ~ khat | a heifer three years old) (s:bawngnuno) (r:23.7.21/4.19.5/24.46.20/1.15.9) (q:draft)
bawngleeng = (t:n) (w:ox cart/cart) (d:bawng, cow or ox, with leeng, cart: a cart drawn by oxen) (e:a pua ~ a netcipsuk bangin) (r:30.2.13) (q:draft)
bawngnawi = (t:n) (w:milk) (d:cow’s milk, also rendered cream or curds; bawngnawi leh khuaizu a luan’na gam is the land flowing with milk and honey) (e:~ leh khuaizu a luan’na hih gam/a hate ~ sangin paak zaw ding hi | his teeth will be whiter than milk/tua nu in ~ pia hi | she gave him milk) (s:nawi) (r:24.32.22/1.49.12/7.5.25) (q:draft)
bawngnawite = (t:n) (w:milk) (d:bawngnawi, milk, with the plural te) (e:note’ dawn ding ~ hong gaihsak mang/ka leenggahzu leh ka ~ ka dawn hi | I have drunk my wine and my milk) (b:bawngnawi) (r:26.25.4/22.5.1) (q:draft)
bawngno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:calf) (d:the young of cattle: bawng, cow, with no, young; also the calf idol that Israel made) (e:Horeb gam sungah ~ khat bawl uh a/~ leh gamsialno bangin | like a calf and a young wild ox/Aaron in a bawlsa ~ amaute in bia uh | they worshipped the calf Aaron had made/khialhna hanga biakna ~ go hi | he slaughtered the calf of the sin offering) (b:bawng) (r:19.106.19/19.29.6/2.32.35/3.9.8) (q:draft)
bawngnote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:calves) (d:plural of bawngno, calf) (e:tuu leh bawngtal leh ~ a tuahtuah munah/a kikhah ~ bangin suakta-in | going free like calves let out/ama bawlsa ~ tungah biakna pia hi | he sacrificed to the calves he had made) (b:bawngno) (r:9.14.32/12.10.29/39.4.2/11.12.32) (q:draft)
bawngnuno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:heifer) (d:bawng, cow, with nu, female, and no, young) (e:keel’ si leh ~’ kangvute in) (s:bawngla) (r:58.9.13) (q:draft)
bawngpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:cow) (d:the female of cattle: bawng with pi, which marks a female or mother animal; the male is bawngtal) (e:~ sawmli leh bawngtal sawm/a thau a zol ~ sagih | seven fat, sleek cows/a no nawi a pia lai ~ nih | two cows that were suckling their calves) (a:bawngtal) (b:bawng) (r:1.32.15/1.41.2/1.41.18/9.6.10) (q:draft)
bawngpite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:cows) (d:plural of bawngpi, the female of cattle) (e:a ~ leeng-ah vawh un/A gawng a gulhgawng ~ in | the lean, ugly cows/~ lam lian dung zui-in | the cows followed the main road/Bashan gam ~ bangin a thau mahmah | very fat like the cows of Bashan) (a:bawngtalte) (b:bawngpi) (r:9.6.7/1.41.20/9.6.12/30.4.1) (q:draft)
bawngsa = (t:n) (w:beef/calf meat) (d:bawng, cow, with sa, meat) (e:le a minsa ~ la-in) (b:bawng) (r:1.18.8) (q:draft)
bawngtal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bull/ox/bullock) (d:the male of cattle, a bull, or an ox used for work and for sacrifice: bawng with tal, male) (e:~ khat leh la khat tawh/leeng nih leh ~ li pia hi | he gave two carts and four oxen/amaute in a ~ go-in | they slaughtered the bull/~’ tha tawh an kihau hi | by the strength of an ox the harvest is plentiful) (a:bawngpi) (r:5.22.10/14.29.33/4.7.7/9.1.25/20.14.4) (q:draft)
bawngtalno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bull/young bull) (d:a young male of cattle, often named as an animal for sacrifice: bawngtal, bull, with no, young) (e:meihal biak nadingin ~ khat/a sitbang lo ~ khat Topa mai-ah | a young bull without defect before the Lord/mihonte in ~ khat pia-in | the assembly shall offer a young bull/~ khat leh a sitbang lo tuutal nih | a young bull and two rams without defect) (b:bawngtal) (r:4.7.15/3.4.3/3.4.14/2.29.1)
bawngtalno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:calf/fattened calf) (e:i ~ limcipen go hi | he has killed our fattened calf/~ limcipen na gawh lai hi | you kill the fattened calf) (s:bawngno) (b:bawngtal) (r:42.15.27/42.15.30)
bawngtalnote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young bulls) (d:plural of bawngtalno, young bull) (e:~, tuutalte, ahih kei leh tuunote) (b:bawngtalno) (r:15.6.9) (q:draft)
bawngtalte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:oxen/bulls) (d:plural of bawngtal: bulls, or oxen used for work and for sacrifice) (e:leengte leh ~ sangin Levi mite pia hi/lo a kho ~ leh late | the oxen and donkeys that work the soil/~ leh keelte tawh | with bulls and goats/bang hang hiam cih leh ~ muktu hi | because the oxen stumbled) (a:bawngpite) (b:bawngtal) (r:4.7.6/19.50.13/23.30.24/19.66.15/10.6.6) (q:draft)
bawngte = (t:n) (w:cattle/cows/herds) (d:plural of bawng: cattle, the cows and oxen that someone owns) (e:A ~ uh pung a/Biakna innpi sungah ~, tuute, vakhute a zuakte | those selling cattle, sheep and doves in the temple/amau ~ zong kiam sak lo hi | he did not let their herds grow fewer/Tuuhonte le ~, a nongek neite | the flocks and cattle that have young) (b:bawng) (r:18.21.10/4.31.38/43.2.14/19.107.38/1.33.13) (q:draft)
Bazlith = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bazlith/Bazluth) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile; the same man as Bazluth in Ezra) (r:16.7.54)
Bazluth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bazluth) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.52)
Be = (t:see) <Be-ersheba>
Be-er = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beer) (d:name of two places: a well in the desert where Israel camped, and a town to which Jotham fled from Abimelek) (e:Tua lai panin ~ munah pai uh hi) (r:4.21.16/7.9.21) (q:draft)
Be-era = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beera) (d:a son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37) (q:draft)
Be-erah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beerah) (d:a leader of the Reubenites, taken into exile by Tiglath-Pileser king of Assyria) (e:a tapa ~ hi a) (r:13.5.6) (q:draft)
Be-eri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeri) (d:name of two men: the Hittite father of Judith, wife of Esau, and the father of the prophet Hosea) (e:~’ tapa Hosea tungah Topa in) (r:28.1.1/1.26.34) (q:draft)
Be-erlahairoi = (t:name) (c:well) (w:Beer Lahai Roi) (d:well between Kadesh and Bered where the angel of the Lord found Hagar; Isaac later lived near it) (e:tua tuikhuk pen ~ kici hi) (r:1.16.14/1.24.62) (q:draft)
Be-eroth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beeroth) (d:one of the four Gibeonite towns, allotted to the tribe of Benjamin) (e:~ mite Gittaim-ah tai uh a) (r:10.4.3/6.18.25) (q:draft)
Be-ersheba = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beersheba) (d:town in the Negev in the far south of Judah, linked with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob) (e:panin amah ~-ah paito hi) (r:1.26.23/6.15.28) (q:draft)
Be-eshterah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Be Eshterah) (d:town in Bashan given to the Gershonite Levites from the half-tribe of Manasseh) (e:leh ~ a lonona gamte tawh) (r:6.21.27) (q:draft)
Bealiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bealiah) (d:a Benjamite warrior who joined David at Ziklag) (r:13.12.5)
Bealoth = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bealoth) (d:town in the far south of Judah; the name also stands for a district named with Asher under Solomon) (r:6.15.24)
beba = (t:adv) (w:wide open/gaping) (d:describes the mouth opened as wide as it will go, after kamkat or kam ka, open the mouth; said of gaping in scorn or in greed) (e:kei hong kamkat ~ uh hi/a kam ka ~ a | it opens its mouth wide/na kam uh ka ~-in na leii uh phen | opening your mouth wide and sticking out your tongue/Amaute in kei hong kamkat ~ uh a | they open their mouths wide at me) (r:19.22.13/23.5.14/23.57.4/19.35.21) (q:draft)
Bebai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bebai) (d:ancestor of a family that returned from the exile, and a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:15.10.28/16.10.15)
Bedad = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedad) (d:father of Hadad, a king of Edom) (r:1.36.35/13.1.46)
Bedan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedan) (d:son of Ulam, a descendant of Manasseh) (r:13.7.17)
Bedciah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedeiah) (d:a descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.35)
Bedeiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedeiah) (d:a descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.35)
bedolak = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bdellium/aromatic resin) (d:a fragrant gum resin, named with singnai, resin; manna is said to look like it) (e:tua munah ~ singnai leh onik suang/a meel in ~ singnai tawh kibang hi | its appearance was like resin) (r:1.2.12/4.11.7)
beek = (t:adv) (w:even/at all/not even) (d:stresses the smallest amount, mostly with a negative: khat beek with kei means not even one, and neukha beek means even a little) (e:Midik khat ~ a om kei hi/kamkhat ~ a dawn’ kik loh | he did not answer even one word/a pum neukha ~ a kizan thei kei hi | she could not straighten up at all/adang sawltakte khat ~ ka mu kei hi | I did not see even one of the other apostles) (s:nangawn) (r:45.3.10/48.1.19/40.27.14/42.13.11) (q:draft)
beekah = (t:adv) (w:even in/at least to) (d:beek, even, at least, with the place marker ah: khat beekah with a negative, not even in one; kiang beekah, at least to) (e:Hua vokte kiang ~ hong paisak inla/thute khat ~ a mawhna ka mu kei hi | I found no guilt in even one of the charges) (b:beek) (r:41.5.12/42.23.14) (q:draft)
beel = (t:n) (w:pot/jar/vessel) (d:container of clay, metal, wood or stone used for cooking, for storing things or for carrying water; beel kitam is a broken pot, a potsherd) (e:~ kitam khat tawh ka kibang hi/Job in ~ kitam them khat la-in | Job took a piece of broken pot/a khut tungah a ~ niamsuksakin | lowering her jar onto her hand/suang ~ khempeuh sung nangawnah sisan | blood even in all the stone vessels) (r:19.31.12/24.19.10/18.2.8/1.24.18/2.7.19) (q:draft)
Beel = (t:n) (w:pot/jar) (d:beel, pot or jar, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Beel sekpa is the potter, the one who shapes pots) (e:~ sekpa’ innah paisuk in la/~ sekpa’ kiangah pai in la | go to the potter/~ khat la in la | take a jar/~ seekpa pen tungman bangin kingaihsun ding | the potter would be thought to be like the clay) (b:beel) (r:24.18.2/24.19.1/2.16.33/23.29.16) (q:draft)
Beel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeliada) (d:first part of the name Beel-i-ada, Beeliada, a son of David; not a word by itself) (e:Elishama, ~-i-ada, leh Elifelet ahi uh hi) (r:13.14.7) (q:draft)
beela = (t:v) (w:cling to/hold on to) (d:beel, hold fast to a person, apparently the same word as bel, cling to, with a linking it to the following verb) (e:Piter leh Johan ~ a om) (r:44.3.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
Beeliada = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeliada) (d:son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:13.14.7)
beelin = (t:v) (w:take refuge in/cling to/rely on) (d:bel written with a long vowel and the linking ending in: holding fast to a person or taking shelter in something, and so doing a further action) (e:Mi kimkhat in Paul ~ thu a um/ama na semin amah ~ | serving him and holding fast to him/Khat ~ khat a simmawh ding hi | he will hold to the one and despise the other/thuman mite in ~ lungmuangin om thei uh hi | the righteous take refuge in it and are safe) (s:belin) (r:44.17.34/5.10.20/40.6.24/20.18.10) (q:draft)
beellekuang = (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/pots and bowls) (d:beel, pot, le, and, kuang, bowl, written as one word: the vessels of a house or of the temple) (e:sumngo kibawl ~ khawngte sawp ding/~ a puate aw, khuasung panin paikhia unla | you who carry the vessels, come out of the city) (s:umlebeel) (r:41.7.4/23.52.11) (q:draft)
beellekuangte = (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/dishes) (d:plural of beellekuang: the dishes and vessels that belong to a table or a house) (e:sabuai tunga om ding ~) (s:kuanglekeute/umlebeelte) (b:beellekuang) (r:2.37.16) (q:draft)
beelmang = (t:n) (w:soot/pot black) (d:the black that gathers on a cooking pot; in the verse beauty is smeared with it, that is, made loathsome) (e:Na meel hoihna ~ na kizutnelh hi) (r:26.16.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
beelpa = (t:n) (w:one who relies on) (d:beel, take refuge in or rely on, with pa marking a man: the man who put his trust in something) (e:ama hauhna a ~ en un) (r:19.52.7) (q:draft)
beelpei = (t:n) (w:griddle/flat pan) (d:flat cooking vessel on which bread is baked; beelpei kitam is a broken piece of it, a potsherd; also spelled belpei) (e:~ daii tunga ki-em an tawh/Tua pen ~ tung khatah sathau tawh kibawl ding | it is to be made with oil on a griddle/A khecinte, ~ kitamte tawh kibang a | its undersides are like broken potsherds/Meibung hitaleh ~ hitaleh kisuzan ding hi | whether oven or cooking pot, it must be broken) (s:belpei) (r:3.2.5/3.7.9/3.6.21/18.41.30/3.11.35) (q:draft)
beelpi = (t:n) (w:large pot/cauldron/vat) (d:beel, pot, with pi, big; leenggahzu kholna beelpi is a wine vat) (e:beel sung, ~ sung, leh sikbeel daite/leenggahzu kholna ~ ah na pai uh ciangin | when you went to the wine vat/beel-uk ahi a, ~ ahi a | or the kettle or the cauldron) (b:beel) (r:14.35.13/37.2.16/9.2.14) (q:draft)
beelseek = (t:n) (w:potter) (d:one who shapes clay pots, from beel, pot, and seek, mould; followed by pa for a man) (e:~ pa’ inn-ah paisuk inla/~ pa’ lo a lei uh hi | they bought the potter's field/nang pen ~ pa bang na hi a | you are like the potter/~ pa’ khutsunga buan tawh kibangin | like clay in the hand of the potter) (s:beelsekpa/seekpa/sekpa) (r:24.18.2/24.18.4/40.27.7/23.64.8/24.18.6) (q:draft)
beelseekpa = (t:n) (w:potter) (d:beelseek, potter, with pa marking a man) (e:~’ beel den’khap bangin) (s:beelsekpa/seekpa/sekpa) (b:beelseek) (r:19.2.9) (q:draft)
beelseekte = (t:n) (w:potters) (d:plural of beelseek: people whose work is making clay pots) (e:Hihte in ~ hi a) (b:beelseek) (r:13.4.23) (q:draft)
beelsekpa = (t:n) (w:potter) (d:beel, pot, and sek, shape, with pa for a man: the man who shapes pots) (e:~ in hoih a sak bangin/~’ khut sunga buan tawh kibangin | like clay in the hand of the potter/hih ~’ beel kisukham a | as this potter's jar is smashed) (s:beelseekpa/seekpa/sekpa) (r:24.18.4/24.18.6/24.19.11) (q:draft)
beelte = (t:n) (w:pots/vessels/jars/articles) (d:plural of beel: pots, jars and other vessels; um-le-beelte is vessels and articles of every kind) (e:Hih tui ~ tui na dimsak un/hih ~ khempeuh sungah sung in | pour it into all these jars/amaute in ~, kawbiate, taitehte | they took the pots, shovels and wick trimmers) (s:belte) (b:beel) (r:43.2.7/19.58.9/12.4.4/12.25.14) (q:draft)
Beelzebub = (t:name) (w:Beelzebul/Beelzebub) (d:name given to the prince of demons, by whose power the Pharisees said Jesus drove out demons) (r:40.12.24/40.10.25)
Beelzebul = (t:name) (w:Beelzebul) (d:name given to the prince of demons, by whose power the Pharisees said Jesus drove out demons) (r:40.12.24/42.11.15)
beem = (t:n) (w:homer/cor) (d:a large measure for grain, equal to ten bung; translates the Hebrew homer and cor) (e:khaici ~ khat in an seu khat/mangbuh ~ tul sawmnih dim pia a | he gave twenty thousand cors of wheat/mangbuhham ~ khat a pawina leitang | land sown with a homer of barley/~ khatah an bung sawm | ten measures of grain to one homer) (r:23.5.10/26.45.14/11.5.11/3.27.16/26.45.11) (q:draft)
beemlepang = (t:n) (w:storehouse/barn/provisions) (d:beem le pang written as one word: the bins where grain and food are stored, and so the food kept there) (e:Amaute in ~ zong nei lo napi-in/Ama ~ thupha tampi ka pia ding a | I will richly bless her provisions) (r:42.12.24/19.132.15) (q:draft)
beempi = (t:n) (w:reservoir) (d:in tui beempi, a large store made to hold water) (e:kikal ah tui ~ khat na bawl) (r:23.22.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
beeng = (t:v) (w:slap/hit/strike) (d:strike with the open hand, especially on the face) (e:ci-in khut tawh a ~ uh hi/Nang kua in hong ~ hiam | who hit you/Kimkhat in khutpeek-in a ~ uh hi | others slapped him with the palm of the hand/ka paang a ~ dingin | to strike my cheek/bang hangin hong ~ na hi hiam | why did you strike me) (s:beng/bet) (r:43.19.3/42.22.64/40.26.67/18.16.10/43.18.23) (q:draft)
beeng = (t:v) (w:clap) (d:with khut, hand: clap the hands, in joy or in scorn) (e:na khut uh ~ un/sing khempeuh in a khut uh ~ ding uh hi | all the trees will clap their hands/Na khut ~ in | clap your hands/Kei zong ka khut ka ~ ding a | I too will clap my hands) (s:beng) (r:19.47.1/23.55.12/26.21.14/26.21.17) (q:draft)
beenggawp = (t:v) (w:strike/smite/slap hard) (d:beeng, strike with the hand, with gawp, severely) (e:Pasian in nang hong ~ taktak ding hi/ka galte khempeuh’ paang nangmah in na ~ a | you strike all my enemies on the jaw) (b:beeng) (r:44.23.3/19.3.7) (q:draft)
beengin = (t:v) (w:beating/striking) (d:beeng, strike, with the linking ending in; awm beengin, beating the breast, a sign of grief) (e:awm ~ a ciah uh hi/en ngam loin a awm ~ | not daring to look up, beating his breast) (b:beeng) (r:42.23.48/42.18.13) (q:draft)
Beer = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beer) (d:a well where Israel camped in the desert, and a town to which Jotham fled; also written Be-er) (e:Tua lai panin ~ munah pai uh hi) (r:4.21.16/7.9.21) (q:draft)
Beera = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beera) (d:son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37) (q:draft)
Beerah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beerah) (d:leader of the tribe of Reuben, taken into exile by Tiglath-Pileser king of Assyria) (r:13.5.6)
Beerelim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beer Elim) (d:town of Moab named in the lament of Isaiah over Moab) (r:23.15.8)
Beeri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeri) (d:name of two men: the Hittite father of Judith, wife of Esau, and the father of the prophet Hosea) (r:1.26.34/28.1.1)
Beerlahairoi = (t:name) (c:well) (w:Beer-lahai-roi/Beer Lahai Roi) (d:well between Kadesh and Bered where the angel of the Lord met Hagar; Isaac later lived near it) (r:1.16.14/1.24.62)
Beeroth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beeroth) (d:town of the Gibeonites, allotted to the tribe of Benjamin) (r:6.18.25/10.23.37)
Beersheba = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Beersheba) (d:town with a well in the far south of Judah, in the Negev, where Abraham and Isaac lived) (r:13.4.28/1.26.33)
Beeshterah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Be Eshterah) (d:town in Bashan, in the half-tribe of Manasseh, given to the Levites of Gershon) (r:6.21.27)
begap = (t:n) (w:pod/husk) (d:the pod of a bean plant, eaten by pigs) (e:Vokte’ ~ nekte nangawn) (r:42.15.16) (q:draft)
begapte = (t:n) (w:pods/husks) (d:plural of begap: the pods that were fed to pigs) (e:vok an nek ~ nangawn duhgawhin) (b:begap) (r:42.15.16) (q:draft)
beh = (t:n) (w:clan/family) (d:group of related families within a tribe) (e:a ~ sungah a lutang ahi mi/a ~ lutang ahi Zur’ tanu Kozbi | Kozbi daughter of Zur, the head of a clan/a ~ tangun tul thum leh zanih | by their clans, three thousand two hundred) (s:phung) (r:4.1.4/15.10.38/4.25.15/4.4.44) (q:draft)
behbeh = (t:adv) (w:by clans/clan by clan) (d:beh, clan, doubled: each clan in turn, according to their clans; usually a behbeh) (e:a ~ a innkuan kuanin sim in/A ~ tawh kizui-in Benjamin minamte’ ading | for the tribe of Benjamin, according to its clans/Benjamin mite a ~, a pawlpawlin a koih hi | he placed the men of Benjamin by clans, in groups/amau’ ~-in a kisim Levi minamte | the Levites counted by their clans) (r:4.3.15/6.18.11/14.25.5/4.26.57) (q:draft)
behbeh = (t:adv) (w:more and more/increasingly) (d:after a verb, beh, in addition, doubled: keep on adding) (e:a suah matengin ngah ~ hi) (s:semsem) (r:1.26.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
behbehin = (t:adv) (w:by clans/clan by clan/by families) (d:each clan or family taken separately) (e:Amau’ ~ Josef minamte in/beh dang khempeuhte zong a ~ | all the other clans too, clan by clan/Hihte in amau’ ~ Dan minamte ahi hi | these were the Danites by their clans/Shemida-te tungah a ~ piakna kibawl hi | an allotment was made to them by their clans) (b:behbeh) (r:4.26.28/38.12.14/4.26.42/6.17.2) (q:draft)
behin = (t:adv) (w:by clans/clan by clan/according to families) (d:beh, clan, with the ending -in; used doubled as a beh behin: each clan in its turn) (e:Levi mite a beh ~ pawl thum suah/a lak minam a beh ~ hong pai ding hi | the tribe he chooses shall come forward clan by clan/Amau’ beh ~ Asher minamte in | the Asherites by their clans/Benjamin mite a beh ~ a pawl pawlin koih hi | he placed the men of Benjamin by clans, in groups) (b:beh) (r:13.23.6/4.26.44/6.7.14/14.25.5) (q:draft)
behlap = (t:v) (w:add/add to/increase) (d:put something more on top of what is already there, and so make it greater) (e:seh nga suah seh khat ~ ding hi/na hauhna na ~ a | you have increased your wealth/Topa in ka dahna leh ka natna hong ~ hi | the Lord has added to my sorrow and my pain/Israel mite’ mawhna na ~ uh hi | you have added to the guilt of Israel) (a:khiam) (r:3.27.13/24.45.3/26.28.5/15.10.10) (q:draft)
behlapin = (t:v) (w:adding/adding to) (d:behlap, add, with the linking ending in: adding one thing to another, and so doing a further action) (e:hih mawhna ~, Johan thong sungah/man zah sehnga suah sehkhat ~ | adding a fifth of its value/Mipilte in a pilna uh ~ | the wise add to their knowledge/kuamah in ~ thu a guang thei kei hi | no one can add anything to it) (b:behlap) (r:42.3.20/3.22.14/20.10.14/48.3.15) (q:draft)
behlaplap = (t:v) (w:keep adding/add more and more) (d:behlap, add, with the last part repeated to show that the action goes on) (e:a mawhna uh ~ uh hi) (r:28.4.2) (q:draft)
behlapsak = (t:v) (w:add to) (d:behlap, add, with sak: add something to what another has said or has) (e:Ama gen lohpi ~ kei in) (b:behlap) (r:20.30.6) (q:draft)
behlapto = (t:v) (w:add on/increase further) (d:behlap, add, with to, upward) (e:kote’ lungdamna hong ~ sawnsawn hi) (b:behlap) (r:47.7.13) (q:draft)
behlapzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to add) (d:behlap, add, with zawh, be able) (e:tawh na ~ nadingun na hanciam) (r:61.1.7) (q:draft)
behlephung = (t:n) (w:descent/lineage/clan and family) (d:beh, clan, le, and, phung, family line, written as one word: the family a person descends from) (e:amau’ ~ a kan thei lo mite) (r:15.2.59/16.7.61) (q:draft)
behnai = (t:n) (w:relative/close kin) (d:beh, clan, with nai, near) (e:Note pen ka ~ na hi) (s:tanau) (r:10.19.12) (q:draft)
behnu = (t:n) (w:kinswoman/female relative) (d:beh, clan, with nu marking a woman) (e:Na ~ Elizabeth zong thei in) (b:beh) (r:42.1.36) (q:draft)
behpa = (t:n) (w:kinsman/relative) (d:beh, clan, with pa marking a man: a male member of the same clan or family) (e:amah tawh a kinai a ~ hong pai-in/Ama’ ~ sal-in a kimatna | that his kinsman had been taken captive/ka topa’ ~’ tanu la dingin | to take the daughter of my master's kinsman) (s:tanaupa) (b:beh) (r:3.25.25/1.14.14/1.24.48) (q:draft)
behtangun = (t:adv) (w:by their clans/clan by clan) (d:beh, clan, with tang and the plural ending un; of a count of men reckoned by clans) (e:Kohath mi pasal a ~ tulnih le zasagih) (r:4.4.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
behte = (t:n) (w:relatives/clan/kindred/family) (d:people of the same clan; after a name, the clan of that person) (e:Ka ~ leh ka lawmte bei ta hi/a ~ sawmgiat tawh ahi hi | with eighty of his relatives/Eri pan Eri ~ ahi uh hi | from Eri, the clan of Eri/amau’ ~ sungah ukpi ahi hi | he was the head of their clan) (s:tanaute/phungte) (b:beh) (r:18.19.14/4.26.16/13.15.9/13.5.15) (q:draft)
bei = (t:v) (w:pass/over/come to an end/be finished) (d:come to an end: said of time that passes, of things that are used up, and of people who are no more) (e:Ka hun ~ ta hi/Nitak hong ~-in, zingsang hong tung a | evening passed and morning came/Nihna gimna a ~ zo hi | the second woe has passed/kum sagih sung hauhna ~ ta hi | the seven years of plenty came to an end) (s:tawp) (a:kipan) (r:1.1.5/18.17.11/66.11.14/1.41.53) as Nitak hong bei-in, zingsang hong tung a
bei = (t:adj) (w:empty/clear/used up/gone) (d:used up or gone, with nothing left) (e:Thawl sunga tui a ~ ciangin | when the water in the skin was gone/ka tha ~ ta hi | my strength is gone/Leenggahtui a ~ ciangin | when the wine was gone) (s:gai) (a:dim) (r:1.21.15/19.39.10/43.2.3)
beibei = (t:v) (w:pass away/keep passing) (d:bei, come to an end, doubled for something that goes on passing) (e:leitung deihnate a ~ ding hita a/Hun ~ a, genkholhnate a tung om lo hi | the days go by and no prophecy comes true) (r:62.2.17/26.12.22) (q:draft)
beikhawm = (t:v) (w:perish together/end together) (d:bei, come to an end, with khawm, together) (e:a lametna teng tawh ~ a) (b:bei) (r:20.11.7) (q:draft)
beikhin = (t:v) (w:be over/be past/be used up) (d:bei, be finished, with khin, already: be completely gone or past) (e:Ka thaneihteng ~ a/a ta neihtheih ding hun ~ napi-in | though she was past the age of bearing children) (s:beikhit) (b:bei) (r:27.10.8/58.11.11) (q:draft)
beikhit = (t:v) (w:be used up/be finished) (d:bei, come to an end, with khit, completed; a beikhit ciangin, after it was all gone) (e:sum khempeuh a ~ ciangin) (s:beikhin) (r:42.15.14) (q:draft)
beikhitna = (t:n) (w:being used up) (d:beikhit with the noun suffix na: the fact that something is all gone) (e:Ka sum uh a ~ ka topa) (b:beikhit) (r:1.47.18) (q:draft)
beikuan = (t:v) (w:be about to end/near the end) (d:bei, come to an end, with kuan, be on the way to; leitung beikuan hun, the time when the world nears its end) (e:Leitung ~ hun sungah) (r:46.10.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
beilam = (t:n) (w:fading/ending) (d:bei, come to an end, with lam: the passing away of something) (e:a vangtaang a ~ Israel mite) (r:47.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
beilawh = (t:v) (w:lose/spend/perish) (d:bei, be finished or used up, with lawh, as a result of something: lose or spend all one has for a thing, or perish because of what has happened) (e:na neih khempeuh na ~ zongin/mi a omlai sunteng in zong ~ ding uh | the remnant too will perish) (r:20.4.7/24.40.15) (q:draft)
beima = (t:see) <beima-in>
beima-in = (t:v) (w:before passing away/before coming to an end) (d:bei, come to an end, with ma-in, before: before it ends, before they pass away) (e:hih khang mite a ~ hih thu khempeuh) (r:42.21.32/41.13.30) (q:draft)
beimang = (t:v) (w:vanish/perish/disappear) (d:pass out of existence or out of sight; bei, come to an end, with mang, away) (e:meikhu bangin ~ a/ama leitang panin minamte ~ ding hi | the nations will perish from his land/ka thupina teng huih letkhiat bangin ~ a | my dignity is driven away as by the wind/Siat denna sungah galte ~ hi | the enemies have perished in endless ruin) (s:maimang/mangthang) (r:19.102.3/18.3.3/19.10.16/18.30.15/19.9.6) (q:draft)
beimangsak = (t:v) (w:destroy/wipe out/put an end to) (d:causative of beimang, vanish: make something disappear altogether) (e:Amah in sihna ~ ding a/Moab gam i ~ ding hi | let us put an end to Moab/Judah ka ~ ding hi | I will make Judah perish) (s:maimangsak/susiamang) (b:beimang) (r:23.25.8/24.48.2/28.5.12) (q:draft)
beimangsakin = (t:v) (w:destroy/wipe out/cut off) (d:beimangsak, make disappear, with in linking it to the following verb) (e:suankhiat ding uh minamte ~) (b:beimangsak) (r:5.12.29) (q:draft)
beimangsakna = (t:n) (w:destruction/wiping out) (d:beimangsak with the noun suffix na; with ding, in order to destroy) (e:Filistia mite simin ka ~ ding thu) (b:beimangsak) (r:26.25.16) (q:draft)
beimangta = (t:v) (w:vanish/disappear) (d:beimang, vanish, with ta marking a change that has now come about) (e:lehang launa ~ hi) (s:maimangta) (b:beimang) (r:62.4.18) (q:draft)
beina = (t:n) (w:end/outcome) (d:the point where something finishes, and also the way a matter turns out; bei, come to an end, with the noun suffix na) (e:A ~ hong tung ta hi/Na khempeuh a ~ hong nai zo hi | the end of all things is near/a ~ a tung nai kei ding hi | the end is not yet/bang ci bangin ~ a hong piang ding hiam | what will the outcome be) (s:tawpna) (a:kipatna) (b:bei) (r:26.7.6/41.13.7/60.4.7/27.12.8) (q:draft)
Beinaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:descendant of Parosh who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.25)
beinate = (t:n) (w:costs/expenses) (d:bei, be used up, with the noun suffix na and the plural te; sum beinate, the money spent) (e:hih sum ~ ahih leh kumpi sum) (s:beiteng) (b:beina) (r:15.6.4) (q:draft)
beipak = (t:v) (w:pass quickly/be fleeting/be short-lived) (d:bei, come to an end, with pak, quickly; of the days of a life) (e:ka nuntakna a ~ hun ding/a nuntak hun uh niliim bangin ~ ding a | their days will pass quickly like a shadow/~ ahih manin nopna ngah kha lo hi | they pass quickly and find no joy) (r:19.39.4/21.8.13/18.9.25) (q:draft)
beisa = (t:adj) (w:past/former/earlier) (d:gone by, of an earlier time: a beisa nate is the former things, a beisa hun time past) (e:a ~ nate ngaihsun kei un/A ~ hunte phawk un la | remember the days of old/a ~ hun sungah | in earlier times/a ~ nate kiciamteh nawn lo | the former things will not be remembered) (b:bei) (r:23.43.18/13.9.20/5.32.7/23.65.17) (q:draft)
beisak = (t:adj) (w:finish/bring to an end/put an end to) (d:bei, come to an end, with the causative sak: finish a period of time, or put an end to people or things) (e:pawi hun sung ~ phot hi/nipi khat sung pawi ~ phot in | first finish the week of the feast/Mi khempeuh ~ ding ka khentat zo hi | I have decided to put an end to all people/leimong dong ah gal ~ hi | he makes wars cease to the ends of the earth) (b:bei) (r:1.29.28/1.6.13/1.29.27/19.46.9) Put an end
beisak = (t:adj) (w:empty/clear) (d:make empty or clear: use up what someone has, or clear people or things out of a place) (e:ama na manpha na ~ hi | you consume what is precious to him/vankahte leh aisante a gamsung panin ~ hi | he cleared the mediums and spiritists out of the land/amaute hong tun ciangin gamteng ~ uh hi | when they came they laid the whole land bare) (b:bei) (r:19.39.11/9.28.3/7.6.5)
beisakin = (t:v) (w:destroying/putting an end to/removing) (d:beisak, cause to be finished, with the linking ending -in before the next verb) (e:note hong piak minamte ~/Gal kidona leengte, Israel gam pan ~ | removing the war chariots from Israel/na saltanna uh hong ~ | putting an end to your captivity) (b:beisak) (r:5.19.1/38.9.10/24.29.14) (q:draft)
beisakkhin = (t:v) (w:have done away with/have put off) (d:beisak, bring to an end, with khin, already) (e:gamtatna lui khempeuh a ~ na hihna) (b:beisak) (r:51.3.9) (q:draft)
beisakkik = (t:v) (w:bring to an end/end) (d:beisak, bring to an end, with kik, back: end a captivity and so restore the people) (e:a saltanna uh ka ~ ni) (b:beisak) (r:24.30.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
beisakmang = (t:v) (w:annihilate/wipe out) (d:beisak, bring to an end, with mang, away altogether) (e:thah ding, ~ dingin hong kizuak hi) (s:susiamang) (r:17.7.4) (q:draft)
beisakmangna = (t:n) (w:annihilation) (d:beisakmang with the noun suffix na; with ding, in order to annihilate) (e:thatin, a ~ ding uh) (b:beisakmang) (r:17.3.13) (q:draft)
beisakna = (t:n) (w:ending/using up) (d:the act of bringing something to an end or using it up, beisak with the noun suffix na; hun beisakna, the passing or wasting of time) (e:man nei lopi-a hun ~ in haina hi/Miliante’ kiphatsaknate a ~ ding | to bring the pride of the great to an end) (b:beisak) (r:20.12.11/23.23.9) (q:draft)
beisakpa = (t:n) (w:remover/one who puts an end to) (d:beisak, put an end to or let pass, with pa, a man: the man who takes something away, or who lets a time go by) (e:hih mindaina a ~ adingin/Kam si bek-a hun mawk ~) (b:beisak) (r:9.17.26/24.46.17) (q:draft)
beisakta = (t:v) (w:put an end to/make cease) (d:beisak, put an end to, with ta, which marks what now comes about) (e:Hih paunak ka ~ ding a) (b:beisak) (r:26.12.23) (q:draft)
beisiang = (t:v) (w:be wiped out/be completely gone) (d:bei, come to an end, with siang, clean: be gone with nothing left; beisiang sak, clear away, purge) (e:Amaute khempeuh a ~ dongin sumai in/amaute a ~ dongin tampi tak a thah khit uh | after they had killed very many, until they were wiped out) (b:bei) (r:19.59.13/6.10.20) (q:draft)
beisiangna = (t:n) (w:complete destruction/utter end) (d:beisiang, be completely gone, with the noun suffix na) (e:leitung khempeuhah ~ a bawl ding hi) (b:beisiang) (r:23.10.23) (q:draft)
beisiangsak = (t:v) (w:wipe out/purge/clear away) (d:beisiang, be completely gone, with sak, cause: remove a thing completely from a place) (e:Jeroboam innkuan ka ~ ding hi/a kisung milimte ~ ding kipan hi | he began to purge the cast idols) (b:beisiang) (r:11.14.10/14.34.3) (q:draft)
beita = (t:v) (w:has ended/is gone/is finished) (d:bei with ta, showing that something has now come to an end) (e:Ka hun uh a ~ hi/na mawhna ~ a | your guilt is taken away/ankungte ~ a, lopa hing om nawn lo hi | the plants are gone and no green grass is left/ka lunggulh theigah ~ hi | the figs I long for are gone/Hih tangthu a ~ hi | this is the end of the matter) (b:bei) (r:25.4.18/23.15.6/23.6.7/33.7.1/27.7.28) (q:draft)
beiteng = (t:n) (w:expenses/all that is spent) (d:bei, be used up, with teng, all; sum beiteng, all the money spent) (e:a sum ~ khempeuh nangmah in sik) (s:beinate) (b:bei) (r:44.21.24) (q:draft)
beitum = (t:v) (w:be consumed/be destroyed/perish) (d:come to a complete end, be used up or destroyed altogether) (e:amaute a ~ mateng ka kileh kei hi/lingkungte leh lingte kang-in ~ ding hi | the thorns and briers will be burned up completely) (r:10.22.38/23.10.17) (q:draft)
beitumsak = (t:v) (w:consume/destroy completely) (d:beitum, be wholly consumed, with sak, cause; said together with beimangsak, cause to perish) (e:Tua ahih manin Israel ka ~ ding a) (b:beitum) (r:28.5.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
beizo = (t:v) (w:have passed away/be gone) (d:bei, come to an end, with zo marking completion) (e:kumpi sagihte lakah nga ~ a) (b:bei) (r:66.17.10) (q:draft)
bek = (t:adv) (w:only/alone) (d:placed after the word it limits: that one and no other, that much and no more) (e:Amah ~ in vanpi zal a/Hih kiciamna note ~ tawh a bawl hi lo a | this covenant is not made with you only/Pasian ~ in pilna lampi thei a | God alone knows the way to wisdom/lam khat ~ zui ni | let us follow only one way/kei ~ hong um kei hi | does not believe in me only) (s:lel) (r:18.9.8/5.29.14/18.28.23/50.3.16/43.12.44) (q:draft)
beka = (t:adv) (w:only/merely) (d:bek, only, with the ending a linking it to the following word: pualam beka is only outward, tungtham beka only on the surface) (e:note tung ~ hong tung ahi hiam/a pualam ~ Jew mi hihna | being a Jew only outwardly/Nang pen zan mah ~ hong pai na hi hi | you came only yesterday/tungtham ~ thugenna in siatna bek piangsak hi | talk that is only on the surface brings nothing but ruin) (b:bek) (r:46.14.36/45.2.28/10.15.20/20.26.28) (q:draft)
beka = (t:n) (w:beka) (d:measure of weight, half a shekel) (e:mi khat ciangin ~ khat) (r:2.38.26) (q:draft)
bekah = (t:adv) (w:only in/only at/only to) (d:bek, only, with the place marker ah: only in, only at or only to that place or person) (e:Goshen gam ~ gialpi kia lo hi/Nail gun sung ~ om ding uh hi | they will remain only in the Nile/Gaza, Gath, leh Ashdod sung ~ pawlkhat om lai hi | only in Gaza, Gath and Ashdod did some remain/Na sanggamte tung ~ na kamsiam uh leh | if you greet only your brothers) (b:bek) (r:2.9.26/47.10.17/2.8.11/6.11.22/40.5.47) (q:draft)
bekbak = (t:adv) (w:thick/heavily) (d:word of manner that strengthens what goes before: khuamial bekbak, thick or utter darkness; man bekbak-in hawl, drive heavily, with difficulty) (e:a lauhuai khuamial ~ lak/khua mial ~ a, lau mahmah hi | it grew thickly dark and he was very afraid/man ~-in hawl uh hi | they drove with great difficulty) (r:24.2.6/2.14.25/1.15.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbakin = (t:adv) (w:with difficulty/heavily) (d:bekbak, heavily, with the adverbial ending in: man bekbakin hawl is to drive slowly and with great difficulty) (e:ahih manin man ~ hawl uh hi) (b:bekbak) (r:2.14.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbakte = (t:n) (d:bekbak, thick or hard, with the plural te: in the verse the places where the ground has dried hard) (e:lei keu-in a sak ~ kua in) (b:bekbak) (r:18.38.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbek = (t:adv) (w:only/nothing but) (d:emphatic doubled form of bek, placed after the word it limits: thusia bekbek is nothing but evil talk) (e:migilote in thusia ~ gen hi/Ka thugente a maan ~ hi a | my words are nothing but true/lam lianpi khempeuh ah kahna ~ a om hi | in all the public squares there is nothing but mourning/ka muhna-ah siatna ~ a bawl uh a | in my sight they have done nothing but evil) (s:vive) (r:20.10.6/20.8.7/24.48.38/24.32.30) (q:draft)
bekbekin = (t:adv) (w:only/solely/nothing but) (d:bekbek, only, with the adverbial ending in, placed after the word it limits: a thuman bekbekin is what is right and that alone) (e:a thuman ~ na gamta ding uh hi/nang a’ ding ~ kong nungta ding hi | I will live for you alone) (b:bekbek) (r:5.16.20/23.38.16) (q:draft)
Bekher = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beriah/Beker) (d:a son of Benjamin; also a son of Ephraim, ancestor of a clan) (r:1.46.21/13.7.6)
bekin = (t:conj) (w:only/merely) (d:bek, only, with in, closing a phrase of reason or purpose: hang bekin and man bekin are only because of, ading bekin is only for) (e:Abraham ading ~ Lai Siangtho sungah gelh/daan kihtakna hang ~ a mang na hi kei | you do not obey only for fear of punishment/mi khempeuh ama khialhna hang ~ kithat ding hi | everyone shall be put to death only for his own sin/tapa a neih loh man ~ | only because he had no son) (b:bek) (r:45.4.23/45.13.5/5.24.16/4.27.4)
bekin = (t:adv) (w:just/only/alone) (d:bek, only, with the adverbial in, limiting the word before it: keimah bekin is I alone, na kam bekin is just by your word) (e:tua bang ciang ~ ngaihsun hi/Tua mangmuhna keimah ~ ka mu hi | I alone saw that vision/Na kam ~ thupia lecin | if you just give the order by your word/Filip ze-etna ~ a dong hi | he asked only to test Philip/Topa kiang pan ~ thutang kingah hi | justice is received only from the Lord) (s:lelin) (b:bek) (r:1.25.34/27.10.7/40.8.8/43.6.6/20.29.26)
bekinah = (t:adv) (w:in only/within just) (d:bekin, only, with the marker ah: nai khat sung bekinah is within just one hour) (e:Nai khat sung ~ thutanna na thuak ta hi/Nai khat sung ~ tua zaha nopsaknate a beisak | in just one hour such great wealth has been destroyed) (b:bekin) (r:66.18.10/66.18.17) (q:draft)
Bekorath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bekorath) (d:a Benjamite, son of Aphiah and ancestor of King Saul) (r:9.9.1)
bekun = (t:adv) (w:only/just/merely) (d:bek, only, with the ending un used when the subject is plural; man bekun is only because of, nading bekun is only so that) (e:na guh guak ~ na om ding/Jesuh a hazat man ~ ama kiangah a paipih | they handed him over only because they envied Jesus/Pasian na biak theih nading ~ ci-in | only so that you may worship God/a kampi ~ thu genin thuciamna a bawl) (b:bek) (r:20.5.11/30.2.6/40.27.18/46.7.35/28.10.4) (q:draft)
bel = (t:v) (w:take refuge in/rely on/cling to) (d:to shelter in or hold on to someone for safety, most often said of trusting in God; also written belh) (e:amah a ~ mite lim takin kem hi/Nangmah ka hong ~ hi | I cling to you/Topa ka ~ hi | I take refuge in the Lord/Amah a ~ mi in lungdam hi | the one who takes refuge in him is glad/Amaute in Topa ~ ahih manin | because they take refuge in the Lord) (s:muang) (a:taisan) (r:34.1.7/19.63.8/19.11.1/19.34.8/19.37.40) (q:draft)
bel = (t:part) (w:most/very) (d:placed after a word of order or degree to mark the extreme, as in a masa bel the very first, a nunung bel the very last and a sang bel the highest) (e:A nunung ~ nite lai takin/A sang ~ Pasian’ Tapa Zeisu aw | Jesus, Son of the Most High God/kikhopna inn sungah tokhom sang ~ | the most important seat in the synagogue/a masa ~ Piter kici, Simon | first Simon, who is called Peter/A mawhnei pha ~ ka hihna | my being the worst of sinners) (r:55.3.1/41.5.7/42.11.43/40.10.2/54.1.16) (q:draft)
Bel = (t:part) (w:most) (d:capitalised form of bel in titles, as in Siangtho Bel Mun, the Most Holy Place, and Sang Bel Pasian, God Most High) (e:Siangtho ~ Mun kici dei khat/Sang ~ Pasian’ Tapa kici ding hi | he will be called the Son of the Most High God/Siangtho ~ Munah paina lampi | the way into the Most Holy Place/Sang ~ Topa’ kamsangpa hong kici ding hi | you will be called a prophet of the Lord Most High/Sang ~ Pasian’ tate na hi ding uh hi | you will be children of the Most High God) (s:Pen) (b:bel) (r:58.9.3/42.1.32/58.9.8/42.1.76/42.6.35) (q:draft)
Bel = (t:name) (w:Bel) (d:the chief god of Babylon, also known as Marduk) (r:24.51.44/23.46.1/24.50.2) (q:draft)
bela = (t:part) (w:very/most) (d:bel, which marks the extreme of an order, with a joining it to what follows: a nunung bela piang, born at the very last) (e:khang a nunung ~ piang eite) (b:bel) (r:46.10.11) (q:draft)
bela = (t:v) (w:built against/adjoining) (d:bel, cling to or lean on, with a: built against or attached to a wall) (e:biakinn kawm pang ~ kibawl inndei neute) (b:bel) (r:26.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bela = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Bela) (d:a city in the plain of the Jordan, also called Zoar; the same name is borne by several men, among them the firstborn son of Benjamin and a king of Edom) (r:1.14.2/1.14.8)
belapin = (t:v) (w:add to) (d:apparently behlap, add, written without h, with in linking it to the following verb) (e:hih laite ~ a guan’ beh leh) (s:behlapin) (r:66.22.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
belawi = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bean) (d:a kind of bean, named among the grains and pulses used for bread) (e:mangbuh, mangbuhham, ~, beli, taang) (s:bepi) (r:26.4.9) (q:draft)
belh = (t:v) (w:take refuge in/rely on/trust in) (d:to go to someone for shelter and safety, most often said of trusting in God; a form of bel) (e:Topa ~ ding hoihzaw hi/a tate’ ~ theih ding ahi hi | he is one his children can take refuge in/Ka ~ ding suangpi hong hi in | be a rock for me to take refuge in/Eite ~ Suangpi, a nasepna kicing a | the Rock we take refuge in, his work is perfect) (s:muang) (a:taisan) (r:19.118.8/20.14.26/19.31.2/5.32.4) (q:draft)
belh = (t:n) (w:refuge/fortress/stronghold) (d:the one or the place that someone takes refuge in) (e:Jakob’ Pasian in eima ~ ahi hi/Topa in ama ~ ahi hi | the Lord is his refuge/ka gentheih hunin keima ~ na hi hi | you are my refuge in my time of trouble/ka munmuanhuai leh ka ~ | my stronghold and my refuge) (s:bukna/hutna/munkip/belhna) (r:19.46.7/19.59.16/19.14.6/10.22.3) (q:draft)
belh = (t:v) (w:cling to/hold fast to/stick to) (d:to stay fastened to someone or something, said of holding fast to God and also of a disease that will not leave) (e:note tungah tuate hong ~ ding hi/ama thupiakte zuih ding, amah ~ ding | to keep his commands and to hold fast to him/Na-aman’ phakna hong ~ tawntung ta hen | may Naaman's leprosy cling to you for ever/na tunga ngasa ~ khempeuh tawh | with all the fish sticking to you/Topa na Pasian uh na ~ theih nadingun | so that you may hold fast to the Lord your God) (s:toncip/lenkip) (r:5.28.60/6.22.5/12.5.27/26.29.4/6.23.6) (q:draft)
belhin = (t:n) (w:as a refuge/as shelter) (d:belh, refuge, with in: belhin nei, have as a place of shelter) (e:a liimnuai ~ a nei uh hi) (b:belh) (r:26.31.6) (q:draft)
belhna = (t:n) (w:refuge/shelter/hiding place) (d:belh, take refuge, with the noun suffix na: a place of refuge or the act of taking refuge) (e:bukna leh ~ hi ding hi/huihpi panin ~, guahpi panin bukna | a shelter from the wind, a refuge from the storm/ka biakna tau a ~ nangawn panin | even from my altar where he has taken refuge) (s:bukna/hutna/belh) (b:belh) (r:23.4.6/23.32.2/2.21.14) (q:draft)
belhpa = (t:n) (w:refuge) (d:the one in whom refuge is taken, said of God; pa marks a male person) (e:ka lum leh ka ~/gimna hong tun’ cianga kong ~ na hi hi | you are my refuge when disaster comes/keima ~ na hih manin | because you are my refuge/ama mite’ ~ hi a | he is the refuge of his people/ka suangpi, ka ~, ka lum | my rock, my refuge, my shield) (s:buknapa) (b:belh) (r:19.144.2/24.17.17/19.31.4/29.3.16/19.18.2) (q:draft)
belhsak = (t:v) (w:make stick to/cause to cling) (d:belh, cling to, with sak, cause) (e:nangma tungah ka ~ ding hi) (b:belh) (r:26.29.4) (q:draft)
belhtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to take refuge in/can rely on) (d:belh, take refuge in, with theih, can) (e:a tate’ ~ ding mi kician) (s:muantheih) (b:belh) (r:20.14.26) (q:draft)
beli = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:lentil) (d:a pulse named after belawi, bean, among the grains used for bread) (e:mangbuhham, belawi, ~, taang) (s:basan/besan) (r:26.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
Belial = (t:name) (w:Belial) (d:a name for the devil, the power of evil set against Christ) (r:47.6.15)
belin = (t:adv) (w:most/of all/at the most) (d:bel, most, with the marker in, after a descriptive word: a masa belin, first of all; a nunung belin, last of all; a tam belin, at the most) (e:Lungdamna Thu a masa ~ mipawl khempeuh/A nunung ~ a hun cing lopi-a suak | last of all, to one born out of due time/nih ahi zongin, a tam ~ thum ahi zongin | two, or at the most three/A masa ~ a kung | first the stalk) (b:bel) (r:41.13.10/46.15.8/46.14.27/41.4.28) (q:draft)
belin = (t:v) (w:cling to/rely on/take refuge in) (d:form of bel, cling to or take refuge in, with the linking suffix in; also after another verb in belin nei, have as the chief thing one relies on or dwells on) (e:suangpi pang peuh ~ toncip uh hi | they cling to the rocks/thuman mite in ~ lungmuangin om thei uh hi | the righteous take refuge in it and are safe) (s:beelin) (b:bel) (r:18.24.8/45.2.17/20.18.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
belna = (t:n) (w:the highest/the highest place/the utmost) (d:bel, most, with the noun suffix na: a sang belna is the highest place) (e:Van a sang ~-ah Pasian minthang ta hen/Van a sang ~-ah Hosanna | hosanna in the highest heaven/tokhom a sang ~-ah na tu kei un | do not sit in the highest seat/A sang ~-ah minthan’na om ta hen | glory in the highest) (b:bel) (r:42.2.14/41.11.10/42.14.8/42.19.38) (q:draft)
belnate = (t:n) (w:the highest ones/highest powers) (d:belna, the utmost, with the plural te; a sang belnate, those in the highest places) (e:a sang ~ ahi zongin) (b:belna) (r:51.1.16) (q:draft)
belpa = (t:n) (d:bel, most, with pa marking a man; a masa belpa, the very first man) (e:A masa ~ in a topa) (b:bel) (r:42.19.16) (q:draft)
belpei = (t:n) (w:griddle/flat pan) (d:flat cooking vessel; belpei kitam is a broken piece of it, a potsherd; also spelled beelpei) (e:~ dai tunga ki-em an tawh/~ tung khatah sathau tawh kibawl ding hi | it must be prepared with oil on a griddle/~ kitam a hiamte tawh kibang a | they are like sharp potsherds/meibung hita leh ~ hita leh kisuzan ding hi | whether oven or cooking pan, it must be broken) (s:beelpei) (r:3.2.5/3.7.9/3.6.21/18.41.30/3.11.35) (q:draft)
Belshazaar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belshazzar) (d:king of Babylon who saw the writing on the wall and was killed that night; a spelling of Belshazzar) (r:27.5.22)
Belshazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belshazzar) (d:king of Babylon in the time of Daniel, who saw the writing on the wall and was killed that night) (r:27.5.30/27.8.1)
Beltashazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belteshazzar) (d:the Babylonian name given to Daniel; a spelling of Belteshazzar) (r:27.4.18/27.4.19)
belte = (t:n) (w:those who take refuge/those who rely on) (d:bel, take refuge in, with the plural te: the people who shelter in or rely on someone) (e:amah a ~ khempeuh tungah/nang hong ~ khempeuh lungdam sak in | let all who take refuge in you be glad/na taklam khut hong ~’ Honpa aw | Saviour of those who take refuge at your right hand) (b:bel) (r:20.30.5/19.31.19/19.5.11/19.17.7) (q:draft)
belte = (t:n) (w:vessels) (d:spelling of beelte, pots or vessels, used as a figure for people who receive mercy) (e:hehpihna a ngah ~ ahi | they are vessels that receive mercy) (s:beelte) (r:45.9.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
Belteshazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belteshazzar) (d:the Babylonian name given to Daniel by the chief official of King Nebuchadnezzar) (r:27.2.26/27.4.8)
bem = (t:adj) (w:round/circular) (d:round in shape; also a round band or rim) (e:tua in a ~ hi a/tong lang a sang vial ~ khat om hi | there was a round band half a cubit high/a khawkte in sikli nei a, ~ lo hi | the panels were square, not round) (s:vial) (r:11.7.23/11.7.35/11.7.31) (q:draft)
bem = (t:adj) (d:in bem gial, marked with round spots or rings, said of animals, beside dung gial streaked) (e:dung gial, ~ gial/keeltal a dung gial leh a ~ gialte | the male goats that were streaked and those that were spotted) (r:1.31.10/1.30.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
bemeh = (t:n) (w:lentil stew/bean stew) (d:be, bean or lentil, with meh, cooked dish eaten with the staple) (e:Jakob in an leh ~ Esau pia hi) (r:1.25.34) (q:draft)
Ben = (t:see) <Ben-Hinnom>
Ben-ammi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Ammi) (d:son of Lot by his younger daughter, ancestor of the Ammonites) (e:a min ~ phuak hi) (r:1.19.38) (q:draft)
Ben-ejaakan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bene Jaakan) (d:a place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped on the way from Egypt) (e:~ ah giahphual sat uh hi) (r:4.33.31/5.10.6) (q:draft)
Ben-geber = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Geber) (d:one of Solomon's twelve district governors, in charge of Ramoth Gilead) (r:11.4.13) (q:draft)
Ben-Hinnom = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Ben Hinnom) (d:a valley on the south side of Jerusalem where children were burned at Topheth; followed by mualkuam, valley) (e:~ mualkuam-ah a tapate a tanute uh) (r:24.7.31/24.19.2) (q:draft)
Ben-om = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Oni) (d:the name Rachel gave Benjamin; the spelling Ben-om may be a misprint for Ben-oni) (e:amah in a min ~ ci hi) (r:1.35.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
Benabinadab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Abinadab) (d:one of Solomon's district governors, over Naphoth Dor, married to Solomon's daughter Taphath) (r:11.4.11)
Benaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Jehoiada, commander of David's bodyguard and later of Solomon's army) (r:10.8.18/10.23.30)
Benaiahte = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:Benaiah with te closing a list of names, Benaiah and the others; here a temple overseer under King Hezekiah) (b:Benaiah) (r:14.31.13)
Benammi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-ammi/Ben-Ammi) (d:son of Lot by his younger daughter, ancestor of the Ammonites) (r:1.19.38)
Bendeker = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Deker) (d:one of Solomon's district governors, over Makaz, Shaalbim and Beth Shemesh) (r:11.4.9)
Beneberak = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bene Berak) (d:a town in the territory of the tribe of Dan) (r:6.19.45)
Benejaakan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bene Jaakan) (d:a place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped on the way from Egypt) (r:4.33.31/4.33.32)
beng = (t:v) (w:hunt/fish) (d:go after animals or fish to catch them; sa beng hunt game, nga beng catch fish) (e:kei adingin sa va ~ in/Kei nga ~ dingin pai ning | I am going out to fish/a sanggampa ngen tawh ~ hi | he hunts his brother with a net/gamlakah sa a ~ | that hunts game in the wild) (s:gamvak) (r:1.27.3/33.5.8/43.21.3/33.7.2) (q:draft)
beng = (t:v) (w:slap/strike/clap) (d:hit with the open hand; paang beng slap the cheek, khut beng clap the hands, awm beng beat the breast) (e:ka paang a ~ dingin/Kei zong ka khut ka ~ ding a | I too will clap my hands/lungdamin a khut uh ~ ding hi | they will clap their hands for joy/dahin na awm uh ~ un | beat your breasts in grief/Kua in hong ~ ahi hiam, gen in | say who hit you) (s:beeng/bet) (r:18.16.10/26.21.17/34.3.19/23.32.12/41.14.65) (q:draft)
bengbengte = (t:n) (w:those who slap) (d:beng, slap, repeated to show a repeated action, with the plural te) (e:na paang uh a hong ~ na sang) (r:47.11.20) (q:draft)
Bengeber = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Geber) (d:one of Solomon's twelve district governors, in charge of Ramoth Gilead) (r:11.4.13)
bengin = (t:v) (w:clap/slap) (d:beng with the linking suffix in: strike with the open hand, khut beng clap the hands, paang beng slap the cheek; also of beng, hunt, as in sa bengin, hunting game) (e:Mikaiah a paang ~/amaute in a khut uh ~ | they clapped their hands/Note lungdamin khut ~, kipakin na diang uh a | you clapped your hands gladly and jumped for joy) (b:beng) (r:11.22.24/12.11.12/26.25.6) (q:draft)
bengkhia = (t:v) (w:drive away/scare away/chase off) (d:beng with khia, away: drive off birds or animals) (e:amaute a ~ ding mihing om lo ding hi) (s:notkhia) (b:beng) (r:5.28.26) (q:draft)
bengmang = (t:v) (w:hunt down) (d:beng, hunt, with mang, away altogether) (e:panin amaute a ~ ding uh hi) (r:24.16.16) (q:draft)
bengngong = (t:adj) (w:deaf) (d:unable to hear; bengngong kei in is do not be deaf, do not refuse to listen) (e:gul ~ tawh kibang uh hi/~, paumawl mi khat a kiangah a paipih uh | they brought to him a man who was deaf and could hardly speak/ka tungah ~ kei in | do not be deaf to me) (s:bilngong/ngong) (r:19.58.4/41.7.32/19.28.1) (q:draft)
Bengngongte = (t:name) (w:Bengngongte/the deaf) (d:bengngong, deaf, with the plural te, deaf people, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:bengngong) (r:41.7.37/40.11.5)
bengpa = (t:n) (w:hunter) (d:beng, hunt, with pa marking a man: one who hunts) (e:mual tungah vaka a ~ bangin) (s:sabengpa/sabeng) (b:beng) (r:9.26.20) (q:draft)
bengsak = (t:v) (w:let slap/offer to be slapped) (d:beng, slap, with sak: let someone slap, hold out the cheek to be slapped) (e:pang langkhat zong na ~ un) (b:beng) (r:42.6.29) (q:draft)
bengte = (t:n) (w:fishermen/fishers) (d:beng, catch, with the plural te: in ngasa bengte, those who catch fish) (e:Ngasa ~ in gunkuang sung panin paikhia/tuipi dungah ngasa ~ omin | fishermen will stand along the sea/ngasa ~ in a ngen uh pho ding uh hi | fishermen will spread out their nets/ngasa ~ thumin tau ding uh a | the fishermen will groan and lament) (s:ngabengte) (b:beng) (r:42.5.2/26.47.10/26.26.5/23.19.8) (q:draft)
bengtumsuk = (t:v) (w:beat down/bring low) (d:apparently beng, strike, with tum and suk, downward: strike down, of pride being brought low) (e:a khut uh tawh ~ ding uh hi) (r:23.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
