bilte = (t:n) (w:ears) (d:plural of bil, ear) (e:ka ~ in ngai ding hi/gilote’ siatna ka ~ in za khin ta hi | my ears have heard the downfall of the wicked/ama ~ kihong a | his ears are open/a za mite khempeuh’ ~ a vut ding siatna | disaster that will make the ears of all who hear of it tingle) (b:bil) (r:14.7.15/19.92.11/23.42.20/12.21.12) (q:draft)
bilteep = (t:n) (w:earlobe/lobe of the ear) (d:the soft lower part of the ear, from bil, ear, and teep, tip) (e:Aaron’ taklam ~ leh a taklam khutpi/mipa’ taklam ~, a taklam khutpi | the lobe of the right ear of the man and his right thumb) (r:3.8.23/3.14.14) (q:draft)
bilteepte = (t:n) (w:earlobes/lobes of the ears) (d:plural of bilteep, earlobe) (e:amau’ taklam ~ le amau’ taklam khutpite) (b:bilteep) (r:3.8.24) (q:draft)
bilun = (t:n) (w:with ears/ears) (d:bil, ear, with un, the marker in joined to the plural uh; ka bilun is with our own ears) (e:Ka ~ ka zakna uh tawh kizui-in) (b:bil) (r:13.17.20/10.7.22) (q:draft)
bilvang = (t:n) (w:loop/eyelet/eye of a needle) (d:a small hole or loop, from bil, ear, and vang, hole: the loops on the edge of a curtain that take a clasp, and in phim bilvang the eye of a needle) (e:puan khat tungah ~ sawmnga bawlin/phim ~ sungah kalaoh khat a lut ding | for a camel to go through the eye of a needle/a ~ sawmnga mah bawl hi | he made fifty loops there as well) (r:2.36.12/2.26.5/41.10.25/2.36.17) (q:draft)
bilvangte = (t:n) (w:loops) (d:bilvang, loop or eyelet on the edge of a curtain, with plural te) (e:a ~ khat leh khat kitang hi/a ~ sungah kilhnate guangin | putting the clasps into the loops/khau dum tawh a ~ na bawl ding hi | you shall make the loops of blue cord) (b:bilvang) (r:2.36.12/2.26.11/2.26.4) (q:draft)
