cikzethuai = (t:adj) (w:horrifying/repulsive/dreadful) (d:causing horror or disgust, a cikzethuai is a thing of horror) (e:ka vengte tungah a ~ ka hi a/amaute tungah a ~ khatin kei na hong bawl | you have made me a horror to them/note a ~ na hi ding uh hi | you will be a thing of horror/a ~, lamdangsakna, leh a dipkuathuai-in bawl hi | he made them an object of dread, astonishment and horror) (s:cikzet-huai/lauhuai/kihtakhuai/dipkuathuai) (r:19.31.11/5.28.37/19.88.8/5.28.25/14.29.8) (q:draft)
cikziat = (t:v) (w:loathe/be disgusted) (d:with huai, worthy of: a cikziat huai is repulsive, loathsome) (e:a ~ huai khatin kei nong bawl) (r:19.88.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
cil = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate nominative case) (e:a kipat ~/a kipat ~-in a tawpna ding thu ka pulak | I make known the end from the beginning/a kisat ~-a kipan tu ni ciang dong | from when it was first built until today) (r:1.1.1/23.46.10/24.32.31)
cil = (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to form verb past tense) (e:a kipat ~/lungdamna thu na zak ~ lai-un | when you first heard the gospel/a ~-a a itna zah sangin | more than he had loved her at first) (r:51.1.23/10.13.15)
cil = (t:conj) (w:beginning/at first) (d:early stage) (e:a kipat ~/a ~ a kipan/a kipat ~ panin pasal leh numei a piangsak | from the beginning he made male and female/Leitung a ~ panin | from the creation of the world/Zeisu in a ~ panin a thei hi | Jesus knew from the beginning/a ~ pek-a kipan a tawntungin | from the very beginning, forever) (r:41.10.6/66.13.8/43.6.65/35.1.12)
cil = (t:n) (w:spit/saliva) (d:Spit, the saliva of the mouth; cil sia is to spit, and cil tawh phih is to spit on someone.) (e:lei tungah a ~ sia a/~ tawh buan a bawl khit ciangin | after making mud with the saliva/Zeisu ~ tawh phih uh a | they spat on Jesus/a pa in ~ phih leh | if her father had spat) (r:43.9.6/41.8.23/40.27.30/4.12.14)
cila = (t:adv) (w:at the beginning/at first) (d:cil the early stage or beginning, with the ending a: at the beginning of; cila kipan is from the beginning of) (e:na khempeuh a pian’sak ~ kipan/a kipat ~ mual tunga om | set on high from the beginning) (s:cilin) (b:cil) (r:61.3.4/24.17.12) (q:draft)
cilai = (t:v) (w:still say/yet say) (d:ci, say, with lai, still: go on to say, say even so) (e:na ~ uh hi) (r:39.1.6) (q:draft)
cilbawl = (t:v) (w:be scarce/be sparing) (d:cilbawl loin an ne is eat food without scarcity, without having to be sparing; the exact sense is not clear) (e:~ loin an na nek nading uh) (r:5.8.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
cilcil = (t:v) (w:thresh/tread out) (d:cil thresh by treading, repeated to show continuing action: be busy threshing) (e:mangbuh a ~ lai takin a khuadak leh) (s:ancil/buhcil) (r:13.21.20) (q:draft)
cilesa = (t:n) (w:flesh/body/flesh and blood) (d:The flesh of the body; of kin, eima cilesa is our own flesh and blood.) (e:naupangno ~ bangin a ngei bangkikin/amah i sanggampa, eima ~ ahi hi | he is our brother, our own flesh/nangma ~ a ngei hong bangkikin | your flesh will be restored/leitung ~ a nei mite | people who have flesh and blood) (s:silesa) (a:kha) (r:12.5.14/1.37.27/12.5.10/58.2.14) (q:draft)
cilgawp = (t:v) (w:thresh/trample) (d:cil, tread or thresh, with gawp, thoroughly or violently) (e:a ~ ding ahihlam phawk lo uh) (s:tuancil) (r:33.4.12) (q:draft)
cilin = (t:adv) (w:at the beginning/in the beginning/at first) (d:cil, the beginning, with the ending in: at first, in the beginning, often as a kipat cilin.) (e:a kipat ~ tua bang ahi kei hi/a ~ a nungzuite in a theih loh uh hangin | though at first his disciples did not understand/a kipat ~, numei leh pasal a piangsak hi | at the beginning he made them male and female/Israel kong muh ~ hoih mahmah a | when I first found Israel it was very good) (s:cila) (a:nunungin) (b:cil) (r:40.19.8/40.19.4/43.12.16/28.9.10) (q:draft)
cilna = (t:n) (w:winepress/press) (d:place of treading; leenggah cilna is the place where grapes are trodden for their juice) (e:leenggah ~ ah kuamah in leengtui suk lo/Leenggah ~ panin leenggahtui ka luang khiasak nawn kei | I no longer make wine flow from the presses/kumpipa’ leenggah ~ phual ciang dong | as far as the royal winepresses/leenggah ~-a leenggah a cilpa’ puan | the garment of one treading grapes in the winepress) (s:leenggahcilna/leenggahsukna/sukna) (b:cil) (r:23.16.10/23.63.2/24.48.33/38.14.10) (q:draft)
cilna = (t:n) (w:beginning/start/first time) (d:cil, the first stage, with the noun ending na: the beginning of something, as in kipat cilna, the very beginning, and khualzin cilna, the first journey) (e:Tuate khempeuh in gimna kipat ~ ahi hi/Tuate in gimna kipat ~ ahi hi | these are the beginning of birth pains/khualzin ~ kipan uh hi | they set out for the first time/Kisim ~-ah mi pawlkhat a tuk ciangin | when some fall in the first attack) (s:kipatna/patna) (a:tawpna) (b:cil) (r:40.24.8/41.13.8/4.10.13/10.17.9) (q:draft)
cilna = (t:n) (w:threshing floor) (d:in an cilna, the place where grain is trodden out) (e:an ~ pana biakna-in na pia ding/Na an ~ uh leh na leenggah sukna panun | from your threshing floor and your winepress) (s:ancilna/buhcilna) (b:cil) (r:4.15.20/5.16.13) (q:draft)
cilpa = (t:n) (w:treader/one who treads) (d:cil, tread, with pa marking a man: the man who treads grapes in the winepress) (e:leenggah cilna-a leenggah a ~’ puan) (r:23.63.2) (q:draft)
cilphih = (t:v) (w:spit on/spit at) (d:Spit on someone as an insult; from cil, saliva.) (e:a maitang ~ uh a/mite in hih thu za-in kei hong ~ uh hi | people hear of it and spit on me/zahpihin, simmawhin, ~ ding uh hi | they will mock, insult and spit on him/mi pawlkhat in ~ uh a | some spat on him) (s:cilpih) (r:40.26.67/41.15.19/18.17.6/42.18.32/41.14.65) (q:draft)
cilphihin = (t:v) (w:spitting on) (d:cilphih, spit on, with in linking it to the following verb) (e:~, satin a that ding uh hi) (b:cilphih) (r:41.10.34) (q:draft)
cilphihna = (t:n) (w:spitting) (d:noun form of cilphih, spit on: being spat on as an insult) (e:bawlsiatna leh ~ a thuak ding hi/maizumna leh ~ panin ka maitang ka hei kei | I did not turn my face from shame and spitting) (b:cilphih) (r:42.18.32/23.50.6) (q:draft)
cilphuan = (t:n) (w:foam/froth/saliva) (d:foam or running spittle at the mouth; cilphuan bua is to foam at the mouth) (e:a kam sung pan ~ bua a/~ bua-in a kipeek sawnsawn hi | he rolled around foaming at the mouth/a khamul tungah a ~ kai suk sak hi | he let his saliva run down his beard) (r:41.9.18/9.21.13/41.9.20) (q:draft)
cilpih = (t:v) (w:spit at/spit on) (d:cil, saliva, with pih: spit on someone in contempt) (e:kei hong ~ uh hi) (s:cilphih) (b:cil) (r:18.17.6) (q:draft)
cilsate = (t:n) (w:threshed grain) (d:cil, thresh, with sa, already done, and plural te: what has been threshed) (e:A buh ~ a zapsiang nadingin) (r:42.3.17) (q:draft)
ciltang = (t:n) (w:testicle) (e:A ~ a kitam ahih kei leh/meima nei leh ~ kitam mi | one with sores or crushed testicles) (r:5.23.1/3.21.20) (q:draft)
ciltangte = (t:n) (w:testicles) (d:plural of ciltang) (e:A ~ a sanim, a kisukham) (b:ciltang) (r:3.22.24) (q:draft)
cilte = (t:n) (w:firstborn) (d:cil first with the plural te, after tapa son: tapa cilte is firstborn sons) (e:Na tapa ~ khempeuh uh na tanh ding/Na tapa ~ uh keima' tungah nong pia ding | you shall give me your firstborn sons) (s:tacilte) (b:cil) (r:2.34.20/2.22.29) (q:draft)
ciltel = (t:adj) (w:fine/small) (d:describes the manna lying on the ground, something small and thin like flakes; the exact sense is not clear) (e:a pum ~, a khal) (r:2.16.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
cilun = (t:conj) (w:when first/at first) (d:cil at first, in the early stage, with the plural ending un: when they first did something) (e:Tua lai-ah a ten ~ amaute in) (b:cil) (r:12.17.25) (q:draft)
cilvui = (t:v) (w:thresh to powder/grind fine) (d:cil thresh or tread, with vui fine as dust: thresh grain until it is crushed) (e:Mi khatpeuh in antang ~ ahi hiam) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
cim = (t:v) (w:fall/collapse) (d:Fall down or cave in, said of a city, a wall or a mountain.) (e:Babilon khuapi a ~ hi/Ko tungah hong ~ in | fall on us/mi tul-sawmnih leh tulsagih tungah kulhpi ~ hi | the wall fell on twenty-seven thousand men/Babilon khua kulhpi a ~ ta hi | the wall of Babylon has fallen) (s:puk/kicim) (r:66.18.2/66.6.16/11.20.30/24.51.44) (q:draft)
cim = (t:v) (w:be weary of/have enough/be tired of) (d:Have had enough of something, be sated or fed up with it.) (e:Mit in a muh ~ thei lo a/bil in a zak ~ thei lo hi | the ear never has enough of hearing/gim lo ~ loin na thuak | you have endured without growing weary) (s:cimtak) (r:21.1.8/66.2.3) (q:draft)
cimang = (t:v) (w:die out/perish/be wiped out) (d:Die out and leave no descendants; said of a person or family whose line comes to an end.) (e:Migilote in sihna tuakin ~ a/Note na ~ ding uh a | you will die out/Pasian ngaihsun lote mi ~ suak a | the godless become barren/A ~ khinin a kingaihsun hih mi khat | this one man, thought to be as good as dead) (s:cimit/mangthang) (r:20.12.7/34.1.14/18.15.34/58.11.12) (q:draft)
cimawh = (t:adj) (w:needy/helpless/destitute) (d:In want or distress with no one to help; also used as a verb, be helpless.) (e:a ~ mite tungah huhna pia hi/ahih manin kei ka ~ hi | so I am helpless/ka mite a ~ uh hi | my people are destitute/A zawng a ~ a kicial nasempa | a hired worker who is poor and needy) (s:zawng/zawngkhal) (a:hau) (r:20.31.20/19.69.20/25.1.16/5.24.14) (q:draft)
cimawhin = (t:adv) (w:helplessly/in distress/desperately) (d:cimawh with the adverb ending in: in a helpless or distressed way) (e:tuu leh bawngte ~ ham uh a/amau zong ~ huhna a nget ciangun | when they too cry for help in distress/galhang pente nangawn ~ kap ding uh hi | even the bravest warriors will weep in distress/Eite ~ i om laitakin | while we were still helpless) (b:cimawh) (r:29.1.18/20.21.13/36.1.14/45.5.6) (q:draft)
cimawhpa = (t:n) (w:needy man/the needy) (d:cimawh, needy, with pa marking a man) (e:mi ~’ taklam-ah amah hong ding) (s:zawngpa) (a:haupa) (b:cimawh) (r:19.109.31) (q:draft)
cimawhsak = (t:v) (w:leave helpless/afflict/fail) (d:make someone helpless or destitute, cimawh with the causative sak) (e:note hong ~ lo ding a/nang hong ~ loin, zong hong nusia lo ding | he will not fail you nor forsake you/Pasian in kei hong zawngkhalsak hong ~ ahih manin | because God has afflicted me) (s:zawngkhalsak) (b:cimawh) (r:5.31.6/18.30.11/5.31.8) (q:draft)
cimawhte = (t:n) (w:the needy/the poor/the destitute) (d:people who are in need, often as mi cimawhte) (e:a ~ dahpih hilo ka hi hiam/mi ~’ nuntakna hon hi | he saves the lives of the needy/A ginalote leh a ~ hon un | rescue the weak and the needy/mi ~’ thungetna kin-in | attending to the prayer of the destitute) (s:mizawngte/zawngte/cimmawhte) (a:haute/mihaute) (b:cimawh) (r:18.30.25/19.72.13/19.82.4/19.102.17) (q:draft)
cimbeng = (t:n) (w:glaze/silver dross) (d:a coating smeared on an earthen pot, where the NIV has silver dross) (e:~ kizut leibel tawh kibang hi) (r:20.26.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimin = (t:v) (w:collapse/fall down) (d:form of cim with the linking suffix in, collapsing and then going on to the next action) (e:khuapi seh sawm suah seh khat ~/Mualte pukin, keente ~ | the mountains fall and the cliffs crumble/a khuapite uh ~ kuamah teng lo hi | their towns have fallen and no one lives there) (s:pukin) (b:cim) (r:66.11.13/26.38.20/24.2.15) (q:draft)
cimit = (t:v) (w:perish/be wiped out/die out) (d:be destroyed so that none is left) (e:a sia ~ na hi nai kei) (s:cimang/mangthang) (r:39.3.6) (q:draft)
cimitna = (t:n) (w:complete destruction/total ruin) (d:cimit come to a complete end, with the noun suffix na; in siat cimitna, total destruction) (e:siat ~ a pian’ loh nadingin) (b:cimit) (r:14.12.12) (q:draft)
cimkhiasak = (t:v) (w:make collapse/bring down) (d:cim, fall or collapse, with khia, out, and causative sak: cause a wall to fall down) (e:a khuapi kulh a ~ uh hi) (s:cimsak) (r:58.11.30) (q:draft)
cimmai = (t:v) (w:collapse/fall down flat) (d:of a wall: cim fall down, here fall flat to the ground) (e:Khuapikulh ~ ding a, mi khempeuh/nakpitakin awng uh a, kulhpi ~-in | they gave a loud shout and the wall collapsed) (s:cim/cimsuk) (r:6.6.5/6.6.20) (q:draft)
cimmawhte = (t:n) (w:the needy/needy people) (d:plural, another spelling of cimawh, needy, with te) (e:Mizawng mi ~ khem-in) (s:cimawhte/mizawngte) (r:26.18.12) (q:draft)
cimsa = (t:adj) (w:fallen/broken down/collapsed) (d:cim fall down or collapse, with sa already done) (e:a ~ kulh khempeuh) (s:kicimsa) (b:cim) (r:14.32.5) (q:draft)
cimsak = (t:v) (w:bring down/make collapse/shake) (d:cim fall down, with the causative sak: cause walls to fall; the NIV has tremble) (e:gin’na in khuapi kulhte ~ ding a) (s:cimkhiasak) (b:cim) (r:26.26.10) (q:draft)
cimsuk = (t:v) (w:collapse/fall down/come crashing down) (d:cim, collapse, with suk, downward; of a wall or building, also bring a building down on people) (e:mi khempeuh tungah innpi ~ hi/Babilon khua kulhpi lei lakah ~ ding a | the wall of Babylon will be leveled to the ground) (s:cim/puksuk) (b:cim) (r:7.16.30/24.51.58) (q:draft)
cimtaak = (t:v) (w:be weary of/be tired of) (d:another spelling of cimtak) (e:kei nong ~ hi) (s:cimtak) (r:23.43.22) (q:draft)
cimtak = (t:v) (w:be weary of/be tired of/loathe) (d:Be fed up with something or someone, be tired of doing something.) (e:Ka nuntakna ka ~ ta hi/na hoih sep ding ~ kei ni | let us not grow weary of doing good/gamtat ding na ~ ngei het kei ta un | never tire of doing right/Israel aw, kei nong ~ hi | Israel, you have grown weary of me) (s:cim/cimtaak) (b:cim) (r:18.10.1/53.3.13/48.6.9/23.43.22) (q:draft)
cimtakhuai = (t:adj) (w:wearisome/tiresome/troublesome) (d:cimtak, be weary of, with huai, worthy of: such as to make one weary) (e:~ ka sa kei a) (r:50.3.1) (q:draft)
cimtakin = (t:v) (w:be weary of/be tired of/be fed up with) (d:cimtak be fed up with someone, with the linking ending in) (e:hong ~ hong mudah kha ding hi) (b:cimtak) (r:20.25.17) (q:draft)
cimtakta = (t:v) (w:have grown weary of/be disgusted with) (d:cimtak, be weary of, with ta marking a change that has now come about) (e:hih na lunggulh mite na ~ hi) (b:cimtak) (r:26.23.22) (q:draft)
cimzan = (t:v) (w:be levelled/collapse completely) (d:of a city: cim fall down, here be brought down flat) (e:a khuapi pen ~ ding hi) (r:23.32.19) (q:draft)
cin = (t:v) (w:be completed/be fulfilled/come to an end) (d:Of a period of time, be full or reach its end; written cin’ before another word, as in kum sagih a cin’ ciangin, at the end of seven years.) (e:Kum sawmsagih a ~’ khit ciangin/Kum sagih a ~’ simin | at the end of every seven years/Kum tul a ~’ khit ciangin | when the thousand years are over/a ni a ~’ ciangin a gil kial hi | when the days were ended he was hungry) (r:24.25.12/5.15.1/66.20.7/42.4.2) (q:draft)
cin = (t:v) (w:plant/sow) (e:huanah a ~ ankam tang tawh kibang hi) (s:suan/ciin) (r:42.13.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
cin = (t:part) (d:Ending of a conditional clause addressed to you, after le or le uh: hong ciahkik le uh cin is if you return; it also expresses a wish.) (e:hong ciahkik le uh ~/Hong hilh thei le uh ~ | if you can teach me/Babilon kumpipa’ na sepsak le uh ~ | if you serve the king of Babylon/biakinn kongkhakte khak le uh ~ ka ut hi | I wish you would shut the temple doors) (r:38.1.3/20.8.32/18.6.24/24.40.9/39.1.10) (q:draft)
cina = (t:adj) (w:sick/ill) (d:Sick, ill; also used as a verb, be ill or fall sick, often as cina-in om.) (e:Jeroboam’ tapa Abijah a ~ hi/Lazaras kici mi khat ~-in a om hi | a man named Lazarus was sick/tua nasempa ~-in a si dek tak hi | that servant was sick and about to die/Hezekiah ~-in si dektak a | Hezekiah became ill and nearly died) (a:cidam) (r:11.14.1/25.5.17/43.11.1/42.7.2/14.32.24) (q:draft)
cina = (t:n) (w:sick person/the sick) (d:A sick person, or sick people as a group.) (e:~ dangte hong pai uh a/~ khempeuh a damsak hi | he healed all the sick/~ mi tampi sathau zutin a damsak uh hi | they anointed many sick people with oil and healed them/Sabbath ni-in ~ damsak ding | to heal the sick on the Sabbath) (r:44.28.9/41.3.10/40.12.15/41.6.13/42.14.3) (q:draft)
cinapa = (t:n) (w:sick man/invalid/patient) (d:cina, sick, with -pa marking a man: the man who is sick) (e:~ in an ne zo lo a/lupna tawh ~ a khaisuk uh hi | they lowered the sick man on his mat/Tua ~ kiangah Paul in lut a | Paul went in to that sick man/siampipa in ni sagih sung ~ khumcip ding hi | the priest shall isolate the sick man for seven days) (b:cina) (r:18.33.20/43.5.7/41.2.4/44.28.8/3.13.4) (q:draft)
cinasak = (t:v) (w:make sick/strike with illness) (d:causative of cina, sick) (e:Lamet tun lohna in lungsim ~ a/Topa’ vantungmi in Herod ~ a | an angel of the Lord struck Herod with illness) (s:natsak) (a:damsak) (b:cina) (r:20.13.12/44.12.23) (q:draft)
cinasakin = (t:v) (w:making sick/striking with disease) (d:cinasak, make sick, with in linking it to the following verb; said here of plants struck with blight) (e:na ankungte uh ~ a kang dikdekin) (b:cinasak) (r:30.4.9) (q:draft)
cinat = (t:adj) (w:sick/ill) (d:form of cina used before another word such as thu, laitak or ciangin: being sick, the fact of being sick) (e:amaute a ~ uh ciangin/Lazaras’ ~ thu a zak ciangin | when he heard that Lazarus was sick/ka ~ laitakin nong veh uh a | when I was sick you looked after me/a sanggamnu Tamar hangin ~ lawh hi | he made himself ill because of his sister Tamar) (s:cina) (a:cidam) (b:cina) (r:19.35.13/43.11.6/40.25.36/10.13.2) (q:draft)
cinate = (t:n) (w:the sick/sick people) (d:plural of cina: people who are sick; cinate damsak is heal the sick) (e:tua munah ~ a damsak hi/~ khempeuh a damsak hi | he healed all the sick/~ damsak ding ahi zongin a sawl hi | he also sent them to heal the sick/~ in damna ngah ding ahi zongin | and for the sick to receive healing) (s:micinate/veite) (a:cidamte) (b:cina) (r:40.19.2/42.5.31/40.14.14/42.9.2/42.5.15) (q:draft)
cinatna = (t:n) (w:sickness/disease/illness) (d:cinat, be sick, with the noun suffix na: the state of being ill, or a particular disease; cinatna vei is suffer from a disease) (e:Mihingte’ lungsim in ~ thuak zo sak/~ nam tuamtuam a vei tampi damsak a | he healed many who had various diseases/Dawi gilo lut leh ~ a damsak numeite | women who had been cured of evil spirits and diseases/~ dam a, dawi gilote a paikhia uh hi | the illnesses were cured and the evil spirits left) (s:natna/lunatna) (a:cidamna/damna) (b:cinat) (r:20.18.14/42.7.21/41.1.34/42.8.2/44.19.12) (q:draft)
cinatnate = (t:n) (w:diseases/sicknesses) (d:plural of cinatna: the different sicknesses that people suffer from) (e:~ a damsak dingin kuankhia sakin/Topa in a natsakna ~ a muh uh ciangin | when they see the diseases with which the Lord has afflicted it) (s:natnate) (b:cinatna) (r:42.9.2/5.29.22) (q:draft)
cinatsakna = (t:n) (w:affliction with sickness/sickness) (d:the making of someone sick, sickness sent upon a person) (e:Pasian in ~ tawh mihingte thuhilh a) (r:18.33.19) (q:draft)
