citengah = (t:adv) (w:in every/at every/everywhere) (d:citeng every with the place marker ah, after a noun; mun citengah is in every place, in all directions) (e:mun ~ ka thehthang ding a/Kongzing ~ milim biak nading mun na bawl a | you built places for idol worship in every street/Konglak mun ~ a tate uh kisatlum hi | their children were dashed to death at every street corner/kitotna le kiselna, mun ~ om hi | strife and conflict are everywhere) (b:citeng) (r:26.12.14/26.16.31/34.3.10/35.1.3) (q:draft)
cithak = (t:n) (w:sore/scall/itch) (d:an itching or festering disease of the skin, in the laws about skin diseases) (e:a ~ in a vun sung a lawh/mit hoih lo leh ~ a vei | one who has a bad eye or an itching disease/meima lip neite leh ~ tawh | with scabby sores and the itch) (r:3.13.35/3.21.20/5.28.27) (q:draft)
cithei = (t:v) (w:prosper/flourish/be well off) (d:be in a good and prosperous state; a cithei-in bawl kik means restore the fortunes of) (e:A gam sung uh ~ semsem leh/na khuaneute zong na ~ kik ding uh hi | your daughter towns too will prosper again/amaute a ~-in ka bawl kik ding hi | I will make them prosper again/A tawpna-ah note na ~ kik ding uh hi | in the end you will prosper again) (s:daupai) (r:28.10.1/26.16.53/26.16.55/26.39.25/36.3.20) (q:draft)
citheibek = (t:v) (w:only prosper) (d:cithei, prosper, with bek, only; citheibek loin is not only prospering) (e:Mi gamtatsiate ahihleh ~ loin) (r:39.3.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
citheikik = (t:v) (w:prosper again/flourish again) (d:cithei, prosper, with kik, again) (e:Amaute khangin ~ ding uh a) (b:cithei) (r:28.1.11) (q:draft)
citheisak = (t:v) (w:make prosper/restore) (d:causative of cithei, prosper; with kik, restore someone to former prosperity) (e:Topa in Job ~ kik a/nang Jerusalem zong kong ~ kik ding hi | I will restore you too, Jerusalem/amaute, ~ kik ding hi | he will make them prosper again) (s:daupaisak) (b:cithei) (r:18.42.10/26.16.53/36.2.7) (q:draft)
citheisakkik = (t:v) (w:restore the fortunes of/make prosperous again) (d:citheisak, make prosper, with kik, again) (e:Topa in Job ~ a/nang Jerusalem zong kong ~ ding hi | I will restore your fortunes too, Jerusalem) (s:hausakkik) (b:citheisak) (r:18.42.10/36.2.7/26.16.53) (q:draft)
citheite = (t:n) (w:the prosperous/those of high standing) (d:cithei, be well off, with plural te: people who are well off and respected) (e:Gentail mi numei ~ holhthawh uh a) (b:cithei) (r:44.13.50) (q:draft)
citheizaw = (t:adj) (w:more prosperous) (d:cithei, prosper, with zaw, more) (e:a ~ a tamzaw-in note hong bawl) (b:cithei) (r:5.30.5) (q:draft)
cithuah = (t:v) (w:add/say further/also say) (d:ci, say, with thuah, add on: say something more after what has already been said) (e:hong ~ lai hi/~ lai veve hi | he also went on to say) (s:genthuah/genbeh) (r:26.8.13/11.22.28/59.2.11) (q:draft)
citna = (t:n) (w:generosity/willingness/kindness) (d:a free and open heart in giving; citna tawh, generously or willingly) (e:~ tawh tampi na pia ding hi/lungsim ~ a nei peuhmah | everyone who has a willing heart/mizawngte tungah ~ in Pasian zahtakna ahi hi | kindness to the poor is honouring God/Topa tungah ~ tawh a kipia na ahi hi | it is a thing freely given to the Lord) (s:piaknopna/citpiakna) (r:5.15.14/13.29.17/2.35.5/20.14.31/15.8.28) (q:draft)
Citna = (t:name) (w:Citna)
citpiak = (t:v) (w:give generously/be generous) (d:cit generous with piak give: give freely to people) (e:Amah in mi ~ ngitngetin) (r:19.37.26) (q:draft)
citpiakna = (t:n) (w:generosity/generous giving) (d:citpiak, give generously, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ tawh a tampi a vawhte) (s:citna) (b:citpiak) (r:47.9.6) (q:draft)
cizaw = (t:v) (w:say rather/say instead) (d:ci, say, with zaw, rather: say this and not the other thing) (e:a ~ ding uh hi/na ~ uh hi | you would say instead) (s:genzaw) (b:ci) (r:24.16.15/42.17.8) (q:draft)
cizo = (t:v) (w:have said) (d:ci, say, with zo marking that the action is done) (e:hong ~ hi) (b:ci) (r:5.31.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
da = (t:todo) (q:draft, occurs only in aktui da kang in Job 6.6, taken as the white of an egg; the meaning of da by itself cannot be told from the verse)
daai = (t:n) (w:hedge/fence) (d:a fence or hedge put round a field or a person to protect it) (e:A ~ ka lakhia ding a/a kimkotah Pasian in ~ a khaknelh mipa | a man whom God has hedged in on every side/a kimkotah ~ khan hi lo na hi hiam | have you not put a hedge around him) (s:gawl) (r:23.5.5/18.3.23/18.1.10) (q:draft)
daai = (t:v) (w:become calm/grow still/be quiet) (d:of the sea or of noise, become calm) (e:uh leh tuipi a ~ pah hi/no adingin tuipi a hong ~ ding hi | the sea will become calm for you) (s:daih) (r:32.1.15/32.1.12) (q:draft)
daaisak = (t:v) (w:calm/still/make subside) (d:daai, become calm, with causative sak; said here of anger) (e:na hehna ~ in la) (s:daisak) (b:daai) (r:2.32.12) (q:draft)
daan = (t:n) (w:punishment/penalty) (d:what a wrongdoer is made to suffer for a wrong; daan pia is punish, daan thuak is be punished) (e:muhna-ah mawhneite ~ pia hi/Izipt, ~ ka piak ciangin | when I inflict punishment on Egypt/amau’ haina mah in ~ thuak sak hi | their own folly brings punishment on them/ama thuak ding ~ mah thuaksak zaw in | rather let him bear the penalty he deserves) (s:gawtna/gimpiakna/daantatna) (a:thaman) (r:18.34.26/47.2.6/26.30.19/20.16.22/20.19.19) (q:draft)
daang = (t:v) (w:turn pale/be pale) (d:of the face or the blood, lose colour from fear) (e:a mel ~ semsem a/kumpipa lau lua mahmah a, a mai ~ gawpin | the king was very afraid and his face turned pale/ka meel a ~ gawp hi | my face turned pale) (r:27.5.9/27.5.6/27.7.28) (q:draft)
daanggawp = (t:v) (w:turn pale/turn deathly pale) (d:daang turn pale, with gawp completely) (e:ka mel a ~ hi/a maitang uh ~ hi | their faces turn pale) (b:daang) (r:27.7.28/29.2.6) (q:draft)
daangkoih = (t:v) (w:forsake/set aside/neglect) (d:put someone aside, have nothing more to do with) (e:Na lawmte ~ kei inla) (s:nusiat/taisan) (r:20.27.10) (q:draft)
daangsak = (t:v) (w:make pale/let turn pale) (d:daang turn pale, with the causative sak: let the face lose its colour) (e:lungkham lua-in na mel ~ ngeingai zenzen/na mai ~ zenzen na hi hiam | why do you let your face turn so pale) (s:sidaangsak) (b:daang) (r:27.5.10) (q:draft)
daanpia = (t:v) (w:punish/repay) (d:daan, punishment, with pia, give) (e:Topa in a galte a ~ a) (s:daantat/gawt) (r:23.66.6) (q:draft)
daanpiak = (t:v) (w:punish) (d:daan punishment with piak, the form of pia give used before another word; daanpiak ni is the day of punishment) (e:minam khempeuh ~ nadingin a kizan ahi hi/~ ni ahi ding hi | it will be the day of punishment) (s:daantat/daantah/gimpiak) (b:daanpia) (r:23.14.26/42.21.22) (q:draft)
daanpiakna = (t:n) (w:punishment) (d:daanpiak, punish, with the noun suffix na; daanpiakna hai is the cup of punishment) (e:Topa in ~ hai, note hong dawnsak) (s:daantatna/gawtna/gimpiakna) (a:thaman) (b:daanpiak) (r:35.2.16) (q:draft)
daantah = (t:v) (w:punish) (d:make someone suffer for a wrong; daantah ni or daantah hun is the day or time of punishment, daantah nading is for punishing) (e:Pasian in mihingte ~ nading ahi a/ka ~ hun ciangin | at the time when I punish them/amaute ~ ding ka genkholhnate | my warnings that I would punish them/Vanglianpen Topa in amaute ~ ding a ngimna hangin | because of what the Lord Almighty plans in order to punish them) (s:daantat/gawt/gimpiak) (r:18.37.13/24.9.25/24.11.23/26.6.10/23.19.17) (q:draft)
daantahna = (t:n) (w:punishment) (d:daantah, punish, with the noun suffix na: the punishing of a wrong, or the suffering it brings) (e:Mite’ thuak dinga kilawm ~ mah/Tua kong ~ hangin | because of that punishment of mine on you/~ i thuak ding hi | we will be punished/amaute tungah ~ tuikhang bangin ka tungsak ding hi | I will bring punishment on them like a flood) (s:daantatna/gawtna/daan) (a:thaman) (b:daantah) (r:28.4.9/26.5.10/12.7.9/28.5.10) (q:draft)
daantat = (t:v) (w:punish) (d:give someone the penalty for wrongdoing; built from daan, law or penalty, and tat, strike) (e:leitung kumpite ~ ding hi/Hih thute hangin amaute ~ lo ding ka hi hiam | should I not punish them for these things/No a mite kong ~ ding a | I will punish your people/Pasian in a mawhte mahmah ~ hen la | let God punish the guilty themselves) (s:daantah/dantah/daanpiak/gimpiak) (a:maisak) (r:23.24.21/18.21.19/24.5.29/26.5.10) (q:draft)
daantatin = (t:v) (w:punishing) (d:daantat, punish, with in linking it to the following verb) (e:amah a langpangte ~, a galte thukkik) (s:gawtin) (b:daantat) (r:34.1.2) (q:draft)
daantatna = (t:n) (w:punishment/retribution/judgment) (d:penalty given for wrongdoing; daantat, punish, with the noun suffix na; daantatna thuak is to suffer punishment) (e:migilote’ thaman in ~ ahi hi/bang zah a lianzaw ~ a thuak ding | how much greater punishment he will suffer/~ thuak ding cih kihtakhuai | the fearful prospect of suffering punishment/kisiat tawntungna ahi mawhna’ ~ a thuak ding uh hi | they will suffer the punishment of sin, which is everlasting destruction) (s:daantahna/dantahna/gimpiakna/gawtna) (b:daantat) (r:20.10.16/58.10.29/58.10.27/53.1.9) (q:draft)
daantatpa = (t:n) (w:punisher/one who punishes) (d:daantat, punish, with pa marking a man: the one who punishes) (e:note a hong ~ ka hihna) (b:daantat) (r:26.7.9) (q:draft)
daantatsakin = (t:v) (w:keeping under punishment/causing to be punished) (d:daantat, punish, with causative sak and linking in) (e:Ni dongin ~ kikhum nading) (b:daantat) (r:61.2.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
daante = (t:n) (w:punishments/penalties) (d:plural of daan; mawhna daante is the penalties of sin, where the NIV has transgressions) (e:i mawhna ~ gamlapi-ah amah in) (b:daan) (r:19.103.12) (q:draft)
daantuah = (t:v) (w:be punished/meet punishment) (d:receive the penalty one deserves; daan, penalty, with tuah, meet with; daantuah ni is the day of punishment) (e:na ~ ni ding hita hi/a ~ nading uh hun tungta ahih manin | because the time for their punishment has come/Hadrak gamte’ ~ nading Topa in thukhen zo a | the Lord has passed judgment for the punishment of the land of Hadrak/migilote’ ~ ding teng tuak zawsop a | they meet with what the wicked ought to suffer) (s:kidaantat/gimthuak) (r:26.21.25/38.9.1/26.21.29/21.8.14) (q:draft)
daantuahna = (t:n) (w:punishment) (d:daantuah meet with punishment, with the noun suffix na: the punishment that someone receives) (e:a ~ uh kibang ding hi/na ~, numei honpi en sak ding | they will make a crowd of women watch your punishment) (s:daantatna/daantahna/gawtna) (b:daantuah) (r:26.14.10/26.16.41) (q:draft)
