dah = (t:v) (w:mourn/grieve/be sad) (d:feel sorrow, above all over a death or a loss; the opposite of lungdam, be glad) (e:Zeisu tawh kipawlte ~ a/David hangin amah ~ hi | he was grieved because of David/Lo khote aw, ~ un | mourn, you farmers/kammal hangin a ~ pen uh hi | they grieved most because of the word) (a:lungdam/kipak) (r:41.16.10/1.27.41/9.20.34/29.1.11/44.20.38)
dahhuai = (t:adj) (w:sad/grievous/miserable/pitiful) (d:causing sorrow or deserving pity; dah, be sad, with huai, worthy of; a dahhuai mahmah hi often stands where English has woe) (e:a ~ nuntakna khat ahi hi/A ~ mahmah thu in | a most grievous thing is this/kei a dingin a ~ mahmah ahi hi | it is most grievous for me, woe to me/Hih mite a dingin ~ mahmah hi | woe to these people) (s:lungkhamhuai) (a:lungdamhuai) (r:21.4.8/21.5.16/46.9.16/65.1.11) (q:draft)
dahhuaisa = (t:v) (w:be distressed/be grieved/be outraged) (d:dahhuai, grievous, with sa, feel or consider: find something grievous) (e:~ mahmah uh ahih manin) (b:dahhuai) (r:40.18.31) (q:draft)
dahin = (t:adv) (w:mourning/grieving/in sorrow) (d:dah, mourn, with the linking ending in: grieving, while doing the action of the next verb) (e:Abraham ~ kap a/khakunin ~ ka om hi | I was in mourning/a zak ciangin ~ ama puante balkeek a | when he heard it he tore his clothes in grief/~ a dip uh hum uh hi | mourning, they beat their breasts) (s:khakunin) (a:lungdamin/kipakin) (b:dah) (r:1.23.2/27.10.2/23.37.1/34.2.7) (q:draft)
dahlekah = (t:n) (w:mourning and weeping/lament) (d:dah, mourn, le, and, kah, weep, written as one word) (e:~ thu le thumletau thute) (r:26.2.10) (q:draft)
dahlua = (t:see) <dahlua-in>
dahlua-in = (t:adv) (w:in great sorrow/with deep grief) (d:dah, grieve, with lua, too much, and the ending in: overcome with grief while doing the next action) (e:khangham khit nungin ~ ka si ding hi/Job ~ a puan balkek a | Job in great grief tore his robe/Peter in phawkkik a, ~ a kap hi | Peter remembered and wept in great sorrow/Tua hikeileh ~ siatlawh kha ding hi | otherwise he may be ruined by too much sorrow) (r:1.42.38/41.14.72/18.1.20/47.2.7) (q:draft)
dahluat = (t:v) (w:grieve too much/grieve greatly) (d:dah, grieve, with luat, too much) (e:na ~ loh nadingun) (r:52.4.13) (q:draft)
dahmai = (t:adj) (w:downcast/sad-faced) (d:dah, grieve, with mai, face: having a sad face; dahmai pua is to wear a sad face) (e:a maisuah uh ~ mahmah lai hi/a maisuah ~ nawn lo hi | her face was no longer downcast) (a:maitai) (r:42.24.17/9.1.18) (q:draft)
dahna = (t:n) (w:sorrow/grief/mourning) (d:the feeling of sadness, and mourning for the dead; dah, be sad, with the noun suffix na; dahna limin is as a sign of mourning) (e:Ka ~ dam thei lo a/Ka ~ hangin ka mit mial a | my eyes have grown dim with grief/note lungsung uh ~ tawh a kidim zo hi | your hearts are filled with grief/Mipilte, ~ lakah om tual a | the wise stay in the midst of mourning) (s:lungdahna/lungkhamna/lunggimna) (a:lungdamna/kipahna) (b:dah) (r:24.8.18/21.7.4/18.17.7/43.16.6) (q:draft)
dahnate = (t:n) (w:sorrows/griefs) (d:plural of dahna, sorrow) (e:a ~ uh kipahna ka suaksak ding hi/Ka ~ kimangngilh bawlin | trying to forget my sorrows/gimna leh ~ a tung ding uh hi | trouble and sorrows will come) (a:lungdamnate) (b:dahna) (r:24.31.13/18.9.27/45.2.9) (q:draft)
dahpih = (t:v) (w:mourn with/grieve for/sympathize with) (d:dah, mourn, with pih, together with: share in the sorrow of someone) (e:a dah mite ~ un/a cimawhte ~ hilo ka hi hiam | did I not grieve for the poor/kua in nang hong ~ ding ahi hiam | who will mourn with you/kuama ~ lohin amah kihemkhia hi | he passed away with no one mourning him) (a:lungdampih) (b:dah) (r:45.12.15/18.30.25/23.51.19/14.21.20) (q:draft)
dahsa = (t:see) <dahsa-in>
dahsa-in = (t:adv) (w:sadly/sorrowfully) (d:dah, be sad, with sa, feel, and the marker in: feeling sad) (e:maikhingin a ~ a paikhia hi) (r:41.10.22) (q:draft)
dahsak = (t:v) (w:grieve/sadden) (d:cause grief to someone; dah, be sad, with the causative sak; said of people who grieve God or his Spirit) (e:sehnel gam sungah amah ~ uh hi/a Kha Siangtho ~ uh hi | they grieved his Holy Spirit/tua thu in ama' lungsim ~ hi | that grieved his heart/Pasian’ Kha Siangtho na ~ kei un | do not grieve the Holy Spirit of God) (s:lungkhamsak/khasiatsak) (a:lungdamsak/nuamsak) (b:dah) (r:19.78.40/47.2.2/23.63.10/1.6.6/49.4.30)
dahsak = (t:v) (w:mourn/make mourn) (d:make someone mourn, bring grief on a person) (e:tahai in a nu ~ hi | a foolish child brings grief to his mother/Ta hai in a pa ~ a | a foolish child brings grief to his father) (b:dah) (r:20.10.1/20.17.25)
dahsak = (t:v) (w:sorrow/cause sorrow/make sad) (d:make someone sorry or sad, as by a rebuke or a letter) (e:deihna tawh kituakin ka hong ~ hi/keimah in note ka hong ~ leh | if I make you sad/note tawlkhat bek hong ~ hi | it made you sad only for a little while/kei hong ~ lua ahi kei hi | it is not so much me that he has grieved) (a:lungdamsak) (b:dah) (r:47.7.9/47.2.2/47.7.8/47.2.5)
dahsaka = (t:v) (w:grieving/making sad) (d:dahsak, make sad, with a linking it to the following verb) (e:hong ~ hong kisiksak ahih manin) (b:dahsak) (r:47.7.9) (q:draft)
dahsakte = (t:n) (w:those grieved/those made sad) (d:dahsak, make sad, with plural te: the people whom one has grieved) (e:ka hong ~ longal) (b:dahsak) (r:47.2.2) (q:draft)
dahte = (t:n) (w:mourners/those who mourn/the sorrowful) (d:dah, mourn, with the plural ending te; used after a, a dahte, those who mourn) (e:A ~ in thupha a ngah ding/a ~ lungnuam sak hi | he comforts those who mourn/a ~’ annekte pawl zong na ne kei ding | you shall not eat the food of mourners/a ~ bang ahi zongin a nuam tawntung | as sorrowful, yet always glad) (s:kapte/kahte) (a:lungdamte) (b:dah) (r:40.5.4/18.5.11/26.24.22/47.6.10) (q:draft)
dahzaw = (t:v) (w:grieve more/be sadder) (d:dah mourn or be sad, with zaw more) (e:Jonathan sangin David nakpitakin ~ a) (b:dah) (r:9.20.41) (q:draft)
dai = (t:adj) (w:quiet/calm/silent/still) (d:without noise or movement, of people, wind or sea; also as a verb, be quiet, fall silent, die down; dai takin is quietly, dai dide utterly still) (e:huihnung tawpa a ~ pah hi/tuihual a taai khit ciangin a ~ ta hi | after he rebuked the waves it became calm/~ takin ka om ding hi | I will be calm/~ dide in om kei in | do not remain silent) (s:daii/gamdai/daicip) (r:41.4.39/19.107.29/40.8.26/26.16.42/19.109.1) (q:draft)
daicip = (t:adj) (w:silent/utterly quiet/still) (d:dai, quiet, with cip, completely, of a person who says nothing or a place left empty) (e:bang hangin ~ na hi hiam/kuamah om nawn loin ~ ding hi | no one will be there any more and it will lie silent/Tuipi sungah a ~ suak Tai-ar khuapi | the city of Tyre that has become silent in the sea) (s:dai/gamdai) (b:dai) (r:35.1.13/26.27.32/38.7.14) (q:draft)
daicipsak = (t:v) (w:silence/put to silence) (d:daicip, utterly silent, with causative sak) (e:ka awging ~ kei in) (s:daihsak/gamdaisak) (b:daicip) (r:18.16.18) (q:draft)
daicipsuak = (t:v) (w:be silenced/become silent) (d:daicip, utterly silent, with suak, become) (e:Tuipi sungah a ~ Taia khuapi) (r:26.27.32) (q:draft)
daigawl = (t:n) (w:fence/hedge/wall) (d:the fence or wall round a vineyard or field) (e:nangmah in a ~ suvang na hi hiam) (s:gawl) (r:19.80.12) (q:draft)
daih = (t:v) (w:be quiet/be silent/calm down) (d:be quiet, stop making noise; of wind and sea, calm down; the form of dai used before words such as leh, khit, nading and theih) (e:hih mite a ~ uh leh/Mihonpite in a ~ nadingin a taai uh | the crowd rebuked him to make him be quiet/amaute in a ~ khit uh ciangin | when they had become silent/Huihpi nun’ a ~ khit ciangin zin ling a | after the great wind had died down the earth shook) (s:gamdaih/kidai) (b:dai) (r:42.19.40/32.1.11/41.10.48/44.21.40/11.19.11) (q:draft)
daihawh = (t:v) (w:visit the tomb/visit a grave) (d:with hawh visit: go to see a grave, said of the women going to the tomb of Jesus) (e:~ dingin a pai uh hi) (r:40.28.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
daihna = (t:n) (w:quietness/quiet/stillness/solitude) (d:the state of being quiet and undisturbed; daih, be quiet, with the noun suffix na; gam daihna is a quiet, solitary place) (e:~ leh lungmuan’ tawntungna om ding hi/Gam ~-ah hong pai un la | come away to a quiet place/gamlak gam ~-ah a pai uh hi | they went to a solitary place in the wilderness/tungah kilemna leh ~ ka pia ding hi | I will give peace and quiet to it) (s:hithiatna) (a:gamlumna) (b:daih) (r:23.32.17/41.6.32/41.6.31/13.22.9) (q:draft)
daihsak = (t:v) (w:silence/quiet/make quiet) (d:make people stop speaking or making noise; daih, be quiet, with the causative sak) (e:mihonpi a ~ khit ciangin/galte leh langpangte na ~ nadingin | so that you silence the enemies and the foes/na gamtat hoihna un a ~ ding | that your good conduct should silence them) (s:daicipsak/gamdaisak) (b:daih) (r:44.19.35/60.2.15/19.8.2) (q:draft)
daihsakna = (t:n) (w:silencing) (d:daihsak, silence, with the noun suffix na; daihsakna dingin is in order to silence) (e:langpangte na ~ dingin) (b:daihsak) (r:19.8.2) (q:draft)
daihtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to calm down/can become calm) (d:daih, calm down, with theih, can) (e:tuipi a hong ~ nadingin) (b:daih) (r:32.1.11) (q:draft)
daihual = (t:n) (w:boundary/border/limits) (d:the boundary line of a town) (e:ama bukna khuapi ~ pua lamah) (s:gamgi) (r:4.35.27) (q:draft)
daii = (t:adj) (w:quiet/silent/still/calm) (d:without noise or disturbance; daii takin, quietly; also as a verb, fall silent) (e:amaute ~ takin om uh a/naupang bangin ~ takin ka om dide | I stay quiet and still like a child/laiza tawh la saknate ~ ta hi | the songs with the harp have fallen silent/~ tak-a omna leh muanna in | in quietness and trust) (s:dai/gamdai) (r:23.36.21/23.24.8/19.131.2/23.30.15) (q:draft)
daii = (t:v) (w:be profaned/be dishonoured) (d:of a name, lose its honour; the same word is also written dai, and daisak is to profane) (e:keima min a ~ dingin ka omsak/mite’ lakah ka min ~ ding ahih manin | because my name would be profaned among the people) (r:26.39.7/26.20.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
daikhak = (t:v) (w:be profaned/be dishonored) (d:dai in the sense seen in daisak, profane, with khak, happen to: come to be dishonored, said of a name) (e:ka min a ~ ding khualna tawh) (r:26.20.44) (q:draft, low confidence)
daikik = (t:v) (w:die down again/be quenched) (d:dai, be still, with kik, again; said of a fire that goes out) (e:amaute ~ pak uh hi) (b:dai) (r:19.118.12) (q:draft)
daina = (t:n) (w:shame/dishonour) (d:dai in the sense of losing honour, as in daisak dishonour, with the noun suffix na; daina thuak is suffer dishonour) (e:bang tanvei ~ thuak ding ahi hiam) (s:mindaina/maizumna) (b:dai) (r:19.4.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
daina = (t:n) (w:quiet place/solitude) (d:dai quiet with the noun suffix na; gam daina is a quiet, lonely place) (e:Zeisu in gam ~-ah a om lai takin) (s:daihna) (b:dai) (r:41.4.10) (q:draft)
daingo = (t:n) (w:dew) (d:the dew that settles at night; compare daitui dew) (e:Ka lu tungah ~ kia a) (s:daitui) (r:22.5.2) (q:draft)
