dawntuahin = (t:v) (w:meet/encounter) (d:dawntuah with the linking suffix in, meeting someone on the way, followed by another verb) (e:Topa in Moses ~ thah a sawm hi/humpinelkai khat in amah ~ that hi | a lion met him and killed him/Jesuh in lampi-ah tua numeite na ~ | Jesus met the women on the way) (s:dawnin) (b:dawntuah) (r:2.4.24/11.20.36/40.28.9) (q:draft)
dawntuahpa = (t:n) (w:the one who meets) (d:dawntuah meet, with pa marking a man; the one who came to meet him) (e:a masapa in a ~ kiangah) (b:dawntuah) (r:38.2.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
