dawnzum = (t:n) (w:peak/pointed summit) (d:dawn top with zum pointed; a mountain with many peaks is called rugged in the English) (e:aw mual ~ tampi a nei Bashan mual) (s:mualvum) (r:19.68.15/19.68.16) (q:draft)
dawt = (t:v) (w:stab/thrust through/pierce) (d:drive a sword or dagger into someone) (e:a langpa’ pang ~ ciat uh hi/kei hong ~ letin hong mawlpih kha ding | they will run me through and abuse me) (r:10.2.16/9.31.4) (q:draft)
dawtlet = (t:v) (w:run through/pierce through) (d:stab right through with a sword) (e:tua tawh hong ~ in) (s:sunlet) (r:9.31.4) (q:draft)
dawtletin = (t:v) (w:running through/piercing through) (d:dawtlet stab through, with the linking suffix in) (e:kei hong ~ hong mawlpih kha) (s:sunletin) (b:dawtlet) (r:9.31.4) (q:draft)
