dedu = (t:adv) (w:intently/deeply) (d:placed after lungngai think: describes thinking long and hard about something, pondering) (e:nangma thu lungngai ~ ding uh a) (r:23.14.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
deek = (t:v) (w:bargain/barter/haggle) (d:bargain over a thing in order to buy it) (e:lei dingin hong ~ ding a) (s:sumdek) (r:18.41.6) (q:draft)
deen = (t:v) (w:strike/hit/fall on) (d:hit with something that falls or is thrown, such as a stone or hail; written with an apostrophe before the next word) (e:suang tawh ~’ dingin hong zong uh/a ~’ khak peuhmahte kizangawp ding hi | anyone it falls on will be crushed/gialpi in a ~’ baang kung khempeuh | every plant that the hail left standing) (r:43.11.8/40.21.44/2.10.12) (q:draft)
deeng = (t:v) (w:throw at/pelt/stone) (d:throw something at a person; suang tawh deeng is stone someone) (e:suang tawh ~ dingin suang a tawm/numei suang tawh ~ masa hen | let him be the first to stone the woman/khat suang tawh a ~ uh hi | they stoned another/Suang tawh kei hong ~ dingin | to stone me/a lu guh ~ kham hi | it struck and cracked his skull) (s:deng) (r:43.10.31/40.21.35/43.8.7/2.17.4/7.9.53) (q:draft)
deengin = (t:v) (w:stone/pelt/throw at) (d:deeng, throw at or strike, with the linking ending in; suang tawh deengin is to stone someone) (e:suang tawh nang hong ~) (s:dengin) (b:deeng) (r:26.16.40) (q:draft)
deenglum = (t:v) (w:stone to death/stone) (d:kill by throwing stones, usually as suang tawh deenglum; deeng throw at, with lum, which shows that the blow kills) (e:suang tawh amah ~ ding uh hi/Suang tawh ~ un | stone them to death) (s:denglum/denlup) (r:3.20.2/43.8.5) (q:draft)
deengtan = (t:v) (w:break off/strip) (d:strike so that it breaks off, said of hail stripping the trees; deeng strike with tan cut off) (e:gamlak singkung khempeuh ~ hi) (r:2.9.25) (q:draft)
deh = (t:v) (w:sting/strike) (d:pierce with a sting, said of a scorpion) (e:momai in mi a ~ ciangin) (s:pet) (r:66.9.5) (q:draft)
dehthei = (t:v) (w:be able to sting) (d:deh sting with thei can: have the power to sting) (e:mei nei-in mi ~ uh a) (b:deh) (r:66.9.10) (q:draft)
dei = (t:n) (w:room/chamber) (d:a room of a house or building; dei tungnung is an upstairs room) (e:kici ~ khat a om hi/~ tungnung ah koih uh hi | they placed her in an upstairs room/Tua ~ sungah na bawl khol un | make preparations in that room/a kibawlsa ~ tungnung a lian khat | a large furnished upstairs room) (s:inndei/adei) (r:58.9.3/44.20.8/44.9.37/42.22.12)
deidai = (t:adv) (w:very/intensely) (d:placed after kha bitter, to strengthen it: very bitter, as bitter as the venom of snakes) (e:gulgu a khapen zahin kha ~ hi) (r:18.20.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
deidan = (t:v) (w:show favoritism/discriminate/be partial) (d:treat people unequally, favouring some over others; mi deidan is to show partiality) (e:Pasian in kuamah ~ loin/mi na ~ uhleh note a khial na hi uh a | if you show favoritism, you sin/Mi ~ loin a kibangin en un | regard everyone alike, without partiality/mi na ~ kei un | do not show favoritism) (r:45.2.11/59.2.9/45.12.16/59.2.1) (q:draft)
deidanna = (t:n) (w:partiality/discrimination/favoritism/distinction) (d:deidan treat people unequally, with the noun suffix na; mi deidanna is partiality toward people) (e:Gentail mite ~ hong nei lo a/mi ~, leh sumgolh laknate deih lo hi | he does not want partiality or the taking of bribes/Israel minam sung panin kuamah ~ om loin | with no distinction made among the tribes of Israel) (s:angvanna/kideidanna) (b:deidan) (r:44.15.9/14.19.7/26.48.19) (q:draft)
