dinkik = (t:v) (w:repay/reward/recompense/make restitution) (d:give back what is due, whether a reward for good or payment for a wrong) (e:ka khut siangthona tawh kizui-in hong ~ hi/ka siangthona tawh kizui-in hong ~ khin hi | he has repaid me according to my cleanness/keimah in kong ~ ding hi | I will repay you/a tatkhialhna-ah a kicingin ~ ding a | he shall make full restitution for his wrong) (s:thukkik/lohkik) (r:19.18.20/10.22.21/10.22.25/9.12.3/4.5.7) (q:draft)
dinkipna = (t:n) (w:foothold/firm footing) (d:din, stand, with kip, firm, and the noun suffix na: a place to stand firmly) (e:Khe tawh ~ ding mun a om lohna) (s:khesikna) (r:19.69.2) (q:draft)
dinlam = (t:n) (d:din, stand, with lam, the fact or manner: the fact that someone is standing somewhere) (e:lampi-ah na ~ thei lo ka hih manin) (r:4.22.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
dinna = (t:n) (w:standing place/place where one stands) (d:din, stand, with na: the standing, or with mun the place where someone or something stands; a mai-ah ka dinna, before whom I stand) (e:Na ~ mun pen a siangtho leitang/Siampite’ khe a ~ mun mahmah | the very place where the feet of the priests stand/A mai-ah ka ~ Vanglian Topa | the Lord Almighty, before whom I stand/nangma ~ mun, leitang siangtho ahi hi | the place where you stand is holy ground) (b:din) (r:44.7.33/2.3.5/6.4.3/11.18.15) (q:draft)
dinnasa = (t:v) (w:had stood) (d:din, stand, with na, place, and sa, already done; a dinnasa mun is the place where one had stood) (e:Topa mai-ah a ~ munah/siampite’ khe a ~ mun | the place where the feet of the priests had stood) (b:din) (r:1.19.27/6.4.9) (q:draft)
dinsa = (t:see) <dinsa-in>
dinsa-in = (t:adv) (w:standing/while standing) (d:din, stand, with sa, already, and the adverbial in: standing where one is) (e:amaute in ~ amau’ khialhnate) (r:16.9.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
dinsakkik = (t:v) (w:set up again/restore) (d:din, stand, with the causative sak and kik, again: make stand again, of a ruined building) (e:puahkikin ka ~ theih nading uh) (s:dingsakkik/dingtosakkik) (r:15.9.9) (q:draft)
dinsih = (t:v) (w:die/drop dead) (d:the verse has died; apparently din, stand, with sih, die: die on the spot) (e:Benaiah’ tapa Pelatiah hong ~ hi) (r:26.11.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
dintheih = (t:v) (w:be able to stand) (d:din, stand, with theih, be able) (e:Mihing Tapa mai-ah na ~ nadingun) (s:dingzo) (b:din) (r:42.21.36) (q:draft)
Dionisias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dionysius) (d:member of the Areopagus council in Athens who became a believer through the preaching of Paul) (r:44.17.34)
Diotrefes = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Diotrephes) (d:church leader who loved to be first and refused to accept the authority of John, the writer of 3 John) (r:64.1.9)
dip = (t:n) (w:heart/breast/chest) (d:the heart as the place that pounds with feeling, or the breast; dip kuasak is make the heart pound or burn and dip hum is beat the breast in grief) (e:dahin a ~ uh hum uh hi/Hih huihpi in ka ~ hong kuasak a | this storm makes my heart pound/i ~ kuasak hilo ahi hiam | were not our hearts burning/Dahna tawh na ~ hum in | beat your breast in grief/a ~ humin kuncip a | beating his breast, he bowed low) (s:awm/lungtang) (r:34.2.7/42.24.32/18.37.1/26.21.12/42.18.13) (q:draft)
dip = (t:v) (w:draw/scoop) (d:draw or scoop up water, as in tui dip; tui dip nading is something to draw water with) (e:nangmah in tui ~ nading na nei kei hi/tuikhuk a, tui ~ nading ahi zongin | or for scooping water out of a cistern) (s:tawi) (r:43.4.11/23.30.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
dipkua = (t:v) (w:be appalled/be horrified/be terrified) (d:be struck with fear or shock; dipkua sak is to startle or terrify someone) (e:kamsangte a ~ ding uh hi/amaute ~ vatin tai uh hi | struck with terror, they fled/minam tampite ~ sak ding a | he will startle many nations/Kei hong ~ sak dingin | in order to terrify me) (s:mulkim/lipkhap/linglawng) (r:24.4.9/19.48.5/23.52.15/25.2.22) (q:draft)
dipkuasak = (t:v) (w:terrify/startle/horrify) (d:dipkua, be appalled or terrified, with the causative sak: fill someone with fear or shock) (e:minam tampite ~ ding a/Kei a hong ~ dingin | in order to terrify me) (s:lausak/lauthawng) (b:dipkua) (r:23.52.15/25.2.22) (q:draft)
dipkuat = (t:v) (w:be terrified/be struck with dread) (d:in the verses always followed by huai: dipkuat huai is awesome, terrifying) (e:a ~ huai mang ka mu hi/A ~ huai, a patauh huai thu khat | a horrible and shocking thing/Nangma bawlnate bangzah takin ~ huai | how awesome are your deeds/Amah in a ~ huai siatna piangsak ding a | he will cause terrifying destruction) (s:lipkhap/mulkim) (r:27.4.5/24.5.30/19.66.3/27.8.24) (q:draft)
dipkuathuai = (t:adj) (w:awesome/terrifying/dreadful) (d:causing dread or awe, used of God and his deeds and of disasters; dipkuat, be terrified, with huai, causing) (e:Amah in a ~ siatna piangsak ding a/a bawlnate-ah amah ~ hi | he is awesome in his deeds/Topa, a Sangpenpa, ~ a | the Lord Most High is awesome/Nangma bawlnate bangzahta-in ~ | how awesome are your deeds) (s:lauhuai/kihtakhuai/lipkhaphuai/mulkimhuai) (r:27.8.24/19.66.5/19.47.2/19.66.3) (q:draft)
dipkuatna = (t:n) (w:terror/dread/horror) (d:dipkuat, be terrified, with the noun suffix na: sudden fear that comes upon someone) (e:thakhat thu-a ~, zawngkhalna) (s:launa/kihtakna/patauhna) (b:dipkuat) (r:3.26.16) (q:draft)
dipna = (t:n) (w:scooping/drawing) (d:dip, scoop or draw water, with the noun suffix na; tui dipna ding is something to scoop water with) (e:tuikhuka om tui ~ ding ahi zongin) (b:dip) (r:23.30.14) (q:draft)
dipsakin = (t:v) (w:filling) (d:with tawh, filling a container with something, as bags with grain; the causative sak and the linking suffix in on dip, which here seems to mean be full) (e:ipte antang tawh ~) (s:thunin) (r:1.42.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
