doin = (t:v) (w:fighting/attacking) (d:do, fight, with the linking suffix in: fighting or attacking and then going on to the next action) (e:David in amah ~ zo hi/amaute ~ ka hawl khia zo kha ding | perhaps I can fight them and drive them out/Shamaneser amah ~ kuanto hi | Shalmaneser came up to attack him/amah in Israel ~, amaute kimkhat sal-in man | he attacked Israel and took some of them captive) (s:simin) (b:do) (r:13.18.3/12.17.3/4.22.11/4.21.1) (q:draft)
dok = (t:v) (w:draw/pull out/withdraw) (d:pull something out or back, as a sword from its sheath or a hand; with kik, draw back) (e:Ka namsau ka ~ ding a/tangvalpa in a namsau ~ lo hi | the young man did not draw his sword/Na namsau ~ in la kei hong that in | draw your sword and kill me/a paai panin ~ a | he drew it from its sheath) (s:kaikhia) (r:2.15.9/19.74.11/7.8.20/7.9.54/9.17.51) (q:draft)
dok = (t:v) (w:exact/collect/levy/charge) (d:collect money, tax or interest from people, with tung panin for those who must pay) (e:Israelte tung panin sum ~ hi/a meet na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not charge interest/a gam sung mite’ ngun leh kham ~ hi | he exacted the silver and gold of the people of the land) (s:khon/siik) (r:12.15.20/2.22.25/12.23.35) (q:draft)
dokhawmna = (t:n) (w:striving together/fighting together) (d:do, fight, with khawm, together, and the noun suffix na) (e:deihna kikhatin na ~ thu uh) (r:50.1.27) (q:draft)
dokin = (t:v) (w:drawing/pulling out) (d:dok with in, the linking form before a following verb; used of drawing a sword) (e:migilote in namsau ~ a thal uh/a namsau ~ siampi lianpen pa’ nasempa a sat | he drew his sword and struck the high priest's servant/namsau a paai panin ~ note kong delh ding | I will draw the sword from its sheath and pursue you) (b:dok) (r:19.37.14/41.14.47/40.26.51/3.26.33) (q:draft)
dokkhia = (t:see) <dokkhia-in>
dokkhia-in = (t:v) (w:pulling out/drawing out) (d:dok, pull, with khia, out, and the linking suffix in) (e:ama a dingin pawlkhat ~ ama top dingin) (r:8.2.16) (q:draft)
dokkik = (t:v) (w:draw back/withdraw/take back) (d:pull back a hand, anger, kindness or a word once given; dok, pull, with kik, back) (e:a khut ~ lo hi/Bang hangin na khut ~ a | why do you draw back your hand/a thu gensate ~ loin | not taking back the words he has spoken/Pasian in ama hehna ~ het lo | God does not withdraw his anger at all/na thumanna ~ ngei kei in | never withdraw your faithfulness) (s:lakik) (b:dok) (r:6.8.26/45.11.29/19.74.11/23.31.2/18.9.13/9.20.15) (q:draft)
