doksakin = (t:v) (w:making draw/causing to draw) (d:dok, draw a sword, with the causative sak and the linking suffix in) (e:a galkapte uh a namsau uh ~) (b:dok) (r:26.32.12) (q:draft)
dolah = (t:todo) (q:draft, one verse, sakin dolah nei lo is said of the hard heart of Leviathan, the meaning of dolah is not clear from it)
dom = (t:v) (w:lift up/hold up/bear up) (d:take up and support with the hands, often as dom to, lift up; nau dom is to help at a birth) (e:khut tawh nang hong ~ ding uh hi/Jonah ~ to-in tuipi sungah a khiat uh | they lifted Jonah up and threw him into the sea/~ to-in la tungah tua nu koih hi | he lifted her up and put her on the donkey/~ toin ka biang ciangah ka tawi a | I lifted them up and held them to my cheek) (s:lamto/laamto/phong) (a:khiasuk) (r:42.4.11/32.1.15/7.19.28/28.11.4) (q:draft)
domin = (t:v) (w:lifting up/carrying/holding up) (d:dom, lift or hold up in the hands, with the linking ending in; nau dom is to help a woman at a birth) (e:galkapte in Paul ~ a pua uh hi/Amah in ~ a nu kiangah a paipih ciangin | when he had lifted him up and taken him to his mother/Hebru numeite nau ~ | helping the Hebrew women give birth) (b:dom) (r:44.21.35/12.4.20/2.1.16) (q:draft)
domkhia = (t:v) (w:lift out/pull out/take up out of) (d:dom, lift up, with khia, out) (e:dum sung panin ~ to uh a) (s:kaikhia) (b:dom) (r:1.37.28) (q:draft)
domsakte = (t:n) (w:midwives) (d:in nau a domsakte, those who help a woman deliver a child; dom, lift or hold up, with sak and the plural te) (e:Hebru mi nau a ~) (s:naudomte) (r:2.1.15) (q:draft)
