emin = (t:v) (w:bake) (d:em, bake, with the linking suffix in: bake, said as a command that is followed by another) (e:Na em dingte uh ~) (b:em) (r:2.16.23) (q:draft)
Emin = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Emites/Emim) (d:people of great height living in Shaveh Kiriathaim, defeated by Kedorlaomer) (s:Emim) (r:1.14.5) (q:draft)
emkhawm = (t:v) (w:bake together) (d:em, bake, with khawm, together: bake in one oven together) (e:sungah na anlum uh ~ ding a) (b:em) (r:3.26.26) (q:draft)
Emmanuel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Immanuel) (d:name given to Jesus in the Gospel of Matthew, meaning God with us) (r:40.1.23)
Emmaus = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Emmaus) (d:village about seven miles from Jerusalem, to which two disciples walked on the day of the resurrection) (r:42.24.13)
emna = (t:n) (w:baking) (d:em, bake, with the noun suffix na; moh emna meikhuk is an oven for baking bread and emna ding mun is a place for baking) (e:an tawh biakpiaknate a ~ ding mun/moh ~ meikhuk sunga | in the oven for baking bread) (b:em) (r:26.46.20/28.7.4) (q:draft)
emsa = (t:adj) (w:baked/broiled/roasted) (d:em, bake, with sa for a completed act; used alone it means baked food, and sik emsa is a hot iron) (e:nga ~ tum khat a pia uh hi/~ bangmah ka nei kei a | I have nothing baked/sik ~ tawh tatgawp bangin | as if seared with a hot iron) (b:em) (r:42.24.42/11.17.12/54.4.2) (q:draft)
emsak = (t:v) (w:bake for) (d:em, bake, with sak, here doing the action for someone else: bake for someone) (e:silngo sawh loh anlum ~ a) (b:em) (r:1.19.3) (q:draft)
en = (t:v) (w:look/see/behold) (d:look at someone or something; the commands en in, to one person, and en un, to several, are often rendered behold) (e:~ un!/a kimkot a ~ hi | he looked around/Vantung ~ to dih in | look up at the heavens/na sathau nilhpa’ maitang ~ in | look on the face of your anointed/amah ka ~ hi | I behold him) (s:khuadak/dak) (r:1.1.31/41.5.32/18.35.5/19.84.9/4.24.17)
En = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En) (d:first part of place names written with a hyphen, such as En-gedi and En-gannim) (e:~-gedi gam leenggui lo-a) (r:22.1.14/6.19.21) (q:draft)
En-eglaim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Eglaim) (d:place on the shore of the Dead Sea in the vision of Ezekiel) (e:En-gedi khua panin ~ khua ciang dong) (s:Eneglaim) (r:26.47.10) (q:draft)
En-gannim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Gannim) (d:town in the territory of Issachar, given to the Levites) (s:Engannim) (r:6.19.21) (q:draft)
en-gedi = (t:todo) (q:draft, the place name En-gedi, NIV En Gedi, counted in lowercase where it opens a sentence or a bracket in 26.47.10 and 14.20.2; a lowercase keyword cannot take type name)
En-gedi = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Gedi) (d:oasis and town on the western shore of the Dead Sea, where David hid from Saul) (e:David paito-in ~ munmuanhuai-ah om hi) (s:Engedi) (r:9.23.29/6.15.62) (q:draft)
enai = (t:see) <Elio-enai>
Enaim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Enaim) (d:place on the road to Timnah where Tamar waited for Judah) (r:1.38.14/1.38.21)
Enam = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Enam) (d:town in the lowland of Judah) (e:Zanoah, Engannim, Tappuah, ~) (r:6.15.34) (q:draft)
Enan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enan) (d:father of Ahira, the leader of the tribe of Naphtali in the wilderness) (r:4.1.15/4.10.27) (q:draft)
encian = (t:v) (w:look carefully/pay attention/observe) (d:en, look, with cian, clearly: look at something carefully and take notice of it) (e:ahih hangin tuate ~ lo hi) (r:23.42.20) (q:draft)
encik = (t:v) (w:watch closely/keep an eye on) (d:keep looking at someone carefully, in order to guard or to find fault) (e:a kipanin Saul in David ~ hi/ka gamtatna khempeuh hong ~ hi | he watches all my ways/nang leh kei’ kikal hong ~ hen | may he keep watch between you and me/misia, mipha, hong ~ kim hi | he watches both the evil and the good) (r:9.18.9/18.33.11/1.31.49/20.15.3) (q:draft)
encikin = (t:v) (w:watching closely/observing carefully) (d:encik, watch closely, with the linking suffix in: watching closely and so doing the next action) (e:mite in a lim ~ ama tung panin/Daniel’ nasepna ~ a mawhna zon ding | watching the work of Daniel closely to find fault) (b:encik) (r:11.20.33/27.6.4) (q:draft)
encikpa = (t:n) (w:watcher) (d:encik, watch closely, with pa marking a male person: the one who keeps watching) (e:Mihingte a ~ aw) (b:encik) (r:18.7.20) (q:draft)
Endor = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Endor) (d:town in the territory of Manasseh where Saul consulted a medium) (r:6.17.11/9.28.7)
Eneglaim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Eglaim) (d:place on the shore of the Dead Sea in the vision of Ezekiel) (s:En-eglaim) (r:26.47.10)
enen = (t:v) (w:keep looking/look on/watch) (d:en, look, doubled for an action that goes on) (e:ding mite in a ~ uh hi/Amaute in ~ napi-in mu thei lo uh a | though they keep looking they cannot see/khatlekhat ki-~ mawk na hi uh hiam | why do you just keep looking at one another) (r:42.23.35/40.13.13/1.42.1) (q:draft)
enenin = (t:v) (w:gazing/looking for a long time) (d:en, look, doubled for an action that goes on, with the linking suffix in) (e:vantung lam ~ a om laitakun/Ahi zongin sauveipi ~ | but after watching for a long time) (b:enen) (r:44.1.10/44.28.6) (q:draft)
eng = (t:v) (w:envy/be envious of/be jealous of) (d:feel envy or jealousy toward someone who has what one lacks; eng kei in is do not envy) (e:Migilote ~ kei in la/Filistia mite in amah ~ uh hi | the Philistines envied him/amah in a sanggamnu ~ hi | she envied her sister/a man lo-a gamta mite ~ kei in | do not envy those who do wrong) (s:haza/el) (r:20.24.1/19.73.3/1.26.14/1.30.1/19.37.1) (q:draft)
eng = (t:adj) (w:yellow) (d:yellow in colour; mul eng is yellow hair) (e:siampipa in mul ~ a zon’ ding/a sungah mul ~ om loin | with no yellow hair in it/kat banga ~ awmdalnate a nei uh hi | they had breastplates yellow as sulfur) (r:3.13.36/3.13.32/66.9.17) (q:draft)
Engannim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:En-gannim/En Gannim) (d:name of two towns, one in the lowland of Judah and one in Issachar given to the Levites) (s:En-gannim) (r:6.15.34)
engdum = (t:adj) (w:dark blue) (d:a colour named between fiery red and sulphur yellow; eng is yellow and dum is blue or green, so the exact colour is uncertain) (e:~ leh kat banga eng awmdalnate) (r:66.9.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
engdup = (t:adj) (w:blue) (d:colour of cloth, named beside sandup where the English has blue and purple) (e:puan ~ leh puan sandup tawh) (r:24.10.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
Engedi = (t:name) (c:land) (w:En Gedi) (d:oasis and town on the western shore of the Dead Sea, where David hid from Saul) (s:En-gedi) (r:9.23.29/6.15.62)
engiau = (t:v) (w:peer/peek) (d:look in through a narrow opening) (e:kawmvang panin hong ~ hi) (r:22.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
engin = (t:v) (w:be zealous for/be jealous over) (d:eng, envy or be jealous, with the linking suffix in; here of people eagerly courting others) (e:note hong ~ hong kin mahmah uh hi) (b:eng) (r:48.4.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
engkha = (t:v) (w:envy/come to envy) (d:eng envy with kha, which shows the action coming to happen; used with kei in warnings not to envy) (e:Mawhnei mite ~ kei inla/A ngongtat thei mite ~ kei inla | do not envy the violent) (s:eng/haza) (r:20.23.17/20.3.31) (q:draft)
Enhaddah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Haddah) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.21)
Enhakkore = (t:name) (c:well) (w:En Hakkore) (d:spring at Lehi that God opened for Samson when he was thirsty) (r:7.15.19)
Enhazor = (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Hazor) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.37)
enin = (t:v) (w:looking at/looking) (d:en, look, with the linking suffix in: looking at someone or something and then doing the next action) (e:Zeisu in amaute ~/Abner in a nung ~ | Abner looked behind him/vantung lam ~ ding niloh na hi uh hiam | why do you stand looking into the sky/Mi kiphasakte ~ niamkhiat in la | look at the proud and bring them low) (s:khuadakin/dakin) (b:en) (r:40.19.26/44.1.11/10.2.20/18.40.12) (q:draft)
enkak = (t:v) (w:compare/look at side by side) (d:look at two together to see how they differ; used with tawh, with) (e:khangnote tawh hong ~ khawm in la) (s:enteh/tehkak) (r:27.1.13) (q:draft)
enkhong = (t:v) (w:look on/merely watch) (d:en, look, with khong: keep looking on without acting) (e:bang tanvei hong ~ ding na hi hiam) (s:enen) (r:19.35.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
enluatna = (t:n) (w:envy/bitterness) (d:in enluatna lungsim, a heart of envy or bitterness; apparently eng, envy, with luat, too much, and the noun suffix na) (e:nangmah in ~ lungsim nei-in) (s:enna/hazatna) (r:44.8.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
Enmishpat = (t:name) (c:land) (w:En-mishpat/En Mishpat) (d:another name for Kadesh) (r:1.14.7)
enna = (t:n) (w:envy/jealousy) (d:ill feeling at the good of another, not from en, look; enna lungsim is an envious mind and enna mit an envious eye) (e:~ le huaihamna a om nakleh/~ lungsim a neihtheih nading uh | so that they might become envious/thusia le ~ lungsim tawh a gamtate | those who lived in malice and envy/~ mit tawh na en ding a | you will look with an envious eye) (s:hazatna/enluatna/elna) (r:59.3.16/41.7.22/45.11.11/56.3.3/9.2.32) (q:draft)
enneu = (t:v) (w:look down on/stare at with contempt) (d:en, look, with neu, small: look at someone as of little worth) (e:Ka vom manin hong ~ kei un) (s:simmawh) (r:22.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
Enok = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enoch) (d:son of Jared and father of Methuselah, who walked with God; also the name of a son of Cain) (r:1.5.21)
Enos = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enosh/Enos) (d:son of Seth, named in the genealogy of Jesus; spelled Enosh in the NIV) (e:Kainan in ~’ ta hi) (s:Enosh) (r:42.3.38) (q:draft)
Enosh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enosh) (d:son of Seth and father of Kenan) (s:Enos) (r:1.5.6)
enpha = (t:see) <ki-enpha>
Enrimmon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Rimmon) (d:town in Judah where people settled after the exile) (r:16.11.29)
Enrogel = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Rogel) (d:spring near Jerusalem on the border between Judah and Benjamin) (r:6.18.16/11.1.9)
ensak = (t:v) (w:let see/make look/show) (d:en, look, with the causative sak: make or let someone look at something) (e:na omna ka ~ ding hi/ka galte hong ~ ding hi | he will let me look on my enemies/numei honpi ~ ding uh hi | they will let a crowd of women see it) (s:musak) (b:en) (r:26.16.37/19.59.10/26.16.41) (q:draft)
ensawn = (t:v) (w:watch in turn/oversee in turn) (d:en, look, with sawn, passing on: of a higher official who in turn watches those below) (e:tungah a ~ a lianzaw khat omlai hi) (r:21.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
Enshemesh = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Shemesh) (d:spring on the border between Judah and Benjamin) (r:6.15.7/6.18.17)
ensim = (t:v) (w:spy out/watch secretly/keep watch on) (d:look at a place or person closely without being noticed) (e:Paito un la a gam va ~ un/Ai khua va ~ uh hi | they went and spied out Ai/amaute in Zeisu ~ uh a | they kept watch on Jesus/Ka khialh khakna hong ~ niloh na hih manin | because you keep watching for my offense/Laish gam a ~ dingin a pai mi ngate | the five men who went to spy out the land of Laish) (s:kansim/vilsim) (r:6.7.2/42.20.20/18.10.14/7.18.14) (q:draft)
ensimin = (t:v) (w:spying out/watching secretly) (d:ensim, spy out, with the linking suffix in: spying out and then doing the next action) (e:Dan mite in gam ~ a va zong dingin) (b:ensim) (r:7.18.2) (q:draft)
ensuk = (t:v) (w:look down) (d:en, look, with suk, downward: look down from a high place, often of God looking down from heaven) (e:Topa in vantung panin hong ~ a/thumanna in vantung panin ~ ding hi | righteousness will look down from heaven/Topa in vantung panin mihing’ tate ~ hi | the Lord looks down from heaven on mankind/Vantung panin ~ in la, mu in | look down from heaven and see) (s:khuadaksuk) (a:ento) (b:en) (r:19.33.13/19.14.2/19.85.11/19.80.14) (q:draft)
ensukin = (t:v) (w:looking down/look down) (d:form of ensuk with the linking suffix in, looking down and then going on to the next action) (e:Topa in hong ~ a hong muh ciangin/Vantung panin hong ~ hong mu in | look down from heaven and see/ama siangtho mun panin hong ~ | he looked down from his holy place) (b:ensuk) (r:25.3.50/19.80.14/19.102.19) (q:draft)
Entappuah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Tappuah) (d:place on the border between Manasseh and Ephraim, near the town of Tappuah) (r:6.17.7)
ente = (t:n) (w:those who look/onlookers/watchers) (d:en, look, with the plural te: those who look at something; gam ente are the spies who look over a land) (e:khialh nopna lungsim tawh a ~ in/gam ~ zawlin manin a inn tungsak | she welcomed the spies into her house/Nang hong ~ khempeuh’ muhna-ah | in the sight of all who were watching you) (b:en) (r:40.5.28/58.11.31/26.28.18) (q:draft)
enteh = (t:v) (w:compare/liken) (d:en, look, with teh, measure: set one thing beside another to compare them; used with tawh, with) (e:kua tawh hong ~ ding na hi uh hiam) (s:genteh/tehkak/tehpih/enkak) (r:23.46.5) (q:draft)
entel = (t:v) (w:examine/search/test/look into) (d:look at closely and thoroughly, from en, look, with tel, clearly; often said of God searching the heart and mind) (e:ka ngaihsutna hong ~ in/a mit tawh mihing’ tate ~ hi | his eyes examine the children of men/Pasian aw, kei hong ~ in | search me, O God/nangmah in kei nong ~-a nong thei khin hi | you have searched me and you know me/a manphatna ~ a | he appraised its worth) (s:kantel/sin/sit/vel) (r:19.26.2/18.28.27/19.11.4/19.139.23/19.139.1) (q:draft)
entelin = (t:v) (w:examining/testing/searching) (d:entel, examine, with the linking suffix in: examining and then going on to the next action) (e:Nangmah in lungsim ~ thumanna ah/a kisem na khempeuh ~ a thu kan ding | to examine all that is done and inquire into it/a ci mite dongtel ~ | questioning and testing those who say so) (s:velin) (b:entel) (r:13.29.17/21.1.13/66.2.2) (q:draft)
entheih = (t:v) (w:come to envy/be moved to envy) (d:en, a form of eng, envy, with theih, be able: come to envy; hong entheih nading is so that they may envy) (e:ka mipihte in note hong ~ nading uh) (r:45.11.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
ento = (t:v) (w:look up/look upward/look up to) (d:en, look, with to, upward: raise the eyes, often vantung lam ento, look up to heaven; also look to someone for help) (e:nangmah kong ~ hi/Keimah in mual tung lam ka ~ hi | I look up to the mountains/vantung lam ~-in thupha a piak | looking up to heaven he gave thanks/tua mun a tun’ ciangin ~ a | when he reached the place he looked up/bang hangin vantung lam ~ na hi uh hiam | why are you looking up at the sky) (s:dakto/khuadakto) (a:ensuk/khuadaksuk) (b:en) (r:19.123.1/41.7.34/19.121.1/42.9.16/42.19.5/44.1.11) (q:draft)
enzo = (t:v) (w:be able to look after/be able to care for) (d:en, look, here look after, with zo, be able; with kei it means not able to care for someone alone) (e:note kong ~ kei ding hi) (b:en) (r:5.1.9) (q:draft)
