galkapte = (t:n) (w:soldiers/army/troops) (d:plural of galkap: soldiers, or all of them together as an army) (e:sakol ~ bangin tai uh hi/~ in gunkuang khau sat tat uh a | the soldiers cut the ropes of the boat/Saul in Filistia ~ a muh ciangin lau a | when Saul saw the Philistine army he was afraid/ama ~ la-in | taking his army with him) (b:galkap) (r:29.2.4/42.23.36/44.27.32/9.28.5/2.14.6) (q:draft)
