galpi = (t:n) (w:great war/war) (d:Gal, war, with pi, great: a great war.) (e:Izipt gamah ~ tung ding a) (b:gal) (r:26.30.4/26.30.5) (q:draft)
galsap = (t:v) (w:call out/cry out) (d:Gal, from far off, with sap, call: call out to someone who is at a distance.) (e:Nakpi takin Topa ka ~ a) (r:19.3.4) (q:draft)
galsiam = (t:adj) (w:skilled in war/fit for battle) (d:Gal, war, with siam, skilled: trained and able in fighting; galsiam mi is a skilled warrior.) (e:hih mite khempeuh ~ mi ahi hi/Amah in ~ nadingin kei hong hilh a | he trains me to be skilled in war) (r:7.20.17/10.22.35) (q:draft)
galsim = (t:v) (w:go to war/fight/do battle) (d:Gal, enemy or war, with sim, attack: go to war, go into battle; also used like a noun for battle, as in galsim mite, fighting men.) (e:la un la, ~ dingin kuankhia un/~ dingin kuamah kuan khia lo ding hi | no one will go out to battle/Sakol ~ ding a tai bangin | like a horse charging into battle/Jerusalem khuapi hutna-in ~ ding uh a | they will fight in defence of the city of Jerusalem/mihingte lak panin ~ mite bei-in | when the fighting men among the people were gone) (s:galdo) (r:24.46.3/5.2.16/26.7.14/24.8.6/38.14.14) (q:draft)
galsimin = (t:v) (w:going to war/go to war) (d:Galsim, go to war, with the linking suffix in: going to war, followed by the next action.) (e:~ kumpite kuankhia zel uh hi/Kumpite in khuakhal sungin ~ kuankhia zel uh hi | in the spring kings go off to war) (b:galsim) (r:13.20.1) (q:draft)
galsimna = (t:n) (w:raid/battle/war/campaign) (d:Galsim, go to war, with the noun suffix na: an act or occasion of going out to fight, a raid, battle or campaign.) (e:Siria mite in a ~ khat uhah/Kote pen ~ ah nang tawh kong kuan ding | we will go with you to the war/Amah in ka ~-ah kei hong honin | he rescues me in my battle/a ~ panun David’ nasemte Joab tawh hong tung uh | David’s men came with Joab from the raid) (s:galdona/galkidona) (b:galsim) (r:12.5.2/19.55.18/14.18.3/10.3.22) (q:draft)
galsimnate = (t:n) (w:wars/battles/campaigns) (d:Plural of galsimna: the wars or campaigns that someone has fought.) (e:leh a ~, leh a omziate) (s:galdonate/galkidonate) (b:galsimna) (r:14.27.7) (q:draft)
galsimpih = (t:v) (w:fight alongside/go to war with) (d:Galsim, go to war, with pih, together with: join someone in battle.) (e:Satan in a ~ dingin tuipi) (s:dopih/simpih) (b:galsim) (r:66.20.8) (q:draft)
galsimte = (t:n) (w:raiders/raiding parties) (d:Galsim, go to war, with the plural te: those who go out to attack, raiding parties.) (e:~ pawl thumin hong kuankhia uh hi/khuacingte leh ~ nangawn liing uh hi | even the outposts and the raiding parties trembled) (b:galsim) (r:9.13.17/9.14.15) (q:draft)
galsimzia = (t:n) (w:way of fighting/art of war) (d:Galsim, go to war, with zia, manner: the way to fight, the skill of war.) (e:Amah in ~ kei hong hilh a) (r:10.22.35) (q:draft)
galsung = (t:n) (w:battle/war) (d:Gal, war, with sung, inside: the battle or the war as the place one is in; galsung pan is from the battle and galsung nazatte are weapons of war.) (e:~ pan a tai uh ciangin/~ panin a hong ciahkik | returning from battle/a ~ nazatte le a leeng nate | his weapons of war and the equipment of his chariots/~ panin hong tungte’ langkhatah pangin | standing against those who were arriving from the war) (s:galdona/galkidona) (a:galdaihna) (r:10.19.3/26.32.28/33.2.8/9.8.12/14.28.12) (q:draft)
galsunga = (t:adv) (w:in battle/in war) (d:Galsung, battle, with the place ending a: in battle; galsunga site are those who die in battle.) (e:~ site hampha zaw lai hi/~ si hi lo uh hi | they did not die in battle) (b:galsung) (r:25.4.9/23.22.1) (q:draft)
galtai = (t:n) (w:fugitive) (d:Gal, enemy, with tai, flee: a person who flees from an enemy or from war; galtai-in means as a fugitive, in flight.) (e:~ mite hek kei in/nang pen a ~, leitunga a vakvai na hi ding | you will be a fugitive and a wanderer on the earth/a tapate ~-in, a tanute galmatin | his sons as fugitives, his daughters as captives/note pen ~-in paikhia loin | you will not go out in flight) (r:23.16.3/1.4.12/4.21.29/23.52.12)
galtai = (t:n) (w:refugee) (d:A person who has fled from war to find safety in another place.) (e:a ~ ama mite Zoar khua) (r:23.15.5)
galtaina = (t:n) (w:flight/fleeing from the enemy) (d:Galtai, flee from the enemy, with the noun suffix na: fleeing before enemies.) (e:kha thum sung ~) (s:taina) (b:galtai) (r:13.21.12) (q:draft)
galtaite = (t:n) (w:fugitives/refugees) (d:Plural of galtai: people who flee from an enemy or from war.) (e:Efraim ~ na hi uh hi/~, an tawh dawn un | meet the fugitives with food/Efraim ~ khat peuhpeuh in | whenever one of the fugitives of Ephraim/~ in Heshbon khua hong beel uh hi | the fugitives took shelter at Heshbon) (b:galtai) (r:7.12.4/23.21.14/7.12.5/24.48.45) (q:draft)
galte = (t:n) (w:enemies/foes) (d:Plural of gal: enemies, those who fight against or hate someone.) (e:Ka ~ khempeuh in hong simmawhin/ka ~ kiang panin ka suakta hi | I am saved from my enemies/Topa aw, ka ~ tam mahmah | Lord, how many are my enemies/A ~ un amaute nengniam uh a | their enemies oppressed them) (s:langte/mudahte/langpangte/galbawlte) (a:lawmte) (b:gal) (r:25.3.46/19.7.4/19.18.3/19.3.1/19.106.42) (q:draft)
galvan = (t:n) (w:weapons/arms/armor) (d:Gal, war, with van, goods: the equipment of war, weapons and armor; galvan koihna is an armory and galvan puapa an armor-bearer.) (e:A ~ puapa in Saul a sihna/a ~ teng ama puanbukah a koih hi | he put all his weapons in his own tent/a ~ koihna inn khempeuh | his whole armory/Leinuai-ah a ~ teng uh tawh pai-in | going down to the realm of the dead with all their weapons) (s:galhiam) (r:13.10.5/16.3.19/9.17.54/23.39.2/26.32.27) (q:draft)
galvante = (t:n) (w:armor/weapons/war gear) (d:Galvan with the plural te: the things worn and carried for battle.) (e:Saul in a ~ David silhsak hi) (s:galhiamte) (b:galvan) (r:9.17.38) (q:draft)
galvanteng = (t:n) (w:all the weapons/weapons of war) (d:Galvan, weapons, with teng, all: all the weapons of a soldier.) (e:a ~ uh tawh pai-in) (b:galvan) (r:26.32.27) (q:draft)
galvil = (t:n) (w:watchman/lookout/sentry/guard) (d:Gal, enemy, with vil, watch: one who keeps watch for the enemy; also the act of keeping watch, as in galvil koih, post a guard.) (e:sun leh zanin ~ ka koih uh hi/Pai in, ~ khat koih in la | go, post a lookout/~ tangvalpa in a lu sang sakin khuadak a | the young man on watch looked up/~ leh ~ kimaituah hi | guard stood facing guard) (s:galvilpa/vilpa/khuacing) (r:16.4.9/23.21.6/10.13.34/13.26.16) (q:draft)
galvilna = (t:n) (w:watch/lookout/guard post) (d:Galvil, keep watch, with the noun suffix na: keeping watch against an enemy, or the place for it; galvilna bukno is a watchtower and galvilna inndei a guardroom.) (e:~ bukno akipan kulh a nei/pawlkhatte ~ munah, pawlkhatte amau’ inn mai ciatah | some at their posts and some in front of their own houses/~ inndei neu thum tuak om hi | there were three small guardrooms on each side) (s:vilna) (b:galvil) (r:12.18.8/14.20.24/16.7.3/26.40.7) (q:draft)
galvilpa = (t:n) (w:watchman/lookout) (d:Galvil, watch, with pa, which marks a man: a man who keeps watch for the enemy.) (e:~ in samin kumpipa kiangah gen hi/Israel minamte’ ~ dingin nang kong koih hi | I have made you a watchman for the people of Israel/Jezre-el tausang tungah ~ ding a | the lookout was standing on the tower in Jezreel/~ in midang khat hong tai mu hi | the watchman saw another man running) (s:galvil/vilpa) (b:galvil) (r:10.18.25/26.33.3/26.3.17/12.9.17/10.18.26) (q:draft)
galvilte = (t:n) (w:watchmen/guards/lookouts) (d:Plural of galvil: watchmen or guards who keep watch for the enemy.) (e:~ in zingsang a ngaklah sangin/na kulhte tungah ~ ka koih khin hi | I have posted watchmen on your walls/Ama ~ mit taw uh a | his watchmen are blind/Saul’ ~ in en uh hi | Saul’s lookouts were watching) (s:vilte/khuacingte/cingte) (b:galvil) (r:19.130.6/9.14.16/23.62.6/23.56.10) (q:draft)
galzak = (t:v) (w:hear of/hear from afar) (d:Gal, from far off, with zak, hear: hear about someone or something that is elsewhere.) (e:Zeisu thu a ~ ciangin) (r:42.7.3) (q:draft)
galzawh = (t:v) (w:win in war/conquer) (d:Gal, war, with zawh, the form of zo, overcome, used before another word; galzawh van is plunder, the goods won in war.) (e:~ van dingin la uh hi) (r:6.11.14) (q:draft)
galzawhna = (t:n) (w:victory) (d:Galzawh, win in war, with the noun suffix na: victory in battle.) (e:ahi zongin ~ pen) (s:gualzawhna/zawhna) (a:guallelhna/lelhna) (b:galzawh) (r:20.21.31) (q:draft)
galzote = (t:n) (w:conquerors/victors) (d:Gal, war, with zo, win, and the plural te: those who win a war.) (e:~ in a sal matte a kaih) (s:gualzote) (r:51.2.15) (q:draft)
galzuih = (t:v) (w:follow at a distance) (d:Gal, from afar, with zuih, follow: follow at a distance; nung galzuih is follow behind someone from far off.) (e:nung ~ a, siampi lianpen/Jesuh’ nung ~ a, bang thu a piang hiam | followed Jesus at a distance, to see what would happen) (r:41.14.54/40.26.58) (q:draft)
gam = (t:n) (w:country) (d:A country or region with its people; mualtung gam is hill country.) (e:Efraim mualtung ~ mi Mikah/Izipt ~ in leitung ~ khempeuh ah | Egypt, among all the countries of the earth/Arabia ~, leh Libia ~ panin | from the country of Arabia and the country of Libya) (r:7.17.1/26.30.7/26.30.5)
gam = (t:n) (w:territory) (d:The area of land that belongs to a people, a tribe or a ruler.) (e:Sihon in ama ~ Israelte kantan sak lo/A ~ in Jezre-el, Khesulloth, Shunem | their territory was Jezreel, Kesulloth and Shunem/A ~ in Helkath, Hali, Beten, Akshaf | their territory was Helkath, Hali, Beten and Akshaph) (r:4.21.23/1.14.7/6.19.18/6.19.25)
gam = (t:n) (w:kingdom/realm) (d:The land that a king rules; kumpi gam is a kingdom.) (e:kumpi ~ kipatna in Babilon/Darias in Babilon ~ teng a uk hi | Darius ruled the whole kingdom of Babylon/~ khat panin ~ khatah a vak kawikawi | wandering from one kingdom to another) (s:kumpigam) (r:1.10.10/5.3.13/27.9.1/19.105.13)
gam = (t:n) (w:land) (d:Land as the place where people live; after a name it means the land of, as in Kanaan gam, the land of Canaan.) (e:tua ~-a khamte hoih hi/~ sungah gal simna aw kiza a | the noise of battle is heard in the land/Israel ~ khuapi siate sunga teeng mite | the people living in the ruined cities of the land of Israel) (s:leitang) (r:1.2.12/1.23.12/24.50.22/26.33.24)
Gam = (t:n) (w:kingdom) (d:Gam written with a capital for the kingdom of God or of heaven, as in Pasian’ Gam and Vantung Gam.) (e:Vantung ~ hong nai zo hi/Pasian’ ~ in bang tawh ka genteh ding hiam | what shall I compare the kingdom of God to/Vantung ~ in suang manpha a zong | the kingdom of heaven is like one looking for precious stones/Ka pa in Kumpi ~ khat hong piak | my Father gave me a kingdom) (s:Kumpigam) (b:gam) (r:40.10.7/42.13.20/40.13.45/42.22.29) (q:draft)
gam-bawngtal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:Gam, wild country, with bawngtal, bull: a wild ox; also written gambawngtal.) (s:gambawngtal/gamsial/zangsial)
gama = (t:n) (w:of the land/in the land) (d:Gam with the ending a, which joins the land to the word that follows: of or in that land.) (e:Tua ~ mi khempeuh in/tua ~ piang ante na nek uh ciangin | when you eat the food of that land/Izipt ~ teeng mite | those who live in the land of Egypt/Judah ~ Khazih sungah a om pawlpi mite | the churches of Judea that are in Christ) (b:gam) (r:40.12.23/4.15.19/24.44.13/48.1.22) (q:draft)
Gamad = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gammad) (d:place, of uncertain location, whose men guarded the towers of Tyre) (r:26.27.11)
gamah = (t:n) (w:in the land/to the land/land/country) (d:Gam with the place marker ah: in or to the land of.) (e:Judah gam pan Galile ~ a paikik hi/Seir mual tung ~ Esau teng hi | Esau settled in the hill country of Seir/Absalom in Gilead ~ giahphual sat uh hi | Absalom camped in the land of Gilead/Tui om lohna lei keu ~ | in a dry land where there is no water) (b:gam) (r:43.4.2/1.37.1/1.36.8/10.17.26/26.19.13) (q:draft)
Gamah = (t:n) (w:in the kingdom/into the kingdom/in the land) (d:Gam, the capitalised word for kingdom or land, with ah, the marker of place: in or into the Kingdom, as in Vantung Gamah, in the kingdom of heaven.) (e:Vantung ~ a lian noptuamna na ngah ding/Vantung ~ na tung zo peuhmah kei ding uh hi | you will certainly not enter the kingdom of heaven/note ading a kibawlkholsa ~ hong pai un | come into the kingdom prepared for you/Thuciam ~ zong lutin | he will also enter the Promised Land) (b:Gam) (r:40.5.12/27.11.16/40.5.20/40.25.34) (q:draft)
Gamaliel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gamaliel) (d:name of two men: the son of Pedahzur, leader of the tribe of Manasseh in the wilderness, and a Pharisee and teacher of the law in Jerusalem) (r:4.7.54/4.10.23)
gambawngtal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ox) (e:~ in nangma na hong sem ding) (r:18.39.9)
gambawngtal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:Gam, wild country, with bawngtal, bull: a wild ox that cannot be made to work.) (e:Na ganbukah ~ hong giak nuam ding) (s:gamsial/zangsial/gam-bawngtal) (r:18.39.9)
gambulak = (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserted land) (d:Wild, empty country where no one goes; lam lianpite gambulak suak means the highways have become deserted.) (e:Lam lianpite ~ suak a) (s:gamlakpi) (r:23.33.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
gambup = (t:n) (w:the whole land) (d:Gam, land, with bup, whole: the whole of a land.) (e:Havilah ~ kimkot-a luang pen/mi khat bek hi napi-in ~ kipia hi | though he was only one man, the whole land was given to him) (r:1.2.11/26.33.24)
gambup = (t:n) (w:the entire country) (d:The whole extent of a country or region, from one border to the other.) (e:Argob ~, khuapi sawmgukte ahi hi/~ nisuahna gamgi panin ~ nitumna gamgi dong | from the eastern border of the whole country to its western border) (r:5.3.4/26.48.8)
gambuppi = (t:see) <gambuppi-ah>
gambuppi-ah = (t:n) (w:in the whole land/on the whole land) (d:Gam, land, with bup, whole, the intensifier pi and the place marker ah: in or upon the whole land.) (e:~ siatna ding thukhenna ka za khin) (r:23.28.22) (q:draft)
gamdai = (t:adj) (w:quiet/silent/peaceful) (d:Still and without noise, said of a land at peace or of people who stop speaking; gamdai takin is quietly and gamdai-in om is keep silent.) (e:tawlnga-in ~ takin om ta uh a/~-in om in la, kei thu hong gensak in | be silent and let me speak/Israelte aw, ~ un la, ngai un | Israel, be silent and listen/Numeite in ~ takin kiniamkhiatna tawh thu ngai-in | women should listen quietly and with humility/gam zai-in, ~-in, a nopna mun mu uh hi | they found a spacious, quiet and pleasant place) (s:dai) (r:23.14.7/18.29.10/18.33.31/5.27.9/54.2.11/13.4.40) (q:draft)
gamdaih = (t:v) (w:be quiet/be silent/fall silent) (d:Form of gamdai, quiet, used before nading and khit: become quiet, stop making noise.) (e:Mite a ~ khit ciangin/mite a ~ nadingin a khut a van hi | he motioned with his hand for the people to be quiet/mihonte a ~ nadingin a khut hong van a | he motioned with his hand for the crowd to be quiet/lai-at pa in mihonte a ~ nadingin khozo a) (s:daih) (a:gamlum) (b:gamdai) (r:44.21.40/44.19.35/44.19.33) (q:draft)
gamdaihna = (t:n) (w:solitary place/lonely place/desolate place) (d:Gamdaih, be quiet, with the noun suffix na: quiet country where no one is; often followed by mun, place.) (e:~ mun a zuan dingin a pai uh hi/~ mun khatah na pai-in thu a ngen hi | he went to a solitary place and prayed/~ munah Jesuh paikhia-in thu a ngen hi | Jesus withdrew to a lonely place and prayed/Zion mual in ~-ah kinusia khin ahih manin | because Mount Zion has been left desolate) (s:mundai) (b:gamdaih) (r:41.6.32/25.5.18/41.1.35/42.5.16) (q:draft)
gamdaisak = (t:v) (w:quiet/calm/silence) (d:Gamdai, quiet, with the causative sak: make people be quiet.) (e:Levi mite in mite ~ a) (s:daihsak/daisak) (b:gamdai) (r:16.8.11) (q:draft)
gamdaisakin = (t:v) (w:quieting/silencing) (d:Gamdaisak, make quiet, with the linking suffix in: quieting people before going on to speak.) (e:Moses’ mai-ah mite ~) (b:gamdaisak) (r:4.13.30) (q:draft)
gamdaizaw = (t:adj) (w:quieter/more quiet) (d:Gamdai, quiet, with the comparative zaw: quieter than before.) (e:amaute ~ kan uh ahih manin) (b:gamdai) (r:44.22.2) (q:draft)
gamdang = (t:adj) (w:foreign/strange) (d:Gam, land, with dang, other: of another country; gamdang mi is a foreigner or stranger and gamdang pasian a foreign god.) (e:~ mite in kei hong mai-et uh hi/amaute kiangah ~ pasian om lo hi | no foreign god was with them/ka innsung uhah ~ mite a teeng uh hi | foreigners live in our homes/~ numei a ten’pih mite | the men who had married foreign women) (s:namdang) (r:19.18.44/5.32.12/25.5.2/15.10.17) (q:draft)
gamdang = (t:n) (w:foreign land/foreign country) (d:Gam, land, with dang, other: a land that is not one’s own; gamdang khatah is to another land.) (e:~ ah bangci sak thei ding/Jakob kiang panin ~ khatah paikhia hi | he moved away from Jacob to another land/kumpigam khat pan ~ khatah a pai lai-in | as they went from one kingdom to another land/Solomon in ~ panin sakol a laknate | the horses Solomon brought in from abroad) (s:gamdangpi) (r:19.137.4/1.36.6/13.16.20/14.1.16) (q:draft)
gamdangah = (t:adv) (w:in a foreign land/to another land/among the nations) (d:Gamdang, foreign land, with the place marker ah: in or to another land, among other nations.) (e:i muh bangin amaute ~ lawn hi/Israel mite, ~ ka thehthang hun ciangin | when I scatter the people of Israel among the nations/lo khote khawhlawhsakin ~ a pai hi | he rented it to farmers and went to another country/Amaute in Israel mite, ~ thehthang uh a | they scattered the people of Israel among the nations) (b:gamdang) (r:5.29.28/26.4.13/41.12.1/29.3.2) (q:draft)
Gamdangah = (t:name) (w:Gamdangah) (d:not a proper name: the word gamdangah, in a foreign land, written with a capital at the start of a sentence)
gamdangmi = (t:n) (w:foreigner/stranger) (d:Gamdang, foreign, with mi, person: a person from another country.) (e:eite ~ bangin hong ngaihsun hi lo/~ kuamah in ne lo ding hi | no foreigner may eat it/~ khempeuh panin Israel mite tuam om uh a | the Israelites kept themselves apart from all foreigners) (s:khualmi/mikhual/minamdang) (a:tualsuak/gammi) (b:gamdang) (r:1.31.15/16.9.2/2.12.43) (q:draft)
gamdangpi = (t:n) (w:foreign land/foreign country) (d:Gamdang, foreign land, with the intensifier pi: a land wholly foreign to a person.) (e:~ hinapi-in peemta-in va om phot) (s:gamdang) (b:gamdang) (r:58.11.9) (q:draft)
gamdangte = (t:n) (w:nations/foreign nations/foreign lands) (d:Plural of gamdang: other countries and their peoples, the nations.) (e:~ in a zu a dawn manun/~ kiangah peengkul mut un | blow the trumpet among the nations/nang hong zangin ~ ka satnen a | with you I shatter nations/keimah in ~ sangin nang kong neusak zaw a | I will make you smaller than the nations) (b:gamdang) (r:24.51.7/24.46.1/24.51.27/24.51.20/24.49.15) (q:draft)
gamdong = (t:adv) (w:as far as the land/down to the realm) (d:Gam, land, with dong, until: as far as the land or realm of, in the verse the realm of the dead.) (e:Leinuaite’ ~ a kuang hi) (r:5.32.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamdung = (t:n) (w:length of the land) (d:Gam, land, with dung, length; paired with gamvai, the breadth of the land.) (e:~ gamvai kantanin pai in) (a:gamvai) (r:1.13.17) (q:draft)
gamgei = (t:n) (w:edge of the land/border) (d:Gam, land, with gei, side or edge; sehnel gamgei is the edge of the desert.) (e:Hori mite sehnel ~ a) (s:gamgi/gammong) (r:1.14.6) (q:draft)
gamgi = (t:n) (w:border/boundary/limit) (d:Gam, land, with gi, boundary: the border or limit of a land, of a city or of the sea.) (e:Moab ~ kantan ding na hi uh hi/Edom ~ Hor Mual ah | at Mount Hor on the border of Edom/Amor mite’ ~ in Akrabbim kahtohna | the boundary of the Amorites was from the ascent of Akrabbim/Tuipi ~ ding ciamteh sakin | marking out the limit for the sea) (s:gi/gammong) (r:5.2.18/7.1.36/4.20.23/18.38.10) (q:draft)
gamgite = (t:n) (w:borders/boundaries/territory) (d:Plural of gamgi: the borders of a land, and so the land within them.) (e:na ~ uh ka phut ding hi/mihingte’ ~ lakhia-in | removing the boundaries of the peoples/na ~ uh nomau’ adingin ka keek ding hi | I will enlarge your territory for you) (b:gamgi) (r:2.23.31/23.10.13/2.34.24) (q:draft)
gamh = (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage) (d:Land or property that is handed down in a family or tribe; gamh luah is to receive an inheritance.) (e:amau’ ~ in kip den ding hi/~ a kipia nai lo minam sagih om hi | there were seven tribes that had not yet been given an inheritance/a topa’ ~ pawlkhat a luah hi | he inherits a part of his master’s inheritance/minam khat pan a dangah ~ paikhia lo ding | no inheritance shall pass from one tribe to another) (s:gamhluah/gamluah/luah/luahna) (r:19.37.18/6.18.2/20.17.2/4.36.9) (q:draft)
gamhal = (t:v) (w:burn the land/set fire to the forest) (d:gam, land or wild country, with hal, burn) (e:tu-in ~ a kipan ding ka hi) (r:26.20.47) (q:draft)
gamhluah = (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage) (d:Gamh, inheritance, with luah, inherit: land or possession received as a share to keep.) (e:Judah minamte’ ~ ahi hi/Efraim mite in amau’ ~ ngah uh hi | the people of Ephraim received their inheritance/Gad mite’ ~ ahi hi | the inheritance of the Gadites) (s:gamh/gamluah/luahna/gamhluahna) (r:6.15.20/6.16.4/6.13.28) (q:draft)
gamhluah = (t:n) (w:heir) (d:The person who inherits.) (e:sila in keima ~ hi ding hi) (s:gamhluahpa/innluahpa) (r:1.15.3) (q:draft)
gamhluahin = (t:n) (w:as an inheritance) (d:Gamhluah, inheritance, with the marker in: as an inheritance, for a possession.) (e:~ na tanh dingin kong pia ding hi/na neih dingun ~ hong piak leitang tungah | in the land he is giving you to possess as an inheritance) (b:gamhluah) (r:13.16.18/5.15.4) (q:draft)
gamhluahna = (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage/property) (d:Gamhluah with the noun suffix na: the land or place that a person or tribe has inherited.) (e:amau’ ~ ciatah ciah uh hi/a ~ uh-ah ciahkik uh a | they returned to their inheritance/ama ~-ah a site min a kizop theih nadingin | so that the name of the dead may continue on his property) (s:gamhluah/gamh/luahna) (b:gamhluah) (r:7.21.24/8.4.10/7.21.23) (q:draft)
gamhluahpa = (t:n) (w:heir) (d:Gamhluah with pa, which marks a man: the man who inherits.) (e:mahmah na ~ hi ding hi/Hih mipa in nangma ~ hilo ding hi | this man will not be your heir) (s:innluahpa) (b:gamhluah) (r:1.15.4) (q:draft)
gamhluahte = (t:n) (w:heirs) (d:Gamhluah with the plural te: those who inherit.) (e:Tate i hih leh, ~ i hi hi) (b:gamhluah) (r:45.8.17) (q:draft)
gamhluahte = (t:n) (w:inheritance/inherited lands) (d:Gamhluah with the plural te: the shares of land that pass to the heirs.) (e:sungah amau’ ~ a kip hi/Zelofehad’ ~ a tanute tungah piak dingin | to give the inheritance of Zelophehad to his daughters) (s:gamhte) (b:gamhluah) (r:4.36.12/4.36.2) (q:draft)
gamhoih = (t:n) (w:good land) (d:Gam, land, with hoih, good: the good land that God promised.) (e:piak dinga ka ciam ~ mu lo ding) (s:gamnuam) (r:5.1.36) (q:draft)
gamhte = (t:n) (w:inheritances/inherited lands) (d:Plural of gamh: the shares of land handed down in a tribe or family.) (e:Israel mite’ ~ minam khat pan/amau’ ~ aisanna tawh kipia hi | their inheritances were assigned by lot/Moab zanglei-ah Moses in a hawm ~ ahi hi | the inheritances Moses gave out in the plains of Moab) (s:gamhluahte) (b:gamh) (r:4.36.7/6.14.2/6.13.32) (q:draft)
gamin = (t:n) (w:land/country) (d:Gam with the marker in written together: as a country, or the land as the subject of the sentence.) (e:a ~ ahi zongin na dingzo nawn/hih ~ eima aa hi taktak hi | this land is truly ours) (b:gam) (r:26.25.7/26.33.24) (q:draft)
gamkeel = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild goat) (d:Gam, wild country, with keel, goat: a wild goat.) (e:~ in a lawmte sam ding hi) (r:23.34.14) (q:draft)
gamkeelte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild goats) (d:Plural of gamkeel: wild goats.) (e:tua munah ~ laam ding uh hi) (b:gamkeel) (r:23.13.21) (q:draft)
gamkeu = (t:n) (w:dry land/parched land) (d:Gam, land, with keu, dry: land without water.) (e:tui om lohna ~ bangin ka pumpi) (s:leikeu/leikeuna) (r:19.63.1) (q:draft)
gamkhat = (t:n) (w:kingdom/country) (d:Gam, land or kingdom, written together with khat, one: one kingdom, a kingdom; gamkhat leh gamkhat is kingdom against kingdom.) (e:~ leh ~ hong kido ding uh hi) (r:42.21.10/41.3.24) (q:draft)
gamkhin = (t:see) <gamkhin'na>
gamkhin'na = (t:n) (w:desolation/ruin) (d:The state of a place laid waste; related to gamkhing, desolation, and also written gamkhinna.) (e:Khuapi sungah ~ bek om a) (s:gamkhinna/gamkhing) (r:23.24.12) (q:draft)
gamkhing = (t:n) (w:desolation/wasteland/desolate place) (d:A land or place laid waste and left without people; gamkhing suak is become desolate and gamkhing suaksak is make desolate.) (e:Jerusalem khua ~ a suak hi/leitung in sehnel ~ suak ding hi | the earth will become a desolate waste/Seir Mualtung gam khempeuh ~ ka suaksak ding a | I will make all of Mount Seir a desolation/Izipt ~ suaksakin | making Egypt desolate) (s:gamsia/mundai/gamkhinna) (r:23.64.10/33.7.13/26.35.7/26.32.15) (q:draft)
Gamkhing = (t:n) (w:Desolate) (d:Gamkhing, wasteland, written with a capital as a name given to the land.) (e:na leitang pen ~, kici nawn lo ding) (b:gamkhing) (r:23.62.4) (q:draft)
gamkhingin = (t:adv) (w:desolate/as a wasteland) (d:Gamkhing, desolate place, with the ending in: in a desolate state; with om it means lie desolate and with bawl make desolate.) (e:~ a om sung teng leitang in/Nang a ~ ka hong bawl ding hi | I will make you desolate/A ~ kong bawl paisuak ding a | I will make you desolate forever/~ a om sungteng a tawlnga hi ding hi | all the time it lies desolate it will have rest) (b:gamkhing) (r:3.26.43/26.35.9/26.35.3/3.26.35) (q:draft)
gamkhingpen = (t:adj) (w:most desolate) (d:Gamkhing, desolation, with the superlative pen: the most desolate of all.) (e:a ~ suak ding a) (b:gamkhing) (r:26.30.7) (q:draft)
gamkhinna = (t:n) (w:desolation/ruin) (d:The state of a place laid waste; related to gamkhing, desolation, and also written gamkhin'na.) (e:Khuapi sungah ~ bek om a) (s:gamkhin'na/gamkhing) (r:23.24.12) (q:draft)
gamkuam = (t:n) (w:valley) (d:gam, land, with kuam, valley: a valley region; Sukkot gamkuam is the Valley of Sukkoth) (e:Sukkot ~ ka sehkhia ding hi) (s:kuam/guam/mualkuam) (r:19.60.6/19.108.7) (q:draft)
gamla = (t:adj) (w:far/distant/far away) (d:far in place; with a before it and panin or ah after it, it is used as a noun: a gamla panin is from a distance, a gamla-ah is at a distance) (e:ka kiang panin ~ om kei in/a ~ mahmah gam panin | from a very distant country/mualtung ~ ahih manin | because the hills are far away/a ~ panin hong pai gamdang mi | the foreigner who comes from afar/mite a ~-ah ding uh hi | the people stood at a distance) (a:kinai) (r:19.38.21/41.5.6/6.9.9/1.19.19/5.29.22/2.20.21) (q:draft)
gamlak = (t:n) (w:forest) (e:Mei in ~ a haltum bang/~ ganhing khempeuh a vakkhiat hun | the time when all the beasts of the forest prowl) (s:tulak) (r:19.83.14/19.104.20)
gamlak = (t:n) (w:field) (e:nang in ~ kungte na ne ding hi/Esau ~ panin hong ciahin | Esau came in from the field/~ leh a sunga om khempeuh diang hen | let the fields and everything in them be jubilant/~ singkung khempeuh deengtan hi | it broke every tree of the field) (s:lolai) (r:1.3.18/2.9.25/1.25.29/13.16.32)
gamlak = (t:n) (w:wood) (e:~ panin vom a pi nih hong pai-in) (r:12.2.24)
gamlak = (t:n) (w:jungle/wilderness) (d:wild country where no one lives; the land the Israelites crossed after leaving Egypt) (e:Mei in ~ a haltum bang/pai khiatpihin ~ ka tun’pih a | leading them out, I brought them into the wilderness/~ gamsate in hong su lo ding hi | the wild animals will not harm you) (r:19.83.14/26.20.10/18.5.23)
gamlaka = (t:adv) (w:in the field/in the wilderness/in the open country) (d:gamlak with the place ending a, the short form of ah: that is in the field or wilderness; gamlaka om gamsate are the beasts of the field) (e:~ lopa omte kangin a puak ziazua/~ om gamsate, huih laka leeng vasate | the beasts of the field, the birds that fly in the air/Moan ~ om suangpi-ah amah paisuk hi | he went down to the rock in the Desert of Maon/Samaria khuapi, ~ ninkholna mun | the city of Samaria, a rubbish heap in the open field) (b:gamlak) (r:29.2.5/9.23.25/28.2.18/33.1.6) (q:draft)
gamlakah = (t:n) (w:field/in the field/in the wilderness) (d:gamlak with the place marker ah: in or into the field, the open country or the wilderness) (e:Amaute ~ a om ciangun/a ganhingte ~ nusia hi | he left his livestock in the field/Moses in ~ gul a khai bangin | as Moses lifted up the snake in the wilderness/Pawlkhatte ~ gammang uh a | some wandered in the wilderness) (b:gamlak) (r:1.4.8/26.39.5/2.9.21/43.3.14/19.107.4)
gamlakpi = (t:n) (w:wasteland/wilderness/desolate place) (d:gamlak, wild country, with pi, great: land left wild and empty; gamlakpi suak is become a wasteland) (e:Zion zong ~ suak a/~ a suak ding hi | it will become a wasteland/gamsate in tuate suksiatsakin ~ suak ding hi | wild animals will ruin them and it will become a wilderness) (s:gamkhing/gamsimtham/gamsia) (b:gamlak) (r:23.64.10/28.2.12/24.50.13) (q:draft)
gamlakte = (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserts/wild places) (d:gamlak with the plural te: the wild, uncultivated parts of a land) (e:ama ~ Eden huan ka bang sak ding) (b:gamlak) (r:23.51.3) (q:draft)
gamlapen = (t:adj) (w:farthest/most distant) (d:gamla, far, with pen, most; leimong gamlapen is the farthest end of the earth) (e:leimong ~ panin gam lian khat/Leitung a ~ mun panin huihpi hong nung hi | a mighty storm is rising from the farthest part of the earth/kumpi tampi leimong ~ panin | many kings from the farthest end of the earth) (a:naipen/kinaipen) (b:gamla) (r:24.6.22/24.25.32/24.50.41) (q:draft)
gamlapi = (t:adv) (w:far away/afar/far off) (d:gamla, far, with pi, great: at, to or from a great distance; gamlapi-ah is to a far place, gamlapi panin is from afar) (e:~ panin an hong ciahpih hi/amau’ gam panin ~-ah paipihin | taking them far from their own land/Gentailte kiangah ~-ah nang kong sawl ding hi | I will send you far away to the Gentiles/ka ngaihsutnate ~ pek panin na thei hi | you perceive my thoughts from afar) (s:pekah/peka) (a:kimnai-a) (b:gamla) (r:20.31.14/18.27.21/29.3.6/44.22.21/19.139.2) (q:draft)
gamlat = (t:adj) (w:far/distant) (d:form of gamla used before another word; a gamlat mah bangin is as far as) (e:nitumna panin a ~ mah bangin) (b:gamla) (r:19.103.12) (q:draft)
gamlatna = (t:n) (w:distance) (d:gamla far in its form gamlat with the noun suffix na: how far away something is) (e:khuapite a ~ teh ding uh hi/lampi a ~ hangin | because of the length of the road) (b:gamlat) (r:5.21.2/5.19.6) (q:draft)
gamlazaw = (t:adj) (w:farther/more distant) (d:gamla, far, with the comparative zaw) (e:gungal a ~ deuhin a ding pa) (a:naizaw) (b:gamla) (r:27.12.6) (q:draft)
gamlelei = (t:n) (w:whole land/land) (d:apparently gam, land, le, and, lei, earth, written as one word: the land and the ground) (e:awging in ~ lingsak hi) (r:24.8.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamlian = (t:n) (w:great nation/great country) (d:gam, land, with lian, great) (e:~ khat leh kumpi tampi) (r:24.50.41) (q:draft)
gamluah = (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage) (d:gam, land, with luah, inherit: land or a share received as an inheritance) (e:~ hoih nei ka hi hi/Manasseh mite’ ~ sung panin | from within the inheritance of the Manassites/a sanggamte lakah ~ nei lo ding uh hi | they shall have no inheritance among their brothers) (s:gamh/gamhluah/luah) (r:19.16.6/6.16.9/5.18.2) (q:draft)
gamluahna = (t:n) (w:inheritance/possession of land) (d:gamluah, inheritance, with the noun suffix na: the holding of land by inheritance) (e:~ tawh tua leitang a nei mipa) (s:gamhluahna) (b:gamluah) (r:3.27.24) (q:draft)
gamlum = (t:n) (w:noise/uproar/tumult/commotion) (d:loud confused noise of a crowd or of battle) (e:gal kidona ~ sungah Moab mite si ding/mihonpi ~ bangin mual tungte ah | on the mountains, like the noise of a great multitude/~ leh mi tampi kap a | a commotion and many people weeping) (s:gamlumna/husa/huging) (a:daihna) (r:30.2.2/23.13.4/41.5.38) (q:draft)
gamlum = (t:v) (w:be in uproar/make a commotion/be noisy) (d:be full of noise and disorder, said of a crowd, an army or a town) (e:galkapte in a ~ uh hi/khuapi sung ~ hi | the city is in an uproar/awng-in a ~ henhan uh hi | they roar with a great noise/mihonpi ~ a, om a muh ciangin | when he saw the crowd making a commotion) (s:kigamlum/kibuai) (a:gamdaih/daai) (r:44.12.18/11.1.45/24.51.55/40.9.23) (q:draft)
gamlumin = (t:adv) (w:in an uproar/in confusion) (d:gamlum uproar with the suffix in; gamlumin om is be in an uproar) (e:Jerusalem khuazang ~ a om uh/A kikhawm mite zong ~ om uh | the assembled people too were in confusion) (b:gamlum) (r:44.21.31/44.19.32) (q:draft)
gamlumna = (t:n) (w:noise/uproar/tumult/commotion) (d:gamlum, uproar, with the noun suffix na: the loud noise of a crowd, of rejoicing, of mourning or of a riot) (e:Ngai un, khuapi sunga ~/a cingte leh mite’ ~ a zak ciangin | when she heard the noise of the guards and the people/Tua ~ a bei khit ciangin | when the uproar had ended/Nangma zak in hih ~ ahi hi | that is the noise you hear) (s:gamlum/husa/huging) (a:daihna) (b:gamlum) (r:23.66.6/12.11.13/44.20.1/11.1.45) (q:draft)
gamlumnate = (t:n) (w:noises/noise/clamour) (d:plural of gamlumna, the loud noise of people, of singing or revelry) (e:La sa-in na ~ uh khawl un/khuasung ~ na bil in za thei nawn loin | when your ears can no longer hear the noises of the street/lungdam a, ~ om nawn lo a | the noise of those who rejoice is no more) (b:gamlumna) (r:30.5.23/23.24.8/21.12.4) (q:draft)
gamlumsak = (t:v) (w:cause an uproar/start a riot) (d:gamlum, uproar, with the causative sak) (e:khua sung a ~ uh a) (b:gamlum) (r:44.17.5) (q:draft)
gamlumte = (t:n) (w:tumult/uproar) (d:gamlum with plural te; mi gamlumte is the peoples in tumult, the turmoil of the nations) (e:mi ~ a daisakpa aw) (b:gamlum) (r:19.65.7) (q:draft)
gammang = (t:v) (w:stray/wander/be lost) (d:go astray and be lost, said of animals and of people; before tulak it describes wild overgrown land, as in gammang tulak, a wild thicket) (e:Israel pawl a ~ tuute kiangah/a tuu ahi zongin a ~ na muh leh | if you see his sheep straying/Pawlkhatte gamlakah ~ uh a | some wandered in the wilderness/A ~ tuu bangin lam ka pial khin hi | I have strayed like a lost sheep) (s:lampial/vakmang) (r:40.10.6/5.22.1/19.107.4/19.119.176) (q:draft)
gammanpih = (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to wander) (d:take others along in going astray and wandering lost) (e:lamkhialin a ~ uh hi) (s:lampialsak) (r:24.50.6) (q:draft)
gammi = (t:n) (w:citizen/native/inhabitant) (d:person belonging to a land; after a place name it names a person of that place, as Shuah gammi, the Shuhite) (e:Shuah ~ Bildad in dawng a/Rom ~ ahihlam ka theih ciangin | when I learned that he was a Roman citizen/peemta hitaleh ~ hitaleh | whether foreigner or native-born/Pasian’ mite tawh ~ khat na hi uh hi | you are fellow citizens with God's people) (s:khuami/tualsuak) (a:peemta/gamdangmi/khualmi) (b:gam) (r:18.8.1/49.2.19/44.23.27/2.12.19) (q:draft)
gammite = (t:n) (w:people of the land/subjects/citizens) (d:gammi with plural te, the people who belong to a land or to a ruler) (e:~ lungdam uh a, migilote in/Midian ~ a linna ka mu hi | I saw the people of Midian trembling/ama ~ in hih ulianpa mudah uh | his subjects hated this nobleman/tuipi gei-a om ~ tungah ka sawl ding hi | I will send them to the peoples who live by the sea) (s:khuamite) (a:khualmite) (b:gammi) (r:20.29.2/42.19.14/35.3.7/23.66.19) (q:draft)
gammong = (t:n) (w:end of the land/border/frontier) (d:gam, land, with mong, end: the farthest part of a country) (e:~ khat panin ~ khat dongah/Moab gam ~ dongin | as far as the end of the land of Moab) (s:gamgi) (r:24.12.12/24.48.45) (q:draft)
gammongah = (t:n) (w:in a remote area/at the end of the land) (d:gammong, the farthest part of a land, with the place marker ah) (e:Efraim mualtung ~ peemin) (b:gammong) (r:7.19.1) (q:draft)
gamnawl = (t:see) <gamnawl-ah>
gamnawl-ah = (t:n) (w:on the border/at the edge of the land) (d:gamnawl, the border or edge of a land, with the place marker ah) (e:Kanaan ~ Reuben mite leh Gad mite) (r:6.22.11) (q:draft)
gamneu = (t:n) (w:province) (d:gam land with neu small: one of the smaller lands that make up an empire) (e:~ za khat sawmnih-le-sagih a uk) (r:17.1.1) (q:draft)
gamneute = (t:n) (w:provinces) (d:gamneu, province, with the plural te) (e:Asia ~ a uk ulian kimkhatte) (b:gamneu) (r:44.19.31) (q:draft)
gamnin = (t:n) (w:unclean land/polluted land) (d:gam, land, with nin, unclean) (e:a ninsa ~ ahi hi) (r:15.9.10) (q:draft)
gamnuam = (t:n) (w:pleasant land/good land) (d:gam land with nuam pleasant) (e:Amaute in ~ simmawh uh a/a kibawlkholsa ~ hong luah un | come and inherit the good land prepared beforehand) (s:gamhoih) (a:gamsia) (r:19.106.24/33.7.14/40.25.34) (q:draft)
gampa = (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserted place/lonely place) (d:uninhabited country; in the verses always as gampa lakah, in or into the wilderness) (e:Zeisu ~ lakah a sawl pah hi/~ lakah khomun a ne uh a | they ate the manna in the wilderness/amah ~ lakah pai a, thu a ngen hi | he went into the lonely places and prayed/khuanawl ~ lakah a om hi | he stayed outside the town in lonely places) (s:gampalak/gamdaihna) (r:41.1.12/43.6.49/42.5.16/41.1.45) (q:draft)
gampalak = (t:n) (w:wilderness/desert) (d:gampa, uninhabited country, written together with lak, among: the wilderness) (e:~ mi kikhopna lakah ahi zongin) (s:gampa/sehnel) (r:44.7.38) (q:draft)
gampalakah = (t:n) (w:in the wilderness/in the desert) (d:gampalak, wilderness, with the place marker ah) (e:Sinai Mual ~, mei a kuang) (b:gampalak) (r:44.7.30) (q:draft)
Gampalakah = (t:adv) (w:in the wilderness) (d:gampalak wilderness with the marker ah, written with a capital) (e:~ kum sawmli tawntung) (b:gampalakah) (r:44.7.42) (q:draft)
gampan = (t:adv) (w:from the land) (d:gam, land, with pan, from: from the land or region of a named place) (e:Rimmon ~ hong kipanin Ai-ath khua) (r:23.10.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
gampi = (t:n) (w:boundary/border/edge of territory) (d:the limit of a land; the other Bible text has gamgi in the same verse) (e:Reuben mite’ ~ pen Jordan ahi hi) (s:gamgi/gammong) (b:gam) (r:6.13.23/4.22.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:beast) (e:a lauhuai ~ khempeuh ka beisak ding/~ khat in amah netum khin zo hi | a wild beast has devoured him/~ khempeuhte’ kumpi ahi hi | he is king over all the beasts) (s:sahang) (a:innsa) (r:26.34.25/26.14.15/1.37.33/18.41.34)
gamsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wildlife) (e:tuu leh bawng khempeuh, ~ khempeuh zong | all sheep and cattle, and all the animals of the wild too) (r:19.8.7)
gamsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild animal) (d:gam, wild country, with sa, animal: an animal that lives in the wild, set against innsa, an animal kept at the house) (e:innsa, ~, leh a bokvak ganhingte/~ khatpeuh in a sikkhap khak ding | that some wild animal may trample them/~ peuhmah ama' nam ciat | every wild animal according to its kind) (a:innsa) (r:1.1.24/18.39.15/1.7.14)
gamsai = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wormwood/bitter herb) (d:a bitter plant; gamsai tawh vak, feed with wormwood, is a picture of bitter suffering; also the name of the star Wormwood in Revelation) (e:amaute ~ tawh ka vak ding a/hih mite ~-in ka vak ding a | I will feed this people with wormwood/tui seh thum suah seh khat in ~-tui suak a | a third of the waters became wormwood water) (r:24.23.15/66.8.11/24.9.15) (q:draft)
Gamsai = (t:name) (c:star) (w:Wormwood) (d:gamsai, wormwood, written with a capital as the name of the star that makes the waters bitter) (e:Tua aksi a min in ~ kici hi) (b:gamsai) (r:66.8.11) (q:draft)
gamsate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild animals/beasts) (d:gamsa, wild animal, with the plural te) (e:~ leh innsate khempeuh/leitung ~ na kihta kei ding hi | you will not fear the wild animals of the earth/~ in a hiangte tuancil ding uh hi | the wild animals will trample its branches/huih lak vasate leh gamlak ~ tungah | to the birds of the air and the wild animals) (s:sahangte) (a:innsate) (b:gamsa) (r:19.148.10/18.37.8/18.5.22/26.31.13/9.17.44) (q:draft)
gamsia = (t:n) (w:wasteland/desolate land) (d:gam, land, with sia, bad or ruined) (e:Edom gam in ~ suak ding hi) (s:gamkhing/gamsimtham/gamlakpi) (a:gamnuam/gamhoih) (r:29.3.19) (q:draft)
gamsial = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:gam, wild country, with sial, the mithun: a strong wild ox, in older English Bibles the unicorn) (e:~ tha bang hatna nei uh hi/a kite in ~ kite ahi hi | his horns are the horns of a wild ox) (s:gambawngtal/zangsial/gam-bawngtal) (r:4.23.22/5.33.17) (q:draft)
gamsialno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young wild ox) (d:gamsial wild ox with no, young) (e:bawngno leh ~ bangin) (b:gamsial) (r:19.29.6) (q:draft)
gamsialte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild oxen) (d:gamsial, wild ox, with the plural te) (e:~’ ki panin a cimawh keimah) (b:gamsial) (r:19.22.21) (q:draft)
gamsimtham = (t:n) (w:wasteland/desolate land) (d:gam land with simtham desolate: a land left empty with no one living in it) (e:Babylon gam ~ suaksak a/Tua gam pen ~ suakin, hawmsuak ding hi | that land will become a wasteland and lie empty) (s:gamkhing/gamsia/gamlakpi) (r:24.51.29/23.34.11) (q:draft)
gamsung = (t:n) (w:land) (d:gam, land, with sung, inside: a land or country as an area, often after its name) (e:Hebron ~/~ teng uih hi | the whole land stank/Izipt ~ khempeuhah pai hi | he went throughout the land of Egypt/Beor’ tapa Bela in Edom ~ uk hi | Bela son of Beor ruled the land of Edom) (s:gam) (r:2.8.14/19.105.33/1.41.46/1.36.32)
gamsung = (t:adj) (w:wild) (d:of the open country, said of animals and plants that live or grow wild and of a man who lives outdoors) (e:~ ganhing/~ ganhing khempeuh min vawh hi | he gave names to all the wild animals/Esau in ~ mi sabet siam khat hi a | Esau was a man of the open country, a skilful hunter) (r:1.2.19/1.2.20/1.25.27)
gamsunga = (t:adv) (w:in the land/in the country) (d:gamsung, the inside of a land, with the ending a that links it to the words that follow: in the land of, that is in the land) (e:Izipt ~ a om kum sagih/Edom ~ kumpite ahi uh hi | they were the kings in the land of Edom/Kanaan ~ a lam a neihsa khempeuh | all the goods he had acquired in Canaan/Kanaan ~ ama' neih Esau’ tapate | the sons of Esau born to him in Canaan) (b:gamsung) (r:1.41.53/1.36.31/1.36.6/1.36.5) (q:draft)
gamsungah = (t:adv) (w:in the land/into the land) (d:gamsung with the place marker ah; follows the name of the land) (e:Tu-in ~ kialpi nasia semsem hi/Amah Paran ~ teng hi | he lived in the Desert of Paran/Tua gam panin Assiria ~ amah pai a | from that land he went into Assyria/hih ~ sum na bawl thei ding uh hi | you can trade in this land) (b:gamsung) (r:1.43.1/1.21.21/1.10.11/1.42.34) (q:draft)
gamta = (t:n) (w:motion)
gamta = (t:v) (w:act/do/behave/conduct oneself) (d:act or conduct oneself in a certain way; the word before it says how, as in a manin gamta, do what is right, and a sia gamta, do evil) (e:midikte a man-in ~ uh hi/a thupiak bangin Zelofehad’ tanute ~ uh hi | the daughters of Zelophehad did as he commanded/pilna tawh ~ un la | act with wisdom/Mihingte bang lelin ~ na hi hiam | do you act merely as mortals do/hoih takin ~ in la, paubaang kei in | walk rightly and be blameless) (r:20.21.8/4.36.10/51.4.5/18.10.4/1.17.1)
gamtaang = (t:v) (w:move) (e:leitungah a ~, a nungtate) (r:1.1.28)
gamtaang = (t:v) (w:stir)
gamtaang = (t:v) (w:be active) (e:amah a ~ ahihna lak hi | he shows that he is the one at work) (r:18.37.7)
gamtakha = (t:v) (w:act/do/happen to do) (d:gamta, act, with kha, which shows the act is fallen into or happens to be done; with kei, do not act so) (e:gamtat bangin ~ kei in/a man loin ~ kei un | do not act wrongly/hih bangin ka ~ uh hi | that is why we did this/a sia bekbek a ~ ka hihna ka thei hi | I find that I end up doing only evil) (r:20.3.31/45.7.21/20.23.4/6.9.24) (q:draft)
gamtakhial = (t:v) (w:do wrong/act wrongly) (d:gamta, act, with khial, err) (e:Jesuh ~ hi, ci-in a mawhsak nuam) (r:41.3.2) (q:draft)
gamtakik = (t:v) (w:act again/do again) (d:gamta, act, with kik, again or back: go back to a way of acting, whether evil or good) (e:Israel mite a sia ~ uh a/a man a hoihin hong ~ hen la | and he turns to do what is just and right/gamtat hoih lote mah a ~ nuam na hi hi | you wanted to do those evil deeds again) (s:hihkik) (b:gamta) (r:7.13.1/26.33.14/26.23.21) (q:draft)
gamtalai = (t:v) (w:still act/go on acting) (d:gamta, act, with lai, still) (e:bangun ~ veve uh hi) (r:36.3.7) (q:draft)
gamtang = (t:adj) (w:moving) (e:leitunga a ~ khempeuh/A nungta a ~ peuhmah | everything that lives and moves/tuipi leh a sunga ~ khempeuhte | the seas and all that move in them) (r:1.8.19/1.9.3/19.69.34)
gamtang = (t:n) (w:movement)
gamtang = (t:n) (w:motion)
gamtang = (t:phrase) (w:in motion) (e:tua tuitung teng ah Pasian’ Kha a ~ hi | the Spirit of God was moving over the waters) (r:1.1.2)
gamtangsak = (t:v) (w:cause to walk/cause to live) (d:gamtang, move about, with the causative sak: make people move about and live on the land) (e:na leitang uhah kong ~ kik ding) (b:gamtang) (r:26.36.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtangsakkik = (t:v) (w:cause to walk again/cause to live again) (d:gamtangsak with kik, again) (e:na leitang uhah kong ~ ding hi) (b:gamtangsak) (r:26.36.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtangtang = (t:v) (w:move along/go by) (d:doubled form of gamtang, move: keep moving on) (e:amah ~ a, ahih hangin amah) (r:18.9.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtangzo = (t:v) (w:be able to move about/be able to go about) (d:gamtang, move about, with zo, be able) (e:keima ut bangin ka ~ nawn kei) (b:gamtang) (r:5.31.2) (q:draft)
gamtapa = (t:n) (w:one who acts/one who walks) (d:gamta act, behave, with pa marking a man: the man who conducts himself in the way named) (e:ama lungkim banga a ~ amah in kipsak hi/mawhna tawh a ~ leh a galte’ | the one who goes on in sin and his enemies) (b:gamta) (r:19.37.23/19.68.21) (q:draft)
gamtasak = (t:v) (w:make act/cause to behave/lead into) (d:gamta act with the causative sak) (e:makaite pen mihai bangin ~ hi/mi khempeuh amau utbang ciatin hong ~ hi | he let all people go their own way) (b:gamta) (r:18.12.17/66.2.14/44.14.16) (q:draft)
gamtasak = (t:v) (w:pasture/let graze) (d:let animals move about and feed) (e:unok pak lakah a tuute ~ hi/Israel gam lonona mun khempeuhah ka ~ ding hi | I will pasture them in all the grazing places of the land of Israel/Bashan le Gilead gam nuamah amaute ~ in | let them feed in the good land of Bashan and Gilead/bawnghon ahi zongin ~ kei in | do not let even the herds graze) (s:tasak/anvak) (b:gamta) (r:22.6.3/2.34.3/26.34.14/33.7.14) (q:draft)
gamtat = (t:v) (w:behave) (d:form of gamta used before words such as ding, bangin, leh, kei, khin and nading) (e:ut bangin ka ~ kei leh/Bangcia hici ~ na hi hiam | what is this you have done/Bang hangin hici ~ na hi hiam | why are you acting like this/Tu-in na hai ~ khin hi | now you have acted foolishly) (b:gamta) (r:43.10.37/1.3.13/26.24.19/1.31.28)
gamtat = (t:v) (w:act/do) (e:a sia-in ~ ding nuam a sa/a pa David ~ bangin | as his father David had done/keima' gen bangin na ~ uh leh | if you do as I say/ka gitloh ~ khin uh hi | we have acted wickedly) (b:gamta) (r:20.2.14/20.11.19/11.15.11/2.23.22/19.106.6)
gamtate = (t:n) (w:those who act/those who behave) (d:plural: people who conduct themselves in the way stated before the word) (e:A man loin a ~ tungah/a man-a ~ tungah lungkim hi | he delights in those who act rightly/Topa in a sia-a ~ mudah a | the Lord detests those who do evil/Tua uite, gilo-a ~ na peel un | watch out for those dogs, those evildoers) (s:gamtatte) (b:gamta) (r:18.31.3/20.11.20/20.3.32/50.3.2) (q:draft)
gamtateng = (t:v) (w:all who do/all who act) (d:gamta, act, with teng, all: all those who act so) (e:deihna bangin a ~ bek lutthei ding) (b:gamta) (r:40.7.21) (q:draft)
gamtatin = (t:v) (w:acting/behaving) (d:gamtat with the linking ending -in: acting in the way named before it, as in hai gamtatin, acting foolishly) (e:kote hai ~ ka khialhna hangun/Cingh ~ mi tungah leitawi pia a | acting generously, he lends to others/kihhuai ~, ahoih-a gamta kuamah om lo hi | they act vilely; there is no one who does good/amaute in bangci ~ a si uh | how they lived and died) (b:gamtat) (r:4.12.11/19.14.1/19.112.5/58.13.7) (q:draft)
gamtatkha = (t:v) (w:act/behave) (d:gamtat, act, with kha, which marks something one comes to do without meaning to; in the verses of having acted wrongly or foolishly) (e:kote a khial ~ ka hi uh hi/Ka hai ~ a, nakpitakin ka khial khin hi | I have acted like a fool and have been terribly wrong/ka hai ~ khin hi | I have done a very foolish thing) (r:16.9.33/9.26.21/10.24.10) (q:draft)
gamtatkhak = (t:v) (w:act/behave) (d:form of gamtatkha, come to act in a way not intended, used before ding; a sia-in gamtatkhak is fall into doing evil) (e:a sia-in na ~ ding hong kem) (b:gamtatkha) (r:20.2.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtatkik = (t:v) (w:act rightly again/return to right conduct) (d:gamtat, behave, with kik, again or back) (e:a manin a ~ theih nadingin thunem) (b:gamtat) (r:48.6.1) (q:draft)
gamtatna = (t:n) (w:action/deed/conduct/works) (d:gamtat, act, with the noun suffix na: what a person does, his deeds and way of acting) (e:a ~ panun kimukhia thei hi/Hehpihna hangah ahih leh, ~ hang ahi kei hi | if it is by grace, it is not because of works/hih in keima ~ ahi hi | this is what I have done/zuihna-ah ka ~ kip ta hen | may my ways be steadfast in obeying) (s:hihna/tatna) (b:gamtat) (r:20.20.11/1.9.24/45.11.6/6.7.20/19.119.5)
gamtatna = (t:n) (w:activity/movement) (b:gamtat)
Gamtatna = (t:n) (w:deeds/conduct/works) (d:gamtatna, conduct or deeds, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in Gitloh Gamtatna, lawlessness) (e:Gitloh ~ kigamta khinta a | lawlessness is already at work/~ hoih om lo na upna hong lak in | show me your faith without good deeds/~ tawh kipaaikhia ahi hiam | is it excluded by works) (b:gamtatna) (r:53.2.7/59.2.18/45.3.27) (q:draft)
gamtatnasa = (t:n) (w:deeds/past conduct) (d:gamtatna, deed, with sa, already done: what someone has done, things already committed) (e:a ~ khempeuh gen hi/A pu a pate’ ~ khempeuh bangin | just as all his fathers had done/ama ~ khialhna ama tungah a va kihilh leh | if the sin he has committed is made known to him/Ama ~ mawhnate kimaisak ding hi | the sins he has committed will be forgiven) (s:hihnasa) (b:gamtatna) (r:1.24.66/12.24.9/12.23.37/3.4.23/26.33.16) (q:draft)
gamtatnasate = (t:n) (w:deeds/past conduct/practices) (d:plural of gamtatnasa: the things someone has done, past conduct) (e:Na ~ hangin na maizum ding a/A muhdahhuai na ~ uh hangin | because of your detestable practices/na ~ uh hangin thu hong khenin | judging you according to your conduct) (s:hihnasate) (b:gamtatnasa) (r:26.16.54/26.7.8/26.7.9) (q:draft)
gamtatnate = (t:n) (w:deeds/ways/practices/actions) (d:plural of gamtatna: the things a person does, his ways of acting) (e:Ka ~ ka ngaihsun a/minamte’ zat a kihhuai ~ mah bangin | following the detestable practices of the nations/amau ~ tawh palhngulhna a bawl uh hi | by their deeds they prostituted themselves/ka ~ na mit-in en gige in | let your eyes keep watching my ways) (s:hihnate/septe/nasepnate) (b:gamtatna) (r:19.119.59/14.33.2/19.106.39/20.23.26) (q:draft)
gamtatnateng = (t:n) (w:all the deeds/all the practices) (d:gamtatna deed, conduct, with teng, all of them) (e:na zumhuai ~ na thuak kul hi/Na paktat ~ hong kipholak ding hi | all your acts of prostitution will be exposed) (b:gamtatna) (r:26.16.58/26.23.29) (q:draft)
gamtatnaziate = (t:n) (w:actions/ways of acting/conduct) (d:gamtatna, action, with zia, manner, and the plural te) (e:a ~ uh tawh kizui-in amaute tungah) (r:26.36.19) (q:draft)
gamtatnop = (t:v) (w:want to do/wish to do) (d:gamtat, act, with nop, want) (e:A hoih ka ~ teng gamta loin) (s:hihnop/sepnop) (r:45.7.19) (q:draft)
gamtatnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to do/will to act) (d:gamtatnop, want to do, with the noun suffix na) (e:a hoih ~ lungsim a om hangin) (s:bawlnopna/sepnopna) (b:gamtatnop) (r:45.7.18) (q:draft)
gamtatpha = (t:n) (w:good deed/good conduct/good) (d:gamtat behave with pha good: doing what is good) (e:~ tawh gitlohna na zo un/~ apawlpawl tawh na dim mahmah nadingun | so that you may abound in every kind of good work) (s:hoihtatna) (a:gamtatsia/gamtatsiatna) (r:45.12.21/47.9.8) (q:draft)
gamtatsa = (t:v) (w:have done/did) (d:gamtat, act, with sa, already done; gamtatsa bangin is as someone had done) (e:Ahab’ innkuante’ ~ bangin Topa’ muhna-ah) (b:gamtat) (r:12.8.27) (q:draft)
gamtatsia = (t:adj) (w:evil-doing/wicked/corrupt) (d:of bad conduct; gamtatsia mite are evildoers) (e:~ mite huh lo ding hi/a ~ tapate | children given to corruption/a ~ mite na thuakzo kei hi | you cannot tolerate evildoers/Note ~ na hih manun | because you have done evil) (s:gilo/gitloh) (r:18.8.20/18.34.22/23.1.4/35.1.13/33.3.4) (q:draft)
gamtatsia = (t:n) (w:evil behaviour/wrongdoing/misconduct) (d:gamtat, conduct, with sia, bad) (e:~ leh thuzuau ka mudah hi/na innsung pan ~ khempeuh bei sak in la | remove all wickedness from your house/Amau’ ~ khempeuh Gilgal phual pan akipan hi a | all their wickedness began at Gilgal/ama ~ pen ama luzang mah ah tu hi | his wrongdoing comes down on his own head) (s:gamtatsiatna) (a:gamtatpha) (r:20.8.13/18.22.23/28.9.15/19.7.16) (q:draft)
gamtatsiat = (t:v) (w:do wrong/act corruptly/behave badly) (d:gamtat, behave, with siat, bad: do what is wrong or evil; the form of gamtatsia used before ding, ngei, zah and nawn, where it can also be read as wrongdoing) (e:~ ding ut lo a/~ ding a manlangte | those who are quick to do wrong/Mihaite in ~ ding nuamsa uh a | fools enjoy doing wrong/na ~ nawn loh nading | so that you do wrong no more/a ~ ngei bangin gamta lai veve uh | they still acted as corruptly as before) (b:gamtatsia) (r:26.18.8/20.6.18/20.10.23/18.34.32/36.3.7) (q:draft)
gamtatsiate = (t:n) (w:evildoers/the wicked) (d:gamtatsia, of bad conduct, with the plural te: people who do evil) (e:Mi ~ ahih leh cithei bek loin/~ bang tanvei kihisak lai ding uh a | how long will the evildoers go on boasting) (s:migilote/misiate/tatsiate) (a:midikte/mihoihte) (b:gamtatsia) (r:39.3.15/19.94.4) (q:draft)
gamtatsiate = (t:n) (w:evil deeds/wrongdoings) (d:gamtatsia, bad conduct, with the plural te: the wrong things that someone has done) (e:na ~ uh hangin gim kong pia ding | I will punish you for your evil deeds/kote’ ~ le a lian ka mawhnate uh hangin | because of our evil deeds and our great sins/a mindaihuai ~ gamtat ding hong kipan leh | if he begins to do shameful evil deeds) (s:gamtatsiatnate/tatsiatnate/siatnate) (a:hoihnate) (b:gamtatsia) (r:15.9.13/24.23.2/26.18.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtatsiatna = (t:n) (w:evil deed/wicked conduct/wrongdoing) (d:gamtat, conduct, with siat, bad, and -na: bad behaviour or the evil things a person has done) (e:Amau’ ~ hangin gim ka pia ding hi/Amau’ ~ khempeuh ka phawk lam tak | that I remember all their evil deeds/na ~ uh tawh kizui-in daan kong tat ding | I will punish you according to your evil conduct/tua a ~ hangin amah si ding hi | he will die because of that wrongdoing) (s:tatsiatna/gamtatsia) (a:gamtatpha) (r:28.7.12/26.18.26/28.7.2/26.7.3/26.33.18) (q:draft)
gamtatsiatnate = (t:n) (w:evil deeds/wrongdoings) (d:plural of gamtatsiatna: the evil things that people have done) (e:Na ~ uh ka mangngilh ngei kei ding hi/a ~ uh tawh Pasian ze-et napi-un | though they put God to the test with their evil deeds) (s:gamtatsiate/tatsiatnate/siatnate) (a:hoihnate) (b:gamtatsiatna) (r:30.8.7/39.3.15) (q:draft)
gamtatte = (t:n) (w:practices/deeds/doings) (d:gamtat used as a noun with plural -te: the things someone does, ways of behaving) (e:a kihhuai a ~ mah uh bangin/a muhdahhuai a ~ uh tawh lungkim nai lo | not yet satisfied with their detestable practices) (s:gamtatnate/tatnate/gamtatziate) (b:gamtat) (r:12.16.3/26.8.17) (q:draft)
gamtatte = (t:n) (w:those who act/those who behave/doers) (d:people who behave in the way named before it; a kiphatsak gamtatte are those who act proudly) (e:a kiphatsak ~ nakpi takin thuk hi/a kihhuai ~ kihhuai gamtat lailai hen la | let those who act vilely go on acting vilely/a hoih ~ hoih gamtat lailai hen la | let those who do right go on doing right) (b:gamtat) (r:19.31.23/66.22.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtatzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to act/be able to do) (d:gamtat, act, with zawh, be able; cit gamtatzawh is be able to act generously) (e:note na cit ~ tawntung nadingun) (s:hihzawh) (r:47.9.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtatzia = (t:n) (w:conduct/way of acting/example/practice) (d:the manner in which someone acts, and so an example for others; gamtatzia zui means follow the example of) (e:keima ~ hong zui ta un/Khrih ~ ka zuih mah bangin | just as I follow the example of Christ/Kote’ ~ bangin a gamta ding | to act according to our example/note’ etteh ding ~ a hong lak | showing you a way of acting to imitate/Pasian’ ~ ding kuamah in sawl thei lo | no one can prescribe how God should act) (s:tatna/nuntakzia) (r:46.11.1/9.2.13/53.3.7/53.3.9/18.36.23) (q:draft)
gamtatziate = (t:n) (w:actions/ways of acting/doings) (d:plural of gamtatzia: the ways in which someone acts) (e:na ~ uh khel un la) (s:gamtatnate/tatnate/gamtatnaziate) (b:gamtatzia) (r:24.26.13) (q:draft)
gamtazaw = (t:v) (w:act rather/act instead/behave rather) (d:gamta, act, with zaw, rather: do this and not the other thing) (e:Pasian’ sila bangin na ~ un/ci-in a kigelh bangin ~ un | act rather as it is written) (b:gamta) (r:60.2.16/45.12.20) (q:draft)
gamtazo = (t:v) (w:carry out/do/act) (d:gamta, act, with zo, be able or have done fully: manage to act as required, have done as told) (e:nong gen bangin ka ~ hi/Thukham deihna bangin a ~ mi khempeuh | everyone who does as the Law requires/keima deihna bangin a ~ mite tungah | to those who do my will) (s:hihzo) (b:gamta) (r:9.28.21/66.2.26/45.10.5) (q:draft)
gamte = (t:n) (w:lands/countries/territories/kingdoms) (d:plural of gam; kumpi gamte are kingdoms, and a lonona gamte the pasturelands of a town) (e:A luah ~ in Zorah, Eshtaol, Irshemesh/kumpi ~ khempeuh tungah a tung thute | the things that came upon all the kingdoms/Nisuahna leh nitumna ~ panin ka mite ka honkhia | I will save my people from the countries of the east and the west/hih ~ khempeuh’ pasiante’ lakah | among the gods of all these countries) (s:leitangte) (b:gam) (r:6.19.41/19.79.6/13.29.30/38.8.7/23.36.20) (q:draft)
gamteng = (t:n) (w:region/district/territory/whole land) (d:gam, land, with teng, all: the whole extent of a land; it follows the name of the region) (e:Benjamin ~ zong uh a/amaute in mualtung ~ luah uh a | they took possession of the hill country/Darias in Babylon ~ a uk hi | Darius ruled over the whole land of Babylon/amaute hong tun ciangin ~ beisak uh hi | when they came they laid the whole land waste) (b:gam) (r:9.9.4/27.9.1/7.1.19/7.6.5) (q:draft)
gamthuk = (t:n) (w:depths/deep realm) (d:gam, land, with thuk, deep; sihna gamthuk is the deep realm of death) (e:sihna ~ sungah a om khitna thu) (r:20.9.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamtuu = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mountain sheep/wild sheep) (d:gam wild country with tuu sheep; last in the list of clean wild animals) (e:leh ~ ahi hi) (r:5.14.5) (q:draft)
Gamul = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gamul) (d:priest in the time of David, head of the twenty-second priestly division) (r:13.24.17)
gamvai = (t:n) (w:breadth of the land) (d:gam, land, with vai, breadth; paired with gamdung, the length of the land) (e:gamdung ~ kantanin pai in) (r:1.13.17) (q:draft)
gamvak = (t:v) (w:hunt/go hunting) (d:gam, wild country, with vak, go about: go about the wilds after game) (e:tua munah mihingte ~ ding uh hi) (s:beng/bet) (r:23.7.24) (q:draft)
gamvengte = (t:n) (w:neighbours) (d:gam, land, with veng, neighbour, and the plural te: those who live in the land next to one) (e:na ~ uh niamkhiatin na mindaisak) (s:vengte/innvengte/pamte) (r:35.2.15) (q:draft)
gamzai = (t:n) (w:spacious land/broad land) (d:gam, land, with zai, wide: a broad and roomy land) (e:na piak ~ leihoih ah omin) (r:16.9.35) (q:draft)
gan = (t:n) (w:livestock/cattle/animal) (d:domestic animals kept by people, such as cattle, sheep and goats; gan-an is fodder and gan gam is land that is good for livestock) (e:a suksiat gamte in ~ gam hi/a gam in ~ gam ahi hi | the land was land for livestock/~ kaihkhop hun hi lo hi | it is not time to gather the livestock/~ khat go-in an bawl in | slaughter an animal and prepare a meal/a vengte’ ~ khat peuhpeuh kawm a | borrows any animal from his neighbour) (s:ganhing/innsa) (r:4.32.4/1.24.25/4.32.1/1.29.7/1.43.16/2.22.14) (q:draft)
gan = (t:v) (w:weave) (d:make cloth by crossing threads on a loom; puan gan is weave cloth) (e:a puan ding ~ tawm hi/a gial-in na ~ ding a | you shall weave it with a pattern/sam lom sagihte la-in siamin ~ hi | she took the seven locks of hair and wove them on the loom/saihadial puan a ~ minamte | the clans who weave linen cloth/a silh ding uh puan zong ~ lo uh | nor do they weave cloth to wear) (r:20.31.19/2.28.39/7.16.14/13.4.21/42.12.27) (q:draft)
ganbuk = (t:n) (w:stall/pen/fold) (d:gan, livestock, with buk, hut: shelter where animals are kept) (e:~ khempeuh a hawm khin zongin/na ~ pan uh-a keeltal hita leh | or a he-goat from your pens) (r:35.3.17/19.50.9) (q:draft)
ganbukah = (t:n) (w:in the stall/at the stable) (d:ganbuk, shelter for animals, with the place marker ah: in or at the stall) (e:Na ~ gambawngtal hong giak nuam ding/mi dim khinta ahih manin ~ tung uh a | as every place was full they came to a stable) (b:ganbuk) (r:18.39.9/42.2.7) (q:draft)
ganbukte = (t:n) (w:stalls/pens) (d:plural of ganbuk: shelters where livestock are kept) (e:adingin ~, leh tuubukte bawl hi) (b:ganbuk) (r:14.32.28) (q:draft)
gancing = (t:n) (w:shepherd/herdsman) (d:gan, livestock, with cing, guard: one who keeps animals) (e:~ pa in tuu le keelte a khen/Saul’ ~ makaipipa, Edom mi ahi hi | Saul’s chief herdsman, an Edomite) (s:tuucingpa) (r:40.25.32/9.21.7) (q:draft)
gancingpa = (t:n) (w:shepherd/herdsman) (d:gancing, keeper of animals, with pa marking a man) (e:~ in tuu leh keelte a tuam) (s:tuucingpa) (b:gancing) (r:40.25.32) (q:draft)
gancingte = (t:n) (w:herders/herdsmen) (d:plural of gancing, one who tends livestock) (e:namsau tawh ~ that khin uh hi/Abram’ ~ leh Lot’ ~ kitawng zel hi | Abram’s herders and Lot’s herders kept quarrelling/Gerar ~ leh Isaak’ ~ kitawng uh a | the herders of Gerar and Isaac’s herders quarrelled/nang’ ~ leh kei’ ~’ kikal-ah | between your herders and mine) (s:gankemte/tuucingte) (b:gancing) (r:18.1.15/1.13.7/1.26.20/1.13.8) (q:draft)
gangan = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after pai, walk, for the proud gait of a he-goat, beside kuahkuah for the rooster and lanlan for the king) (e:a kihihsak pai ~ keetal) (r:20.30.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
gangawh = (t:n) (w:animal sacrifice/slaughter of animals) (d:gan, animal, with gawh, slaughter; gangawh biakna is sacrifice, an offering of slaughtered animals) (e:~ biakna leh piakna na deih kei hi) (s:sagawh) (r:58.10.5/27.9.27) (q:draft)
gangawhna = (t:see) <gangawhna-in>
gangawhna-in = (t:n) (w:for slaughtering animals) (d:gan, animal, with gawh, slaughter, the noun suffix na and the marker in: in the slaughtering of animals for sacrifice) (e:~ a zat uh na khempeuh) (r:26.40.42) (q:draft)
ganhing = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:animal/beast/creature) (d:living creature other than a human being, tame or wild; mihing ganhing is people and animals) (e:nangma mai-ah ~ tawh ka kibang hi/~ a thatpa in a ~ mah-in loh ding | whoever kills an animal must replace it with an animal/gamlak ~ khempeuh a vakkhiat hun | the time when all the beasts of the forest roam/mihing leh ~ tacil khempeuh vatmai hi | he struck down all the firstborn of people and animals) (s:gan) (r:19.73.22/4.31.11/3.24.18/19.104.20/19.135.8)
ganhingin = (t:n) (w:animals) (d:ganhing, animal, with the ending in; in the phrase a mihing a ganhingin, people and animals alike) (e:a mihing a ~ a taimang ding uh hi/a mihing a ~ ka siasak ding hi | I will destroy both its people and its animals/A mihing a ~ kong pungsak ding a | I will multiply both people and animals/a mihing a ~ ka thahmangna ding thu | that I will kill both people and animals) (b:ganhing) (r:24.50.3/26.14.13/26.36.11/26.25.13) (q:draft)
ganhingnote = (t:n) (w:young animals/small creatures) (d:ganhing, animal, with no, young or small, and the plural te: the young of livestock, also small creatures) (e:a uk ding om lo ~ bangin/~ uh leh na leitang panun a piang gahte | the young of your livestock and the crops of your land) (s:gannote) (r:35.1.14/5.28.51) (q:draft)
ganhingte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:animals/livestock/beasts) (d:more than one animal; used both of livestock and of wild creatures) (e:na nek theih ding uh ~ ahi hi/a bokvak ~ leh a leeng vasate | creeping animals and flying birds/mual tul tampite’ tunga ~ keima-a’ ahi hi | the animals on a thousand hills are mine/a ~ uh gial tawh denglum a | he struck down their livestock with hail) (b:ganhing) (r:5.14.4/19.147.9/19.148.10/19.50.10/19.78.48) plural form of <ganhing>
ganhingteng = (t:n) (w:all the animals/the beasts) (d:ganhing, animal, with teng, all of them) (e:A nuai-a ~ le a hiang tunga/~ le vasate a uk dingin | to rule over all the animals and the birds) (b:ganhing) (r:27.4.14/27.2.38) (q:draft)
ganhon = (t:n) (w:flock/herd) (d:gan, livestock, with hon, group: a flock or herd of animals kept together) (e:gam lakah ~ bangin amaute lam lak hi/tuuhon leh ~ leh puanbukte nei a | he had flocks and herds and tents/Laban’ ~ a omlai teng an a vak hi | he fed the rest of Laban’s flock/zanglei ah ~ tampi nei ahih manin | because he had much livestock in the plain) (r:19.78.52/14.17.11/1.13.5/1.30.36/14.26.10)
ganhonte = (t:n) (w:flocks/herds) (d:plural of ganhon: flocks or herds of livestock) (e:kuam sunga om ~ tungah/tuuhonte leh ~ tampi koih hi | he acquired many flocks and herds/i ~’ tacilte leh i tuuhonte’ tacilte | the firstborn of our herds and of our flocks/ni thum paina gamlapi-ah tua ~ a paipih hi | he took those flocks a three-day journey away) (b:ganhon) (r:13.27.29/14.32.29/16.10.36/1.30.36)
ganin = (t:v) (w:weave/plait) (d:form of gan, weave, with the linking suffix in, weaving and then going on to the next action) (e:ling tawh lukhu ~ ama lu tangah/siamkhau tawh ~ ciampek tawh khen bikbek lecin | if you weave them with the loom thread and fasten them tight with the pin) (b:gan) (r:43.19.2/7.16.13) (q:draft)
gankemte = (t:n) (w:keepers of livestock/herdsmen) (d:gan, livestock, with kem, keep, and the plural te: people who look after livestock) (e:amaute in ~ ahih manin tuucing ahi/kipan tu hun dongin ~ ka hi uh hi | we have been keepers of livestock until now/na nasem kote pen ~ ka hi uh hi | we your servants are keepers of livestock) (s:gancingte) (r:1.46.32/1.46.34/1.47.3) (q:draft)
gankhahna = (t:n) (w:pasture) (d:gan, livestock, with khah, let loose, and the noun suffix na: the place where animals are let out to graze) (e:ama ~ sunga om a tuute ihi hi/Mizawngte in keima ~ sungah an ne ding uh | the poor will feed in my pasture/~ mun zaina-ah na ganhingte un lopa ne ding | your animals will eat grass in broad pastures) (s:lono/lonona/khahna) (r:19.100.3/23.30.23/23.14.30) (q:draft)
gankhawite = (t:n) (w:livestock/flocks) (d:gan, animal, with khawi, keep or rear, and the plural te: animals that are kept) (e:a ~ uh keek tawh denglum hi) (s:innsate) (r:19.78.48) (q:draft)
gankhawk = (t:n) (w:fold/pen/enclosure) (d:gan livestock with khawk, a marked-off section: place where a flock is gathered, named beside tuubuk sheep pen; the NIV has pasture) (e:~ sunga tuuhon kaihkhop bangin) (r:33.2.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
ganmul = (t:n) (w:wool/fleece) (d:gan, livestock, with mul, hair: the wool of sheep; ganmul mette are the shearers) (e:~ mette na neihna ka za hi/ka ~ mette’ adingin ka gawh ka sate | the meat I have slaughtered for my shearers) (s:tuumul/samul) (r:9.25.7/9.25.11) (q:draft)
gannim = (t:see) <En-gannim>
ganno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young animal/lamb/kid/calf) (d:gan, animal, with no, young: the young of sheep, goats or cattle) (e:~ khat zong kinusia lo ding hi/amaute in ~ khat ciat la ding uh hi | each of them shall take a lamb/hih ~ ka puak a | I sent this young goat/~ khat’ adingin innkuan a tawm luat leh | if the household is too small for one lamb) (b:gan) (r:2.10.26/2.12.4/2.12.3/1.38.23) (q:draft)
gannote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young animals/animals) (d:plural of ganno, the young of sheep, goats or cattle; in Proverbs 12:10 a person's own animals in general) (e:Midikte in a ~ hoihtak don a/migilote in a ~ bawlsia hi | the wicked mistreat their animals/bawngtalte leh ~, leh tuunote | the bulls and the young animals and the lambs/sa gilote in ~ a phialgawp bangin | as fierce beasts tear at the young animals) (s:ganhingnote) (b:ganno) (r:20.12.10/9.15.9/44.20.29) (q:draft)
ganpite = (t:n) (w:beasts/large animals) (d:gan livestock with pi, large, and plural te; named after ganhon, the herds, for the other animals a people keeps) (e:leh na ~ in a dawn dingin) (b:gan) (r:12.3.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
gantawm = (t:v) (w:weave) (d:gan, weave, with tawm, for oneself: weave one's own cloth) (e:a puan ding ~ hi) (r:20.31.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
gante = (t:n) (w:weavers) (d:gan, weave, with the plural te: those who weave) (e:patpuan a ~ lungkham ding uh hi) (s:siamgante) (b:gan) (r:23.19.9/2.35.35) (q:draft)
gapgap = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after ki-en, look at each other, for people staring at one another in alarm) (e:khat leh khat a ki-en ~ uh a) (r:24.36.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
