gatna = (t:n) (w:weaving) (d:gat, form of gan weave, with the noun suffix na; gatna mun is the place where weaving is done) (e:a kizang puante a ~ mun) (s:siamgat) (b:gat) (r:12.23.7) (q:draft)
gaw = (t:see) <gaw-in>
gaw-in = (t:adj) (w:shrivelled/withered) (d:gaw with the linking suffix in, after keu, dry: dried up and shrunken, said of skin) (e:sing bangin keu ~, a guh guakin) (r:25.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawh = (t:v) (w:slaughter/kill) (d:kill an animal for food or sacrifice; form of go used before ding, hun and similar words) (e:~ hun om a, khawi hun om hi/gan gote tuu ~ ding bangin | like sheep to be slaughtered by the butchers/a gannote uh a ~ ding hun | the time for them to slaughter their animals/ka ~ ka sate la-in | taking the meat I have slaughtered/~ dinga kikoih tuu bangin kaikhia in | drag them off like sheep set apart for slaughter) (r:21.3.3/38.11.4/19.44.22/2.12.6/9.25.11/24.12.3) (q:draft)
gawhna = (t:n) (w:slaughtering/slaughter/killing) (d:gawh, slaughter, with the noun suffix na: the killing of an animal for food or sacrifice; a gawhna mun is the place where it is slaughtered) (e:meihal biakna a ~ mun uhah/bawngtalte leh tuute ~, sa nekna | slaughtering of cattle and sheep, eating of meat/ganhingte ~-a kizang ahi hi | they are used for slaughtering the animals) (b:gawh) (r:3.7.2/23.22.13/26.40.41) (q:draft)
gawhnate = (t:n) (w:sacrifices/slaughterings) (d:gawh, slaughter, with the noun suffix na and the plural te; gan gawhnate is animal sacrifices) (e:biakna tau tunga gan ~ le biakna) (b:gawhna) (r:41.12.33) (q:draft)
gawhsak = (t:v) (w:slaughter for/kill for) (d:gawh, slaughter, with sak, here doing it for someone: kill an animal to feed a guest) (e:ama ading bawngno thau na ~ hi/ama kianga a tung mipa adingin ~ hi | he slaughtered it for the man who had come to him) (b:gawh) (r:42.15.30/10.12.4) (q:draft)
gawi = (t:v) (w:grind/gnash/gnaw) (d:crush between stones or between the teeth; an gawi grind grain, ha gawi gnash the teeth) (e:Stefen tungah a ha a ~ uh hi/An ~ khawm numei nih | two women grinding grain together/suangte la in la, an ~ in | take the stones and grind grain/a leii uh a ~ uh hi | they gnawed their tongues/thong sung angawina-ah an ~ hi | he ground grain in the prison mill) (r:44.7.54/42.17.35/23.47.2/66.16.10/7.16.21) (q:draft)
gawigawi = (t:see) <gawigawi-a>
gawigawi-a = (t:v) (w:gnashing/grinding) (d:doubled form of gawi, gnash, with the linking a: ha gawigawi is keep gnashing the teeth) (e:a ha ~ tuimang hi) (r:19.112.10) (q:draft)
gawigawi-in = (t:v) (w:gnashing/grinding) (d:doubled form of gawi, gnash, with the linking suffix in: ha gawigawi is keep gnashing the teeth) (e:a ha ~ a tuimang hi) (r:19.112.10) (q:draft)
gawigawp = (t:v) (w:thresh/crush) (d:gawi, grind, with gawp, severely: grind down utterly) (e:Gilead gammite ~ uh hi) (s:sugawp) (b:gawi) (r:30.1.3) (q:draft)
gawina = (t:n) (w:grinding/gnashing) (d:gawi, grind or gnash, with the noun suffix na: an gawina suang is a millstone, and ha gawina is gnashing of teeth) (e:Kahna leh ha ~ a om ding hi/An ~ suangte la in la | take the millstones/an ~ suangpeek tungnung | an upper millstone/thong sung an ~-ah an a gawi hi | he ground grain at the mill in the prison/mi zawngte na ~ uh | your grinding of the poor) (b:gawi) (r:40.13.42/23.47.2/7.9.53/7.16.21/23.3.15) (q:draft)
gawisan = (t:v) (w:gnash/grind) (d:with ha, tooth: grind the teeth at someone in anger) (e:a ha uh kei hong ~ uh hi/Migilo in thumanpa sawm a, a ha ~ hi | the wicked plots against the righteous and gnashes his teeth at him/heh uh a, a ha uh ~ uh hi | they were furious and gnashed their teeth at him) (b:gawi) (r:19.35.16/19.37.12/44.7.54) (q:draft)
gawisanin = (t:v) (w:gnashing at) (d:gawisan, gnash the teeth at someone, with the linking suffix in) (e:a ha hong ~ hong heh et hi) (b:gawisan) (r:18.16.9) (q:draft)
gawivui = (t:v) (w:grind to powder/crush to dust/pulverize) (d:gawi, grind, with vui, dust: grind something until it is powder) (e:~-in tui tungah theh a/a kisung milimte sukhamin ~ a | he broke the cast idols and ground them to powder/na khempeuh sat nen a, a ~ bangin | as it breaks everything and grinds it to powder) (s:satvui/suvui) (r:2.32.20/14.34.4/27.2.40) (q:draft)
gawizan = (t:v) (w:crush/grind/thresh/trample) (d:crush or tread something until it is broken small, as grain is threshed or grapes are trodden) (e:leivui bangin a neel dongin ka ~ hi/mual neute pen ansi bangin na ~ ding uh | you will crush the hills like chaff/angawina suang tawh ~ bangin | as one threshes with a grinding stone) (r:5.9.21/23.41.15/30.1.3) (q:draft)
gawizansak = (t:v) (w:trample/crush) (d:gawizan, crush or tread, with the causative sak) (e:leenggah gawizan bangin a hong ~ hi) (b:gawizan) (r:25.1.15) (q:draft)
gawl = (t:n) (w:neck/throat) (d:the neck or throat; gawl meek is to choke or strangle) (e:a ~ meekin/Na galte’ ~ na meek ding a | you will grip the neck of your enemies/~ sungah a tum suk hit-hit thei | that goes smoothly down the throat/~ meek kithat sa ahi zongin | or the meat of strangled animals) (s:ngawng/gawlgui) (r:40.18.28/20.23.31/1.49.8/44.15.20) (q:draft)
gawl = (t:n) (w:fence/wall) (d:a fence or wall round a field or yard; gawl sung is the space inside it, a court) (e:a ~ ka susia ding a/a kiliing ~ tawh a kibang mi khat | a man who is like a tottering fence/pua lamah a om ~ sung teh kei in | do not measure the court that is outside) (s:daai/daigawl) (r:23.5.5/19.62.3/66.11.2) (q:draft)
gawlgui = (t:n) (w:throat) (d:the throat, the passage inside the neck for breath, voice and food) (e:ka ~ keu ta hi/Amau ~ un a kihongsa hankhuk ahi uh hi | their throats are open graves/amau ~ in a kihongsa hankhuk tawh kibang hi | their throat is like an open grave) (s:gawl) (r:19.69.3/45.3.13/19.5.9) (q:draft)
gawlin = (t:n) (w:with a fence/with a hedge) (d:gawl, fence, with the marker in, by means of: gawlin um is enclose with a fence) (e:~ a um khit ciangin/leenggah kungte suan a, ~ uum a | he planted vines and enclosed them with a fence) (b:gawl) (r:40.21.33/41.12.1) (q:draft)
gawlin = (t:n) (w:by the throat/by the neck) (d:gawl, throat or neck, with the marker in: a gawlin man is seize him by the throat) (e:Tua pa a ~ manin/Pasian in ka ~ hong manin | God seized me by the neck) (b:gawl) (r:40.18.28/18.16.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawlmek = (t:v) (w:strangle/choke) (d:gawl, throat, with mek, squeeze; gawlmek a kigo sa is the meat of a strangled animal) (e:~ a kigo sate a nek loh) (r:44.21.25) (q:draft)
gawlzawhna = (t:n) (w:victory) (d:apparently another spelling of gualzawhna, victory) (e:~ na piakna sungah amah naknuam mahmah) (s:gualzawhna/galzawhna) (a:guallelhna) (r:19.21.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawm = (t:v) (w:join/combine/blend/add together) (d:put things together into one: join forces, blend ingredients, add up a number; gawm khawm is join together) (e:Pasian in a ~ khawmsate mite in/a thahatna uh ~ hi | they joined their forces/nilh dingin hihte na ~ ding hi | you shall blend these for anointing/paknamtui bawlte’ ~ bangin | as the perfumers blend it/galdo mite a phazah a ~ pia hi | he gave the total number of the fighting men/sehnga suah sehkhat ~ behin | adding a fifth to it) (a:khen) (r:40.19.6/2.30.25/1.14.3/2.37.29/10.24.9/3.5.16) (q:draft)
gawmin = (t:v) (w:joining/combining/putting together) (d:gawm, join or combine, with the linking ending in; often rendered together or all together) (e:amaute neihsa khempeuh ~ a zangkhawm uh hi/amau galkapte ~ Israel mite tawh a kido dingin | joining their armies to fight against Israel/lo khat leh khat, ~ a la thuah tawntung | always adding field to field/a om na khempeuh ~ Khazih uk sak ding | to bring all things together under the rule of Christ) (a:khenin) (b:gawm) (r:44.2.44/6.11.5/23.5.8/49.1.10) (q:draft)
gawmkik = (t:v) (w:join again/reunite) (d:gawm, join, with kik, again or back: make into one again) (e:amaute minam khatin ka ~ ding hi) (b:gawm) (r:26.37.22) (q:draft)
gawmsa = (t:adj) (w:joined/joined together) (d:gawm, join, with sa, already done: what has been joined) (e:Pasian in a ~ mite/Pasian’ ~ mite, kuamah in khen kei ta hen | let no one separate those whom God has joined) (b:gawm) (r:40.19.6/41.10.9) (q:draft)
gawng = (t:adj) (w:lean/thin/gaunt) (d:thin from lack of flesh, said of animals and of a wasted body) (e:a gulhgawng bawngpi ~ sagihte/A ~ a gulhgawng bawngpite in | the lean, ugly cows/a gulhgawng a ~ bawngpi dang sagih | seven other cows, ugly and lean) (a:thau) (r:1.41.4/1.41.20/1.41.3) (q:draft)
gawngin = (t:adj) (w:lean/wasted) (d:gawng, thin and wasted, with the linking suffix in) (e:~ na guhguak bekun na om) (b:gawng) (r:20.5.11) (q:draft)
gawngte = (t:adj) (w:lean/thin) (d:gawng, lean, with the plural te: the lean ones, as in tuu gawngte, lean sheep) (e:tuu thaute leh tuu ~ kong khen ding hi) (a:thaute) (b:gawng) (r:26.34.20) (q:draft)
gawp = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done severely or completely, to the point of ruin) (e:Midian mite gimsak ~ in la/Izipt mite leh Kanaan mite vul ~ uh hi | Egypt and Canaan wasted away/amaute tukin kitamzan ~ ding uh hi | they will fall and be shattered/leitung panin nuaimang ~ in | wipe them out from the earth/Mual leh tausangte zong kisia ~ ding a | hill and watchtower too will be utterly ruined) (r:4.25.17/1.47.13/23.8.15/25.3.66/23.32.14) (q:draft)
gawpgawp = (t:part) (w:severely/harshly) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done severely and again and again; hih gawpgawp is to treat harshly, to oppress) (e:amaute hih ~ uh hi/Gamdang mite in hih ~ nawn lo ding uh | foreign peoples will no longer plunder them/a samatsa uh a bal ~ ngia hon | a pack of wolves tearing their prey/nakpi takin a hong kihawl ~ hi | we are driven very hard) (b:gawp) (r:16.9.27/26.34.28/26.22.27/25.5.5) (q:draft)
gawpgawpna = (t:n) (w:harshness/ruthlessness/rigour) (d:severe treatment; hih gawpgawpna tawh uk means rule over someone ruthlessly) (e:hih ~ tawh amah uk lo ding hi/hih ~ tawh na ki-uk kei ding uh hi | you must not rule over one another ruthlessly) (b:gawpgawp) (r:3.25.53/3.25.43/3.25.46) (q:draft)
gawpgawpnate = (t:n) (w:harsh acts/severities) (d:gawpgawp, severely and again and again, with the noun suffix na and the plural te; tawn’ gawpgawpnate is harsh threats) (e:tawn’ ~ zang nawn kei un) (b:gawpgawpna) (r:49.6.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawpin = (t:part) (w:utterly/severely) (d:gawp, severely, with the linking suffix in: placed after a verb to show that the action is done violently, thoroughly or to destruction) (e:Nineveh khuapi susia ~/Kei hong kinengcip ~ ka thahatna beimang khin a | I am utterly crushed and my strength is gone/zo ~ susia mang ding uh hi | they will utterly defeat and destroy them/Kulh kongpite cim ~ lei in vukcip a | the gates have collapsed and the earth has covered them) (b:gawp) (r:36.2.13/33.5.9/19.38.8/25.2.9) (q:draft)
gawpmang = (t:part) (w:utterly/completely) (d:placed after a verb: gawp, severely, with mang, away or to nothing, as in susia gawpmang destroy utterly) (e:khempeuh ka susia ~ a) (r:18.29.17) (q:draft)
gawpna = (t:part) (d:gawp, severely, with the noun suffix na: placed after a verb, it makes a noun for an action done severely or thoroughly, as siat gawpna, utter ruin, and tuatcil gawpna, trampling) (e:ka huang sung na tuatcil ~ uh/a siat ~ hangin lamdang sa-in | astonished at its utter ruin/buaina leh tuatcil ~ leh kitawhzauna | tumult and trampling and terror/kihihsakna tawh a hih ~ thei na hih manin | because you knew how arrogantly they treated them) (b:gawp) (r:23.1.12/24.49.17/23.22.5/16.9.10) (q:draft)
gawpnate = (t:part) (d:gawpna with plural te, placed after a verb: makes a plural noun for the results of a severe action; satnim gawpnate are bruises from heavy blows) (e:satnim ~ leh meimapite) (b:gawpna) (r:23.1.6) (q:draft)
gawppa = (t:part) (d:the particle gawp, severely, with pa, the man who: after a verb, the one who does it thoroughly; a sut gawppa is the plunderer) (e:Kua in a sut ~ tungah Jakob pia/eite hong vat ~ in amah hi lo hi | he is not the one who struck us/kumpi gamte a lok ~ | the one who shook kingdoms/Rahab a satzan ~ | the one who cut Rahab to pieces) (b:gawp) (r:23.42.24/23.14.16/9.6.9/23.51.9) (q:draft)
gawpsa = (t:see) <gawpsa-in>
gawpsa-in = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: gawp, severely, with sa, already done, and the linking suffix in: having done the action severely, as in kikui gawpsa-in having gashed themselves) (e:uh a kikui ~ Topa’ biakinn-ah) (r:24.41.5) (q:draft)
gawpsak = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: gawp, severely or utterly, with the causative sak, so that the action is done or caused to be done to the point of ruin, as in cim gawpsak demolish) (e:khuapi kulhte a cim ~ thei/amau leh amau kisat ~ hi | he made them cut one another down/biakna Biakinnpi a zan ~ hi | he has laid the temple of worship in ruins/ko a hong mudahte na zahhuai ~ khin hi | you have put those who hate us to utter shame) (b:gawp) (r:47.10.4/7.7.22/25.2.6/19.44.7) (q:draft)
gawpsakin = (t:part) (d:gawpsak, placed after a verb for an action done or caused severely, with the linking suffix in) (e:na nawi hong kinuai ~) (b:gawpsak) (r:26.23.21) (q:draft)
gawpsate = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: gawp, utterly, with sa, already done, and the plural te: the ones that have been utterly so, as in a sia gawpsate the things that are ruined) (e:A sia ~ zong, ka bawl kik) (r:44.15.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawpta = (t:part) (d:gawp, placed after a verb for an action done severely or completely, with ta, now or already, as in kitan gawpta is now shattered) (e:Merodak pasian kitan ~ hi) (b:gawp) (r:24.50.2) (q:draft)
gawpte = (t:part) (d:gawp, which shows an action done severely, with the plural te: those who do, or who suffer, the action thoroughly, as in luh gawpte, plunderers) (e:tuute a thehthang ~ ahi uh hi/eite hong luh ~’ thuak ding ahi hi | it is the lot of those who plunder us/a luh ~’ tungah Israel pia | gave Israel over to the plunderers/a thumang lo, a phengtat ~ hi lo ding | they are not to be disobedient or wild) (b:gawp) (r:42.11.23/23.42.24/23.17.14/56.1.6) (q:draft)
gawpzo = (t:part) (d:gawp, placed after a verb for an action done severely or completely, with zo, be able, as in thalnial gawpzo be able to demolish) (e:a man lote ka thalnial ~ uh) (b:gawp) (r:47.10.5) (q:draft)
gawsem = (t:n) (w:harp) (d:a musical instrument, rendered harp in Revelation, where tamngai is the pipe; gawsem tumte is those who play it; in everyday use perhaps the gourd mouth organ, a wind instrument) (e:~ tumte, la siamte, tamngai tumte/~ tumte’ ~ tum aw tawh kibang hi | it was like the sound of harpists playing their harps/~ aw ahi zongin, tamngai aw ahi zongin | whether the sound of the harp or of the pipe) (r:66.18.22/66.14.2/46.14.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawsemte = (t:n) (w:harps/pipes) (d:plural of gawsem, a musical instrument; used for the harps of Revelation and for the pipes of Daniel 3:5) (e:Pasian’ ~ tawi-in tua limlang tuipi kiangah/harp lasakna gingte, ~ leh tum theih a tuamtuamte | the sound of harps, pipes and all kinds of instruments) (b:gawsem) (r:66.15.2/27.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawt = (t:v) (w:afflict/oppress/mistreat/punish) (d:lay a heavy hand on someone: treat harshly, afflict or punish; gawt bawl is to mistreat a person) (e:Sarai in amah ~ bawl a/Ashdod khuamite nakpi takin ~ a | he afflicted the people of Ashdod severely/eite leh i pasian Dagon hong ~ hi | he afflicts us and our god Dagon/Josef innkuante in amaute ~ semsem a | the house of Joseph pressed them harder and harder/amaute nak ~ mahmah hi | he afflicted them very heavily) (s:gimsak/bawlsia/nengniam) (r:1.16.6/9.5.6/9.5.7/7.1.35/9.5.11) (q:draft)
gawtbawl = (t:v) (w:mistreat/treat harshly) (d:gawt, afflict, with bawl, do: treat someone harshly) (e:Ka ute in kei hong ~ uh a) (s:gimbawl/bawlsia) (b:gawt) (r:22.1.6) (q:draft)
gawtin = (t:v) (w:afflicting/punishing) (d:gawt, afflict, with the linking suffix in) (e:kei zong note hong ~) (s:gimsakin) (b:gawt) (r:3.26.24) (q:draft)
gawtna = (t:n) (w:punishment/affliction) (d:gawt afflict with the noun suffix na: the heavy hand laid on someone) (e:note hong ~ thu na thei ding/amah in hong ~ hong zangsak kha ding hi | perhaps he will lighten his hand on you) (s:gimpiakna/daantatna) (b:gawt) (r:9.6.3/9.6.5) (q:draft)
Gaza = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gaza) (d:Philistine city on the coast in the south-west of Canaan, one of the five chief cities of the Philistines) (r:7.1.18/30.1.7)
Gazez = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gazez) (d:name of two men in the family of Caleb: a son of Caleb by his concubine Ephah, and a son of Haran) (r:13.2.46)
Gazzam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gazzam) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:16.7.51)
Gazzan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gazzam) (d:spelling of Gazzam in Ezra 2:48, ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.48)
Ge = (t:see) <Ge-uel>
Ge-uel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Geuel) (d:son of Maki, the man of the tribe of Gad sent by Moses to explore Canaan) (e:Makhi’ tapa ~ ahi hi) (r:4.13.15) (q:draft)
Geba = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Geba) (d:town of the tribe of Benjamin north of Jerusalem, given to the Levites) (e:~ khua-ah zan khat giak uh hi) (r:23.10.29/16.11.31) (q:draft)
Gebal = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gebal/Byblos) (d:Phoenician port city north of Sidon, called Byblos in the NIV, known for its builders and shipwrights) (r:6.13.5/11.5.18)
Gebeah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gibeah) (d:spelling of Gibeah in 1 Samuel 14:2, the town of Saul in Benjamin) (r:9.14.2)
geber = (t:see) <Ezion-geber>
Geber = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Geber) (d:son of Uri, governor of King Solomon in the land of Gilead) (e:Uri’ tapa ~ ahi hi) (r:11.4.19) (q:draft)
Gebim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gebim) (d:place north of Jerusalem whose people fled before the Assyrian advance in Isaiah 10) (r:23.10.31)
Gedaliah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gedaliah) (d:name of several men, chiefly the son of Ahikam whom Nebuchadnezzar made governor of Judah and whom Ishmael killed at Mizpah) (r:12.25.22/24.41.3)
Gedeliah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gedaliah) (d:spelling of Gedaliah in Jeremiah 39:14, the son of Ahikam to whose care Jeremiah was given) (r:24.39.14)
Geder = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Geder) (d:Canaanite royal town whose king was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.12.13)
Gederah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gederah) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.36/13.4.23)
Gederoh = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gederoth) (d:spelling of Gederoth in 2 Chronicles 28:18, a town in the foothills of Judah taken by the Philistines) (r:14.28.18)
Gederoth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gederoth) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah, taken by the Philistines in the time of King Ahaz) (e:~, Bethdagon, Na-amah, leh Makkedah) (r:6.15.41/14.28.18) (q:draft)
Gederothaim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gederothaim) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah, listed next to Gederah) (r:6.15.36)
gedi = (t:see) <En-gedi>
Gedor = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gedor) (d:name of a town in the hill country of Judah and of several men, among them a Benjamite son of Jeiel) (r:6.15.58)
geel = (t:v) (w:plan/devise/design) (d:think out beforehand what is to be done or made) (e:Mihing in thu ~ a/Mite in bangbang a ~ zongin | whatever people may plan/ka ~ khin a, ka sem ding hi | I have planned it and I will do it/a khut siam, a ~ siam | skilled with his hands, skilled in design) (s:ngim) (r:20.16.9/23.46.11/20.16.1/2.38.23) (q:draft)
geelgeel = (t:v) (w:devise/plot/ponder/meditate) (d:doubled form of geel, plan: keep planning or turning something over in the mind) (e:lung sung uh ah thusia ~ uh a/lung ka ~ a, ka gim mahmah hi | I pondered, and I grew very weary/a sia thei pen ding a ~ uh hi | they keep plotting the worst that can be/Siatna bekbek na ~ uh a | you keep plotting nothing but evil) (s:gelgel/ngaihsunsun/lungngaingai) (r:19.140.2/19.77.3/19.41.7/23.59.7) (q:draft)
geelgeelin = (t:v) (w:pondering/meditating) (d:form of geelgeel with the linking suffix in; lung geelgeelin is turning something over in the heart) (e:lung ~ thu ka kan ciangin) (b:geelgeel) (r:19.77.6) (q:draft)
geelgeelna = (t:n) (w:careful planning/planning) (d:geelgeel, keep planning, with the noun suffix na) (e:Limtakin ngaihsunin ~ pen hauhna lampi) (b:geelgeel) (r:20.21.5) (q:draft)
geelgeelte = (t:n) (w:plotters/those who devise) (d:geelgeel keep planning with plural te: the people who keep plotting something) (e:lumin gitlohna a ~ in gimna ngah) (s:sawmsimte/geelte) (b:geelgeel) (r:33.2.1) (q:draft)
geelin = (t:v) (w:planning/designing/devising) (d:geel, plan, with the linking suffix -in: planning something and then doing it) (e:Pasian in ~ a lam/siat nading ~ kithukhat uh hi | plotting destruction, they are of one mind/Thu ~ ka semkhia a | I make plans and carry them out) (b:geel) (r:58.11.10/19.83.5/20.8.14) (q:draft)
geelkholh = (t:v) (w:plan beforehand/prepare in advance) (d:geel, plan, with kholh, beforehand) (e:Topa in ngapi khat a ~ sa) (r:32.1.17) (q:draft)
geelkholhsa = (t:v) (w:planned beforehand/prepared in advance/prescribed) (d:geelkholh, plan ahead, with sa marking a completed action) (e:Tanglai pek panin ka ~ hi a/David in a ~ bangin Topa a phat dingin | to praise the Lord as David had prescribed/Topa in ngapi khat a ~ hi a | the Lord had prepared a great fish) (b:geelkholh) (r:12.19.25/15.3.10/32.1.17) (q:draft)
geelna = (t:n) (w:plan/purpose/counsel/design) (d:geel, plan, with the noun suffix na: what someone has planned or intends to do; biakinn geelna is the design of the temple) (e:hih ~ pen kumpipa leh/mite’ ~ khaktan hi | he thwarts the plans of the peoples/ka ~ teng maimang a | all my plans have come to nothing/a ~ banga a sap mite | those he has called according to his purpose) (s:ngimna/vaihawmna/gelna) (b:geel) (r:14.30.4/19.33.10/18.17.11/45.8.28) (q:draft)
geelnasa = (t:n) (w:purpose/plan already made) (d:geelna, plan, with sa, already done: what has been planned) (e:ama ~ a kheel ngei het lo) (s:ngaihsutsa) (b:geelna) (r:58.6.17) (q:draft)
geelnate = (t:n) (w:plans/purposes) (d:plural of geelna: things that have been planned) (e:Na ~ khempeuh Topa ap in/amau’ ~ ka siasak ding hi | I will bring their plans to nothing/nangma' ~ kei hong lak in | show me your plans) (s:ngimnate/vaihawmnate/geelsate) (b:geelna) (r:20.16.3/23.19.3/2.33.13) (q:draft)
geelpa = (t:n) (w:planner/one who planned) (d:geel, plan, with pa marking a man: the one who planned it) (e:a na ~ na don kei hi) (s:vaihawmpa) (b:geel) (r:23.22.11) (q:draft)
geelsa = (t:adj) (w:planned/purposed/designed) (d:geel plan with sa already done; also what has been planned, a plan) (e:Ka ~ bangin piang ding a/Nasep ding khempeuh ~ bangin sep dingin | to do all the work according to the plan/Vanglian Pasian’ ~ teng | all that Almighty God has planned/ama ~ bangin hong sem a | he acted according to what he had purposed) (s:vaihawmsa) (b:geel) (r:23.14.24/13.28.19/18.27.11/49.1.9) (q:draft)
geelsate = (t:n) (w:plans/purposes/things planned) (d:geelsa planned with plural te: what someone has planned or decreed) (e:a ~ amah in tungsak ding hi) (s:geelnate) (b:geelsa) (r:18.23.14) (q:draft)
geelsiam = (t:adj) (w:skilled in design) (d:geel design with siam skilled; geelsiam nasep is the work of a designer or skilled craftsman) (e:khutsiam nasep, ~ nasep) (r:2.35.35) (q:draft)
geelsim = (t:v) (w:plan in secret) (d:geel, plan, with sim, secretly; a geelsim thute is the things he planned in secret) (e:Pasian in a ~ thute a kisep) (r:49.3.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
geeltawm = (t:v) (w:make up/devise oneself) (d:geel, plan, with tawm, on one's own: think something up out of one's own mind) (e:a lungsim uhah a ~ uh thu) (s:geltawm/phuahtawm) (r:24.23.16) (q:draft)
geelte = (t:n) (w:those who plan/plotters) (d:geel, plan, with plural te: those who plan something; siat nading a geelte, those who planned the destruction) (e:siat nading a ~ a su dingin) (s:geelgeelte/sawmsimte) (b:geel) (r:17.9.2) (q:draft)
geelte = (t:n) (w:plans/things planned) (d:geel, plan, with plural te: what someone has planned) (e:ama ip thusim a ~ hong semkhia ding hi) (s:geelnate/geelsate) (b:geel) (r:66.10.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
geeltheih = (t:v) (w:be able to plan/be able to direct) (d:geel, plan, with theih, be able) (e:ama kalsuanna ding ama ~ hi lo) (b:geel) (r:24.10.23) (q:draft)
gega = (t:adv) (w:staring/fixedly) (d:placed after en, look, or sal: with a fixed wide-open stare; mit san gega is eyes glaring red) (e:sal ~-in kei hong en uh hi/a etna mun mah en denin Hazael sal ~ hi | he kept his eyes fixed and stared at Hazael/Nangmah hong mu mite in nang hong en ~-in | those who see you stare at you/kuate a mit san ~ hiam | who has bloodshot eyes/lei ka en suk ~ lel hi | I could only stare down at the ground) (r:19.22.17/12.8.11/23.14.16/20.23.29/27.10.15) (q:draft)
gegupi = (t:see) <gegupi-in>
gegupi-in = (t:adv) (w:full well/clearly) (d:after thei, know: knowing full well; the meaning rests on one verse) (e:ci-in a thei ~ ama tungah) (r:9.24.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
geh = (t:n) (w:eunuch) (d:a castrated man; geh bang, like a eunuch) (e:pan ~ bang mi a om hi/Vantung Gam hangah ~ bang a suak zong om hi | there are also those who become like eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven) (r:40.19.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Geharashim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ge Harashim) (d:valley and settlement of craftsmen in Judah, founded by Joab son of Seraiah and later lived in by Benjamites; the name means valley of craftsmen) (r:13.4.14/16.11.35)
Gehazi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gehazi) (d:servant of the prophet Elisha, struck with leprosy for his greed) (r:12.4.12/12.8.4)
gehsa = (t:n) (w:eunuch) (d:geh, eunuch, with sa, already: one who is already a eunuch, here from birth) (e:a pianpihin ~ bang om a) (b:geh) (r:40.19.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
