genzaw = (t:v) (w:speak rather/speak instead/teach rather) (d:gen, speak, with zaw, rather: speak in this way and not in the other; follows a clause with gen loin, not speaking as) (e:aana neite bangin thu a ~ hi/aana nei mite bangin thu a ~ hi | he spoke rather as those who have authority) (s:pauzaw/cizaw) (b:gen) (r:40.7.29/41.1.22) (q:draft)
genzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to tell/express fully/tell in full) (d:gen, tell, with zawh, be able to finish; nearly always with loh, not: genzawh loh and genzawh lohin mean beyond telling, more than can be told or counted) (e:~ lohin a lamdang na tampi/kama ~ loh zah dongin | to a degree the mouth cannot tell/kuama ~ ding hi lo hi | no one is able to tell it all/~ loh lungsim zaina pia a | he gave a breadth of mind beyond telling) (s:gentheih) (r:18.5.9/11.4.29/60.1.8/21.1.8) (q:draft)
genzo = (t:v) (w:have said/have spoken/have told) (d:gen, tell, with zo, marking the act as carried through: has said, has told) (e:Topa in thu a ~ hi/a thuman hong ~ hi | he has told you the truth/na gamtatna ding zia kong ~ hi | I have told you the way you should walk/upna hang hi, ci-in i ~ hi | we have said that it is by faith) (s:genkhin/cizo) (b:gen) (r:24.13.15/43.5.33/20.4.11/45.3.28) (q:draft)
Gera = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gera) (d:name of several men of Benjamin, among them a son of Bela and the father of Ehud the judge) (e:~, Shefufan, leh Huram, ahi uh hi) (r:13.8.5/1.46.21) (q:draft)
