Gershonte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Gershonites) (d:Levite clan descended from Gershon, in charge of the curtains and coverings of the tabernacle) (b:Gershon) (r:4.3.25/4.4.24)
Geshan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Geshan) (d:son of Jahdai in the family of Caleb, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.47)
Geshem = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Geshem) (d:the Arab who with Sanballat and Tobiah opposed Nehemiah when he rebuilt the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.6.1/16.6.2)
Geshur = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Geshur) (d:small Aramean kingdom east of the Sea of Galilee, where Absalom fled; also a people living in the south near the Philistines) (r:10.14.23/6.13.2)
Gether = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gether) (d:son of Aram and grandson of Shem) (r:1.10.23)
Gethsemane = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gethsemane) (d:place at the foot of the Mount of Olives where Jesus prayed on the night of his arrest) (r:41.14.32/40.26.36)
Geuel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Geuel) (d:son of Maki, the man of the tribe of Gad sent by Moses to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.4)
Gezer = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gezer) (d:Canaanite city on the western edge of the hill country of Ephraim, given to the Levites and later rebuilt by Solomon) (r:6.10.33/11.9.17)
gi = (t:n) (w:boundary/border) (d:the boundary of a piece of land; found in gi-suang, a boundary stone or landmark, and in gamgi, the border of a land) (e:Taanglai ~-suang khin kei in la/Na pu na pate’ phuhsa ~-suang | the boundary stone set up by your ancestors/A vengpa’ ~-suang a botkhia mipa | the man who pulls up the boundary stone of his neighbour/na vengte’ ~-suang na khin kei ding uh hi | you shall not move the boundary stone of your neighbours) (s:gamgi) (r:20.23.10/5.27.17/20.22.28/5.19.14) (q:draft)
gi = (t:adj) (w:good/kind/upright) (d:good in character, the opposite of gilo bad; a gi, a gilote, the good and the bad) (e:a ~, a gilote, a muh khempeuh/Na tote un mi ~ a, lungnemna hoih nei uh | your masters being good and gentle) (s:hoih) (a:gilo) (r:40.22.10/60.2.18) (q:draft)
