Giah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Giah) (d:place near the hill of Ammah on the road to the wilderness of Gibeon, reached by Joab in his pursuit of Abner) (e:lampi-a om ~ mai-ah a kikhung) (r:10.2.24) (q:draft)
giahbuk = (t:n) (w:camp/tent) (d:giah lodge with buk hut: a shelter to stay in, and the camp made of them; giahbuk pualam is outside the camp) (e:~ pualam ama kiangah nai ni/gan pumpi ~ pua lamah mei in a hal | the body of the animal is burned outside the camp) (s:giahphual/phual) (r:58.13.13/58.13.11) (q:draft)
giahna = (t:n) (w:lodging place/camp/resting place) (d:giah, stay the night, with the noun suffix na: the place where one stops for the night, a lodging place or camp) (e:Lampi-ah a ~ khatah/a ~ uh munah tuate pua uh a | they carried them to the place where they camped/~ inn uh a thei nawn kei uh hi | they no longer know their resting place/ka ~ mun uh ka tun’ uh ciangin | when we reached the place where we stopped for the night) (s:giahphual/phual) (b:giah) (r:2.4.24/1.43.21/6.4.8/24.50.6) (q:draft)
giahphual = (t:n) (w:camp/encampment) (d:the place where a people or an army stops and sets up its tents; giahphual sat is pitch camp) (e:Israel upate ~ ah a ciahkik uh hi/Gilead gamah ~ sat uh hi | they pitched camp in the land of Gilead/biakbuk leitaw lam pangah ~ satin | camping on the south side of the tabernacle/amau ~ laizang, amau omna kiim khempeuhah | in the middle of their camp, all around where they stayed) (s:phual/giahbuk) (r:4.11.30/10.17.26/4.3.29/19.78.28)
giahphuala = (t:adv) (w:in the camp) (d:giahphual, camp, with the place ending a: in the camp) (e:Topa in ~ om mi khempeuh/Filistiate’ ~ buaina hong lian semsem hi | the tumult in the camp of the Philistines grew greater and greater) (s:phuala) (b:giahphual) (r:7.7.22/9.14.19) (q:draft)
giahphualah = (t:n) (w:camp/in the camp/to the camp) (d:giahphual, camp, with the place ending ah: in the camp or to the camp) (e:khatvei pai uh a, ~ ciahkik uh hi/~ uliante pai uh a | the officers went through the camp/~ a zan giak uh hi | they spent the night in the camp/Mihonte ~ hong ciah ciangin | when the people came back to the camp) (b:giahphual) (r:6.6.14/6.3.2/6.6.11/9.4.3)
giahphualate = (t:n) (w:those camping/those in the camp) (d:giahphuala, in the camp, with the plural te: the ones encamped) (e:lam panga ~ ding khia ding) (b:giahphuala) (r:4.10.5) (q:draft)
