gimpiak = (t:v) (w:punish/afflict) (d:gim suffering with piak give: make someone suffer as punishment; gimpiak ni is the day of punishment) (e:A thuman mi ~ ding hoih lo a/Pasian’ ~ ding kihta ka hih manin | because I feared punishment from God/ka hehna mite ~ nadingin | to punish the people I am angry with/~ hun hong tung ding hi | the time of punishment will come/a thuman lo a citak lo khempeuh ~ ding | to punish all who are disobedient and unfaithful) (s:daantat/daanpia) (r:20.17.26/23.10.3/18.31.23/23.10.5/24.9.25/47.10.6) (q:draft)
