guntui = (t:n) (w:river/river water/stream) (d:gun river with tui water, the flowing water of a river) (e:ka khitui ~ luang a bang hi/bawngnawi leh khuaizu ~ bangin a luang | milk and honey flowing like a river/~ luangte na kangsak hi | you dried up the flowing rivers/~ bangin sehnel gamah a luang hi | it flowed like a river in the desert) (s:luitui) (r:25.3.48/19.74.15/18.20.17/19.105.41) (q:draft)
guntuite = (t:n) (w:river waters/rivers/streams) (d:plural of guntui, the water of a river) (e:Nail ~ keu ding a/amau’ ~ amah in sisan a suaksak hi | he turned their rivers into blood) (s:luituite/gunte) (b:guntui) (r:23.19.5/19.78.44) (q:draft)
Gunva = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:water bird/pelican) (d:gun, river, with va, bird: a bird that roosts in the ruins of Nineveh, named with gunvapi; the NIV has desert owl and older versions pelican or cormorant; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ leh gunvapite, bangtung zawl-ah tuang ding) (r:36.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
gunvapite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:storks/large water birds) (d:gun river with vapi big bird and plural te, named with gunva as birds that roost in a ruined city; the English versions have owl, bittern or pelican here, so the kind of bird is not certain) (e:Gunva le ~ bangtung zawlah tuangin) (r:36.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
gup = (t:v) (w:save/rescue) (d:form of gum, save, used before thei, nop, zawh, tuak, ding and nading) (e:midangte a ~ theih hangin/kimkhat ka ~ zawh khak nadingin | so that I may manage to save some/nang na pasal na ~ theih ding | whether you can save your husband/Nuntakna khatpeuh ~ tuak ahi hiam | is it right to save a life/Ka ~ nopte ka gum ding hi | I will save those I wish to save) (s:hon/honkhia/hotkhiat) (a:siatsak) (r:41.15.31/45.9.15/45.11.14/46.7.16/41.3.4) (q:draft)
gupa = (t:n) (w:thief) (d:gu steal with pa, the man who does it: the one who stole) (e:A ~ a kimuh kei leh/a ~ a kimuh leh | if the thief is found) (s:guta/gutapa) (b:gu) (r:2.22.8/2.22.7) (q:draft)
gupha = (t:adj) (w:venomous/deadly/poisonous) (d:having strong venom or a deadly bite, of a snake, a scorpion or fangs; from gu poison) (e:humpinelkai pi ha bangin ~ hi/Gul ~ tawh a kibang sumngo gul khat bawl inla | make a bronze snake like a venomous snake/Jonathan’ thaltang ~ a | Jonathan’s arrow was deadly) (s:gunei) (r:29.1.6/5.32.33/4.21.8/10.1.22) (q:draft)
guphate = (t:adj) (w:venomous/poisonous) (d:gupha, venomous, with the plural te; gul guphate, venomous snakes) (e:mite’ lakah gul ~ khah a) (s:guneite) (b:gupha) (r:4.21.6) (q:draft)
gupkhiat = (t:v) (w:rescue/save/deliver) (d:gup, save, with khiat, out: bring out to safety) (e:mi pawlkhat a ~ khit ciangin/khut sung pan ahi zongin, hong ~ nadingin | to rescue us from the hand/lam khatpeuh mah tawh ka ~ theih nadingin | so that by any means I might save) (s:honkhia/hotkhiat/suaktasak) (b:gup) (r:65.1.5/42.1.74/46.9.22) (q:draft)
