hawkkhia = (t:v) (w:strip off/take off/strip) (d:hawk, strip, with khia, off: strip clothing, armour or a covering from someone or something) (e:a galhiam ~ uh a/a kithatte’ nate a ~ dingin hong pai ciangin | when they came to strip the slain/tua pa’ puan ~ a | they stripped him of his clothes/khamte ~-in Assiria kumpipa tungah pia hi | he stripped off the gold and gave it to the king of Assyria) (s:suahkhia) (a:silhsak) (b:hawk) (r:9.31.9/22.5.7/13.10.8/42.10.30/12.18.16) (q:draft)
