hawlkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:drive out/cast out for someone) (d:hawlkhiat, drive out, with sak: drive out on behalf of someone, or have something driven out) (e:dawi a ~ nadingin a hong thum hi/hong langpang khempeuh hong ~ khin hi | he has driven out all who opposed you/note’ mai-ah amaute hong ~ ahih manin | because he drove them out before you/a dawi hong ~ nading uh ka thum a | I begged them to drive out the demon) (b:hawlkhiat) (r:41.7.26/36.3.15/5.4.38/42.9.40) (q:draft)
hawlkhiatsakte = (t:n) (d:hawlkhiatsak, have something driven out, with the plural te: those out of whom evil spirits were driven) (e:a sungpan dawi a ~) (b:hawlkhiatsak) (r:42.8.2) (q:draft)
hawlkhiatte = (t:n) (w:exiles/outcasts/those driven out) (d:hawlkhiat, drive out, with te, those who: the people whom someone has driven out) (e:Elam gam panin ka ~ mun khempeuhah) (s:kihawlkhiate) (b:hawlkhiat) (r:24.49.36) (q:draft)
hawlkhiazo = (t:v) (w:be able to drive out/drive out) (d:hawlkhia, drive out, with zo, be able, succeed) (e:dawite nangawn ka ~ uh hi/Kanaan mite na ~ ding uh hi | you will be able to drive out the Canaanites/amaute ka ~ kha ding hi | perhaps I will be able to drive them out/gamgi ciang dong hong ~ uh a | they have driven you to the border) (b:hawlkhia) (r:42.10.17/6.17.18/6.14.12/31.1.7) (q:draft)
hawlkik = (t:v) (w:drive back/bring back) (d:hawl, drive, with kik, back: take a strayed animal back to its owner) (e:ama kiangah na ~ ding uh hi) (b:hawl) (r:2.23.4) (q:draft)
hawlna = (t:n) (w:driving/driving away) (d:noun form of hawl, drive: the act of driving animals or people, or the place to which they are driven; tuu hawlna ciangkhut is a goad) (e:Topa in note hong ~ minamte lakah/vantungmi’ ~ tawh | with the angel driving them/tuu ~-in a zat ciangkhut | the stick used for driving sheep) (b:hawl) (r:5.4.27/19.35.5/21.12.11) (q:draft)
hawlpa = (t:n) (w:driver/charioteer/helmsman) (d:hawl, drive, with pa, the man who does it: the driver of a chariot or the man who steers a ship; leeng hawlpa is a chariot driver) (e:amah in a leeng ~ kiangah/a ~’ deihna bangin | as the helmsman wishes) (b:hawl) (r:11.22.34/14.18.33/59.3.4) (q:draft)
hawlte = (t:n) (w:drivers/sailors) (d:hawl, drive, with the plural te: those who drive a chariot or sail a ship; teembaw hawlte are sailors) (e:Tarshish teembaw ~ aw/teembaw ~ lau uh a | the sailors were afraid/Leengte leh leeng ~ ka lawnthal ding a | I will overthrow chariots and their drivers/sakollengte leh a ~ | chariots and their drivers) (b:hawl) (r:23.23.14/24.51.21/32.1.5/37.2.22) (q:draft)
hawlzia = (t:n) (w:driving/way of driving) (d:hawl, drive, with zia, manner: the way someone drives a chariot) (e:A ~ in Nimshi’ tapa Jehu’ hawl tawh kibang) (r:12.9.20) (q:draft)
hawlzo = (t:v) (w:be able to drive/be able to lead) (d:hawl, drive animals, with zo, be able) (e:naupangno khat nangawn in tuate ~ ding hi) (b:hawl) (r:23.11.6) (q:draft)
hawm = (t:v) (w:divide/distribute/share) (d:give each person a part of something: divide land, goods or spoil among people, or share what one has with others) (e:lai aisaanin a puante a ~ uh a/amau lakah ka puante ~ uh a | they divide my clothes among them/no Israel minamte lakah ~ un | distribute it among the tribes of Israel/i ngah khempeuh i ~ ding hi | we will share all we get/A nate uh ka ~ ding a | I will divide their spoils) (s:khen/sehkhen) (r:40.27.35/45.12.13/19.22.18/26.47.21/20.1.14/2.15.9) (q:draft)
