hawmin = (t:adj) (w:empty/empty-handed) (d:hawm, empty, with the suffix in: in an empty state; used as a hawmin, empty or with nothing) (e:Topa in a ~ hong ciahpih kik hi/Beel hawm bangin a ~ hong koih a | he has left us empty like an empty jar) (b:hawm) (r:8.1.21/24.51.34) (q:draft)
hawmin = (t:v) (w:share/distribute) (d:hawm, share out, with the linking suffix -in: sharing and then giving) (e:hehpihna lungsim tawh ~ na piakna uh) (b:hawm) (r:47.9.13) (q:draft)
hawmkhawm = (t:v) (w:plot together/consult together) (d:hawm with khawm, together; with vai: vai hawmkhawm, take counsel together, conspire) (e:amaute in vai ~ a) (s:kithukhat) (r:19.31.13) (q:draft)
hawmkhia = (t:v) (w:distribute/give out/issue) (d:hawm, share out, with khia, out: hand out to many people; also issue a written decree) (e:a kituak letsongte zong ~ hi/thu piakna lai a ~ hi | he issued the written decree/amau’ ngah ding ciat a ~ dingin | to distribute to each his portion/Amah in ~ zuahzuah a, mizawngte tungah pia khin hi | he has scattered freely, he has given to the poor) (s:sehkhen) (b:hawm) (r:17.2.18/27.6.9/14.31.19/19.112.9) (q:draft)
hawmkhiat = (t:v) (w:distribute/allot/give out) (d:form of hawmkhia used before uh and other following words) (e:aisanna tawh a ~ uh gamh ahi hi) (b:hawmkhia) (r:6.19.51) (q:draft)
hawmkhiatsa = (t:adj) (w:issued/given out) (d:hawmkhiat, give out or issue, with sa, already done) (e:kumpipa in a ~ thupiakna) (b:hawmkhiat) (r:27.6.15) (q:draft)
hawmna = (t:n) (w:dividing/distribution/allotment) (d:noun form of hawm, divide: the sharing out of land or goods) (e:amaute in leitang ~ zo uh hi/Annek tuidawn, sumlepai ~-ah | in the distribution of food and money/Jerusalem-a vante ~ ding ai a san ni-in | on the day they cast lots to divide the goods of Jerusalem) (b:hawm) (r:6.19.51/31.1.11/44.6.1) (q:draft)
hawmnate = (t:n) (w:sharing/acts of sharing) (d:hawmna, sharing out, with the plural te; sum hawmnate, sharing of money) (e:Thupha bawlna, sum ~ na mangngilh kei un) (b:hawmna) (r:58.13.16) (q:draft)
hawmpi = (t:n) (w:emptiness/nothing/vanity) (d:hawm, empty, with pi: a thing wholly empty or worthless; a hawmpi hi is it comes to nothing, and huih hawmpi is empty wind) (e:migilote’ lametna in a ~ hi/Izipt’ huhna bangmah man loin a ~ hi a | the help of Egypt is worthless and empty/amau’ milimte pen huih ~ ahi uh hi | their images are empty wind/miliante pen a ~ ahi hi | the highborn are nothing) (s:amawknapi/thumawkna) (b:hawm) (r:20.10.28/23.30.7/23.41.29/19.62.9) (q:draft)
Hawmpi = (t:n) (w:pit/hollow) (d:hawm, hollow or empty, with pi, great: the great hollow under the earth, the pit) (e:tua lei sung ~ sung panin) (b:hawmpi) (r:32.2.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawmpite = (t:n) (w:caverns/great hollows) (d:hawm, hollow, with pi, great, and the plural te; suang hawmpite are caves in the rocks) (e:suang ~ sung leh keen hawmte sungah) (s:leihawmte) (b:hawm) (r:23.2.20) (q:draft)
hawmsak = (t:v) (w:distribute/divide among/share out) (d:hawm, share out, with sak: divide something and give it out to others) (e:a tute lakah a ~ hi/ama deihna bangin mikim tungah a ~ hi | he distributes them to each one as he wills/a tate tungah a sum ~ hi | he divided his property between his sons/amaute khempeuh lakah a ~ hi | he divided them among them all) (s:sehkhen/hawmkhia) (b:hawm) (r:43.6.11/46.12.11/42.15.12/41.6.41) (q:draft)
hawmsawn = (t:v) (w:share/pass on) (d:hawm, share, with sawn, on to another: share what one has with someone else) (e:a hoihna a om khempeuh ~ ta hen) (r:48.6.6) (q:draft)
hawmsuak = (t:v) (w:become empty/be desolate/come to nothing) (d:hawm, empty, with suak, become: of houses left without people, a land laid waste, or courage that fails; with sak, lay waste) (e:inn tampi tak ~ ding a/Izipt mite’ lungsim ~ ding a | the Egyptians will lose heart/Khuapi ~ pen kisiacip ta a | the ruined city lies broken/Topa in leitung ~ sakin | the Lord will lay waste the earth) (r:23.5.9/23.24.1/23.19.3/23.24.10) (q:draft)
hawmte = (t:n) (w:corpses/dead bodies) (d:second part of luang hawmte, dead bodies; luang hawm is a lifeless body, literally an empty body) (e:na luang ~ uh hih gamlakah lum ding hi/Israel misi luang ~ ka thehthang gawp ding a | I will scatter the dead bodies of the Israelites/na milim’ siluang ~ uh tungah | on the lifeless forms of your idols) (s:luanghawmte) (b:hawm) (r:4.14.32/26.6.5/3.26.30) (q:draft)
hawmthang = (t:v) (w:distribute widely/scatter abroad) (d:hawm, share out, with thang, spreading far) (e:Amah in a ~ zo hi) (r:47.9.9) (q:draft)
hawmthawh = (t:v) (w:count as too little/be dissatisfied with) (d:in the question hawmthawh lai na hi hiam: do you still count it a small thing, is it not enough for you) (e:~ lai na hi hiam/nong paikhiatpihna thu ~ lai na hi hiam | is it too small a thing that you brought us out) (r:4.16.10/4.16.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawmthawh = (t:v) (w:cherish/care for tenderly/hold dear) (d:of children one has looked after and loved) (e:Ka ~ ka it ka tate) (r:25.2.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawmthawhin = (t:v) (w:counting as too little/not being satisfied with) (d:hawmthawh count as too little with the linking ending in: as if it were not enough) (e:Peor-a i khialhna ~, tuni-in Topa zuihna panin) (b:hawmthawh) (r:6.22.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawng = (t:n) (w:skin/husk/bark) (d:outer covering of a fruit or of a tree: the skin of a grape, the bark of a fig tree) (e:a ~ nangawn ahi zongin ne lo ding hi/A ~ khempeuh netum uh a | they have eaten off all its bark) (r:4.6.4/29.1.7) (q:draft)
haza = (t:v) (w:be jealous/envy) (d:feel jealousy or envy toward someone; a haza Pasian is a jealous God; with lo, not grudge or hold back something) (e:A sanggamte in amah ~ uh a/a ~ Pasian ahi hi | he is a jealous God/Tua pawlte’ pate in Josef a ~ uh a | the patriarchs were jealous of Joseph/mihonpi a muh uh ciangin ~ uh a | when they saw the crowds they were jealous) (s:eng/een/aam) (r:1.37.11/5.4.24/44.7.9/44.13.45) (q:draft)
Hazael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazael) (d:king of Aram in Damascus who took the throne after Ben-Hadad and oppressed Israel in the days of Jehu and Jehoahaz) (r:12.13.24/12.13.22)
Hazaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazaiah) (d:man of Judah, an ancestor of Maaseiah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.11.5)
Hazaraddar = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hazar Addar) (d:place on the southern border of Canaan between Kadesh Barnea and Azmon) (r:4.34.4)
Hazarenan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hazar Enan) (d:place at the north-eastern corner of the promised land, on the border of Damascus) (r:4.34.9/4.34.10)
Hazargaddah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazar-gaddah/Hazar Gaddah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.27)
Hazarmaveth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazarmaveth) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.26)
Hazarshual = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazar-shual/Hazar Shual) (d:town in the far south of Judah near Beersheba, allotted to the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.15.28/6.19.3)
Hazarsusah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hazar Susah) (d:town in the south allotted to the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.19.5)
Hazarsusim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hazar Susim) (d:town of the tribe of Simeon, the same place as Hazar Susah) (r:13.4.31)
hazat = (t:v) (w:be jealous of/envy) (d:form of haza, be jealous, used before endings such as nading and uh ciangin; hazat nading piangsak is to stir up jealousy) (e:Aaron a ~ uh ciangin/ama ~ nading piangsak uh hi | they stirred up his jealousy/Nangma ~ hehna, mei bangin kuang paisuak ding ahi hiam | will your jealous anger burn like fire for ever/amaute’ ~ theih nading ka bawl ding hi | I will make them envious) (b:haza) (r:19.106.16/5.32.16/11.14.22/19.79.5/5.32.21) (q:draft)
hazatna = (t:n) (w:envy/jealousy) (d:hazat, be jealous, with the noun suffix na: the feeling of envy or jealousy) (e:~ tawh a dim uh hi/~ in guh muatsak natna ahi hi | envy is a disease that rots the bones/~ siahuai zaw lai hi | jealousy is crueller still/~ leh kidem nopna a om leh | where there is envy and rivalry) (s:enna) (b:hazat) (r:44.5.17/20.14.30/20.27.4/59.3.16) (q:draft)
hazatsak = (t:v) (w:be jealous for/be jealous on behalf of) (d:hazat, be jealous, with sak, here doing it for another person: be jealous for the sake of someone) (e:Keima tangin hong ~ na hi hiam) (b:hazat) (r:4.11.29) (q:draft)
Hazazontamar = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazazon-tamar/Hazezon Tamar) (d:place of the Amorites near the Dead Sea, the same as En Gedi) (r:1.14.7/14.20.2)
Hazekiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezekiah) (d:spelling of Hezekiah in Isaiah 36:4, the king of Judah in the time of Isaiah) (r:23.36.4)
Hazerhattikon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hazer Hattikon) (d:place on the border of Hauran, named on the northern boundary of the land in the vision of Ezekiel) (r:26.47.16)
Hazeroth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hazeroth) (d:camping place of Israel in the wilderness after Kibroth Hattaavah, where Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses) (r:4.33.17/4.33.18)
Haziel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haziel) (d:Levite of the clan of Gershon, son of Shimei) (e:Shelomoth, ~, leh Haran, thum pha uh hi) (r:13.23.9) (q:draft)
Hazo = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazo) (d:son of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, and Milkah) (r:1.22.22)
Hazor = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazor) (d:name of several towns, chiefly the royal Canaanite city in the north whose king Jabin was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.11.1/6.19.36)
Hazorhadattah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazor-hadattah/Hazor Hadattah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.25)
hazzebaim = (t:see) <Pokereth-hazzebaim>
Hazzelelponi = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hazzelelponi) (d:daughter of Etam in the family of Hur of the tribe of Judah, sister of Jezreel, Ishma and Idbash) (r:13.4.3)
Hazzeleponi = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hazzelelponi) (d:spelling of Hazzelelponi in one Tedim text, daughter of Etam of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.3)
Heber = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heber) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Beriah and grandson of Asher, and Heber the Kenite, husband of Jael) (r:1.46.17/13.7.32)
Hebron = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Hebron) (d:city in the hill country of Judah where Abraham lived and where David first reigned as king; also the name of a son of Kohath and grandson of Levi) (r:1.13.18/6.10.36)
Hebru = (t:n) (w:Hebru/Hebrew) (d:a Hebrew, one of the people of Israel, and their language; Hebru mi is a Hebrew person and Hebru pau the Hebrew language) (e:~ mi nih na kilai uh hi/~ pau-in nakpi takin kiko a | he called out loudly in Hebrew/~ kamin Armageddon a kici munah | at the place called Armageddon in Hebrew/leivang panin ~ mite hong pusuakkhia uh hi | the Hebrews are coming out of the holes) (r:2.2.13/23.36.13/66.16.16/9.14.11)
Hebrute = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Hebrews) (d:the Hebrews, the people of Israel, as in Hebrute’ Pasian, the God of the Hebrews) (b:Hebru) (r:2.9.1/2.5.3)
heek = (t:v) (w:wring/twist) (d:twist round with force, as the head of a bird at its neck or the neck of an enemy) (e:a lu ~ ding a/na galte’ ngawng na ~ ding a | you will wring the necks of your enemies) (r:3.5.8/1.49.8) (q:draft)
heek = (t:n) (w:wink) (d:in the compound mit-heek, a wink of the eye; mit-heek pia is to wink at someone) (e:a mit-~ hong pia-in/mit-~ kipiasak kei in | do not let them wink the eye) (s:mitheek) (r:20.6.13/19.35.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
heekcip = (t:v) (w:bind tight/twist tight/grip) (d:heek, twist, with cip, tightly: wind round and hold fast) (e:ka puan tawh hong ~ hi) (b:heek) (r:18.30.18) (q:draft)
heekgawp = (t:v) (w:twist violently/wrench) (d:heek, twist, with gawp, violently or thoroughly) (e:Topa’ awging in singkungte ~ a) (b:heek) (r:19.29.9) (q:draft)
heeksat = (t:v) (w:wring off/twist off/sever) (d:heek, wring, with sat, cut: twist right off; in the verse the head is wrung but not severed) (e:ahih hangin ~ lo ding hi) (s:heektat) (r:3.5.8) (q:draft)
heektat = (t:v) (w:wring off/twist off) (d:heek, wring, with tat, be severed: twist until it comes off) (e:a lu ~ ding a) (s:heeksat) (r:3.1.15) (q:draft)
heekte = (t:n) (w:accusers/betrayers/those who sue) (d:heek with te, those who; here heek means accuse or hand over, not wring: those who take someone to court, those who betrayed the Righteous One) (e:zum innah hong ~ puanza zong/tua Midik Pa a ~, a thatte | those who betrayed and killed that Righteous One) (s:mawhsakte) (b:heek) (r:40.5.40/44.7.52) (q:draft, low confidence)
heem = (t:adv) (w:aside/sideways/indirectly) (d:off the straight line: a heem lam is the edge or outer part, heem pai is turn aside from the course, heem gen is say in a veiled way) (e:hong ~ pai kuamah om lo hi/a ~ lam bek hi pan hi | it is only the outer edge/Hih thu ~ gen ahih ciangin | because this was said in a veiled way) (r:29.2.7/42.18.34/18.26.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
heempai = (t:v) (w:swerve/turn aside) (d:heem, aside, with pai, go) (e:a hong ~ kuamah om lo hi) (s:pial) (r:29.2.7) (q:draft)
heengte = (t:n) (w:crevices/clefts) (d:plural with te; suangpi heengte are the clefts in the rocks) (e:suangpi ~ sung leh lingkung kawmte) (s:kawmte) (r:23.7.19) (q:draft)
Hefer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hepher) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Gilead of the tribe of Manasseh and father of Zelophehad; also a town and district west of the Jordan) (r:4.26.33/4.26.32)
Hefzibah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hephzibah) (d:mother of King Manasseh of Judah, wife of King Hezekiah) (r:12.21.1)
Hegai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hegai) (d:eunuch of King Xerxes who had charge of the women in the palace at Susa) (r:17.2.8/17.2.15)
Heglam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heglam) (d:in 1 Chronicles 8:7 another name of Gera of the tribe of Benjamin, father of Uzza and Ahihud; the NIV translates the word instead of giving a name) (r:13.8.7)
heh = (t:adj) (w:angry) (d:feeling anger; the person one is angry with is followed by tungah) (e:Tua ahih ciangin Kain ~ mahmah a/Rachel’ tungah Jakob ~ mahmah a | Jacob became very angry with Rachel/Jonah lungkim het loin a ~ hi | Jonah was not at all pleased and was angry/Balaam’ tungah Balak ~ mahmah a | Balak was very angry with Balaam) (r:1.4.5/32.4.1/1.30.2/4.24.10)
heh = (t:adj) (w:irate) (e:Na ~ ding kilawm na sa hiam/hih thute ka zak ciangin ka ~ mahmah hi | when I heard these things I was very angry/Moses ~ mahmah a | Moses was very angry) (r:32.4.4/16.5.6/4.16.15)
heh = (t:v) (w:irritate/be angry/get angry) (d:be or become angry with someone; heh kei in is do not be angry) (e:Topa ~ kei in | may the Lord not be angry/Bang hangin nang ~ a | why are you angry/Amaute tungah Moses ~ hi | Moses was angry with them/amah ~ paisuak lo ding hi | he will not stay angry forever) (s:lungham/thangpai/sinso) (r:1.18.30/1.4.6/2.16.20/19.103.9)
hehbaih = (t:adj) (w:quick-tempered/hot-tempered/easily angered) (d:heh, angry, with baih, easy or quick: quick to become angry) (e:A ~ mite tawh kipawl kei in la) (s:lungtom) (a:hehhak/lungduai) (r:20.22.24) (q:draft)
hehgawp = (t:v) (w:be furious/rage/pour out wrath) (d:heh, be angry, with gawp, violently: let anger loose on someone) (e:kumpi gamte tungah ~ in) (s:hehlua/thangpai/lungham) (b:heh) (r:19.79.6) (q:draft)
hehhak = (t:adj) (w:slow to anger) (d:heh, angry, with hak, slow or hard: not easily made angry) (e:a hehpih thei Pasian, a ~, a migi mahmah | a gracious God, slow to anger, very kind) (s:lungduai) (a:hehbaih/lungtom) (r:32.4.2) (q:draft)
hehhakin = (t:adj) (w:slow to anger) (d:hehhak with the linking ending in) (e:~ itna kip lianpi nei hi) (b:hehhak) (r:19.145.8) (q:draft)
hehhuai = (t:adj) (w:offensive/provoking anger) (d:heh angry with huai, causing or worthy of; the NIV has a stumbling block) (e:Jew mite a dingin a ~ thu hi a) (r:46.1.23) (q:draft)
Hehiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jehiel) (d:spelling of Jehiel in 1 Chronicles 15:20, a Levite musician who played the lyre before the ark) (r:13.15.20)
hehin = (t:adv) (w:angrily/in anger) (d:heh, be angry, with the linking suffix in: being angry, in anger) (e:Pasian ~ daan a piak ciangin/ci-in ~ ka kiciam hi | so I swore in my anger/Uzza tungah Topa ~ daan pia ahih manin | because the Lord in anger punished Uzzah/ka lawmte uh ~ nang hong hih ding | my companions will attack you in anger) (s:hehsa-in) (b:heh) (r:18.21.30/58.3.11/13.13.11/7.18.25) (q:draft)
hehkik = (t:v) (w:be angry again) (d:heh, be angry, with kik, again) (e:Israel-te tungah Topa hong ~ a) (b:heh) (r:10.24.1) (q:draft)
hehlua = (t:v) (w:be very angry/be furious/rage) (d:heh, be angry, with lua, too much: be angry beyond measure) (e:~ loin kei hong hilh in/Topa nak ~ mahmah ahih manin | because the Lord was exceedingly angry/Hong ~ lecin kei ka si ding hi | if you are too angry with me I will die/Amaute’ tungah Topa ~ kha ding ahih manin | because the Lord might break out in anger against them/Mihonte ~-in awngkekgawp uh a | the crowd shouted in fury) (s:hehgawp/thangpai/lungham) (b:heh) (r:24.10.24/4.11.10/2.19.22/44.22.23) (q:draft)
hehluat = (t:v) (w:be very angry/be furious) (d:form of hehlua used before another word, as in hehluat mahmahna, great wrath) (e:~ mahmahna tawh amaute linglawng sakin) (b:hehlua) (r:19.2.5) (q:draft)
hehluatna = (t:n) (w:wrath/fury/great anger) (d:heh, be angry, with luat, too much, and the noun suffix na: great or fierce anger) (e:ka ~ hangin tuate ka la khia/na ~ in kote hong laugawp sak hi | your wrath terrifies us/Tua ciangin Topa’ ~ a dai hi | then the fierce anger of the Lord subsided) (s:thangpaihna/lunghamna/sinsona) (b:hehluat) (r:28.13.11/19.90.7/6.7.26) (q:draft)
hehmai = (t:n) (w:angry face/angry look/stern look) (d:heh, angry, with mai, face) (e:Jesuh in ~ tawh a kiim a pam en/a ~ bei sak hi | it makes his hard look disappear) (s:hehmel) (r:41.3.5/21.8.1) (q:draft)
hehmel = (t:n) (w:angry look/fierce look) (d:heh, angry, with mel, appearance; hehmel a pua is fierce-looking) (e:~ a pua kumpi khat) (s:hehmai) (r:27.8.23) (q:draft)
hehna = (t:n) (w:anger/wrath/fury) (d:heh, be angry, with the noun suffix na: anger, wrath, of people and often of God) (e:na ~ tawh amaute niamkhiat gawp in/Na ~ khempeuh na damsak a | you set aside all your wrath/na sanggampa’ ~ a bei mateng | until your brother’s anger is over/Pasian’ ~ hangin, ama hauhna khempeuh kisusia ding hi | because of the wrath of God all his wealth will be destroyed) (s:thangpaihna/sinsona/lunghamna) (b:heh) (r:18.40.11/19.85.3/1.27.44/18.20.28) (q:draft)
hehnate = (t:n) (w:wrath/anger) (d:plural of hehna, here of the outpourings of the wrath of God held in the bowls) (e:Pasian’ ~ va sungkhia un) (b:hehna) (r:66.16.1) (q:draft)
hehnateng = (t:n) (w:all the anger/full wrath) (d:hehna, anger, with teng, all: the whole of one’s wrath) (e:a nitsakna hangun ka ~ ka thuaksak hi/ka ~ gamlakah thuaksak gawpin | pouring out all my wrath on them in the wilderness) (b:hehna) (r:26.36.18/26.20.21) (q:draft)
hehnem = (t:v) (w:comfort/console) (d:soothe a person who is sad or in trouble; the form hehnep is used before nading, na and bangin) (e:a kinuaisiah mite a ~ thei Pasian/Ka mite ~ un | comfort my people/amah ~ dingin a sanggamte hong pai uh hi | his relatives came to comfort him/kua in nang hong ~ ding ahi hiam | who will comfort you) (s:lungnuamsak) (a:dahsak) (r:47.7.6/23.40.1/13.7.22/23.51.19) (q:draft)
hehnemin = (t:v) (w:comfort/encourage/console) (d:form of hehnem, comfort, with the linking suffix in: comforting and then going on to the next action) (e:thu hoih tawh note hong ~/Amah ~ inn-ah a ompih mite | the people who were with her in the house comforting her/a dah a kapte ~ ka lungdamsak ding hi | comforting those who mourn and weep I will make them glad/Note hong ~ ka hong hanthawn uh a | we comforted and urged you) (b:hehnem) (r:18.16.5/43.11.31/23.57.18/52.2.12) (q:draft)
hehnempa = (t:n) (w:comforter) (d:hehnem, comfort, with pa, the man or the one who does it: the one who comforts) (e:note hong ~ ka hi hi) (b:hehnem) (r:23.51.12) (q:draft)
hehnemsak = (t:v) (w:comfort/give comfort) (d:hehnem, comfort, with the causative sak) (e:hehnepna hangin zong hong ~ hi) (b:hehnem) (r:47.7.7) (q:draft)
hehnemta = (t:v) (w:have comforted/comfort) (d:hehnem, comfort, with ta, which marks the action as now done) (e:Topa in ama mite ~ a) (b:hehnem) (r:23.52.9) (q:draft)
hehnemte = (t:n) (w:comforters) (d:hehnem, comfort, with te, those who: people sent to comfort the bereaved) (e:nangma kiangah ~ hong sawl manin/David in nang kiangah ~ hong sawlna hangin | because David has sent comforters to you) (b:hehnem) (r:10.10.3/13.19.3) (q:draft)
hehnemzaw = (t:v) (w:comfort instead/rather comfort) (d:hehnem, comfort, with zaw, rather or instead) (e:maisak ta unla ~ un) (b:hehnem) (r:47.2.7) (q:draft)
hehnep = (t:v) (w:comfort/console/encourage) (d:form of hehnem used before bangin, nading, na and sawm) (e:A nu in a ta a ~ bangin/note lungsim hong ~ nadingin | so that he may encourage your hearts/note ~ nading thu ka gen ding hi | I would speak words to comfort you/amawknapi tawh ~ nong sawm uh hi | you try to comfort me with empty things) (r:23.66.13/49.6.22/18.16.5/18.21.34) (q:draft)
hehnepna = (t:n) (w:comfort/consolation) (d:hehnep, comfort, with the noun suffix na: comfort given or received) (e:Jerusalem khua sungah ~ na ngah ding uh/ahi zongin ~ ka ngah kei hi | but I found no comfort/dikna leh ~ kam tawh vantungmi dawng a | he answered the angel with kind and comforting words) (b:hehnep) (r:23.66.13/18.16.2/19.77.2/38.1.13) (q:draft)
hehnepnate = (t:n) (w:comforts/consolations) (d:plural of hehnepna: comforts, words of comfort) (e:amau’ ~ a mawknapi hi lel hi) (b:hehnepna) (r:38.10.2) (q:draft)
Hehoahaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jehoahaz) (d:spelling of Jehoahaz in 2 Kings 13:25, king of Israel, son of Jehu and father of Jehoash) (r:12.13.25)
hehpa = (t:n) (w:angry man) (d:heh, angry, with pa, a man: a man who is angry; galkap a hehpa is an enraged soldier) (e:galkap a ~ bangin hong hih gawp hi) (b:heh) (r:18.16.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehpih = (t:v) (w:have mercy on/pity/have compassion on) (d:feel and show pity or kindness to someone in need; hong hehpih in, have mercy on me, is a common prayer) (e:Zeisu aw, hong ~ in/a topa in ~ a | his master took pity on him/ama mite ~ hi | he took pity on his people/Na nasemte hong ~ in | have compassion on your servants) (s:khasiat/lainat) (r:42.18.38/19.103.13/40.18.27/29.2.18/19.90.13) (q:draft)
hehpihhuai = (t:adj) (w:pitiable/pitiful/wretched) (d:hehpih, pity, with huai, worthy of: deserving pity, wretched; hehpihhuai sa means feel compassion for) (e:mihonpite a muh ciangin ~ a sa hi/Zeisu in ~ sa a | Jesus had compassion/puansilh ding a nei lo, a ~, a lungkhamhuai | having nothing to wear, pitiable and wretched) (s:khasiathuai) (r:40.9.36/1.41.19/40.20.34/66.3.17) (q:draft)
hehpihhuaina = (t:n) (w:wretchedness/pitiable state) (d:hehpihhuai, pitiable, with the noun suffix na) (e:pumpi lunggimna, ~, zawnna, mittawtna) (b:hehpihhuai) (r:66.3.17) (q:draft)
hehpihhuaipa = (t:n) (w:poor man/pitiable man) (d:hehpihhuai, pitiable, with pa, a man: a man who is to be pitied) (e:Hih mi ~ kiko-in) (b:hehpihhuai) (r:19.34.6) (q:draft)
hehpihhuaisa = (t:v) (w:feel pity/have compassion/take pity) (d:hehpihhuai, pitiable, with sa, consider: find someone pitiable, be moved with compassion) (e:tua numei a muh ciangin ~ a/a liam pa a muh ciangin ~ a | when he saw the wounded man he took pity on him/~ mahmah ahih manin va delhin | being filled with compassion he ran to him/Zeisu in ~-in a khut zanin lawng a | Jesus, moved with pity, reached out his hand and touched him) (s:lainat) (b:hehpihhuai) (r:42.7.13/42.15.20/42.10.33/41.1.41) (q:draft)
hehpihin = (t:v) (w:have mercy on/have compassion on/be gracious to) (d:form of hehpih with the linking suffix in, showing mercy and then doing the next action) (e:kei hong ~ hong dawng in/Topa in Jakob ~ Israel teel kik ding a | the Lord will have compassion on Jacob and choose Israel again/Pasian in eite hong ~ thupha hong pia hen | may God be gracious to us and bless us/Topa in amaute ~ amaute khasiat a | the Lord was gracious to them and had compassion on them) (b:hehpih) (r:19.27.7/23.14.1/19.67.1/12.13.23) (q:draft)
hehpihkik = (t:v) (w:have compassion again/have mercy again) (d:hehpih, have mercy on, with kik, again) (e:ka ~ ding a) (b:hehpih) (r:24.12.15) (q:draft)
hehpihna = (t:n) (w:grace/mercy/compassion) (d:hehpih, have mercy on, with the noun suffix na: mercy, compassion, and in the letters the grace of God; hehpihna thupha is the blessing of grace) (e:Topa Zeisu’ ~ thupha note tungah/i Pasian in ~ nei hi | our God is full of compassion/~, nopna leh itna khang semsem ta hen | may mercy, peace and love increase more and more) (s:lainatna) (b:hehpih) (r:46.16.23/19.116.5/65.1.2) (q:draft)
Hehpihna = (t:n) (w:Favor/grace) (d:hehpihna, grace, written with a capital as the name of one of the two staffs of the shepherd in Zechariah) (e:~ a kici ciangkhut la-in ka kuaitan a/khat pen ~ ci-in min ka phuak a | one I named Favor) (b:hehpihna) (r:38.11.10/38.11.7) (q:draft)
hehpihnate = (t:n) (w:mercies/compassions) (d:plural of hehpihna: mercies, acts of compassion) (e:hehna tawh ama ~ humcip khin ahi hiam) (b:hehpihna) (r:19.77.9) (q:draft)
hehpihnop = (t:v) (w:want to have mercy on/wish to pity) (d:hehpih, have mercy on, with nop, the form of nuam, want, used before a noun) (e:ka ~ mite ka hehpih ding hi) (r:2.33.19) (q:draft)
hehpihpa = (t:n) (w:merciful one/benefactor) (d:hehpih, have mercy on, with pa marking a man: the one who shows mercy or kindness) (e:Tua a ~ in a lawmpa ahi hi/a ukte mi ~ a ci uh hi | those who rule are called benefactors/amaute a ~ in amaute lamkaih ding a | he who has compassion on them will guide them) (b:hehpih) (r:42.10.37/42.22.25/23.49.10) (q:draft)
hehpihsak = (t:v) (w:have mercy on) (d:hehpih, have mercy on, with sak; here mercy asked for another person on the behalf of the speaker) (e:ka tapa hong ~ in) (b:hehpih) (r:40.17.15) (q:draft)
hehpihzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to show favour/find favour with) (d:hehpih, have mercy on, with zawh, the form of zo, be able; nong hehpihzawh a, if you can show me favour, is a polite opening of a request to a king) (e:Kumpipa in nong ~ a) (r:17.7.3/17.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehsa = (t:see) <hehsa-in>
hehsa-in = (t:adv) (w:angrily/in anger/in a rage) (d:heh, be angry, with sa, already, and the linking in: being angry, in wrath) (e:amah kihei-in a ~ paikhia hi/A ~ leitungah na pai a | in wrath you strode through the earth/kumpipa ~ an nekna pan ding khia-in | the king got up from the meal in a rage/a ~ kei hong taii kei inla | do not rebuke me in your anger) (s:hehin/hehsapi-in/sinsosa-in) (r:12.5.12/35.3.12/17.7.7/19.38.1) (q:draft)
