hehsakin = (t:v) (w:provoke/anger/make angry) (d:hehsak, make angry, with the linking ending in: provoking, and so going on to the next verb) (e:note’ nasepna tawh amah ~/ama nasepna tawh amah ~ | arousing his anger by what he did/hong ~ hong thangpaisak ahih manin | because it has angered and enraged me) (b:hehsak) (r:5.31.29/24.32.31/11.16.7) (q:draft)
hehsakkha = (t:v) (w:anger/provoke) (d:hehsak, make angry, with kha, which marks that the thing came to happen) (e:vantung Pasian ~ uh ahih manin) (r:15.5.12) (q:draft)
hehsakna = (t:n) (w:provocation/provoking) (d:the act of making someone angry, in the verses of provoking God to anger) (e:kei nong ~ hang leh Israel na khialhsakna/Israel Pasian, Topa a ~ hang ahi hi | it was because he provoked the Lord, the God of Israel/gamlakah phin-in na ~ uh phawk un la | remember how you provoked him in the wilderness) (s:phinna/hehsuahna) (b:hehsak) (r:11.21.22/11.15.30/5.9.7) (q:draft)
hehsaknate = (t:n) (w:offences/provocations) (d:hehsakna, making angry, with plural te: the things by which others make one angry) (e:mi’ hong ~ kiphawkmawh bawlna in) (b:hehsakna) (r:20.19.11) (q:draft)
hehsakte = (t:n) (w:those who anger/those who insult) (d:hehsak, make angry, with the plural te: the people who do so) (e:Kha Siangtho a ~’ thuak ding) (b:hehsak) (r:58.10.29) (q:draft)
hehsapi = (t:see) <hehsapi-in>
hehsapi-in = (t:adv) (w:in anger/angrily) (d:heh, be angry, with sa, pi and the linking ending in: while still in great anger) (e:a ~ a paikhia hi) (s:hehsa-in) (r:4.12.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehsuahna = (t:n) (w:provocation/cause of anger) (d:heh, anger, with suah, bring out, and the noun suffix na: what makes someone angry, said of the idol that provokes God) (e:Pasian’ ~ milim ka mu hi/Pasian a ~ ahi milim a omna mun | the place where the idol that provokes God stood) (s:hehsakna) (r:26.8.5/26.8.3) (q:draft)
hehsuak = (t:v) (w:be angry/be vexed/be enraged) (d:heh, angry, with suak, come out or become: break out in anger) (e:gunpite tungah na ~ a/Migilo in hih thu mu-in a ~ a | the wicked will see this and be vexed) (r:35.3.8/19.112.10) (q:draft)
hehtaak = (t:adj) (w:deserving anger/blameworthy) (d:heh, be angry, with taak, worthy; hehtaak sa is to count something worth being angry at, to find fault with it) (e:Kamging mawkmawk ~ sa a) (r:18.6.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehte = (t:n) (w:those who are angry) (d:heh, angry, with the plural te: the people who are angry) (e:sanggamte tungah a ~ khempeuh in) (b:heh) (r:40.5.22) (q:draft)
hehtheih = (t:v) (w:get angry/be provoked) (d:heh, be angry, with theih, the form of thei, can, used before nading; a hehtheih nadingin bawl is to act so as to make someone angry) (e:a ~ nadingin bawl kei unla) (b:heh) (r:49.6.4) (q:draft)
