heihei = (t:adv) (w:to and fro/round about) (d:expressive word after kikawi, of a ship being driven this way and that) (e:tuipi sungah ka kikawi ~ lai takun) (r:44.27.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
heikhia = (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside/pervert/take away) (d:turn something away from its place or right course; of justice, pervert; of the heart, lead astray) (e:sumgolh la-in thuman ~ uh hi/pasian dangte lamah ama lungsim ~ uh hi | they turned his heart towards other gods/a mai uh ~ uh a | they turned their faces away/Thutang na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not pervert justice) (b:hei) (r:9.8.3/11.11.3/11.11.4/14.29.6/5.16.19) (q:draft)
heikhiat = (t:v) (w:turn away/pervert) (d:form of heikhia used before another word such as sak; thutang heikhiat sak is to turn justice away from someone) (e:ka mite thutang ~ sakin) (b:heikhia) (r:23.10.1) (q:draft)
heikhiatna = (t:n) (w:perversion/injustice) (d:heikhiat, turn away, with the noun suffix na; thuman heikhiatna is the perverting of justice) (e:thuman ~, mi deidanna) (b:heikhiat) (r:14.19.7) (q:draft)
heikhiatsak = (t:v) (w:pervert/turn aside/thwart) (d:cause to turn away from its course: deny or twist justice, bring wisdom to nothing) (e:thuman mite’ thu ~ hi/miteite’ teina ka ~ ding hi | I will frustrate the intelligence of the intelligent/na mi zawngpa’ thutan’na na ~ kei ding hi | do not deny justice to your poor/meigong numeite ading thutang a ~ mipa | the man who withholds justice from the widow) (b:heikhiat) (r:2.23.8/46.1.19/2.23.6/5.27.19) (q:draft)
heikik = (t:v) (w:turn back) (d:hei, turn, with kik, back; here of the heart turning back to Egypt) (e:Izipt gamah a lung a ~ uh hi) (b:hei) (r:44.7.40) (q:draft)
heikikna = (t:n) (w:turning back) (d:heikik, turn back, with the noun suffix na) (e:amaute’ lungsim na ~ thu) (b:heikik) (r:11.18.37) (q:draft)
heina = (t:n) (w:rudder/helm) (d:the part a ship is steered with, from hei turn) (e:a ~ neu khat tawh ki-ukzo hi/a neu mahmah ~ tawh a hei thei hi | he can steer it with a very small rudder/teembaw ~ a kizang sing peekpi | the plank used as the rudder of the ship) (s:hawhna) (b:hei) (r:59.3.4/44.27.40) (q:draft)
heina = (t:n) (d:the place or direction one turns to; ka heina khempeuh ah, wherever I turn) (e:Ka ~ khempeuh ah mite in) (b:hei) (r:18.17.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
heipi = (t:n) (w:axe/large axe) (d:hei, axe, with pi, big) (e:~ tawh sing a phuk bang uh hi) (s:hei) (b:hei) (r:19.74.5) (q:draft)
heisak = (t:v) (w:turn/change into/pervert/turn aside) (d:causative of hei, turn a thing in another direction or into something else, as a curse into a blessing, of justice pervert it or deny it to someone) (e:ading thutang na ~ kei ding uh a/samsiatna pen note adingin thupha-in hong ~ hi | he turned the curse into a blessing for you/Ahithofel’ thugente haina-in na ~ in | turn the counsel of Ahithophel into foolishness/thutang kimlai a khialin ~ lo hi | he does not pervert justice) (b:hei) (r:5.24.17/5.23.5/10.15.31/18.34.12) (q:draft)
heisakkik = (t:v) (w:turn back/restore) (d:heisak, cause to turn, with kik, back or again; thu a hoihlamin heisakkik is to turn matters back to good) (e:thu a hoihlamin a ~ ding hi) (b:heisak) (r:18.33.26) (q:draft)
heisakzaw = (t:v) (w:turn instead/change into) (d:heisak, cause to turn, with zaw, rather or instead, as a curse turned into a blessing) (e:note a dingin thupha-in hong ~ hi) (b:heisak) (r:5.23.5) (q:draft)
heitang = (t:n) (w:axhead/axe head) (d:the iron head of an axe, hei) (e:a ~ tui sungah kia hi/a khut zanin a ~ a la hi | he reached out his hand and took the axe head/a ~ a ga panin kikhong-in | the axe head flies off the handle) (r:12.6.5/5.19.5/12.6.7) (q:draft)
heite = (t:n) (w:axes) (d:plural of hei, axe) (e:tuzumte leh ~ tawh na a sem dingin) (b:hei) (r:10.12.31/13.20.3) (q:draft)
hek = (t:v) (w:accuse/denounce/betray/inform against) (d:bring a charge against someone, or give him away to those who are looking for him; hek sim is to denounce secretly) (e:galtai mite ~ kei in/Judah mite a ~ sim uh hi | they denounced the Jews/kumpipa kiangah Daniel ~ dingin a pai uh hi | they went to the king to accuse Daniel/a ~ teng khempeuh | all those who had accused him) (s:mawhsak/ngawh) (r:23.16.3/27.3.8/27.6.12/27.6.24) (q:draft)
heksim = (t:v) (w:denounce/accuse secretly/inform against) (d:hek, accuse, with sim, secretly: denounce someone behind his back) (e:Jew mite a ~ uh hi) (r:27.3.8) (q:draft)
heksuk = (t:n) (w:sitting down/going down) (d:the sitting or going down of a person, paired with hektohna, the rising up, to mean everything someone does; na heksuk na hektohna khempeuhah is in all that you do and wherever you go) (e:na ~ na hektohna khempeuhah) (a:hektohna) (r:11.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
