Helam = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Helam) (d:town east of the Jordan where David defeated the Arameans led by Shobak) (r:10.10.16/10.10.17)
Helbah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Helbah) (d:town in the territory of Asher whose Canaanite inhabitants were not driven out) (r:7.1.31)
Helbon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Helbon) (d:town near Damascus known for its wine) (r:26.27.18)
Heldai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heldai) (d:name of two men: a Netophathite who commanded the army division of the twelfth month under David, and an exile who returned from Babylon in the time of Zechariah) (r:38.6.14/13.27.15)
Heleb = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heleb/Heled) (d:son of Baanah the Netophathite, one of David's mighty warriors, called Heled in the NIV) (r:10.23.29)
Heled = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heled) (d:son of Baanah the Netophathite, one of David's mighty warriors) (r:13.11.30)
Helef = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Heleph) (d:town on the border of the territory of Naphtali) (e:A gamgi in ~, Za-anannim-a om tawsaw) (r:6.19.33) (q:draft)
Helek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Helek) (d:son of Gilead in the tribe of Manasseh, ancestor of the Helekite clan) (r:4.26.30/6.17.2)
Helez = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Helez) (d:name of two men: one of David's mighty warriors, called the Paltite or the Pelonite, who commanded the army division of the seventh month, and a descendant of Jerahmeel in Judah) (r:10.23.26/13.11.27)
helhawt = (t:see) <thu-helhawt>
helhel = (t:adv) (d:expressive adverb after takhawm, born together, in the picture of twin fawns; paired with hialhial, it seems to stress being close together and alike) (e:a takhawm ~ sakhi peeng/a takhawm ~ sanang nih tawh) (r:22.7.3/22.4.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
helhhawtte = (t:n) (w:ruthless people/violent people) (d:plural, used after mi: mi helhhawtte are ruthless people who seek to kill someone, named beside the arrogant) (e:mi ~ in thah dingin hong zong uh hi) (s:ngongtatte) (r:19.54.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
Heli = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heli) (d:father of Joseph, the husband of Mary, in the family line of Jesus given by Luke) (e:Josef in ~’ ta hi) (r:42.3.23/42.3.24) (q:draft)
Heliopolis = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Heliopolis) (d:city in Egypt known for the worship of the sun, also called On; the NIV has the temple of the sun in Jeremiah 43:13) (r:24.43.13)
Helkai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Helkai) (d:head of a priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim, after the exile) (r:16.12.15)
Helkath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Helkath) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher, given to the Levites) (r:6.21.31/6.19.25)
Helkathhazzurim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Helkath Hazzurim) (d:place at Gibeon where twelve men of Abner and twelve men of Joab killed one another) (r:10.2.16)
helkhawmin = (t:v) (w:mixing together) (d:hel, mix, with khawm, together, and the linking ending in: mixing things together and then doing the next action) (e:tuate ~ anlum-in bawl in) (r:26.4.9) (q:draft)
hell = (t:n) (w:hell/Hades) (d:loanword from English hell, the place of punishment after death; often hell khuk, the pit of hell) (e:Tua ~ khuk sungah thante si ngei lo/~ khuk sungah gimna thuakin a om hi | he was in torment in the pit of hell/Khe kim nei-in ~ sungah hong kikhiat sangin | than to be thrown into hell with both feet/~ khuk sungah a khiathuah theilai Pasian | God, who can still throw into the pit of hell) (s:hel) (a:vantung) (r:41.9.48/42.16.23/41.9.45/42.12.5) (q:draft)
Hell = (t:n) (w:hell/Hades) (d:hell written with a capital; Hell khuksung is the pit of hell, and in Revelation Hell follows the rider named Death) (e:a nungah ~ in a zui hi/~ khuk sungah hong kilawnsuk ding hi | you will be thrown down into the pit of hell/~ khuk tun nading kongvang pen lianin | the gate that leads to the pit of hell is wide/~ khuksung a tung ding uh ahi hi | they will end up in the pit of hell) (s:Hel) (b:hell) (r:66.6.8/50.3.19/42.10.15/40.7.13) (q:draft)
Helon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Helon) (d:father of Eliab, the leader of the tribe of Zebulun in the wilderness) (r:4.1.9/4.10.16)
helsa = (t:adj) (w:mixed) (d:hel, mix, with sa, already done: mixed; zu helsa is mixed wine) (e:zu ~ hai sungah a dim/lim takin ~ leh balnensa-in na paipih ding | you shall bring it well mixed and broken in pieces) (s:sawhsa) (b:hel) (r:23.65.11/3.6.21) (q:draft)
helsak = (t:v) (w:have asked for in marriage/send to woo) (d:hel, ask for a woman in marriage, with the causative sak: have others ask for her on one's behalf) (e:ama zi dingin Abigail ~ hi) (b:hel) (r:9.25.39) (q:draft, low confidence)
hem = (t:adj) (w:deformed/disfigured/blemished) (d:having a part of the body damaged, misshapen or missing; mai hem is a disfigured face) (e:Amaute sitbang a, ~ ahih manin/mittaw, khelbai, mai ~ leh khut-leh-khe sau lua | blind, lame, disfigured in the face or with a limb too long/a gamtang thei lo, a ~ | the injured, the maimed) (s:sitbang/sitbaang) (r:3.22.25/3.21.18/3.22.22) (q:draft)
hem = (t:v) (w:be diminished/be impaired) (d:be lessened or damaged; with a negative, as in bangmah hem tuan lo, not diminished in any way) (e:ama hoihna bangmah ~ tuan lo hi) (s:kikhiam) (r:18.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
hem = (t:n) (w:rumour/hint) (d:in thu hem, a report of which only a part is heard, a mere rumour) (e:a thu ~ zak bek ung) (s:hemlam) (r:18.28.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
Heman = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hemam/Heman/Homam) (d:name of several men, chiefly Heman son of Joel, a Kohathite who led the temple singers under David; also a wise man of the family of Zerah, and in Genesis 36:22 a son of Lotan the Horite, Homam in the NIV) (r:1.36.22)
Hemante = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heman) (d:Heman with the plural te: Heman and those named with him, the leaders of the temple musicians under David) (b:Heman) (r:13.25.6)
Hemdan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hemdan) (d:son of Dishon, a Horite chief in the land of Seir) (r:1.36.26)
hemkhia = (t:v) (w:remove/put away/clear away/take away) (d:move a person or thing away from where it is, with khia, out; muhna panin hemkhia is to remove from one's sight) (e:ka muhna panin ka ~ ding hi/ama muhna panin amaute ~ hi | he removed them from his presence/Na kiang panin na leenggahzu ~ in | put your wine away from you/mual tunga biaknate ~-in | removing the high places) (s:koihkhia/khinkhia/lakhia) (b:hem) (r:24.32.31/12.17.18/9.1.14/12.18.4) (q:draft)
hemlam = (t:n) (w:hint/faint whisper/fringe) (d:what is only hinted at or barely heard of a matter, not the whole of it) (e:a ~ bek hi pan hi) (s:hem) (r:18.26.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hemzak = (t:v) (w:hear a rumor of/hear indirectly) (d:hear of a thing only faintly or by report; with zak, the form of za hear) (e:a thu ~ bek ung) (r:18.28.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
hen = (t:v) (w:let/may) (d:placed at the end of a sentence, after the verb, for a wish or a command about someone else: let him, may it be so; often ta hen, and kei hen for let him not) (e:bil nei mi in za ta ~/mual tungah tai ta ~ | let them flee to the mountains/puan la dingin ciahkik kei ~ | let him not go back to get his cloak/na tate uh hong pung sak ta ~ | may he make your children increase) (r:40.11.15/1.1.3/40.24.16/40.24.18/19.115.14)
Hena = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hena) (d:city conquered by the Assyrians, named together with Sepharvaim and Ivvah) (e:Sefarvaim khuapi kumpipa, ~ kumpipa) (r:12.19.13/12.18.34) (q:draft)
Henadad = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Henadad) (d:Levite whose descendants helped to rebuild the temple and the wall of Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.3.24/16.3.18)
hencip = (t:v) (w:bind fast/tie up) (d:hen, bind, with cip, tightly: tie someone up firmly so that there is no getting loose) (e:Shadrak, Meshak leh Abednego ~ sa-in/khauhual tawh kong ~ ding a | I will tie you up with ropes/hih kawnggak nei pa ~ ding a | they will bind the owner of this belt/Satan in a ~ Abraham’ tanu | a daughter of Abraham whom Satan has kept bound) (s:gakcip/khihcip) (a:khah/phel) (r:27.3.23/27.3.21/26.4.8/44.21.11/42.13.16) (q:draft)
hencipin = (t:v) (w:binding fast/bound fast) (d:hencip, bind fast, with the linking ending in: binding fast and then doing the next action) (e:a tawntungin ~ a khum hi/ka khialhnate un hong ~ ka tha uh beita | our sins bind us fast and our strength is gone) (b:hencip) (r:65.1.6/26.33.10) (q:draft)
hencipsa = (t:see) <hencipsa-in>
hencipsa-in = (t:v) (w:being bound/firmly tied) (d:hencip, bind fast, with sa, already done, and the connective in: in a bound state) (e:Mihing thum ~ mei phualpi sungah) (r:27.3.24/27.3.23) (q:draft)
henhan = (t:adv) (w:surging/tumultuously) (d:expressive word after a verb for a great noisy mass in motion, as a clamouring crowd or surging waves) (e:mihonpi a gamlum ~ a muh ciangin/tuipi hualte bangin hong kuan ~ ding uh hi | they will come surging up like the waves of the sea/khuasung mi khempeuh gamlum ~ uh a | all the people of the city were in an uproar/awng-in a gamlum ~ uh hi | they shout and make a great uproar/Meiipi leeng bangin hong pai ~ hih teembawte | these ships that come sweeping along like flying clouds) (r:40.9.23/26.26.3/40.21.10/24.51.55/23.60.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
henhanin = (t:adv) (w:in an uproar) (d:henhan, expressive word for a great noisy mass in motion, with the adverbial ending in; buaisak henhanin is throwing into uproar) (e:Khuasung khempeuh buaisak ~) (b:henhan) (r:44.17.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
henhanna = (t:n) (w:spreading/moving in a mass) (d:henhan, expressive word for a great mass in motion, with the noun ending na; meiite a pai henhanna is the way the clouds move along) (e:Meiite a pai ~ thu hita leh) (b:henhan) (r:18.36.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
henhante = (t:n) (w:those moving in a mass/those flying along) (d:henhan, expressive word for a great mass in motion, with te, those who; hong leeng henhante are those who come flying along like a cloud) (e:bangin hong leeng ~ kua ahi hiam) (b:henhan) (r:23.60.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
henhen = (t:adv) (w:pressed down) (d:reduplicated expressive word in a henhen, a tahtah, a dimletin, of a measure pressed down, shaken together and running over) (e:a ~, a tahtah, a dimletin) (r:42.6.38) (q:draft, low confidence)
henin = (t:v) (w:binding/tying up) (d:hen, bind, with the linking ending in: binding someone or tying something up and then doing the next action) (e:numei leh pasal ~, thong sungah khumin/~, thong sungah a khia hi | he bound him and put him in prison/ngun talen nih ip nihin ~ | tying up two talents of silver in two bags/Nang hong ~ amaute’ khut sungah kong pia bek | we will only tie you up and hand you over to them) (r:44.22.4/40.14.3/12.5.23/7.15.13) (q:draft)
henkhawm = (t:v) (w:tie together/bind together) (d:hen, tie or bind, with khawm, together) (e:suang khat tawh ~ inla) (s:henkop/gakkhawm) (r:24.51.63) (q:draft)
henkhit = (t:v) (w:have bound/have tied) (d:hen, bind or tie, with khit, finished; before ciangin it means after binding) (e:Jesuh a ~ uh ciangin paikhiatpihin/pumpeeng dawnah a ~ ciangin | after he had tied it to the end of a reed) (r:41.15.1/41.15.36) (q:draft)
henkop = (t:v) (w:bind together/tie together) (d:hen, bind, with kop, pair or join) (e:Vana om Seguk ~ thei a) (s:henkhawm/gakkhawm) (r:18.38.31) (q:draft)
henla = (t:part) (d:hen, let it be so, with la, and: placed after a verb for a wish or command that is followed by another clause, let him do this and) (e:ama gamtatna ciat entel ~/ama gamtatna siksanin kisial ~ | and let him take pride on the ground of his own conduct) (r:48.6.4) (q:draft)
henna = (t:n) (w:bond/binding/bondage) (d:hen, bind, with the noun ending na: the state of being bound, or what binds; henna khau is a cord that binds) (e:migilote’ ~ khaute su-tat khin hi/ka ~ khaute a sutat khin zo uh hi | they have torn off my bonds/~ sunga om ama mite simmawh lo hi | he does not despise his people who are in bonds) (s:khihna/kihenna) (r:19.129.4/24.5.5/19.69.33) (q:draft)
henna = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:henna) (d:loanword from English: the henna shrub, grown for its fragrant flowers) (e:~ leh nard sing namtuite) (r:22.4.13) (q:draft)
hennate = (t:n) (w:bonds/chains/fetters) (d:plural of henna, bond, the things with which someone is bound) (e:Amau’ hong ~ su-tat khia-in) (s:sikkhaute/kolte) (b:henna) (r:19.2.3) (q:draft)
henpa = (t:n) (w:binder) (d:hen, tie or bind, with pa, the man who does it; buhlom henpa is the binder of sheaves) (e:buhlom ~ in a ang-a a pom loh) (r:19.129.6) (q:draft)
hensuk = (t:v) (w:push down/thrust down) (d:with suk, downward: of a woman pushed back down into a basket; whether the first part is hen bind is not certain) (e:ciangpi sungah tua numei ~ kik a) (r:38.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
hente = (t:n) (w:bundles/bound sheaves) (d:hen, bind or tie, with the plural te: things tied up; anlom hente are the bundles of cut grain) (e:Anlom ~ lak panin zong) (s:kihente) (b:hen) (r:8.2.16) (q:draft)
henzo = (t:v) (w:be able to bind/be able to tie) (d:hen, bind or tie, with zo, be able) (e:sikkhau tawh ~ nawn lo uh hi/a leii ~ ding na hi hiam | can you tie down its tongue) (s:khihzo) (b:hen) (r:41.5.3/18.41.1) (q:draft)
hep = (t:v) (w:remove/put away) (d:seen with khiat out, hep khiat, remove from a place or position; usually written as one word, hepkhiat) (e:nangma ma-a ka ~ khiat Saul) (r:10.7.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
hepkhiat = (t:v) (w:remove/put away/take away) (d:hep, remove, with khiat, out: take a person or thing away from a place; the form of hepkhia used before another word such as ding, dongin or sak) (e:note lak panin na ~ ding uh ahi hi/Topa in ama muhna panin Israel a ~ dongin | until the Lord removed Israel from his presence/nangma ma-a ka ~ Saul’ tung panin | from Saul, whom I removed from before you/a biakna taute ~ sakin | having his altars removed) (s:hemkhia/koihkhia/khinkhia) (b:hep) (r:46.5.2/12.17.22/10.7.15/12.18.22) (q:draft)
hepkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:take away/remove) (d:hepkhiat, remove, with sak: take something away from a person, or remove it for him) (e:note kiang panin hong ~ ding hi/kei’ muhna panin lungkhamna hong ~ lo hi | it did not take trouble away from my sight) (b:hepkhiat) (r:66.22.19/18.3.10) (q:draft)
hepkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:removing/having removed) (d:hepkhiatsak, remove, with the linking ending in: having removed something and then doing the next action) (e:le biakna taute ~ Jerusalem tungah) (b:hepkhiatsak) (r:12.18.22) (q:draft)
Heres = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Heres) (d:place east of the Jordan known from Heres kahtohna, the Pass of Heres, by which Gideon returned from battle) (e:~ kahtohna lam tawnin ciahkik hi) (r:7.8.13) (q:draft)
Heresh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heresh) (d:Levite who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (e:Bakbakkar, ~, Galal) (r:13.9.15) (q:draft)
Hereth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hereth) (d:forest in the land of Judah where David hid from Saul) (r:9.22.5)
Hermas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hermas) (d:Christian in Rome to whom Paul sends greetings) (r:45.16.14)
Hermes = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hermes) (d:name of a Greek god, which the people of Lystra gave to Paul because he was the chief speaker, and of a Christian in Rome greeted by Paul) (r:44.14.12/45.16.14)
Hermogenes = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hermogenes) (d:man of the province of Asia who deserted Paul, named with Phygelus) (r:55.1.15)
Hermon = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Hermon) (d:high mountain on the northern border of Israel, called Sirion by the Sidonians and Senir by the Amorites) (r:5.3.9/19.42.6)
Hernon = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Hermon) (d:spelling of Hermon in Deuteronomy 4:47, the high mountain on the northern border of Israel) (r:5.4.47)
Herod = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Herod) (d:name of several rulers of the Jews under Rome, among them Herod the Great, king when Jesus was born, and Herod Antipas, who had John the Baptist put to death) (r:40.2.22/40.14.1)
Herodias = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Herodias) (d:wife of Herod Antipas, earlier the wife of his brother Philip, who brought about the death of John the Baptist) (r:42.3.19/41.6.19)
Herodion = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Herodion) (d:Jewish Christian in Rome whom Paul greets as his kinsman) (r:45.16.11)
Heron = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hebron) (d:spelling of Hebron in 2 Samuel 5:5, the city in Judah where David reigned for seven and a half years) (r:10.5.5)
Heshbon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Heshbon) (d:city east of the Jordan, the capital of Sihon king of the Amorites, later given to the tribe of Reuben and to the Levites) (r:6.13.17/4.32.37)
Heshmon = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Heshmon) (d:town in the far south of the territory of Judah) (r:6.15.27)
Heshmonah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hashmonah) (d:camping place of the Israelites in the wilderness, between Mithkah and Moseroth) (r:4.33.29/4.33.30)
het = (t:adv) (w:at all/in the least) (d:placed after a verb and before a negative to strengthen it: hi het kei, hih het lo, not at all, never) (e:bangmah hih ~ lo hi/amaute in mang nuam ~ lo uh a | they would not obey at all/Nang tungah tua bang hi ~ kei hen | may it never be so for you/hih bangin ka gamta ~ kei ding hi | I will never do such a thing/amah si ~ lo ding a | he will certainly not die) (s:zenzen) (r:30.3.7/1.21.11/38.7.11/9.20.9/13.11.19/26.18.28) (q:draft)
hetchiai = (t:v) (w:sneeze/snort) (d:sneeze, said of a person; of a great beast, snort) (e:Amah a ~ ciangin mei-ek bangin/naupang sagih vei ~-in a mit hak hi | the boy sneezed seven times and opened his eyes) (s:hetthiai) (r:18.41.18/12.4.35) (q:draft)
Heth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heth) (d:son of Canaan and ancestor of the Hittites) (r:1.10.15/13.1.13)
Hethlon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hethlon) (d:place on the northern border of the land of Israel in the vision of Ezekiel, the Hethlon road in the NIV) (r:26.47.15/26.48.1)
hetkei = (t:adv) (w:not at all/not in the least) (d:het, at all, written together with the negative kei, placed after a verb) (e:ka thaneem ~ uh hi/Lungsim kawina ka deih ~ a | I want nothing at all to do with a crooked heart/simtham tatnate ka zang ~ uh hi | we do not use secret ways at all/huhna bangmah pianuam ~ leh | if he is not willing to give any help at all) (s:hetlo) (r:47.4.1/19.101.4/47.4.2/62.3.17) (q:draft)
hetlo = (t:adv) (w:not at all) (d:het, at all, with lo, not, placed after a describing word or verb: lungkim hetlo, not pleased at all) (e:lungkim ~ ka hih manin/nuam ~-a kha keei hi | it is not pleasant at all, but bitter) (s:hetkei) (b:het) (r:16.13.8/24.2.19) (q:draft)
hetloh = (t:part) (w:not at all) (d:placed after a verb: not at all, in no way; form of hetlo used before a noun or ding) (e:Ka theihzawh ~ a lamdang mahmah thu/a thu na theih ~ siatna | a disaster you know nothing about/bangmah a ngah ~ ding | that he will receive nothing at all/ka zuau ~ lamtak a hong thei hi | he knows that I am not lying at all) (b:hetlo) (r:20.30.18/59.1.7/23.47.11/47.11.31) (q:draft)
hetlohna = (t:part) (d:ending of a verb phrase: hetloh, not at all, with na, which makes a noun: the fact of not doing something at all, or a place where it cannot be done at all) (e:kuamah ka khem ngei ~/taikhiatzawh ~ kulhpi sungah hong koih hi | he has put me inside a wall from which there is no escape/Pasian itna na neih ~ uh | that you have no love of God at all/ka paubaan ~ hong mu ding hi | he will see that I am blameless) (b:hetloh) (r:18.31.5/47.12.16/25.3.7/43.5.42/18.31.6) (q:draft)
hetloin = (t:adv) (w:not at all/without any) (d:hetlo, not at all, with the linking ending in, placed after a verb or describing word: without doing or being so at all) (e:lungkia ~ na omna uh/lunghihmawhna khat zong nei ~ Pasian ka muang hi | I trust in God without any fear at all/kumpipa’ heh ding lau ~ Egypt gam panin paikhia | he left Egypt without fearing the anger of the king at all/hehpih ngaihsut ~ leenkhiamang ding hi | it will sweep them away without any thought of pity) (b:hetlo) (r:66.2.3/25.3.3/19.56.11/58.11.27/18.27.22) (q:draft)
hetthiai = (t:v) (w:sneeze/snort) (d:spelling of hetchiai: sneeze, or of a great beast, snort) (e:A ~ ciangin taang zaizai a) (s:hetchiai) (r:18.41.18) (q:draft)
heu = (t:v) (w:be gleaned/be gathered in) (d:said of fruit and grapes in a heu hun, apparently the time when the picking is over and only gleanings are left; exact meaning not certain) (e:leenggah a ~ hun laitakin) (r:33.7.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
heuh = (t:v) (w:lop off/strip off/trim) (d:cut or strip branches or leaves from a tree) (e:sing hiangte ~ ding hi/a teh teng ~ siang in la | strip off all its leaves/A hiangte ~ khiatsak in | strip off her branches) (s:heuhkhia) (r:23.10.33/27.4.14/24.5.10) (q:draft)
heuhau = (t:adv) (w:glowing/gleaming) (d:expressive adverb after taang shine or san red, glowing like metal in a fire) (e:sumngo bangin taang ~ a/sumsan kinawtngil tawh kibangin san ~ hi | it glowed red like polished bronze) (r:26.1.27/26.8.2) (q:draft)
heuhkhia = (t:v) (w:lop off/cut away/prune off) (d:heuh, lop or trim, with khia, off: cut branches away from a tree or vine) (e:a hiangte ~ ding hi) (s:atkhia) (b:heuh) (r:23.18.5) (q:draft)
heuhkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:strip off/lop off/cut away) (d:heuh, lop or strip, with khiat, off, and sak: cut or strip the branches off a vine or tree) (e:A hiangte ~ in) (s:heuhsiang) (r:24.5.10) (q:draft)
heuhna = (t:n) (w:pruning/trimming) (d:heuh, prune, with the noun suffix na: the cutting back of branches; singhiang heuhna temkawi is a pruning hook or pruning knife) (e:singhiang ~ temkawi tawh a selte atkhia/singhiang ~ temkawite teipi-in seek un | beat your pruning hooks into spears/a teipite uh singhiang ~ temkawi-in seek ding | they will beat their spears into pruning hooks) (b:heuh) (r:23.18.5/23.2.4/29.3.10) (q:draft)
heuhsiang = (t:v) (w:strip off/strip clean) (d:heuh, strip or lop, with siang, clean: strip a tree bare of its leaves) (e:A tehteng ~ inla/A tehteng ~ inla, a gahteng thehthang in | strip off its leaves and scatter its fruit) (s:heuhkhiatsak) (b:heuh) (r:27.4.14) (q:draft)
Hezekiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezekiah) (d:king of Judah, son of Ahaz and father of Manasseh, who ruled in the days of the prophet Isaiah; also the name of other men) (r:12.18.9/23.37.15)
Hezekiahte = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezekiah) (d:Hezekiah with the plural te, closing a list of the kings of Judah: Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz and Hezekiah) (b:Hezekiah) (r:23.1.1/33.1.1)
Hezion = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezion) (d:father of Tabrimmon and grandfather of Ben-Hadad king of Aram) (r:11.15.18)
Hezir = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezir) (d:name of two men: a priest to whom the seventeenth lot fell in the time of David, and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.20/13.24.15)
Hezro = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezro) (d:the Carmelite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (e:Karmel khuami ~, Arbi mi Pa-arai) (r:10.23.35/13.11.37) (q:draft)
hezron = (t:see) <Kerioth-hezron>
Hezron = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezron) (d:name of two men: a son of Reuben, and a son of Perez and grandson of Judah, the father of Ram and an ancestor of David) (r:1.46.9/13.2.5)
hi = (t:ppm) (d:word indicating nominative case) (e:Pasian thu ~/Nuntakna khomun ka ~ hi | I am the bread of life/Ka ngaihno in keima aa ~ | my beloved is mine/tua a hiangte Topa a’ ~ lo hi | those branches are not the Lord’s) (r:43.6.48/22.2.16/24.5.10)
hi = (t:ppm) (d:word indicating the verb ending a sentence) (e:a piangsak ~/a gen ~/Zeisu Oliv Mual ah a pai ~ | Jesus went to the Mount of Olives/misipa tho a, thu a gen ~ | the dead man sat up and spoke/Mi a thatpa kithat ding ~ | whoever kills a person shall be put to death) (r:1.1.1/43.11.35/43.8.1/42.7.15/3.24.17)
HI = (t:part) (d:the sentence-final word hi written in capitals, closing the notice fixed on the cross: is) (e:JUDAHTE’ KUMPIPA ~/HIHPA IN JUDAHTE’ KUMPIPA ~ | this is the king of the Jews/HIH PA IN JUDAHTE’ KUMPIPA ZEISU ~ | this is Jesus, the king of the Jews/NAZARETH KHUAMI ZEISU AHI ~ | is Jesus of Nazareth) (r:41.15.26/42.23.38/40.27.37/43.19.19) (q:draft)
hi maw = (t:phrase) (w:is that so/really/yes) denoting interrogation or exclamation
hi'ng = (t:v) (w:am/I am) (d:hi, be, with the first person singular ending ing shortened: I am, at the end of a statement) (e:kei in ama aa ~/Kei a kamsia ~ | I am wretched/kei, pasian bang ~ | I am like a god/Keimah ~, kei sim loh midang om kei | I am, and there is no one besides me) (r:22.2.16/33.7.1/26.28.9/23.47.10) (q:draft)
hia = (t:det) (w:that/yonder) (d:points to someone or something away from the speaker; hia lai-ah is over there, in contrast with hih lai-ah, here) (e:~ lai-ah va tusuk in/~ siahdongpa tawh kibang ka hi kei hi | I am not like that tax collector) (s:hua) (r:20.25.7/19.36.12/42.18.11) (q:draft)
hiah = (t:adv) (w:here) (d:in or at this place; Hiah om ing, here I am, is the answer of someone who is called) (e:~ om ing/~ om ing, ka ta | here I am, my son/ka kepsa na sum tawi ~ a om hi | here is your money that I have kept/~ om ing; ka ta aw | here I am, my son) (s:hihlai-ah) (a:tuasan) (r:42.19.20/23.65.1/1.22.7/1.27.18)
hial = (t:v) (w:roll up) (d:roll up, said of a weaver rolling up the finished cloth; kihial is be rolled up) (e:siamgante in a ~ bangin/a ~ bangin ka nuntakna kihial khin a | my life is rolled up as a weaver rolls up cloth) (s:zial) (r:23.38.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
hialbawl = (t:v) (w:adjourn/put off/postpone) (d:said of a judge closing a hearing for the time being without giving a decision) (e:a thusitna ~ a/Feliks in a thusitna ~ a | Felix adjourned the hearing) (r:44.24.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
hialhial = (t:adv) (d:expressive adverb after omkhawm or takhawm in the picture of twin fawns; paired with helhel, it seems to stress being closely together or alike) (e:a omkhawm ~ sanang nih tawh kibang hi/a takhawm ~ sakhi peeng tawh | like twin fawns of a gazelle) (s:helhel) (r:22.7.3/22.4.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiam = (t:part) (d:final particle of an interrogative sentence, collocating with initial particles such as bang and kua) (e:na min bang ~?/gal bangin hong ngaihsun na hi ~ | do you consider me an enemy/gamdang ah bangci sak thei ding i hi ~ | how can we sing it in a foreign land/kei hong gimsak ding na hi ~ | will you go on tormenting me) (r:44.21.22/18.10.4/18.13.24/19.137.4/18.19.2)
hiam = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:Bang hang ~ cih leh/Bang hang ~ i cih leh | for, because/bang ahi ~ ci-in kanin | finding out what it is/bang hang ~ cih leh tua a hiangte | because those branches) (r:1.2.3/58.4.12/49.5.10/24.5.10)
hiamin = (t:adj) (w:sharp) (d:hiam, sharp, with the ending in; tat hiamin and kitat hiamin are whet or be whetted until sharp) (e:kitat ~ kipuah siang hi/na teipite uh tat ~ | sharpen your spears) (a:mawl) (r:26.21.11/24.46.4) (q:draft)
hiamin = (t:n) (w:weapon) (d:hiam, weapon, with the marker in: as a weapon) (e:galsim nadingin ~ thuman ka zang uh hi) (s:galhiam) (r:47.6.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiamna = (t:n) (w:sharpening) (d:hiam, sharp, with the noun suffix na; seek hiamna is the forging of a tool to make it sharp again) (e:tu-zum seek ~ thaman in) (r:9.13.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiamsa = (t:see) <hiamsa-in>
hiamsa-in = (t:adv) (w:sharpened/ready sharpened) (d:hiam sharp with sa already and the ending in, in a sharpened state, said of an arrow kept ready for use) (e:a ~ zat pah dingin) (r:23.49.2) (q:draft)
hiamsak = (t:v) (w:sharpen) (d:hiam, sharp, with sak, cause: make sharp) (e:Sik in sik mah ~ thei a) (s:taat) (r:20.27.17) (q:draft)
hiamtawi = (t:adj) (w:armed) (d:hiam, weapon, with tawi, carry: bearing weapons; hiamtawi mite are the armed men) (e:singkuang mai-ah ~ mite paisak un/siampite mai-ah ~ mite pai uh a | the armed men went ahead of the priests) (r:6.6.7/6.6.9) (q:draft)
hiamtawite = (t:n) (w:armed men) (d:hiamtawi armed with the plural te, those who bear weapons) (e:amaute mai-ah ~ pai-in) (b:hiamtawi) (r:6.6.13) (q:draft)
hiamte = (t:n) (w:weapons/arms) (d:plural of hiam, weapon: the arms a man carries, such as sword, spear, bow and quiver) (e:a ~ a naupangpa kiangah pia-in/ka ~ ahi zongin kong la man kei hi | I have not brought my weapons either/meivak, meilah leh ~ tawi-in | carrying torches, lanterns and weapons/galdona-a ka zat uh ~ | the weapons we fight with) (s:galhiamte/galvan) (r:9.20.40/9.21.8/43.18.3/47.10.4) (q:draft)
hiamte = (t:adj) (w:sharp) (d:hiam, sharp, in the plural after the thing named, as thaltang hiamte, sharp arrows, and namsau hiamte, sharp swords) (e:na thaltang ~ lut a/Galhangpa’ thaltang ~ leh sesing hol am | a warrior’s sharp arrows and glowing coals/amau leite in namsau ~ ahi hi | their tongues are sharp swords) (a:mawl) (r:19.45.5/19.120.4/19.57.4) (q:draft)
hiamzaw = (t:adj) (w:sharper) (d:hiam, sharp, with zaw, more: sharper, used with sangin, than) (e:namsau sangin ~ lai hi/lang nih a hiam namsau sangin ~ a | sharper than a double-edged sword) (r:58.4.12) (q:draft)
hiang = (t:n) (w:branch/bough) (d:branch or bough of a tree or vine, also an arm of the lampstand) (e:a ~ sau a/leenggui tungah ~ thum om hi | on the vine were three branches/a ~ in taamtaak singliante khuh a | its branches covered the mighty cedars/a ~ sang pen dawnah pumnih pumthum | two or three on the topmost branch) (s:singhiang) (r:26.31.7/19.80.10/1.40.10/23.17.6) (q:draft)
Hiang = (t:n) (w:Branch) (d:hiang, branch, written with a capital of the promised king from the line of David, the righteous Branch) (e:a diktat ~ khat ka khangsak ding a/a diktat ~ khat ka khan’ khiatsak ni | the day when I raise up a righteous Branch) (s:Sel) (b:hiang) (r:24.33.15/24.23.5) (q:draft)
hiangah = (t:n) (w:in the branches/on the branches) (d:hiang, branch, with the place marker ah: on or in the branches, where birds nest and perch) (e:vasate in a ~ bu a bawl uh hi/vasate in a ~ a tuang thei uh hi | the birds can perch in its branches/vasate in a ~ bu bawl uh a | the birds nested in its branches) (b:hiang) (r:27.4.21/42.13.19/27.4.12) (q:draft)
hiangpa = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:plane tree/fir) (d:a kind of tree, used in the Bible for the plane tree and the fir; said with kung or sing, tree) (e:~ sing leh taak sing ka suankhawm ding/poplar kung, almond kung leh ~ kungte | poplar, almond and plane trees/taaksan sing, ~ sing leh taaksingte | the juniper, the fir and the cypress) (r:23.41.19/1.30.37/23.60.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiangpha = (t:adj) (w:spreading/branching) (d:hiang, branch, with pha, good or plentiful: having many spreading branches, said of a vine) (e:a ~ leengguipi hong suak hi) (r:26.17.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiangte = (t:n) (w:branches/boughs) (d:plural of hiang: the branches of a tree or vine) (e:a tunga ama ~ a si ta hi/tuipi lamah a ~ zam-in | its branches spread toward the sea/A ~ zong golin sau mahmah hi | its boughs too grew thick and very long/a ~ kang sengsang hi | its branches are left white) (s:singhiangte) (b:hiang) (r:18.18.16/26.31.5/19.80.11/29.1.7) (q:draft)
hiangteng = (t:n) (w:branches/all the branches) (d:hiang, branch, with teng, all of them: all the branches of a tree) (e:A singkung phuk inla, a ~ sattan in) (b:hiang) (r:27.4.14) (q:draft)
hiat = (t:adv) (w:calmly/quietly/in peace) (d:after a verb, usually doubled as hiat-hiat or hit-hiat: in a calm, undisturbed way) (e:Guta mite nuam takin om hit-~ a/gentheihna thuak se loin si ~ uh hi | they die in peace without suffering/Om hit-~ un la, Pasian ka hihna thei un | be still, and know that I am God/kam khum takin pau ~-~ hi | she speaks gently and calmly) (s:hithiat/dide) (r:18.12.6/18.21.13/19.46.10/20.31.26) (q:draft)
hiat = (t:v) (w:rub/comb) (d:draw or press something across a surface; sam hiat is comb or dress the hair, and in Lamentations 3:16 the face is rubbed on the ground) (e:ka sam zong ka ~ kei hi/ka maitang lei ah hong ~ a | he has rubbed my face in the dust) (r:27.10.3/25.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiathiat = (t:adv) (w:calmly/quietly/at ease) (d:follows a verb, often of speaking, to show that the action goes on in a calm, even and unhurried way) (e:mipilpa in dam taka a gen ~/midikte ahih leh lungmuangin kampau ~ uh hi | the upright speak calmly and with confidence/tel takin thugen ~ ding uh hi | they will speak clearly and calmly/tutphah nip tungah a kizia ~ | lounging at ease on soft couches) (s:hithiat/hit-hiat) (a:lualua) (r:21.9.17/30.6.4/20.21.29/23.32.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiathiatin = (t:adv) (w:quietly/calmly) (d:hiathiat with the adverbial ending in; na sem hiathiatin is working quietly and steadily) (e:na sem ~ amau’ nuntak nadingun) (s:hithiatin) (b:hiathiat) (r:53.3.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiau = (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb of going, apparently showing that the going is swift and direct, as in a paikhia hiau hi, he went straight on his way) (e:Jesuh a paikhia ~ hi) (r:42.4.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
