HIH = (t:pron) (w:this) (d:hih written in capitals in the inscription on the cross; HIH PA is this man) (e:~ PA IN JUDAHTE’ KUMPIPA ZEISU HI) (r:40.27.37) (q:draft)
hihgawp = (t:v) (w:attack/assault/treat violently) (d:hih, do, with gawp, roughly or violently: fall upon someone, treat with violence) (e:mihonpi in hong ~ uh hi/galkap a heh pa bangin kei hong ~ hi | he rushes at me like an angry warrior/theihkholh lohin i ~ ding hi | we will fall on him without warning/amau a mudahte a ut utun ~ uh hi | they did as they pleased to those who hated them) (s:simgawp) (r:47.6.5/18.16.14/10.17.12/17.9.5) (q:draft)
hihin = (t:v) (w:doing/by doing) (d:hih, do, with the linking ending in: doing or by doing, followed by another verb) (e:thatanghat thu tawh ~ amah luppih hi/Tua mi in gamtatna hoihte ~ | let that person do good deeds/theih lohna hangin ~ a khialh leh | if he sins by doing it without knowing/amaute in ~ a mawh uh leh | if they do it and become guilty) (b:hih) (r:10.13.14/59.3.13/3.4.27/3.4.13) (q:draft)
hihkha = (t:v) (w:happen to do/do/commit) (d:hih, do, with kha, which marks an act that happens to be done, by mistake or as something that may come about) (e:mawhna lianpi ~ ihih manin/Ka hihnopteng ~ loin | not doing what I want to do/theih lohna hangin ~-in a mawh ciangin | when he does it without knowing and is guilty/namsau tawh kote hong ~ ding ahih manin | because he may strike us with the sword) (s:gamtakha) (r:15.10.13/3.4.22/45.7.15/2.5.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
