hinpih = (t:v) (w:live with/remain alive with) (d:hin, live, with pih, together with: go on living with others, remain alive among them) (e:note ka hong ~ lai ding hi) (b:hin) (r:50.1.25) (q:draft)
hinsak = (t:v) (w:let live/make alive/raise up) (d:hin, live, with the causative sak: let someone live by sparing his life, or give life to the dead) (e:amaute a ~ nading thuciamna/nitawp ni ciangin ka ~ ding | I will raise them up at the last day) (s:hingsak/nungtasak/nuntaksak) (a:sihsak/that) (b:hin) (r:6.9.15/43.6.40) (q:draft)
hinsakkik = (t:v) (w:raise up/make alive again) (d:hinsak, make alive, with kik, again: bring back to life, raise the dead) (e:nitawp ni ciangin ka ~ ding ahi hi) (s:hinkiksak/thokiksak) (b:hinsak) (r:43.6.39) (q:draft)
hinsakna = (t:n) (w:restoring to life/making alive) (d:hinsak, make alive, with the noun suffix na: the act of bringing the dead to life) (e:a sisa mi a ~ thu) (s:hinkiksakna) (b:hinsak) (r:12.8.5) (q:draft)
hinsuahzo = (t:v) (w:keep alive/be able to keep alive) (d:hin, live, with suah and zo, be able: manage to bring through alive, as animals in a drought) (e:la-sakolte i ~ kha ding a) (r:11.18.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hintheih = (t:v) (w:can live/be able to live) (d:hin live with theih, the form of thei can used before nading: na hintheih nadingun, so that you may live) (e:na ~ nadingun nuntakna teel unla/Topa na Pasian uh itin na ~ nadingun | so that you may love the Lord your God and live) (s:nungtazo) (b:hin) (r:5.30.19/5.30.6) (q:draft)
hintheihna = (t:n) (w:life/power to live) (d:hintheih, can live, with the noun suffix na: the power to live; hintheihna hu is the breath that gives life) (e:sungah ~ hu om nai lo hi/Tua pumpite sungah ~ hu hong lut a | the breath of life entered those bodies) (b:hintheih) (r:26.37.8/26.37.10) (q:draft)
hipa = (t:n) (w:the one who is/he who is) (d:hi, be, with pa, a man: a hipa is the one who is so, said of a male and often of God) (e:zahtak ding a ~’ tungah/ama' min Aam a ~ in | he whose name is Jealous/nalamdang lian a bawl amah bek a ~' tungah | to him who alone does great wonders) (s:ahipa) (r:19.76.11/2.34.14/19.136.4) (q:draft)
Hirah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hirah) (d:man of Adullam, the friend of Judah) (r:1.38.1/1.38.12)
Hiram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hiram/Huram) (d:name of the king of Tyre who supplied Solomon with timber for the temple, and of the bronze craftsman Solomon brought from Tyre, called Huram in the NIV) (e:Solomon in ~ kiangah kam khak a) (r:11.5.2/11.7.13) (q:draft)
hisak = (t:v) (w:make be/cause to become/let be) (d:hi, be, with the causative sak: make someone or something be what is named before it, or let it be so) (e:Na cihsa bangin ~ in/meikuangte nangma nasemte na ~ hi | you make flames of fire your servants/na topa’ tapa’ zi ~ un | let her become the wife of your master’s son/nang leh kei’ kikal-ah teci ~ ni | let us make it a witness between you and me) (s:suaksak) (b:hi) (r:1.30.34/1.24.51/19.104.4/1.31.44) (q:draft)
hisuak = (t:v) (w:become/come to be) (d:hi, be, with suak, become: come to be; ama a’ hisuak is become his own) (e:tua lo ama a’ ~ ding hi) (r:3.27.19) (q:draft)
hisuk = (t:v) (w:be down to/reach down to) (d:hi, be, with suk, downward: said of a boundary that runs down as far as a place) (e:Tamar khuapi ciang ~ ding hi) (r:26.47.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
hit = (t:see) <hit-hiat>
Hit = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Hittite/Heth) (d:people of Canaan descended from Heth; used before mi or mite, Hit mi is a Hittite and Hit mite are the Hittites) (e:~ mite in Abraham dawngin) (r:1.23.5/13.11.41) (q:draft)
hit-hiat = (t:adv) (w:still/quietly/calmly) (d:placed after a verb such as om, stay, dai, be quiet, or lum, lie: staying still, quiet and undisturbed) (e:Om ~ un la, Pasian ka hihna thei un/Guta mite nuam takin om ~ a | robbers live at ease, undisturbed/a daii ~-a a om naupang | a child that stays quiet and still/a cimawhte lungmuang takin lum ~ ding hi | the needy will lie down in safety/Sau veipi sung pau loin ka om ~ manin | because I have long kept silent) (s:hithiat/hiat/dide) (r:19.46.10/18.12.6/19.131.2/23.14.30/23.57.11) (q:draft)
hit-hit = (t:adv) (w:smoothly) (d:expressive word after tum suk go down, of wine going down the throat smoothly) (e:gawl sungah a tum suk ~ thei) (s:hithit) (r:20.23.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
hita = (t:conj) (w:whether/or) (d:hi, be, with ta, followed by leh and repeated after each choice: whether it is this or that, be it this or that) (e:pasal tawh a kibang ~ leh numei/a bawk ~ leh meima ~ leh | whether a swelling or a rash/Apha ~ leh asia ~ leh | whether it is good or evil/puan tung ~ leh inn sung ~ leh | whether on fabric or in a house/Ama' pa ~ leh, ama' nu ~ leh | whether his father or his mother) (b:hi) (r:5.4.16/3.14.56/21.12.14/3.14.55/2.21.15) (q:draft)
hita = (t:part) (d:hi, be, with ta, which shows that a state has now come about or is about to: ka hita hi, I now am; hita hen, let it be so) (e:Note a man na ~ uh hi/A si ding ka ~ hi | I am about to die/Na cih bang ~ hen | let it be as you say/silate’ sila ~ hen | let him be a slave of slaves) (b:hi) (r:26.7.6/1.25.32/2.10.29/1.9.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitaleh = (t:adv) (w:also) (d:hi, be, with ta and leh, repeated after each of two or more choices: both this and also that, whether this or that) (e:hun laitak ~ tua khit ~/A tanu a luplam ~ a thawhlam ~ | whether his daughter lay down or got up/Ama pa ~ ama nu ~ | whether his father or his mother) (r:1.6.4/1.19.35/2.21.15)
hitaleh = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:after one item or the last of several: even if it is, be it even, whatever it may be) (e:mihing nitna ~, mu loin a lawnkhak leh | even human uncleanness, if he touches it without seeing it/lupna ~ na khat peuhpeuh ~ | whether the bed or anything else) (r:3.5.3/3.15.23)
hitalehang = (t:conj) (w:though we are/even if we are) (d:hi be with ta, leh if and hang, the ending for we including the hearer: however we may be) (e:eite bangzahin ginalo ~) (r:45.8.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitaseleh = (t:conj) (w:although/even though/yet) (d:though it is so; after a statement it means although, and tua hitaseleh or tua bang hitaseleh opens a sentence as yet or nevertheless) (e:lampi tom pen ~/Tua bang ~ ama thu ngai-in amah a um | yet those who received his word and believed in him/Tua ~ amaute a daupaisak Pasian hi a | yet it was God who made them prosper/amau’ mawhna hangin a si ~ | though they die because of their own sin/bangbang ~ Khrih’ thu gen uh | however it may be, they preach Christ) (s:taseleh/hinapi/napi) (r:2.13.17/43.1.12/18.22.18/26.33.6/50.1.18) (q:draft)
hite = (t:pron) (w:these) (d:these, these ones, standing at the start of a sentence; a spelling of hihte) (e:~ tawh note a nin na suak/~ in Sinai Mual tungah | these, at Mount Sinai) (s:hihte) (r:3.11.24/4.3.1) (q:draft)
hite = (t:n) (w:those who are/what is so) (d:hi, be, with the plural te, used after a: those who are, the things that are; ka gal a hite is those who are my enemies) (e:Thuman lopi-a ka gal a ~ thahat a/kham a ~ kham mahin la-in | what was gold he took as gold/ngun a ~ a ngun mahin la hi | what was silver he took as silver/ka gal a ~ kei tungah lungdamsak kei in | do not let those who are my enemies gloat over me) (s:ahite) (b:hi) (r:19.38.19/40.5.37/12.25.15/19.35.19) (q:draft)
hithei = (t:v) (w:be possible/can be/may be) (d:hi, be, with thei, can: can be, may be, be possible; a hithei khat hileh means if it were possible) (e:Nuihna pen cihmawh seelna zong ~ a/Ngaihbaanna pen zuaupi ~ a | charm can be deceptive/A umte a dingin na khempeuh ~ | for those who believe everything is possible/cidam le-ung kum sawmgiat bang ~ hi | if we are strong it may be about eighty years) (s:piantheih/hikhathei) (b:hi) (r:20.14.13/48.4.20/20.31.30/41.9.23/19.90.10) (q:draft)
hithiat = (t:adv) (w:at ease/quietly/securely/still) (d:placed after a verb such as om or tu: staying calm and undisturbed, without care) (e:Thuman mite lungnuamin om ~ a/a gimte tawlnga ~ ding hi | the weary will be at rest/nuam takin ka om ~ ding hi | I would be at rest/na om ~ ding uh hi bek hi | you need only be still) (s:hit-hiat/hiat/dide/daitakin) (r:20.10.9/19.73.12/18.3.17/19.55.6/2.14.14) (q:draft)
hithiatin = (t:adv) (w:quietly/at rest/peacefully/still) (d:hithiat with the ending -in, after verbs such as lum, lie, and tu, sit: staying calmly in that position) (e:a tanu nuamtakin lum ~ a om/amaute lum ~ bangmah in lausak lo ding hi | they will lie down and nothing will make them afraid/Jakob ahihleh inn-ah om ~ | as for Jacob, staying quietly at home/Note hih laitakah om ~ | while you sit here at ease/damtakin tu ~ i thuakzo ding hi | sitting quietly in silence we will be able to bear it) (s:daitakin) (b:hithiat) (r:41.7.30/23.17.2/1.25.27/4.32.6/25.3.28) (q:draft)
hithiatna = (t:n) (w:calmness/quietness/ease) (d:noun form of hithiat: staying calm and quiet; also the place where people live at ease) (e:om ~ in khialhna lianpi maisak thei hi/nuam takin mite a om ~ Magog gam | the land of Magog where people live at ease/hoihtakin om ~, no tawh a kisai thu bek | living quietly and minding only your own business) (s:daihna) (b:hithiat) (r:21.10.4/26.39.6/52.4.11) (q:draft)
hithit = (t:adv) (w:smoothly) (d:describes how wine goes down the throat, smoothly and easily) (e:a tumsuk ~ thei leenggahzu) (s:hit-hit) (r:20.23.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
