hiuhiau = (t:adv) (w:strikingly/brightly) (d:placed after a describing word such as hoih, beautiful, or san, red, to picture a striking, shining look) (e:Lebanon tausang bangin hoih ~ hi/na samphekte san ~ a | your tresses shine red/sing suih siamte’ suih bang ~ hi | strikingly like the work of skilled carvers/Savun puanbuk bangin ka ang ~ a) (r:22.7.4/22.7.5/22.7.1/22.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hiv = (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Hivites/Hivite) (d:people of Canaan descended from Canaan son of Ham; used before mite, Hiv mite are the Hivites) (r:1.10.17)
hizah = (t:adv) (w:this many/so many/this much) (d:hi, this, with zah, amount: this many, as much as this; mi hizah tak is so many people as this) (e:mi ~ tak a tam lakah) (s:hihzah) (r:43.6.9) (q:draft)
hizaw = (t:v) (w:be rather/be instead) (d:hi, be, with zaw, rather or more: it is rather this than that, used in contrasts and in either-or questions) (e:a hong pia lo na ~ uh hi/Kei in zong ka ~ hi | I too am so, and more/Topa’ deihna bang bekin a piang ding ~ hi | rather it is only what the Lord wills that comes about/note’ hamphatna a kibehlap nading ka deihna ~ hi | rather what I desire is that your benefit be increased) (b:hi) (r:47.6.12/24.7.19/47.11.23/20.16.1/50.4.17) (q:draft)
