Hoih = (t:adj) (w:Beautiful) (d:hoih, good or beautiful, written with a capital in the name of a temple gate: Hoih Kongkhak or Kongpi Hoih, the Beautiful Gate) (e:~ Kongkhak kici gei-ah ni simin/biakna innpi ~ Kongkhak gei-ah khutdawh ngen-a om mipa | the man who sat begging at the temple gate called Beautiful/~ kicin’na, Zion panin, Pasian hong taangkhia hi | from Zion, perfect in beauty, God shines forth) (b:hoih) (r:44.3.2/44.3.10/19.50.2) (q:draft)
hoihah = (t:adj) (w:good) (d:hoih good with the place marker ah, which belongs to the whole phrase; leitang hoihah, in or into the good land) (e:hong piak leitang ~ ka lut loh nadingin/amaute tungah na piak gamzai lei ~ omin | living in the spacious good land you gave them/leitang ahi gam ~ note hong paipih hi | he brings you into the good land) (b:hoih) (r:5.4.21/5.11.17/16.9.35/5.8.9) (q:draft)
