Innah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imnah) (d:a Levite, father of Kore; apparently a misprint of Imnah) (e:Levi mi ~ tapa Kore in) (r:14.31.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
innbul = (t:n) (w:foundation) (d:inn, house, with bul, base: the base on which a building stands) (e:thong ~ zong liing a) (r:44.16.26/24.51.26) (q:draft)
inncin = (t:see) <inncin'na>
inncin'na = (t:n) (w:guarding/guard duty) (d:inncing guard with the noun suffix na; inncin’na inndei is the guardroom) (e:~ inndei sungah tuate koihkik zel) (r:11.14.28) (q:draft)
inncing = (t:n) (w:guard/palace guard/bodyguard) (d:one who guards a house or palace; inncing mangpa is the captain of the guard) (e:~ mangpa’ inn sungah) (r:1.40.3/14.12.10) (q:draft)
inncingte = (t:n) (w:guards) (d:plural of inncing) (e:~ in tuate pua-in) (b:inncing) (r:11.14.28) (q:draft)
inncinna = (t:n) (w:guarding/guard duty) (d:inncing guard with the noun suffix na; inncinna inndei is the guardroom) (e:~ inndei sungah tuate koihkik zel) (r:11.14.28) (q:draft)
inndap = (t:n) (w:ceiling/roofing) (d:the lining of boards over a room; inn house with dap, cover or line with boards) (e:taamtaak peekte tawh ~ bawl hi) (r:11.6.9/11.6.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
inndei = (t:n) (w:room/chamber) (d:a room or a section of a building) (e:Hih ~ golzaw a teh ciangin) (r:26.40.8/11.6.30) (q:draft)
inndeineu = (t:n) (w:small room) (d:inndei room with neu small) (e:kawm a nei ~ khat bawlin) (r:12.4.10) (q:draft)
inndeipi = (t:n) (w:main hall/portico/great room) (d:inndei room with pi great; in Ezekiel the large hall of the temple) (e:Hih ~ sung kawmte tungah) (b:inndei) (r:26.41.26/26.41.23) (q:draft)
inndeite = (t:n) (w:rooms/chambers/storerooms) (e:inn sung vankoihna ~ a uk dingin) (b:inndei) (r:16.13.4/11.6.29) (q:draft)
inndung = (t:n) (w:length of the building) (d:inn house with dung length) (e:hih ~ tong za khat hi a) (r:26.42.2) (q:draft)
inngualte = (t:n) (w:rows of rooms/rows of houses) (d:inn house with gual row and plural te: rooms or buildings standing in a row) (e:tua ~ tawh a paikhawm) (r:26.42.7) (q:draft)
innhikpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:chameleon)
innhikpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizard) (e:savokphual, zusa, ~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.29)
Innhikte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizards/lizard) (d:a small creature that can be held in the hand and yet lives in the palaces of kings; apparently innhik with the plural suffix te; the NIV has lizard and older versions spider) (e:~: khut sunga tawi zawh ganhing) (r:20.30.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkalte = (t:n) (w:beams/rafters) (d:plural with te; the timbers laid across a house to carry the ceiling or roof) (e:~ leh taamtaak peekte tawh inndap bawl) (r:11.6.9) (q:draft)
innkam = (t:n) (w:beam/rafter/timber) (d:a large beam of wood in the frame of a house) (e:a ~ khat kidawh khiatsakin) (r:15.6.11/11.7.2) (q:draft)
innkamte = (t:n) (w:beams/rafters/joists) (d:plural of innkam, a timber that carries the roof or floor of a house) (e:~ in zong kikopih ding uh hi) (b:innkam) (r:35.2.11/11.6.9) (q:draft)
innkhangte = (t:n) (w:neighbours below) (d:those whose houses are on the lower side of one's own; innsak and innkhang together are the neighbours on either side) (e:a innsak a ~’ kiangah) (r:24.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkhuam = (t:n) (w:pillar/post/foundation) (d:the post that carries a house; in the letters used for the foundation of a building) (e:Zeisu Khazih longal ~ dang kuamah in) (r:46.3.11/26.26.11) (q:draft)
innkhuampi = (t:n) (w:pillar/main pillar) (d:innkhuam house post with pi, great) (e:a ~ sagih a phut hi) (b:innkhuam) (r:20.9.1) (q:draft)
innkhuamte = (t:n) (w:pillars/supports/posts) (e:Topa’ biakinn le kumpipa’ ~) (b:innkhuam) (r:11.10.12) (q:draft)
innkhum = (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the top of a house; innkhum zang is the flat roof or an upper room) (e:~ tungah a omte in zong) (r:40.24.17/19.102.7) (q:draft)
innkhumdawn = (t:n) (w:rooftop/housetop/roof) (d:the top of the roof of a house) (e:~ zangah na taangko un) (r:40.10.27) (q:draft)
innkhumzang = (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the flat top of a house, where people can walk or stay) (e:~ kiu khat-a tang teen’ hoihzaw) (r:20.21.9/6.2.8) (q:draft)
innkhumzanga = (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop) (d:innkhumzang, roof, with the place marker a) (e:~ lopate bangin a om laitak) (b:innkhumzang) (r:12.19.26/9.9.26) (q:draft)
innkhumzangah = (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop/to the roof) (d:innkhumzang, the flat roof of a house, with the place ending -ah) (e:~ Peter a kahto hi) (b:innkhumzang) (r:44.10.9/10.16.22) (q:draft)
innkiim = (t:see) <innkiim-ah>
innkiim-ah = (t:adv) (w:around the house) (d:innkiim, the surroundings of a house, with ah, at) (e:kote’ omna ~ hong pang uh hi) (r:7.20.5) (q:draft)
innkim = (t:n) (w:surroundings of the house) (d:the area all around a house, here the temple; probably the same word as innkiim) (e:biakna tau leh ~ ah koih hi) (r:14.23.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkiu = (t:n) (w:corner of a house) (d:inn house with kiu corner; innkiu suang is the cornerstone) (e:~ suang bulpi suak khin ta hi) (r:19.118.22/41.12.10) (q:draft)
innkiunuai = (t:n) (w:cornerstone/foundation of the corner) (d:inn house, kiu corner, nuai under; innkiunuai suang is the cornerstone) (e:Khazih in tua ~ suang ahi hi) (r:49.2.20) (q:draft)
innkongah = (t:adv) (w:at the doorway/to the door of the house) (d:innkong, the doorway of a house, with ah, at or to) (e:innsung panin ~ siampipa paikhia ding a) (r:3.14.38) (q:draft)
innkuan = (t:n) (w:family) (e:~ ciat tawh ahi) (r:2.1.1)
innkuan = (t:n) (w:household) (e:~ ading cik ciangin) (r:1.30.30/1.20.18)
innkuanin = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by households) (d:innkuan family with in; repeated as innkuan innkuanin, one family after another) (e:a innkuan ~ hong pai ding hi) (b:innkuan) (r:6.7.14) (q:draft)
innkuankuan = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families) (d:innkuan family doubled, each family in turn) (e:a ~ leh a beh beh-in) (r:4.4.42/4.1.2) (q:draft)
innkuankuanin = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families/by clans) (d:innkuankuan, each family in turn, with -in) (e:a beh tawh kizui-in a ~) (b:innkuankuan) (r:4.2.34/4.3.15) (q:draft)
innkuankuanun = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by their families) (d:innkuankuan with un, the plural marker uh joined with in) (e:Mite a ~ a milipin) (b:innkuankuan) (r:4.11.10/4.3.39) (q:draft)
innkuanmi = (t:n) (w:household members/people of the household) (d:innkuan household with mi, person) (e:a ne ding ~ a tawmluat leh) (b:innkuan) (r:2.12.4) (q:draft)
innkuanpih = (t:n) (w:family) (e:tu-a kipanin ~ nga a om) (r:42.12.52/10.2.3)
innkuanpih = (t:n) (w:relative)
innkuanpihte = (t:n) (w:families) (e:i pa leh na ~ uh la un) (b:innkuanpih) (r:1.45.18)
innkuanpite = (t:n) (w:household/whole family/family members) (d:all the members of a household; Genesis 46:31 has innkuanpite and innkuanpihte side by side for the same thing, so probably innkuanpih, family member, with plural -te) (e:nang leh na ~ leh na neih khempeuh) (b:innkuan) (r:1.45.11/5.11.6) (q:draft)
innkuansung = (t:n) (w:household/family) (d:those within one house and family) (e:a tate le a ~ hoihtakin a ukzote) (r:54.3.12/20.31.27) (q:draft)
innkuante = (t:n) (w:household/family/house) (d:the members of a family or household) (e:Aaron ~ in ci ta uh hen) (b:innkuan) (r:19.118.3/55.4.19) (q:draft)
innlak = (t:n) (w:relative/kin) (d:of the father's family; innlak pa is an uncle, innlak nu an aunt, innlak sanggampa a cousin) (e:ka ~ sanggampa Hanamel tawh) (r:24.32.12/3.25.49) (q:draft, low confidence)
innlam = (t:n) (w:building/house-building) (d:the building of houses, also of ships; innlam siamte are skilled builders) (e:lei-le-suang ~ siamte zong puak hi) (r:10.5.11/44.4.11) (q:draft)
innlam = (t:n) (w:way home) (d:the direction of one's house) (e:a ~ zon’na in gim ding uh) (r:21.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
innlamna = (t:n) (w:house-building/construction) (d:innlam building of houses, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ panin a meet i ngah ding) (b:innlam) (r:26.11.3) (q:draft)
innlamte = (t:n) (w:builders) (d:those who build houses, plural) (e:khutsiamte leh ~ tungah pia uh hi) (b:innlam) (r:14.34.11/12.22.6) (q:draft)
innlelo = (t:n) (w:home/homestead/house and land) (d:inn house, le and, lo field written as one word: a home of one's own with its land; innlelo nei lo is homeless) (e:a tenna ding ~ guan a) (r:19.68.6/25.3.19) (q:draft)
innliim = (t:n) (w:portico/porch/colonnade) (d:the roofed porch at the front of a building, in the verses that of the temple; also spelled innlim) (e:Inn mai-a ~ in inn vai tawh) (r:14.3.4/43.10.23) (q:draft)
innlim = (t:n) (w:portico/porch) (d:the roofed porch at the front of a building, in the verses that of the temple; also spelled innliim) (e:~ kongkhakte zong khakin) (r:14.29.7/11.6.3) (q:draft)
innlimah = (t:adv) (w:at the portico/to the portico) (d:innlim portico with the place marker ah) (e:biakinn ~ khuampite a phut hi) (b:innlim) (r:11.7.21/14.29.17) (q:draft)
innluah = (t:v) (w:inherit/be heir) (d:take over the house and property of the family; innluah mi, heir; innluah za, the right of the heir) (e:thuciamna bangin ~ mi na hi uh hi) (r:48.3.29/48.4.30) (q:draft)
innluahna = (t:n) (w:inheritance) (d:innluah inherit, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ in thukham tawh kipawl ahih leh) (b:innluah) (r:48.3.18) (q:draft)
innluahpa = (t:n) (w:heir) (d:innluah, inherit the house, with pa, a man: the son who inherits) (e:Pasian hangin ~ zong na hi uh hi) (b:innluah) (r:48.4.7/48.4.1) (q:draft)
innluahza = (t:n) (w:birthright/right of the firstborn) (d:the right to inherit the house, from inn house and luah inherit) (e:Na ~ hong pia lecin) (r:1.25.31/13.5.2) (q:draft)
innmong = (t:n) (w:end of the house) (d:inn house with mong, end or edge) (e:Eliashib’ ~ ciang dong) (r:16.3.21) (q:draft)
innpi = (t:n) (w:temple/great house/hall) (d:literally big house; biakna innpi is the temple) (e:Biakna ~ dalna puan) (b:inn) (r:42.23.45/58.10.21) (q:draft)
innpite = (t:n) (w:palaces/great houses) (d:innpi, a great house such as a palace or temple, with plural te) (e:Saiha tawh kibawl ~ panin) (b:innpi) (r:19.45.8/7.16.26) (q:draft)
innpua = (t:see) <innpua-ah>
innpua-ah = (t:adv) (w:outside/outside the house) (d:innpua, the outside of a house, with ah, at) (e:~ om uh hi) (r:42.8.20) (q:draft)
innsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:livestock) (e:~, gamsa, leh a bokvak ganhingte) (r:1.1.24/1.7.14)
innsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:pet)
innsak = (t:n) (w:neighbour above) (d:the house or people on the upper side of one's own; innsak and innkhang together are the neighbours on either side) (e:a ~ a innkhangte’ kiangah) (b:inn) (r:24.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
innsate = (t:n) (w:livestock/cattle/domestic animals) (d:innsa, animal kept at the house, with plural -te; set against gamsate, the wild animals) (e:Gamsate leh ~ khempeuh) (b:innsa) (r:19.148.10/1.7.21) (q:draft)
innsia = (t:n) (w:ruins/ruined house) (d:inn, house, with sia, spoiled: houses fallen into ruin; innsia losia is ruined houses and fields, a heap of ruins) (e:~ lakah a om ngiate tawh) (r:26.13.4/24.51.37) (q:draft)
innsualte = (t:n) (w:floors) (d:the floors of the rooms of a house) (e:inndei sung ~ amah in kham tawh) (r:11.6.30) (q:draft)
innsun = (t:n) (w:ceiling/ceiling beam/rafter) (d:the top of a room or the beams there; sual panin innsun dong, from floor to ceiling) (e:Amah in sual panin ~ dong) (r:11.6.16/11.7.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
innsung = (t:n) (w:household/family/home) (d:literally inside the house) (e:numei haite in ~ susia hi) (r:20.14.1/20.15.27) (q:draft)
innsunga = (t:adv) (w:in the house/in the household) (d:innsung, the inside of a house or a household, with the place ending a; innsunga om, who or which is in the house) (e:a ~ om mi khempeuh tui kiphum) (b:innsung) (r:44.16.15/12.20.17) (q:draft)
Innsungah = (t:adv) (w:into the house/in the house/indoors) (d:innsung, the inside of the house, with the place marker ah, here at the start of a sentence) (e:~ Jesuh a tumkhit ciangin) (r:41.9.28/41.10.10) (q:draft)
innsungmang = (t:n) (w:court official/eunuch/palace officer) (d:an official who serves inside the royal house, in the Bible often a eunuch) (e:kumpipa’ ~ Hegai’ kep dingin) (r:17.2.3/27.1.3) (q:draft)
innsungmangte = (t:n) (w:court officials/eunuchs/attendants) (e:kumpipa’ ~ hong pai a) (b:innsungmang) (r:17.6.14/17.1.12) (q:draft)
innsunte = (t:n) (w:ceiling beams/rafters) (e:a ~, a sangkilte, a kawmte) (b:innsun) (r:14.3.7/11.6.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
innte = (t:n) (w:houses/buildings) (e:kulhpi siate puah nadingin ~ na phel hi) (b:inn) (r:23.22.10/16.7.4) (q:draft)
innteek = (t:n) (w:house owner/householder/master of the house) (d:the person to whom a house belongs; innteek pa is the man who owns the house, also the master for whom someone works) (e:a ~ pa kiangah) (r:42.22.11/42.14.21) (q:draft)
inntual = (t:n) (w:courtyard/court) (d:the open space in front of or enclosed by a house) (e:~ lai zangah mei cih uh a) (r:42.22.55/41.14.66) (q:draft)
inntualah = (t:adv) (w:in the courtyard/into the courtyard) (d:inntual courtyard, the open space before a house, with the place marker ah) (e:Piter ~ a tut lai takin) (b:inntual) (r:40.26.69/41.15.16) (q:draft)
inntualte = (t:n) (w:courts/courtyards) (d:inntual, courtyard, with plural te) (e:Ka inn leh ka ~ a bawl dingpa) (b:inntual) (r:13.28.6/13.23.28) (q:draft)
inntuan = (t:v) (w:divide the inheritance/give a share of the property) (d:literally set up a separate house; give a brother his share of the family property) (e:kei hong ~ nadingin hong gensak in) (r:42.12.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
innveng = (t:n) (w:neighbourhood/neighbour) (d:the houses near one's own and those who live there) (e:Mikah’ ~ a om mite) (r:7.18.22) (q:draft)
innvengte = (t:n) (w:neighbors) (d:plural of innveng: people who live in the houses nearby) (e:a ~’ zite mawhpih uh a) (b:innveng) (r:24.29.23/24.9.8) (q:draft)
innzom = (t:n) (w:next door/adjoining house) (d:inn house with zom, join; innzom a vengte are the nearest neighbours) (e:amau’ ~ a vengte tawh) (r:2.12.4) (q:draft)
insek = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:insect) (d:apparently the English word insect; insek ganhing, insect creatures, of small winged creatures) (e:Kha a nei ~ ganhing khempeuh) (r:5.14.19/5.14.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
Iob = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jashub) (r:1.46.13)
ip = (t:n) (w:bag/purse/sack) (e:Na ~ sung uhah tawisuang nam nih) (r:5.25.13/12.12.10) (q:draft)
ip = (t:v) (w:hold back/restrain/keep in/conceal) (d:hold in, as words or anger, or keep a matter hidden; pau ip, to hold the tongue) (e:pau ~ theite mipil hi) (r:20.10.19/20.25.2) (q:draft)
ipbawl = (t:v) (w:hold back/conceal/keep to oneself) (d:ip hold in or conceal, with bawl, do) (e:na ~ loin a siangtakin na genkhia) (b:ip) (r:43.1.20) (q:draft)
ipcip = (t:v) (w:keep hidden/hold back/shut up) (d:ip hold in or conceal with cip, tightly; ki-ipcip, hold oneself back) (e:selcipin ~ ding ahi hi) (b:ip) (r:27.12.9/46.2.7) (q:draft)
