khawi = (t:v) (w:spare/keep alive/let live) (d:keep and not kill, often as hing khawi, keep alive; in Ecclesiastes 3:3 it is the opposite of killing) (e:Numei aisannu na hing ~ kei ding uh) (r:2.22.18/12.10.14) (q:draft)
khawi = (t:v) (w:keep/rear) (d:keep and look after an animal or a person in one's charge: vasa khawi is a pet bird, sila-in khawi is keep as a slave; in Numbers 6:5 of letting the hair grow long) (e:vasa ~ bangin bawl zong ding) (r:18.41.5/24.34.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawikik = (t:v) (w:keep again/take back) (d:khawi keep, with kik, again; sila-in khawikik, keep as a slave again) (e:sila-in ~ thei nawn lo ding hi) (b:khawi) (r:24.34.10) (q:draft)
khawilevulh = (t:n) (w:nurture/rearing) (d:khawi rear, le and, vulh feed: the rearing and feeding of young; the English has blessings of the breast and womb) (e:~ le tuletate) (r:1.49.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawilo = (t:v) (w:not spare) (d:khawi, keep alive, with lo, not; hin’ khawilo, did not keep alive) (e:kuamah hin’ ~ a) (b:khawi) (r:19.78.50) (q:draft)
khawipa = (t:n) (w:breeder/keeper) (d:khawi, keep or rear, with pa marking a man; tuu khawipa is a man who raises sheep) (e:Mesha in tuu ~ ahi hi) (b:khawi) (r:12.3.4) (q:draft)
khawite = (t:n) (w:domestic animals/livestock/pets) (d:khawi, rear or keep animals, with plural -te: animals that are kept; gan khawite is livestock and ui khawite are house dogs) (e:na gan ~ ka that khin ding hi) (b:khawi) (r:26.32.13/40.15.27) (q:draft)
khawk = (t:n) (w:section/portion/plot/column) (d:one marked-off part of something longer or larger, as a stretch of wall, a plot of land or a column of writing) (e:~ dang khat sung puah uh hi) (r:16.3.11/24.36.23) (q:draft)
khawkte = (t:n) (w:sections/panels/compartments) (d:plural of khawk, a section or enclosed part; tuu-khawkte are sheep pens) (e:tuate in a ~ nei-in) (b:khawk) (r:11.7.28/4.32.36) (q:draft)
khawl = (t:v) (w:accompany)
khawlcip = (t:v) (w:stand still/stop completely/come to a standstill) (d:khawl stop, rest with cip firmly) (e:tuipi ~ thei lo a) (b:khawl) (r:23.57.20/15.4.24) (q:draft)
khawlei = (t:n) (d:see <khawlei-uikai>) (e:~ uikai a pai nading lampi) (r:18.38.32)
Khawlei = (t:n) (c:star) (w:the Bear) (d:first part of Khawlei-uikai, the constellation of the Bear, also written as two words) (e:~ uikai a pai nading lampi) (b:khawlei) (r:18.38.32/18.9.9) (q:draft)
khawlei uikai = (t:n) (d:see <khawlei-uikai>)
khawlei-uikai = (t:n) (w:the Bear)
khawlin = (t:v) (w:stop/cease/turn from) (d:khawl with the ending -in: stopping, leaving off, before the next action) (e:tawlkhat ~ ngai in la) (b:khawl) (r:18.37.14/11.15.21) (q:draft)
khawlmun = (t:n) (w:haven/resting place/harbour) (d:khawl stop or rest, with mun place; teembaw khawlmun is a place where ships stop) (e:amah in teembaw ~ suak ding a) (r:1.49.13) (q:draft)
Khawlmun = (t:n) (w:haven/resting place/lodging place) (d:khawlmun, a place to stop and rest, capitalised in place names: Khawlmun Nuam, Fair Havens; Khimham Khawlmun, Geruth Kimham) (e:Lasia khua tawh kinai ~ Nuam kici mun) (b:khawlmun) (r:44.27.8/24.41.17) (q:draft)
khawlmunte = (t:n) (w:harbours/resting places) (d:khawlmun, a place to stop and rest, with the plural te; of ships, a harbour) (e:~ om nawn lo ahih manin) (b:khawlmun) (r:23.23.1) (q:draft)
khawlna = (t:n) (w:rest/resting place/stopping place/harbour) (d:place or act of stopping to rest; teembaw khawlna is a harbour for ships) (e:Krete gam teembaw ~ mun hi a) (b:khawl) (r:44.27.12/20.26.2) (q:draft)
khawlpah = (t:v) (w:stop at once/stop immediately) (d:khawl stop with pah, at once) (e:si puate zong a ~ uh hi) (r:42.7.14/41.5.29) (q:draft)
khawlpak = (t:v) (w:stop/break off) (d:khawl stop, with pak, for a while or promptly: leave off a quarrel) (e:a nasiat ma-in kitot ~ in) (r:20.17.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawlsak = (t:v) (w:stop/halt/detain) (d:make someone or something stop or rest; khawl with sak, cause) (e:Mangpa in leeng ~ a) (b:khawl) (r:44.8.38/18.37.7) (q:draft)
khawlsakin = (t:v) (w:stopping/making rest) (d:khawlsak, make stop or rest, with the linking suffix in) (e:amah in a puate tawlkhat ~) (b:khawlsak) (r:10.6.13/27.8.11) (q:draft)
khawlsakna = (t:n) (w:stopping) (d:khawlsak make stop, with the noun suffix na; teembaw khawlsakna sikkawipi, the iron hook for stopping a ship, is an anchor) (e:teembaw ~ sikkawipi li khiasuk uh a) (b:khawlsak) (r:44.27.29) (q:draft)
khawm = (t:adv) (w:along/together/side by side) (e:ama min pahtawi ~ ni) (r:19.34.3/5.22.11)
khawma = (t:adv) (w:together) (d:khawm with the linking a; ding khawma om, be standing together with) (e:amaute tawh ding ~ om a muh uh ciangin) (b:khawm) (r:44.4.14) (q:draft)
khawmin = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/bring together) (d:verb khawm with the linking suffix in, gathering people before a following action) (e:Jehu in mi khempeuh ~ amaute kiangah) (b:khawm) (r:12.10.18/2.35.1) (q:draft)
khawmin = (t:adv) (w:together) (d:after another verb, doing it together with others) (e:mite tawh kei kap ~) (b:khawm) (r:18.30.25) (q:draft)
khawmkhawm = (t:v) (w:gather/gather together) (d:khawm, bring together, said twice: keep gathering; set against kithehthangsak, scatter) (e:Keimah tawh a ~ lote in) (b:khawm) (r:40.12.30/42.11.23) (q:draft)
khawmkik = (t:v) (w:gather again/gather up/collect) (d:khawm gather with kik, again or back) (e:a khamvalte uh ~ uh a) (b:khawm) (r:40.14.20/10.6.1) (q:draft)
khawmkikin = (t:v) (w:gather again/gather back) (d:khawmkik with the linking suffix in) (e:Amaute ka thehthangna gam panin ~) (b:khawmkik) (r:26.11.17) (q:draft)
khawmluzepna = (t:n) (w:capital) (d:the ornamental top of a pillar; apparently another spelling of khuamluzepna, which stands in the same verse) (e:lu dawnah a om ~ nihte) (r:14.4.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawmna = (t:n) (w:togetherness/fellowship) (d:khawm, together, with the noun suffix na, after a verb: the doing of something together, as kipawl khawmna, fellowship, and gamtat khawmna, acting together) (e:kipawl ~, khomun balnenna leh thungetna) (b:khawm) (r:44.2.42/9.10.11) (q:draft)
khawmnate = (t:n) (w:meetings/gatherings) (d:khawmna, doing together, with the plural te; kikhop khawmnate are the meetings together) (e:eite in kikhop ~ pelh loin om ni) (b:khawmna) (r:58.10.25) (q:draft)
khawmpa = (t:n) (w:fellow/companion/co-worker) (d:khawm together with pa, the man: after a verb, the man who does it together with someone; nasem khawmpa is a fellow worker) (e:kei tawh nasem ~ lang pang in) (b:khawm) (r:38.13.7/45.16.9) (q:draft)
khawmpih = (t:adv) (w:together with/along with/fellow) (d:khawm, together, with pih, with someone: after a verb, do it together with someone or share in it; after a noun, a fellow, as in galkap khawmpih fellow soldier) (e:Ankuang ka sawk ~ pa in) (b:khawm) (r:40.26.23/57.1.2) (q:draft)
khawmpihpa = (t:n) (w:one who shares with/fellow) (d:khawmpih, do together with someone, with pa, the man: the man with whom one does it, as the one who dips in the dish with me) (e:kei tawh ankuang ka sawk ~ ahi hi) (b:khawmpih) (r:41.14.20/40.26.23) (q:draft)
khawmpihte = (t:n) (w:companions/those together with) (d:khawmpih, do together with someone, with the plural te: the people with whom one does it; a tut khawmpihte, those who sat at table with him, his guests) (e:a tut ~ a zahtak manin) (b:khawmpih) (r:40.14.9/41.6.26) (q:draft)
khawmsa = (t:adj) (w:already together) (d:khawm, together, with sa, already done; lum khawmsa is having lain together with someone) (e:pasal tawh a lum ~ numei khempeuh) (b:khawm) (r:7.21.11) (q:draft)
khawmsak = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/bring together) (e:Israel mite leh kamsangte ~ hi) (b:khawm) (r:11.18.20) (q:draft)
khawmsak = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: cause or allow someone to do the action together with others) (e:gamh luah ~ hi) (b:khawm) (r:18.42.15/47.4.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawmsate = (t:n) (w:those joined together) (d:khawmsa, already together, with the plural te; a gawm khawmsate are those who have been joined together) (e:Pasian in a gawm ~ mite in) (b:khawmsa) (r:40.19.6) (q:draft)
khawmte = (t:n) (w:those together with/companions/fellow) (d:khawm, together, with plural -te, placed after a verb: the people who do the action together, as an ne khawmte, those eating together) (e:Amah tawh an ne ~ in) (b:khawm) (r:42.7.49/58.3.14) (q:draft)
