kiang = (t:n) (w:presence/side) (d:the place beside or with someone, mostly in kiangah to and kiang panin from) (e:Topa ~ panin kha gilo in) (r:9.16.14/44.17.33) (q:draft)
kianga = (t:prep) (w:to/with/near/beside) (d:kiang with the suffix a, used where the phrase describes a following noun or verb, as in pasian kianga thu nget, praying to God, and a kianga ding, standing beside him) (e:pasian ~ thu a nget a mu) (b:kiang) (r:27.6.11/43.18.22) (q:draft)
kiangah = (t:prep) (w:to) (e:Pasian ~ ngen in) (b:kiang) (r:2.6.10/5.2.17)
