kiangpan = (t:prep) (w:from) (d:from a person, from someone's presence; kiang with pan, more often written kiang panin) (e:Pasian ~ hong kipia Kha i ngah zo hi) (r:46.2.12/18.3.19) (q:draft)
kiangpanin = (t:prep) (w:from/away from) (d:from a person or from someone's presence; kiangpan with the suffix in) (e:Absalom’ ~ ka tai lai-in) (b:kiangpan) (r:11.2.7) (q:draft)
kiasak = (t:v) (w:cause to fall/bring down/send down/drop) (d:kia fall with causative sak) (e:kumpi tokhom tung pan ~ a) (b:kia) (r:42.1.52/2.9.18) (q:draft)
kiasakin = (t:v) (w:sending down/causing to fall) (d:kiasak cause to fall with the linking ending in) (e:vantung panin mei ~ tua mite) (b:kiasak) (r:42.9.54/26.13.13) (q:draft)
kiasuk = (t:v) (w:fall down/sink/go down/descend) (d:kia fall with suk downward) (e:a thukna sungah amaute ~ uh hi) (b:kia) (r:2.15.5/19.104.8) (q:draft)
kiasukin = (t:v) (w:falling down) (d:kiasuk fall down with the linking suffix in) (e:meikuang bangin hong ~ gunte le) (b:kiasuk) (r:66.8.10) (q:draft)
kiat = (t:v) (w:fall) (d:form of kia used before leh, ciangin and other endings) (e:leibeel khatpeuh peuh sungah a ~ leh) (b:kia) (r:3.11.33/20.23.27) (q:draft)
kiat = (t:v) (w:lose heart/falter/faint) (d:with lung, heart: lung a kiat, the heart falls, one is discouraged or grows faint) (e:na lung a ~ leh) (b:kia) (r:20.24.10/32.2.7) (q:draft)
kiat = (t:v) (w:shave/scrape/shave off) (d:cut hair off close with a blade, or scrape a surface; kiat khia, shave off or scrape away) (e:khamul nawlhui zong ~ loin) (r:3.21.5/26.5.1) (q:draft)
kiate = (t:n) (w:those that fall/fallen ones) (d:kia fall with the plural te: things that have fallen, as seed or crumbs) (e:Ling lakah a ~ in) (b:kia) (r:41.4.18/40.15.27) (q:draft)
