kiguk = (t:v) (w:be stolen) (d:form of kigu be stolen, used before leh if) (e:inn panin a ~ leh) (b:kigu) (r:2.22.7) (q:draft)
kigukhia = (t:v) (w:be stolen away/be kidnapped/be carried off) (d:passive ki with gukhia steal away) (e:gam panin kei hong ~ a) (b:gukhia) (r:1.40.15) (q:draft)
kiguksak = (t:v) (w:be stolen from/be robbed of) (d:passive ki with guk steal and sak: have something stolen from one) (e:hong ~ lai-in a gu pa) (r:7.17.2) (q:draft)
kigum = (t:v) (w:save oneself) (d:often with pumpi body, save your own self) (e:na pumpi ~ in) (b:gum) (r:42.23.37/41.15.30) (q:draft)
kigumkhia = (t:v) (w:save oneself/rescue oneself) (d:gumkhia rescue with the reflexive ki) (e:mite lak panin ~ un) (b:gumkhia) (r:44.2.40/23.63.5) (q:draft)
kih = (t:v) (w:abhor/detest/loathe) (d:feel strong dislike or disgust for someone or something) (e:ama luah minamte a ~ hi) (r:19.106.40/3.26.11) (q:draft)
kihaamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/object of cursing) (d:a person or place that people name when they curse, another spelling of kihamsiatna) (e:mite’ ~ suakin kuamah teeng nawn lo hi) (b:haamsiatna) (r:24.44.22/24.26.6) (q:draft)
kihah = (t:v) (w:be tended/be pruned/be dressed) (d:of vines; a kihah lo leenggui is a vine left untended) (e:a ~ lo leengguite panin zong) (b:hah) (r:3.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
