kikhennate = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:plural of kikhenna: the groups into which the priests were divided for their service) (e:siampite a pawlpawlin a ~) (b:kikhenna) (r:14.8.14) (q:draft)
kikhensa = (t:adj) (w:divorced/separated) (d:kikhen, separate, with sa, already done; pasal tawh a kikhensa numei, a woman divorced from her husband) (e:Pasal tawh a ~ numei) (b:kikhen) (r:42.16.18) (q:draft)
kikhensak = (t:v) (w:separated) (e:mite in ~ kei uh hen) (b:kikhen) (r:1.1.6/41.10.9)
