kilakna = (t:n) (w:appearance/appearing/showing oneself) (e:a nungzuite kiangah thumvei a ~ ahi hi) (b:kilak) (r:43.21.14/42.24.35) (q:draft)
kilakna = (t:n) (w:taking/charging) (d:the act of something being taken; leiba ameet kilakna, the charging of interest on a debt) (e:Leiba ameet ~ phiat ni) (b:kilak) (r:16.5.10/3.16.27) (q:draft)
kilaksa = (t:v) (w:shown/have been shown) (d:kilak, be shown, with sa for a completed action; hong kilaksa bangin, as it was shown to you) (e:nang tungah hong ~ bangin kibawl ding hi) (b:kilak) (r:2.27.8) (q:draft)
kilaksak = (t:v) (w:be robbed of/be deprived of/be taken from) (d:have something taken away; passive of laksak) (e:A no a ~ vompi bangin) (b:laksak) (r:28.13.8/20.20.16) (q:draft)
kilaksakmang = (t:v) (w:be carried off/be taken away) (d:be caused to be taken away, of herds taken as plunder) (e:a bawnghonte uh ~ ding hi) (b:laksakmang) (r:24.49.32) (q:draft)
kilaktawm = (t:v) (w:present oneself/show oneself) (d:go and show oneself to someone of one's own accord) (e:Ahab kiangah amah a ~ dingin Elijah) (r:11.18.2) (q:draft)
kilaktoh = (t:v) (w:be taken up/be lifted up) (d:be taken upward, used of Jesus being taken up to heaven) (e:a tunglam a ~ ni dong) (b:kilak) (r:44.1.2/42.9.51) (q:draft)
kilam = (t:v) (w:be built/be set up) (d:passive form of lam build) (e:Pilna tawh inn ~ a) (b:lam) (r:20.24.3/2.40.17) (q:draft)
