kilehdo = (t:v) (w:contend with/strive against/rebel against) (d:lehdo, rebel, with the prefix ki; used with tawh) (e:beelseek pa tawh a ~ lei beel) (b:lehdo) (r:23.45.9) (q:draft)
kilehhawl = (t:v) (w:be driven back/be routed) (d:of soldiers beaten and forced to turn back) (e:A galkapte uh ~ a) (r:24.46.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilehheek = (t:v) (w:be betrayed/be handed over) (d:lehheek, betray, with the passive prefix ki) (e:migilote’ khut sungah ~ zo hi) (b:lehheek) (r:41.14.41) (q:draft)
kilehhei = (t:v) (w:turn around/turn back/turn about) (d:often followed by kik, back) (e:Israel mite hong ~ uh a) (b:lehhei) (r:7.20.41/14.18.32) (q:draft)
kilehhek = (t:v) (w:be betrayed/betray one another) (d:lehhek, betray, with the prefix ki: be betrayed, or with khatlekhat, betray each other) (e:Topa Jesuh a ~ ding nitakin) (b:lehhek) (r:46.11.23/40.24.10) (q:draft)
kilehin = (t:v) (w:return/turn back) (d:kileh, turn back, with the linking ending in: going back and then) (e:~ Jordan gunpang ah ding hi) (b:kileh) (r:12.2.13) (q:draft)
kilehkik = (t:v) (w:return/turn back/come back) (d:kileh with kik, back or again; also of turning back to God) (e:Amah hong ~ nawn kei ding a) (b:kileh) (r:24.22.11/24.4.1) (q:draft)
kilehkiksak = (t:v) (w:make turn back/cause to withdraw) (d:kilehkik, turn back, with the causative sak) (e:amah ~ thei kha ding hi) (b:kilehkik) (r:24.21.2) (q:draft)
kilehngat = (t:v) (w:turn away from/be opposed to/be contrary) (d:face the opposite way from someone or something, used with tawh) (e:Topa tawh a lungsim a ~ mi in) (b:lehngat) (r:24.17.5/48.3.21) (q:draft)
kilehngatin = (t:adv) (w:contrary/in opposition/hostilely) (d:facing against someone, used with tawh and pai: walk contrary to, be hostile toward) (e:kei tawh ~ na pai lai uh leh) (b:kilehngat) (r:3.26.27/3.26.24) (q:draft)
kilehsuk = (t:v) (w:rush back and forth/go to and fro) (d:kileh, go back and forth, with suk, down; paired with kilehto) (e:kongzing lakah ~ kilehto uh a) (b:kileh) (r:34.2.4) (q:draft)
kilehto = (t:v) (w:rush back and forth/go to and fro) (d:kileh, go back and forth, with to, up; paired with kilehsuk) (e:lakah kilehsuk ~ uh a) (b:kileh) (r:34.2.4) (q:draft)
kilei = (t:v) (w:be bought/be purchased) (d:lei buy with ki, passive) (e:kham tawh a ~ zo hi lo a) (b:lei) (r:18.28.15/46.7.23) (q:draft)
kileikik = (t:v) (w:be bought again) (d:kilei, be bought, with kik, again) (e:hih gamah lo ~ ta ding hi) (b:kilei) (r:24.32.43) (q:draft)
kileina = (t:n) (w:purchase/buying) (d:kileina lai is a deed of purchase; a kileina-pa is the man from whom a thing was bought) (e:Baruk kiangah ~ lai ka piak khit ciangin) (b:kilei) (r:24.32.16/24.32.12) (q:draft)
kileinapa = (t:n) (w:seller) (d:the man from whom a thing was bought; kileina, purchase, with pa, the male one) (e:a lo pen a ~) (b:kileina) (r:3.27.24) (q:draft)
kileipa = (t:n) (w:bought slave/one who is bought) (d:kilei, be bought, with pa marking a man: a man bought with money, set beside one born in the household) (e:na sum tawh a ~ hita leh) (b:kilei) (r:1.17.13) (q:draft)
kileitawi = (t:v) (w:lend to one another) (d:leitawi, loan, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:ngahkik dingin khatlekhat ~ uh hi) (b:leitawi) (r:42.6.34) (q:draft)
kileizo = (t:v) (w:can be bought/be able to be bought) (d:kilei be bought with zo, be able; used with hi lo for what cannot be bought) (e:kham tawh a ~ hi lo a) (b:kilei) (r:18.28.15/18.28.16) (q:draft)
kilelsak = (t:v) (w:let oneself be defeated/pretend to be beaten) (d:lel, be defeated, with the prefix ki and causative sak; with khem, deceive: act as if beaten) (e:amau mai-ah ~ khem uh a) (b:lelsak) (r:6.8.15/6.8.20) (q:draft)
kilem = (t:v) (w:be at peace/be reconciled/make peace) (d:be on good terms with one another, used with tawh for the other party) (e:mi khempeuh tawh na ~ un) (r:45.12.18/40.5.24) (q:draft)
kilemin = (t:v) (w:be at peace/be reconciled) (d:kilem with the linking ending in: being at peace or reconciled with someone) (e:khat leh khat ~ om un) (b:kilem) (r:41.9.50/46.7.11) (q:draft)
kilemkik = (t:v) (w:be reconciled/be at peace again) (d:kilem, be at peace, with kik, again or back; used with tawh) (e:amah tawh ~ theih nading hong omsak) (b:kilem) (r:51.1.20/45.5.1) (q:draft)
kilemkim = (t:v) (w:be in harmony together/agree all alike) (d:of the parts of the body all being at one with each other; the English has have equal concern for each other) (e:a vekpi-in a ~ uh hi) (r:46.12.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilemlo = (t:v) (w:be at odds/not be at peace/oppose) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the negative lo; used with tawh) (e:migilote tawh ~ uh hi) (b:kilem) (r:20.28.4) (q:draft)
kilemlohna = (t:n) (w:hostility/enmity/discord) (d:the state of not being at peace with one another; kilemlohna bawl, rebel) (e:Khazih in singlamteh hangin ~ thatin) (r:49.2.16/58.3.16) (q:draft)
kilemna = (t:n) (w:atonement/reconciliation) (d:kilemna bawl is to make atonement) (e:note adingin ~ bawl nadingin keel a pa khat) (b:kilem) (r:4.28.30/4.28.22) (q:draft)
kilemna = (t:n) (w:peace) (d:being on good terms after or instead of fighting) (e:Israel kumpipa tawh zong ~ bawl hi) (b:kilem) (r:11.22.44/19.120.6) (q:draft)
kilemsa = (t:see) <kilemsa-in>
kilemsa-in = (t:adv) (w:reconciled/at peace) (d:kilem, be at peace, with sa, already, and in: having been put right with someone; the English has justified) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ a inn-ah ciah) (r:42.18.14) (q:draft)
kilemsak = (t:v) (w:reconcile/make peace between) (d:kilem be at peace with sak causative) (e:tapate leh pate lemtuahin ~ kik ding hi) (b:kilem) (r:39.4.6/47.5.18) (q:draft)
kilemsakkik = (t:v) (w:reconcile/bring back to peace) (d:kilemsak, reconcile, with kik, again; of the one who makes peace between two parties) (e:Pasian le mite a hong ~ thei) (b:kilemsak) (r:54.2.5/39.4.6) (q:draft)
kilemsakkikin = (t:v) (w:reconciling/bringing back to peace) (d:kilemsakkik, reconcile, with the linking suffix in) (e:Pate le tate ~) (b:kilemsakkik) (r:42.1.17) (q:draft)
kilemsakna = (t:n) (w:reconciliation) (d:kilemsak, reconcile, with the noun suffix na) (e:tua ~ thu kote hong pia hi) (b:kilemsak) (r:47.5.19) (q:draft)
kilemte = (t:adj) (w:at peace/secure) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the plural te; gam kilemte, lands that are at peace) (e:gam ~ nangawn a sim ding hi) (b:kilem) (r:27.11.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilen = (t:v) (w:hold one another/embrace) (d:len, hold, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:khatlekhat ~ kikawi-in a kap uh hi) (b:len) (r:44.20.37) (q:draft)
kilenin = (t:v) (w:holding/being held) (d:kilen with the linking suffix in; a khut kilenin is holding him by the hand) (e:a khut ~ a paipih dingin) (b:kilen) (r:44.13.11) (q:draft)
kilenkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:be blown away/be driven away) (d:of smoke made to fly off) (e:Meikhu a ~ bangin amaute hawlkhia ding) (r:19.68.2) (q:draft)
kilensa = (t:see) <kilensa-in>
kilensa-in = (t:v) (w:holding one another/hand in hand) (d:len, hold, with the reciprocal prefix ki, sa for a completed action and the linking ending in; khut kilensa-in, holding hands) (e:a lawmpa tawh khut ~) (r:22.8.5) (q:draft)
kiletna = (t:n) (w:handshake/clasping of hands) (d:found in khut kiletna, the giving of the hand to one another as a sign of fellowship) (e:Barnabas tawh khut ~ hong bawl uh) (r:48.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilh = (t:v) (w:nail/fasten) (d:fasten something with nails so that it cannot be moved) (e:sik tawh a ~ uh hi) (r:24.10.4) (q:draft)
kilhcip = (t:v) (w:nail fast/crucify) (d:kilh, nail, with cip, tightly; singlamteh tungah kilhcip is nail to the cross) (e:singlamteh tungah Jesuh ~ uh a) (b:kilh) (r:42.23.33) (q:draft)
kilhcipin = (t:v) (w:nailing/nailing fast) (d:kilhcip, nail fast, with the linking suffix in) (e:singlamteh tungah ~ a beisak ta hi) (b:kilhcip) (r:51.2.14) (q:draft)
kilhna = (t:n) (w:clasp/hook/fastener) (d:a small hook or pin that holds two pieces together) (e:kham ~ sawmnga bawlin) (b:kilh) (r:2.36.13/2.26.6) (q:draft)
kilhnate = (t:n) (w:clasps/hooks/nails) (d:plural; fasteners that hold things together) (e:~ tawh puante khat leh khat kimatsak hi) (b:kilhna) (r:2.36.13/14.3.9) (q:draft)
kiliah = (t:v) (w:be hidden/be concealed) (d:be out of sight or kept from someone's knowledge; ki with liah cover, hide) (e:nangma kiang pan ~ lo hi) (b:liah) (r:19.69.5/40.5.14) (q:draft)
kiliahin = (t:v) (w:being hidden/being covered) (d:kiliah, be hidden, with the linking suffix in; of the light of understanding, where the English has darkened) (e:pilna khuavak ~ Pasian’ nuntakna tawh) (b:kiliah) (r:49.4.18) (q:draft)
kiliahna = (t:n) (w:veil/covering/screen) (d:something that screens or hides; kiliahna puan is a veil over the face) (e:~ puan tawh a maitang khuhkik hi) (b:kiliah) (r:2.34.35/2.34.33) (q:draft)
kiliamsak = (t:v) (w:be wounded/hurt one another/harm) (e:khat leh khat ~ lo ding uh a) (b:liamsak) (r:23.11.9/23.53.5) (q:draft)
kilian = (t:v) (w:make oneself great/be haughty) (d:lian great with ki, oneself: in kilian sak, exalt oneself, be arrogant; kilian ngaihsut is think oneself great) (e:~ sakin a kiphasak mite ahi) (b:lian) (r:20.21.24/45.12.3) (q:draft)
kiliansak = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be proud/be haughty) (d:make oneself great; also set oneself up against someone) (e:Topa dem-in ~ uh hi) (b:liansak) (r:24.48.42/19.131.1) (q:draft)
kiliansakin = (t:v) (w:exalting oneself/being haughty) (d:kiliansak with the linking suffix in) (e:Haggith’ tapa Adonijah amahmah ~) (b:kiliansak) (r:11.1.5/24.48.29) (q:draft)
Kiliansakin = (t:name) (w:Kiliansakin)
kiliansakte = (t:n) (w:those who exalt themselves/the proud) (e:A ~ khempeuh in niamkhiatna thuak ding) (b:kiliansak) (r:40.23.12/19.35.26) (q:draft)
kiliatsak = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be lifted up) (d:liatsak, make great, with the reflexive prefix ki; of the heart being lifted up over others) (e:ama lungsim a ~ loh nading) (b:liatsak) (r:5.17.19/5.17.20) (q:draft)
kiliatsakna = (t:n) (w:arrogance/pride/haughtiness) (e:Mite’ ~ kiniamkhiat ding a) (b:kiliatsak) (r:23.2.17/19.73.8) (q:draft)
kiliin = (t:v) (w:sway/shake/tremble) (d:liin, tremble, with the prefix ki; of a reed moving in the water) (b:liin) (r:11.14.15) (q:draft)
kiliing = (t:v) (w:shake/tremble/quake) (e:Topa mai-ah mualte ~ hi) (b:liing) (r:7.5.5/19.112.6) (q:draft)
kiliingsak = (t:v) (w:shake/make tremble) (d:kiliing, shake, with the causative sak) (e:kumpi gamte ~ gawp hi) (b:kiliing) (r:23.23.11) (q:draft)
Kilikia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Cilicia) (r:48.1.21/44.6.9)
kilikkhia = (t:v) (w:be rolled away) (d:of a stone rolled off from an opening) (e:Han vang pan suang ~ a) (b:likkhia) (r:42.24.2/41.16.4) (q:draft)
kilim = (t:todo) (q:draft, found only in thupha hong kilim piak, be blessed, Deuteronomy 7.14; what kilim adds is not clear)
kilin = (t:v) (w:shake/quake/sway) (d:short form of kiling, written kilin with an apostrophe before the next word) (e:a tunga teengte khempeuh a ~’ ciangin) (r:19.75.3/11.14.15) (q:draft)
kiling = (t:v) (w:be shaken/be moved/shake) (d:to be made to shake or lose firmness, of the earth, a building or a person) (e:ka ~ kei ding hi) (r:19.16.8/19.96.10) (q:draft)
kilinggawp = (t:v) (w:be shaken violently/be shaken/quake) (d:kiling be shaken with gawp, severely) (e:vantung bulpite ~ hi) (b:kiling) (r:10.22.8/44.4.31) (q:draft)
kilingin = (t:v) (w:tremble/shake) (d:kiling, be shaken, with the linking ending in; of the earth trembling) (e:a et ciangin tua leitung ~) (b:kiling) (r:19.104.31) (q:draft)
kilingsak = (t:v) (w:shake/cause to shake/let be shaken) (d:kiling with the causative sak; a kilingsak zo lo, that cannot be shaken) (e:biakinn kongkhak khuam bulpite ~ a) (b:lingsak) (r:23.6.4/58.12.28) (q:draft)
kilingsakin = (t:v) (w:being shaken) (d:kilingsak, cause to shake, with the linking suffix in) (e:a kipiangsak nate ~ kipaikhia ding a) (b:kilingsak) (r:58.12.27) (q:draft)
kilkel = (t:adv) (d:intensifier after a descriptive word, with the sense of clear, fresh or gleaming: vot kilkel is cool and clear, hing kilkel is fresh and green, kipuah kilkel is polished bright) (e:a vot ~ luite kang ngei) (r:24.18.14/23.66.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilo = (t:v) (w:be called/be named/be mentioned) (d:of a name, be spoken or used; min kilo is the name is called or mentioned) (e:a min ~ kha nawn lo ding hi) (r:28.2.17/24.32.34) (q:draft)
kiloh = (t:v) (w:be paid/be repaid) (d:loh, pay off, with the passive prefix ki; kiloh sak is make someone pay) (e:azah sagih-in ~ sak a) (b:loh) (r:20.6.31) (q:draft)
kilohsak = (t:v) (w:be made to pay/be made to repay) (d:lohsak, pay for, with the passive prefix ki) (e:a zah sagihin ~ a) (b:lohsak) (r:20.6.31) (q:draft)
kilok = (t:v) (w:be shaken/be tossed/quake/be rough) (d:be moved to and fro, of the earth quaking or of water stirred up by the wind; tui kilok is a wave or rough water) (e:nung ahih ciangin tui a ~ hi) (b:lok) (r:43.6.18/13.16.30) (q:draft)
kilokgawp = (t:v) (w:be shaken violently/be tossed about) (d:of the earth, a boat or water thrown about by wind or earthquake) (e:Leitung khangkhamin ~ ding a) (b:lokgawp) (r:23.24.19/43.6.18) (q:draft)
kilokha = (t:v) (w:be mentioned/be invoked/be called on) (d:of a name being spoken) (e:a min ~ nawn lo ding hi) (r:28.2.17) (q:draft)
kilokhia = (t:v) (w:be designated/be called out) (d:kilo, be named, with khia, out; a minin a kilokhia, singled out by name) (e:a minin a ~ midang omlai hi) (b:kilo) (r:13.16.41/15.10.16) (q:draft)
kilokna = (t:n) (w:surge/current/tossing) (d:kilok, be tossed, with the noun suffix na; tui kilokna is moving water, a current or surf) (e:Tui ~ nih kituahna mun) (b:kilok) (r:44.27.41) (q:draft)
kiloksak = (t:v) (w:stir up/trouble/shake) (d:kilok, be shaken, with the causative sak; of stirring the water of a pool) (e:zel a, tui a ~ hi) (b:kilok) (r:43.5.4) (q:draft)
kilokzo = (t:v) (w:can be shaken) (d:kilok, be shaken, with zo, be able; with ngei lo, can never be shaken) (e:a phuhsa sutpi ~ ngei lo ding) (b:kilok) (r:55.2.19) (q:draft)
kilomin = (t:v) (w:huddle together/crowd together) (d:of people gathered close in a heap; compare lom, heap) (e:sawlkawm nuai-ah ~ omkhawm uh hi) (b:lomin) (r:18.30.7) (q:draft)
kilong = (t:v) (w:come off/be detached/be dislocated) (d:of an arm coming away from the shoulder, with khia, out) (e:ka liang bul panin ~ khia ta) (r:18.31.22) (q:draft)
kilongkhia = (t:v) (w:come off/fall out of joint) (d:kilong with khia, out; of an arm coming away from the shoulder) (e:ka liang bul panin ~ tahen) (b:kilong) (r:18.31.22) (q:draft)
kilosa = (t:adj) (w:named/specified) (d:kilo, be named, with sa, already done; a min kilosa, whose names have been called) (e:a min ~ hih mite khawmin) (b:kilo) (r:4.1.17) (q:draft)
kilote = (t:n) (w:those called/those named) (d:kilo, be called or named, with plural te: those whose names are given, those called by a name) (e:keima min tawh a ~ khempeuh) (b:kilo) (r:23.43.6/13.9.9) (q:draft)
kiluah = (t:v) (w:be inherited/be passed down) (d:passive of luah, inherit: property comes down from parents or from one generation to the next) (e:pate tung panin a ~ hi a) (b:luah) (r:20.19.14/26.44.28) (q:draft)
kiluan = (t:v) (w:be poured/flow) (d:ki with luan, a form of luang flow: of molten gold poured for an image; in Joel 2:30 of blood being shed) (e:kham a ~, a kisung na milimte) (b:luan) (r:23.30.22/29.2.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiluangkhiasak = (t:v) (w:be drained/be made to flow out) (d:luangkhiasak, make flow out, with the passive prefix ki; of the blood of a slaughtered animal) (e:a si ~ loin gawlmek a kigo) (b:luangkhiasak) (r:44.21.25) (q:draft)
kiluansak = (t:v) (w:be shed/be poured out) (d:kiluan, flow, with the causative sak; of blood) (e:sisan a ~ khit ciang bekin) (b:kiluan) (r:58.9.22) (q:draft)
kiluansakna = (t:n) (w:shedding/flowing) (d:with sisan, blood: sisan kiluansakna is bloodshed, where the English has only blood) (e:Sisan ~, meikatna le meikhu sahpi) (b:kiluansak) (r:44.2.19/29.2.30) (q:draft)
kiluh = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ransacked/be looted) (e:innte ~ gawpin) (b:luh) (r:38.14.2/23.42.22) (q:draft)
kiluhgawp = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ravaged/be sacked) (d:kiluh, be plundered, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action) (e:Khaldea gam ~ ding a) (b:kiluh) (r:24.50.10/26.36.35) (q:draft)
kiluhin = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be looted) (d:kiluh, be plundered, with the linking ending in) (e:inn ~, a zite uh kibuansak ding hi) (b:kiluh) (r:23.13.16) (q:draft)
kilui = (t:v) (w:be served/be set before) (d:of food, be laid out in front of someone to eat) (e:nek dingin a mai-ah an ~ hi) (r:1.24.33/46.10.27) (q:draft)
kilukham = (t:v) (w:be laid under the head/be used as a pillow) (d:lukham, pillow, with the prefix ki; of the swords of buried warriors, with sak) (e:a namsau uh ~ sakin) (b:lukham) (r:26.32.27) (q:draft)
kilukhamsakin = (t:v) (w:having laid under the head) (d:kilukham with the causative sak and the linking suffix in) (e:a namsau uh ~) (b:kilukham) (r:26.32.27) (q:draft)
kilukhuhsa = (t:see) <kilukhuhsa-in>
kilukhuhsa-in = (t:v) (w:with head covered/having covered the head) (d:lu, head, and khuh, cover, with the reflexive prefix ki, sa for a completed action and the linking ending in; a sign of grief or shame) (e:Haman ahih leh ~ a thuum kawmin) (r:17.6.12) (q:draft)
kilumlet = (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be overturned) (d:lumlet, overturn, with the passive prefix ki; gam kilumlet is an uprising in the land) (e:gam ~ nading thu ahi zongin) (b:lumlet) (r:42.21.9) (q:draft)
kilumletin = (t:v) (w:be overturned/overturn) (d:kilumlet, be turned over, with the linking ending in; of a tent knocked over) (e:puanbuk ~ lei lakah kiphah hi) (b:kilumlet) (r:7.7.13) (q:draft)
kilumletsak = (t:v) (w:turn upside down/throw into disorder) (d:kilumlet, be overturned, with the causative sak) (e:gam khempeuh a ~ hih mite in) (b:kilumlet) (r:44.17.6) (q:draft)
kilumsak = (t:v) (w:be made to lie down/be laid down to sleep) (d:lumsak, make lie down, with the passive prefix ki) (e:galkap nih kikalah ~ a) (b:lumsak) (r:44.12.6) (q:draft)
kilung = (t:v) (d:lung, heart or mind, with the reciprocal prefix ki; found with tuak: kilung tuak is be of one mind with one another) (e:khat leh khat ~ tuakin na om) (b:lung) (r:45.15.6) (q:draft)
kilungdamsak = (t:v) (w:be pleased/be made glad/rejoice) (d:lungdamsak make glad, with the prefix ki, passive or reflexive: be pleased, or make oneself glad) (e:Upna loin Pasian ~ zo lo hi) (b:lungdamsak) (r:58.11.6/59.1.10) (q:draft)
kilunggim = (t:v) (w:be troubled/lose heart) (d:lunggim, be troubled, with the prefix ki; kilunggim sak kei in is do not let yourself be troubled) (e:ahih manin ~ sak kei in) (b:lunggim) (r:23.7.4) (q:draft)
kilunggimsak = (t:v) (w:trouble oneself/make oneself anxious) (d:lunggimsak, make heavy in heart, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Note ~ kei un la) (b:lunggimsak) (r:21.11.10) (q:draft)
kilunggulh = (t:v) (w:lust for one another/desire one another) (d:lunggulh desire, with the reciprocal prefix ki; kilunggulh luatna, too much desire of woman and man for each other, is lust) (e:khat leh khat ~ uh a) (b:lunggulh) (r:45.1.27/51.3.5) (q:draft)
kilunggulhna = (t:n) (w:lust/desire for one another) (d:kilunggulh, desire one another, with the noun suffix na; of sexual desire) (e:pasal le pasal ~ ciang dong) (b:kilunggulh) (r:65.1.7/52.4.4) (q:draft)
kilunghimawh = (t:v) (w:worry/be troubled) (d:lunghimawh, worry, with the prefix ki used without a named subject: one has worry or sorrow) (e:Pil semsem lehang ~ semsem a) (b:lunghimawh) (r:21.1.18) (q:draft)
kilungkhamsak = (t:v) (w:distress oneself/be upset) (d:lungkhamsak, make troubled, with the reflexive prefix ki; with kei in, do not let yourself be troubled) (e:Hih thu hangin nangmah ~ kei in) (b:lungkhamsak) (r:10.11.25) (q:draft)
kilungkim = (t:v) (w:be content with one another/be satisfied with each other) (d:lungkim, be satisfied, with the reciprocal prefix ki; with lo, have a grievance against one another) (e:khatlekhat a ~ lo na om uh) (b:lungkim) (r:51.3.13) (q:draft)
kilungnemsak = (t:v) (w:be humbled/be made low) (d:the English has in his humiliation) (e:A ~ lai takin midangte in) (r:44.8.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilungnuamsak = (t:v) (w:comfort oneself/set one's mind at ease) (d:lungnuamsak, make glad or at ease, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Bangbang hitaleh ~ in, ka sanggamnu aw) (b:lungnuamsak) (r:10.13.20) (q:draft)
kilungsim = (t:n) (w:ill will/malice) (d:found in kilungsim neihna, holding something in the heart against one another, where the English has malice) (e:kitotna, kikona, ~ neihna khempeuh beisak) (r:49.4.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilungso = (t:v) (w:fret/be vexed) (d:lungso, lung heart with so hot, with the reflexive prefix ki: work oneself into anger or worry; found in kilungso tawmsak, make oneself fret) (e:Nangmah ~ tawmsak ke’n) (b:lungso) (r:19.37.8/19.37.7) (q:draft)
kilungsosak = (t:v) (w:fret/vex oneself) (d:kilungso fret, with the causative sak: make oneself angry or worried) (e:nangmah ~ kei in la) (b:kilungso) (r:19.37.1/19.37.8) (q:draft)
kilungtuak = (t:v) (w:agree together/be of one mind/conspire) (d:be of the same mind with one another to do something) (e:bang hangin ~ na hi uh hiam) (r:44.5.9) (q:draft)
kilup = (t:v) (w:be lain with) (d:lup, lie down, with the prefix ki; kilup khoppih, be lain with, of sexual intercourse) (e:Hong ~ khoppih lohna mun) (b:lup) (r:24.3.2) (q:draft)
kilutpih = (t:v) (w:be brought in/be taken in) (d:lutpih, bring in, with the prefix ki; of goods carried into a town) (e:khua sungah van hong ~ loh nadingin) (b:lutpih) (r:16.13.19) (q:draft)
kilutsak = (t:v) (w:be let in/be admitted/be welcomed in) (d:passive of lutsak let in, with the prefix ki) (e:kongpi-ah kuamah ~ lo ahih manin) (b:lutsak) (r:17.4.2/42.16.9) (q:draft)
kim = (t:n) (w:surroundings/around) (d:the area round about; kim-ah, around; khua kim, the country round a town) (e:Mite nangma ~-ah kikhawmsak in la) (r:19.7.7) (q:draft)
kim = (t:adv) (w:every/all) (d:all of them without exception, each one, placed after a noun or verb) (e:khialhna nam ~ na tang un) (r:52.5.22/46.12.26) (q:draft)
kim = (t:n) (w:half/middle/part) (d:kim ciang, halfway up, the middle of; zan kim lai, the middle of the night; kim khat, a part of, some of) (e:zan ~ lai takin amah tho-in) (r:11.3.20/42.13.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kima = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:of a woman who has been put away by her husband; listed beside meigong widow) (e:meigong ahi a, a ~ ahi zongin) (r:3.22.13/4.30.9) (q:draft)
kima-sialh = (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:boast about oneself; compare kisialh, boast) (e:Zing ciang hun-a ding ~ kei in) (r:20.27.1) (q:draft)
kimaakna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:kimaakna lai is a certificate of divorce) (e:khialhna hangin ~ lai pia-a ka hawlkhiat) (r:24.3.8) (q:draft)
kimah = (t:prep) (w:around/round about) (d:kim, surroundings, with the place marker ah, placed after a noun) (e:biakna tau ~ na theh ding hi) (b:kim) (r:2.29.20/11.11.24) (q:draft)
kimai = (t:v) (w:face each other/face) (d:mai, face, with the prefix ki, each other; found with ngat, turn toward, or tuah, meet) (e:khat leh khat ~ tuah ni) (b:mai) (r:14.25.17/1.30.40) (q:draft)
kimaingat = (t:v) (w:face each other/face one another) (d:maingat face, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:amaute khatlekhat ~ uh hi) (b:maingat) (r:2.37.9/2.25.20) (q:draft)
kimaisak = (t:v) (w:be forgiven) (d:passive of maisak, forgive; mawhna kimaisak is sins are forgiven) (e:Na mawhna ~ zo hi) (b:maisak) (r:42.7.48/19.32.1) (q:draft)
kimaisakin = (t:v) (w:be forgiven/be pardoned) (d:form with the linking suffix -in, in Romans 2.15 excusing one another) (e:hih thu hangin Jakob’ mawhna ~) (b:kimaisak) (r:23.27.9/23.40.2) (q:draft)
kimaisakna = (t:n) (w:forgiveness) (d:kimaisak, be forgiven, with the noun suffix na; mawhna kimaisakna, forgiveness of sins) (e:mawhna ~ thu nomau kiangah hong kihilh) (b:kimaisak) (r:44.13.38/44.5.31) (q:draft)
kimaisakte = (t:n) (w:those who are forgiven) (d:kimaisak, be forgiven, with the plural te) (e:tawmno bek a ~ in a itna) (b:kimaisak) (r:42.7.47) (q:draft)
kimaitaisak = (t:v) (w:cheer oneself up/put on a cheerful face) (d:maitaisak, make cheerful, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Ka dahnate kimangngilh bawlin ~ ding) (b:maitaisak) (r:18.9.27) (q:draft)
kimaituah = (t:v) (w:face each other/meet face to face/confront) (d:stand face to face with someone, as opponents in battle or in court) (e:khat leh khat gal sungah ~ uh hi) (r:14.25.21/44.25.16) (q:draft)
kimaituahin = (t:v) (w:face each other/be opposite each other) (d:kimaituah with the connective in: facing one another, face to face) (e:khat leh khat ~ gal kido uh hi) (b:kimaituah) (r:12.14.11/11.20.29) (q:draft)
kimaizumsak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be shamed) (d:maizumsak, put to shame, with the prefix ki) (e:Siatna hun ciangin amaute ~ lo a) (b:maizumsak) (r:19.37.19) (q:draft)
kimakai = (t:v) (w:be led/be guided) (d:makai lead, with the prefix ki, passive; kimakai sak is let oneself be led, and kimakai khialsak let oneself be led astray) (e:Kha Siangtho ~ sakin) (b:makai) (r:49.4.3/14.32.15) (q:draft)
kimakna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:makna, divorce, with the prefix ki; kimakna lai, certificate of divorce) (e:Moses in ~ lai gelhsakin masak thei hi) (b:makna) (r:41.10.4/23.50.1) (q:draft)
kimamsak = (t:v) (w:be straightened/be made straight) (d:mamsak, straighten, with the prefix ki) (e:A kawisate ~ thei lo a) (b:mamsak) (r:21.1.15) (q:draft)
kiman = (t:adj) (w:finished) (e:tuate ~ khin hi) (r:14.29.29/1.2.1)
kiman = (t:v) (w:arrested) (e:Paul ~ ahih ciangin) (r:20.6.31/23.13.15)
kimancip = (t:v) (w:be held captive/be seized) (d:mancip, seize and hold fast, with the prefix ki; a kimancip before a noun is captive) (e:A ~ Jerusalem mite aw) (b:mancip) (r:23.52.2) (q:draft)
kimang = (t:v) (w:be of use/be used/be in effect) (d:mostly negative, bangmah-a kimang lo is worthless, of no use; also last or stay in use for a time) (e:Bangmah-a ~ lo pasian kua in bawl a) (r:23.44.10/20.12.19) (q:draft)
kimangin = (t:v) (w:being used/being in effect) (d:kimang, be in use, with the linking suffix in; here of a gift that is in use only for a time) (e:tawlkhat sung bek ~) (b:kimang) (r:46.13.8) (q:draft)
kimangngailh = (t:v) (w:be forgotten) (d:of past troubles no longer remembered) (e:a beisa huna haksatnate ~ khin a) (r:23.65.16) (q:draft)
kimangngilh = (t:v) (w:be forgotten) (d:mangngilh forget with ki, passive; also make oneself forget) (e:migilote ~ pah hi) (b:mangngilh) (r:20.10.7/1.41.30) (q:draft)
kimangngilhkha = (t:v) (w:be overlooked/be forgotten by chance) (d:of dead bodies left unburied because no one noticed them) (e:a ~ siluanghawmte zongin a phum dingin) (r:26.39.14) (q:draft)
kimangpah = (t:v) (w:be used straight on/continue in use) (d:kimang, be used, with pah, straight away; of the existing priests simply being kept in use) (e:siampi omsa a ~ ding ahi hi) (r:58.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimangthangsak = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be destroyed) (d:passive with ki of mangthangsak, cause to perish) (e:amau pawl lak pan ~ ding hi) (b:mangthangsak) (r:44.3.23) (q:draft)
kimangzaw = (t:v) (w:be more useful/be better) (d:kimang be of use, with zaw more) (e:a om i vengpa ~ hi) (b:kimang) (r:20.27.10) (q:draft)
kimanin = (t:v) (w:being caught/being captured/being arrested) (d:kiman with in joining it to the next verb) (e:Na kampauna hangin nang hong ~) (b:kiman) (r:20.6.2/24.34.3) (q:draft)
kimanna = (t:n) (w:use/usefulness/value) (d:what something is good for; kimanna om lo or nei lo means useless, worthless) (e:a ~ om lo ahih manin) (r:58.7.18/32.2.8) (q:draft)
kimansiang = (t:v) (w:be completed/be finished) (d:kiman, finished, with siang, clean: be wholly finished, of work carried through to the end) (e:nasep khempeuh ~ hi) (b:kiman) (r:14.8.16) (q:draft)
kimante = (t:n) (w:captives/those captured/prisoners) (d:those who have been taken, kiman with plural -te; sal-a kimante are people taken captive, and after a battle it is also the plunder taken) (e:sal-a a ~ tungah suahtakna thu) (b:kiman) (r:23.61.1/4.31.27) (q:draft)
kimanzo = (t:v) (w:can be caught) (d:kiman be caught, with zo be able; here of fish, enough being caught) (e:khamzah ding ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:kiman) (r:4.11.22) (q:draft)
kimap = (t:v) (w:be spared) (d:of a life, be spared, be left alive) (e:na nuntakna hong ~ ding hi) (r:24.38.20/24.38.17) (q:draft)
kimasa = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:of a woman who has been sent away by her husband; kima, divorced, with the completive suffix sa) (e:Meigong numei, a ~ numei, a kininsaksa numei) (b:kima) (r:3.21.14/26.44.22) (q:draft)
kimat = (t:v) (w:arrest/seize) (e:Paul ~ nading thu, Moses ~ sawm ahih man in) (r:44.12.4/24.2.26)
kimat = (t:adj) (w:sticky/adhesive/gluey) (e:sing leh sing ~)
kimatcip = (t:v) (w:stick fast/be sealed/be tightly joined) (d:kimat with cip, firmly; of a hand stuck to a sword, a sealed book, scales closed together) (e:a khut a namsau-ah ~ hi) (b:kimat) (r:10.23.10/23.29.11) (q:draft)
kimatheih = (t:v) (w:be known beforehand/be foreseen) (d:theih, know, with ma, before, and the prefix ki; a kimatheih lo, that cannot be known in advance) (e:cih a ~ lo mah ahi hi) (r:10.11.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimatin = (t:v) (w:be joined to/adjoin/be attached to) (d:kimat be joined with the linking in; after tawh, next to or connected with) (e:Hih kawm tawh a ~ biakinn kimkotah inndei) (b:kimat) (r:26.41.5/49.4.16) (q:draft)
kimatna = (t:n) (w:capture/arrest/seizure) (d:the fact of being caught or taken) (e:Johan’ ~ thu Zeisu in a zak ciangin) (b:kimat) (r:40.4.12/9.4.19) (q:draft)
kimatsak = (t:v) (w:fasten together/join/couple) (d:kimat hold to each other with sak cause: join things so that they hold together, as curtains with clasps) (e:puante khat leh khat ~ hi) (b:kimat) (r:2.36.13/2.26.11) (q:draft)
kimatsakin = (t:v) (w:fasten together/join) (d:kimatsak, join things so that they hold together, with the linking ending in; of foxes tied tail to tail) (e:a meite leh a meite ~) (b:kimatsak) (r:7.15.4) (q:draft)
kimawhsak = (t:v) (w:condemn oneself/blame oneself/blame one another) (d:ki- reflexive or reciprocal form of mawhsak) (e:amah le amah a ~ ahi hi) (b:mawhsak) (r:45.14.23/51.3.13) (q:draft)
kimawhsakin = (t:v) (w:condemning one another/accusing/condemning oneself) (d:kimawhsak blame oneself or one another, with the linking ending in) (e:khatlekhat ~ thu kikhen kei unla) (b:kimawhsak) (r:45.14.13/46.4.3) (q:draft)
kimawhsakna = (t:n) (w:accusation/charge/blame) (d:accusation made against someone, also the condemning of oneself in the heart) (e:a ~ lai pia loin paisak leng) (b:mawhsakna) (r:44.25.27/40.5.11) (q:draft)
kimawhsaknate = (t:n) (w:accusations/charges) (d:the things a person is accused of) (e:amah a ~ kam khat beek dawng) (b:kimawhsakna) (r:40.27.14/25.3.59) (q:draft)
kimawk = (t:adv) (w:idly/without cause) (d:the prefix ki joined to mawk, idly or for no reason, and written before the verb that ki belongs to: kimawk tot, quarrel for no reason; kimawk hoho, chat idly with one another; kimawk phat, praise oneself emptily) (e:mi tawh ~ hoho kei un) (b:mawk) (r:42.10.4/20.3.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimawkphat = (t:v) (w:flatter oneself) (d:reflexive ki with mawkphat flatter, praise idly) (e:manin amah ~ tawm hi) (b:mawkphat) (r:19.36.2) (q:draft)
kimawksai = (t:v) (w:spring/go off) (d:of a trap, spring shut with nothing in it) (e:thang ~ ahi hiam) (r:30.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
