kimeeltheih = (t:v) (w:be acquainted/know each other) (d:ki each other, with meel face and theih know: know one another by sight; tawh marks the other person) (e:siampi ukpa tawh ~ a) (r:43.18.15/43.18.16) (q:draft)
kimeetsak = (t:v) (w:be shorn/be sheared) (d:passive with ki of meetsak, have the wool cut off) (e:a mul a ~ tuuno) (b:meetsak) (r:44.8.32) (q:draft)
kimeltheih = (t:v) (w:be acquainted/get acquainted/be associated) (d:meltheih know by face, with the reciprocal prefix ki: know each other; the other person is marked by tawh, with) (e:Kefas tawh ~ nadingin) (b:meltheih) (r:48.1.18/16.13.4) (q:draft)
kimemat = (t:v) (w:be connected/have to do with each other) (d:of two things, belong together or rest on one another; here said of keeping the law and faith, with lo: have nothing to do with each other) (e:upna thu na ~ kha lo hi) (r:48.3.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimematna = (t:n) (w:claim/connection/share) (d:kimemat be connected with, with the noun suffix na: something that ties a person to a matter and gives a right in it) (e:bangmah ~ na nei kei uh hi) (b:kimemat) (r:16.2.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimet = (t:v) (w:be shaved/be shorn) (e:a ~ khit ciangin) (b:met) (r:7.16.22/22.4.2) (q:draft)
kimetcip = (t:v) (w:collapse/sink down/be levelled) (d:said of the age-old hills before God, in parallel with kitamkham crumble; how the word is built is not certain) (e:a om tawntung mualneute ~ hi) (r:35.3.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimetmai = (t:v) (w:be shaved off/be cut off) (d:of a beard, be shaved clean away; passive ki with met shave) (e:khamul khempeuh ~ hi) (r:23.15.2) (q:draft)
kimettol = (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/be shaved) (d:passive of mettol: of the head, be shaved completely, as a sign of mourning) (e:Dahna limin lu khempeuh ~ a) (b:mettol) (r:23.15.2) (q:draft)
kimettolsak = (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/have the head shaved) (d:kimettol be shaved bald, with sak: have the hair shaved off completely, as a sign of mourning) (e:A sam uh ~ ding a) (b:kimettol) (r:26.7.18) (q:draft)
kimin = (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in full/all) (d:kim complete with -in: the whole of it, with nothing and no one left out; often as a kimin) (e:sawm-ah khat a ~ hong paipih un) (b:kim) (r:39.3.10/4.29.40) (q:draft)
kimindaisak = (t:v) (w:be dishonoured/be disgraced) (d:passive with ki of mindaisak, bring a name into disgrace) (e:hong kipahtawi-in hong ~ zel a) (b:mindaisak) (r:47.6.8) (q:draft)
kiminsia = (t:see) <kiminsia-sak>
kiminsia-sak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be disgraced) (d:be given a bad name, min name with sia bad and the causative sak, passive with ki) (e:zahhuai-in ~ khin ahih ciangin) (r:19.71.24) (q:draft)
kiminthan = (t:see) <kiminthan'sak>
kiminthan'sak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honoured) (d:passive of minthangsak glorify; minthang is shortened to minthan before sak) (e:Ama sungah Pasian a ~ leh) (r:43.13.32/23.61.3) (q:draft)
kiminthangsak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honored) (e:Tu-in Mihing Tapa ~ a) (b:minthangsak) (r:43.13.31/3.10.3) (q:draft)
kiminthansak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be made famous) (d:passive with ki of min name, than be renowned and the causative sak) (e:amah a ~ theih nadingin) (r:23.61.3) (q:draft)
kiminthansakna = (t:n) (w:glorification/display of splendour) (d:kiminthansak be glorified, with the noun suffix na; that by which someone is glorified) (e:keimah hong ~ ding ka nasempa) (b:kiminthansak) (r:23.49.3) (q:draft)
kimitsak = (t:v) (w:be put out/be extinguished/be quenched) (d:passive of mitsak, of a fire or of anger) (e:~ lo ding hi) (b:mitsak) (r:3.6.13/12.22.17) (q:draft)
Kimittawsak = (t:v) (w:blind oneself/make oneself blind) (d:mittaw blind with the prefix ki, oneself, and sak, cause) (e:~ unla a mittaw hi un) (r:23.29.9) (q:draft)
kimkhat = (t:det) (w:some) (e:a um lo mi ~ a om hi) (r:43.6.64/1.3.6)
kimkhat = (t:prep) (w:among)
