kipawl = (t:v) (w:mix)
kipawlbawl = (t:v) (w:become friends/make friends with each other) (d:kipawl associate, with bawl make) (e:tegel kilem kikin ~ uh hi) (b:kipawl) (r:42.23.12) (q:draft)
kipawlin = (t:v) (w:join/associate/unite/band together) (d:form of kipawl with the linking ending in; the partner is marked by tawh, with) (e:mi namdangte tawh ~ tua mite) (b:kipawl) (r:28.7.8/7.20.11) (q:draft)
kipawlkha = (t:v) (w:join with/associate with) (d:kipawl associate, with kha happen to; with kei, do not get involved with) (e:amau a langpangte tawh ~ kei in) (r:20.24.21) (q:draft)
kipawlkhawm = (t:v) (w:become allies/form an alliance) (d:kipawl associate, with khawm together) (e:kumpipa in a ~ theih nadingin) (b:kipawl) (r:27.11.6) (q:draft)
kipawlkhawmna = (t:n) (w:alliance/union) (d:kipawlkhawm, join together as allies, with the noun suffix na) (e:tua ~ kip lo ding a) (b:kipawlkhawm) (r:27.11.6) (q:draft)
kipawlkhin = (t:v) (w:be already united/have been joined) (d:kipawl, join or associate, with khin, already done; used with tawh, with) (e:Pasian tawh ~ na hih manun) (b:kipawl) (r:45.8.10) (q:draft)
kipawlna = (t:n) (w:alliance/treaty/union/fellowship) (d:a joining together of people or nations; kipawlna bawl, make an alliance) (e:Assiria tawh ~ bawl uh a) (b:kipawl) (r:28.12.1/46.1.9) (q:draft)
Kipawlna = (t:n) (w:Union) (d:kipawlna, union, written with a capital as the name of one of the two staffs of the shepherd in Zechariah) (e:~ a kici ciangkhut la-in ka kuaitan leuleu a) (b:kipawlna) (r:38.11.14/38.11.7) (q:draft)
kipawlnate = (t:n) (w:joints/joinings/connections) (d:plural of kipawlna, a joining; here the places where bones and sinews of the body join) (e:a taang tawh a ~ hangin) (b:kipawlna) (r:51.2.19) (q:draft)
kipawlpih = (t:v) (w:associate with/ally with/mix with) (d:kipawl associate, with pih together with; a kipawlpih, those one has joined with) (e:A ~ mi namdangte in) (b:kipawl) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft)
kipawlpihte = (t:n) (w:allies/friends/associates) (d:kipawlpih, be allied with, with plural te: those who are joined with someone) (e:hih mite pen Abram’ ~ ahi hi) (b:kipawlpih) (r:1.14.13/25.1.19) (q:draft)
kipawlsa = (t:adj) (w:joined/united) (d:kipawl, join, with the completive suffix sa: having been joined; Pasian tawh a kipawlsa mite, people who have been united with God) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ mite) (b:kipawl) (r:46.6.11) (q:draft)
kipawlsak = (t:v) (w:unite/join) (d:kipawl, join, with the causative sak: cause to be joined with someone) (e:Khrih Jesuh tawh a hong ~ Kha Siangtho) (b:kipawl) (r:45.8.2) (q:draft)
kipawlte = (t:n) (w:those who are joined with/associates/companions) (d:people who associate with or belong to someone or something, plural; used with tawh, with) (e:Topa tawh ~ in Topa tawh lungsim khat) (b:kipawl) (r:46.6.17/41.16.10) (q:draft)
kipawlthei = (t:v) (w:be able to associate/can be united) (d:kipawl with thei, be able to join or have fellowship with; in the 1977 text Pasian tawh kipawlthei renders being justified, put right with God) (e:Midik le mimawh bangci-in ~ ding a) (b:kipawl) (r:47.6.14/45.9.30) (q:draft)
kipden = (t:v) (w:endure/remain firm/last for ever) (d:kip, be firm, with den, always) (e:amau’ gamh ~ ding hi) (r:19.37.18) (q:draft)
kipeek = (t:v) (w:roll about/writhe/thrash) (d:said of a person lying on the ground in a convulsion) (e:cilphuan bua-in a ~ sawnsawn hi) (r:41.9.20) (q:draft)
kipeh = (t:v) (w:be grafted/be grafted in) (d:passive of peh, graft: a branch is joined onto another tree) (e:Eite tawh hong ~ theih nadingin) (b:peh) (r:45.11.19/45.11.24) (q:draft)
kipeh = (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:with khat leh khat, one another; said of people who attack each other) (e:khat leh khat na ~, na kinek uh leh) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kipehthei = (t:v) (w:can be grafted/be grafted) (d:kipeh, be grafted, with thei, be able) (e:oliv kung tungah hong ~ ahihleh) (b:kipeh) (r:45.11.24) (q:draft)
kipei = (t:v) (w:whirl/spin/swirl) (d:of a whirlwind, turn round and round; pei is wheel) (e:huihpi nungin pingpei ~ a) (b:pei) (r:34.1.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipeksat = (t:see) <kipeksat-in>
kipeksat-in = (t:v) (w:be broken) (d:passive of peksat, break, with the linking ending in; said of a treaty or agreement) (e:Thuciamnate ~, thukimnasate kipalsat a) (r:23.33.8) (q:draft)
kipeksatin = (t:v) (w:be broken) (d:passive of peksat, break, with the linking ending in; said of a treaty or agreement) (e:Thuciamnate ~, thukimnasate kipalsat a) (b:peksatin) (r:23.33.8) (q:draft)
kipelh = (t:v) (w:be free from/escape/keep away from) (d:used with tawh for the thing avoided) (e:lungkhamna tawh ~ hi) (b:pelh) (r:20.21.23/20.12.13) (q:draft)
kipelhin = (t:v) (w:escape/be free from/avoid) (d:kipelh, be free from, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; used with tawh for the thing escaped) (e:upna hangin sihna tawh ~ a kilato hi) (b:kipelh) (r:58.11.5/61.1.4) (q:draft)
kipelhkhia = (t:v) (w:be released from/be freed from) (d:kipelh, be free from, with khia, out; used with tawh for the thing one is freed from) (e:tua numei in thukham tawh a ~ a) (b:kipelh) (r:45.7.3) (q:draft)
kipelhkik = (t:v) (w:be averted/be turned back/be revoked) (d:kipelh, be kept away, with kik, back; said of an evil plan that is to be undone) (e:a ~ theih nadingin va thum hi) (b:kipelh) (r:17.8.3) (q:draft)
kipelhna = (t:n) (w:avoiding/escape/turning away) (d:keeping clear of something, used with tawh) (e:sihna thang tawh ~ ahi hi) (b:kipelh) (r:20.13.14/20.16.6) (q:draft)
kipelhsak = (t:v) (w:keep from/spare from/turn away from/take away) (d:cause to pass by or be kept away from someone, from kipelh; with a negative, not let go of a promise) (e:Hih hai kei tawh ~ in) (b:kipelh) (r:41.14.36/20.14.27) (q:draft)
kipelhsakna = (t:n) (w:sparing/deliverance) (d:kipelhsak, keep from, with the noun suffix na: being spared from something, with tawh) (e:sihna tawh nong ~ ding ahi hi) (b:kipelhsak) (r:17.7.3) (q:draft)
kipelhzaw = (t:v) (w:rather be spared/rather keep free from) (d:kipelh, be free from, with zaw, more or rather; used with tawh) (e:tuate tawh ~ le-uh hoih ka sa hi) (b:kipelh) (r:46.7.28) (q:draft)
kipengsak = (t:v) (w:be exempted/be made free from) (d:passive of pengsak: be released from a duty or a tax) (e:siah khempeuh ~ ding hi) (b:pengsak) (r:9.17.25) (q:draft)
kipetkha = (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:ki, each other, with pet, bite, and kha, happen to) (e:khatlekhat kiphuai-in ~ le-uhcin) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kiphah = (t:v) (w:be spread/be laid out) (d:be spread or laid flat, as a bed, paving stones or a body on the ground) (e:Saul adingin lupna khat na ~ a) (b:phah) (r:9.9.25/26.40.17) (q:draft)
kiphal = (t:v) (w:be allowed/be permitted) (e:thu a gen ding uh ~ lo hi) (b:phal) (r:46.14.34/40.18.18) (q:draft)
kiphamat = (t:v) (w:follow one upon another/overtake one another) (d:in a ciah leh a kuan kiphamat, those leaving and those setting out catch up with each other: said of people or messengers coming and going without a break) (e:a ciah leh a kuan ~ uh a) (r:24.51.31/41.6.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphamawh = (t:v) (w:be necessary/be obliged) (d:from phamawh, necessary; with hi lo, there is no obligation to do something) (e:gamtat ding a ~ hi lo hi) (b:phamawh) (r:45.8.12) (q:draft)
kiphamawhte = (t:n) (w:those addicted/those dependent on) (d:people who cannot do without something; zunek kiphamawhte, those addicted to drinking wine) (e:zunek ~ ahih loh nading) (b:kiphamawh) (r:56.2.3) (q:draft)
kiphan = (t:v) (w:be woven/be embroidered) (d:of cloth, be woven or worked with a pattern) (e:a kizem a ~ puan hoihte la-in) (r:26.16.18/43.19.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphasak = (t:v) (w:be proud/be arrogant/boast) (d:think highly of oneself; a kiphasak mite are the proud) (e:A ~ mite en in la) (r:18.40.11/19.75.4) (q:draft)
kiphasakin = (t:v) (w:be proud/boast/exalt oneself) (d:kiphasak with the linking suffix -in, being proud and then doing the next action; also proudly) (e:na lungsim uh ~ kei nong mangngilh) (b:kiphasak) (r:28.13.6/1.16.4) (q:draft)
kiphasaknate = (t:n) (w:pride/boastings) (d:kiphasak, be proud, with the noun suffix na and the plural te) (e:Mi liante’ ~ a beisak nading) (b:kiphasak) (r:23.23.9) (q:draft)
Kiphasakpa = (t:n) (w:proud man/vain man/foolish person) (d:kiphasak be proud or boast, with pa marking a man; used in address) (e:~ aw, gamtatna hoih om loin) (r:59.2.20) (q:draft)
kiphasakte = (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant) (d:kiphasak with plural te, those who are proud; often mi kiphasakte) (e:Pasian in mi ~ niamkhiat a) (b:kiphasak) (r:18.22.29/20.15.25) (q:draft)
kiphasakteng = (t:n) (w:the arrogant/all the proud) (d:kiphasak, be proud, with teng, all: after mi, all the people who are proud) (e:mi ~ mah in thupha ngahin) (b:kiphasak) (r:39.3.15) (q:draft)
kiphat = (t:v) (w:be praised/be commended) (d:passive of phat praise) (e:Pasian min ~ tawntung ta hen) (b:phat) (r:27.2.20/20.11.26) (q:draft)
kiphat = (t:v) (w:commend oneself/praise oneself) (d:reflexive of phat praise, with amahmah himself) (e:amahmah a ~ mi in san’ huai lo hi) (b:phat) (r:47.10.18) (q:draft)
kiphatin = (t:v) (w:being praised/praised) (d:kiphat be praised, with the linking ending in) (e:Mipilte ~ kipahtawi a) (b:kiphat) (r:20.12.8) (q:draft)
kiphatna = (t:n) (w:praise/commendation) (d:praise that someone receives; kiphatna lai is a letter of recommendation) (e:nangmah hong ~ in zong a zel hi) (b:phatna) (r:19.48.10/47.3.1) (q:draft)
kiphatnate = (t:n) (w:praises) (d:kiphatna praise, with the plural te) (e:nangmah a hong ~ phawk kikkik inla) (b:kiphatna) (r:19.9.14/23.42.8) (q:draft)
kiphatphat = (t:v) (w:be praised again and again/be praised continually) (d:passive of phatphat keep praising) (e:nangma nasepnate ~ ding a) (b:phatphat) (r:19.145.4) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/be arrogant) (d:praise oneself; before pau or gamtat it means speak or behave proudly) (e:na ~ gamtat nawn kei ding uh) (b:kiphat) (r:33.2.3/19.17.10) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be praised) (d:ki- form of phatsak, let someone or something be praised) (e:mi cimawhte nangma min ~ in) (b:phatsak) (r:19.74.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphatsakna = (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boasting) (e:~ in pukna hong piang sak hi) (r:20.16.18/19.75.5) (q:draft)
kiphatsaknate = (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boastings) (d:plural: acts or kinds of pride) (e:a ~ uh a lakkhia ahi hi) (b:kiphatsakna) (r:18.36.9/23.23.9) (q:draft)
kiphatsakpih = (t:v) (w:take pride in/boast of) (d:kiphatsak with pih: be proud on account of something; before a noun or standing alone, the thing one is proud of, the pride) (e:a ~ uh kizepna a manphate) (b:kiphatsak) (r:26.7.20/3.26.19) (q:draft)
kiphattawm = (t:v) (w:commend oneself/praise oneself/boast) (e:nangma kamin ~ kei in) (r:20.27.2/47.10.18) (q:draft)
kiphatte = (t:n) (w:those who commend themselves) (d:kiphat, praise oneself, with the plural te) (e:Amau mah a ~ tawh) (b:kiphat) (r:47.10.12) (q:draft)
kiphawk = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be missed) (d:passive of phawk; with nawn lo, be forgotten) (e:amah ~ tawntung ding hi) (b:phawk) (r:19.112.6/9.20.18) (q:draft)
kiphawkin = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be realised) (d:kiphawk, be remembered or noticed, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:hih nite ~ a kitan’ nading) (b:kiphawk) (r:17.9.28/41.14.9) (q:draft)
kiphawkkha = (t:v) (w:be remembered/come to mind) (d:mostly with nawn lo, be remembered no more) (e:A beisa nate ~ nawn lo a) (b:phawkkha) (r:21.1.11/23.65.17) (q:draft)
kiphawkkhia = (t:v) (w:be found/be discovered) (d:passive of phawkkhia, find out: come to light, here of something found written in a book) (e:a kihel ngei loh nading thu ~ hi) (b:phawkkhia) (r:16.13.1) (q:draft)
kiphawkmawh = (t:v) (w:overlook/pretend not to notice/hold back) (d:with bawl, do: act as if one had not noticed a wrong, let it pass) (e:mi’ hong hehsaknate ~ bawlna in minthan’na hi) (r:20.19.11/26.24.14) (q:draft)
kiphawkna = (t:n) (w:memory/remembrance) (d:the fact of being remembered; with bei or beisak, the memory of someone is wiped out) (e:leitung panin amah a ~ bei ta hen) (b:kiphawk) (r:19.109.15/5.32.26) (q:draft)
kiphawkphawk = (t:v) (w:be long remembered/be remembered continually) (e:mipilte zong ~ tuan lo hi) (b:phawkphawk) (r:21.2.16/20.10.7) (q:draft)
kiphawksak = (t:v) (w:cause to be remembered/keep in memory/be remembered) (d:kiphawk be remembered with sak causative) (e:Israel min ~ nawn kei ni) (b:kiphawk) (r:19.83.4/19.45.17) (q:draft)
kiphawktel = (t:v) (w:realise/perceive/know clearly) (d:phawktel, realise, with the prefix ki) (e:ama kumpigam a liatsakna ~ hi) (b:phawktel) (r:10.5.12) (q:draft)
kipheek = (t:adj) (w:braided/plaited) (d:said of hair, with sam) (e:a ~ sam tawh ahi zongin) (r:54.2.9) (q:draft)
kiphel = (t:v) (w:be loosed/be untied/be taken down) (e:vantungah a ~ ding hi) (b:phel) (r:40.18.18/4.10.17) (q:draft)
kiphel = (t:v) (w:split apart/split open) (e:amau’ nuai-ah lei ~ kham hi) (b:phel) (r:4.16.31) (q:draft)
kiphel = (t:v) (w:defend oneself/clear oneself) (d:speak to free oneself from a charge or to prove innocence) (e:a ~ nading thu hong gen a) (b:phel) (r:44.26.1/1.44.16) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (t:v) (w:be quenched/be put out) (d:passive of phelh quench, of a fire) (e:mei a ~ zo kei ding hi) (b:phelh) (r:24.17.27) (q:draft)
