kisinna = (t:n) (w:training/exercise/practice) (d:kisin train oneself, with the noun ending na) (e:Pumpi kisekin ~ manpha hi) (b:kisin) (r:54.4.8) (q:draft)
kisinsa = (t:v) (w:have learned/trained) (d:kisin learn or train oneself, with sa, already: one who has learned) (e:a lungkimthei dingin a ~ ka hi hi) (b:kisin) (r:50.4.12/50.4.11) (q:draft)
kisinsak = (t:v) (w:train/teach/be trained) (d:kisin, learn or practise, with causative sak: make someone or something learn; also of a person who has been given training) (e:zuauthu gen dingin ~ uh a) (b:kisin) (r:24.9.5/27.1.4) (q:draft)
kisisak = (t:v) (w:bring death on oneself/destroy oneself) (d:sisak cause to die, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:na mawhna hangun ~ kei un) (b:sisak) (r:26.18.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisit = (t:v) (w:be tried/be examined/be tested) (d:be examined, of a case heard in court as thu kisit, or of a person tested as by fire) (e:Amah thu a ~ ciangin) (r:19.109.7/60.4.12) (q:draft)
kisitin = (t:v) (w:be tried/be judged/be examined) (d:kisit with the linking ending in; thu kisitin, when the case is tried, and) (e:thu ~ mawhsakna a thuak uh ciangin) (b:kisit) (r:19.141.6) (q:draft)
kisitna = (t:n) (w:veil/covering) (d:the thing that covers, here the veil over the heart) (e:tua a ~ a kipaaikhia hi) (r:47.3.16) (q:draft)
kisitsak = (t:v) (w:be kept for/be set aside for) (d:be kept back for someone; written kisiitsak in the other text) (e:nang a dingin hong ~ ahi hi) (r:9.9.24) (q:draft)
kisittel = (t:v) (w:examine oneself/be tested) (d:test or examine oneself, a kisittel zo lo is one who fails the test) (e:nomau pumpi uh na ~ ciat un) (b:sittel) (r:47.13.5/47.13.6) (q:draft)
kisosuah = (t:v) (w:flare up/be stirred up/rouse oneself) (d:of anger, flare up, of a person, rouse oneself to act) (e:amau hehna a ~ ciangin) (b:sosuah) (r:19.124.3/19.35.23) (q:draft)
kisu = (t:v) (w:be struck/be touched) (d:passive of su, touch or strike; with kha: be struck or touched by something, as by the heat of the sun) (e:tawh a ~ kha nawn kei ding uh hi) (b:su) (r:66.7.16) (q:draft)
kisu = (t:v) (w:wrong each other/harm each other) (d:su, harm, with the prefix ki, each other; with khatlekhat, one another) (e:Note khatlekhat ~-in) (b:su) (r:46.6.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisu = (t:v) (w:be pounded/be crushed) (d:passive of su, pound; sum sunga a kisu, what is pounded in a mortar) (e:sum sunga a ~ gawp bangin) (b:su) (r:23.41.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuah = (t:v) (w:be made into/be divided into/be split into) (d:after a number with phel or khen: be torn or divided into that many parts) (e:a nuai lam dongin phel nih ~ hi) (b:suah) (r:41.15.38/40.27.51) (q:draft)
kisuahin = (t:v) (w:become/be made into/be divided into) (d:kisuah, be made into, with the linking ending in; after a number of parts: forming that many groups) (e:Gam khat peuhpeuh phelnih ~ kido le-uh) (b:kisuah) (r:41.3.24/7.9.34) (q:draft)
kisuahtak = (t:v) (w:escape/get away/save oneself) (d:form of suahtak with ki-, often before thei or zo, be able to escape) (e:a tai hatte nangawn ~ zo lo ding a) (b:suahtak) (r:30.2.15/24.51.6) (q:draft)
kisuai = (t:v) (w:be portrayed/be drawn/be engraved) (d:of figures and pictures, be drawn or worked on a surface) (e:mangkawlsing lim a ~ hi) (r:24.52.22/26.8.10) (q:draft)
kisuak = (t:v) (w:be made to become/be made into) (d:suak become, with the prefix ki; found with the causative sak written apart, as innkuan khat kisuak sak, be made one family) (e:innkuan khat ~ sakin sim khatin kisim khawm hi) (b:suak) (r:13.23.11) (q:draft)
kisuaksak = (t:v) (w:make oneself become/turn oneself into) (d:suaksak cause to become, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:mi na ~ kei ding uh hi) (b:suaksak) (r:5.7.26) (q:draft)
kisuaktasak = (t:v) (w:be delivered/be set free/be spared) (d:passive of suaktasak with the prefix ki) (e:Nang hong ~ tuan ding ahi hiam) (b:suaktasak) (r:23.37.11) (q:draft)
kisuam = (t:v) (w:be attacked/be assassinated/be struck down) (d:passive of suam with the prefix ki) (e:Gedaliah a ~ ni zing ciang) (b:suam) (r:24.41.4) (q:draft)
kisuampa = (t:n) (w:the man who was attacked/victim) (d:kisuam be attacked, with pa for a man: the man who was set upon by robbers) (e:a ~ a dingin a koi pen) (b:kisuam) (r:42.10.36) (q:draft)
kisuan = (t:v) (w:be planted) (d:passive of suan, said of trees, vines and seed) (e:inn sungah amaute ~ a) (b:suan) (r:19.92.13/26.17.8) (q:draft)
kisuan = (t:v) (w:set out/move) (d:said of a camp that breaks up and moves on) (e:giahphual a ~ ding ciangin) (r:4.4.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuan = (t:v) (w:feel guilty/reproach oneself) (d:found with the ending na as guilt or fault; lungsim kisuan'na is the conscience, a guilty conscience) (e:lungsim ~’na om lohna) (r:54.1.5/20.4.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuan'takna = (t:n) (w:self-defence/defending oneself) (d:speaking to clear or justify oneself; kisuan'takna kampau is words of self-defence) (e:tu dongin ~ kampau hi ci-in) (r:47.12.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuang = (t:v) (w:be set on/be placed upon) (d:be set or mounted on top of something, as gold on silver or a wreath on the head) (e:kham tang khat a ~ tawh kibang hi) (r:20.25.11/23.28.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuang = (t:v) (w:blush/feel shame) (d:feel shame or guilt; lungsim kisuang het loin is with a clear conscience) (e:~ thei beek lo uh hi) (r:24.8.12/1.20.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuangthei = (t:v) (w:be able to blush/be able to feel shame) (d:kisuang with thei, can; used with lo: not know how to blush) (e:~ beek lo uh hi) (b:kisuang) (r:24.8.12/24.6.15) (q:draft)
kisuanin = (t:v) (w:carry on the shoulder/take up/shoulder) (d:kisuan, put a load on one's own shoulder, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:ka liangko-ah van ~ ka paikhia hi) (b:kisuan) (r:26.12.7/40.16.24) (q:draft)
kisuankhia = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be driven out/be conquered) (e:Edom mite ~ ding a) (b:suankhia) (r:4.24.18/24.31.40) (q:draft)
kisuankhiatna = (t:n) (w:being driven out/overthrow) (d:suankhiatna driving out, with the passive prefix ki) (e:a ~ ding le a kisiatna ding) (b:suankhiatna) (r:24.31.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuanna = (t:n) (w:self-reproach/guilty conscience/guilt) (d:the accusing of oneself in the heart for a wrong done) (e:ka lungsim-ah ~ om loin siang mahmah hi) (r:18.27.6/62.3.21) (q:draft)
kisuanna = (t:n) (w:planting/place of planting) (d:being planted; a kisuanna mun is the place where a thing was planted) (e:Tua a ~ munah keutum lel ding) (b:kisuan) (r:26.17.10) (q:draft)
kisuannasa = (t:n) (w:place where planted/planting) (d:kisuanna with sa, already; ama kisuannasa mun is the place where it had been planted) (e:ama ~ mun-a tui a ngahsa sangin) (b:kisuanna) (r:26.17.7) (q:draft)
kisuantawm = (t:v) (w:bring on oneself/incur) (d:of guilt, be laid on oneself by one's own act) (e:mawhna a ~ suakin si ding) (r:2.28.43) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuanto = (t:v) (w:lift onto/put up on/load on) (d:with liangko-ah: lift a load up onto one's own shoulder) (e:na van na liangko-ah ~ in la) (r:26.12.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisugawp = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be destroyed/be oppressed) (d:passive ki- form of sugawp, crush) (e:kulh kongpi gei-ah amaute ~ a) (b:sugawp) (r:18.5.4/5.28.33) (q:draft)
kisuh = (t:v) (w:be seized/be plundered/be confiscated) (d:passive of suh with the prefix ki, of goods or animals taken by force) (e:na sum na paite uh hong ~ ciangin) (b:suh) (r:58.10.34/24.49.32) (q:draft)
kisuhna = (t:n) (w:plunder/pillage/seizure) (d:kisuh with the noun ending na; neihsa kisuhna is the seizing of what one owns) (e:neihsa ~, leh maizumna thuak uh a) (b:kisuh) (r:15.9.7) (q:draft)
kisui = (t:v) (w:be carved/be hewn/be graven) (d:shaped by cutting; a kisui milim is a carved image, named beside a kisung milim, a cast image) (e:A ~ milimte muangin) (b:sui) (r:23.42.17/19.144.12) (q:draft)
kisuih = (t:v) (w:stumble/trip) (d:suih stumble, with the prefix ki; kisuih khak is a thing stumbled against, a stumbling block) (e:~ khak a, kipukna ahi zongin) (b:suih) (r:45.11.9) (q:draft)
kisuikha = (t:see) <kisuikha-in>
kisuikha-in = (t:v) (w:stumbling) (d:sui stumble, with the prefix ki, kha, happen to strike, and in linking to the next verb) (e:amaute ~ puk ding uh hi) (r:19.27.2) (q:draft)
kisuipuk = (t:v) (w:slip/stumble) (d:of the feet, slip so that one nearly falls) (e:ka khete ~ dektak a) (r:19.73.2) (q:draft)
kisuk = (t:v) (w:strike against/knock against/hit) (d:in kisuk khak, happen to strike against something, said of a foot against a stone) (e:suang tawh a ~ khak loh nadingin) (r:42.4.11/40.4.6) (q:draft)
kisuk = (t:v) (w:go down/rush down) (d:suk downward, with the prefix ki, paired with kito go up: kisuk leh kito, go down and up, rush back and forth) (e:~ leh kito leh uh a) (b:suk) (r:34.2.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisukcipna = (t:n) (w:oppression/suppression) (d:the state of being pressed down or crushed by others) (e:~ leh khemna veng lo hi) (b:sukcipna) (r:19.55.11/19.44.24) (q:draft)
kisukcipnate = (t:n) (w:oppressions) (d:kisukcipna oppression, with the plural te) (e:hong ~ mangngilh na hi hiam) (b:kisukcipna) (r:19.44.24) (q:draft)
kisukgawpna = (t:n) (w:violence/ravaging/destruction) (d:sukgawpna with the prefix ki: the striking down or ravaging of one another) (e:Kisuksiatna leh ~ in hong umcih a) (b:sukgawpna) (r:35.1.3) (q:draft)
kisukha = (t:v) (w:have to do with/associate with/come into contact with) (d:touch or affect one another; with tawh, to have dealings with someone, and of a dead body, to come into contact with it) (e:a gamta mite tawh ~ vet kei un) (b:sukha) (r:49.5.7/4.5.2) (q:draft)
kisukham = (t:v) (w:be broken/be smashed/be crushed) (d:passive ki- form of sukham, break in pieces, said mostly of a clay pot) (e:a kihuanna leibeel ~ ding hi) (b:sukham) (r:3.6.28/24.19.11) (q:draft)
kisukkhak = (t:v) (w:be touched/come into contact/be harmed) (d:passive of sukkhak, touch; used with tawh for the thing touched; of a person, have a hand laid on him) (e:misi tawh a ~ manin mi nin) (b:sukkhak) (r:37.2.13/6.2.19) (q:draft)
kisukmang = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out/be annihilated) (d:passive of sukmang with the prefix ki) (e:Amaute a ~ nadingin Susa khua panin) (b:sukmang) (r:17.4.8) (q:draft)
kisukmit = (t:v) (w:be put out/be snuffed out/be extinguished) (d:of a lamp or fire, be made to go out) (e:meivak ~ sak ngei ahi hiam) (r:18.21.17) (q:draft)
kisukmitsak = (t:v) (w:be snuffed out/be put out/be extinguished) (d:of a lamp, be made to go out: kisukmit with the causative sak) (e:amaute’ meivak ~ ding hi) (b:kisukmit) (r:20.24.20/18.21.17) (q:draft)
kisuksiat = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be ruined) (d:passive of suksiat, the form used before khit, loh, nading and similar words) (e:ka tapa a ~ loh nadingin) (b:suksiat) (r:10.14.11/5.12.30) (q:draft)
kisuksiatna = (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin) (d:the destroying of people or things, also people destroying one another) (e:ngongtatna leh ~ ka za ngitnget a) (b:suksiatna) (r:24.6.7/35.1.3) (q:draft)
kisuksiatsak = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be demolished/be ruined) (d:passive ki- form of suksiatsak, destroy) (e:a innte uh ~ ding hi) (b:suksiatsak) (r:36.1.13/24.4.20) (q:draft)
kisuktat = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be blotted out) (d:passive of suktat with the prefix ki; of the memory of a person, be wiped from the earth) (e:a kiphawkna a ~ nadingin) (b:suktat) (r:19.34.16) (q:draft)
kisuliam = (t:v) (w:wound oneself/cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:su strike and liam wound, with the reflexive prefix ki; no leh no kisuliam is wound yourselves) (e:no leh no ~ ding na hi) (r:24.47.5) (q:draft)
kisumai = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out) (d:passive of sumai destroy with the prefix ki) (e:a vekpi-in ~ ding hi) (b:sumai) (r:38.5.4) (q:draft)
kisumit = (t:v) (w:be put out/be extinguished/be quenched) (d:passive of sumit, put out a fire or lamp) (e:Migilopa’ meivak ~ ding a) (b:sumit) (r:18.18.5/24.7.20) (q:draft)
kisun = (t:prep) (w:like) (e:a ~ lel ahi hi) (r:43.9.9)
kisun = (t:adj) (w:similar) (e:a ~ lel ahi hi) (r:43.9.9)
kisun'napa = (t:n) (d:the man on whom something has been poured; here the priest on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (r:3.21.10) (q:draft)
kisuncip = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be thrust down/be struck down) (d:found with suk, down, of people struck down so that they cannot rise) (e:amaute ~ sukin, tho zo lo uh hi) (r:19.36.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
