kisunin = (t:n) (w:likeness) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ a kibawl) (b:kisun) (r:1.5.1/59.3.9)
kisunnapa = (t:n) (d:the man on whom something has been poured; here the priest on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (e:nilh sathau a ~) (r:3.21.10) (q:draft)
kisupaisa = (t:adj) (w:torn down/demolished/broken down) (d:ki with supai tear down and sa, already: that has been torn down) (e:biakna tau a ~ khat puah kik hi) (r:11.18.30) (q:draft)
kisusia = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be ruined) (d:passive of susia, destroy) (e:Moab gam ~ khin ta a) (b:susia) (r:24.48.4/19.73.19) (q:draft)
