kisutkhia = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be taken away) (d:passive of sutkhia take away by force, with the prefix ki) (e:A thahatte’ neihsa nate ~ a) (b:sutkhia) (r:19.76.5) (q:draft)
kisutkhiat = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be taken away) (d:form of kisutkhia used before sak and other following words) (e:A kalaohte uh ~ sak ding a) (b:kisutkhia) (r:24.49.32) (q:draft)
kisutsak = (t:v) (w:let be robbed/be deprived of) (d:kisut be robbed, with sak; with kei un, do not let something be taken from you) (e:note lungdamna ~ kei un) (b:kisut) (r:51.2.18) (q:draft)
kisutte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:things taken by force, usually van kisutte plundered goods) (e:galte’ van ~ hawm uh a) (b:kisut) (r:19.68.12/14.14.14) (q:draft)
kisutuah = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:of people, come together in one place) (e:nasem ding bekin tua lai-ah ~ uh hi) (r:16.5.16/26.33.31) (q:draft)
kisuvui = (t:v) (w:be ground/be crushed to powder) (d:passive of suvui with the prefix ki; a kisuvui mangbuh is ground wheat) (e:a ~ mangbuh beem tul sawmnih) (b:suvui) (r:14.2.10) (q:draft)
kisuzan = (t:v) (w:be broken in pieces/be crushed/be shattered) (d:passive of suzan; of olives, be pressed or beaten for oil) (e:a biak milim ~ ding hi) (b:suzan) (r:28.8.6/2.27.20) (q:draft)
kisuzanin = (t:v) (w:being broken to pieces/being smashed) (d:kisuzan be broken in pieces, with in linking to the next verb) (e:A milim manphate khempeuh ~) (b:kisuzan) (r:33.1.7) (q:draft)
kisuzante = (t:n) (w:pressed ones/crushed ones) (d:kisuzan with plural te: things that have been crushed; oliv gah a kisuzante are pressed olives) (e:oliv gah a ~ panin sathau siangtho) (b:kisuzan) (r:3.24.2) (q:draft)
kitaaklah = (t:v) (w:meddle/interfere) (d:busy oneself with matters that are not one's own) (e:kisai lo thute ah a ~) (r:53.3.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitaangko = (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be announced) (d:passive of taangko with the prefix ki) (e:kisiatna ding thu hong ~ hi) (b:taangko) (r:24.4.15/3.23.24) (q:draft)
kitaangsapna = (t:n) (w:need/want) (d:what a person is lacking and has to be helped with) (e:midangte’ ~ huh tawntung in) (r:20.3.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitaat = (t:v) (w:be cut/be ground) (d:of gemstones, be worked or shaped before setting; taat is sharpen or whet) (e:onik suangte ~ a) (b:taat) (r:2.39.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
