laknop = (t:v) (w:want to take/want to marry) (d:lak take, with nop want; here of taking a woman as wife) (e:a sanggampa’ zi a ~ kei leh) (r:5.25.7) (q:draft)
lakpa = (t:n) (w:one who shows) (d:the one who shows, lak with -pa marking a male person; lam a lakpa, one who shows the way, is a guide or adviser) (e:itna kip a ~ ka hi hi) (r:5.5.10/11.4.5) (q:draft)
lakpan = (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:lak, among, with pan, from) (e:misite ~ Ta upa a suak hi) (r:51.1.18/40.5.19) (q:draft)
lakpanin = (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:lakpan with the linking suffix in) (e:Ukpa sawmthumte ~ mi thumte paisukin) (b:lakpan) (r:10.23.13) (q:draft)
laksa = (t:adj) (w:taken/captured/seized) (d:lak, take, with -sa, already taken; a laksa before a noun is what someone has taken or captured) (e:David in Amalekte’ ~ khempeuh ngah kik hi) (b:lak) (r:9.30.18/14.17.2) (q:draft)
laksak = (t:v) (w:take away from/seize/plunder) (d:take something from someone, lak with sak) (e:Izipt kumpipa’ neih khempeuh ~ khin) (b:lak) (r:12.24.7/4.31.9) (q:draft)
laksak = (t:v) (w:take for/get for) (d:take something on behalf of another, as a wife for a son) (e:ama adingin zi nih ~ a) (b:lak) (r:14.24.3/1.34.4) (q:draft)
laksakin = (t:v) (w:take away/seize/rob) (d:laksak take from someone with the linking ending in: taking away, having seized) (e:Topa in a neih khempeuh ~) (b:laksak) (r:38.9.4/20.28.24) (q:draft)
laksakmang = (t:v) (w:take away completely/plunder) (d:laksak take away from, with mang, so that it is gone) (e:na nate uh hong ~ khin ding hi) (r:35.2.7) (q:draft)
laksakte = (t:n) (w:those who take away/those who seize) (d:laksak, take away from, with plural te) (e:a hong ~ tung panin lakik kei un) (b:laksak) (r:42.6.30/24.49.2) (q:draft)
laksakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to plunder/be able to take away) (d:laksak take away from, with zo be able) (e:ciang bekin ~ pan bek ding hi) (b:laksak) (r:41.3.27) (q:draft)
laksate = (t:n) (w:captives/those captured) (d:laksa, taken, with plural te: the people someone has taken) (e:galmatin na ~ that ding na hi hiam) (b:laksa) (r:12.6.22) (q:draft)
laksuk = (t:v) (w:take down/bring down) (d:lak take, with suk downward) (e:Zeisu’ luang a ~ khit ciangin) (b:lak) (r:41.15.46) (q:draft)
lakte = (t:n) (w:things taken/plunder/takings) (d:lak take or get with the plural te: the things or people taken or received; na lakte, things taken, plunder) (e:Hih in David’ na ~ ahi hi) (b:lak) (r:9.30.20/11.10.28) (q:draft)
lakte = (t:n) (w:those who show/guides/counselors) (d:lak show with the plural te; thu hong lakte, those who show me what to do) (e:tuate in keimah thu hong ~ ahi hi) (r:19.119.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
laktel = (t:v) (w:show clearly/make plain/prove/point out) (d:make something plainly known, as the truth of a word or the fault of a person) (e:nang’ khialhna hong ~ kik leh) (r:20.25.8/23.43.26) (q:draft)
laktelsak = (t:v) (w:let show clearly/make plain to) (d:laktel show clearly, with sak cause or allow) (e:geelsa teng hong ~ dih un) (b:laktel) (r:18.27.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakteng = (t:n) (w:all that was taken) (d:lak take, with teng all; a galvan lakteng is all the goods he has taken, his spoil) (e:a galvan ~ tawh a gamah ciahkik ding) (b:lak) (r:27.11.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakthei = (t:v) (w:be able to show/prove) (d:lak show with thei can) (e:a manna thu hong ~ het lo ding) (b:lak) (r:44.24.13/44.9.22) (q:draft)
laktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to take/be able to capture) (d:lak take with theih, the form of thei can before nadingin, so that one can take; phu laktheih is be able to take revenge) (e:Amaute in khuapi a ~ nadingin) (b:lak) (r:14.32.18/12.9.7) (q:draft)
laktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to present/be able to show) (d:lak show with theih, the form of thei can before nadingin) (e:ama kiangah hong ~ nadingin) (b:lak) (r:51.1.22) (q:draft)
lakthuah = (t:v) (w:take in addition/marry also) (d:lak, take, with thuah, in addition: take another wife besides the one already had) (e:zi dang khat a ~ leh) (r:2.21.10/3.20.14) (q:draft)
lakto = (t:v) (w:raise/lift up/hold up) (d:lak with to, up: hold something up high to be seen, as a banner) (e:mite tungah ka lim ka ~ ding hi) (b:lak) (r:23.49.22/23.13.2) (q:draft)
lakzawhna = (t:n) (w:conquest/capture) (d:lak take, with zawh succeed and the noun suffix na: the taking of a town) (e:Lodebar khua bang lel na ~ uhah) (r:30.6.13) (q:draft)
lakzo = (t:v) (w:have shown/make known) (d:lak show, with zo, marking the action as accomplished) (e:ka gen ding thu nong ~ hi) (b:lak) (r:27.2.23) (q:draft)
lal = (t:v) (w:migrate/move/wander/sojourn) (d:move from one place to live in another; lal-a om, to live as a sojourner away from home) (e:Amaute nisuahna lamah ~ uh a) (r:1.11.2/60.1.17) (q:draft)
lalcin = (t:n) (w:lantern) (e:~ leh meilah de-in) (r:43.18.3) (q:draft)
lalsak = (t:v) (w:move/resettle/cause to migrate) (d:lal, migrate, with sak, cause) (e:hih gamah tua khua panin a ~ hi) (b:lal) (r:44.7.4) (q:draft)
lam = (t:n) (w:way) (e:~ ka pial ngei kei hi) (r:18.23.11)
lam = (t:n) (w:path)
lam = (t:n) (w:direction) (e:koi ~ pai ding?) (r:1.2.8/4.3.29)
Lam = (t:n) (w:road/way) (d:Lam kawi is a crooked road) (e:~ kawi khempeuh kitangsak ding hi) (b:lam) (r:42.3.5) (q:draft)
lam-ethuai = (t:adj) (w:worth hoping for/to be looked forward to) (d:lam-et hope, with huai worthy of) (e:a ~ bangmah a om kei hi) (r:21.11.8) (q:draft)
lama = (t:prep) (w:on the side of/toward/facing) (d:lam, side or direction, with the suffix a joining it to what follows; nisuahna lama om is that is on the east side) (e:biakinn nisuahna ~ om kongpi-ah hong paipih a) (b:lam) (r:26.43.1/1.2.14) (q:draft)
lama = (t:ppm) (d:after a verb, at the time of doing or on the way; a kuan lama is as he goes in) (e:a kuan ~ a tot lampi teng mah) (b:lam) (r:26.46.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lama = (t:adv) (w:why) (d:Aramaic word quoted untranslated in the cry of Jesus on the cross, NIV lema) (r:41.15.34) (q:draft)
lamah = (t:n) (w:direction) (e:nisuahna ~) (b:lam) (r:11.18.6)
lamah = (t:n) (w:side/area) (e:hih ~ hong pai ve) (b:lam) (r:1.3.24)
lambaangin = (t:adv) (w:turning aside/stopping on the way) (d:leaving one's road to call on someone; the exact sense of baang is not confirmed) (e:hong ~, damlenat kitheihsakna-in hong hawh ding) (r:24.15.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
lambehte = (t:n) (w:side rooms/annexes) (d:rooms built on against the wall of a house; plural te) (e:a inn buppi tungah a ~ zomin) (r:11.6.10) (q:draft)
lamdan = (t:adj) (w:wonderful/marvellous/amazing) (d:lamdang written short, with an apostrophe, before mahmah) (r:47.12.7) (q:draft)
lamdang = (t:n) (w:surprise) (e:ka cihna ~ sa kei in) (r:43.3.7)
lamdang = (t:n) (w:shock)
lamdang = (t:v) (w:astonish/amaze/nonplus/startle/astound/stun)
lamdangdang = (t:adj) (w:strange/various strange) (d:lamdang, strange, with its last syllable repeated: strange things of many kinds) (e:a ~ thuhilhna thak zui kei un) (r:58.13.9/20.23.33) (q:draft)
lamdangin = (t:adv) (w:wonderfully/marvellously/strangely) (d:lamdang with in; pau lamdangin, in a strange tongue) (e:meel ~ kilang uh a) (b:lamdang) (r:42.9.30/19.31.21) (q:draft)
lamdanglua = (t:adj) (w:too wonderful/too amazing) (d:lamdang with lua, too much) (e:kei a dingin a ~ thu) (b:lamdang) (r:18.42.3) (q:draft)
lamdangpi = (t:adj) (w:very strange/marvellous/foreign) (d:lamdang with the intensifier pi; thu lamdangpi is a strange thing, a lamdangpi khatin is in a wonderful way) (e:thu ~ khatin ngaihsun lel uh hi) (b:lamdang) (r:28.8.12/14.26.15) (q:draft)
lamdangpipi = (t:adj) (w:very marvellous/most wonderful) (d:lamdangpi with pi repeated for emphasis; na lamdangpipi are marvellous things) (e:na ~ piang a) (b:lamdangpi) (r:18.37.5) (q:draft)
lamdangsa = (t:v) (w:be amazed/be astonished/be surprised/wonder) (d:find something strange or wonderful, lamdang with sa) (e:note hong muhdah uh leh, ~ kei un) (b:lamdang) (r:62.3.13/40.12.23) (q:draft)
lamdangsak = (t:v) (w:be surprised at/find strange/wonder at) (d:form of lamdangsa used before ding and huai: lamdangsak ding hi lo hi, it is no wonder) (e:Tua pen ~ ding hi lo hi) (b:lamdangsa) (r:47.11.14/30.5.13) (q:draft)
lamdangsakna = (t:n) (w:spectacle) (e:mite in ~ tawh nang hong en ding) (b:lamdangsak) (r:34.3.6/1.43.33)
lamdangte = (t:n) (w:wonders/wonderful deeds/marvels) (d:plural of lamdang wonderful, after na thing or nasepna deed) (e:nangma nasepna ~ ka gen kawm hi) (b:lamdang) (r:19.26.7/18.37.14) (q:draft)
lamding = (t:v) (w:build) (d:lam, build, with ding written as one word: to build, going to build) (e:inn ~ kipan napi-in zozo lo hi) (b:lam) (r:42.14.30/42.14.28) (q:draft)
lamdung = (t:n) (w:street/roadside/along the road) (d:the length of the road, the streets where people pass) (e:~ tengah vak tawntung hi) (r:20.7.11/20.7.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lamdungah = (t:adv) (w:along the road/along the path/on the street) (d:lamdung, the length of a road, street, with the marker ah; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khaici a tukna munte) (r:42.8.12/20.7.8) (q:draft)
Lamek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lamech) (r:1.5.28)
lamen = (t:v) (w:hope for/expect/look forward to) (e:midang khat ka ~ lai ding uh hiam) (r:40.11.3/61.3.13) (q:draft)
lamenin = (t:v) (w:hope/expect/wait for) (d:lamen with the linking ending in, hoping or expecting while another action follows) (e:a ngah ding ~ sawltakte a ento hi) (b:lamen) (r:44.3.5/45.8.19) (q:draft)
lamenpa = (t:n) (w:one who hopes for/one who waits for) (d:lamen with pa, the man who looks forward to something) (e:Pasian Gam a ~ hong pai-in) (b:lamen) (r:41.15.43) (q:draft)
lamente = (t:n) (w:those who wait for/those who look forward to) (d:lamen expect with the plural te) (e:amah a ~ gum dingin) (b:lamen) (r:58.9.28/55.4.8) (q:draft)
lamet = (t:v) (w:hope/hope for/expect/look for) (d:also used as a noun stem, hope, as in lamet tun’lohna, hope not fulfilled) (e:I muh loh nate i ~ leh) (r:45.8.25/18.30.26) (q:draft)
lametet = (t:v) (w:hope for/expect eagerly/long for) (d:lamet, hope, with its last syllable repeated: keep hoping for over a long time) (e:i ~ David’ suan hi lo ding) (r:40.12.23/50.1.20) (q:draft)
lamethuai = (t:adj) (w:hopeful/worth hoping for) (d:lamet, hope, with huai, worthy of; a lamethuai bangmah om lo is there is nothing to hope for) (e:Mailamah a ~ bangmah a om kei hi) (r:21.11.8/25.2.13) (q:draft)
lametin = (t:adv) (w:as one's hope) (d:lamet, hope, with in; lametin nei is to have as one's hope, put one's hope in) (e:amah bek mah ~ nei ding uh hi) (b:lamet) (r:40.12.21/19.62.10) (q:draft)
lametna = (t:n) (w:hope/expectation) (e:Mihoihte’ ~ in lungdamna hi a) (r:20.10.28/25.3.29) (q:draft)
lametnate = (t:n) (w:hopes/things hoped for) (d:plural of lametna) (e:Upna in ~ telcianna hi a) (b:lametna) (r:58.11.1) (q:draft)
lametnateng = (t:n) (w:all hope/every expectation) (d:lametna with teng, all) (e:A pi’ ~ beita hi) (b:lametna) (r:26.19.5) (q:draft)
lametpa = (t:n) (w:hope/the one hoped in) (d:lamet with pa, the male person in whom others hope; said of the Lord) (e:Israel mite’ ~ aw) (b:lamet) (r:24.17.13) (q:draft)
lametsakna = (t:n) (w:giving of hope/cause for hope) (d:lamet, hope, with sak, cause, and na: that by which someone is made to hope) (e:Keimah nong ~ ahi na nasempa’) (r:19.119.49) (q:draft)
lamette = (t:n) (w:things hoped for) (d:lamet with the plural te, the things one hopes for) (e:i ~ ngah takpi ding) (b:lamet) (r:58.11.1) (q:draft)
lamgal = (t:n) (w:side/bank) (d:the land on one side of a river; hih lamgal is this side) (e:Jordan hih ~ nisuahna lam) (r:4.32.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
