lamlahnate = (t:n) (w:instructions/directions/guideposts) (d:lamlahna, guidance, with plural te; on a road, the signs that show the way) (e:hih bang ~ kong piak uh/Lampi-ah ciamtehnate bawl unla, ~ phut un | set up road signs, put up guideposts) (s:vaikhaknate) (b:lamlahna) (r:52.4.2/24.31.21) (q:draft)
lamlak = (t:v) (w:guide/counsel/advise/direct) (d:show the way; thu lamlak is to give counsel and thu lamlak pa a counselor) (e:minamte leitungah ~ na hih manin/Topa in a mite ~ ahih manin | because the Lord guided his people/thu ~ pa bangin kua in amah hilh | who has taught him as his counselor/thu ~ tampi neihna in lungmuan’ na hi | having many advisers is safety/thu ~ amaute lakah om lo hi | there is no one among them to give counsel) (s:lamkaih/makaih) (a:lampialsak/lakkhial) (r:19.67.4/20.11.14/23.63.14/23.40.13/23.41.28) (q:draft)
lamlakin = (t:v) (w:guiding/directing/instructing) (d:lamlak, guide, with the linking ending in) (e:leitung minamte khempeuh ~ makai na hih manin/kumpipa’ uliante ama ut bangin ~ | directing the king's officials as he pleased) (b:lamlak) (r:19.67.4/19.105.21) (q:draft)
lamlakpa = (t:n) (w:counselor/adviser) (d:lam way and lak show, with pa for a man, one who shows the way; thu lamlakpa is a counselor) (e:amah thu ~ Ahuzzath leh a galkap mangpa/thu ~ bangin kua in amah hilh | who has taught him as his counselor/thu ~ leh khut siampa | the counselor and the skilled craftsman) (s:thulamlakpa/vaihawmpa) (b:lamlak) (r:1.26.26/23.40.13/23.3.3) (q:draft)
lamlakte = (t:n) (w:advisers/counselors/guides) (d:those who show the way, lamlak with plural -te; thu lamlakte are advisers) (e:a thu ~ in/Faro’ mipil thu ~ in thu haihuai gen | Pharaoh's wise counselors give senseless advice/kumpipa le a thu ~ le a uliante | the king, his advisers and his officials) (s:thulamlakte) (b:lamlak) (r:15.7.15/23.19.11/15.8.25) (q:draft)
lamlam = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after kot, circle around, for birds hovering round and round overhead) (e:A kot ~ vasate bangin) (r:23.31.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamlian = (t:n) (w:main road/highway/street) (d:lam road with lian big; contrasted with lamneu, a lane or small path) (e:~ lam tawnin ka pai to ding/Khua sung ~ ah ahi zongin | whether in the streets of the town/~ kiu khempeuh ah amaute lum uh hi | they lie at every street corner/bawngpite ~ dung zui-in Bethshemesh lamah | the cows followed the road toward Beth Shemesh) (s:lamlianpi/kongzing) (a:lamneu) (r:4.20.19/42.14.21/23.51.20/9.6.12) (q:draft)
Lamlian = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Lamlian/Highway) (d:the Highway, in Kumpipa' Lamlian the King's Highway, the main road through Edom and the Amorite land east of the Jordan) (r:4.20.17/4.21.22)
lamlianpi = (t:n) (w:main road/highway/street) (d:lamlian main road, with pi big; set against lamneu, small path) (e:Nasemte zong ~-ah va pai uh a/~-ah va pai unla | go out to the main roads/Nangma ~ tuipi tung hi a | your highway was through the sea) (s:lamlian) (a:lamneu) (b:lamlian) (r:40.22.10/19.77.19/40.22.9) (q:draft)
lamliante = (t:n) (w:main roads/highways/roads) (d:lamlian, main road, with the plural te; set against lamneute, lanes) (e:Gam sung ~ le lamneute-ah va pai inla) (a:lamneute) (b:lamlian) (r:42.14.23) (q:draft)
lammat = (t:v) (w:seize/compel/press into service) (d:lam way with mat seize: lay hold of a passer-by and force him to do something) (e:a pua dingin ~ uh hi) (r:41.15.21) (q:draft)
lammatin = (t:v) (w:seizing/compelling) (d:lammat with the linking suffix in) (e:amah ~ Jesuh’ singlamteh a puasak uh hi) (b:lammat) (r:40.27.32) (q:draft)
lamna = (t:n) (w:building/construction) (d:the act of building a house, altar or temple) (e:biakna tau khat ~ tawh/biakinn khat a ~ thu | the news of the building of a temple/tua a ~-in kum sagih bei hi | he spent seven years building it) (s:innlamna/kilamna) (b:lam) (r:6.22.16/15.4.1/11.6.38) (q:draft)
lamna = (t:n) (w:dancing/dance) (d:the act of dancing, as a sign of joy and in praise; another spelling of laamna) (e:bawngno leh ~ a muh phetin/Khuang le ~ tawh amah phat unla | praise him with timbrel and dancing/a gualnuamte’ ~-ah na va kihel ding hi | you will join in the dance of the joyful/ka taunate ~ tawh nong heisak a | you turned my wailing into dancing) (s:laamna) (r:2.32.19/19.150.4/24.31.4/19.30.11) (q:draft)
lamnal = (t:n) (w:slippery path/slippery way) (d:lam way with nal slippery) (e:khuamial lak ~ hi ding a) (r:24.23.12) (q:draft)
lamnasa = (t:adj) (d:lam, build or set up, with the endings na and sa: where something has been built or pitched; a puanbuk lamnasa leitang is the ground where he had pitched his tent) (e:a puanbuk ~ leitang dangka zakhat tawh) (b:lamna) (r:1.33.19) (q:draft)
lamnawl = (t:n) (w:roadside/side of the road) (d:lam, road, with nawl, edge; lamnawl lam tawnin pai is to pass by along the far side of the road) (e:~ lam tawnin a paisan hi/~ lam tawnin a paisan leuleu hi | he too passed by on the other side) (r:42.10.31/42.10.32) (q:draft)
lamneu = (t:n) (w:lane/alley/small path) (d:lam, road, with neu, small; set against lamlian, main road) (e:~ ah ahi zongin pai in la/nangma ~ in tui liante tung ahi hi | your path was through the great waters) (a:lamlian/lamlianpi) (r:42.14.21/19.77.19) (q:draft)
lamneute = (t:n) (w:lanes/small paths) (d:lamneu, small path, with the plural te; set against lamliante, main roads) (e:nangma ~ zong luiliante’ tung mah ahi hi/lamliante le ~-ah va pai inla | go out to the roads and the lanes) (a:lamliante) (b:lamneu) (r:19.77.19/42.14.23) (q:draft)
lamnop = (t:v) (w:want to build/wish to build) (d:lam build with nop, the form of nuam want; a lamnop khempeuh is all that he wished to build) (e:Solomon in a ~ khempeuh a lamkik hi/kumpi inn le a ~ khempeuh | the royal palace and all he wished to build/ama ukna gam sung khempeuhah a ~ khempeuh | all he wished to build throughout his realm) (r:11.9.19/11.9.1/14.8.6) (q:draft)
lamnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to build/will to build) (d:lamnop want to build, with the noun suffix na) (e:biakinn ~ lungsim a guan hi) (b:lamnop) (r:37.1.14) (q:draft)
lamnu = (t:n) (w:builder) (d:lam build, with nu, the woman who built) (e:Uzzenerah khua a ~ ahi hi) (b:lam) (r:13.7.24) (q:draft)
lampa = (t:n) (w:builder) (d:lam, build, with pa, which marks a man: the man who builds; inn lampa is the builder of a house) (e:Inn ~ in inn sangin) (s:lamkippa) (b:lam) (r:58.3.3) (q:draft)
lampai = (t:v) (w:walk/travel/go on a journey) (d:lam, road, and pai, go, also used as a noun, journey) (e:Tuipi nuai leitam tungah ~ ngei/tua khuavak sungah ~ leh pukkha cih om lo | whoever walks in that light does not stumble/zan khuamial sungah ~ leh | if one walks in the dark of night/~ kawmin lungdamna a ko dingin | to give thanks while walking/lungdam takin a ~ a zom hi | he went on his way rejoicing) (s:khualzin) (r:18.38.16/43.11.9/43.11.10/16.12.31/44.8.39) (q:draft)
