lampang = (t:n) (w:side) (d:the side lying in a given direction, as in leilu lampang, north side) (e:Leilu ~ a ding zong/nisuahna ~ teh a | he measured the east side/Leitaw ~ a dingin khuam sawmnih | twenty frames for the south side/Leilu ~ a om kulhkongpi thumte | the three gates on the north side) (s:pang) (r:2.38.11/26.48.10/26.42.16/2.36.23/26.48.30) (q:draft)
lampangah = (t:n) (w:on the side/at the side) (d:lampang side with the place marker ah; with a direction word, on the south side, on the north side) (e:biakbuk leitaw ~ giahphual sat ding uh a/biakna tau tung leilu ~ go ding a | he is to slaughter it at the north side of the altar/tua ~ thaltang thum ka lawn ding hi | I will shoot three arrows to that side/leitaw ~ nga omin | five being on the south side) (b:lampang) (r:4.3.29/9.20.20/3.1.11/11.7.49) (q:draft)
lampangte = (t:see) <lampangte-ah>
lampangte-ah = (t:adv) (w:on the sides) (d:lampang side, with the plural te and ah at) (e:hih lampang le hua ~ kaisuk ding hi) (r:2.26.13) (q:draft)
lampangteng = (t:n) (w:whole side/all of the side) (d:lampang, side, with teng, all of: the whole area on that side) (e:nisuahna ~ Gilead gam hi a/Jordan Gun nitumna ~ Israel gam hi-in | the whole west side of the Jordan being the land of Israel) (s:lamteng) (b:lampang) (r:26.47.18) (q:draft)
lampha = (t:v) (w:rebuild/build up/restore) (d:build again what was ruined, from lam, build) (e:tang lai-a a siasate ~ ding uh/Elath khua zo kikin ~ a | he retook Elath and rebuilt it/a kisia a khuapite uh ~ kikin | rebuilding their ruined cities/Solomon in ~-in tuate sungah Israel mite teeng sak | Solomon rebuilt them and settled Israelites in them) (s:lamkik/puahkik/bawlpha) (a:susia/phel) (r:23.61.4/12.14.22/30.9.14/14.8.2) (q:draft)
lamphei = (t:see) <lamphei-ah>
lamphei-ah = (t:n) (w:on a level path/on level ground) (d:lamphei, a level or even road, with the place marker ah) (e:ka galte hangin ~ hong kha in/Kei hong hehpih in la, ~ hong kha in | have mercy on me and lead me on level ground) (r:19.27.11/19.143.10) (q:draft)
lampi = (t:n) (w:way) (d:the way to a place, and the way of life a person follows) (e:Nopna ~ amau in a thei kei/pai nading mun ~ na thei uh hi | you know the way to the place I am going/thuman ~ ka zui a | I follow the way of righteousness) (s:lam/lamzin) (b:lam) (r:45.3.17/1.3.24/43.14.4/20.8.20)
lampi = (t:n) (w:footpath/path) (e:thutang ~ ka tawn hi | I walk along the paths of justice) (b:lam) (r:20.8.20)
lampi = (t:n) (w:road) (e:~-ah puante a phah uh hi/Tua ~ ah siampi khat paikha zenzen a | a priest happened to be going along that road) (b:lam) (r:42.19.36/42.10.31)
Lampi = (t:n) (w:way/road/path) (d:lampi written with a capital, mostly at the start of a sentence, also as a title, the Way as a name for the Christian faith, and in Lampi Siangtho, the Way of Holiness) (e:~ thu hangin thusia a piang hi/~ a pai lai takun tui omna-ah | as they went along the road they came to water/~ man panin ka pial a | if I have turned from the right path/nuntakna ~ nong hilh zo a | you have made known to me the path of life) (b:lampi) (r:44.19.23/23.35.8/44.8.36/18.31.7/44.2.28) (q:draft)
lampial = (t:v) (w:stray/turn aside/go astray) (d:leave the right way, lam way with pial turn off) (e:themkhat zong ~ lo hi/ka kalsuan uh ~ nai lo hi | our steps had not strayed/a teek dongin ~ nawn lo ding hi | even when old he will not turn from it/a gamtatna khempeuhah ~ het lo hi | in all his conduct he does not stray at all) (s:pial/pialkhia/gammang) (r:14.34.2/19.44.18/20.22.6/19.37.31) (q:draft)
lampial = (t:adj) (w:perverse/warped/wayward) (d:having left the right way, said of a perverse generation) (e:a ~ khang mite hi a/a ~, lungsim kawi khang mite | a warped and crooked generation) (r:5.32.20/5.32.5) (q:draft)
lampialgawp = (t:v) (w:be thrown off course/go wildly astray) (d:lampial leave the way, with gawp marking violent action; here of the heavenly bodies) (e:pai thei loin ~ ding hi) (b:lampial) (r:40.24.29) (q:draft)
lampialin = (t:v) (w:turning aside/going astray) (d:lampial turn aside, stray, with the linking ending in) (e:Kote khialin ~ ka gitloh tat uh hi/amah ~ a va et leh | when he turned aside to look) (s:pialin) (b:lampial) (r:11.8.47/7.14.8) (q:draft)
lampialna = (t:n) (w:straying/going astray/fall) (d:lampial, stray, with the noun suffix na: a leaving of the right way, a fall from where one stood) (e:na ~ uh phawkin) (s:pialna) (b:lampial) (r:66.2.5) (q:draft)
lampialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:lampial, go astray, with sak, cause) (e:omsak a, Judah mite ~ hi/amaute’ makaite in ~ uh hi | their leaders lead them astray) (s:pialsak/lakkhial/khialsak) (a:lamlak) (b:lampial) (r:14.21.11/23.9.16) (q:draft)
lampialte = (t:n) (w:strays/those who go astray) (d:lampial stray, with the plural te; of sheep that have strayed, and of people who have left the right way) (e:A ~ na khiang kei uh a/a mangte zongin, a ~ kaikhawmin | searching for the lost and gathering the strays) (s:pialte/pialkhiate) (b:lampial) (r:26.34.4/66.21.8/26.34.16) (q:draft)
lampidung = (t:n) (w:along the path/roadside) (d:lampi road with dung length, the stretch along a road) (e:pawlkhatte ~ tu a) (s:lamdung) (r:42.8.5) (q:draft)
lampih = (t:v) (w:build with/help build) (d:lam build, with pih together with) (e:Topa in inn ~ kei leh) (b:lam) (r:19.127.1) (q:draft)
lampite = (t:n) (w:ways/paths/roads) (d:lampi, way, with the plural te: roads and paths, also the ways of God, the conduct he asks for) (e:na ~ hong hilh in/nangma ~ ka mitsuan ding hi | I will fix my eyes on your ways/ama ~ i zuih theih nadingin | so that we may walk in his paths/note’ ~ in gamkhing suak ding hi | your roads will become deserted) (b:lampi) (r:19.25.4/23.41.3/19.119.15/23.2.3/3.26.22) (q:draft)
lampiteng = (t:n) (w:the same way/the whole way) (d:lampi way with teng, all of it; a tot lampiteng is the way by which he came) (e:a kuanlamin a tot ~ mah) (b:lampi) (r:26.46.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamsa = (t:adj) (w:built) (d:lam build with sa, already done: that someone has built, placed after the builder and before the thing built) (e:Mihingte’ ~ khuapi leh tausangpi/ama ~ a inn | the palace he had built/a ~ khuapi min Samaria phuak hi | he named the city he had built Samaria/ama ~ saiha inn | the ivory palace he built) (s:kilamsa) (r:1.11.5/11.10.4/11.16.24/11.22.39) (q:draft)
