lamsang = (t:n) (w:side/direction/respect) (d:with ah, on the side of, in the matter of, with regard to) (e:A pha ~ ah gamta a/mi ~ ah bang phattuamna a ngah | what did he gain on the human side/Thusia ~ a deih mite | people who want what is evil/lokhawhna ~ a lunghimawh kumpi | a king who cares about farming) (r:45.2.7/45.4.1/20.24.8/21.5.9) (q:draft)
lamsangah = (t:prep) (w:as regards/concerning/in respect of/according to) (d:lamsang, side or aspect, with ah; after a noun it means in the matter of) (e:Ci-le-sa ~ Israelte na en ta un/pilna ~ pil lo mi ka hi kei | in knowledge I am not untrained/thukham ~ mawhsakna a om lo | blameless as regards the law/piakna ~ cingh thei mahmah uh hi | in giving they were very generous) (s:tungtangah) (b:lamsang) (r:46.10.18/47.11.6/44.22.12/47.8.2) (q:draft)
lamsate = (t:n) (w:things built/buildings) (d:lamsa built, with the plural te: what someone has built) (e:keimah in ka ~ ka phelkik a/midangte’ inn ~ sutin a tang hi | he seized houses that others built) (b:lamsa) (r:24.45.4/18.20.19) (q:draft)
