lamto = (t:v) (w:lift up/raise) (d:lift something upward, said of raising the hand and of raising a person up from a low place) (e:na khut ~ in la/leivui panin mizawngte ~-in | raising the poor from the dust/a khut taklam vantung lamah ~ a | he raised his right hand toward heaven/a khut ~-in thupha a pia hi | he lifted up his hands and blessed them) (s:domto/laamto) (r:19.10.12/19.113.7/66.10.5/42.24.50) (q:draft)
lamun = (t:adv) (d:lam way, direction, with un, the ending in as used with a plural subject: in the direction of, in the course of; a nung leh lamun is backwards, an a zonna lamun is while they looked for food) (e:a nung leh ~ pai-in/an a zon’na ~ siampite leh makaite | while searching for food the priests and elders) (b:lam) (r:1.9.23/25.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
