langah = (t:prep) (w:against) (d:on the opposing side of, after a possessive as in ka langah against me) (e:teci man lote ka ~ pang khin a/leitung in ama ~ teci pang hi | the earth testifies against him/Na ~ siat nading vaihawm a | they plot harm against you/Na galte ~ kuanin | going out against your enemies) (s:langkhatah/langpangin) (b:lang) (r:19.27.12/18.20.27/19.21.11/5.23.9) (q:draft)
langaih = (t:n) (w:melody/music/sweet song) (d:pleasing song, la, song, with ngaih, lovely; langaih sa is to make music) (e:ama tungah ~ sa un/laiza lasakna leh ~ tawh phat un | praise with the music of the harp and with melody) (r:19.149.3/19.98.5) (q:draft)
langbawl = (t:v) (w:turn against/oppose/be hostile to) (d:lang side with bawl make: set oneself against someone) (e:a gamtatsia mite Topa in a ~ hi/nangawn in kei hong ~ uh hi | even they have turned against me/mi khempeuh ~ uh hi | they are hostile to everyone) (s:langpang/galbawl/langneih) (b:lang) (r:60.3.12/18.19.19/52.2.15) (q:draft)
langbawlna = (t:n) (w:opposition/hostility) (d:langbawl turn against, with the noun suffix na; in Proverbs 28:21 mi langbawlna is taking sides between people, partiality) (e:mawhnei mite’ ~ a thuaknate ngaihsun unla/Mi ~ hoih lo a | showing partiality is not good) (s:langpanna/kilangbawlna) (b:langbawl) (r:58.12.3/20.28.21) (q:draft)
langgen = (t:v) (w:show partiality/take the side of/favor) (d:lang, side, with gen, speak: speak for one side in a judgment) (e:mizawngte ~ loin, a liante thu zui loin) (s:angvan) (r:3.19.15) (q:draft)
langkhat = (t:n) (w:one side/other side/half) (d:one of two sides or of a pair, as in khut langkhat, one hand, and gam langkhat, half the kingdom) (e:pang ~ zong na dawh lai un/ka gam ~ dongin kong pia ding hi | I will give you up to half my kingdom/a khut ~ mah bangin a dam hi | it was restored like the other hand) (r:40.5.39/41.6.23/40.12.13) (q:draft)
langkhatah = (t:prep) (w:against) (d:on the opposite side; langkhatah pang is stand against, langkhatah teci pang is testify against) (e:na vengpa ~ teci pang kei in/note’ ~ teci ka pang ding hi | I will testify against you/Mihonpite in amau ~ a ding uh a | the crowd rose up against them/no ~ teci na pang uh hi | you testify against yourselves) (s:langah/langpangin) (r:20.24.28/23.14.22/19.50.7/44.16.22/40.23.31) (q:draft)
langkhiasak = (t:v) (w:display/make known/reveal) (d:lang, appear, with khia, out, and sak, cause: bring something out into open view) (e:mite lakah nangma vangliatna a ~ khin Pasian) (s:langsak/kilangsak) (r:19.77.14) (q:draft)
langmuh = (t:see) <langmuh-a>
langmuh-a = (t:adv) (w:with partiality/taking sides) (d:lang side and muh see, with a: looking to one side, showing favour) (e:Mi ~ thukhenna hoih lo hi) (r:20.24.23) (q:draft)
langneih = (t:v) (w:be against/oppose/take sides) (d:lang side with neih have: take a side about someone, mostly against; na langneih mite is your enemies; in Exodus 23:3 of taking sides over a poor man in a lawsuit) (e:mote in a teeknu uh ~ uh hi/Na ~ mite’ bawngtal | your enemies' ox/mizawng pa na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not take sides over a poor man) (s:langbawl) (r:33.7.6/2.23.4/2.23.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
langnih = (t:n) (w:both sides/two sides) (d:lang, side, with nih, two; langnih a hiam is sharp on both sides, double-edged; of a pair, as feet or parties, it means both) (e:~ a hiam namsau khat/a khe a ~-in a bai hi | he was lame in both feet/a pang ~ tuakah a kigelh suangpeekte | tablets written on both sides/thuneite a ~ tuakin | both parties to the dispute) (r:66.1.16/10.9.13/2.32.15/5.19.17) (q:draft)
langnihin = (t:adv) (w:on both sides/both) (d:langnih, both sides, with in; of a sword, double-edged; of feet, both) (e:a ~ a hiam mahmah namsau/a khe a ~ a zaw hi | he was lame in both feet) (b:langnih) (r:66.2.12/10.9.13) (q:draft)
langpa = (t:n) (w:opponent/other party/adversary) (d:lang, opposing side, with pa, which marks a man: the man on the other side) (e:a ~ in a thuk mateng/namsau tawh a ~’ pang dawt ciat uh hi | each thrust his sword into his opponent's side) (s:galpa) (b:lang) (r:20.18.17/10.2.16) (q:draft)
langpan = (t:v) (w:oppose/rise against/rebel against) (d:form of langpang, written langpan’ before a following word) (e:Mi tampi in kei hong ~’ nainai hi/kote in nang ka hong ~’ uh hi | we have rebelled against you/Hong ~ mi zong tampi a om uh hi | there are also many who oppose me/mi lehdote in ~’ kei uh hen | let the rebellious not rise against him) (s:langbawl/galbawl/lehdo) (r:19.3.1/27.9.9/46.16.9/19.66.7) (q:draft)
langpang = (t:v) (w:oppose/resist/rebel against) (d:take a stand against someone, lang, side, with pang, stand; the one opposed comes directly before it) (e:Amaute bangin hong ~ kei in/Topa ~ na hih manin | because you opposed the Lord/Izipt mite in ama thu ~ uh hi | the Egyptians rebelled against his word) (s:langbawl/galbawl/lehdo) (a:panpih) (r:26.2.8/19.35.1/24.50.24/19.105.28) (q:draft)
langpang = (t:n) (w:adversary/opponent) (d:one who stands against another, an opponent or enemy) (e:Solomon’ lang khatah ~ khat/hong ~ ahi a, thusia ahi zongin om lo | there is neither adversary nor disaster) (s:galpa/langpa) (r:11.11.14/11.5.4) (q:draft)
langpanga = (t:adv) (w:against/in opposition to) (d:langpang oppose, with a) (e:keimah ~ hong dingte kiang panin) (b:langpang) (r:19.59.1) (q:draft)
langpangin = (t:prep) (w:against) (d:langpang, oppose, with the linking suffix in; opposing, in opposition to) (e:na sanggamte ~ thu na gen uh hi/Topa leh ama sathau nilhpa ~ vaihawm uh a | they plot against the Lord and his anointed/keimah ~ kikaikhawm uh hi | they gathered against me/Pasian ~ a khuttum a lahsan | he shakes his fist against God) (s:langah/langkhatah) (b:langpang) (r:19.50.20/19.35.15/19.2.2/18.15.25) (q:draft)
langpangte = (t:n) (w:foes/adversaries/enemies/opponents) (d:langpang, oppose, with the plural te: those who stand against someone) (e:amah a ~ daantatin/a kimkot-a om ama ~ kangtum hi | it burns up his foes all around/amah ~ in leivui liak ta uh hen | may his foes lick the dust/Amah in, a ~ zo a | he defeated his foes) (s:galte/demte) (a:lawmte) (b:langpang) (r:34.1.2/19.97.3/19.72.9/19.78.66) (q:draft)
langpanin = (t:v) (w:opposing/against/defying) (d:form of langpan with -in; after its object it can be translated against) (e:Saul in Topa’ nungzuite ~ tawng a/amah in Topa ~ kiliansak hi | he exalted himself against the Lord/Zeisu’ min ~ ahi thei zahzaha sep ding | to do all that is possible against the name of Jesus/~ lim leh nalamdang na bawl hi | you performed signs and wonders against them) (b:langpan) (r:44.9.1/24.48.26/44.26.9/16.9.10) (q:draft)
langpanna = (t:n) (w:opposition/rebellion/protest) (d:langpan, oppose, with the noun suffix na: the act of standing against someone, rebellion against God) (e:Paul in ~ tawh ama puan singkhia-in/Topa ~ thu gen na hih manin | because you have preached rebellion against the Lord/a hong ~ khempeuhte uh ka maisak ding hi | I will forgive all their rebellion against me) (s:langbawlna/lehdona) (b:langpan) (r:44.18.6/24.33.8/24.28.16) (q:draft)
langsak = (t:v) (w:reveal/show/make known/bring to light) (d:cause to appear or be seen openly) (e:Mihaite in a hehna uh ~ pah a/ama thumanna ~ khin hi | he has revealed his righteousness/minam khempeuh tungah ka ~ ding a | I will make it known to all nations/keima minthan’na hong ~ ding hi | he will reveal my glory) (s:kilangsak/pulak) (a:seel) (r:20.12.16/55.1.10/19.98.2/26.38.23/43.16.14) (q:draft)
langsakin = (t:v) (w:showing/revealing/making known) (d:langsak make known with the linking ending in; a dikna langsakin is showing him to be in the right) (e:a dikpa a dikna ~ ama dikna tawh/na lungkhamna uh ~, leivui lakah kikhuk un | showing your grief, roll in the dust) (s:theisakin) (b:langsak) (r:11.8.32/33.1.10) (q:draft)
langsakkik = (t:v) (w:show again/renew) (d:langsak show, with kik again) (e:na hong ~ thei uh hi) (b:langsak) (r:50.4.10) (q:draft)
langsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who shows forth/vindicator) (d:langsak with pa, the male one who makes something appear; with thumanna, he who shows a person to be in the right) (e:ka thumanna a ~ Pasian a nai-ah) (b:langsak) (r:23.50.8) (q:draft)
langsakpah = (t:v) (w:show at once/reveal immediately) (d:langsak show, with pah at once) (e:Mihaite in a hehna uh ~ uh a) (r:20.12.16) (q:draft)
langsakta = (t:v) (w:reveal/have shown) (d:langsak show, with ta marking a state now reached) (e:na mawhna hong ~ hi) (b:langsak) (r:18.15.6) (q:draft)
langtang = (t:see) <langtang-a>
langtang-a = (t:adv) (w:openly/in the open) (e:a ~ taina hoihzaw hi) (r:20.27.5) (q:draft)
langtangin = (t:adv) (w:openly/publicly/plainly) (d:used as a langtangin, without hiding) (e:Sodom bangin amaute a ~ gamta uh a) (r:23.3.9/47.4.2) (q:draft)
langte = (t:n) (w:half) (d:one side or half of a group, as in Manasseh minam a langte, the half-tribe of Manasseh) (e:Manasseh minam a ~ tungah) (b:lang) (r:6.1.12) (q:draft)
langte = (t:n) (w:enemies/foes/adversaries) (d:those on the opposing side) (e:Tui in amau’ ~ tummang a) (b:lang) (r:19.106.11/19.143.9) (q:draft)
langtuakah = (t:adv) (w:on each side/on both sides/on each) (d:lang side with tuak each and ah at: on each of the two sides; a khut langtuakah, on each of his hands) (e:a khut ~ khutme guk) (r:10.21.20/43.19.18) (q:draft)
langva = (t:todo) (q:draft, part of a measure of oil in Luke 16:6, sathau langva phel zakhat, the meaning of langva alone is not clear)
lanlan = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after pai, walk, for the stately walk of a king before his people, beside kuahkuah for the rooster and gangan for the he-goat) (e:a mite mai-ah a pai ~ kumpipa) (r:20.30.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
lanluat = (t:n) (w:lewdness/debauchery/excessive lust) (d:lan, lustful, with luat, too much) (e:kihhuaina le ~ khialhna gamta uh hi) (r:7.20.6/48.5.19) (q:draft)
lanluatna = (t:n) (w:lewdness/outrageous act) (d:lanluat with the noun suffix na) (e:Israel-te sungah ~ tawh a khialhna uh) (b:lanluat) (r:7.20.10) (q:draft)
lanna = (t:n) (w:lewdness/debauchery/lust) (d:shameless sexual behaviour; often paired with huk or hukna) (e:hukna, ~ kihhuaina ahi zongin) (b:lan) (r:45.13.13/26.22.9) (q:draft)
lannate = (t:n) (w:lewd acts/debauchery) (d:plural of lanna) (e:numei tawh mawhna, hukna, ~ hangin) (b:lanna) (r:47.12.21) (q:draft)
