Lungkhamna = (t:n) (w:trouble/distress) (d:lungkhamna written with a capital in Lungkhamna Kuam, Valley of Trouble, the Valley of Achor) (e:~ Kuam pen lametna kongpi ka suaksak) (b:lungkhamna) (r:28.2.15) (q:draft)
lungkhamnate = (t:n) (w:troubles/distresses/anxieties) (e:na ~ khempeuh uh ama kiang tunpih un) (b:lungkhamna) (r:60.5.7/47.6.4) (q:draft)
lungkhampihin = (t:v) (w:grieve with/be troubled with) (d:lungkham be troubled with pih, together with someone, and -in) (e:A thaneem a om ciangin ~) (b:lungkham) (r:47.11.29) (q:draft)
lungkhamsak = (t:v) (w:distress/trouble/grieve/cause sorrow) (d:lungkham, be troubled, with the causative -sak: make someone troubled or sad) (e:a pian’na a nu zong ~ hi) (b:lungkham) (r:20.17.25/5.28.53) (q:draft)
lungkhamsakna = (t:n) (w:distressing/tormenting) (d:lungkhamsak distress with the noun suffix na: the distress caused to someone) (e:Lot a ~ panun) (b:lungkhamsak) (r:61.2.7) (q:draft)
lungkhamsakpa = (t:n) (w:troubler) (d:lungkhamsak distress, trouble, with pa, which marks a man: the man who troubles) (e:Israel mite a ~ na hi hiam) (b:lungkhamsak) (r:11.18.17) (q:draft)
lungkhamsakte = (t:n) (w:those who distress/troublers) (d:lungkhamsak distress with the plural te) (e:a kulhpi simin a ~ khempeuh) (b:lungkhamsak) (r:23.29.7) (q:draft)
lungkhamte = (t:n) (w:the distressed/the troubled) (d:those who are in distress, lungkham with plural te; NIV has the needy) (e:mi cimawhte le a ~ domto a) (b:lungkham) (r:19.113.7) (q:draft)
lungkhauh = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/stiff-necked/hard-hearted/harsh) (d:literally hard of heart: lung heart with khauh hard; said of people who will not listen, and in 1 Peter 2:18 of harsh masters) (e:a ~ mite ahi uh hi) (r:2.32.9/5.21.18) (q:draft)
lungkhauhin = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/hard-hearted) (d:lungkhauh with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows) (e:ka tapa uh ~ lehdo thei a) (b:lungkhauh) (r:5.21.20/27.5.20) (q:draft)
lungkhauhna = (t:n) (w:stubbornness/hardness of heart) (d:refusal to listen or believe; lungkhauhna tawh gen is to say something firmly, to insist) (e:amaute ~ hangin dah a) (b:lungkhauh) (r:41.3.5/9.15.23) (q:draft)
lungkhauhnate = (t:n) (w:stubborn ways/stubbornness) (e:a ~ uh ahi zongin khia lo uh hi) (b:lungkhauhna) (r:7.2.19) (q:draft)
lungkhauhsak = (t:v) (w:harden) (d:lungkhauh with sak, cause: make someone hard-hearted) (e:a hehpih hi, a ~ nopte) (b:lungkhauh) (r:45.9.18) (q:draft)
lungkheel = (t:adj) (w:fickle/changeable) (d:lung heart with kheel change: changing one's mind easily) (e:~ mi ka hi hiam) (r:47.1.17) (q:draft)
lungkhuah = (t:todo) (r:56.3.2) (q:draft, one verse only, lungkhuah nei loin is something of the heart that one should be without, between not quarrelling and being gentle, but which fault it names cannot be told)
lungkia = (t:v) (w:be discouraged/lose heart/be dismayed) (e:Gamdang mite ~ uh a) (r:10.22.46/49.3.13) (q:draft)
lungkiagawp = (t:v) (w:be utterly dismayed/be confounded) (d:lungkia lose heart with gawp, which marks a thorough or violent action) (e:Bang hangin mi ~ bangin omin) (b:lungkia) (r:24.14.9) (q:draft)
lungkiasak = (t:v) (w:discourage/dishearten) (d:lungkia, lose heart, with -sak, cause) (e:ka sanggamte in mite ~ uh) (b:lungkia) (r:6.14.8/4.32.7) (q:draft)
lungkiasakin = (t:v) (w:discourage/dishearten) (d:lungkiasak discourage with -in, linking it to the next verb) (e:Judah mite ~) (b:lungkiasak) (r:15.4.4) (q:draft)
lungkiat = (t:v) (w:lose heart/be discouraged/give up) (d:form of lungkia used before nading, loh and ngei) (e:kuamah a ~ loh nadingin) (b:lungkia) (r:52.3.2/42.18.1) (q:draft)
lungkiatna = (t:n) (w:discouragement/loss of heart/dismay) (e:thanem ~ ka nei kei uh hi) (b:lungkiat) (r:47.4.1/58.12.3) (q:draft)
lungkim = (t:v) (w:be satisfied/be pleased/be content) (e:tua thu a zak ciangin a ~ hi) (r:3.10.20/58.10.6) (q:draft)
lungkimhuai = (t:adj) (w:pleasing/acceptable/satisfying) (d:lungkim, be satisfied, with huai, worthy of: such as pleases; with lo, displeasing) (e:mai-ah a ~ hi ding hi) (r:39.3.4/1.38.10) (q:draft)
lungkimin = (t:adv) (w:contentedly/with contentment/confidently) (d:form of lungkim with -in, being content or assured) (e:a om zah tawh ~ i om ding hi) (b:lungkim) (r:54.6.8/54.6.6) (q:draft)
lungkimlo = (t:adj) (w:displeased/sullen/discontented) (d:lungkim be pleased with lo, not) (e:a innah ~) (b:lungkim) (r:11.20.43) (q:draft)
lungkimlohna = (t:n) (w:displeasure/indignation) (d:lungkim be pleased with loh, not, and the noun suffix na; in the verse beside hehna and thangpaihna for God's wrath) (e:ka ~ lianpi tawh) (r:24.32.37) (q:draft)
lungkimna = (t:n) (w:pleasure/delight/favour/satisfaction) (d:being pleased with someone or something) (e:amau sungah ka ~ teng om hi) (b:lungkim) (r:19.16.3/19.147.10) (q:draft)
lungkimpih = (t:v) (w:be pleased with/approve/consent to) (d:lungkim with pih: be pleased about a thing, agree to it) (e:Pasian in hong ~ kha ding hi) (b:lungkim) (r:4.23.27) (q:draft)
lungkimsak = (t:v) (w:please/satisfy) (e:a ngetna in Topa ~ hi) (b:lungkim) (r:11.3.10/19.90.14) (q:draft)
lungkimsakin = (t:v) (w:please/satisfy) (d:lungkimsak with the linking suffix in) (e:amaute ~ amaute tungah kam hoih pau lecin) (b:lungkimsak) (r:14.10.7/45.12.2) (q:draft)
lungkimte = (t:n) (w:those who are satisfied/the complacent) (d:lungkim be satisfied, with the plural te) (e:Nomau tumtakin a ~ aw, linglawng un) (b:lungkim) (r:23.32.11/19.49.13) (q:draft)
lungkimthei = (t:v) (w:be able to be content) (d:lungkim be content with thei, can) (e:a ~ dingin a kisinsa ka hi hi) (b:lungkim) (r:50.4.12) (q:draft)
lungkimzo = (t:v) (w:be satisfied) (d:lungkim with zo, be able, in the verses always negated, lungkimzo nai lo, still not satisfied) (e:na ~ nai sam kei hi) (b:lungkim) (r:26.16.28/26.16.29) (q:draft)
lungkip = (t:v) (w:stand firm/be steadfast/be strong in heart) (d:lung heart with kip firm) (e:ka ~ hi ci-in a ki-um mi) (r:46.10.12/45.1.11) (q:draft)
lungkipin = (t:adv) (w:steadfastly/firmly/with perseverance) (d:lungkip be steadfast, with the adverb ending in) (e:a manin ~ a thuakzawh nadingun) (b:lungkip) (r:56.2.2/46.15.58) (q:draft)
lungkipna = (t:n) (w:steadfastness/firmness/endurance) (d:lungkip firm of heart with the noun suffix na) (e:itna ka neihna, ka ~) (b:lungkip) (r:55.3.10/61.3.17) (q:draft)
lungkipsak = (t:v) (w:encourage/strengthen/make steadfast) (d:lungkip be steadfast, with the causative sak) (e:nungzuite a ~ uh a) (b:lungkip) (r:44.14.21/44.15.32) (q:draft)
lungli = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:poplar/balsam tree/mulberry tree) (d:a kind of tree, named with kung as lungli kung; English versions differ on which tree is meant) (e:~ kungte gal panin amaute hih in) (r:10.5.23/13.14.14) (q:draft)
lungman = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be perplexed/be amazed) (d:form of lungmang written with an apostrophe before na; lungman’na is trouble of heart, anxiety or amazement) (e:a ~’na leh dahna a kipan hi) (r:41.14.33/44.3.10) (q:draft)
lungmang = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be perplexed/be dismayed) (d:be upset or at a loss in the heart, from worry, fear or wonder) (e:Note ~ kei un) (r:43.14.1/48.4.20) (q:draft)
Lungmang = (t:v) (w:wonder/be amazed/be dismayed) (e:~ un la, taimang un) (b:lungmang) (r:44.13.41) (q:draft)
lungmangin = (t:v) (w:be perplexed/be troubled/be in anguish) (d:form of lungmang with -in, being at a loss or deeply troubled) (e:tawlnga loin ~ gimin ka om hi) (b:lungmang) (r:45.9.2/42.21.25) (q:draft)
lungmangsak = (t:v) (w:unsettle/upset/trouble) (d:lungmang be troubled, perplexed, with the causative sak; in the verse of upsetting the faith of believers) (e:thu um mi pawlkhat ~ uh hi) (b:lungmang) (r:55.2.18) (q:draft)
lungmanhuai = (t:adj) (w:surprising/astonishing) (d:lungmang be amazed with huai, which marks what causes or deserves a feeling; negated in the verse: it is no wonder) (e:Hih thu in ~ hi lo hi) (r:47.11.14) (q:draft)
lungmuan = (t:v) (w:be secure/be confident/be at peace) (d:form of lungmuang used before na; lungmuan'na is security, confidence, peace of mind) (e:~’na tawh ama kiangah i om) (r:62.2.28/19.122.7) (q:draft)
lungmuang = (t:adj) (w:secure/safe/at ease/confident) (d:free from fear or danger; lungmuang takin means safely, in safety) (e:~ takin na nungta ding a) (r:20.3.23/18.21.23) (q:draft)
lungmuanga = (t:adv) (w:securely/at ease/without care) (d:lungmuang with a, used before om: living in safety) (e:hutna sungah ~ om dingin) (b:lungmuang) (r:19.61.4/33.2.8) (q:draft)
lungmuangin = (t:adv) (w:securely/safely/confidently) (d:with a mind at rest, without fear: lungmuang with the adverb ending -in) (e:thuman mite ~ om tawntung uh hi) (b:lungmuang) (r:20.10.25/20.18.10) (q:draft)
lungmuangsak = (t:v) (w:make secure/keep safe/give confidence) (d:lungmuang secure, with the causative sak) (e:Topa muanna in hong ~ hi) (b:lungmuang) (r:20.29.25/21.7.12) (q:draft)
lungmuangte = (t:n) (w:those at ease/the complacent) (d:lungmuang at ease, secure, with the plural te) (e:a ~ aw, liinglawng un) (b:lungmuang) (r:23.32.11) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuai = (t:adj) (w:safe/secure/reassuring) (d:giving peace of mind, free from danger; lungmuang at ease with huai, which marks what causes or deserves a feeling) (e:ka lampi ~ sak hi) (r:10.22.33/9.20.21) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuaina = (t:n) (w:safety/security) (d:lungmuanhuai safe with the noun suffix na; a lungmuanhuaina mun is a place of safety) (e:a ~ mun) (b:lungmuanhuai) (r:51.1.13) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuaisak = (t:v) (w:make secure/make safe) (d:lungmuanhuai safe with the causative sak) (e:ka lampi khempeuh ~ hi) (b:lungmuanhuai) (r:10.22.33) (q:draft)
lungmuanna = (t:n) (w:security/safety/confidence/peace of mind) (e:Topa a zahtak mi in ~ nei a) (b:lungmuan) (r:20.14.26/23.39.8) (q:draft)
lungmuannate = (t:n) (w:securities/things trusted in) (d:plural of lungmuanna; in the verse beside hauhna wealth, of what the wicked rely on) (e:hauhna le ~ haksa loin beimang ding) (b:lungmuanna) (r:26.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungmuansak = (t:v) (w:give security/make secure) (d:lungmuan be secure with the causative sak) (e:Sum in hong ~ bangin) (b:lungmuan) (r:21.7.12) (q:draft)
lungneemna = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness/patience) (d:lung heart with neem soft and the noun suffix na) (e:sin kiniamsakna, ~, heh baih lohna lungsimte) (r:51.3.12/45.9.22) (q:draft)
lungnem = (t:adj) (w:meek/gentle/humble) (d:of a soft and mild heart, from lung, heart, and nem, soft) (e:A ~ mite in Pasian’ ciamsa leitang) (r:40.5.5/4.12.3) (q:draft)
lungnemin = (t:adv) (w:meekly/patiently) (d:lungnem with in: with a gentle heart, without resisting) (e:~ na thuak uh leh) (b:lungnem) (r:60.2.20) (q:draft)
lungnemna = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness/humility) (d:noun from lungnem, a soft and gentle heart; also patience in waiting) (e:Khazih’ ~ leh hehpihna tawh) (b:lungnem) (r:47.10.1/49.4.2) (q:draft)
lungnemnate = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness) (d:lungnemna with te, which here closes a list of qualities) (e:thuakzawhna, ~ na phak matengin) (b:lungnemna) (r:54.6.11) (q:draft)
lungnemsak = (t:v) (w:please/win the favor of) (d:lungnem soft-hearted with the causative sak: soften the heart of someone, win them over; mite lungnemsak mi is one who pleases people) (e:Mite ~ mi bangin) (b:lungnem) (r:49.6.6) (q:draft)
lungnemte = (t:n) (w:the meek/the gentle/the humble) (d:lungnem with plural te) (e:~ in leitang luahin) (b:lungnem) (r:19.37.11/36.3.12) (q:draft)
lungnemzaw = (t:adj) (w:more humble/meeker) (d:lungnem humble with the comparative zaw) (e:mi khempeuh sangin a ~ ahi hi) (b:lungnem) (r:4.12.3) (q:draft)
lungngai = (t:v) (w:ponder/consider/think about) (d:think over in the heart; also have in mind or intend to do something) (e:a lungsim sungah a ~ hi) (r:42.2.19/44.15.37) (q:draft)
Lungngai = (t:v) (w:remember/think about) (d:with nawn lo, remember no more) (e:~ nawn loin ka om ding hi) (b:lungngai) (r:58.10.17) (q:draft)
lungngaih = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/reflect) (d:think deeply about something; lungngaih kik is come to one’s senses) (e:Ka ~ ciangin ka lung so semsem hi) (b:lungngai) (r:19.39.3/42.15.17) (q:draft)
lungngaih = (t:n) (w:thought/intention) (d:what a person thinks or plans in the heart) (e:Ama ~ hoih lo pen ama lu tungah) (b:lungngai) (r:19.7.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungngaihna = (t:n) (w:thought/inner thought) (d:lungngaih ponder with the noun suffix na: what a person thinks in the heart) (e:mite’ selsim ~ a khen Ni ciangin) (b:lungngaih) (r:45.2.16/42.2.34) (q:draft)
lungngaihngaih = (t:v) (w:meditate on/keep thinking about) (d:lungngaih ponder, with the last part doubled) (e:Sun tawntungin ka ~ ahi hi) (r:19.119.97/19.63.5) (q:draft)
lungngaingai = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/reflect on) (d:keep thinking something over; the doubled ngai shows continued action) (e:Nangma thuciamna a ~ dingin) (r:19.119.148/19.145.5) (q:draft)
lungniam = (t:v) (w:be dismayed/be discouraged/be downcast) (d:lung heart with niam low: the heart sinks) (e:nang hong su a, na ~ hi) (r:18.4.5) (q:draft)
Lungniamkhiat = (t:adj) (w:humble/meek) (d:lung heart with niam low and khiat; Lungniamkhiat mite are the humble) (e:~ mite in Topa sungah) (r:23.29.19) (q:draft)
lungniamkhiatna = (t:n) (w:humility/humbleness) (d:lung heart, niam low and khiat bring down, with the noun suffix na: bringing the heart low) (e:~ na nei un) (r:60.3.8) (q:draft)
lungniamsakte = (t:n) (w:the humble) (d:those who make the heart low: lung heart, niam low, the causative sak and the plural te) (e:a ~ kiangah hehpihna thupha a pia hi) (r:60.5.5) (q:draft)
lungno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:worm/maggot) (e:in ~ khat bang ka hi lel a) (r:19.22.6/32.4.7) (q:draft)
lungnop = (t:v) (w:delight) (e:Ka ~ nadingin la a sa ding) (r:21.2.8)
lungnopmawhna = (t:n) (w:distress/offence/unease) (d:a heart that is not at ease: lung heart, nop pleasant, mawh hard or wrong, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ na piansak uhleh itna lungsim) (r:45.14.15) (q:draft)
lungnopmawhsak = (t:v) (w:offend/distress/cause to stumble) (d:make the heart of someone uneasy, with the causative sak) (e:na ~ loh nadingun na gamta un) (r:46.10.32) (q:draft)
lungnopna = (t:n) (w:peace/contentment/joy) (d:a glad and easy heart) (e:~ in pumpi cidamsak a) (b:lungnop) (r:20.14.30/25.5.15) (q:draft)
lungnopnate = (t:n) (w:peace/joys) (d:plural of lungnopna, here of the kinds of peace the world gives) (e:a kip lo ~ pawl hi lo hi) (b:lungnopna) (r:43.14.27) (q:draft)
lungnopsak = (t:v) (w:refresh/gladden/cheer) (d:lungnop be glad at heart with the causative sak) (e:note hong ~ mah bangin) (b:lungnop) (r:46.16.18) (q:draft)
lungnuam = (t:v) (w:delight) (e:~ takin kumpipa tawh pai in) (r:17.5.14)
lungnuamin = (t:n) (w:integrity)
lungnuamsak = (t:v) (w:cheer/gladden/comfort/refresh) (d:lungnuam with causative sak: make someone glad or at ease) (e:tamveipi kei hong ~ ahih manin) (b:lungnuam) (r:55.1.16/18.5.11) (q:draft)
lungphamawh = (t:v) (w:be concerned about/care for) (d:have something on the heart as a care or a need: lung heart with phamawh be of concern) (e:a nongek neite ka ~ hi) (r:1.33.13) (q:draft)
lungphatmawhna = (t:n) (w:concern/worry/care) (d:the having of something on the heart as a care; with nei lo, not concern oneself) (e:bangmah ~ nei lo hi) (r:1.39.8) (q:draft)
lungpil = (t:adj) (w:wise/sensible) (d:with lo, foolish) (e:~ mi kiangah ka gen mah bangin) (r:46.10.15/45.1.22) (q:draft)
Lungpil = (t:n) (w:understanding/intelligence/good sense) (d:lung heart with pil wise; Lungpil a neite are the intelligent) (e:~ a neite a lungpilna ka sugawp ding hi) (b:lungpil) (r:46.1.19) (q:draft)
lungpilna = (t:n) (w:wisdom/knowledge/understanding) (e:Note in zong ~ nei nai lo) (b:lungpil) (r:40.15.16/42.7.35) (q:draft)
lungpilte = (t:n) (w:the wise/wise people/sages) (d:plural of lungpil, also those in their right mind) (e:ci-in ~ kiangah a ngen uh hi) (b:lungpil) (r:40.25.8/46.1.27) (q:draft)
lungsi = (t:v) (w:lose heart/be dismayed/falter) (d:literally the heart dies, lung heart with si die; said of sudden fear or loss of courage) (e:~ lo, lungkia lo ding hi) (r:23.42.4/1.42.28) (q:draft)
lungsiangtho = (t:n) (w:righteousness/purity of heart) (d:lung heart with siangtho holy, pure; in the verse the thing hungered for, righteousness in the English) (e:an duh banga ~ a deihte in) (r:40.5.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungsim = (t:n) (w:thought) (e:~ ngaihsutna peuhmah a sia) (r:1.6.5)
Lungsim = (t:n) (w:heart/mind) (d:Lungsim takpi tawh is with a true heart, sincerely) (e:~ takpi tawh ka hong it) (b:lungsim) (r:64.1.1) (q:draft)
lungsimah = (t:n) (w:in the heart/in the mind) (d:lungsim heart or mind with the locative marker ah) (e:ama thute na ~ ciamteh in) (b:lungsim) (r:18.22.22/12.10.30) (q:draft)
lungsimin = (t:adv) (w:in spirit/in heart/inwardly) (d:lungsim heart, mind, with the ending in: in or with the heart) (e:ka ~ note tawh ka hong omkhawm a) (b:lungsim) (r:51.2.5/1.43.30) (q:draft)
lungsimkawi = (t:adj) (w:perverse/crooked) (d:lungsim heart, mind with kawi crooked: of a crooked mind) (e:~ mi hihna sangin) (r:20.28.6) (q:draft)
lungsimkhem = (t:n) (w:false motive/deceitful heart) (d:lungsim heart, mind with khem deceive; set against lungsim hoih, a good heart) (e:~ tawh a kihilh ahi zongin) (r:50.1.18) (q:draft)
lungsimmawl = (t:adj) (w:senseless/dull-minded) (d:lungsim mind with mawl, dull) (e:~ mi in theithei lo a) (r:19.92.6/19.94.8) (q:draft)
lungsimnem = (t:adj) (w:gentle/mild) (d:lungsim heart with nem soft) (e:~ mi, kitot a uk lo mi) (r:54.3.3) (q:draft)
lungsimniam = (t:adj) (w:humble/gentle/lowly) (d:lungsim heart with niam low; lungsimniam tawh is with humility) (e:na Kumpipa, ~ tawh) (r:40.21.5) (q:draft)
lungsimsia = (t:v) (w:be bitter in spirit/be grieved) (d:lungsim heart with sia bad: be sore at heart) (e:a tapate uh hangin ~ uh ahih manin) (r:9.30.6) (q:draft)
lungsimtak = (t:n) (w:sincerity/whole heart/good faith) (d:lungsim heart, mind with tak true; lungsimtak tawh is sincerely, wholeheartedly) (e:~ tawh zui ahih manin) (b:lungsim) (r:6.14.14/42.8.15) (q:draft)
lungsimtawng = (t:n) (w:inmost heart/inner thoughts) (d:what is at the bottom of the heart: a person's real thoughts and motives) (e:amau ~ thei ahih manin) (r:41.12.15/42.16.15) (q:draft)
