mualpangah = (t:n) (w:on the hillside/at the hillside) (d:mualpang hillside with the place marker ah) (e:tua nai-a om ~ vok hon tampi) (b:mualpang) (r:41.5.11/10.16.13) (q:draft)
mualpawn = (t:n) (w:bare hill/barren height) (d:mual hill with pawn bare land: a hill with no trees) (e:a sang ~ khatah amah pai hi) (r:4.23.3/23.49.9) (q:draft)
mualpi = (t:n) (w:great mountain/mountain) (d:mual mountain with pi great) (e:~ banga lian a) (b:mual) (r:24.51.25/66.8.8) (q:draft)
mualsang = (t:n) (w:high mountain/height/high hill) (d:mual, mountain, with sang, high) (e:~ leh mual neute tung khempeuh ah) (r:23.30.25/40.17.1) (q:draft)
mualsangte = (t:n) (w:high hills/heights/high mountains) (e:~ in sathak’ ading hi a) (b:mualsang) (r:19.104.18/24.17.2) (q:draft)
mualsuang = (t:n) (w:memorial stone/pillar/tombstone) (d:a stone set up in memory of someone, as over a grave, with suang stone) (e:ama han tungah ~ khat a phut hi) (r:1.35.20) (q:draft)
mualsuangte = (t:n) (w:memorial stones/pillars/monuments) (d:plural of mualsuang; of the monuments of the dead and of the sacred pillars of Egypt) (e:Heliopolis khua-a ~ a susia ding a) (b:mualsuang) (r:24.43.13/40.23.29) (q:draft)
mualtan = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:viper/snake) (d:a poisonous snake; in the verses always in the address translated brood of vipers) (e:No ~’ suante aw) (r:40.12.34/40.3.7) (q:draft)
mualte = (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (e:~ ka et leh kiliing damdam uh a) (b:mual) (r:24.4.24/19.65.6) (q:draft)
