mualtungah = (t:adv) (w:on the mountain/in the hill country/to the hills) (d:mualtung with the place marker ah) (e:Jakob in ~ biak piakna pia-in) (b:mualtung) (r:1.31.54/40.24.16) (q:draft)
mualtungte = (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (d:mualtung with plural -te) (e:mihonpi lungdam bangin ~ ah gamlumna) (b:mualtung) (r:23.13.4/26.35.12) (q:draft)
mualvum = (t:n) (w:mountain top/summit/peak) (d:the top of a mountain) (e:Lebanon ~ bangin ahi zongin na hoih hi) (r:24.22.6/2.24.17) (q:draft)
mualzang = (t:n) (w:plateau/tableland) (d:level high ground, mual hill with zang flat) (e:~ tunga om a khuapite khempeuh) (r:6.13.17/6.13.9) (q:draft)
muam = (t:v) (w:hold in the mouth/suck) (d:keep something in the mouth without swallowing; doubled, muam muam, keep on holding it there) (e:amah in ~ muam nuamin siakhia nuam lo a) (r:18.20.13) (q:draft)
muammuam = (t:v) (w:keep in the mouth/savour) (d:muam hold in the mouth, doubled: go on holding and tasting something) (e:amah in ~ nuamin siakhia nuam lo a) (r:18.20.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
muamua = (t:adv) (w:in great numbers/in swarms/teeming) (d:follows a verb to picture many people or creatures moving or gathered together) (e:minamte khempeuh pai ~ ding uh a) (r:23.2.2/26.36.38) (q:draft)
muan = (t:v) (w:trust/rely on) (d:stem two form of muang; muan’na is trust, confidence or hope, and muan’huai is trustworthy) (e:Mi i ~’ sangin Topa belh) (r:19.118.8/19.71.5) (q:draft)
