nununga = (t:adj) (w:latter/later/last) (d:nunung, last, with a, describing the noun that follows; opposite of a masa, the first) (e:a ~ na gamtatnate in a masa) (b:nunung) (r:66.2.19) (q:draft)
nunungin = (t:adv) (w:last/behind/afterwards) (d:nunung, last, with in; opposite of a masa-in, in front) (e:lasate, a ~ tamngai tumte) (b:nunung) (r:19.68.25) (q:draft)
nunungna = (t:n) (w:the last/latter one) (d:nunung, last, with the noun suffix na, after a verb: the later time of doing; khem nunungna is the last deception) (e:sangin a khem ~ uh hong husiazaw) (b:nunung) (r:40.27.64) (q:draft)
nunungpen = (t:adj) (w:last/very last/lowest) (d:nunung, last, with pen, most; in Luke 22.26 of the follower of lowest rank, the one who serves) (e:a tum ~ pan a kipanin) (b:nunung) (r:40.20.8/42.22.26) (q:draft)
nunungte = (t:n) (w:the last/last ones) (d:those who come last; also after a noun, as in kam nunungte, last words) (e:A tum ~ in nai khat bek) (b:nunung) (r:40.20.12/10.23.1) (q:draft)
nupa = (t:n) (w:couple) (e:Sapfira min nei ~ khat in) (r:44.5.1/1.7.2)
nupate = (t:n) (w:married couple/husband and wife) (d:nupa couple, with te; tua nupate is that couple, the two of them) (e:Tua ~ tawh a kimu dingin) (b:nupa) (r:44.18.2/40.19.10) (q:draft)
nupi = (t:n) (w:woman/married woman) (d:adult woman, paired with papi for men and women) (e:papi, ~ leh naupangte i susia hi) (b:nu) (r:5.3.6/24.6.24) (q:draft)
nupite = (t:n) (w:women) (d:plural of nupi, grown or married women) (e:~ leh naupangte a muh ciangin) (b:nupi) (r:1.33.5/19.68.12) (q:draft)
nusia = (t:v) (w:leave) (e:a nu leh a pa ~-in a zi) (r:1.2.24/43.14.18)
nusia = (t:v) (w:pass away)
nusiacip = (t:v) (w:abandon/leave behind/forsake) (d:nusia, leave, with cip, firmly: leave and not come back for it) (e:gamah kei nong ~ kei ding a) (b:nusia) (r:44.2.27/26.31.12) (q:draft)
nusiakha = (t:v) (w:neglect/leave out/leave behind) (d:nusia, leave, with kha, happen to) (e:a thupiteng na ~ uh a) (r:40.23.24) (q:draft)
nusiakhawm = (t:v) (w:leave together with) (d:nusia, leave, with khawm, together) (e:gamlak lopate tawh ~ in) (b:nusia) (r:27.4.23) (q:draft)
nusiakik = (t:v) (w:desert/turn away from/leave again) (d:nusia, leave, with kik, back or again) (e:note a hong sam Pasian ~ pakin) (b:nusia) (r:48.1.6) (q:draft)
nusialai = (t:v) (w:leave behind/leave remaining) (d:nusia, leave, with lai, still) (e:a zawngpente pawlkhat a ~ hi) (r:24.52.16) (q:draft)
nusian = (t:n) (w:goddess) (e:Sidon mite’ ~ Ashtoreth) (r:11.11.5/24.17.2) (q:draft)
nusiapa = (t:n) (w:deserter/one who abandons) (d:nusia, leave, with pa marking a man: the man who leaves) (e:a tuuhonte a ~ in gimna ngah ta hen) (b:nusia) (r:38.11.17) (q:draft)
nusiat = (t:v) (w:leave/forsake/abandon) (d:form of nusia used before a following word such as hangin, or to describe a noun) (e:ka pa in hong ~ hangin) (b:nusia) (r:19.27.10/7.2.21) (q:draft)
nusiate = (t:n) (w:those who forsake/those who leave) (d:people who have left or abandoned someone or something) (e:Topa a ~ pen kibeimangsak ding hi) (b:nusia) (r:23.1.28/40.19.29) (q:draft)
nusiatin = (t:v) (w:left lying/abandoned) (d:nusiat, leave, with in: in the manner of a thing left lying; ek nusiatin is like dung left on the ground) (e:leilakah ek ~ a kinusia ding uh hi) (b:nusiat) (r:24.25.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
nusiatkhak = (t:v) (w:come to abandon/happen to forsake) (d:nusiat, leave, with khak, form of kha, happen to) (e:na ~ ding uh ka lunghimawh hi) (r:47.11.3) (q:draft)
nusiatlai = (t:adj) (w:left behind/remaining/spared) (d:nusiat, leave, with lai, still: describes people or things that someone has left where they were) (e:ka nuntaksak, ka ~ mite a mawhna uh) (r:24.50.20/24.27.19) (q:draft)
nusiatlam = (t:n) (w:having left behind) (d:nusiat, leave, with lam, the fact that: that they had left someone behind) (e:a ~ uh thei lo uh hi) (r:42.2.43) (q:draft)
nusiatna = (t:n) (w:forsaking/abandonment/desertion) (d:nusiat, forsake, with the noun suffix na; kei hong nusiatna uh is their forsaking me) (e:kei hong ~ uh leh keimah sangin milim) (b:nusiat) (r:26.6.9) (q:draft)
nusiatte = (t:n) (w:what is left/things left behind/those left behind) (d:nusiat leave with plural te; van nusiatte is goods left behind, plunder) (e:a ~ tungah a uk dingin) (b:nusiat) (r:12.25.22/2.23.11) (q:draft)
nusiazo = (t:v) (w:have forsaken/have abandoned/have left) (d:nusia leave, forsake, with zo showing that the act has been carried through) (e:Na tate un kei hong ~ uh a) (b:nusia) (r:24.5.7/19.71.11) (q:draft)
nuta = (t:n) (w:mother and young/mother and child) (d:nu, mother, with ta, child; a mother together with her young, as in la nuta, a donkey and her colt) (e:la ~ thakhatin na mu ding uh) (b:nu) (r:40.21.2/40.21.7) (q:draft)
nutate = (t:n) (w:mother and daughter/mother and child) (d:nuta, mother and child, with the plural ending te; in the verse a woman and her mother who are married to one man) (e:tuapa leh a ~, mei tawh kihallum ding hi) (b:nuta) (r:3.20.14) (q:draft)
nute = (t:n) (w:mothers) (d:nu with plural te; na nute na pate, your parents) (e:ka ~ uh a meigong khin uh) (b:nu) (r:25.5.3/20.30.11) (q:draft)
nutsiat = (t:v) (w:leave/leave behind/abandon) (d:spelling of nusiat, the form of nusia leave used before ding and khit and to describe a noun) (e:thong sungah khumin a ~ mi khat) (r:44.25.14/44.27.40) (q:draft)
