paat = (t:v) (w:be worn out/wear thin/be thin) (d:become thin through wear, said of clothes and sandals, of eyes worn by weeping, and of a wall that narrows) (e:khual gamlapi zinna-in ~ gawp hi) (r:6.9.13/26.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
paatgawp = (t:v) (w:be badly worn out/fail) (d:paat, be worn out, with gawp, badly or thoroughly; said of eyes worn by weeping) (e:ka mit ~ ta a) (b:paat) (r:25.2.11) (q:draft)
paatgawpta = (t:v) (w:be badly worn out) (d:paatgawp with ta, marking that the state has now been reached; said of clothes and sandals) (e:khual gamlapi zinna-in ~ hi) (b:paatgawp) (r:6.9.13) (q:draft)
paatkhia = (t:v) (w:wear out/become worn out) (d:said of cloth that grows old and thin) (e:amaute pen puan bangin ~ ding hi) (r:19.102.26/23.51.6) (q:draft)
paatsa = (t:adj) (w:worn-out/old/tattered) (d:of sacks, wineskins, sandals and clothes that are old and falling apart) (e:a ~ puante tawh pai uh hi) (b:paat) (r:6.9.5/6.9.4) (q:draft)
paatsak = (t:v) (w:wear out/wear down/exhaust) (d:paat, be worn out, with sak, cause) (e:Pasian aw, kei nong ~ ngiingei a) (b:paat) (r:18.16.7) (q:draft)
Padaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pedaiah) (r:12.23.36)
Paddan = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Paddan) (d:first part of Paddan-aram, Paddan Aram, the region where Laban lived) (r:1.28.2/1.35.26) (q:draft)
Paddan-aram = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Paddan Aram) (r:1.28.2/1.35.26) (q:draft)
Paddanaram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paddan-aram) (r:1.25.20/1.31.18)
