Pagiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pagiel) (r:4.1.13/4.10.26)
pah = (t:adv) (w:immediately/at once/right away/instantly) (e:a dam ~ hi) (r:41.1.42/41.1.12)
pah = (t:conj) (w:as soon as)
Pahathmoab = (t:name) (w:Pahath-Moab) (r:15.8.4/16.10.14)
Pahathmoabte = (t:name) (w:Pahath-Moab) (b:Pahathmoab) (r:15.2.6/16.7.11)
pahin = (t:adv) (w:immediately/at once/straightaway) (d:pah with the linking suffix in, after a verb: doing it at once, and then) (e:meivak a nget khit ciangin lut ~) (b:pah) (r:44.16.29/44.25.17) (q:draft)
pahpah = (t:adv) (w:immediately) (e:a min hi ~ hi) (r:1.2.19)
pahpah = (t:adv) (w:straight away/at once/right away/instantly) (e:Heh ~ kei in, hehna in haihuai hi) (r:21.7.9)
pahpah = (t:conj) (w:as soon as)
pahpahin = (t:adv) (w:immediately/at once/right away) (d:pahpah with the adverbial ending in) (e:khialhnate kimu ~ mawhsakna thuakpah uh a) (b:pahpah) (r:54.5.24) (q:draft)
pahpahpa = (t:n) (w:one who acts at once) (d:pahpah, immediately, with pa, the one who: hong huh pahpahpa is the one who helps at once) (e:haksat hunin hong huh ~ ahi hi) (b:pahpah) (r:19.46.1) (q:draft)
pahpahte = (t:n) (d:pahpah at once, readily, with the plural te, making a noun of the verb phrase before it: those who are quick to do something; a heh pahpahte is those who are quick to anger) (e:A heh ~ in kitotna piangsak a) (b:pahpah) (r:20.29.22/59.2.6) (q:draft)
pahtaak = (t:n) (w:favour/approval) (d:the good opinion of others; spelling of pahtak) (e:mihing ~ ding ut-a) (r:51.3.22) (q:draft)
pahtak = (t:v) (w:favour/delight in/approve of) (d:be pleased with someone and hold him in regard) (e:pa in a ~ a tapa) (r:20.3.12) (q:draft)
pahtak = (t:n) (w:favour/approval/honour) (d:the good opinion of others; pahtak ngah is to gain honour) (e:Mite’ ~ ding hanciam ka hi hiam) (r:48.1.10/20.20.3) (q:draft)
pahtakbawl = (t:v) (w:speak well of/praise/treat with favour) (d:pahtak, favour or approval, with bawl, do or make: show someone approval) (e:kamsang zuaute a ~ uh hi) (b:pahtak) (r:42.6.26) (q:draft)
pahtakhuai = (t:adj) (w:honoured/admirable/worthy of honour) (d:pahtak favour, honour, with huai, worthy of) (e:a deihhuai, le a ~ thute ahi hi) (r:50.4.8/23.43.4) (q:draft)
pahtaklam = (t:n) (w:favour/the fact of favouring) (d:pahtak, favour or be pleased with, with lam, the fact or manner of) (e:Nangma nong ~ na pa in) (r:9.20.3) (q:draft)
pahtakna = (t:n) (w:approval/favour/honour/praise) (d:being approved or praised by someone) (e:a topa a kempa in ~ ngah hi) (b:pahtak) (r:20.27.18/45.5.4) (q:draft)
pahtawi = (t:v) (w:honor/exalt/glorify) (e:lungdamna tawh amah ka ~ ding hi) (r:19.69.30/17.6.7) (q:draft)
pahtawihuai = (t:adj) (w:honourable/worthy of honour) (d:pahtawi honour, with huai, worthy of) (e:a sanggamte sangin ~ zaw hi) (r:13.4.9/23.58.13) (q:draft)
pahtawina = (t:n) (w:honor) (e:hauhna leh ~ zong hong pia hi) (b:pahtawi) (r:20.3.16/17.8.16) (q:draft)
Pahtawina = (t:see) <Pahtawina-a>
Pahtawina-a = (t:n) (w:to the honor of/in honor of) (d:pahtawina honor with the marker a, at or for) (e:Siangtho Pa ~ hong puak uh ahi) (r:23.60.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
pahtawinate = (t:n) (w:praises/honors) (e:Israelte’ ~ tungah na tu hi) (b:pahtawina) (r:19.22.3) (q:draft)
pahtawipa = (t:n) (w:one who honors) (d:pahtawi, honor or exalt, with pa, the one who) (e:hong ~ in Pasian ahi hi) (b:pahtawi) (r:47.1.21) (q:draft)
pahtawite = (t:n) (w:those who honor) (d:pahtawi, honor, with te, those who) (e:kei hong ~ ka pahtawi ding a) (b:pahtawi) (r:9.2.30) (q:draft)
pahtawizawk = (t:v) (w:honor more/be honored more) (d:pahtawi, honor, with zawk, more, the form of zaw used before ding) (e:Moses sangin Jesuh ~ ding ahi hi) (r:58.3.3) (q:draft)
pahte = (t:adv) (d:pah, at once or readily, after a verb, with te, those who: a zuak pahte, those who sell readily, a mang pahte, those who accept at once) (e:lei nop hun-a a zuak ~ kiphat hi) (b:pah) (r:20.11.26/42.8.13) (q:draft)
pai = (t:v) (w:come) (e:Hong ~-in ka damsak ding hi) (r:40.8.7)
pai = (t:v) (w:go) (e:Oliv Mual ah a ~ hi) (r:43.8.1/40.10.6)
Pai = (t:v) (w:go) (d:pai, go, written with a capital at the start of quoted speech) (e:Lau kei un, ~ un la) (b:pai) (r:40.28.10/12.2.18) (q:draft)
Pai = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Pau/Pai) (d:the city of Hadad king of Edom; Pau in the NIV, Pai in older English Bibles) (e:ama khuapi min in ~ hi a) (r:13.1.50) (q:draft)
paidak = (t:v) (w:forsake/abandon/cast off) (e:ama luahte ~ lo ding hi) (r:19.94.14/28.11.8) (q:draft)
paih = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast/throw off/reject) (d:form of paai used before khit, nading and other endings) (e:Amah in a puan a ~ khit ciangin) (r:41.10.50/3.14.40) (q:draft)
paihdak = (t:v) (w:cast away/throw down) (d:paih, throw away, with dak; in the verse of God casting his people into deep darkness; what dak adds is not clear) (e:khuamialpi sungah nong ~ dinga kilawm zahin) (r:19.44.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
paihkhiat = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast out/thrust out/forsake) (d:form of the verb used before words such as bangin, dongin, hun and thu) (e:Kep hun om a, ~ hun om hi) (b:paih) (r:21.3.6/12.17.20) (q:draft)
paihkhiatna = (t:n) (w:casting out/rejection/setting aside) (d:paihkhiat throw out with the noun ending na) (e:ahih ciangin ~ a ngah zo hi) (b:paihkhiat) (r:58.7.18/12.24.20) (q:draft)
paihkhiatpih = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out) (d:used in the verse beside paikhiatpih with the same meaning; perhaps a misprint of that word) (e:Filistia mite ka ~ a) (r:30.9.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
paihkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:remove/take away/deprive of) (d:take something away from someone, cause it to be thrown out) (e:khanghamte’ pilna ~ hi) (b:paihkhiat) (r:18.12.20/38.3.9) (q:draft)
paihkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:removing/taking away) (d:paihkhiatsak remove, take away from someone, with the linking ending in) (e:suang lungtang ~ mihing lungtang ka guan ding hi) (b:paihkhiatsak) (r:26.11.19/33.5.10) (q:draft)
paihmang = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast out/abandon) (d:paih, throw, with mang, away or lost) (e:a ~ nadingun) (r:44.7.19) (q:draft)
paihmawk = (t:v) (w:throw away/throw out) (d:paih, throw, with mawk, simply or to no purpose) (e:~ a kul hi) (r:42.14.35) (q:draft)
paihna = (t:n) (w:throwing/casting down) (d:paih, a form of paai, throw, with the noun suffix na; the act of throwing or casting down, and before a noun the place where a thing was thrown) (e:luang khempeuh a ~ tuikhuk pen) (b:paih) (r:24.41.9/14.25.8) (q:draft)
paihsak = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast/hurl) (d:throw away or cast down something that belongs to another; paih with sak) (e:tuipi sungah ~ ding a) (b:paih) (r:38.9.4/33.7.19) (q:draft)
paihsakin = (t:v) (w:throw/cast) (d:paihsak with the ending in, linking it to the following verb: throwing) (e:meikhuk sungah ~ susia khin hi) (b:paihsak) (r:23.37.19) (q:draft)
paihtuam = (t:n) (w:partiality/discrimination) (d:setting one person aside from the rest; paired with guptuam for favouritism and partiality) (e:kuamah guptuam ~ nei hetloin) (r:54.5.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
paii = (t:v) (w:conceive/be pregnant with/carry in the womb) (e:Nang hong ~ gil leh na teep nawi) (r:42.11.27) (q:draft)
paii = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/throw away) (d:throw something down or away, as a net onto the water; also written paai) (e:tui tungah ngeen a ~ mite thanem ding) (r:23.19.8/40.18.8) (q:draft)
paiite = (t:n) (w:goods/valuables/treasures) (d:used together with sum, money, as sum leh paiite and na sum na paiite, money and possessions; compare sumlepai) (e:a neihsa uh sum leh ~) (r:37.2.7/24.15.13) (q:draft)
paikawm = (t:v) (w:while going/while walking) (d:pai, go, with kawm, while: as one goes along, at the same time as another action) (e:Mihaite lampi-ah a ~ nangawnin hai tat uh) (r:21.10.3/44.3.8) (q:draft)
paikawmin = (t:v) (w:while going/going along) (d:pai go with kawm, at the same time, and the linking suffix -in: doing something else while on the way) (e:manawhin a ~ thu a hilh hi) (b:paikawm) (r:42.13.22/18.22.14) (q:draft)
paikawmun = (t:v) (w:as they go/while going/on the way) (d:pai with kawm, while, and the plural ending un: as they went along, doing something else at the same time) (e:A ~ hih thupiangte kikumkum uh hi) (b:paikawm) (r:42.24.14/9.6.12) (q:draft)
paikha = (t:v) (w:happen to go/pass by/go near) (d:pai go with kha, happen to or come upon) (e:siampi khat ~ zenzen a) (r:42.10.31/20.5.8) (q:draft)
paikhak = (t:v) (w:go near/happen to go/come near) (d:form of paikha used before ciangin) (e:biakinn nai-ah Israel mite a ~ ciangin) (b:paikha) (r:4.8.19) (q:draft)
paikhawm = (t:adv) (w:together with) (e:keimah tawh a ~ ding uh hi) (b:pai) (r:46.16.4/42.14.25)
paikhawmin = (t:v) (w:go together/go with) (d:paikhawm with the linking ending in, going together) (e:Andru le Filip ~ Jesuh kiangah) (b:paikhawm) (r:43.12.22/7.1.17) (q:draft)
paikhawmpa = (t:n) (w:one who goes with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with pa, the one who) (e:note tawh hong ~ in Topa) (b:paikhawm) (r:5.20.4) (q:draft)
paikhawmsak = (t:v) (w:send together with/let go with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with sak, make or let) (e:keima nasemte ~ in) (b:paikhawm) (r:11.22.49/44.15.22) (q:draft)
paikhawmte = (t:n) (w:companions/those who go with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with plural te) (e:kei tawh hong ~ kimkot ah) (b:paikhawm) (r:44.26.13) (q:draft)
paikhia = (t:n) (w:getout) (e:Tuate ~ uh a) (r:41.6.12) see <pai> and <khia>
paikhial = (t:v) (w:go astray/turn aside) (d:pai, go, with khial, wrongly) (e:pasian manlote lamah a ~ lo mi) (r:19.40.4) (q:draft)
paikhiapa = (t:n) (w:one who has gone out) (d:paikhia, go out, with pa, the man who) (e:hih mun pan-a ~ Shallum’ thu) (b:paikhia) (r:24.22.11) (q:draft)
paikhiapih = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out) (d:paikhia, go out, with pih, together with: go out taking someone along) (e:amaute ka ~ lai-in) (b:paikhia) (r:3.23.43) (q:draft)
paikhiasak = (t:v) (w:send away/let go/make go out) (d:paikhia, go out, with causative sak) (e:khut guak tawh a ~ zo hi) (b:paikhia) (r:42.1.53/42.14.4) (q:draft)
paikhiasakin = (t:v) (w:send away/send out) (d:paikhiasak with the ending in, linking it to the following verb: sending out) (e:a nin numei le pasal ~) (b:paikhiasak) (r:4.5.3) (q:draft)
paikhiasuak = (t:v) (w:go out/pass out) (d:paikhia, go out, with suak, right on through) (e:tua panin ~ hi lo ahi hiam) (r:40.15.17) (q:draft)
paikhiasuk = (t:v) (w:go out/go away/leave) (d:paikhia, go out, with suk, downward) (e:Amalek mite lak panin ~ un) (b:paikhia) (r:9.15.6) (q:draft)
paikhiat = (t:v) (w:go out/come out/leave/depart) (d:form of paikhia used before lai, ding, phetin and in dependent clauses) (e:Bethani khua pan a ~ lai takin) (b:paikhia) (r:41.11.12/6.2.7) (q:draft)
paikhiata = (t:v) (w:come out/go out) (d:paikhia, go out, with ta, marking a completed event; a paikhiata kipan is since they came out) (e:Israel mite a ~ kipan tuni dongin) (b:paikhia) (r:7.19.30) (q:draft)
paikhiate = (t:n) (w:things that come out) (d:paikhia, come out, with the plural te; a paikhiate, the things that come out) (e:Kam sung pan a ~ in) (b:paikhia) (r:40.15.18/41.7.20) (q:draft)
paikhiatin = (t:v) (w:go out/set out/leave) (d:paikhiat with the ending in: when or as someone set out) (e:Haran panin a ~ Abram) (b:paikhiat) (r:1.12.4) (q:draft)
paikhiatkhak = (t:v) (w:slip out/get out) (d:paikhiat, go out, with khak, happen to; with loh nading, so that no one gets out) (e:kuamah a ~ loh nading thei un) (r:12.9.15) (q:draft)
paikhiatlam = (t:n) (w:going out/departure/leaving) (d:paikhiat go out, with lam, the fact or manner of: that someone has gone out, the leaving of someone) (e:na ~ mi khempeuh musak in) (r:26.12.3/41.6.33) (q:draft)
paikhiatna = (t:n) (w:departure/exodus/going out) (d:noun from paikhiat go out; the act of leaving, or with gam or mun the place someone came out from) (e:Israel mipawlte ~ thu lakin) (b:paikhiat) (r:58.11.22/58.11.15) (q:draft)
paikhiatnapa = (t:n) (w:man from whom something went out) (d:paikhiatna, going out, with pa marking a man: in the verses the man out of whom the demons had gone) (e:Dawite a ~ in Zeisu tawh) (b:paikhiatna) (r:42.8.38/42.8.35) (q:draft)
paikhiatnasa = (t:adj) (w:left/gone out from) (d:paikhiat, go out, with na, place, and sa, already: that one has gone out from) (e:Ka ~ inn mahah ciahkik ning) (b:paikhiat) (r:40.12.44) (q:draft)
paikhiato = (t:v) (w:come up out/go up out) (d:paikhia, go out, with to, upward) (e:pasian khat hong ~ ka mu hi) (b:paikhia) (r:9.28.13) (q:draft)
paikhiatosak = (t:v) (w:send up/make go up out) (d:paikhiato, go up out, with causative sak) (e:kote hong ~ kei in) (b:paikhiato) (r:2.33.15) (q:draft)
paikhiatpih = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out/take out) (d:go out together with someone, leading him out) (e:Izipt panin amaute ~ hi) (b:paikhiat) (r:4.23.22/2.12.51) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihin = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out/take out) (d:paikhiatpih with the linking ending in, followed by another verb: bringing out, brought out and) (e:leenggah lo nawlah ~ a that uh hi) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:40.21.39/12.10.26) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihna = (t:n) (w:bringing out/leading out) (d:noun from paikhiatpih: the act or fact of bringing or leading someone out; also the place or people to which one is led out) (e:Israel mite a ~ thu za hi) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:2.18.1/5.28.37) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihpa = (t:n) (w:one who brought out) (d:the one who led or brought someone out; -pa marks a man) (e:note a hong ~ ka hi hi) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:3.22.33/2.16.6) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihsak = (t:v) (w:let bring out) (d:paikhiatpih, bring out, with sak, cause or allow; in the verse a request to be allowed to bring someone out) (e:amaute hong ~ unla) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:1.19.8) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihte = (t:n) (w:those led out/those taken away) (d:paikhiatpih, lead out, with plural te) (e:a ~ khempeuh hong kilehhei kikin) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:24.41.14) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihto = (t:v) (w:bring up out) (d:paikhiatpih, bring out, with to, upward) (e:Leinuai panin kei nong ~ khin a) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:19.30.3) (q:draft)
paikhiatsak = (t:v) (w:send out/send away/dismiss/let go) (d:make or let someone go out) (e:Zeisu in mihonte a ~ lai takin) (b:paikhiat) (r:40.14.22/2.6.11) (q:draft)
paikhiazo = (t:v) (w:have gone out/have come out/have set out) (d:paikhia, go out, with zo marking the action as done) (e:na tanu sung panin dawi a ~ hi) (b:paikhia) (r:41.7.29/24.4.7) (q:draft)
paikhin = (t:v) (w:have gone/gone already) (d:pai go with khin, marking the action as already done) (e:lui gal khatah ~ zo uh hi) (b:pai) (r:10.17.20/12.19.23) (q:draft)
paikhit = (t:v) (w:have gone/finish going) (d:pai go with khit, completed; a paikhit ciangin is after he had gone) (e:pawikhamna-ah a ~ uh ciangin) (r:43.7.10/12.5.19) (q:draft)
paikhop = (t:v) (w:go together with/come with/accompany) (d:pai, go, with khop, together; form of paikhawm used before ciangin and lai takin) (e:vantungmite tawh hong ~ ciangin) (r:40.25.31/42.12.58) (q:draft)
paikhopna = (t:n) (w:going together/accompanying) (d:paikhop, go together with, with the noun suffix na; nong paikhopna is your going with us) (e:kote tawh nang nong ~ hi lo) (b:paikhop) (r:2.33.16) (q:draft)
paikik = (t:v) (w:return/go back/come back) (e:na pasal sam in la, hong ~ in) (b:pai) (r:43.4.16/11.13.19) (q:draft)
paikikin = (t:v) (w:returning/going back/coming back) (d:paikik with the linking ending -in, used when another action follows: returned and) (e:tua ciangin amaute hong ~ puanbuk dang khatah) (b:paikik) (r:12.7.8/11.20.5) (q:draft)
paikikna = (t:n) (w:return/coming back/coming again) (d:paikik, return, with the noun suffix na) (e:Zion-ah Topa hong ~ amaute in maitang) (b:paikik) (r:23.52.8/61.1.16) (q:draft)
paikim = (t:v) (w:all come/all go) (d:pai, go or come, with kim, all without exception: come every one of them) (e:a ~ ciat dingin sapna thu) (r:27.3.2) (q:draft)
pailai = (t:v) (w:go farther/go on/be still to come) (d:pai go or come with lai, more or still) (e:suanglot khat tan bang ~ a) (r:42.22.41/42.3.16) (q:draft)
pailam = (t:n) (w:coming/going) (d:pai go, come, with lam, the fact of: that someone has come or is coming) (e:Pasian hong ~ na phawk lohna hang ahi hi) (r:42.19.44/8.3.3) (q:draft)
pailet = (t:v) (w:pierce through/pass through/penetrate) (d:pai go, with let through: go right through a body) (e:Thaltang khat in a pumpi ~ a) (r:18.20.25/58.4.12) (q:draft)
pailetin = (t:v) (w:piercing/passing through) (d:going right through something; pailet with the linking suffix -in) (e:a lungtang ~ a leeng sungah) (b:pailet) (r:12.9.24/18.22.14) (q:draft)
paimang = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast away) (d:in the verse, of hair cut off and thrown away) (e:Na sam uh ~ unla) (r:24.7.29) (q:draft)
paimangpih = (t:v) (w:take away/carry off) (d:paimang with pih, together with: go away taking something along) (e:Hih nate na ~ un) (b:paimang) (r:43.2.16) (q:draft)
paimangta = (t:v) (w:abandon/forsake/cast off) (d:paimang with ta, marking that the act is now done) (e:ka luahsa mite ka ~ hi) (b:paimang) (r:24.12.7) (q:draft)
paina = (t:v) (w:walking) (e:Topa Pasian a ~ ging) (b:pai) (r:1.3.8)
painasa = (t:v) (w:have gone/have passed through) (d:pai with na and sa, already, used before a noun of place: the place where someone has gone; a painasa-ah means where it has passed, in its wake) (e:Israel khempeuh tawh ka ~ mun khempeuh) (b:pai) (r:13.17.6/4.14.7) (q:draft)
paingei = (t:v) (w:usually go/be used to going) (d:pai, go, with ngei, be accustomed to; a paingei bangin is as was his custom) (e:a ~ bangin kikhopna inn-ah) (r:42.4.16) (q:draft)
painop = (t:v) (w:want to go/be willing to go) (d:pai go, with nop, the form of nuam want used in dependent clauses, as before kei leh and ciangin) (e:Jerusalem-ah a ~ kei leh) (r:38.14.17/26.1.12) (q:draft)
painopna = (t:n) (w:wish to go/place one wants to go) (d:painop, want to go, with the noun suffix na; the wish to go, and the place where one wants to go) (e:na ~ peuhpeuhah na pai thei hi) (b:painop) (r:24.40.4/44.7.23) (q:draft)
painuam = (t:v) (w:want to go/be willing to go/want to come) (d:pai go, come, with nuam want) (e:kei kiangah nong ~ kei veve uh hi) (r:43.5.40/44.19.30) (q:draft)
paipa = (t:n) (w:one who comes/one who goes) (d:pai with -pa, the man who goes; hong paipa is he who comes) (e:min tawh hong ~ in thupha ngah ta hen) (b:pai) (r:41.11.9/43.6.46) (q:draft)
paipah = (t:v) (w:go at once/hurry/go quickly) (d:pai go with pah at once) (e:humpinelkai kikhumna-ah a va ~ hi) (r:27.6.19/42.1.39) (q:draft)
paipahin = (t:v) (w:going at once/coming straight up) (d:paipah, go at once, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:Judas zong Jesuh kiangah hong ~) (b:paipah) (r:40.26.49/15.5.3) (q:draft)
paipai = (t:v) (w:keep going/go on/go about) (d:pai go, said twice to show that the action continues; kot paipai, keep going round) (e:kulhpi tungah kot ~ uh a) (r:19.55.10/3.15.3) (q:draft)
paipaina = (t:see) <paipaina-ah>
paipaina-ah = (t:adv) (w:wherever it goes) (d:pai, go, doubled, with na, place, and ah, at or to: to whatever place one goes) (e:a pei’ ~ adangte in zui-in) (r:26.10.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipak = (t:v) (w:come soon/come for a while) (d:pai, go or come, with pak, quickly or for a short while) (e:ka hong ~ theih lohna) (r:45.15.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipel = (t:n) (w:basket) (d:large carrying basket) (e:~ sawm le nih a dim hi) (r:40.14.20/41.8.8) (q:draft)
paiphei = (t:v) (w:go across/run along) (d:pai, go, with phei, crosswise or level; in the verse of a row of rooms running along one level of a building) (e:dawl khat gual ~ suak-ah inndei neu sawmthum) (r:26.41.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipih = (t:phrase) (w:go along with) (b:pai)
paipih = (t:v) (w:brought) (e:khomun leh ngasa hong ~ un) (b:pai) (r:40.14.18/1.2.22)
paipihin = (t:v) (w:bring/take/lead) (d:paipih with the linking suffix in, followed by another verb, bringing or taking along) (e:a luang ~ hankhuk sungah a vui) (b:paipih) (r:41.6.29/3.8.6) (q:draft)
paipihkha = (t:v) (w:bring/take along) (d:paipih, take along, with kha, happen to; with loin, so as not to bring) (e:biakna sa le ante ~ loin) (r:26.46.20) (q:draft)
paipihkik = (t:v) (w:bring back/lead back) (d:paipih take along, lead, with kik back) (e:amaute’ gamah ka ~ ding hi) (b:paipih) (r:26.37.21/24.31.9) (q:draft)
paipihmang = (t:v) (w:bring along/bring in) (d:paipih, take along, with mang, wholly; in the verse, bring everyone in) (e:mi khempeuh hong ~ khin in) (r:42.14.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipihna = (t:n) (w:bringing/leading/taking along) (d:noun from paipih; kong paipihna is my bringing you, and before a noun the place to which one is brought) (e:Note kong ~ gamah tungin) (b:paipih) (r:4.15.18/2.19.4) (q:draft)
paipihpa = (t:n) (w:the one who led/he who brought) (d:paipih, take along or lead, with pa, the male one; said of God who led his people) (e:gamlak nawkin ama mite a ~ tungah) (b:paipih) (r:19.136.16/5.8.15) (q:draft)
paipihsak = (t:v) (w:cause to bring/let bring/let carry) (d:paipih with sak: make or let someone bring or take a person or thing along) (e:na sanggampa uh hong ~ un) (b:paipih) (r:1.42.16/41.11.16) (q:draft)
paipihsuk = (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:take someone along down to a place, in Acts before the council) (e:amaute upa vaihawmte kiangah ka ~ hi) (b:paipih) (r:44.23.28/45.10.7) (q:draft)
paipihto = (t:v) (w:take up/bring up/lead up) (d:paipih take along with to, upward) (e:dawimangpa in Zeisu ~ a) (b:paipih) (r:42.4.5/14.1.4) (q:draft)
paipihtoh = (t:v) (w:bring up/take up/lead up) (d:form of paipihto used before a kipan and theih) (e:Israel-te ka ~ a kipan tuni dongin) (b:paipihto) (r:13.17.5/13.15.12) (q:draft)
paipite = (t:todo) (q:draft, follows singhiang, branch, in a list of leafy boughs; the meaning of paipi is not clear from one verse)
paisak = (t:v) (w:send/let go/send away) (d:causative of pai, make or allow someone to go) (e:Zeisu in tua pa thakhatin ~ a) (b:pai) (r:41.1.43/2.9.17) (q:draft)
paisakin = (t:v) (w:sending/letting go) (d:paisak send or let go with the linking ending -in: sending, and so; hong paisakin is letting me go) (e:Efesa khua-ah mi ~ pawlpi upate a sam) (b:paisak) (r:44.20.17/9.20.29) (q:draft)
paisakkik = (t:v) (w:send back/send again/let come again) (d:paisak, send or let go, with kik, again or back) (e:kiangah hong ~ inla) (b:paisak) (r:7.13.8/58.13.19) (q:draft)
paisakna = (t:n) (w:sending) (d:paisak, send or let go, with the noun suffix na; the act of sending) (e:a Tapa a hong ~ thu) (b:paisak) (r:62.4.14/16.2.5) (q:draft)
paisan = (t:v) (w:depart) (e:hong ~ uh hi) (r:24.5.23)
Paisan = (t:n) (w:Passover) (e:A kiseh hunin ~ pawi) (r:4.9.2/42.22.1)
Paisan Pawi = (t:n) (w:Passover) (e:hong ciahkik mite in ~ bawl uh hi) (r:15.6.19/14.35.19)
paisanin = (t:v) (w:leaving/going away from/going off) (d:paisan go away from, leave, with the linking ending in) (e:amaute ~ khua sung pan paikhia a) (b:paisan) (r:40.21.17/52.1.10) (q:draft)
paisanna = (t:n) (w:departure) (b:paisan)
Paisanna = (t:n) (w:Passover/passing over) (d:paisan pass over with the noun suffix na; Topa’ Paisanna is the Lord's Passover) (e:~ hangin biakpiakna ahi hi) (b:Paisan) (r:2.12.27) (q:draft)
paisawm = (t:v) (w:intend to go/plan to go) (d:pai, go, with sawm, intend) (e:hih mipa koi lai-ah ~ hi ding) (r:43.7.35) (q:draft)
paisim = (t:v) (w:go secretly/go in secret) (d:pai go, with sim, secretly, without being seen) (e:Zeisu zong a kilang loin a ~ hi) (r:43.7.10/26.17.15) (q:draft)
paisuak = (t:adj) (w:nonstop) (e:Topa na zahtakna zom ~ in) (r:20.23.17)
paisuak = (t:adv) (w:forever) (e:Mihingte sungah ka Kha om ~ nawn lo ding hi) (r:1.6.3/19.103.9)
paisuakah = (t:adv) (w:all the way along/right around) (d:paisuak, going straight on, with ah, at; in the verse, along the whole circuit of the city) (e:Khuapi kimkot ~ pi zali sawmnih) (b:paisuak) (r:26.48.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
paisuakin = (t:adv) (w:forever/for good/continually) (d:after a verb: going on without end or without turning back) (e:Topa in hong nial ~) (b:paisuak) (r:19.77.7/13.17.14) (q:draft)
paisuakin = (t:v) (w:go on through/pass on/continue on) (d:paisuak with the linking ending in: going straight on through a place) (e:Tua gamah ~ thu-um mite a hansuah) (b:paisuak) (r:44.20.2/6.18.18) (q:draft)
paisuaknop = (t:v) (w:want to go straight on) (d:paisuak, go straight on, with nop, want, the form of nuam used before uh hangin) (e:ka ~ uh hangin) (r:44.27.7) (q:draft)
paisuakpah = (t:v) (w:go straight at once/go directly) (d:pai, go, with suak, right through, and pah, at once: go straight there without delay) (e:Siampipa kiangah ~ inla kivelsak in) (r:42.5.14/41.1.29) (q:draft)
paisuaksak = (t:v) (w:let through/make pass through/let pass) (d:paisuak go right through with sak cause or allow) (e:mong khat dongin a zawl laita ~ hi) (b:paisuak) (r:2.36.33/16.2.7) (q:draft)
paisuaksak = (t:v) (w:make continue/make last) (d:paisuak in its sense of going on without end, with sak cause; keep someone in a state for good) (e:khang tawntungin siampi hi ~ ding hi) (b:paisuak) (r:2.40.15/58.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
paisuakzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to continue/manage to go on) (d:paisuak, right on or continuing, with zawh, be able; placed after another verb, as thuak paisuakzawh, be able to go on enduring) (e:gimna i thuak ~ leh amah tawh i ukkhawm) (r:55.2.12/46.7.11) (q:draft)
paisuakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to get through/be able to carry on) (d:paisuak go right through, go on without stopping, with zo, be able; after another verb, manage to keep on doing it to the end) (e:nangmah in na sem ~ ding hi) (b:paisuak) (r:2.18.23/18.19.8) (q:draft)
paisuk = (t:v) (w:go down/come down/descend) (e:Samson Timnah-ah ~ a) (b:pai) (r:7.14.1/1.11.5) (q:draft)
paisukin = (t:v) (w:going down/go down) (d:paisuk go down with the linking ending -in, used when another verb follows) (e:amah ~ a numei tawh kiho hi) (b:paisuk) (r:7.14.7/2.19.25) (q:draft)
paisukna = (t:n) (w:way down/descent/slope) (d:paisuk go down with the noun ending na, the place where a road goes down) (e:Oliv Mual tung pan a ~ mun) (b:paisuk) (r:42.19.37/12.12.20) (q:draft)
paisukpa = (t:n) (w:one who goes down) (d:paisuk, go down, with pa, the one who) (e:Leinuai-a ~ hong ciahkik ngei nawn lo) (b:paisuk) (r:18.7.9) (q:draft)
paisukpih = (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:paisuk, go down, with pih, together with) (e:i pa hong ~ un) (b:paisuk) (r:1.45.13) (q:draft)
paisuksak = (t:v) (w:let go down/make go down/bring down) (d:paisuk, go down, with the causative sak) (e:zang gamah ~ lo uh hi) (b:paisuk) (r:7.1.34/11.2.6) (q:draft)
paisukte = (t:n) (w:those who go down) (d:often of the dead who go down to the pit) (e:Leihawm sunga ~ tawh a kibang) (b:paisuk) (r:19.28.1/23.14.19) (q:draft)
paita = (t:v) (w:come/be coming) (d:pai with ta, marking that the coming has now begun or happened; with in, an urgent request to come) (e:hih lai-ah hong ~ hi) (b:pai) (r:9.9.17/66.1.7) (q:draft)
paitawm = (t:v) (w:come on one's own/come of one's own accord) (d:pai, go or come, with tawm, by oneself; come without being sent by another) (e:ama thu tawh hong ~ leh) (r:43.5.43/43.8.42) (q:draft)
paite = (t:n) (w:those who come/those who go) (d:pai with the plural ending -te, the people who come or go; with hong before it, those coming this way) (e:leilu lam pan-a hong ~ en dih in) (b:pai) (r:24.13.20/43.12.20) (q:draft)
paithei = (t:v) (w:can go/can come/be able to walk) (d:pai with thei can, may: be able or allowed to go, come or walk) (e:Pa Pasian kiangah i ~ hi) (b:pai) (r:49.2.18/40.11.5) (q:draft)
paitheih = (t:v) (w:be able to come/be able to go) (d:pai go or come with theih can; mostly in paitheih nading, so that one may come) (e:note kiangah ka hong ~ nading) (b:pai) (r:45.1.10/49.3.12) (q:draft)
paitheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to walk/being able to go) (d:paitheih, be able to go, with the noun suffix na; lam a paitheihna ding a hilh is teach to walk) (e:lam a ~ ding a hilh pa) (b:paitheih) (r:28.11.3) (q:draft)
paito = (t:v) (w:go up/ascend) (e:Tua lai mun panin amah Be-ersheba-ah ~ hi) (b:pai) (r:1.26.23/19.47.5) (q:draft)
paitoh = (t:v) (w:go up/come up/ascend) (d:form of paito used before words such as ciangin and leh) (e:Jerusalem khua-ah a ~ ciangin) (b:paito) (r:44.11.2/7.13.20) (q:draft)
paitohna = (t:n) (w:ascent/way up/going up) (d:the act of going up or the place where one goes up; Bethhoron paitohna lampi, the road going up to Beth Horon) (e:Bethhoron ~ lampi-ah amaute delhin) (b:paitoh) (r:6.10.10/19.122.3) (q:draft)
paitosak = (t:v) (w:bring up/let go up/make go up) (d:paito go up, with sak, cause or allow) (e:Egypt panin kote hong ~ na hi hiam) (b:paito) (r:4.20.5/1.50.5) (q:draft)
paizaw = (t:v) (w:go rather/go instead) (d:pai, go, with zaw, rather) (e:Israel mite lakah va ~ un) (b:pai) (r:40.10.6/48.1.17) (q:draft)
paizia = (t:n) (w:way/course) (d:the way something or someone goes, pai go with zia manner; thu paizia is the course of a matter) (e:nomau’ ~ bang hi lo hi) (r:23.55.8/10.14.20) (q:draft)
paiziate = (t:n) (w:ways/manners of going) (e:ka ~ nomau’ paizia bang hi lo hi) (b:paizia) (r:23.55.8/23.55.9) (q:draft)
paizo = (t:v) (w:be able to come/get in) (d:pai, come or go, with zo, be able) (e:David hong ~ peuhmah lo ding hi) (b:pai) (r:10.5.6) (q:draft)
paizo = (t:v) (w:have come) (d:pai, come, with zo marking the action as done) (e:a susia dingte hong ~ uh hi) (b:pai) (r:24.12.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
pak = (t:n) (w:flower/blossom) (e:a nun leh a ~ tawh a om) (r:2.37.20/60.1.24) (q:draft)
pak = (t:adv) (w:quickly/at once/soon) (d:placed after a verb, the action is done quickly, at once or for a short while) (e:a lu kunsuk ~ a, bia hi) (r:2.34.8/19.81.14) (q:draft)
pak = (t:v) (w:bloom/blossom/bud) (e:leengguite a ~ nai hiam) (r:22.7.12/2.9.31) (q:draft)
pakan = (t:n) (w:dish/plate) (d:small dish or bowl; in Numbers a gold dish holding incense) (e:kham ~ khat paknamtui a dim tawh) (r:4.7.14/4.7.20) (q:draft)
pakante = (t:n) (w:dishes/plates) (d:small dishes or ladles among the temple vessels, in these verses for incense) (e:taitehte leh paknamtui adingin ~ leh biakinn sung) (b:pakan) (r:12.25.14/2.37.16) (q:draft)
pakin = (t:adv) (w:quickly/suddenly/at once) (d:pak with the ending in, after a verb: happening fast or all at once) (e:tuate bei ~, kote ka maimang uh hi) (b:pak) (r:19.90.10/18.9.23) (q:draft)
pakkhia = (t:v) (w:blossom/bloom/come into flower) (d:pak, bloom, with khia, out) (e:A sel phetin ~ pah a) (b:pak) (r:1.40.10) (q:draft)
pakkual = (t:n) (w:wreath/garland) (d:pak, flower, with kual, ring; a ring of flowers, in the verses a carved or cast ornament) (e:a pang ciatah ~ om hi) (r:11.7.30/11.7.36) (q:draft)
pakkualte = (t:n) (w:wreaths/garlands) (d:pakkual, wreath, with the plural ending te) (e:bawngtalte le ~ hong paipih hi) (b:pakkual) (r:44.14.13) (q:draft)
pakna = (t:n) (d:pak, quickly or for a short while, with the noun suffix na; after a verb it names the doing of it quickly or briefly, as in hauh pakna, getting rich quickly, and ten’ pakna, staying for a while) (e:Ol tak-a hauh ~ in kiam kik) (b:pak) (r:20.13.11/24.35.7) (q:draft)
paknamtui = (t:n) (w:incense/perfume/spice) (e:tua tungah a namtui ~ hal hi) (r:2.40.27/42.23.56) (q:draft)
paknamtuite = (t:n) (w:spices/perfumes/incense) (e:na ~ tawh na siam tawpin) (b:paknamtui) (r:23.57.9/11.10.25) (q:draft)
pakpak = (t:adv) (w:quickly/easily/readily) (d:pak, quickly, doubled; placed after a verb, be quick to do it, as in heh pakpak, be easily angered) (e:heh ~ lo, mite’ mawhna ciamteh lo) (r:46.13.5/45.3.15) (q:draft)
pakpalh = (t:n) (w:open flower/blossom/flower in bloom) (d:pak, flower, with palh, open out) (e:umgah le ~ lim kigelh hi) (r:11.6.18/18.14.2) (q:draft)
pakpalhte = (t:n) (w:flowers/blossoms/open flowers) (e:nisuh kungte le ~ bawl a) (b:pakpalh) (r:11.6.35/34.1.4) (q:draft)
pakta = (t:v) (w:praise/commend/admire/approve of) (d:think well of someone and say so) (e:a pasal in zong ~ mahmah a) (r:20.31.28/58.11.2) (q:draft)
paktat = (t:adj) (w:promiscuous/loose/immoral) (d:sexually immoral, placed after the noun; numei paktat is a prostitute or harlot, and pasal paktat a male prostitute) (e:numei ~ nih kumpipa kiangah hong pai uh) (r:11.3.16/11.22.46) (q:draft)
paktat = (t:v) (w:prostitute oneself/commit prostitution) (e:Na tanute uh a ~ manun) (r:28.4.14) (q:draft)
paktatin = (t:v) (w:committing prostitution/acting immorally) (d:paktat, prostitute oneself, with in linking it to the next verb; paktatin gamta is behave as a prostitute) (e:Na monu Tamar ~ gamta hi) (b:paktat) (r:1.38.24/66.18.9) (q:draft)
paktatna = (t:n) (w:prostitution/promiscuity/sexual immorality) (d:also used of unfaithfulness to God through idol worship) (e:~ pana piang tate ahih manin) (b:paktat) (r:28.2.4/26.16.26) (q:draft)
paktatnate = (t:n) (w:prostitutions/immoral acts) (d:paktatna, prostitution, with the plural ending te; in the verse of Jezebel, where the English has idolatry) (e:~ leh aisannate tua zahin a tam) (b:paktatna) (r:12.9.22) (q:draft)
paktatnu = (t:n) (w:female prostitute/harlot) (d:paktat, promiscuous, with nu, marking a woman) (e:A ~ a kiguaihna sum ahi a) (b:paktat) (r:5.23.18) (q:draft)
paktatpa = (t:n) (w:male prostitute) (d:paktat, promiscuous, with pa, marking a man) (e:a ~ a kiguaihna sum ahi zongin) (b:paktat) (r:5.23.18) (q:draft)
paktatsak = (t:v) (w:lead into prostitution/make unfaithful) (d:paktat, prostitute oneself, with causative sak) (e:na tapate uh ~ kha ding uh hi) (b:paktat) (r:2.34.16) (q:draft)
