phunsan = (t:v) (w:grumble against/murmur against/complain against) (d:phun grumble with san directed at someone) (e:Moses leh Aaron ~ uh a) (b:phun) (r:4.16.41/4.14.27) (q:draft)
phunsanna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:grumbling against someone) (e:amaute in nang hong ~) (b:phunsan) (r:4.17.5/4.14.27) (q:draft)
phunsansak = (t:v) (w:make grumble against) (d:phunsan grumble against, with sak cause) (e:mihonte Topa a ~) (b:phunsan) (r:4.14.36) (q:draft)
phunsante = (t:n) (w:grumblers/those who grumble against) (d:phunsan grumble against, with the plural te: those who have grumbled against someone) (e:tungsiah, kei hong ~) (b:phunsan) (r:4.14.29) (q:draft)
phusak = (t:v) (w:drive toward/make head for) (d:phu head into or push against, with sak cause; of steering a ship toward the shore) (e:lamah teembaw a ~ uh hi) (b:phu) (r:44.27.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
phusuakin = (t:adv) (w:heading straight on/blundering on) (d:apparently phu head into with suak through and the ending in: going straight on into danger without turning aside) (e:mi mawkmawkte in ~ thuak uh hi) (r:20.27.12/20.22.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
phut = (t:v) (w:set up/erect/establish/plant) (d:set something firmly in place, as a pillar, a foundation or a people) (e:a inn ding khuampi sagih ~ hi) (r:20.9.1/19.104.5) (q:draft)
phutin = (t:v) (w:set up/erect/establish) (d:phut with -in, linking it to the next verb: setting up, having erected) (e:a khuam ~ a min Jakhin phuak hi) (b:phut) (r:11.7.21/9.15.12) (q:draft)
phutkhak = (t:v) (w:encounter/come upon/meet) (d:come up against someone or something on the way) (e:note’ ~ ding mi khempeuh) (r:2.23.27/38.10.11) (q:draft)
phutkhin = (t:v) (w:have established/have set up) (d:phut set up, with khin already done) (e:vantungah ama tokhom ~ a) (b:phut) (r:19.103.19) (q:draft)
phutna = (t:n) (w:press/onset) (d:phut with the noun suffix na; gal in a phutna, the place where battle presses hard, where the English has the heat of battle) (e:gal in a ~ panin hong tai uh) (r:23.21.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutsak = (t:v) (w:have set up/cause to be erected) (d:phut set up, with the causative sak: have someone set a thing up) (e:a khuam ~ hi) (b:phut) (r:17.5.14) (q:draft)
phutthei = (t:v) (w:can lay/can set up) (d:phut set up, with thei can) (e:khuam thupi dang ~ nawn lo ding hi) (b:phut) (r:46.3.11) (q:draft)
pi = (t:n) (w:foot) (d:unit of length, a foot; where the English Bible has cubits the number is converted, one cubit counted as a foot and a half) (e:a tun’ ~ kua val a sang) (r:9.17.4/1.6.15) (q:draft)
pi = (t:n) (w:dam/mother/female) (d:with a before it, the mother of a young animal or the female of an animal, as vom a pi, a she-bear; of a person, a pi is the grandmother) (e:A ~’ lametna teng bei ta hi) (r:26.19.5/12.2.24) (q:draft)
pi = (t:part) (d:suffix added to a noun or adjective, big, great or chief) (e:kham milim ~ khat bawl saka) (r:27.3.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
pia = (t:v) (w:give) (e:Zingsol zong amah ka ~ ding hi) (r:66.2.28/49.4.27)
Pia = (t:v) (w:give) (d:pia khia is give up, hand over) (e:~ khia un, leitaw lam kiangah) (b:pia) (r:23.43.6) (q:draft)
piagawp = (t:v) (w:inflict harshly) (d:pia give, with gawp roughly or severely; gim piagawp is punish severely) (e:khasiat loin gim ~ hi) (b:pia) (r:20.20.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
piak = (t:v) (w:gave) (e:hih bang lamlahnate kong ~ uh) (b:pia) (r:52.4.2/1.3.12)
Piak = (t:v) (w:give) (d:piak, form of pia give used before a noun; Gim Piak Ni, the day suffering is given, is the day of punishment) (b:piak) (r:42.21.22) (q:draft)
piakha = (t:v) (w:may give/happen to give) (d:pia give, with kha perhaps or happen to) (e:thupha hong ~ ding hi) (r:29.2.14) (q:draft)
piakhawm = (t:v) (w:give together/offer along with) (d:pia give with khawm together: give or offer one thing with another) (e:an-a biakna tawh ~ ding hi) (b:pia) (r:3.14.31/2.34.25) (q:draft)
piakhia = (t:v) (w:give out/give away/give up/hand over) (d:pia give with khia out) (e:sihna dongin a nuntakna ~ a) (b:pia) (r:23.53.12/20.21.26) (q:draft)
piakhin = (t:v) (w:have given/have granted) (d:pia with khin, already: the giving is done) (e:deihna nang in na ~ a) (b:pia) (r:19.21.2/62.2.20) (q:draft)
piakhol = (t:v) (w:command beforehand/give in advance) (d:pia give with khol beforehand; thu piakhol, give an order or a word ahead of time) (e:ci-in thu ~ ahih manin) (r:23.36.21/44.7.7) (q:draft)
piakik = (t:v) (w:give back/return/restore) (d:pia give with kik back, again) (e:nang tungah kong ~ ding hi) (b:pia) (r:7.17.3/12.8.6) (q:draft)
piakkhawm = (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing together with another, of the grain offering that goes with an animal offering; piak, give, with khawm, together) (e:tuutal khat tawh ~ dingin) (b:piak) (r:4.15.6/26.46.11) (q:draft)
piakkhiat = (t:v) (w:give out/give up/lay down) (d:give away from oneself; nuntakna piakkhiat is lay down the life) (e:Ka nuntakna ~ theih nading) (b:piak) (r:43.10.18/15.7.16) (q:draft)
piakkhiatnate = (t:n) (w:givings/things given out) (d:piakkhiat give out, with the noun suffix na and plural te; paired with ngahna, receiving) (e:ka ngahna le ka ~) (b:piakkhiat) (r:50.4.15) (q:draft)
piakkhit = (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:piak give, with khit finish; with ciangin, after having given or offered) (e:khatvei a ~ ciangin) (r:58.10.12) (q:draft)
piakkholh = (t:v) (w:command beforehand/tell in advance) (d:piak give with kholh beforehand; the form of piakhol used before bangin: thu a piakkholh bangin, just as he said beforehand) (e:Thu a ~ mah bangin) (r:41.16.7/44.4.27) (q:draft)
piakkholhna = (t:n) (w:promise/word given beforehand) (d:piakkholh, give beforehand, with the noun suffix na; thu piakkholhna, a word given in advance, a promise) (e:ci-in thu ~ bangin) (b:piakkholh) (r:45.4.18/58.7.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakkhong = (t:n) (w:gift/free gift) (d:something given freely; also placed before letsong or na: a freely given gift or thing) (e:Pasian’ ~ na pen sum tawh lei) (r:44.8.20/47.9.15) (q:draft)
piakkhongin = (t:adv) (w:as a gift/as a free gift) (d:piakkhong free gift, with the suffix in) (e:~ kingaihsutsak lo hi) (b:piakkhong) (r:45.4.4) (q:draft)
piakkhongna = (t:n) (w:giving/gift/bestowal) (d:piakkhong, give freely, with the noun suffix na: the giving of something as a free gift, as of grace or of the Holy Spirit) (e:hehpihna hong ~ tawh kizui-in) (b:piakkhong) (r:45.12.6/44.10.45) (q:draft)
piakkhop = (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing along with another; another form of piakkhawm) (e:tuunote tawh ~ ding pen) (r:26.46.7/26.46.5) (q:draft)
piakkik = (t:v) (w:give back/restore/give again) (d:piak give with kik again or back; thu piakkik, give a further order or word) (e:Keimah in thu kong ~ mateng) (b:piak) (r:15.4.21/19.14.7) (q:draft)
piakma = (t:v) (w:before giving) (d:piak give, with ma before: before he gives) (e:ama gamhluah dingteng a ~) (r:48.4.2) (q:draft)
piakna = (t:n) (w:offering) (e:lei pan-a piang gah ~ Topa tungah) (b:piak) (r:1.4.3/1.4.4)
piakna = (t:n) (w:contribution/donation) (e:beh lutangte in ut thu-a ~ bawl uh a) (b:piak) (r:13.29.6/15.1.4)
piaknasa = (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:piak give, with na and sa, already done: what has been given, or the place where one has given) (e:thupha hong ~ tawh kizui-in) (b:piak) (r:5.16.17/11.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
piaknate = (t:n) (w:offerings/sacrifices/gifts) (e:A maan biakna ~ lui un la) (b:piakna) (r:19.4.5/19.107.22) (q:draft)
piaknop = (t:v) (w:want to give/be willing to give) (d:piak, give, with nop, want; ama piaknop zahzah is as much as he wants to give) (e:ka ~ peuhpeuh tungah ka pia thei) (r:42.4.6/26.46.5) (q:draft)
piaknopna = (t:n) (w:willingness to give/willingness/generosity) (d:piaknop want to give, with the noun suffix na) (e:A lungsim-ah ~ a nei mi) (b:piaknop) (r:2.35.21/47.8.12) (q:draft)
piakpa = (t:n) (w:the one given to) (d:the man to whom something is given; piak, give, with pa marking a male person. Topa thupha piakpa is the one blessed by the Lord) (e:amah thupha ka ~ kua ahi hiam) (b:piak) (r:1.27.33/43.13.26) (q:draft)
piakpah = (t:v) (w:give at once/give immediately) (d:piak give, with pah at once) (e:lutang nong ~ ding ka deih hi) (r:41.6.25) (q:draft)
piaksa = (t:adj) (w:given) (d:already given, piak with the completive suffix sa; thu piaksa is what was commanded) (e:tungah a ~ khuapite Solomon in) (b:piak) (r:14.8.2/1.7.9) (q:draft)
piaksak = (t:v) (w:offer for/give on behalf of) (d:piak, give, with sak: give or offer something for another person, as a priest offers a sacrifice for someone) (e:amau’ adingin biakna ~ uh hi) (b:piak) (r:12.17.32/3.7.8) (q:draft)
piaksak = (t:v) (w:make give/have given) (d:piak, give, with causative sak: cause something to be given or handed over) (e:kikhamna sum a ~ khit uh ciangin) (b:piak) (r:44.17.9/7.15.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
piaksate = (t:n) (w:things given/those given) (d:what has been given, also of orders given and loans made) (e:Ta’ khut sungah na ~ khempeuh) (b:piaksa) (r:43.17.2/6.11.15) (q:draft)
piaktawm = (t:v) (w:give of own accord/give voluntarily) (d:piak give, with tawm showing that the subject acts on his own) (e:utna tawh na ~ uh ahi kei hi) (r:7.21.22) (q:draft)
piakte = (t:n) (w:offerings/gifts/things given) (d:the things that someone gives or has given) (e:kei na hong ~ khempeuh in) (b:piak) (r:43.17.7/4.7.13) (q:draft)
piaktheih = (t:v) (w:can give/be able to give) (d:piak give with theih can; with nading, so that one may give or hand over) (e:Jesuh a ~ nading lampi zon ding) (b:piak) (r:42.22.6/43.5.26) (q:draft)
piaktheihna = (t:n) (d:being able to give or hand over; piaktheih can give, with the noun suffix na; with dingzia, the way in which one might hand over) (e:Jesuh a ~ dingzia a kikum uh hi) (b:piaktheih) (r:42.22.4) (q:draft)
piaktuak = (t:adj) (w:fit to be given to) (d:piak give with tuak fitting; piaktuak sa is consider it right to give to) (e:~ ka sakte) (r:24.27.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakzah = (t:n) (w:amount given/as much as given) (d:piak, give, with zah, amount: the amount that was given; a piakzah mah, the same amount as was given) (e:Nang ka hong ~ mah) (r:40.20.14/42.6.34) (q:draft)
piakzaw = (t:v) (w:give more) (d:piak give with zaw more: give more than before or more than to others) (e:a nunung lamah thupha lim ~ hi) (b:piak) (r:18.42.12/5.7.14) (q:draft)
piakzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to give/afford) (d:form of pia zo, can give, used before bangbang, ding and kei leh) (e:a ~ bangbang pia ding hi) (r:3.14.22/3.27.8) (q:draft)
piakzia = (t:n) (w:way of giving/manner of giving) (d:piak give, with zia manner; gim piakzia is the way punishment is dealt out) (e:gim a ~ hih bang ahi hi) (r:18.27.13) (q:draft)
pial = (t:v) (w:turn aside/stray/deviate) (d:leave the path or the right way, often as lam pial) (e:lam ka ~ ngei kei hi) (r:18.23.11/14.34.2) (q:draft)
pialin = (t:v) (w:turning aside/straying/departing) (d:pial with the linking suffix -in) (e:thu-upna lam pan ~ mi kimkhatte’ upna) (b:pial) (r:55.2.18/4.22.23) (q:draft)
pialkha = (t:v) (w:stray/turn aside/go astray) (d:pial, turn aside, with kha, happen to: leave the right way, often with kei in a warning) (e:lam man panin ~ kei un) (r:58.13.9/20.4.27) (q:draft)
pialkhia = (t:v) (w:turn away/stray/depart from) (d:turn aside and leave a path, a command or a way of acting) (e:tua lampi panin ~ lo hi) (b:pial) (r:14.20.32/19.119.21) (q:draft)
pialkhiat = (t:v) (w:turn away/desert/depart from) (d:form of pialkhia used before zawh and endings) (e:kei kiangpan a ~ zawh uh) (b:pialkhia) (r:55.1.15) (q:draft)
pialkhiate = (t:n) (w:those who stray/strays) (d:pialkhia turn away with the plural te: those who turn away from a path or a rule) (e:A kilawm gamtatna panin a ~) (b:pialkhia) (r:20.21.16/19.119.118) (q:draft)
pialkhiatpih = (t:v) (w:lead astray/turn away with) (d:pialkhiat turn away, with pih together with: draw someone away) (e:amaute a ~ ding gamdang mi) (b:pialkhiat) (r:18.15.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialkhin = (t:v) (w:have turned away/have departed) (d:pial turn aside, with khin already done) (e:lampi panin amaute ~ uh a) (b:pial) (r:55.2.18) (q:draft)
pialna = (t:n) (w:straying/turning aside/error) (d:pial, turn aside, with the noun suffix na; lam pialna, leaving the right way) (e:Lam a ~ hang uh) (b:pial) (r:24.3.21/59.5.20) (q:draft)
pialpih = (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:pial turn aside, with pih, take along: make someone leave the right way, as lam pialpih) (e:Israel ka mite lam a ~ uh hi) (b:pial) (r:24.23.13/23.44.20) (q:draft)
pialpual = (t:adv) (d:expressive word placed after satsak, make hot: heated through, inflamed; said of people heated by wine) (e:amaute a satsak ~ matengin) (r:23.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to stray/mislead) (d:pial turn aside with sak cause; lam pialsak, lead off the right way) (e:na thupiaknate panin kei hong ~ kei in) (b:pial) (r:19.119.10/20.12.26) (q:draft)
pialsakin = (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to stray) (d:pialsak cause to stray, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:na lampi panin kote hong ~) (b:pialsak) (r:23.63.17/48.5.7) (q:draft)
pialte = (t:n) (w:strays/those who stray) (d:pial stray with the plural te; a lam pialte, those that have left the way) (e:a lam ~ kaikhawmin) (b:pial) (r:26.34.16/26.34.4) (q:draft)
pian = (t:v) (w:be born/come into being) (d:often written pian’; form of piang used before endings and in compounds: pian’na, birth or origin; pian’sak, create or cause) (e:na ~’na na nu lungdamsak in) (r:20.23.25/59.1.18) (q:draft)
pian = (t:n) (w:likeness/form/appearance) (d:something that looks like another thing; a kibang pian khat, a figure like, what looked like) (e:mihing tawh a kibang ~ khat ka mu hi) (r:26.8.2/26.1.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
pian'napa = (t:n) (w:ancestor/forefather/father) (d:pian be born, come into being, with the noun suffix na, origin, and pa for a man: the man from whom a people descends) (e:leh Hamath mite’ ~ ahi hi) (r:13.1.16/13.1.23) (q:draft)
pian'saksate = (t:n) (w:creatures/created things) (d:piansaksa what has been created, with plural te; written with an apostrophe in this text) (r:18.12.10) (q:draft)
piancil = (t:n) (w:creation/beginning) (d:the time when something first came into being; lei piancil, the creation of the world) (e:Lei ~ akipanin kuamah in) (r:43.9.32/41.10.6) (q:draft)
piancilna = (t:n) (w:origin/beginning/creation) (d:piancil with the noun suffix na: the first coming into being of something; piancilna mun, the place a people came from) (e:amaute’ ~ mun) (b:piancil) (r:26.29.14/66.3.14) (q:draft)
piang = (t:v) (w:become) (e:innkiu suang a ~ hi) (r:41.12.10/1.1.7) begin to be
piangin = (t:v) (w:come into being/arise/spring up) (d:piang be born or come about, with the linking ending in) (e:zan khat thu-in hong ~) (b:piang) (r:32.4.10/66.4.11) (q:draft)
piangkha = (t:v) (w:may be produced/may come about) (d:piang come into being, with kha perhaps or happen to) (e:an ~ ding a) (r:20.13.23) (q:draft)
piangkhia = (t:v) (w:come forth/arise/be born/break out) (d:piang, come into being, with khia, out: spring out of, originate from) (e:Amaute sungah mei hong ~ a) (b:piang) (r:19.106.18/23.48.1) (q:draft)
piangkhiasak = (t:phrase) (w:brought forth) (e:kung tuamtuamte ~ a) (b:piangkhia) (r:1.1.12) (q:?)
piangkik = (t:v) (w:be produced again/come forth again/arise afterward) (d:piang, come into being, with kik, again or in turn: of crops, grow again; of a law or a generation, come later) (e:nektheih ding gah le teh hong ~ hi) (b:piang) (r:59.5.18/48.3.17) (q:draft)
piangsa = (t:adj) (w:happened/past) (d:piang happen with sa already; a piangsa thu, what has happened) (e:a ~ thu khempeuh khat leh khat) (b:piang) (r:42.24.14/44.5.7) (q:draft)
piangsak = (t:v) (w:produce) (e:leitang in tampi ~ a) (b:piang) (r:1.41.47/20.15.4)
Piangsak = (t:v) (w:create/make/bring into being) (d:piangsak, cause to come into being, written with a capital when said of God: a Piangsak pa, the Creator, the Maker) (e:amah a ~ pa bek mah in) (b:piangsak) (r:18.40.19/23.43.15) (q:draft)
piangsaka = (t:v) (w:cause/produce/raise) (d:piangsak cause to be, with the linking a, and) (e:tuipi hualte ~, huihpi nungsak hi) (b:piangsak) (r:19.107.25) (q:draft)
piangsakin = (t:phrase) (w:make) (e:pilna tawh leitung ~) (b:piangsak) (r:24.51.15/1.1.27) (q:?)
piangsakkha = (t:v) (w:cause/bring about) (d:piangsak cause with kha, happen to: bring something about, often without meaning to) (e:mite khempeuh’ sihna ka ~ hi) (r:9.22.22/47.2.4) (q:draft)
piangsakkik = (t:v) (w:cause to happen again/bring about again) (d:piangsak cause to be, with kik again) (e:a piang ngeisa mah ~ zelzel hi) (b:piangsak) (r:21.3.15) (q:draft)
piangsakpa = (t:n) (w:creator/maker/author) (d:he who brings something into being; -pa marks a male) (e:Na khempeuh a ~ in Pasian ahi hi) (b:piangsak) (r:58.3.4/40.19.4) (q:draft)
Piangsakpa = (t:n) (w:Creator/Maker) (d:piangsak, cause to come into being, with -pa marking a male person: the one who made, written with a capital as a title of God) (e:nang hong ~ phawk in) (b:piangsakpa) (r:21.12.1/23.43.15) (q:draft)
piangsakte = (t:n) (w:those who cause/those who stir up) (d:piangsak cause or produce, with te, those who) (e:kitotna a ~ ahi hi) (b:piangsak) (r:20.6.19/23.59.17) (q:draft)
piangsakthei = (t:v) (w:can produce/can give rise to) (d:piangsak cause to be, with thei can) (e:le haitatna a ~ ngaihsutna hoih lote) (b:piangsak) (r:41.7.22) (q:draft)
piangsakzaw = (t:v) (w:cause rather/produce more) (d:piangsak cause to be, with zaw more, used with sangin than) (e:sangin siatna na ~ uh hi) (b:piangsak) (r:46.11.17) (q:draft)
piangsakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to bring about/manage to cause) (d:piangsak cause to be, with zo be able to) (e:ngah nading uh ~ kha dingin) (b:piangsak) (r:45.11.14) (q:draft)
piangsate = (t:n) (w:produce/things produced) (d:piangsa already come into being, with plural te; lo pan-a piangsate is what has grown from the field) (e:lo pan-a ~ na ne ding uh hi) (b:piangsa) (r:3.25.12) (q:draft)
piangtawm = (t:v) (w:arise of itself/spring up by itself) (d:piang come into being with tawm, of oneself: come about on its own, without another cause) (e:Leilak panin gimna hong ~ lo a) (r:18.5.6/43.18.34) (q:draft)
piangte = (t:n) (w:crops/produce/fruit) (d:the things that are produced or come into being, plural noun use of piang) (e:a ~ na kaikhawm ding uh hi) (b:piang) (r:2.23.10/5.7.13) (q:draft)
piangthei = (t:v) (w:can come about/be able to arise/can happen) (d:piang, come into being, with thei, be able) (e:zakna panin upna hong ~ a) (b:piang) (r:45.10.17/46.2.9) (q:draft)
piangthuah = (t:v) (w:be born in addition) (d:piang be born, with thuah in addition, more) (e:tanute le tapate ~ lai hi) (r:10.5.13) (q:draft)
piangvat = (t:v) (w:happen suddenly/come about quickly) (d:piang happen with vat, suddenly) (e:tua thu thakhatin hong ~ hi) (r:14.29.36/42.21.35) (q:draft)
piangzaw = (t:v) (w:arise instead/happen rather) (d:piang happen, with zaw rather or more) (e:buaina ~ kha ding) (b:piang) (r:40.27.24) (q:draft)
piangzo = (t:v) (w:can happen/come to pass) (d:piang happen, with zo be able to) (e:na cih bangun ~ ding hi) (b:piang) (r:42.17.6) (q:draft)
pianin = (t:adv) (w:by birth/at birth) (d:pian be born, come into being, with the ending in: at or by the birth of a person, or when a thing came to be) (e:Kei ka ~ Rom mi-a piang ka hi hi) (b:pian) (r:44.22.28/18.38.21) (q:draft)
piankhak = (t:v) (w:happen/take place) (d:pian happen, with khak happen to, the form used before loh: so that it may not happen) (e:thu hong ~ loh nadingin) (r:41.13.18) (q:draft)
piankhiat = (t:v) (w:come into being/spring forth) (d:pian come into being, with khiat out) (e:Tuate a hong ~ ma-in) (b:pian) (r:23.42.9) (q:draft)
piankhiatna = (t:n) (w:origin/source/place of origin) (d:where a person or thing comes from) (e:hih mipa hong ~ i theih hi a) (b:piankhiat) (r:43.7.27/62.4.7) (q:draft)
piankhit = (t:v) (w:have happened) (d:pian happen, with khit finish; with ciangin, after it had happened) (e:Hih bang thuteng a ~ ciangin) (r:44.19.21) (q:draft)
pianlim = (t:n) (w:shape/form/likeness) (d:the outward form of a thing; of the Son, the exact likeness of God) (e:a liatna le a ~ a kibang) (r:11.7.37/58.1.3) (q:draft)
pianlui = (t:n) (w:old self/old nature) (d:pian nature or form one is born with, with lui old) (e:na ~ uh paikhia unla) (r:49.4.22) (q:draft)
pianma = (t:adv) (w:before the birth of/before the creation of/before it happens) (d:pian, form of piang, be born or come about, with ma, before: before something was born, made or took place; leitung pianma is before the world was made) (e:hihte khempeuh hong ~-in keima hangin) (r:42.21.12/49.1.4) (q:draft)
pianna = (t:n) (w:formation)
pianna = (t:n) (w:generation)
pianngei = (t:n) (w:nature/natural state) (d:pian be born with ngei, the usual or original way: what a person or thing is by birth, by nature) (e:note’ ~ ahi lo a kiciing oliv kung) (r:45.11.24) (q:draft)
pianpih = (t:adj) (w:inborn/natural/from birth) (d:what one is born with; a pianpih mittaw, blind from birth, pianpih lungsim, the natural mind or instinct) (e:a ~ mittaw mi khat a mu hi) (b:pian) (r:43.9.1/49.2.3) (q:draft)
pianpihin = (t:adv) (w:from birth/by birth) (d:pianpih inborn, with the suffix in) (e:Mi pawlkhat a ~ gehsa bang om a) (b:pianpih) (r:40.19.12) (q:draft)
piansak = (t:v) (w:produce/generate) (e:Tua bangte in kitotna a ~ lamtak) (s:piangsak) (r:55.2.23) (q:?)
