puksih = (t:v) (w:die of hunger/starve/perish) (d:form of puksi used before sangin, ding and similar words; puksih ding stands for famine in Job 5:22) (e:Nek ding nei lo-a ~ sangin) (b:puksi) (r:25.4.9/18.5.22) (q:draft)
puksisak = (t:v) (w:cause to perish/starve/kill off) (d:make someone fall dead, in the verses always by famine; puksi with the causative sak) (e:kial tawh ka ~ ding hi) (b:puksi) (r:24.44.12/26.5.16) (q:draft)
puksite = (t:n) (w:the dead/those who have perished) (d:puksi fall dead with the plural te; kialin a puksite, those who have died of famine) (e:kialin a ~ bekbek ka mu hi) (b:puksi) (r:24.14.18) (q:draft)
puksuk = (t:v) (w:fall down/fall/slump down) (d:puk fall with suk downward: fall to the ground, also fall facedown before God) (e:Amah in lei tungah ~ a) (b:puk) (r:44.9.4/12.9.24) (q:draft)
