puksukpah = (t:v) (w:fall down at once/drop down) (d:puk fall with suk down and pah at once) (e:thakhatin si-in ~ a) (r:44.5.5) (q:draft)
pukta = (t:v) (w:has fallen/is fallen) (d:puk fall with ta, which shows that the event has now taken place) (e:Kumpi gilo pa ~ a) (b:puk) (r:23.14.4) (q:draft)
pukte = (t:n) (w:those who fall/the fallen) (d:puk, fall, with plural te: people who fall or fall away; sat pukte, those who struck someone down) (e:thakhatin a ~ ahi hi) (b:puk) (r:40.13.21/23.28.1) (q:draft)
pukthei = (t:v) (w:can stumble/may fall) (d:puk stumble with thei can) (e:khuavak nei lo ahih manin ~ hi) (b:puk) (r:43.11.10) (q:draft)
