sepkhoppih = (t:v) (w:work together with) (d:sep work with khop together and pih with, na ka sepkhoppih is my fellow worker) (e:Khrih Jesuh sungah na ka ~ Prisilla le Aquila) (r:45.16.3/45.16.9) (q:draft)
sepkik = (t:v) (w:serve again/work again) (d:sep, work or serve, with kik, again) (e:biakinn sungah na a ~ theih nadingun) (b:sep) (r:26.44.27) (q:draft)
seploh = (t:v) (w:not worked/not toiled on) (d:sep, work, with loh, not: describes a thing that one did not work for) (e:Note in na ~ uh leitang) (r:6.24.13) (q:draft)
sepna = (t:n) (w:work/labour/toil/deed) (d:nominal form of sem, work) (e:a ~ khempeuh thamanin bang ngah) (b:sep) (r:21.3.9/21.4.9) (q:draft)
sepnate = (t:n) (w:deeds/works/acts) (e:na ~ bangzah takin lian) (b:sepna) (r:19.92.5/19.150.2) (q:draft)
sepnop = (t:v) (w:want to do/be willing to do/wish to serve) (d:form of sem do, work, serve with nuam want, used before kei, nading and in relative clauses) (e:ka ~ khempeuh ka sem ding hi) (r:23.46.10/6.24.15) (q:draft)
sepnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to do/willingness to act) (d:sepnop, want to do, with the noun suffix na) (e:na a manin ~ lungsim nei) (b:sepnop) (r:58.13.18) (q:draft)
seppih = (t:v) (w:work with/work together with/help) (d:sep with pih, do a work together with someone or alongside him) (e:nasemte in nangma nasemte ~ ding uh a) (b:sep) (r:11.5.6/23.44.24) (q:draft)
seppihna = (t:n) (w:working with/help) (d:seppih work with and the noun suffix na, Pasian in na a seppihna is what God did together with them) (e:Pasian in na a ~ thu) (b:seppih) (r:44.15.4/44.14.27) (q:draft)
seppihte = (t:n) (w:helpers/those who work with) (d:seppih work with and te: those who join someone in a work) (e:mawhna nasep a ~ daan a pia hi) (b:seppih) (r:23.31.2) (q:draft)
sepsa = (t:n) (w:work/deed/labour) (d:sep, work, with sa, already: what has been done, work that is finished) (e:Na khut tawh na ~ thaman) (b:sep) (r:19.128.2/19.22.31) (q:draft)
sepsak = (t:v) (w:serve/work for) (d:sep with -sak, do work for someone; na sepsak, to serve) (e:kei in a na ka ~ Pasian’ vantungmi) (b:sep) (r:44.27.23/24.22.9) (q:draft)
sepsak = (t:v) (w:make work/drive to work) (d:sep with causative -sak, cause someone to work) (e:gilkialna in nak ~ semsem zaw hi) (b:sep) (r:20.16.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
sepsakna = (t:n) (w:work done for/deed done for) (d:sepsak, do for someone, with the noun suffix na: what one has done on behalf of another) (e:nangma hong ~ hang ahi hi) (b:sepsak) (r:23.26.12/42.8.39) (q:draft)
sepsaksa = (t:v) (w:served/worked for) (d:sepsak work for someone with sa marking a completed action) (e:nangma na kong ~ na thei hi) (b:sepsak) (r:1.30.26) (q:draft)
sepsan = (t:v) (w:be doing/carry on doing) (d:sep, work, with san; a sepsan laitak is while they are doing it; exact force of san not clear) (e:amaute in a ~ laitak uh ahi hi) (b:sep) (r:14.34.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
sepsate = (t:n) (w:works/deeds/things done) (e:Mi khempeuh in Pasian’ ~ mu uh a) (b:sepsa) (r:18.36.25/19.66.5) (q:draft)
sepsateng = (t:n) (w:all the work done/all the labour) (d:sepsa, work done, with teng, all of) (e:amau’ ~ khempeuh a khu-in leengmang hi) (b:sepsa) (r:35.2.13) (q:draft)
sepsawm = (t:v) (w:purpose to do/intend to do) (d:sep, do, with sawm, intend) (e:Khazih hanga a ~ a sehsa thuthuk) (r:49.1.9) (q:draft)
sepsepte = (t:n) (w:services/regular duties) (d:sep, work, doubled for what is done again and again, with the plural te: the things the priests keep doing) (e:Leitung a siampite’ ~ pen) (r:58.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
septe = (t:n) (w:deeds/works/acts) (d:things done; a lamdang ama septe, his wonderful deeds) (e:a lamdang ama ~ mu uh hi) (b:sep) (r:19.107.24/19.96.3) (q:draft)
septeng = (t:n) (w:all that one does/everything done) (d:sep do with teng, all: all the things someone does) (e:Pa in a ~ mah a Tapa in) (b:sep) (r:43.5.19/43.5.20) (q:draft)
septheih = (t:v) (w:be able to do/be able to work) (d:sep, work or do, with theih, be able, used before nading: so that one can do or carry out) (e:na hoih na phate a ~ nadingun) (b:sep) (r:56.3.14/55.3.16) (q:draft)
sepzaw = (t:v) (w:work more/work harder) (d:sep, work, with the comparative zaw) (e:Amaute sangin na ka nak ~ a) (b:sep) (r:47.11.23) (q:draft)
sepzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to do/accomplish) (d:sep, work or do, with zawh, form of zo, be able; used before nading) (e:~ nading siamna pen Pasian hong piak) (r:47.3.5/54.1.12) (q:draft)
sepzawhna = (t:n) (w:accomplishment/work done/deed) (d:sepzawh, be able to do, with the noun suffix na: what one has managed to do) (e:Eite’ ~ hang hi loin) (b:sepzawh) (r:55.1.9/46.15.10) (q:draft)
sepzia = (t:n) (w:way of working/manner of work) (d:sep, work, with zia, manner) (e:Kote in zong amau’ ~ mah bangin) (r:47.11.12) (q:draft)
serafim = (t:n) (w:seraphim/seraph) (d:heavenly beings with six wings seen by Isaiah; in the text followed by vanmite, heavenly beings) (e:Ama tungah ~ vanmite ding uh hi) (r:23.6.2/23.6.6) (q:draft)
Serah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Serah) (r:4.26.46/13.7.30)
Seraiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seraiah) (r:13.6.14/10.8.17)
