Serug = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Serug) (r:1.11.22)
sese = (t:adv) (w:ever/at all) (d:adds force to a question with bang hangin, why: why ever, why of all things) (e:mi khem hatte gualzo ~ ahi hiam) (r:24.12.1/24.20.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
sesing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cypress/broom tree) (d:a kind of tree; the verses use it for the cypress of Isaiah 44:14 and for the broom bush whose wood makes hot coals in Psalm 120:4) (e:~ kung khat ahi a) (r:23.44.14/19.120.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Seth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seth) (r:1.5.6)
Sethur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sethur) (r:4.13.13)
sette = (t:n) (w:machines/engines/devices) (d:plural of set, machine, here war machines for shooting arrows and hurling stones) (e:mi a siamte in a bawltawm ~) (r:14.26.15) (q:draft)
seu = (t:n) (w:ephah) (d:a dry measure for grain and flour, used for the Hebrew ephah) (e:annel ~ khat sehsawm suah sehthum) (r:4.15.9/28.3.2) (q:draft)
seuhseuh = (t:adv) (d:describes a quick repeated movement: of wine, bubbling up in the cup; of arrows, being shaken to and fro) (e:Hai sungah a phuan ~) (r:20.23.31/26.21.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
seuhseuhin = (t:adv) (d:seuhseuh with the suffix in: with a quick shaking movement, here of arrows shaken to cast lots) (e:a thaltangte sing ~) (b:seuhseuh) (r:26.21.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
