tungsakin = (t:v) (w:bring upon/send upon/cause to come) (d:tungsak with the linking ending in: bringing a thing such as famine, plague or war upon a land, followed by a further action) (e:Tua gamah pulpi ~) (b:tungsak) (r:26.14.19/19.105.16) (q:draft)
tungsakkik = (t:v) (w:bring back upon/bring upon again) (d:tungsak bring upon with kik, back or again) (e:ama lu tung mahah ~ ding hi) (b:tungsak) (r:11.2.32/5.28.60) (q:draft)
tungsakkikin = (t:v) (w:bring back upon/repay) (d:tungsakkik with the linking ending in: making wrongs come back on those who did them) (e:amau’ tung mahah ~) (b:tungsakkik) (r:19.94.23) (q:draft)
tungsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who fulfills/one who brings about) (d:tungsak make come about, with pa for a male doer: he who has made the promise come true) (e:ka pa David tungah a ~ na hi hi) (b:tungsak) (r:14.6.15) (q:draft)
tungsakte = (t:n) (w:those who receive/hosts) (d:tungsak let arrive, with plural te: those who take a traveller into their house) (b:tungsak) (r:42.9.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to bring about/be able to fulfil) (d:tungsak bring about with zo, be able, finish; in Malachi 2:2 said of a curse already brought) (e:Pasian in a thuciamsa ~ taktak ding hi) (b:tungsak) (r:45.4.21/39.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsan = (t:prep) (w:above/right over) (d:in ama omna tungsan innkhum, the roof above where he was) (e:ama omna ~ innkhum a vuhlet) (r:41.2.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsiah = (t:adv) (w:upward/and above/or more) (d:from a stated age or number upward, usually after panin or pan as a tungsiah) (e:kum sawmnih panin a ~ peuhmah) (r:2.30.14/4.3.22) (q:draft)
tungsiahte = (t:n) (w:those above/those older) (d:tungsiah upward with the plural te: the people from a stated age upward) (e:Kum sawmguk pan a ~ pen) (b:tungsiah) (r:3.27.7/14.31.17) (q:draft)
tungsilh = (t:n) (w:outer garment/garment) (d:tung over with silh wear: a garment worn on top) (e:naipuan ~ kong silhsak hi) (r:26.16.10/43.21.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
