vangvang = (t:adv) (w:bitterly/intensely) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done strongly or without letting go; kap vangvang is wail bitterly) (e:sih suah bangin kap ~ in) (r:24.6.26/22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Vaniah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Vaniah) (r:15.10.36)
vanin = (t:v) (w:waving/motioning) (d:of the hand: move it through the air as a sign, with the linking ending in; also written vaanin) (e:a natna mun tungah a khut ~) (r:12.5.11/44.24.10) (q:draft)
vankah = (t:n) (w:medium) (e:~ khat thu dongin a lamlah ding) (r:13.10.13/9.28.7)
vankahna = (t:n) (w:divination/spiritism/consulting of mediums) (d:vankah medium with the noun suffix na: the practice of seeking word from spirits) (e:~ leh aisanna zang uh a) (b:vankah) (r:12.17.17/3.20.6) (q:draft)
vankahte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:gecko)
vankahte = (t:n) (w:medium) (e:~ leh aisante a gamsung panin beisak) (b:vankah) (r:9.28.3/12.23.24)
vankahthei = (t:n) (w:medium/spiritist) (d:one who is able to call up spirits; vankah with thei can) (e:Endor-ah ~ khat om hi) (b:vankah) (r:9.28.7) (q:draft)
vankahtheite = (t:n) (w:mediums/spiritists) (d:vankahthei medium with the plural te) (e:~ leh aisante tawh nasem hi) (b:vankahthei) (r:12.21.6) (q:draft)
vankemte = (t:n) (w:treasurers) (d:van goods with kem keep and plural te: those who keep the king's goods) (e:kumpi ~ khempeuh tungah hih bangin) (r:15.7.21) (q:draft)
vankhai = (t:n) (w:peg/hook) (d:van, thing, with khai, hang: a peg or hook on which things are hung) (e:~ ah a kikhai bangin) (r:23.22.24/23.22.25) (q:draft)
vankhaina = (t:n) (w:peg/hook/hanger) (d:something to hang things on, from van things, khai hang and na) (e:a kician mun khatah ~ bangin ka khenkip) (b:vankhai) (r:23.22.23/2.26.32) (q:draft)
vankhainate = (t:n) (w:hooks/clasps) (d:plural of vankhaina, a thing on which something is hung or fastened, as the hooks and clasps of the tabernacle) (e:a ~ leh a gaknate in ngun) (b:vankhaina) (r:2.38.10/2.35.11) (q:draft)
vankia = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil) (d:goods taken in war; the other text has vankila in the same verse, so this may be a misprint of it) (e:Shinar panin ~ lakah puanhoih khat) (r:6.7.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
vankiate = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil/loot) (d:goods taken by enemies, set beside mat ding mi, people to be captured) (e:mat ding mi le ~ suak ding uh) (b:vankia) (r:12.21.14) (q:draft)
vankila = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil) (d:van goods with kila, taken: goods taken in war) (e:Shinar panin ~ lakah puan hoih khat) (r:6.7.21) (q:draft)
vankim = (t:n) (w:midair/middle of the sky/mid-heaven) (d:used with lai-ah: vankim lai-ah, in the middle of the sky) (e:~ lai-ah a leeng vasa khempeuh) (r:66.19.17/6.10.13) (q:draft)
Vankim = (t:name) (w:Vankim)
vankinusia = (t:n) (w:spoil/plunder) (d:van goods with kinusia left behind: goods left by a defeated enemy) (e:Judah mite in ~ tampi tak pua) (r:14.14.13/19.119.162) (q:draft)
vankinusiate = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:goods left behind by a defeated enemy and taken by the victors) (e:Gal sungah a ngah ~ sung panin) (b:vankinusia) (r:13.26.27/9.15.19) (q:draft)
vankisutte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:van goods with kisut be plundered and plural te: goods taken by force) (e:mite in ~ a hawm ciangun) (r:23.9.3/23.42.22) (q:draft)
vankoihna = (t:n) (w:storehouse/storeroom/treasury) (d:van, goods, with koihna, place of keeping) (e:a tapa tungah ~ inn kipia hi) (r:13.26.15/12.16.8) (q:draft)
vankoihnate = (t:n) (w:storehouses/storerooms/treasuries) (d:vankoihna, storehouse, with the plural te) (e:sathau koihna ding ~ zong a bawl hi) (b:vankoihna) (r:14.32.28/12.18.15) (q:draft)
vankuumpi = (t:n) (w:vault of the sky/dome of heaven) (d:van sky with kuum, arch or vault, and pi, great: the sky seen as a great cover over the earth) (e:~ tawh leitung a khuhsuk hi) (r:30.9.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanlakte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils) (d:van goods with lak taken and plural te: the things taken in war) (e:a ~ uh sung pan puante silhsak) (r:14.28.15) (q:draft)
vanlei = (t:v) (w:buy/buy goods) (d:van goods with lei buy; vanlei vanzuak is buying and selling, trade) (e:~ vanzuakin paikhia thei lo uh hi) (r:66.13.17) (q:draft)
Vanleipa = (t:n) (w:buyer) (d:van, goods, with lei, buy, and pa marking a male person; set against vanzuakpa, the seller) (e:~ in vanzuakpa kiangah) (r:20.20.14) (q:draft)
vanleite = (t:n) (w:buyers) (d:vanlei buy goods with the plural te: those who buy) (e:a tote, ~ leh van zuakte) (b:vanlei) (r:23.24.2) (q:draft)
vanlelei = (t:n) (w:sky and earth/heaven and earth) (d:van sky, le and, lei earth, written as one word; vanlelei kikalah is between sky and earth, in midair) (e:~ kikalah amah a kikhai-in) (r:10.18.9/42.12.56) (q:draft)
vanmanpha = (t:n) (w:treasure/valuables/precious things) (d:van goods with manpha precious; vanmanpha koihna is the treasury, the place where valuables are kept) (e:~ koihna ah kham darik) (r:16.7.71/13.26.22) (q:draft)
vanmanphate = (t:n) (w:treasures/valuables/precious things) (e:kumpipa’ inn-a ~ lakhia hi) (b:vanmanpha) (r:14.12.9/14.36.18) (q:draft)
vanmite = (t:n) (w:heavenly beings/celestial beings/angels) (d:van, heaven, with mi, person, and plural te) (e:Ama tungah serafim ~ ding uh hi) (r:23.6.2/19.89.6) (q:draft)
vanmong = (t:n) (w:end of the heavens/horizon) (d:van sky with mong end, edge: the farthest edge of the sky) (e:Ama suahna ~ khat pan hi a) (r:19.19.6/5.30.4) (q:draft)
vanna = (t:n) (w:hole/opening) (d:kulh a vanna mun is a place where the wall has a hole; probably related to vang, opening) (e:kulh a ~ mun khat hong lak hi) (r:26.8.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
vannuai = (t:todo) (q:draft, mi vannuai khempeuh stands where the NIV has all the rest of the people; meaning of vannuai not clear from one verse)
vannusiatte = (t:n) (w:spoils/goods left behind) (d:van goods with nusiat, leave behind, and the plural te: what a defeated king left) (e:Hadadezer’ ~ sung panin a ap) (r:10.8.11) (q:draft)
vanpi = (t:n) (w:heavens/sky) (d:the great expanse of the sky) (e:~ in ama nasepna taangko hi) (b:van) (r:19.19.1/18.9.8) (q:draft)
vanpite = (t:n) (w:heavens/skies) (e:na ~ niamsak in la hong paisuk in) (b:vanpi) (r:19.144.5/19.147.8) (q:draft)
vanpua = (t:adj) (w:load-carrying/goods-carrying) (d:van goods with pua carry; vanpua leeng is a wagon and vanpua mi a carrier, a porter) (e:Solomon in ~ mi tul sawmsagih) (r:11.5.15/26.23.24) (q:draft)
vanpuakte = (t:n) (w:cargo/goods carried/baggage) (d:van goods with puak carry and plural te: the things a ship or a traveller carries) (e:teembaw le a ~ a siat) (r:44.27.10/40.2.11) (q:draft)
vansak = (t:v) (w:make successful/prosper) (d:in maa vansak, make a journey or undertaking go well; probably vang succeed with the causative sak) (e:ka maa nong ~ ding le) (r:1.24.42) (q:draft, low confidence)
vante = (t:n) (w:goods/wares/cargo/merchandise) (e:~ tui sungah a paaikhia uh hi) (b:van) (r:44.27.18/26.27.33) (q:draft)
vante = (t:n) (w:heavens/skies) (e:~ tunga om tuite aw) (b:van) (r:19.148.4) (q:draft)
vantumgmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:apparently a misprint of vantungmi, angel) (e:Sagihna ~ in peengkul tum ding) (r:66.10.6) (q:draft)
vantung = (t:n) (w:heaven) (e:~ panin Topa in hong en sukin) (r:25.3.50/42.11.16) the promised land
vantung = (t:n) (w:sky) (e:van kuumpi pen ~ ci hi) (r:1.1.8/1.1.20) the upper atmosphere
Vantung = (t:n) (w:heaven/sky) (d:vantung written with a capital, mostly in Vantung Gam, the kingdom of heaven) (e:~ Gam in ama nasemte ciamtehna lai) (b:vantung) (r:40.18.23/1.1.8) (q:draft)
vantunga = (t:adv) (w:in heaven) (d:vantung with the place ending a: in heaven, of heaven) (e:~ a om kote Pa aw) (b:vantung) (r:40.6.9/25.3.41) (q:draft)
vantungah = (t:phrase) (w:in heaven/in the sky) (e:~ a om thei nawn kei uh hi) (b:vantung) (r:66.12.8/40.5.48)
Vantungah = (t:phrase) (w:in heaven) (d:Vantung, heaven, with the place marker ah) (e:~ a om na Pa uh khat bek) (b:Vantung) (r:40.23.9) (q:draft)
vantunggam = (t:n) (w:heavenly realm/heaven) (d:vantung heaven with gam, land or kingdom) (e:~ tawh kipawl hong sapna thupha) (r:58.3.1) (q:draft)
vantungmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (e:Zekhariah in ~ a muh ciangin) (b:vantung) (r:42.1.12/1.22.15) (q:draft)
Vantungmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:vantungmi, angel, capitalised in the title Mi That Vantungmi, the destroying angel) (e:Mi That ~ in Israel mite) (b:vantungmi) (r:58.11.28) (q:draft)
vantungmite = (t:n) (w:angels/heavenly beings) (d:literally people of heaven; also those who belong to heaven) (e:Pasian’ ~ in amah dawn hi) (b:vantungmi) (r:1.32.1/42.12.9) (q:draft)
vantungte = (t:n) (w:heavens) (e:na ~ ka et ciangin) (b:vantung) (r:19.8.3) plural form of <vantung>
vantungte = (t:n) (w:skies) (e:tung-a om ~ thu pia-in) (b:vantung) (r:19.78.23/5.28.23) plural form of <vantung>
vanvan = (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb for hurried, restless or rushing movement: rushing, pounding) (e:Ka lungtang kisai ~ a) (r:24.4.19/20.1.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanvan = (t:v) (w:stretch out/spread out) (d:doubled form of van, stretch out the hands, again and again) (e:amaute in a khut uh ~ ding uh a) (r:23.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanzatte = (t:n) (w:equipment/gear/tackle) (d:van goods with zat use and the plural te: things in use; teembaw vanzatte is a ship's tackle) (e:A thai ciangin teembaw ~ pawlkhat) (r:44.27.19) (q:draft)
vanzuak = (t:v) (w:sell goods/trade) (d:van goods with zuak sell; sumzuak vanzuak is buying and selling, trading) (e:sumzuak ~ cihte om nawn lo ding hi) (r:38.14.21) (q:draft)
vanzuakin = (t:v) (w:selling/trading) (d:vanzuak sell goods with the suffix in) (e:vanlei ~ paikhia thei lo uh hi) (b:vanzuak) (r:66.13.17) (q:draft)
vanzuakna = (t:n) (w:market/selling of goods) (d:vanzuak sell goods with the noun suffix na; vanzuakna phual is a marketplace) (e:Mihon omna ~ phual, lamdung citeng) (b:vanzuak) (r:20.7.12) (q:draft)
vanzuakpa = (t:n) (w:seller) (d:vanzuak sell goods with pa, male person) (e:Vanleipa in ~ kiangah) (b:vanzuak) (r:20.20.14) (q:draft)
vapai = (t:v) (w:go/go there) (d:pai go with va before it, marking movement away to another place) (e:Amaute a ~ lai takun ka ngen tawh) (r:28.7.12) (q:draft)
vapi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:stork) (d:va bird with pi big: large bird; in the verses always gun vapi, river big bird, for the stork) (e:gun ~ bangin kalaoh vasa leng thei lo) (b:va) (r:18.39.13/3.11.19) (q:draft)
vapite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:storks/large birds) (d:plural of vapi, large bird; gun vapite and tui vapite, large water birds, are used for the stork and the ibis) (e:gun ~ in bu a tom uh hi) (b:vapi) (r:19.104.17/24.8.7) (q:draft)
vasa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bird) (e:innkhum dawn-a ~ khatguak om tawh ka kibang) (r:19.102.7/3.14.50)
vasabu = (t:n) (w:nest) (e:~ khat, sing tung ahi a) (r:5.22.6)
Vasabu = (t:n) (w:nest/bird's nest) (d:vasabu, nest, at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khat, sing tung ahi a) (b:vasabu) (r:5.22.6) (q:draft)
vasam = (t:v) (w:go and call/call) (d:sam call with va before it, marking going over to do it) (e:Tua pa ~ un) (r:41.10.49) (q:draft)
vasapi = (t:see) <kalaoh-vasapi>
vasate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:birds) (e:a bokvak ganhingte leh a leeng ~) (b:vasa) (r:19.148.10/1.1.20)
vasateng = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:all the birds/birds) (d:vasa bird with teng, all of them) (e:a hiang tunga ~ hawlkhia in) (b:vasa) (r:27.4.14) (q:draft)
Vashti = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Vashti) (r:17.1.9/17.2.4)
vat = (t:v) (w:strike/smite/attack) (d:strike down, of God or an army striking people) (e:Topa in Nabal ~ hi) (r:9.25.38/2.17.13) (q:draft)
vatak = (t:see) <vatak-um>
vatak-um = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wild gourd) (d:a wild plant with a vine, gui, and gourds, umgah, not fit to eat) (e:~ gui khat mu-in) (r:12.4.39) (q:draft)
vatawt = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:duck/water bird) (d:kind of bird; in the lists of unclean birds gam vatawt and tui vatawt stand where English has owl, swan, pelican or gull) (e:kalaoh-vasa, pengpelep, ~, musi nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.16/3.11.18) (q:draft, low confidence, the English bird names differ from verse to verse)
vatgawp = (t:v) (w:strike down/smite/defeat) (e:Gezer ciang dong Filistiate ~ hi) (b:vat) (r:10.5.25/7.6.16) (q:draft)
vatgawpin = (t:v) (w:striking down/attacking/defeating) (d:vatgawp, strike down, with the linking ending -in) (e:la-in amaute ~ that hi) (b:vatgawp) (r:6.11.17/6.15.16) (q:draft)
vatin = (t:v) (w:strike/smite/attack) (d:vat strike with the linking ending in, striking or having struck; often namsau tawh vatin, with the sword) (e:namsau tawh ~ a khuapi hal uh hi) (b:vat) (r:7.1.8/11.20.37) (q:draft)
vatin = (t:adv) (w:suddenly/all at once) (d:after a verb, of something that comes on abruptly; khuamial hong suak vatin, darkness came suddenly) (e:khuamial hong suak ~ khua na mu) (r:18.22.11/19.48.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
vatkhia = (t:see) <vatkhia-in>
vatkhia-in = (t:v) (w:sweeping away/striking off) (d:vat strike with khia, out, away, and the suffix in) (e:sehkhat ~ leilak a denna hi) (r:66.12.4) (q:draft)
vatlum = (t:v) (w:strike dead/kill/slay) (d:strike so that the person dies, often with the sword) (e:namsau tawh mi khempeuh ~ ding uh hi) (r:26.26.11/10.6.7) (q:draft)
vatmai = (t:v) (w:strike down/smite/cut down/defeat) (d:kill or defeat in great numbers, as with a sword) (e:ama mite namsau tawh ~ hi) (r:2.17.13/19.135.8) (q:draft)
vatmaipa = (t:n) (w:one who struck down/slayer) (d:vatmai, strike down, with pa, the male one who does it: a vatmaipa is he who struck down) (e:Kumpi liante a ~ tungah) (b:vatmai) (r:19.136.17/19.136.10) (q:draft)
vatmaisak = (t:v) (w:strike down/destroy) (d:vatmai strike down with sak, done to what belongs to someone: cut down all that he has built) (e:amaute in hong ~ ding uh hi) (b:vatmai) (r:26.28.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
vatmang = (t:v) (w:cut off/strike down/sweep away) (d:vat strike with mang, away, gone: strike so that the person is no more; of death taking the children from the streets) (e:Kong zinga naupangte a ~ a) (r:24.9.21) (q:draft)
vattansak = (t:v) (w:strike down/cut down) (d:vat strike with tan cut off and sak: strike vines and trees so that they break off) (e:leengguite leh theikungte ~ a) (r:19.105.33) (q:draft)
vattuk = (t:v) (w:strike down/cut down/fell) (e:Jonathan in amaute ~ a) (r:9.14.13/24.46.15) (q:draft)
vattum = (t:v) (w:cut down/slay) (d:vat strike with tum, completely; said of the sword) (e:note uh namsau in ~ ding a) (r:34.2.13) (q:draft)
vawh = (t:v) (w:call/title) (e:nau min ~) (r:1.2.20)
vawh = (t:v) (w:sow) (e:khaici ~) (r:41.4.3/40.13.24)
vawhin = (t:v) (w:saddle/load) (d:form of vawh with the linking suffix in, putting a saddle or load on a pack animal) (e:la van ~ a nasempa kiangah) (r:12.4.24/1.22.3) (q:draft)
vawhin = (t:v) (w:sow/plant) (d:form of vawh with the linking suffix in, sowing seed) (e:khaici ~ na khe tawh tui) (b:vawh) (r:5.11.10) (q:draft)
vawhpa = (t:n) (w:sower/farmer) (d:vawh sow with -pa for a man: the man who sows, in khaici vawhpa) (e:Khaici ~ in thu a vawh hi) (b:vawh) (r:41.4.14/40.13.18) (q:draft)
vawhsa = (t:adj) (w:sown/planted) (d:vawh sow with sa, already done; na vawhsa an is the crop you have sown) (e:vawh lecin na ~ an leh na leenggui) (b:vawh) (r:5.22.9) (q:draft)
vawhsak = (t:v) (w:saddle) (d:in laa van vawhsak, put the gear on a donkey for someone, saddle it) (e:Kei adingin laa van hong ~ un) (r:11.13.13/11.13.23) (q:draft)
vawhsakin = (t:v) (w:saddling/having saddled) (d:vawhsak saddle for someone with the linking ending in) (e:ama a dingin la van ~ a tungah) (b:vawhsak) (r:11.13.13) (q:draft)
vawhte = (t:n) (w:sowers/those who sow) (d:vawh sow with te, the people who sow seed) (e:Thuman lo khaici a ~ in lungkhamna tuak a) (b:vawh) (r:20.22.8/47.9.6) (q:draft)
vawhzo = (t:v) (w:be able to put through/be able to thread) (d:vawh, here put a cord through, with zo be able; not from vawh call or sow) (e:a nakpheh-ah khau ~ ding ahi hiam) (r:18.40.24/18.41.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
vazonei = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:heron) (d:in gun vazonei, a river bird in the list of unclean birds) (e:gun vapi, gun ~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.19/5.14.18) (q:draft)
ve = (t:part) (d:sentence-final particle of emphasis or urging; after a command, often as dih ve, it presses the hearer to go ahead, and after hi, as hi ve’n, it stresses a statement) (e:Kumpi Solomon en dih ~ un) (r:22.3.11/24.44.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
ve'ng = (t:part) (d:sentence-final words after hi in the speech of one person about himself, here I would surely have given; apparently an emphatic ve with a shortened first person ending) (r:10.18.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
veeng = (t:n) (w:quarter/neighbourhood) (d:a part of a town or village; Naioth veeng is the Naioth quarter of Ramah) (e:Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ panin David) (r:9.20.1/9.19.23) (q:draft)
veengah = (t:n) (w:in the quarter/in the neighbourhood) (d:veeng, a quarter or neighbourhood of a town, with the place marker ah, in or to: Naioth veengah is in Naioth, a quarter of Ramah; veeng is the long-vowel spelling of veng) (e:Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ David om hi) (b:veeng) (r:9.19.19/9.19.23) (q:draft)
veengte = (t:n) (w:neighbors) (d:plural of veeng; inn veengte is those who live in the houses nearby) (e:a lawmte leh a inn ~ sam a) (b:veeng) (r:42.15.6/12.4.3) (q:draft)
veh = (t:v) (w:visit/look after/care for) (d:go to see someone in need, as the sick, and care for them) (e:ka om lai takin nong ~ uh hi) (r:40.25.36/42.1.73) (q:draft)
veh = (t:part) (d:sentence-final word of exclamation that calls attention to something happening now, as in listen, people are crying out) (e:Horonain khua-ah mi kiko ~) (r:24.48.3/24.10.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
vei = (t:n) (w:time) (e:khat ~, thum ~) (r:2.23.14/1.43.20)
veii = (t:v) (w:wave) (d:move an offering to and fro before the Lord; veii-a biakna is a wave offering) (e:Topa mai-ah tuate ~ hi) (r:3.8.27/3.9.21) (q:draft)
