zindo = (t:v) (w:show hospitality/entertain/receive as guest) (d:welcome and look after a guest; also used as a noun, hospitality) (e:Hezekiah in amaute na ~ a) (r:12.20.13/45.12.13) (q:draft)
zindona = (t:n) (w:reception/welcome/hospitality) (d:zindo receive as a guest, with the noun suffix na) (e:amah na ~ uh a ngaihsut ciangin) (b:zindo) (r:47.7.15) (q:draft)
zinei = (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:of a man, have or take a wife, from zi wife and nei have; zinei thak pa is the bridegroom, zinei pasalnei is marrying and being given in marriage) (e:~ pasalnei cih om lo ding uh hi) (r:41.12.25/24.25.10) (q:draft)
zineih = (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:form of zinei used before ding and in dependent clauses; zineih ding hun is the time of the wedding) (e:Tuuno’ ~ ding hun hong tungta a) (b:zinei) (r:66.19.7/23.54.6) (q:draft)
zineihna = (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:zineih take a wife, with the noun suffix na; zineihna pawi is a wedding feast) (e:Tuuno’ ~ pawi-ah a kisam mite) (b:zineih) (r:66.19.9) (q:draft)
zineipa = (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:zi nei, take a wife, with -pa for a man) (e:~ a kipaikhiatpih hun hong tung ding) (b:zinei) (r:42.5.35/40.25.5) (q:draft)
zineite = (t:n) (w:married men/those who have a wife) (d:zinei have a wife, with the plural te) (e:Ahi zongin ~ in kikhen ding) (b:zinei) (r:46.7.27) (q:draft)
zineu = (t:n) (w:concubine) (d:zi, wife, with neu, small; a secondary wife) (e:Kumpi-zi sawmguk, kumpi ~ sawmgiat) (r:22.6.8/13.2.48) (q:draft)
zineute = (t:n) (w:concubines) (d:plural of zineu, a lesser wife, zi wife with neu small) (e:a pa’ ~ luppih hi) (b:zineu) (r:10.16.22/10.5.13) (q:draft)
