zingsangin = (t:adv) (w:in the morning) (e:Tuuno khat ~ na pia ding uh a) (b:zingsang) (r:4.28.4/19.90.6) (q:draft)
zingsol = (t:n) (c:star) (w:morning star) (e:Amaute tungah ~ zong ka pia ding hi) (r:66.2.28/66.22.16) (q:draft)
Zingsol = (t:n) (c:star) (w:Morning Star) (d:zingsol, the morning star, written with a capital as a title) (e:a taang khuavak ~ ka hi hi) (b:zingsol) (r:66.22.16/66.2.28) (q:draft)
zingtho = (t:v) (w:rise early/get up early) (d:zing morning, with tho rise: get up early in the morning) (e:Phalvak tungin ~ a) (r:20.31.15) (q:draft)
zingtungin = (t:adv) (w:early in the morning/at dawn) (d:zingtung early morning with the marker -in) (e:kimkhatte ~ hanah pai uh) (r:42.24.22/42.24.1) (q:draft)
zingtuungin = (t:adv) (w:early in the morning) (d:zing morning, with tuung and in) (e:~ a thawhkik khit ciangin) (r:41.16.9) (q:draft)
zinin = (t:v) (w:travelling/journeying) (d:zin, travel, with the linking suffix in; khual zinin is travelling away from home) (e:Paul khual hong ~ Efesa khua) (b:zin) (r:44.19.1) (q:draft)
zinin = (t:adv) (w:as a guest/as a stranger) (d:zin, guest or sojourner, with the suffix in; zinin om is stay as a guest or live as a foreigner) (e:ama ~ ka om uh hi) (b:zin) (r:44.28.7/44.7.29) (q:draft)
zinkhia = (t:v) (w:go away on a journey/set out/leave home) (d:zin, travel, with khia, out) (e:Inn panin gamlapi-ah a ~ mipa) (b:zin) (r:20.27.8/40.25.15) (q:draft)
zinkik = (t:v) (w:travel again/journey back) (d:zin travel, with kik again or back) (e:Note na ~ ngei nawn kei) (b:zin) (r:5.28.68) (q:draft)
zinleleeng = (t:n) (w:guests/visitors/strangers) (d:zin and leeng, guests and visitors of every kind; zinleleeng do is show hospitality) (e:~ do a siam mi) (r:56.1.8/60.4.9) (q:draft)
