zinliingte = (t:n) (w:earthquakes) (d:zin liing the earth quakes, with plural te) (e:khuaphelepte leh ~ a piang hi) (b:zinliing) (r:66.8.5/66.11.19) (q:draft)
zinlin = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:zinling, earthquake, written without the final g and with an apostrophe before ma, before, and before the suffix na) (e:~’ ma kum nih hun laitakin) (r:30.1.1/66.16.18) (q:draft)
zinling = (t:n) (w:earthquake/quake) (d:zin, earthquake, and ling, shake; also written apart as a clause, zin hong ling is the earth quaked) (e:~ khit ciangin meikuang om a) (r:11.19.12/23.29.6) (q:draft)
zinlinna = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:zinlin earthquake, with the noun suffix na) (e:galkapte in ~ le a thupiangte a muh) (b:zinlin) (r:40.27.54/38.14.5) (q:draft)
zinna = (t:n) (w:journey/travel/travelling) (d:zin, travel, with the noun suffix na; ka zinna khempeuhah is everywhere I travelled) (e:khual gamlapi ~-in paat gawp hi) (b:zin) (r:6.9.13/45.15.18) (q:draft)
zinpa = (t:n) (w:guest/visitor) (d:zin guest, with pa for a man: the male guest) (e:~’ zineu om hi) (b:zin) (r:7.19.24) (q:draft)
zinsuk = (t:v) (w:travel down/go down) (d:zin travel, with suk downward; a zinsuk a zintohna is their travelling to and fro) (e:a ~ a zintohna uhah lungmuanna om lo) (b:zin) (r:14.15.5) (q:draft)
zinte = (t:n) (w:guests/strangers/visitors) (d:plural of zin; people who come from elsewhere, guests in a house or foreigners in a place) (e:~ vui nading beel seekpa’ lei) (b:zin) (r:40.27.7/64.1.5) (q:draft)
zintohna = (t:n) (w:travelling up/going up) (d:zin travel, with toh upward and the noun suffix na; a zinsuk a zintohna is their travelling to and fro) (e:a zinsuk a ~ uhah lungmuanna om lo) (r:14.15.5) (q:draft)
