zuazuate = (t:n) (d:zuazua, expressive word for a loud rushing sound or a continuous stream, with plural te making a noun of the phrase before it: ging zuazuate, things that rattle loudly; a piak khiat zuazuate, the things given freely one after another) (e:sakol leeng ging ~ le gamlak) (b:zuazua) (r:29.2.5/15.7.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zubeel = (t:n) (w:wine jar/wineskin) (d:zu, wine or beer, with beel, pot; a vessel for wine) (e:~ khempeuh leenggahzu tawh a kidim ding hi) (r:24.13.12) (q:draft)
Zuf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuph) (r:9.1.1/13.6.35)
zuhai = (t:n) (w:drunkard) (d:zu, liquor: one given to heavy drinking; paired with anhai, glutton) (e:amah in anhai ~ ahi hi) (r:5.21.20/42.7.34) (q:draft)
zui = (t:v) (w:follow/obey/keep) (d:go after someone, or keep a word or law) (e:nusia-in a nung a ~ hi) (r:42.5.28/19.119.55) (q:draft)
zuibup = (t:v) (w:follow completely/follow wholly) (d:zui follow, with bup whole) (e:a pa David bangin Topa ~ lo hi) (r:11.11.6) (q:draft)
zuih = (t:v) (w:follow/obey/keep/observe) (d:form of zui used before ding, nading, man and in dependent clauses) (e:nangma thupiaknate ~ ding ka zekai kei hi) (b:zui) (r:19.119.60/24.9.14) (q:draft)
zuihbeh = (t:v) (w:follow/ensue/result) (d:zuih follow with beh in addition: come as a further consequence) (e:Siatna khatpeuh in a ~ leh) (r:2.21.23/2.21.22) (q:draft)
zuihin = (t:v) (w:follow/observe) (d:zuih follow or observe, with the linking suffix in: zuihin nei, hold to as a rule) (e:cihte ~ nei na hi uh hiam) (b:zuih) (r:51.2.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihkhak = (t:v) (w:fall into following/come to follow) (d:zuih follow, with khak happen to: take up the ways of others) (e:mihoih lote’ gamtatna a ~ ciangin) (r:20.25.26/20.22.25) (q:draft)
zuihlah = (t:v) (w:be unable to follow/fail to keep) (d:zuih follow or keep, with lah fail, not manage) (e:na ~ ding uh zong hi lo hi) (r:5.30.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihlahna = (t:n) (w:failure to keep) (d:zuihlah fail to keep, with the noun suffix na: Thukham zuihlahna, not keeping the Law) (e:Thukham ~ hangin samsiatna panin) (b:zuihlah) (r:48.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihlam = (t:n) (w:following) (d:zuih follow, with lam, the fact or manner of: a zuihlam a muh ciangin, when he saw them following) (e:amau tegel in a ~ a muh ciangin) (r:43.1.38) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihna = (t:n) (w:following/obeying/observance) (d:the act of following or obeying; tuu zuihna is tending sheep) (e:amah ~ panin kihemkhia lo a) (b:zuih) (r:12.18.6/19.119.5) (q:draft)
zuihnop = (t:v) (w:want to follow/want to obey) (d:zuih, the form of zui, follow or obey, with nop, want to) (e:Mi khat in thukham a ~ kei leh) (r:20.28.9/45.8.7) (q:draft)
zuihpah = (t:v) (w:follow at once/go with readily) (d:zuih follow, with pah at once; used before nading) (e:amaute ka ~ nadingin Kha Siangtho in) (r:44.11.12) (q:draft)
zuihpih = (t:v) (w:follow along with/go along with) (d:zuih, follow, with pih, together with: follow a practice along with others, or go with someone along a path) (e:a phuahtawm ngeinate ~ uh hi) (b:zuih) (r:12.17.19/23.42.16) (q:draft)
zuihpihin = (t:v) (w:go along with/lead along) (d:zuihpih follow along with, with the linking suffix in: go with someone along a path) (e:sul ~ ka kha ding hi) (b:zuihpih) (r:23.42.16) (q:draft)
zuihsa = (t:v) (w:have followed/have kept) (d:zuih, follow or keep, with sa, already done: what one has already followed or kept) (e:Hihte khempeuh ka ~ ahi hi) (b:zuih) (r:40.19.20/54.4.6) (q:draft)
zuihsak = (t:v) (w:let go with/send along) (d:zuih follow, with causative sak: let someone accompany) (e:amah nong ~ kei leh kote ka paisuk) (b:zuih) (r:1.43.5) (q:draft)
zuihtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to obey) (d:zuih follow or obey with theih can; the form used before nading, so that one may follow or obey) (e:ama khekhap na ~ nadingun) (b:zuih) (r:60.2.21/41.7.9) (q:draft)
zuihzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to keep) (d:zuih follow, obey, with zawh be able; used before ding and nading) (e:mi khempeuh in a ~ ding hi lo a) (r:40.19.11/50.2.13) (q:draft)
zuihzawhna = (t:n) (w:keeping/observance) (d:zuihzawh be able to keep, with the noun suffix na; Thukham zuihzawhna is keeping the Law) (e:Thukham ~ hang hi loin upna hang hi) (b:zuihzawh) (r:45.3.28/48.2.21) (q:draft)
zuikha = (t:v) (w:follow/be led to follow) (d:zui follow with kha happen to: follow by mistake or be drawn into following, often in warnings) (e:Tua bang mite’ nung ~ kei un) (r:42.21.8/61.3.17) (q:draft)
zuikhawm = (t:v) (w:follow together/go along with) (d:zui follow, with khawm together) (e:tua pa nung a ~ uh hi) (b:zui) (r:40.9.19/55.2.22) (q:draft)
zuikhin = (t:v) (w:have kept/have fulfilled/keep fully) (d:zui, follow or keep, with khin, completely or already) (e:hih thukhamte khempeuh ka ~ hi) (b:zui) (r:41.10.20/45.13.8) (q:draft)
zuikik = (t:v) (w:go back with/follow back) (d:zui, follow, with kik, back or again: go back with someone; in Daniel 11:20 follow after in turn, succeed) (e:nadingin kei hong ~ in) (b:zui) (r:9.15.30/27.11.20) (q:draft)
zuinuam = (t:v) (w:want to follow/be willing to keep) (d:zui follow or keep, with nuam want to) (e:Thukham ~ tuan lo uh hi) (r:48.6.13) (q:draft)
zuipah = (t:v) (w:follow at once/follow immediately) (d:zui follow with pah, at once, without delay) (e:Jesuh nung a ~ uh hi) (r:40.20.34/41.1.18) (q:draft)
zuisak = (t:v) (w:let follow/make follow/send along with) (d:zui follow with sak, cause or allow to follow or go along; also make someone keep a covenant) (e:Kei zong hong ~ in) (b:zui) (r:42.8.38/1.43.4) (q:draft)
zuisakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes follow/one who subjects) (d:zuisak make follow with pa marking a male person: the one who made the creation subject, whose will it follows) (e:~’ deihna bang bek a zui uh hi) (b:zuisak) (r:45.8.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuisuak = (t:v) (w:go on with/keep following/continue in) (d:zui, follow, with suak, through or onward: go along with someone all the way, keep on following) (e:Balaam in Balak’ uliante a ~ hi) (r:4.22.35/59.1.25) (q:draft)
zuisuk = (t:v) (w:follow down/go down along/descend with) (d:zui, follow, with suk for movement downward) (e:sihna lampi ~ lo uh hi) (b:zui) (r:20.15.24/19.49.17) (q:draft)
zuite = (t:n) (w:followers/those who follow/those who keep/those who obey) (d:zui with plural -te, after a: the people who follow or obey) (e:Thukham a ~ a khan’ sau ding a) (b:zui) (r:20.19.16/45.16.11) (q:draft)
zuito = (t:v) (w:follow upward/climb after) (d:zui follow with to upward; the opposite is zuisuk, follow downward) (e:Ka nung hong ~ in) (b:zui) (r:9.14.12/20.15.24) (q:draft)
zuizaw = (t:v) (w:follow rather/follow instead) (d:zui follow with zaw rather, more: follow one way in preference to another) (e:Israel kumpite’ khekhap ~ hi) (b:zui) (r:14.28.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuizo = (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to keep/manage to obey) (d:zui follow or obey with zo be able) (e:mi tawmno bek in a ~ uh hi) (b:zui) (r:40.7.14/43.6.60) (q:draft)
zuk = (t:v) (w:fall/rain) (d:of rain; the form of zu used before loh, nading, mateng and similar words) (e:guah ~ loh kum ciangin zong) (b:zu) (r:24.17.8/59.5.7) (q:draft)
zukham = (t:adj) (w:drunk/drunken/intoxicated) (d:overcome by zu, alcoholic drink; also used for a drunk person, a drunkard) (e:amaute ~ bangin hoisuk hoito uh a) (r:19.107.27/23.51.21) (q:draft)
zukhamin = (t:adv) (w:drunk/in a drunken state) (d:zukham, drunk, with the linking ending in) (e:hih mite in ~ a om kei) (b:zukham) (r:44.2.15/9.1.13) (q:draft)
zukhamna = (t:n) (w:drunkenness/intoxication) (d:the state of being drunk; zukhamna pan a pilvan is to wake from a drunken sleep) (e:~ pen haina ahi hi) (b:zukham) (r:20.20.1/1.9.24) (q:draft)
zukhampa = (t:n) (w:drunkard/drunken man) (d:zukham drunk with pa marking a male person) (e:~ pen ama luak sung mahah) (b:zukham) (r:23.19.14) (q:draft)
zukhamsak = (t:v) (w:make drunk/intoxicate) (d:zukham drunk with sak, cause to be) (e:tua ahih manin amah ~ hi) (b:zukham) (r:10.11.13) (q:draft)
zukhamte = (t:n) (w:drunkards) (e:No ~ aw, tho un la kap un) (b:zukham) (r:29.1.5/19.69.12) (q:draft)
zukna = (t:n) (w:raining/falling of rain) (d:zuk fall, of rain, with the noun suffix na; guah zukna ding mun is the place where rain is to fall) (e:guah ~ ding mun thu pia-in) (b:zuk) (r:18.28.26) (q:draft)
zuksak = (t:v) (w:make rain/send rain/bring rain) (d:cause rain to fall, used with guah rain) (e:Leilu lam huih in guah a ~ bangin) (b:zuk) (r:20.25.23/26.22.24) (q:draft)
zuksakna = (t:n) (w:sending of rain/making rain fall) (d:zuksak make rain fall with the noun suffix na) (e:guah hong ~ ding nangmah in sawl) (b:zuksak) (r:18.38.34) (q:draft)
zul = (t:todo) (r:26.15.4) (q:draft, one verse only, in a zul kat teng for the charred middle part of a stick whose ends are burnt; the meaning of zul alone is not clear)
zulesa = (t:n) (w:drink and meat) (d:apparently zu drink, le and, sa meat: strong drink and meat as feasting; zulesa tawh kidiah, soaked with drink and meat, stands for being drunk) (e:~ tawh kidiahin a om laitakun) (r:34.1.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulhtat = (t:adj) (w:unruly/undisciplined/disorderly) (d:lacking restraint; khuaval zulhtat lo is sober or self-controlled, thadah zulhtat mite are the idle and disorderly) (e:khuaval ~ lo mi, a dik mi) (r:56.1.8/52.5.14) (q:draft)
zulhtatin = (t:adv) (w:disorderly/in an unruly way) (d:zulhtat unruly with in, making an adverb; thadah zulhtatin gamta is to behave in an idle and disorderly way) (e:note lakah thadah ~ ka gamta kei uh hi) (b:zulhtat) (r:53.3.7) (q:draft)
zulhtatna = (t:n) (w:unruliness/wantonness/lack of restraint) (d:zulhtat unruly with the noun suffix na; in the verse the unrestrained conduct of youth that brings shame) (e:na ~ le na meigonna hangin) (b:zulhtat) (r:23.54.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulhzau = (t:adj) (w:faithless/backsliding/unfaithful) (d:turning away and not keeping faith; in the verses said of Israel in Jeremiah, as a zulhzau) (e:Hong kilehkik in, a ~ Israel aw) (r:24.3.12/24.3.11) (q:draft)
zulhzauna = (t:n) (w:backsliding/faithlessness) (d:zulhzau faithless, with the noun suffix na) (e:na ~ uh kong damsak ding hi) (b:zulhzau) (r:24.3.22) (q:draft)
zulim = (t:n) (w:good wine/choice wine) (d:zu wine with lim tasty, parallel to anlim choice food; the verse has new wine) (e:~ nekna in nungakte thadimsak ding hi) (r:38.9.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulkatteng = (t:n) (w:charred part/burnt remainder) (d:apparently zul with kat burn and teng all, the whole: the remaining middle of a stick that the fire has charred; written as three words a zul kat teng in the other text) (e:a omlai a ~, bangin kimang nawn) (r:26.15.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
zum = (t:v) (w:be ashamed/feel shame) (d:often with mai face, mai zum be put to shame) (e:na mai uh ~ ngei lo ding hi) (r:19.34.5/60.4.16) (q:draft)
zum = (t:n) (w:court/office) (d:government office or court of law, as in zum inn and thukhen zum) (e:~ innah hong heekte puanza zong) (r:40.5.40/18.9.32) (q:draft)
zum = (t:adj) (w:pointed/sharp) (d:tapering to a point; mualdawn zum mountain peaks, ciangkhut zum pointed goad) (e:mualdawn ~ tampi a nei) (r:19.68.15/7.3.31) (q:draft)
zuma = (t:n) (w:of the court/at the court) (d:zum court or office with the marker a, of or at: zuma thukhente are the judges of the court) (e:~ thukhente mai-ah hong kaigawpin) (b:zum) (r:42.12.58) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumah = (t:n) (w:in court/at the court) (d:zum court, office with the place marker ah; thukhen zumah is in the law court) (e:Thukhen ~ amah samin hong pai leh) (b:zum) (r:18.9.16/30.5.10) (q:draft)
zumcingte = (t:n) (w:guards/court guards) (d:apparently zum court or office with cing guard and the plural te: those who guard the court; zumcingte omna is the court of the guard) (e:~’ omna ahi tausang tungnung teng) (r:16.3.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumhuai = (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful) (d:causing shame; zumhuai-in gamta is to act shamefully) (e:na ~ gamtatna teng na thuak kul hi) (r:26.16.58/49.5.12) (q:draft)
zumhuaina = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace/nakedness) (d:zumhuai shameful with na: a shameful thing, a disgrace; also the shame of being seen naked) (e:~ thuak khin zo hi) (b:zumhuai) (r:24.48.20/34.3.5) (q:draft)
zumhuaipi = (t:see) <zumhuaipi-in>
zumhuaipi-in = (t:adv) (w:shamefully/disgracefully) (d:zumhuaipi very shameful with the adverb suffix -in) (e:a ~ a gamta uh hi) (r:45.1.27/18.36.14) (q:draft)
zumhuaisak = (t:v) (w:disgrace/put to shame) (d:zumhuai shameful with the causative suffix sak: make shameful, bring disgrace on) (e:A gam buppi ka ~ ding a) (b:zumhuai) (r:24.51.47) (q:draft)
zumin = (t:v) (w:being ashamed/in shame) (d:zum, be ashamed, with the linking suffix in; mai zumin is with shame of face, put to shame) (e:mai ~ ka lungam hi) (b:zum) (r:24.31.19/24.3.25) (q:draft)
zumkhak = (t:n) (w:holiday) (d:apparently zum office with khak shut, a day on which business is closed; in the verse zumkhak hun stands for the New Moon festival when grain could not be sold) (e:~ hun sung i ngak lah hi) (r:30.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumkhakna = (t:n) (w:holiday/day off) (d:zumkhak holiday with the noun suffix na: the keeping of a holiday, with work stopped) (e:pawi bawlna leh nasep khawlin ~ om hi) (b:zumkhak) (r:17.8.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumlai = (t:n) (w:office records/register) (d:apparently zum office with lai writing: galkap zumlai a kem is the one who keeps the army records, the officer who enrols the people) (e:galkap ~ a kem galkap mangpa’ lai-at) (r:24.52.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumna = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (e:~ a thuak kei ding hi) (b:zum) (r:45.10.11/20.19.26) (q:draft)
