zumsak = (t:v) (w:shame/put to shame/humiliate) (d:zum be ashamed with -sak, to make someone ashamed) (e:Lawpna in hong ~ lo ding hi) (b:zum) (r:45.5.5/46.1.27) (q:draft)
zun = (t:n) (w:urine) (e:amau’ ~ mah dawn dingin) (r:12.18.27/23.36.12) (q:draft)
zun = (t:v) (w:be ripe/be fully ripe) (d:of fruit on the tree or vine, often after min ripe: a min a zun, min zun mahmah, very ripe; used where the English has first ripe or early fruit; exact sense not certain) (e:a gah a ~ theikung tawh kibang ding) (r:34.3.12/28.9.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zune = (t:v) (w:drink/feast) (d:drink liquor, from zu and ne; mostly in the pair anne zune, eat and drink) (e:Anne ~ dingin mite tu uh a) (r:46.10.7/21.10.16) (q:draft)
