zunekna = (t:n) (w:drinking/wine drinking/drunkenness) (d:the drinking of zu, wine or other alcoholic drink) (e:~ tawh ka lung nuamsakin) (b:zunek) (r:21.2.3/60.4.3) (q:draft)
zung = (t:n) (w:root) (d:zung kha means take root) (e:a sat ciangin ~ kha zo lo) (r:41.4.6/23.11.10) (q:draft)
Zung = (t:n) (w:root) (d:zung, root, capitalised in the title David’ Zung, the Root of David) (e:David’ ~, Judah pawl pan Humpinelkai) (b:zung) (r:66.5.5) (q:draft)
zungbawh = (t:v) (w:uproot/pull up by the roots) (d:zung root with bawh pull up: tear a plant out with its roots) (e:singkung ~ bangin mawhneite botkhia ding hi) (r:20.2.22/18.8.18) (q:draft)
zungbawhin = (t:v) (w:uproot/pull up by the roots) (d:connective form of zungbawh, uprooting and then) (e:Muvanlai masa pen in ~) (b:zungbawh) (r:26.17.9) (q:draft)
zungbuh = (t:n) (w:ring/signet ring) (d:a finger ring; min gelhna zungbuh or min thuhna zungbuh is a signet ring used for sealing) (e:Faro in a min gelhna ~) (r:1.41.42/17.8.2) (q:draft)
zungbuhin = (t:n) (w:as a ring/as a signet ring) (d:zungbuh ring with the marker in, here as or like: make someone as a signet ring) (e:ka min gelhna ~ kong bawl ding hi) (b:zungbuh) (r:37.2.23) (q:draft)
zungbuhte = (t:n) (w:rings) (d:plural of zungbuh finger ring; min gelhna zungbuhte are signet rings) (e:min gelhna ~ leh nakbuhte) (b:zungbuh) (r:23.3.21/42.15.22) (q:draft)
zungkha = (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:zung, root, with kha: strike root; also written apart as zung kha) (e:a thuk lamah ~ kikin) (r:12.19.30/49.3.17) (q:draft)
zungkha = (t:n) (w:bitter root) (d:in Hebrews 12:15, zungkha a nei singkung, where the English has a bitter root that grows up; perhaps zung, root, with kha, bitter; not confirmed) (e:~ a nei singkung hong khangin) (r:58.12.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
zunglot = (t:v) (w:uproot/pluck up/root out) (d:pull out by the roots; of people, remove them completely from their land) (e:leitang panin nang hong ~ ding hi) (r:19.52.5/5.29.28) (q:draft)
zungpi = (t:n) (w:root/main root) (d:zung root with pi great: the main root that keeps the branches alive) (e:a ~ in note a hong hingsak) (b:zung) (r:45.11.18) (q:draft)
zungte = (t:n) (w:roots) (e:Lei sungah a ~ a teek zongin) (b:zung) (r:18.14.8/18.18.16) (q:draft)
zungthuk = (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:zung root with thuk deep, used with kha: strike deep roots, be firmly rooted) (e:amah in ~ kha-in gam sung a dim hi) (r:19.80.9/51.2.7) (q:draft)
